002	EXO	020	018	Then all the people considered the voices, and the lights, and the sound of the trumpet, and the smoking mountain. And being terrified and struck with fear, they stood at a distance,
002	EXO	020	019	saying to Moses: “Speak to us, and we will listen. Let not the Lord speak to us, lest perhaps we may die.”
002	EXO	020	020	And Moses said to the people: “Do not be afraid. For God came in order to test you, and so that the dread of him might be with you, and you would not sin.”
002	EXO	020	021	And the people stood far away. But Moses approached toward the mist, in which was God.
002	EXO	020	022	Thereafter, the Lord said to Moses: “This you shall say to the sons of Israel: You have seen that I have spoken to you from heaven.
002	EXO	020	023	You shall not make gods of silver, nor shall you make for yourselves gods of gold.
002	EXO	020	024	You shall make an altar from the earth for me, and you shall offer upon it your holocausts and peace-offerings, your sheep and oxen, in every place where the memory of my name shall be. I will come to you, and I will bless you.
002	EXO	020	025	And if you make an altar of stone for me, you shall not build it from cut stones; for if you lift up a tool over it, it will be defiled.
002	EXO	020	026	You shall not ascend by steps to my altar, lest your nakedness be revealed.”
002	EXO	021	001	“These are the judgments which you shall place before them:
002	EXO	021	002	If you buy a Hebrew servant, six years shall he serve you; in the seventh, he shall depart freely, without charge.
002	EXO	021	003	With whatever clothing he arrived, with the like let him depart. If he has a wife, his wife also shall depart, at the same time.
002	EXO	021	004	But if his lord gave him a wife, and she has borne sons and daughters, the woman and her children shall belong to her lord. Yet still, he himself will go out with his clothing.
002	EXO	021	005	And if the servant will say, ‘I love my lord, and my wife and children, I will not depart freely,’
002	EXO	021	006	then his lord shall make an offering for him to the heavens, and it shall be applied to the door and the posts, and he will pierce his ear with an awl. And he shall be his servant in perpetuity.
002	EXO	021	007	If anyone sells his daughter to be a servant, she shall not depart as a female servant is accustomed to go out.
002	EXO	021	008	If she displeases the eyes of her lord, to whom she had been delivered, he shall dismiss her. But he shall have no authority to sell her to a foreign people, even if he despises her.
002	EXO	021	009	But if he has betrothed her to his son, he shall treat her according to the custom with daughters.
002	EXO	021	010	And if he takes another for him, he shall provide to the maiden a marriage, and clothing, and he shall not refuse the price of her chastity.
002	EXO	021	011	If he does not do these three things, she shall depart freely, without money.
002	EXO	021	012	Whoever strikes a man, intending to murder, shall be put to death.
002	EXO	021	013	But if he did not lie in wait for him, but God delivered him into his hands, then I will appoint for you a place to which he must flee.
002	EXO	021	014	If someone murders his neighbor with deliberation, by lying in wait, you shall tear him away from my altar, so that he may die.
002	EXO	021	015	Whoever strikes his father or mother shall die a death.
002	EXO	021	016	Whoever will have stolen a man and sold him, having been convicted of the crime, shall be put to death.
002	EXO	021	017	Whoever speaks evil of his father or mother shall die a death.
002	EXO	021	018	If men will have quarreled, and one of them has struck his neighbor with a stone or a fist, and he does not die, but lies in bed,
002	EXO	021	019	if he gets up again and can walk outside on his staff, he who struck him will be innocent, but only if he makes sufficient restitution for his deeds and for the cost of the physicians.
002	EXO	021	020	Whoever strikes his male or female servant with a staff, and if they have died by his hands, he shall be guilty of a crime.
002	EXO	021	021	But if he survives for one day or two, he shall not be subject to punishment, because it is his money.
002	EXO	021	022	If men will have quarreled, and one of them has struck a pregnant woman, and as a result she miscarries, but she herself survives, he shall be subject to as much damage as the husband of the woman shall petition from him, or as arbitrators shall judge.
002	EXO	021	023	But if her death will have followed, he will repay a life for a life,
002	EXO	021	024	an eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth, a hand for a hand, a foot for a foot,
002	EXO	021	025	a scrape for a scrape, a wound for a wound, a bruise for a bruise.
002	EXO	021	026	If anyone will have struck the eye of his male or female servant, having left them with one eye, he shall release them freely, because of the eye that he has put out.
002	EXO	021	027	Likewise, if he knocks out a tooth of his male or female servant, he shall similarly release them freely.
002	EXO	021	028	If an ox has struck a man or a woman with his horn, and if they die, it shall be stoned. And its flesh shall not be eaten; also, the owner of the ox will be innocent.
002	EXO	021	029	But if the ox had been pushing with his horn, from yesterday and the day before, and they warned his owner, but he did not confine it, and it will have killed a man or a woman, then the ox shall be stoned, and his owner shall be killed.
002	EXO	021	030	But if they have imposed a price on him, he shall give, in exchange for his life, whatever is asked.
002	EXO	021	031	Likewise, if it has struck a son or a daughter with its horns, it shall be subject to a similar verdict.
002	EXO	021	032	If it attacks a male or female servant, he shall give thirty shekels of silver to their lord, yet truly the ox shall be stoned.
002	EXO	021	033	If a man digs or opens a cistern, and does not cover it, and an ox or a donkey falls into it,
002	EXO	021	034	then the owner of the cistern shall repay the price of the beasts, and what is dead will belong to him.
002	EXO	021	035	If the ox of a stranger wounds the ox of another, and it has died, then they shall sell the live ox and divide the price, but the carcass of the dead one they shall distribute between them.
002	EXO	021	036	But if he knew that his ox had pushed with its horns, yesterday and the day before, and its owner did not confine it, then he shall repay an ox for an ox, and he will receive the whole carcass.”
002	EXO	022	001	“If anyone will have stolen an ox or a sheep, and if he kills it or sells it, then he will restore five oxen for one ox, and four sheep for one sheep.
002	EXO	022	002	If a thief will have been discovered breaking into a house, or digging under it, and he has received a mortal wound, he who struck him down will not be guilty of blood.
002	EXO	022	003	But if he did this when the sun was risen, he has perpetrated a homicide, and he shall die. If he does not have the means to make restitution for the theft, he shall be sold.
002	EXO	022	004	If whatever he stole should be found with him, a living thing, either an ox, or a donkey, or a sheep, he shall repay double.
002	EXO	022	005	If there is any damage to a field or a vineyard, when he has released his cattle to pasture on the land of a stranger, he shall repay the best of what he has in his own field, or in his own vineyard, according to the estimation of the damage.
002	EXO	022	006	If a fire will have been discovered departing from brush, and taking hold in stacks of grain, or in crops standing in the fields, whoever ignited the fire shall repay the damages.
002	EXO	022	007	If anyone will have entrusted money, or a container, to his friend to keep, and if these have been stolen from the one who received them: if the thief is found, he shall repay double.
002	EXO	022	008	If the thief is unknown, the lord of the house will be brought before the heavens to swear that he did not lay his hand on the goods of his neighbor,
002	EXO	022	009	so as to perpetrate any fraud, such as with an ox, or a donkey, or a sheep, or clothing, nor to do anything that would be able to cause damage. The case of both shall be brought before the heavens. And if they give judgment against him, he shall repay double to his neighbor.
002	EXO	022	010	If anyone will have entrusted a donkey, an ox, a sheep, or any animal to the keeping of his neighbor, and it will have died, or become disabled, or have been captured by enemies, and no one saw it,
002	EXO	022	011	then there shall be an oath between them, that he did not lay his hand on the goods of his neighbor. And the owner shall accept the oath, and he will not be compelled to make restitution.
002	EXO	022	012	But if it will have been taken away by theft, he shall repay the damages to the owner.
002	EXO	022	013	If it has been eaten by a wild beast, let him carry what was killed to him, and then he shall not make restitution.
002	EXO	022	014	If anyone borrows from his neighbor any of these things, and it has died or been disabled when the owner was not present, he shall be compelled to make restitution.
002	EXO	022	015	But if the owner was present, he shall not make restitution, especially if it had been brought for hired work.
002	EXO	022	016	If a man has led astray a virgin not yet betrothed, and he has slept with her, he shall pay her dowry and have her as a wife.
002	EXO	022	017	If the father of the virgin is not willing to give her, he shall pay money according to manner of a dowry, which virgins are accustomed to receive.
002	EXO	022	018	You shall not permit practitioners of the black arts to live.
002	EXO	022	019	Whoever has sexual intercourse with an animal shall be put to death.
002	EXO	022	020	Whoever immolates to gods, other than to the Lord, shall be killed.
002	EXO	022	021	You shall not harass the newcomer, nor shall you afflict him. For you yourselves were once newcomers in the land of Egypt.
002	EXO	022	022	You shall not harm a widow or an orphan.
002	EXO	022	023	If you hurt them, they will cry out to me, and I will hear their cry.
002	EXO	022	024	And my fury will be enraged, and I will strike you down with the sword. And your wives will become widows, and your sons will become orphans.
002	EXO	022	025	If you lend money to the poor of my people who live among you, you shall not coerce them like a collector, nor oppress them with usury.
002	EXO	022	026	If you take a garment from your neighbor as a pledge, you shall return it to him again before the setting of the sun.
002	EXO	022	027	For it is all that he has to cover himself, to clothe his body; nor does he have anything else in which to sleep. If he cries out to me, I will hear him, because I am compassionate.
002	EXO	022	028	You shall not disparage the heavens, and you shall not speak evil of the leader of your people.
002	EXO	022	029	You shall not delay in paying your tithes and your first-fruits. You shall give the firstborn of your sons to me.
002	EXO	022	030	You shall do likewise with those of the oxen and the sheep. For seven days, let it be with its mother; on the eighth day you shall repay it to me.
002	EXO	022	031	You shall be holy men for me. The flesh, from which beasts will have tasted, you shall not eat, but you will throw it to the dogs.”
002	EXO	023	001	“You shall not accept a lying voice. Neither shall you join your hand so as to give false testimony on behalf of the impious.
002	EXO	023	002	You shall not follow the crowd in doing evil. Neither shall you go astray in judgment, by agreeing with the majority opinion, apart from the truth.
002	EXO	023	003	Likewise, you shall not show pity in judgment of the poor.
002	EXO	023	004	If you come across an ox or a donkey of your enemy, which has gone astray, lead it back to him.
002	EXO	023	005	If you see the donkey of one who hates you, fallen under its burden, you shall not pass by without lifting it up with him.
002	EXO	023	006	You shall not deviate in judgment of the poor.
002	EXO	023	007	You shall flee from lies. The innocent and the just you shall not kill. For I shun the impious.
002	EXO	023	008	Neither shall you accept bribes, which blind even the prudent and subvert the words of the just.
002	EXO	023	009	You shall not harass a sojourner, for you know the life of a newcomer. For you yourselves also were sojourners in the land of Egypt.
002	EXO	023	010	For six years, you shall sow your land and gather its produce.
002	EXO	023	011	But in the seventh year, you shall release it and cause it to rest, so that the poor of your people may eat. And whatever remains, let the beasts of the field eat it. So shall you do with your vineyard and your olive grove.
002	EXO	023	012	For six days, you shall work. On the seventh day, you shall cease, so that your ox and your donkey may rest, and so that the newcomer and the son of your handmaid may be refreshed.
002	EXO	023	013	Preserve all that I have said to you. And by the names of foreign gods you shall not swear; neither shall these be heard from your mouth.
002	EXO	023	014	Three times in each year, you shall celebrate feasts to me.
002	EXO	023	015	You shall keep the solemnity of unleavened bread. For seven days you shall eat unleavened bread, just as I instructed you, at the time of the month of new grain, when you departed from Egypt. You shall not appear empty-handed in my sight,
002	EXO	023	016	for it is the solemnity of the harvest of the first-fruits of your work, of whatever you have sown in the field. Likewise, it is a solemnity at the end of the season, when you will have gathered in all your crops from the field.
002	EXO	023	017	Three times a year, all your males shall appear before the Lord your God.
002	EXO	023	018	You shall not immolate the blood of my victim over leaven, nor shall the fat of my solemnity remain until morning.
002	EXO	023	019	You shall carry the first grain of the land to the house of the Lord your God. You shall not cook a young goat in the milk of its mother.
002	EXO	023	020	Behold, I will send my Angel, who will go before you, and preserve you on your journey, and lead you into the place that I have prepared.
002	EXO	023	021	Heed him, and hear his voice, and do not hold him in disregard. For he will not release you when you have sinned, and my name is in him.
002	EXO	023	022	But if you listen to his voice and do all that I say, I will be an enemy to your enemies, and I will afflict those who afflict you.
002	EXO	023	023	And my Angel will go before you, and he will bring you to the Amorite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, and the Canaanite, and the Hivite, and the Jebusite, whom I will crush.
002	EXO	023	024	You shall not adore their gods, nor worship them. You shall not do their works, but you shall destroy them and break apart their statues.
002	EXO	023	025	And you shall serve the Lord your God, so that I may bless your bread and your waters, and so that I may take away sickness from your midst.
002	EXO	023	026	There will not be fruitless or barren ones in your land. I will fill up the number of your days.
002	EXO	023	027	I will send my terror to run ahead of you, and I will kill all the people to whom you will enter. And I will turn the backs of all your enemies before you,
002	EXO	023	028	sending wasps ahead, so that they will put to flight the Hivite, and the Canaanite, and the Hittite, before you enter.
002	EXO	023	029	I will not cast them out from your face in one year, lest the land be reduced to a wilderness and the wild beasts increase against you.
002	EXO	023	030	I will expel them little by little from your sight, until you have expanded and may possess the land.
002	EXO	023	031	Then I will set your limits to be from the Red Sea to the Sea of the Palestinians, and from the desert all the way to the river. I will deliver into your hands the inhabitants of the land, and I will cast them out from your sight.
002	EXO	023	032	You shall not enter into a pact with them, nor with their gods.
002	EXO	023	033	They may not live on your land, lest perhaps they may cause you to sin against me, if you serve their gods, which certainly would be a temptation for you.”
002	EXO	024	001	He also said to Moses: “Ascend to the Lord, you and Aaron, Nadab and Abihu, and seventy elders out of Israel, and adore from a distance.
002	EXO	024	002	And only Moses will ascend to the Lord, and these shall not approach. Neither shall the people ascend with him.”
002	EXO	024	003	Therefore, Moses went and explained to the people all the words of the Lord, as well as the judgments. And all the people responded with one voice: “We will do all the words of the Lord, which he has spoken.”
002	EXO	024	004	Then Moses wrote all the words of the Lord. And rising up in the morning, he built an altar at the base of the mountain, with twelve titles according to the twelve tribes of Israel.
002	EXO	024	005	And he sent youths from the sons of Israel, and they offered holocausts, and they immolated calves as peace-offerings to the Lord.
002	EXO	024	006	And so Moses took one half part of the blood, and he put it into bowls. Then the remaining part he poured over the altar.
002	EXO	024	007	And taking up the book of the covenant, he read it in the hearing of the people, who said: “All that the Lord has spoken, we will do, and we will be obedient.”
002	EXO	024	008	In truth, taking up the blood, he sprinkled it on the people, and he said, “This is the blood of the covenant, which the Lord has formed with you concerning all these words.”
002	EXO	024	009	And Moses and Aaron, Nadab and Abihu, and seventy of the elders of Israel ascended.
002	EXO	024	010	And they saw the God of Israel. And under his feet was something like a work of sapphire stone, or like the sky, when it is serene.
002	EXO	024	011	Neither did he lay his hand upon those of the sons of Israel who were at a distance. And they saw God, and they ate and drank.
002	EXO	024	012	Then the Lord said to Moses: “Ascend to me on the mountain, and be there. And I will give to you tablets of stone, and the law and the commandments that I have written. So may you teach them.”
002	EXO	024	013	Moses rose up, with Joshua his minister. And Moses, ascending on the mountain of God,
002	EXO	024	014	said to the elders: “Wait here, until we return to you. You have Aaron and Hur with you. If any question arises, you shall refer it to them.”
002	EXO	024	015	And when Moses had ascended, a cloud covered the mountain.
002	EXO	024	016	And the glory of the Lord dwelt upon Sinai, covering it with a cloud for six days. And on the seventh day, he called to him from the middle of the mist.
002	EXO	024	017	Now the appearance of the glory of the Lord was like a burning fire over the summit of the mountain in the sight of the sons of Israel.
002	EXO	024	018	And Moses, entering into the midst of the cloud, ascended the mountain. And he was there for forty days and forty nights.
002	EXO	025	001	And the Lord spoke to Moses, saying:
002	EXO	025	002	“Speak to the sons of Israel, so that they may take the first-fruits to me. You shall accept these from every man who offers of his own accord.
002	EXO	025	003	Now these are the things that you must accept: Gold, and silver, and brass,
002	EXO	025	004	hyacinth and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine linen, the hair of goats,
002	EXO	025	005	and the skins of rams, dyed red, and skins of violet, and setim wood,
002	EXO	025	006	oil to prepare lights, aromatics as ointments and sweet-smelling incense,
002	EXO	025	007	onyx stones and gems to adorn the ephod as well as the breastplate.
002	EXO	025	008	And they shall make a sanctuary for me, and I will live in their midst.
002	EXO	025	009	According to exact likeness of the tabernacle, and all of the vessels for its rituals, that I will reveal to you, so shall you make it.
002	EXO	025	010	Join together an ark of setim wood, whose length shall hold two and one half cubits; the width, one and one half cubits; the height, likewise, one and one half cubits.
002	EXO	025	011	And you shall overlay it with the finest gold, inside and out. And over it, you shall fashion a gold crown all around,
002	EXO	025	012	and four gold rings, which you shall set into the four corners of the ark. Let two rings be on one side and two on the other.
002	EXO	025	013	Likewise, you shall make bars of setim wood and cover them with gold.
002	EXO	025	014	And you shall put them through the rings that are in the sides of the ark, so that it may be carried on them.
002	EXO	025	015	These must always be in the rings, neither shall they ever be drawn out of them.
002	EXO	025	016	And you shall place the testimony, which I will give to you, in the ark.
002	EXO	025	017	You shall also make a propitiatory of the finest gold. Its length shall hold two and one half cubits, and the width, one and one half cubits.
002	EXO	025	018	Likewise, you shall make two Cherubim of formed gold, on both sides of the oracle.
002	EXO	025	019	Let one Cherub be on the one side, and the other be on the other.
002	EXO	025	020	And let them cover both sides of the propitiatory, spreading their wings and covering the oracle, and let them look out toward one another, their faces being turned toward the propitiatory, with which the ark is to be covered,
002	EXO	025	021	in which you will place the testimony that I will give to you.
002	EXO	025	022	From there, I will warn you and speak to you, above the propitiatory and from the middle of the two Cherubim, which will be over the ark of the testimony, about everything that I will command of the sons of Israel through you.
002	EXO	025	023	You shall also make a table of setim wood, having two cubits of length, and one cubit in width, and one cubit and one half cubits in height.
002	EXO	025	024	And you shall overlay it with the purest gold. And you shall make it with a gold lip all around,
002	EXO	025	025	and for the lip itself an engraved crown, four fingers high, and above it another little gold crown.
002	EXO	025	026	Likewise, you shall prepare four gold rings and set them in the four corners of the same table, over each foot.
002	EXO	025	027	Under the crown, there shall be gold rings, so that the bars may be put through them and the table may be carried.
002	EXO	025	028	Likewise, the bars themselves you shall make of setim wood, and surround them with gold, to lift up the table.
002	EXO	025	029	You shall also prepare small cups, as well as bowls, censers, and measuring cups, with which the libations shall be offered, out of the purest gold.
002	EXO	025	030	And you shall place upon the table the bread of the presence, in my sight always.
002	EXO	025	031	You shall also make a lampstand, formed from the finest gold, along with its stem and arms, its bowl and little spheres, as well as the lilies proceeding from it.
002	EXO	025	032	Six branches shall go out from the sides: three out of one side and three out of the other.
002	EXO	025	033	Three bowls, the size of nuts, shall be on each branch, and a little sphere with it, and a lily. And three similar bowls, in the likeness of nuts, shall be on the other branch, and a little sphere with it, and a lily. This shall be the form of the six branches, which are to proceed from the stem.
002	EXO	025	034	Then, in the lampstand itself, there shall be four bowls, the size of nuts, and each with little spheres and lilies.
002	EXO	025	035	Little spheres under two branches in three places, which together make six, shall proceed from one of the stems.
002	EXO	025	036	Thus both the little spheres and the branches shall be made out of the same thing: entirely formed from the purest gold.
002	EXO	025	037	You shall also make seven lamps, and you shall place them upon the lampstand, so that they may give light in every direction.
002	EXO	025	038	Likewise, the candle snuffers, and the place where the candles will be extinguished, shall be made from the purest gold.
002	EXO	025	039	The entire weight of the candlestick, with all its parts, shall hold one talent of the purest gold.
002	EXO	025	040	Observe, and then make it according to the example that was shown to you on the mountain.”
002	EXO	026	001	“Truly, thus shall you make the tabernacle: You shall make ten curtains of fine twisted linen, and hyacinth as well as purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, with diverse embroidery.
002	EXO	026	002	The length of one curtain shall have twenty-eight cubits. The width shall be four cubits. The entire set of curtains shall be of one measure.
002	EXO	026	003	Five curtains shall be joined to one another, and the other five shall be similarly coupled together.
002	EXO	026	004	You shall make loops of hyacinth on the sides at the edges of the curtains, so that they will be able to be joined to one another.
002	EXO	026	005	A curtain shall have fifty loops on each of two sides, inserted in such a manner that loop may come against loop, and one can be fitted to the other.
002	EXO	026	006	You shall also make fifty rings of gold, with which the veils of the curtains are to be joined, so that it shall be one tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	007	You shall also make eleven haircloth canopies to cover the roof of the tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	008	The length of one canopy shall hold thirty cubits, and the width, four. The measure of all the canopies shall be equal.
002	EXO	026	009	Five of these you shall join by themselves, and six of these you shall couple to one another, in such a manner as to double the sixth canopy at the front of the roof.
002	EXO	026	010	You shall also make fifty loops along the edge of one canopy, so that it may be able to be joined with the other, and fifty loops along the edge of the other canopy, so that it may be coupled with the other.
002	EXO	026	011	You shall also make fifty brass buckles, with which the loops may be joined, so that there may be one covering out of all.
002	EXO	026	012	Then what will be left over of the canopies which are prepared for the roof, that is, one canopy which is in excess, from half of it you shall cover the back of the tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	013	And one cubit will hang down on one side, and another on the other side, which is more than the length of the curtains, protecting both sides of the tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	014	You shall also make another covering for the roof from the skins of rams, dyed-red, and above that again, another covering of violet-colored skins.
002	EXO	026	015	You shall also make the standing panels of the tabernacle from setim wood.
002	EXO	026	016	Of these, each shall have ten cubits in length, and in width, one and one half.
002	EXO	026	017	At the sides of the panels, there shall be made two dovetails, by which one panel may be connected to another panel; and in this way all the panels shall be prepared.
002	EXO	026	018	Of these, twenty shall be at the meridian, which lies toward the south.
002	EXO	026	019	For these, you shall cast forty bases of silver, so that two bases will lie under each panel at its two corners.
002	EXO	026	020	Likewise, at the second side of the tabernacle, which lies to the north, there shall be twenty panels,
002	EXO	026	021	having forty bases of silver; two bases shall support each panel.
002	EXO	026	022	Truly, toward the western part of the tabernacle, you shall make six panels,
002	EXO	026	023	and again another two, which will be raised at the corners, behind the back of the tabernacle.
002	EXO	026	024	And these shall be joined together from bottom to top, and one joint shall retain them all. Likewise, two of the panels, which will be set at the corners, shall be served by similar joints.
002	EXO	026	025	And together these will be eight panels, and their bases of silver, sixteen, counting two bases for each panel.
002	EXO	026	026	You shall also make five bars of setim wood, to connect the panels on one side of the tabernacle,
002	EXO	026	027	and five others on the other side, and the same number toward the western part.
002	EXO	026	028	These shall be set along the middle of the panels, from one end all the way to the other end.
002	EXO	026	029	Likewise, the panels themselves you shall overlay with gold, and you shall establish rings of gold in them, by which the bars of the panels may be connected. These you shall cover with layers of gold.
002	EXO	026	030	And you shall raise the tabernacle according to the example which was shown to you on the mountain.
002	EXO	026	031	You shall also make a veil of hyacinth, and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine twisted linen, wrought with a diversity of continuous and beautiful embroidery.
002	EXO	026	032	And you shall suspend it before four columns of setim wood, which themselves certainly shall be overlaid with gold, and have heads of gold, but bases of silver.
002	EXO	026	033	Then the veil shall be inserted through the rings. Beyond the veil, you shall place the ark of the testimony, where both the Sanctuary and the Sanctuary of Sanctuaries shall be divided.
002	EXO	026	034	And you shall place the propitiatory over the ark of the testimony, in the Holy of Holies.
002	EXO	026	035	And the table shall be outside the veil. And opposite the table shall be the lampstand, in the meridian of the tabernacle. For the table shall stand at the north side.
002	EXO	026	036	You shall also make a tent at the entrance of the tabernacle from hyacinth, and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine twisted linen, wrought with embroidery.
002	EXO	026	037	And you shall overlay with gold five columns of setim wood, over which the tent shall be drawn. The heads of these shall be of gold, and the bases of brass.”
002	EXO	027	001	“You shall also make an altar of setim wood, which will have five cubits in length, and the same in width, that is, four equal sides, and three cubits in height.
002	EXO	027	002	Now there shall be horns at the four corners of it, and you shall cover it with brass.
002	EXO	027	003	And you shall make, for its uses, pans to receive the ashes, and tongs as well as small hooks, and receptacles for fire. You shall fabricate all of its vessels from brass,
002	EXO	027	004	along with a grating of brass in the manner of a net. At its four corners there shall be four rings of brass,
002	EXO	027	005	which you shall place under the base of the altar. And the grating will extend even to the middle of the altar.
002	EXO	027	006	You shall also make, for the altar, two bars of setim wood, which you shall cover with layers of brass.
002	EXO	027	007	And you shall lead them through the rings, and they will be on both sides of the altar to carry it.
002	EXO	027	008	You shall not make it solid, but empty and hollow at the interior, just as it was shown to you on the mountain.
002	EXO	027	009	You shall also make the atrium of the tabernacle, at the southern part of which, opposite the meridian, there shall be hangings of fine twisted linen: one side extending for one hundred cubits in length.
002	EXO	027	010	And you shall make twenty columns with the same number of bases of brass, the heads of which, with their engravings, shall be made of silver.
002	EXO	027	011	In like manner also, throughout the length of the north side, there shall be hangings of one hundred cubits, and twenty columns, and the same number of bases of brass, and their heads with their engravings of silver.
002	EXO	027	012	Yet truly, along the width of the atrium that looks out toward the west, there shall be hangings of fifty cubits, and ten columns, and the same number of bases.
002	EXO	027	013	Likewise, along the width of the atrium that looks out toward the east, there shall be fifty cubits,
002	EXO	027	014	along which there shall be assigned hangings of fifteen cubits for one side, and three columns, and the same number of bases.
002	EXO	027	015	And, along the other side, there shall be hangings occupying fifteen cubits, with three columns and the same number of bases.
002	EXO	027	016	Yet truly, at the entrance of the atrium, there shall be made a hanging of twenty cubits, of hyacinth and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine twisted linen, wrought with embroidery. It shall have four columns, with the same number of bases.
002	EXO	027	017	All the columns surrounding the atrium shall be clothed with layers of silver, with silver heads, and with bases of brass.
002	EXO	027	018	In length, the atrium shall occupy one hundred cubits, in width, fifty; the height shall be of five cubits. And it shall be made of fine twisted linen, and it shall have bases of brass.
002	EXO	027	019	All the vessels of the tabernacle, for all uses and ceremonies, even to the tent pegs for its atrium, you shall make of brass.
002	EXO	027	020	Instruct the sons of Israel so that they may bring you the purest oil of the olive trees, crushed with a pestle, so that a lamp may always burn
002	EXO	027	021	in the tabernacle of the testimony, outside of the veil that enshrouds the testimony. And Aaron and his sons shall arrange it, so that it may give light in the presence of the Lord, until morning. This shall be a perpetual observance among the sons of Israel, throughout their successions.”
002	EXO	028	001	“Also, join to yourself your brother Aaron, with his sons from the midst of the sons of Israel, so that they may exercise the priesthood for me: Aaron, Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar.
002	EXO	028	002	And you shall make a holy vestment for Aaron, your brother, with glory and elegance.
002	EXO	028	003	And you shall speak to all the wise of heart, whom I have filled with the spirit of prudence, so that they may make the vestments of Aaron, in which, having been sanctified, he may minister to me.
002	EXO	028	004	Now these shall be the vestments that they shall make: A breastplate and an ephod, a tunic and a close-fit linen garment, a headdress and a wide belt. They shall make the holy vestments for your brother Aaron and his sons, so that they may exercise the priesthood for me.
002	EXO	028	005	And they shall receive gold, and hyacinth, and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine linen.
002	EXO	028	006	Then they shall make the ephod of gold, and hyacinth, and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine twisted linen, wrought with diverse colors.
002	EXO	028	007	It shall have two edges joined at the top on both sides, so that they may respond as one.
002	EXO	028	008	Likewise, the weaving and all the detail work shall be of gold, and hyacinth, and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine twisted linen.
002	EXO	028	009	And you shall take two onyx stones and engrave on them the names of the sons of Israel:
002	EXO	028	010	six names on one stone, and the remaining six on the other, according to the order of their birth.
002	EXO	028	011	By the work of a sculptor and the skill of a jeweler, you shall engrave them with the names of the sons of Israel, enclosed and encompassed with gold.
002	EXO	028	012	And you shall place them on both sides of the ephod, as a memorial to the sons of Israel. And Aaron shall carry their names before the Lord, upon both shoulders, as a remembrance.
002	EXO	028	013	You shall also make hooks of gold,
002	EXO	028	014	and two little chains of the purest gold, linked to one another, which you shall insert into the hooks.
002	EXO	028	015	Likewise, you shall make the breastplate of judgment, wrought with diverse colors according to the weaving of the ephod: of gold, hyacinth and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine twisted linen.
002	EXO	028	016	It shall have four corners and be doubled. It shall have the measure of the palm of a hand, both in length and in width.
002	EXO	028	017	And you shall set within it four rows of stones. In the first row, there shall be a sardius stone, and a topaz, and an emerald.
002	EXO	028	018	In the second, there shall be a garnet, a sapphire, and a jasper.
002	EXO	028	019	In the third, there shall be a zircon, an agate, and an amethyst.
002	EXO	028	020	In the fourth, there shall be a chrysolite, an onyx, and a beryl. They shall be set in gold by their rows.
002	EXO	028	021	And these shall have the names of the sons of Israel. With twelve names shall they be engraved: each stone with one name from the twelve tribes.
002	EXO	028	022	You shall make chains of the purest gold, linked one to another, on the breastplate,
002	EXO	028	023	and two rings of gold, which you shall place at both ends of the breastplate.
002	EXO	028	024	And the golden chains, you shall join to the rings, which are at its edges.
002	EXO	028	025	And the ends of the chains themselves, you shall couple with two hooks, on both sides of the ephod, which looks toward the breastplate.
002	EXO	028	026	You shall also make two rings of gold, which you shall place at the ends of the breastplate, at the borders which are away from the region of the ephod and which look toward its back.
002	EXO	028	027	And then you shall also make two other rings of gold, which are to be suspended on both sides at the bottom of the ephod, which looks out opposite the face of the lower juncture, so that the breastplate can be fitted to the ephod.
002	EXO	028	028	And it shall be drawn tight to the rings of the breastplate, by the rings of the ephod, with a hyacinth band, so that the well-constructed juncture will remain in place, and the breastplate and the ephod will not be able to be separated from one another.
002	EXO	028	029	And Aaron shall carry the names of the sons of Israel on the breastplate of judgment upon his chest, when he enters into the Sanctuary, as a memorial in the presence of the Lord in eternity.
002	EXO	028	030	Then you shall place in the breastplate of judgment, Doctrine and Truth, which shall then be upon Aaron’s chest, when he enters before the Lord. And he shall wear the judgment of the sons of Israel on his chest, in the sight of the Lord always.
002	EXO	028	031	And you shall make the tunic for the ephod entirely of hyacinth,
002	EXO	028	032	and the head will be above its middle, with a hem woven around it, just as is usually made at the end parts of a garment, so that it may not be easily broken.
002	EXO	028	033	Yet truly, beneath it, at the base of the same tunic, all around, you shall make something like pomegranates, from hyacinth, and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, with little bells set in their midst.
002	EXO	028	034	So then, there shall be a little golden bell and a pomegranate, and again another golden bell and a pomegranate.
002	EXO	028	035	And Aaron will be vested with it during the office of his ministry, so that the sound may be heard when he enters and exits the Sanctuary, in the sight of the Lord, and so that he may not die.
002	EXO	028	036	And you shall make a plate of the purest gold, in which you shall engrave, with the skill of a sculptor, ‘Holy to the Lord.’
002	EXO	028	037	And you shall fasten it with a band of hyacinth, and it shall be upon the headdress,
002	EXO	028	038	hanging in front of the high priest. And Aaron shall carry the iniquities of that which the sons of Israel have offered and sanctified, in all their gifts and donations. But the plate will always be at his forehead, so that the Lord may be well pleased with them.
002	EXO	028	039	And you shall draw the tunic tight with fine linen, and you shall make a headdress of fine linen, and a wide belt, wrought with embroidery.
002	EXO	028	040	Furthermore, for the sons of Aaron, you shall prepare linen tunics, and wide belts as well as headdresses, with glory and elegance.
002	EXO	028	041	And with all these you shall vest your brother Aaron, and his sons with him. And you shall consecrate all their hands, and you shall sanctify them, so that they may exercise the priesthood for me.
002	EXO	028	042	You shall also make linen undergarments, in order to cover the flesh of their nakedness, from the kidneys all the way to the thighs.
002	EXO	028	043	And Aaron and his sons will use them when they enter the tabernacle of the testimony, and when they approach toward the altar, in order to minister in the sanctuary, lest, being guilty of iniquity, they may die. It shall be a law forever for Aaron, and for his offspring after him.”
002	EXO	029	001	“But you shall also do this, so that they may be consecrated to me in the priesthood: Take a calf from the herd, and two immaculate rams,
002	EXO	029	002	and unleavened bread, and a crust without leaven that has been sprinkled with oil, likewise, unleavened cakes smeared with oil. You shall make them all from the same wheat flour.
002	EXO	029	003	And, having placed them in baskets, you shall offer them, along with the calf and the two rams.
002	EXO	029	004	And you shall bring forward Aaron and his sons, to the door of the tabernacle of the testimony. And when you will have washed the father with his sons in water,
002	EXO	029	005	you shall clothe Aaron in his vestments, that is, with the linen, and the tunic, and the ephod, and the breastplate, which you shall draw together with the wide belt.
002	EXO	029	006	And you shall place the headdress on his head and the holy plate upon the headdress.
002	EXO	029	007	And you shall pour the oil of unction over his head. And so, by this rite, he shall be consecrated.
002	EXO	029	008	Likewise, you shall bring forward his sons, and you shall clothe them in the linen tunics, and wrap them with the wide belt:
002	EXO	029	009	Aaron, certainly, as well as his sons. And you shall impose headdresses upon them. And they shall be priests to me by a perpetual ordinance. After you have initiated their hands,
002	EXO	029	010	you shall bring forward also the calf, in the presence of the tabernacle of the testimony. And Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands upon its head.
002	EXO	029	011	And you shall sacrifice it in the sight of the Lord, beside the door of the tabernacle of the testimony.
002	EXO	029	012	And taking some of the blood of the calf, you shall place it upon the horns of the altar with your finger, but the remainder of the blood you shall pour next to its base.
002	EXO	029	013	And you shall take all the fat which covers its intestines, and the mesh of the liver, as well as the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, and you shall offer them as a burnt offering upon the altar.
002	EXO	029	014	Yet truly, the flesh of the calf, and the hide and the dung, you shall burn outside, beyond the camp, because it is for sin.
002	EXO	029	015	Likewise, you shall take one ram, and upon its head Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands.
002	EXO	029	016	And when you will have sacrificed it, you shall take from its blood and pour it around the altar.
002	EXO	029	017	Then you shall cut the ram into pieces, and, having washed its intestines and feet, you shall place these upon the cut-up flesh and upon its head.
002	EXO	029	018	And you shall offer the entire ram as a burnt offering upon the altar. It is an oblation to the Lord, a most sweet odor of the victim of the Lord.
002	EXO	029	019	Likewise, you shall take the other ram, upon whose head Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands.
002	EXO	029	020	And when you will have immolated it, you shall take of its blood, and place it on the tip of the right ear of Aaron and his sons, and on the thumbs and big toes of their right hand and right foot, and you shall pour the blood upon the altar, all around.
002	EXO	029	021	And when you have taken from the blood that is on the altar, and from the oil of unction, you shall sprinkle Aaron and his vestment, his sons and their vestments. And after they and their vestments have been consecrated,
002	EXO	029	022	you shall take the fat of the ram, and the rump, and the lard that covers the internal organs, and the mesh of the liver, and the two kidneys along with the fat that is on them, and the right shoulder, because it is the ram of consecration,
002	EXO	029	023	and one turn of bread, a crust sprinkled with oil, and a cake from the basket of unleavened bread, which was placed in the sight of the Lord.
002	EXO	029	024	And you shall place all these in the hands of Aaron and his sons, and you shall sanctify them, lifting them up in the sight of the Lord.
002	EXO	029	025	And you shall take all these things from their hands and burn them upon the altar as a holocaust, as a most sweet odor in the sight of the Lord, because it is his oblation.
002	EXO	029	026	Likewise, you shall take the chest of the ram, with which Aaron was initiated, and you shall sanctify it, lifting it up in the sight of the Lord, and it will fall to your share.
002	EXO	029	027	And you shall sanctify both the consecrated chest and the shoulder that you separated from the ram,
002	EXO	029	028	with which Aaron was initiated with his sons, and these will fall to the share of Aaron and his sons, as a perpetual oath by the sons of Israel. For these are the greatest and the first of their victims of peace, which they offer to the Lord.
002	EXO	029	029	But the holy vestment, which Aaron shall use, his sons shall possess after him, so that they may be anointed in it and their hands may be consecrated.
002	EXO	029	030	For seven days, he who is high priest in his place and who enters the tabernacle of the testimony to minister in the Sanctuary shall use it.
002	EXO	029	031	But you shall take the ram of consecration and cook its flesh in the holy place.
002	EXO	029	032	And Aaron and his sons shall feed on it. Likewise, the loaves which are in the basket, they shall consume in the vestibule of the tabernacle of the testimony,
002	EXO	029	033	so that it may be an appeasing sacrifice, and so that the hands of those who offer may be sanctified. A stranger shall not eat from these, for they are holy.
002	EXO	029	034	And what may remain until morning, of the consecrated flesh or of the bread, you shall burn these remnants with fire. These shall not be eaten, because they have been sanctified.
002	EXO	029	035	All that I have instructed you concerning Aaron and his sons, you shall do. For seven days shall you consecrate their hands,
002	EXO	029	036	and you shall offer a calf for sin on each day, as an atonement. And you shall cleanse the altar when you will have immolated the victim of expiation, and you shall anoint it for sanctification.
002	EXO	029	037	For seven days, you shall expiate and sanctify the altar, and it shall be the Holy of holies. All those who will touch it must be sanctified.
002	EXO	029	038	This is what you shall acquire for the altar: Two one-year-old lambs, each day continually,
002	EXO	029	039	one lamb in the morning, and the other in the evening;
002	EXO	029	040	for the one lamb, a tenth part of fine flour sprinkled with crushed oil, which shall have the measure of the fourth part of a hin, and wine for a libation, of the same measure;
002	EXO	029	041	truly, the other lamb you shall offer in the evening, according to the ritual of the morning oblation, and according to what we have said, as an odor of sweetness.
002	EXO	029	042	It is a sacrifice to the Lord, by a perpetual oblation among your generations, at the door of the tabernacle of the testimony before the Lord, where I resolve to speak to you.
002	EXO	029	043	And there I will instruct the sons of Israel, and the altar shall be sanctified by my glory.
002	EXO	029	044	I will also sanctify the tabernacle of the testimony with the altar, and Aaron with his sons, to exercise the priesthood for me.
002	EXO	029	045	And I will live in the midst of the sons of Israel, and I will be their God.
002	EXO	029	046	And they shall know that I am the Lord their God, who led them away from the land of Egypt, so that I might dwell among them. I am the Lord their God.”
002	EXO	030	001	“You shall also make an altar, for the burning of incense, from setim wood,
002	EXO	030	002	having one cubit in length, and another in width, that is, four equal sides, and two cubits in height. Horns shall proceed from the same.
002	EXO	030	003	And you shall clothe it with the purest gold, both its grating and the walls around it, and also the horns. And you shall make for it a crown of gold in a circle,
002	EXO	030	004	and two gold rings under the crown on each side, so that the bars may be set in them and the altar may be carried.
002	EXO	030	005	Also, you shall make its bars of setim wood, and you shall overlay them with gold.
002	EXO	030	006	And you shall set the altar opposite the veil, which hangs in front of the ark of the testimony, before the propitiatory with which the testimony is covered, where I will speak to you.
002	EXO	030	007	And Aaron shall burn incense upon it, a sweet fragrance, in the morning. When he lights the lamps, he shall burn it.
002	EXO	030	008	And when he assembles them in the evening, he shall burn an everlasting incense before the Lord throughout your generations.
002	EXO	030	009	You shall not offer upon it incense of another composition, nor an oblation, nor a victim; neither shall you offer libations.
002	EXO	030	010	And Aaron shall pray over its horns once a year, with the blood of what was offered for sin. And he shall make atonement over it in your generations. It shall be the Holy of holies to the Lord.”
002	EXO	030	011	And the Lord spoke to Moses, saying:
002	EXO	030	012	“When you have taken the sum of the sons of Israel, according to their number, each shall give a price for their souls to the Lord, and there will be no scourge among them, when they will be reviewed.
002	EXO	030	013	Then all those who pass shall give by name: one half shekel, according to the measure at the temple. A shekel has twenty obols. The half part of a shekel shall be offered to the Lord.
002	EXO	030	014	He who has been numbered from twenty years and above shall give the price.
002	EXO	030	015	The rich shall not add to the half shekel, and the poor shall diminish nothing.
002	EXO	030	016	And the money received, which was collected from the sons of Israel, you shall deliver for the uses of the tabernacle of the testimony, so that it may be a memorial of them before the Lord, and he may act favorably toward their souls.”
002	EXO	030	017	And the Lord spoke to Moses, saying:
002	EXO	030	018	“You shall also make a bronze washtub with its base to wash in; and you shall place it between the tabernacle of the testimony and the altar. And when water has been added,
002	EXO	030	019	Aaron and his sons shall wash their hands and feet in it:
002	EXO	030	020	when they enter the tabernacle of the testimony, and when they approach to the altar so as to offer incense to the Lord upon it,
002	EXO	030	021	otherwise, they may die. This shall be an everlasting law to him, and to his offspring, throughout their successions.”
002	EXO	030	022	And the Lord spoke to Moses,
002	EXO	030	023	saying: “Take for yourself aromatics: of the first and best myrrh, five hundred shekels, and of cinnamon half as much, that is, two hundred and fifty shekels; of sweet flag similarly two hundred and fifty,
002	EXO	030	024	but of cassia, five hundred shekels by the weight of the sanctuary, and of the oil of olives the measure of a hin.
002	EXO	030	025	And you shall make the holy oil of unction, an ointment composed with the skills of a perfumer,
002	EXO	030	026	and with it you shall anoint the tabernacle of the testimony, and the ark of the testament,
002	EXO	030	027	and the table with its vessels, and the lampstand and its utensils, the altars of incense
002	EXO	030	028	and of holocaust, and all the items that pertain to their rituals.
002	EXO	030	029	And you shall sanctify everything, and they shall be the Holy of holies. He who will touch them must be sanctified.
002	EXO	030	030	You shall anoint Aaron and his sons, and you shall sanctify them, so that they may exercise the priesthood for me.
002	EXO	030	031	Likewise, you shall say to the sons of Israel: ‘This oil of unction will be holy to me throughout your generations.
002	EXO	030	032	The flesh of man shall not be anointed from it, and you shall not make any similar compound, for it has been sanctified and it shall be holy to you.
002	EXO	030	033	Whatever man will have composed such a thing and have given it to a stranger, he shall be exterminated from his people.’”
002	EXO	030	034	And the Lord said to Moses: “Take to yourself aromatics: stacte, and onycha, galbanum of sweet odor, and the clearest frankincense, all these shall be of equal weight.
002	EXO	030	035	And you shall make incense composed with the skills of a perfumer, diligently mixed, and pure, and most worthy of sanctification.
002	EXO	030	036	And when you have crushed all these into a very fine powder, you shall place some of it before the tabernacle of the testimony, in the place where I will appear to you. The Holy of holies shall this incense be to you.
002	EXO	030	037	You shall not make such a compound for your own uses, because it is holy to the Lord.
002	EXO	030	038	Whatever man will have made anything similar, so as to thoroughly enjoy its smell, he shall perish from his people.”
002	EXO	031	001	And the Lord spoke to Moses, saying:
002	EXO	031	002	“Behold, I have called by name Bezalel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, from the tribe of Judah,
002	EXO	031	003	and I have filled him with the Spirit of God, with wisdom, and understanding, and knowledge in every craft,
002	EXO	031	004	in order to design whatever must be fabricated from gold, and silver, and brass,
002	EXO	031	005	from marble, and precious stones, and various woods.
002	EXO	031	006	And I have given to him, as his associate, Oholiab the son of Ahisamach, from the tribe of Dan. And I have placed wisdom in the heart of every artisan, so that they may make everything as I have instructed you:
002	EXO	031	007	the tabernacle of the covenant, and the ark of the testimony, and the propitiatory which is over it, and all the vessels of the tabernacle,
002	EXO	031	008	and the table and its vessels, the most pure lampstand with its vessels, and the altars of incense
002	EXO	031	009	and of holocaust and all their vessels, the washtub with its base,
002	EXO	031	010	the holy vestments for the ministry of Aaron the priest, and for his sons, so that they may execute their office of sacred rites,
002	EXO	031	011	the oil of unction, and the incense of aromatics in the Sanctuary. All the things that I have instructed you, they shall make.”
002	EXO	031	012	And the Lord spoke to Moses, saying:
002	EXO	031	013	“Speak to the sons of Israel, and you shall say to them: See that you keep my Sabbath. For it is a sign between me and you among your generations, so that you may know that I am the Lord, who sanctifies you.
002	EXO	031	014	Keep my Sabbath, for it is holy to you. Whoever will have polluted it, shall die a death. Whoever will have done any work in it, his soul shall perish from the midst of his people.
002	EXO	031	015	For six days you shall do work. On the seventh day, it is the Sabbath, a rest sanctified by the Lord. All who will have done work on this day shall die.
002	EXO	031	016	Let the sons of Israel keep the Sabbath, and let them celebrate it throughout their generations. It is an everlasting covenant
002	EXO	031	017	between me and the sons of Israel, and a perpetual sign. For in six days the Lord made heaven and earth, and in the seventh he ceased from work.”
002	EXO	031	018	And the Lord, having completed speaking in this way on Mount Sinai, gave to Moses two stone tablets of testimony, written with the finger of God.
002	EXO	032	001	Then the people, seeing that Moses made a delay in descending from the mountain, gathered together against Aaron, and said: “Rise up, make us gods, who may go before us. But as for this man Moses, who led us away from the land of Egypt, we do not know what has befallen him.”
002	EXO	032	002	And Aaron said to them, “Take the golden earrings from the ears of your wives, and your sons and daughters, and bring them to me.”
002	EXO	032	003	And the people did what he had commanded, carrying the earrings to Aaron.
002	EXO	032	004	And when he had received them, he formed these by the work of a casting furnace, and he made from these a molten calf. And they said: “These are your gods, O Israel, who led you away from the land of Egypt.”
002	EXO	032	005	And when Aaron had seen it, he built an altar before it, and he cried out with a voice of proclamation, saying, “Tomorrow is the solemnity of the Lord.”
002	EXO	032	006	And rising up in the morning, they offered holocausts, and peace victims, and the people sat down to eat and to drink, and they rose up to play.
002	EXO	032	007	Then the Lord spoke to Moses, saying: “Go, descend. Your people, whom you led away from the land of Egypt, have sinned.
002	EXO	032	008	They have quickly withdrawn from the way which you revealed to them. And they have made for themselves a molten calf, and they have worshiped it. And immolating victims to it, they have said: ‘These are your gods, O Israel, who led you away from the land of Egypt.’”
002	EXO	032	009	And again, the Lord said to Moses: “I discern that this people is stiff-necked.
002	EXO	032	010	Release me, so that my fury may be enraged against them, and I may destroy them, and then I will make of you a great nation.”
002	EXO	032	011	Then Moses prayed to the Lord his God, saying: “Why, O Lord, is your fury enraged against your people, whom you led away from the land of Egypt, with great strength and with a mighty hand?
