002	EXO	038	008	He also made the washtub of brass, with its base made from the mirrors of the women who kept watch at the door of the tabernacle.
002	EXO	038	009	He also made the atrium, at the south side of which were hangings of fine twisted linen of one hundred cubits and
002	EXO	038	010	twenty columns of brass with their bases. The heads of the columns and all of the engraving work were of silver.
002	EXO	038	011	Equally, at the northern area, the hangings, the columns, and the bases and heads of the columns were of the same measure and work and metal.
002	EXO	038	012	Yet truly, on that side which looks out toward the west, there were hangings of fifty cubits, and ten columns with their bases of brass. And the heads of the columns and all of the engraving work were of silver.
002	EXO	038	013	Furthermore, toward the east, he prepared hangings of fifty cubits:
002	EXO	038	014	of which, there were fifteen cubits, among three columns with their bases, holding up one side,
002	EXO	038	015	and on the other side, (for between the two he made the entrance of the tabernacle) there were equally hangings of fifteen cubits, and three pillars, and the same number of bases.
002	EXO	038	016	All the hangings of the atrium were woven from fine twisted linen.
002	EXO	038	017	The bases of the columns were of brass, but their heads with all of their engravings were of silver. Now he also overlaid the columns of the atrium themselves with silver.
002	EXO	038	018	And he made, at its entrance, a hanging, wrought with embroidery, of hyacinth, purple, vermillion, and fine twisted linen, which held twenty cubits in length, yet truly it was five cubits in height, as with the measure of all the hangings of the atrium.
002	EXO	038	019	Now the columns at the entrance were four, with bases of brass, and their heads and engravings were of silver.
002	EXO	038	020	Likewise, the tent pegs of the tabernacle and the atrium all around he made of brass.
002	EXO	038	021	These are the instruments of the tabernacle of the testimony, which were enumerated according to the instruction of Moses, with the ceremonies of the Levites, by the hand of Ithamar, the son of Aaron the priest,
002	EXO	038	022	which Bezalel, the son of Uri, the son of Hur from the tribe of Judah, had completed, just as the Lord decreed through Moses.
002	EXO	038	023	He was joined by his associate, Oholiab, the son of Ahisamach, from the tribe of Dan, who himself was also an exceptional artisan of wood, and of weaving, as well as of embroidery, with hyacinth, purple, vermillion, and fine linen.
002	EXO	038	024	All of the gold that was expended in the work of the Sanctuary, and that was offered in donation, was twenty-nine talents and seven hundred thirty shekels, according to the measure of the Sanctuary.
002	EXO	038	025	Now it was offered by those who were past the numbering of twenty years and above: from six hundred and three thousand, five hundred and fifty men able to bear arms.
002	EXO	038	026	There were, beyond that, one hundred talents of silver, from which were cast the bases for the Sanctuary and for the entrance where the veil hangs.
002	EXO	038	027	One hundred bases were made from one hundred talents, a single talent being counted for each base.
002	EXO	038	028	But from one thousand seven hundred and seventy-five, he made the heads of the columns, which he also clothed with silver.
002	EXO	038	029	Likewise, of brass, there was offered seventy-two thousand talents, and four hundred more shekels,
002	EXO	038	030	from which were cast the bases at the entrance of the tabernacle of the testimony, and the altar of brass with its grating, and the vessels which pertain to its use,
002	EXO	038	031	and the bases of the atrium, as much at the circumference as at its entrance, and the tent pegs of the tabernacle and of the atrium all round.
002	EXO	039	001	Truly, from hyacinth and purple, vermillion and fine linen, he made the vestments with which Aaron was clothed when he ministered in the holy places, just as the Lord instructed Moses.
002	EXO	039	002	And so he made an ephod of gold, hyacinth, and purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine twisted linen,
002	EXO	039	003	wrought with embroidery. And he cut thin strips of gold and drew them into threads, so that they could be twisted into the weave of the first colors.
002	EXO	039	004	And he made two edges, coupled to one another at the top of both sides,
002	EXO	039	005	and a wide belt from the same colors, just as the Lord had instructed Moses.
002	EXO	039	006	He also prepared two onyx stones, set and enclosed in gold, and engraved with the skill of a jeweler, with the names of the sons of Israel.
002	EXO	039	007	And he set them in the sides of the ephod, as a memorial to the sons of Israel, just as the Lord had instructed Moses.
002	EXO	039	008	He also made a breastplate, wrought with embroidery, according to the work of the ephod, from gold, hyacinth, purple, and twice-dyed scarlet, and fine twisted linen:
002	EXO	039	009	with four equal sides, doubled, of the measure of the palm of a hand.
002	EXO	039	010	And he set four rows of gems in it. In the first row was a sardius stone, a topaz, an emerald;
002	EXO	039	011	in the second was a garnet, a sapphire, and a jasper;
002	EXO	039	012	in the third was a zircon, an agate, and an amethyst;
002	EXO	039	013	in the fourth was a chrysolite, an onyx, and a beryl, surrounded and enclosed in gold by their rows.
002	EXO	039	014	And these twelve stones were engraved with the names of the twelve tribes of Israel, each one with a single name.
002	EXO	039	015	They also made, in the breastplate, little chains linked to one another, from the purest gold,
002	EXO	039	016	and two hooks, and the same number of gold rings. Moreover, they set the rings at both sides of the breastplate,
002	EXO	039	017	from which two golden chains would hang, which they connected with the hooks that projected from the corners of the ephod.
002	EXO	039	018	These were both in front and in back so that they met one another, and so that the ephod and the breastplate were woven together,
002	EXO	039	019	being fastened to the wide belt and strongly coupled with rings, to which a hyacinth band was joined, lest they should shake loose and be moved away from one another, just as the Lord instructed Moses.
002	EXO	039	020	They also made the tunic of the ephod entirely from hyacinth,
002	EXO	039	021	with the head in the upper part at the middle, and a woven edge all around the head.
002	EXO	039	022	Then, at the feet below, they also made pomegranates from hyacinth, purple, vermillion, and fine twisted linen,
002	EXO	039	023	and little bells from the purest gold, which they set between the pomegranates at the very bottom of the tunic all around.
002	EXO	039	024	So then, the high priest approached, adorned with gold bell and pomegranate, when he performed his ministry, just as the Lord had instructed Moses.
002	EXO	039	025	They also made fine linen tunics with woven work, for Aaron and his sons,
002	EXO	039	026	and headdresses with their little crowns of fine linen,
002	EXO	039	027	and also linen undergarments of fine linen.
002	EXO	039	028	Truly, they also made a wide band of fine twisted linen, hyacinth, purple, as well as vermillion, twice-dyed, with skillful embroidery, just as the Lord had instructed Moses.
002	EXO	039	029	They also made the plate of sacred veneration from the purest gold, and they wrote on it, with the skill of a jeweler: “Holy to the Lord.”
002	EXO	039	030	And they fastened it to the headdress with a hyacinth band, just as the Lord had instructed Moses.
002	EXO	039	031	And so all the work of the tabernacle and of the covering of the testimony was completed. And the sons of Israel did all that the Lord had instructed Moses.
002	EXO	039	032	And they offered the tabernacle, and the covering, and all of the articles: the rings, the panels, the bars, the columns and bases,
002	EXO	039	033	the cover of the skins of rams, dyed red, and the other cover of violet skins,
002	EXO	039	034	the veil, the ark, the bars, the propitiatory,
002	EXO	039	035	the table, with its vessels and the bread of the presence,
002	EXO	039	036	the lampstand, the lamps, and their utensils with the oil,
002	EXO	039	037	the altar of gold, and the ointment, and the incense of aromatics,
002	EXO	039	038	and the tent at the entrance of the tabernacle,
002	EXO	039	039	the altar of brass, the grating, the bars, and all of its vessels, the washtub with its base, the hangings of the atrium, and the columns with their bases,
002	EXO	039	040	the hanging at the entrance of the atrium, and their little cords and pegs. Nothing was lacking of the articles that were commanded to be made for the ministry of the tabernacle and for the covering of the covenant.
002	EXO	039	041	Likewise, the vestments, which the priests, namely, Aaron and his sons, make use of use in the Sanctuary,
002	EXO	039	042	the sons of Israel offered, just as the Lord had instructed.
002	EXO	039	043	After this, when Moses saw that everything was completed, he blessed them.
002	EXO	040	001	And the Lord spoke to Moses, saying:
002	EXO	040	002	“In the first month, on the first day of the month, you shall raise the tabernacle of the testimony,
002	EXO	040	003	and you shall place the ark in it, and you shall release the veil before it.
002	EXO	040	004	And having brought in the table, you shall place the things which were solemnly commanded upon it. The lampstand shall stand with its lamps,
002	EXO	040	005	and the altar of gold, in which the incense is burned, shall stand before the ark of the testimony. You shall place the tent at the entrance of the tabernacle,
002	EXO	040	006	and before it, the altar of holocaust.
002	EXO	040	007	The washtub shall stand between the altar and the tabernacle, and you shall fill it with water.
002	EXO	040	008	And you shall encompass the atrium and its entrance with hangings.
002	EXO	040	009	And, having taken up the oil of unction, you shall anoint the tabernacle along with its articles, so that they may be sanctified.
002	EXO	040	010	The altar of holocaust and all its vessels,
002	EXO	040	011	the washtub with its base, and all things, you shall consecrate with the oil of unction, so that they may be the Holy of holies.
002	EXO	040	012	And you shall bring forward Aaron and his sons to the entrance of the tabernacle of the testimony, and, having washed them with water,
002	EXO	040	015	you shall clothe them in the holy vestments, so that they may minister to me, and so that their unction may accomplish an everlasting priesthood.”
002	EXO	040	016	And Moses did all that the Lord had instructed.
002	EXO	040	017	Therefore, in the first month of the second year, on the first day of the month, the tabernacle was put in place.
002	EXO	040	018	And Moses raised it up, and he positioned the panels as well as the bases and the bars, and he set up the columns,
002	EXO	040	019	and he stretched out the roof over the tabernacle, imposing a cover above it, just as the Lord had decreed.
002	EXO	040	020	And he placed the testimony in the ark, applying the bars beneath, and the oracle above.
002	EXO	040	021	And when he had brought the ark into the tabernacle, he drew the veil before it, in order to fulfill the commandment of the Lord.
002	EXO	040	022	And he placed the table in the tabernacle of the testimony, at the north side, beyond the veil,
002	EXO	040	023	arranging before it the bread of the presence, just as the Lord had instructed Moses.
002	EXO	040	024	And he placed the lampstand in the tabernacle of the testimony, away from the table, on the south side,
002	EXO	040	025	setting the lamps in order, according to the precept of the Lord.
002	EXO	040	026	He also positioned the altar of gold under the roof of the testimony, opposite the veil,
002	EXO	040	027	and he heaped upon it the incense of aromatics, just as the Lord had commanded Moses.
002	EXO	040	028	And he positioned the tent at the entrance of the tabernacle of the testimony,
002	EXO	040	029	and the altar of holocaust in the vestibule of the testimony, offering the holocaust and the sacrifices upon it, just as the Lord had decreed.
002	EXO	040	030	Likewise, he stationed the washtub between the tabernacle of the testimony and the altar, filling it with water.
002	EXO	040	031	And Moses and Aaron, along with his sons, washed their hands and feet,
002	EXO	040	032	whenever they would enter the covering of the covenant, and when they approached to the altar, just as the Lord had instructed Moses.
002	EXO	040	033	And he raised up the atrium around the tabernacle and the altar, drawing the hanging at its entrance. After all these things were perfected,
002	EXO	040	034	the cloud covered the tabernacle of the testimony, and the glory of the Lord filled it.
002	EXO	040	035	Neither could Moses enter the covering of the covenant: the cloud was covering all things, and the majesty of the Lord was flashing. For the cloud had covered everything.
002	EXO	040	036	Whenever the cloud departed from the tabernacle, the sons of Israel set out by their companies.
002	EXO	040	037	But if it remained hanging over it, they remained in the same place.
002	EXO	040	038	Certainly, the cloud of the Lord lay over the tabernacle by day, and the fire by night, being seen by all the people of Israel throughout all their resting places.
