003	LEV	011	034	Any of the foods that you eat, if water from such a vessel will have been poured upon it, it shall be unclean. And every liquid which one may drink from such a vessel shall be unclean.
003	LEV	011	035	And if anything from among these kinds of dead things has fallen upon it, it shall be unclean, whether it be an oven, or a pot with feet, these shall be unclean and shall be destroyed.
003	LEV	011	036	Yet truly, fountains and cisterns, and all reservoirs of water shall be clean. Whoever will have touched their carcasses shall be defiled.
003	LEV	011	037	If it falls upon seed grain, it shall not defile it.
003	LEV	011	038	But if anyone has poured water upon the seed grain, and afterwards it was touched by the carcasses, it shall be immediately defiled.
003	LEV	011	039	If any animals will have died, from which it is lawful for you to eat, whoever will have touched its carcass shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	011	040	And whoever will have eaten or carried anything of these shall wash his clothes, and he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	011	041	All that creeps across the earth shall be abominable, neither shall it be taken up as food.
003	LEV	011	042	Whatever advances by four feet upon the chest, or that has many feet, or that drags across the soil, you shall not eat, because it is abominable.
003	LEV	011	043	Do not be willing to contaminate your souls, nor shall you touch any of these, lest you become unclean.
003	LEV	011	044	For I am the Lord your God. Be holy, for I am Holy. Do not pollute your souls with any creeping thing, which moves across the land.
003	LEV	011	045	For I am the Lord, who led you away from the land of Egypt, so that I would be your God; you shall be holy, for I am Holy.
003	LEV	011	046	This is the law of animals and flying things, and of every living soul that moves in the waters or creeps upon the land,
003	LEV	011	047	so that you may know the difference between clean and unclean, and so that you may know what you ought to eat, and what you ought to refuse.
003	LEV	012	001	And the Lord spoke to Moses, saying:
003	LEV	012	002	Speak to the sons of Israel, and you shall say to them: A woman, if she has received the seed to bear a male, shall be unclean for seven days, just as in the days of separation due to menstruation.
003	LEV	012	003	And on the eighth day, the little infant shall be circumcised.
003	LEV	012	004	Yet truly, she herself shall remain for thirty-three days in the blood of her purification. She shall not touch anything holy, nor shall she enter into the Sanctuary, until the days of her purification are completed.
003	LEV	012	005	But if she will bear a female, she shall be unclean for two weeks, according to the custom of her monthly flow, and she shall remain in the blood of her purification for sixty-six days.
003	LEV	012	006	And when the days of her purification have been completed, for a son or for a daughter, she shall bring to the door of the tabernacle of the testimony, a one-year-old lamb as a holocaust, and a young pigeon or a turtledove for sin, and she shall deliver them to the priest.
003	LEV	012	007	He shall offer them in the sight of the Lord, and he shall pray for her. And so she shall be cleansed from the issue of her blood. This is the law for one who bears a male or a female.
003	LEV	012	008	And if her hand has not obtained or been able to offer a lamb, she shall take two turtledoves or two young pigeons: one as a holocaust, and the other for sin. And the priest shall pray for her, and so she shall be cleansed.
003	LEV	013	001	And the Lord spoke to Moses and Aaron, saying:
003	LEV	013	002	The man in whose skin or flesh there will have arisen a diverse color, or a pustule, or something that seems to shine, which is the mark of leprosy, shall be brought to Aaron the priest, or to anyone you wish among his sons.
003	LEV	013	003	And if he sees that leprosy is in his skin, and that the hair has turned a white color, and that the place where the leprosy appears is lower than the rest of the skin and the flesh, then it is the mark of leprosy, and at his judgment he shall be separated.
003	LEV	013	004	But if there will be a shining whiteness in the skin, but it is not lower than the rest of the flesh, and the hair is of unaffected color, the priest shall seclude him for seven days.
003	LEV	013	005	And on the seventh day he shall examine him, and if the leprosy certainly has not increased further, and has not spread itself in the skin, he shall seclude him again, for another seven days.
003	LEV	013	006	And on the seventh day, he shall evaluate him. If the leprosy has become obscured, and has not increased in the skin, he shall declare him clean, because it is a scab. And the man shall wash his clothes, and he shall be clean.
003	LEV	013	007	But if the leprosy increases again, after he was seen by the priest and restored to cleanness, he shall be brought to him,
003	LEV	013	008	and he shall be condemned of uncleanness.
003	LEV	013	009	If the mark of leprosy has been in a man, he shall be brought to the priest,
003	LEV	013	010	and he shall look upon him. And when there is a white color in the skin, and it has an altered appearance in its hair, and also the same flesh seems alive,
003	LEV	013	011	it shall be judged a chronic leprosy, which has grown into the skin. And so the priest shall declare him contaminated, and he shall not seclude him, because he is clearly unclean.
003	LEV	013	012	But if the leprosy will have flourished, coursing through the skin, and will have covered all the skin from the head even to the feet, whatever falls under the sight of the eyes,
003	LEV	013	013	the priest shall examine him, and he shall judge that the leprosy that he possesses is very clean, because it has all turned to whiteness, and for this reason the man shall be clean.
003	LEV	013	014	Yet truly, when the living flesh shall appear in him,
003	LEV	013	015	then by the judgment of the priest he shall be polluted, and he shall be considered to be among the unclean. For the live flesh, if it is spotted with leprosy, is unclean.
003	LEV	013	016	And if again it will have turned into whiteness, and will have covered the entire man,
003	LEV	013	017	the priest shall examine him, and he shall discern him to be clean.
003	LEV	013	018	But when there has been an ulcer in the flesh and the skin, and it has healed,
003	LEV	013	019	and in the place of the ulcer, there appears a white or reddish scar, the man shall be brought to the priest.
003	LEV	013	020	And when he will have seen the place of the leprosy lower than the rest of the flesh, and that the hair has turned white, he shall declare him contaminated. For the plague of leprosy has arisen from the ulcer.
003	LEV	013	021	But if the hair is of the usual color, and the scar is somewhat obscure and is not lower than the nearby flesh, he shall seclude him for seven days.
003	LEV	013	022	And if it will have certainly increased, he shall judge him to have leprosy.
003	LEV	013	023	But if it stays in its place, it is the scar of an ulcer, and the man shall be clean.
003	LEV	013	024	But if flesh and skin has been burned by fire, and, having been healed, now has a white or red scar,
003	LEV	013	025	the priest shall examine it, and if he sees that it has turned white, and that its place is lower than the rest of the skin, he shall declare him contaminated, for the mark of leprosy has arisen in the scar.
003	LEV	013	026	But if the color of the hair has not been changed, nor is the mark lower than the rest of the flesh, and the leprosy itself appears to be somewhat obscure, he shall seclude him for seven days,
003	LEV	013	027	and on the seventh day he shall evaluate him. If the leprosy will have increased further in the skin, he shall declare him contaminated.
003	LEV	013	028	But if the whiteness stays in its place and is not very clear, it is the mark of a burn, and for this reason he shall be declared clean, because it is only the scar from a burn.
003	LEV	013	029	If leprosy will have sprung up in the head or the beard of a man or woman, the priest shall look upon them,
003	LEV	013	030	and if the place is certainly lower than the rest of the flesh, and the hair is golden, and thinner than usual, he shall declare them contaminated, because it is the leprosy of the head and the beard.
003	LEV	013	031	But if he sees that the place of the spot is equal with the nearby flesh, and that the hair is black, he shall seclude him for seven days,
003	LEV	013	032	and on the seventh day he shall examine it. If the spot has not increased, and the hair has kept its color, and the place of the mark is equal with the rest of the flesh,
003	LEV	013	033	the man shall be shaven, except in the place of the spot, and he shall be secluded for another seven days.
003	LEV	013	034	On the seventh day, if the mark seems to have stayed in its place, and it is not lower than the rest of the flesh, he shall declare him clean, and, his clothes having been washed, he shall be clean.
003	LEV	013	035	But if, after his cleansing, the spot will have increased again in the skin,
003	LEV	013	036	he shall no longer inquire as to whether the hair has turned yellow, because he is plainly unclean.
003	LEV	013	037	Furthermore, if the spot has not increased, and the hair is black, let him know that the man is healed: and let him confidently pronounce him clean.
003	LEV	013	038	If a whiteness will have appeared in the skin of a man or a woman,
003	LEV	013	039	the priest shall examine them. If he detects an obscured whiteness shining in the skin, may he know that it is not leprosy, but a white-colored blemish, and that the man is clean.
003	LEV	013	040	The man whose hair falls off of his head is bald and clean.
003	LEV	013	041	And if the hair falls off of his forehead, he is bald in front and clean.
003	LEV	013	042	But if in the bald head or bald forehead there has arisen a white or reddish color,
003	LEV	013	043	and the priest will have seen this, he shall condemn him without doubt of leprosy, which has arisen in the baldness.
003	LEV	013	044	Therefore, whoever will have been spotted by leprosy, and who has been separated at the judgment of the priest,
003	LEV	013	045	shall have his clothes unstitched, his head bare, his mouth covered with a cloth, and he himself shall cry out that he is contaminated and filthy.
003	LEV	013	046	The entire time that he is a leper and unclean he shall live alone outside the camp.
003	LEV	013	047	A woolen or linen garment that will have held the leprosy,
003	LEV	013	048	in the main fibers or in any of the threads, or certainly in a skin, or whatever has been made from a skin,
003	LEV	013	049	if it has been infected with a white or red spot, it shall be considered to be leprosy, and it shall be shown to the priest.
003	LEV	013	050	And he, having examined it, shall close it up for seven days.
003	LEV	013	051	And on the seventh day, having looked at it again, if he detects an increase, it is a persistent leprosy; he shall judge the garment to be polluted, along with everything with which it has been found.
003	LEV	013	052	And because of this, it shall be burned in flames.
003	LEV	013	053	But if he will have seen that it has not increased,
003	LEV	013	054	he shall instruct them, and they shall wash whatever has the leprosy in it, and he shall close it up for another seven days.
003	LEV	013	055	And when he will have seen that the former appearance has not returned, even if the leprosy has not increased, he shall judge it to be unclean, and he shall burn it with fire, for the leprosy has been infused in the exterior of the garment, or throughout the whole.
003	LEV	013	056	But if the place of the leprosy has become somewhat darker, after the garment has been washed, he shall tear it away, and separate it from the part that is sound.
003	LEV	013	057	But if, after this, there will appear in those places which before were immaculate, a flying and wandering leprosy, it must be burned with fire.
003	LEV	013	058	If it will have ceased, he shall wash with water the parts which are pure for a second time, and they shall be clean.
003	LEV	013	059	This is the law about leprosy for any woolen or linen garment, in the weave and in the threads, and for all items made from skins, how it must be declared either clean or contaminated.
003	LEV	014	001	And the Lord spoke to Moses, saying:
003	LEV	014	002	This is the rite for a leper, when he is to be cleansed. He shall be brought to the priest,
003	LEV	014	003	who, departing from the camp, when he has found the leprosy to be cleansed,
003	LEV	014	004	shall instruct him who is to be purified to offer for himself two living sparrows, which it is lawful to eat, and cedar wood, and vermillion, and hyssop.
003	LEV	014	005	And he shall order that one of the sparrows be immolated in an earthen vessel over living waters.
003	LEV	014	006	But the other living one, with the cedar wood, and the scarlet, and the hyssop, he shall dip in the blood of the immolated sparrow.
003	LEV	014	007	And he shall sprinkle him who is to be cleansed seven times, so that he may be purified justly. And he shall release the living sparrow, so that it may fly away into the field.
003	LEV	014	008	And when the man will have washed his clothes, he shall shave all the hair from his body, and he shall be washed with water. And having been purified, he shall enter into the camp, only to this extent: that he may remain outside his own tent for seven days.
