003	LEV	014	019	And he shall pray for him in the sight of the Lord, and he shall accomplish the sacrifice on behalf of sin. Then he shall immolate the holocaust,
003	LEV	014	020	and place it upon the altar with its libations, and the man will be duly cleansed.
003	LEV	014	021	But if he is poor, and his hand is not able to find what has been said, he shall take a lamb as an offering for transgression, so that the priest may pray for him, and a tenth part of fine wheat flour sprinkled with oil, as a sacrifice, and a twelfth hin of oil,
003	LEV	014	022	and two turtledoves or two young pigeons, of which one may be for sin, and the other as a holocaust.
003	LEV	014	023	And he shall offer them on the eighth day of his purification to the priest at the door of the tabernacle of the testimony in the sight of the Lord.
