003	LEV	014	042	and that other stones be put back, in place of those which had been taken away, and that the house be plastered with other mortar.
003	LEV	014	043	But if, after the stones have been dug out, and the dust wiped away, and it is plastered with other clay,
003	LEV	014	044	the priest, upon entering, will have seen that the leprosy has returned, and that the walls are sprinkled with spots, then it is a persistent leprosy and the house is unclean.
003	LEV	014	045	And so they shall promptly destroy it, and shall cast its stones and timber, and also all the dust, outside the town in an unclean place.
