003	LEV	015	001	And the Lord spoke to Moses and Aaron, saying:
003	LEV	015	002	Speak to the sons of Israel, and say to them: The man who undergoes a flow of seed shall be unclean.
003	LEV	015	003	And then he shall be judged subject to this fault, if a filthy fluid, at each moment, adheres to his flesh and gathers there.
003	LEV	015	004	Every bed on which he sleeps shall be unclean, and every place where he sits.
003	LEV	015	005	If any man has touched his couch, he shall wash his clothes, and having washed with water, he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	006	If he will have sat where that man has sat, he shall also wash his clothes, and having washed with water, he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	007	Whoever has touched his flesh shall wash his clothes, and having washed with water, he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	008	If such a man has cast his spittle upon him who is clean, he shall wash his clothes, and having washed with water, he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	009	The saddle on which he has sat shall be unclean.
003	LEV	015	010	And whatever has been under him who has undergone a flow of seed shall be polluted until evening. Whoever carries any of these things shall wash his clothes, and having washed with water, he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	011	All whom such a one has touched, not having washed his hands before, shall wash his clothes, and having washed with water, he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	012	If he has touched an earthen vessel, it shall be broken. But if it is a wooden vessel, it shall be washed with water.
003	LEV	015	013	If he who suffers from this affliction will have been healed, he shall number seven days after his cleansing, and having washed his clothes and his entire body in living water, he shall be clean.
003	LEV	015	014	Then, on the eighth day, he shall take two turtledoves or two young pigeons, and he shall advance, in the sight of the Lord, toward the door of the tabernacle of the testimony, and he shall give these to the priest,
003	LEV	015	015	who shall offer one for sin, and the other as a holocaust. And he shall pray for him before the Lord, so that he may be cleansed from the flow of his seed.
003	LEV	015	016	A man from whom the seed of sexual intercourse goes out shall wash his entire body with water, and he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	017	The garment or skin which he will have, he shall wash with water, and it shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	018	The woman with whom he has had sexual intercourse shall be washed with water, and she shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	019	The woman who, at the return of the month, undergoes the flow of blood shall be separated for seven days.
003	LEV	015	020	All who will touch her shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	021	And everything on which she sleeps or sits, in the days of her separation, shall be polluted.
003	LEV	015	022	Whoever will have touched her bed shall wash his clothes, and having washed himself with water, he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	023	Anyone who will have touched any item on which she has sat shall wash his clothes, and having washed himself with water, he shall be polluted until evening.
003	LEV	015	024	If a man has sexual intercourse with her in the time of her monthly flow of blood, he shall be unclean for seven days, and every bed on which he sleeps shall be polluted.
003	LEV	015	025	The woman who undergoes a flow of blood many days beyond her time of menstruation, or whose blood does not cease to flow after the menstrual blood, as long as she is subject to this affliction, she shall be unclean, just as if she were in her time of menstruation.
003	LEV	015	026	Every bed on which she sleeps, and every item on which she sits, shall be polluted.
003	LEV	015	027	Whoever will have touched these shall wash his clothes, and having washed himself with water, he shall be unclean until evening.
003	LEV	015	028	If the blood has stopped and has ceased to flow, she shall number seven days for her purification,
003	LEV	015	029	and on the eighth day she shall offer for herself, to the priest, two turtledoves or two young pigeons, at the door of the tabernacle of the testimony.
003	LEV	015	030	And he shall offer one for sin, and the other as a holocaust, and he shall pray for her before the Lord, and for the flow of her uncleanness.
003	LEV	015	031	Therefore, you shall teach the sons of Israel to be cautious of uncleanness, so that they may not die in their filth, when they will have polluted my tabernacle, which is among them.
003	LEV	015	032	This is the law of him who undergoes a flow of seed, or who is polluted by sexual intercourse,
003	LEV	015	033	and of her who is separated in the time of menstruation, or who has a continual flow of blood, and of the man who sleeps with her.
003	LEV	016	001	And the Lord spoke to Moses, after the death of the two sons of Aaron, when they were destroyed for offering strange fire.
003	LEV	016	002	And he instructed him, saying: Speak to your brother Aaron, so that he may not, at any time, enter into the Sanctuary, which is within the veil, before the propitiatory by which the ark is covered, so that he may not die, (for I will appear in a cloud above the oracle)
003	LEV	016	003	unless he will have done these things beforehand. He shall offer a calf for sin, and a ram as a holocaust.
003	LEV	016	004	He shall be vested with a linen tunic. He shall conceal his nakedness with linen undergarments. He shall be wrapped with a linen belt, and he shall impose a linen headdress on his head. For these are holy vestments. All of these he shall put on, after he has been washed.
003	LEV	016	005	And he shall receive, from the entire multitude of the sons of Israel, two he-goats for sin, and one ram as a holocaust.
