004	NUM	028	007	And you shall offer a libation of wine, of the fourth part of a hin for each lamb, in the Sanctuary of the Lord.
004	NUM	028	008	And you shall offer the other lamb similarly, in the evening, according to all the rites of the morning sacrifice and its libations, as an oblation of most sweet odor to the Lord.
004	NUM	028	009	Then, on the Sabbath day, you shall offer two immaculate one-year-old lambs, and two tenths of fine wheat flour sprinkled with oil, as sacrifice, as well as the libations
004	NUM	028	010	that are usually poured out on each Sabbath as a perpetual holocaust.
004	NUM	028	011	Then, on the first day of the month, you shall offer a holocaust to the Lord: two calves from the herd, one ram, seven immaculate one-year-old lambs,
004	NUM	028	012	and three tenths of fine wheat flour sprinkled with oil, as sacrifice, for each calf, and two tenths of fine wheat flour sprinkled with oil, for each ram,
004	NUM	028	013	and one tenth of fine wheat flour with oil, as a sacrifice, for each lamb. It is a holocaust of most sweet odor and also an incense to the Lord.
004	NUM	028	014	Now these shall be the libations of wine, which are to be poured out for each victim: one half portion of a hin for each calf, one third for a ram, and one fourth for a lamb. This shall be the holocaust for all the months, as they succeed one another in the turning of the year.
004	NUM	028	015	Likewise, a he-goat shall be offered to the Lord for sin, with the perpetual holocaust and its libations.
004	NUM	028	016	Then, in the first month, the fourteenth day of the month shall be the Passover of the Lord.
004	NUM	028	017	And the fifteenth day shall be a solemnity. For seven days, they shall eat unleavened bread.
