004	NUM	032	001	Now the sons of Ruben and of Gad had many herds, and their substance in cattle was inestimable. And when they had seen that the lands of Jazer and Gilead were suitable for feeding animals,
004	NUM	032	002	they went to Moses, and to Eleazar the priest and the leaders of the multitude, and they said:
004	NUM	032	003	“Ataroth, and Dibon, and Jazer, and Nimrah, Heshbon, and Elealeh, and Sebam, and Nebo, and Beon,
004	NUM	032	004	the land, which the Lord has struck in the sight of the sons of Israel, is a very fertile region for pasturing animals. And we, your servants, have very many cattle.
004	NUM	032	005	And so we beseech you, if we have found favor before you, that you give it to us, your subjects, as a possession, and that you not cause us cross the Jordan.”
004	NUM	032	006	And Moses answered them: “Should your brothers go to battle, while you sit here?
004	NUM	032	007	Why do you subvert the minds of the sons of Israel, so that they might not dare to cross into the place which the Lord will give to them?
004	NUM	032	008	Did not your fathers act in the same way, when I sent them from Kadesh-Barnea to explore the land?
004	NUM	032	009	And when they had gone all the way to the Valley of the Cluster of Grapes, having viewed the entire region, they subverted the hearts of the sons of Israel, so that they would not enter into the parts that the Lord gave to them.
004	NUM	032	010	And being angry, the Lord swore an oath, saying:
004	NUM	032	011	‘These men, who ascended out of Egypt, from twenty years and above, will not see the land, which I have promised under an oath to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. For they were not willing to follow me,
004	NUM	032	012	except Caleb, the son of Jephunneh the Kenizzite, and Joshua the son of Nun; these have fulfilled my will.’
004	NUM	032	013	And the Lord, being angry against Israel, led them in a course through the desert for forty years, until the entire generation, which had done evil in his sight, was consumed.
004	NUM	032	014	And behold,” he said, “you have risen up in the place of your fathers, the offshoots and the nurslings of sinful men, in order to augment the fury of the Lord against Israel.
004	NUM	032	015	But if you are not willing to follow him, he will leave the people behind in the wilderness, and you will have been the cause of all our deaths.”
004	NUM	032	016	But approaching closer, they said: “We will manufacture sheep pens and cattle stalls, as well as fortified cities, for our little ones.
004	NUM	032	017	But we ourselves will continue on, armed and girded for battle, before the sons of Israel, until we lead them to their places. Our little ones, and whatever we may be able to have, shall be in walled cities, because of the treachery of the inhabitants.
004	NUM	032	018	We will not return to our houses, even until the sons of Israel may possess their inheritance.
004	NUM	032	019	Neither will we seek anything across the Jordan, because we already have our possession on its eastern side.”
004	NUM	032	020	And Moses said to them: “If you accomplish what you have promised, you may go out, equipped for battle, before the Lord.
004	NUM	032	021	And let every fighting man cross over the Jordan, until the Lord overthrows his enemies,
004	NUM	032	022	and all the land is subjected to him. Then you will be guiltless with the Lord and with Israel, and you will obtain the regions which you desire before the Lord.
004	NUM	032	023	But if you do not do what you have said, no one could doubt that you will have sinned against God. And know this: your sin shall overtake you.
004	NUM	032	024	Therefore, build cities for your little ones, and pens and stables for your sheep and cattle; and fulfill what you have promised.”
004	NUM	032	025	And the sons of Gad and of Ruben said to Moses: “We are your servants, we shall do what you, our ruler, orders.
004	NUM	032	026	We will leave behind our little ones, and our wives, and the sheep and cattle, in the cities of Gilead.
004	NUM	032	027	And we, your servants, all well-equipped, will go forth to battle, just as you, our ruler, has spoken.”
004	NUM	032	028	Therefore, Moses instructed Eleazar the priest, and Joshua the son of Nun, and the princes of the families throughout the tribes of Israel, and he said to them:
004	NUM	032	029	“If the sons of Gad and the sons of Ruben cross over the Jordan with you, all armed for war before the Lord, and if the land becomes subject to you, give them Gilead as a possession.
004	NUM	032	030	But if they are not willing to cross with you, armed, into the land of Canaan, then let them receive places among you for their dwellings.”
