# BOOK	005	DEU	Deuteronomy	Deuteronomy
005	DEU	001	001	These are the words which Moses spoke to all of Israel, across the Jordan, in the plain of the wilderness opposite the Red Sea, between Paran and Tophel and Laban and Hazeroth, where gold is very plentiful,
005	DEU	001	002	eleven days from Horeb, by way of Mount Seir as far as Kadesh-barnea.
005	DEU	001	003	In the fortieth year, on the eleventh month, on the first day of the month, Moses told the sons of Israel all that the Lord had instructed him. And so he spoke to them,
005	DEU	001	004	after he had struck down Sihon, the king of the Amorites, who lived at Heshbon, and Og, the king of Bashan, who resided at Ashtaroth and at Edrei,
005	DEU	001	005	across the Jordan in the land of Moab. And so, Moses began to explain the law, and to say:
005	DEU	001	006	“The Lord our God spoke to us at Horeb, saying: ‘You have remained long enough on this mountain.
005	DEU	001	007	Turn back and go to the mountain of the Amorites, and to the other places which are near it: the plains as well as the mountainous regions, and the low-lying places opposite the south and along the shore of the sea, the land of the Canaanites, and Lebanon, as far as the great river Euphrates.’
005	DEU	001	008	‘Lo,’ he said, ‘I have delivered it to you. Enter and possess that which the Lord swore to your fathers, Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, that he would give it to them, and to their offspring after them.’
005	DEU	001	009	And I said to you, at that time:
005	DEU	001	010	‘I alone am not able to sustain you. For the Lord, your God, has multiplied you, and you are today like the stars of heaven, very many.
005	DEU	001	011	May the Lord, the God of your fathers, add to this number many thousands more, and may he bless you, just as he has said.
005	DEU	001	012	Alone, I do not have the strength to endure your arbitrations and judgments and disputes.
005	DEU	001	013	Offer, from among you, wise and experienced men, those whose conversation has been proven within your tribes, so that I may appoint them as your rulers.’
005	DEU	001	014	Then you responded to me: ‘What you intend to do is a good thing.’
005	DEU	001	015	And so, I took from your tribes men, wise and noble, and I appointed them as rulers, as tribunes and centurions, and as leaders over fifty and over ten, who would teach you each thing.
005	DEU	001	016	And I instructed them, saying: ‘Listen to them, and judge what is just, whether he is one of your citizens or a sojourner.
005	DEU	001	017	There shall be no favoritism to any persons. So you shall listen to the little as well as to the great. And you shall not accept anyone’s reputation, for this is the judgment of God. But if anything seems difficult to you, then refer it to me, and I will hear it.’
005	DEU	001	018	And I instructed you in all that you were obliged to do.
005	DEU	001	019	Then, setting out from Horeb, we crossed through a terrible and great wasteland, which you saw along the way of the mountain of the Amorite, just as the Lord our God had instructed us. And when we had arrived at Kadesh-barnea,
005	DEU	001	020	I said to you: ‘You have arrived at the mountain of the Amorite, which the Lord our God will give to us.
005	DEU	001	021	Gaze upon the land that the Lord your God gives to you. Ascend and possess it, just as the Lord our God has spoken to your fathers. Do not be afraid, and do not become terrified by anything.’
005	DEU	001	022	And you all approached me and said: ‘Let us send men who may consider the land, and who may report as to the way by which we ought to ascend, and as to which cities we ought to travel.’
005	DEU	001	023	And since the word was pleasing to me, I sent from among you twelve men, one from each tribe.
005	DEU	001	024	These, when they had set out and had ascended the mountains, arrived as far as the valley of the cluster of grapes. And having considered the land,
005	DEU	001	025	having taken from its fruits in order to show its fertility, they brought these to us, and they said: ‘The land that the Lord our God will give to us is good.’
005	DEU	001	026	Yet you were not willing to go there. Instead, being incredulous to the word of the Lord our God,
005	DEU	001	027	you murmured in your tents, and you said: ‘The Lord hates us, and therefore he has led us away from the land of Egypt, so that he might deliver us into the hand of the Amorite and destroy us.
005	DEU	001	028	To where should we ascend? The messengers have terrified our heart by saying: “The multitude is very great, and taller than us. And the cities are great, and the walls extend even to the sky. We have seen the sons of the Anakim there.”’
005	DEU	001	029	And I said to you: ‘Do not be apprehensive, nor should you fear them.
