005	DEU	014	001	“Be sons of the Lord your God. You shall not cut yourselves, nor make yourselves bald, because of the dead.
005	DEU	014	002	For you are a holy people, for the Lord your God. And he chose you, so that you may be a people particularly his, out of all the nations on earth.
005	DEU	014	003	You shall not eat the things that are unclean.
005	DEU	014	004	These are the animals which you ought to eat: the ox, and the sheep, and the goat,
005	DEU	014	005	the stag and the roe deer, the gazelle, the wild goat, the addax, the antelope, the giraffe.
005	DEU	014	006	Every beast which has a hoof divided into two parts and which also chews the cud, you shall eat.
005	DEU	014	007	But those which chew over again, but do not have a divided hoof, you must not eat, such as the camel, the hare, and the hyrax. Since these chew the cud, but do not have a divided the hoof, they shall be unclean to you.
005	DEU	014	008	The pig also, since it has a divided hoof, but does not chew over again, shall be unclean. Their flesh shall not be eaten, and you shall not touch their carcasses.
