010	2SA	007	014	I will be a father to him, and he shall be a son to me. And if he will commit any iniquity, I will correct him with the rod of men and with the wounds of the sons of men.
010	2SA	007	015	But my mercy I will not take away from him, as I took it away from Saul, whom I removed from before my face.
010	2SA	007	016	And your house shall be faithful, and your kingdom shall be before your face, for eternity, and your throne shall be secure continuously.’”
010	2SA	007	017	According to all these words, and according to this entire vision, so did Nathan speak to David.
010	2SA	007	018	Then king David entered and sat before the Lord, and he said: “Who am I, O Lord God, and what is my house, that you would bring me to this point?
