011	1KI	022	024	Then Zedekiah, the son of Chenaanah, drew near and struck Micaiah on the jaw, and he said, “So then, has the Spirit of the Lord left me, and spoken to you?”
011	1KI	022	025	And Micaiah said, “You shall see in the day when you will enter into a room within a room, so that you may conceal yourself.”
011	1KI	022	026	And the king of Israel said: “Take Micaiah, and let him dwell with Amon, the ruler of the city, and with Joash, the son of Amalech.
011	1KI	022	027	And tell them: ‘Thus says the king: Put this man in prison, and sustain him with the bread of affliction, and with the water of distress, until I return in peace.’”
011	1KI	022	028	And Micaiah said, “If you will have returned in peace, the Lord has not spoken through me.” And he said, “May all the people hear it.”
011	1KI	022	029	And so, the king of Israel, and Jehoshaphat, the king of Judah, ascended to Ramoth Gilead.
