013	1CH	002	001	And the sons of Israel: Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, and Zebulun,
013	1CH	002	002	Dan, Joseph, Benjamin, Naphtali, Gad, and Asher.
013	1CH	002	003	The sons of Judah: Er, Onan, and Shelah. These three were born to him from the daughter of Shua, the Canaanite. But Er, the firstborn of Judah, was evil in the sight of the Lord, and so he killed him.
013	1CH	002	004	Now Tamar, his daughter-in-law, bore to him Perez and Zerah. Therefore, all the sons of Judah were five.
013	1CH	002	005	And the sons of Perez: Hezron and Hamul.
013	1CH	002	006	Also, the sons of Zerah: Zimri, and Ethan, and Heman, as well as Calcol and Dara, five altogether.
013	1CH	002	007	The sons of Carmi: Achar, who disturbed Israel and sinned by the theft of what was anathema.
013	1CH	002	008	The sons of Ethan: Azariah.
013	1CH	002	009	And the sons of Hezron who were born to him: Jerahmeel, and Ram, and Chelubai.
013	1CH	002	010	Then Ram conceived Amminadab. And Amminadab conceived Nahshon, a leader of the sons of Judah.
013	1CH	002	011	Also, Nahshon conceived Salma, from whom Boaz rose up.
013	1CH	002	012	Truly, Boaz conceived Obed, who also himself conceived Jesse.
013	1CH	002	013	Now Jesse conceived the firstborn Eliab, the second Abinadab, the third Shammah,
013	1CH	002	014	the fourth Nethanel, the fifth Raddai,
013	1CH	002	015	the sixth Ozem, the seventh David.
013	1CH	002	016	Their sisters were Zeruiah and Abigail. The sons of Zeruiah: Abishai, Joab, and Asahel, three.
013	1CH	002	017	And Abigail conceived Amasa, whose father was Jether, the Ishmaelite.
013	1CH	002	018	Truly, Caleb, the son of Hezron, took a wife named Azubah, of whom he conceived Jerioth. And her sons were Jesher, and Shobab, and Ardon.
013	1CH	002	019	And when Azubah had died, Caleb took as wife Ephratha, who bore to him Hur.
013	1CH	002	020	Now Hur conceived Uri. And Uri conceived Bezalel.
013	1CH	002	021	And afterwards, Hezron entered to the daughter of Machir, father of Gilead. And he took her when he was sixty years old. And she bore to him Segub.
013	1CH	002	022	And then Segub conceived Jair, and he possessed twenty-three cities in the land of Gilead.
013	1CH	002	023	And he seized Geshur and Aram, towns of Jair, and Kenath and its villages, sixty cities. All these were sons of Machir, father of Gilead.
013	1CH	002	024	Then, when Hezron had died, Caleb entered to Ephratha. Also, Hezron had as wife Abia, who bore to him Ashhur, the father of Tekoa.
013	1CH	002	025	Now sons were born to Jerahmeel, the firstborn of Hezron: Ram, his firstborn, and Bunah, and Oren, and Ozem, and Ahijah.
013	1CH	002	026	Jerahmeel also married another wife, named Atarah, who was the mother of Onam.
013	1CH	002	027	Then too, the sons of Ram, the firstborn of Jerahmeel, were Maaz, Jamin, and Eker.
013	1CH	002	028	And Onam had sons: Shammai and Jada. And the sons of Shammai: Nadab and Abishur.
013	1CH	002	029	Truly, the name of the wife of Abishur was Abihail, who bore to him Ahban and Molid.
013	1CH	002	030	Now the sons of Nadab were Seled and Appaim. And Seled died without children.
013	1CH	002	031	Truly, the son of Appaim was Ishi. And Ishi conceived Sheshan. Then Sheshan conceived Ahlai.
013	1CH	002	032	But the sons of Jada, the brother of Shammai, were Jether and Jonathan. Then Jether also died without children.
013	1CH	002	033	And Jonathan conceived Peleth and Zaza. These were the sons of Jerahmeel.
013	1CH	002	034	Now Sheshan did not have sons, but only daughters, and an Egyptian servant named Jarha.
013	1CH	002	035	And so he gave to him his daughter as wife, who bore to him Attai.
013	1CH	002	036	Then Attai conceived Nathan, and Nathan conceived Zabad.
013	1CH	002	037	Also, Zabad conceived Ephlal, and Ephlal conceived Obed.
013	1CH	002	038	Obed conceived Jehu; Jehu conceived Azariah.
013	1CH	002	039	Azariah conceived Helez, and Helez conceived Eleasah.
013	1CH	002	040	Eleasah conceived Sismai; Sismai conceived Shallum.
013	1CH	002	041	Shallum conceived Jekamiah; then Jekamiah conceived Elishama.
013	1CH	002	042	And the sons of Caleb, the brother of Jerahmeel, were Mesha, his firstborn, who was the father of Ziph, and the sons of Mesha, the father of Hebron.
013	1CH	002	043	Now the sons of Hebron were Korah, and Tapuah, and Rekem, and Shema.
013	1CH	002	044	Then Shema conceived Raham, the father of Jorkeam. And Rekem conceived Shammai.
013	1CH	002	045	The son of Shammai was Maon, and Maon was the father of Bethzur.
013	1CH	002	046	Now Ephah, the concubine of Caleb, bore Haran, and Moza, and Gazez. And Haran conceived Gazez.
013	1CH	002	047	And the sons of Jahdai: Regem, and Jotham, and Geshan, and Pelet, and Ephah, and Shaaph.
013	1CH	002	048	And Maacah, the concubine of Caleb, bore Sheber and Tirhanah.
013	1CH	002	049	Then Shaaph, the father of Madmannah, conceived Sheva, the father of Machbenah, and the father of Gibea. Truly, the daughter of Caleb was Achsah.
013	1CH	002	050	These were the sons of Caleb, the son of Hur, the firstborn of Ephratha: Shobal, the father of Kiriath-jearim;
013	1CH	002	051	Salma, the father of Bethlehem; Hareph, the father of Bethgader.
013	1CH	002	052	Now there were sons for Shobal, the father of Kiriath-jearim, who saw half the places of rest.
013	1CH	002	053	And from the kindred of Kiriath-jearim: the Ithrites, and the Puthites, and the Shumathites, and the Mishraites. From these, the Zorathites and the Eshtaolites went forth.
013	1CH	002	054	The sons of Salma: Bethlehem, and the Netophathites, the crowns of the house of Joab, and half the places of rest of the Zorathites,
013	1CH	002	055	as well as the families of the scribes living in Jabesh, those singing and making music, and those dwelling in tents. These are the Kenites, who went forth from Calor, the father of the house of Rechab.
013	1CH	003	001	Truly, David had these sons, who were born to him in Hebron: the firstborn Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelite; the second Daniel, from Abigail the Carmelite;
013	1CH	003	002	the third Absalom, the son of Maacah, daughter of Talmai, king of Geshur; the fourth Adonijah, the son of Haggith;
013	1CH	003	003	the fifth Shephatiah, of Abital; the sixth Ithream, from his wife Eglah.
013	1CH	003	004	Therefore, six were born to him in Hebron, where he reigned for seven years and six months. Then he reigned for thirty-three years in Jerusalem.
013	1CH	003	005	Now in Jerusalem, sons were born to him: Shammua, and Sobab, and Nathan, and Solomon, these four from Bathsheba, the daughter of Ammiel;
013	1CH	003	006	also Ibhar and Elishama,
013	1CH	003	007	and Eliphelet, and Nogah, and Nepheg, and Japhia,
013	1CH	003	008	indeed also Elishama, and Eliada, and Eliphelet, nine.
013	1CH	003	009	All these were sons of David, aside from the sons of the concubines. And they had a sister, Tamar.
013	1CH	003	010	Now the son of Solomon was Rehoboam, from whom Abijah conceived a son, Asa. And from him, there was born Jehoshaphat,
013	1CH	003	011	the father of Jehoram. And Jehoram conceived Ahaziah, from whom there was born Jehoash.
013	1CH	003	012	And his son, Amaziah, conceived Azariah. Then Jotham, the son of Azariah,
013	1CH	003	013	conceived Ahaz, the father of Hezekiah, from whom was born Manasseh.
013	1CH	003	014	Then too, Manasseh conceived Amon, the father of Josiah.
013	1CH	003	015	Now the sons of Josiah were these: the firstborn Johanan, the second Jehoiakim, the third Zedekiah, the fourth Shallum.
013	1CH	003	016	From Jehoiakim was born Jeconiah and Zedekiah.
013	1CH	003	017	The sons of Jeconiah the captive were: Shealtiel,
013	1CH	003	018	Malchiram, Pedaiah, Shenazzar, and Jekamiah, Hoshama, and Nedabiah.
013	1CH	003	019	From Pedaiah, there rose up Zerubbabel and Shimei. Zerubbabel conceived Meshullam, Hananiah, and their sister Shelomith,
013	1CH	003	020	as well as Hashubah, and Ohel, and Berechiah, and Hasadiah, Jushab-hesed, five.
013	1CH	003	021	Now the son of Hananiah was Pelatiah, the father of Jeshaiah, whose son was Rephaiah. And his son was Arnan, from whom was born Obadiah, whose son was Shecaniah.
013	1CH	003	022	The son of Shecaniah was Shemaiah, whose sons were these: Hattush, and Igal, and Bariah, and Neariah, and Shaphat, six in number.
013	1CH	003	023	The sons of Neariah: Elioenai, and Hizkiaj, and Azrikam, three.
013	1CH	003	024	The sons of Elioenai: Hodaviah, and Eliashib, and Pelaiah, and Akkub, and Johanan, and Delaiah, and Anani, seven.
013	1CH	004	001	The sons of Judah: Perez, Hezron, and Carmi, and Hur, and Shobal.
013	1CH	004	002	Truly, Reaiah, the son of Shobal, conceived Jahath; from him were born Ahumai and Lahad. These are the kindred of the Zorathites.
013	1CH	004	003	And this is the stock of Etam: Jezreel, and Ishma, and Idbash. And the name of their sister was Hazzelelponi.
013	1CH	004	004	Now Penuel was the father of Gedor, and Ezer was the father of Hushah. These are the sons of Hur, the firstborn of Ephratha, the father of Bethlehem.
013	1CH	004	005	Truly, for Ashhur, the father of Tekoa, there were two wives: Helah and Naarah.
013	1CH	004	006	And Naarah bore to him: Ahuzzam, and Hepher, and Temeni, and Haahashtari. These are the sons of Naarah.
013	1CH	004	007	And the sons of Helah were Zereth, Izhar, and Ethnan.
013	1CH	004	008	Now Koz conceived Anub, and Zobebah, and the kindred of Aharhel, the son of Harum.
013	1CH	004	009	But Jabez was renowned, more so than his brothers, and his mother called his name Jabez, saying, “For I bore him in sorrow.”
013	1CH	004	010	Truly, Jabez called upon the God of Israel, saying, “If only, when blessing, you will bless me, and will broaden my borders, and your hand will be with me, and you will cause me not to be oppressed by evil.” And God granted to him the things for which he prayed.
013	1CH	004	011	Now Chelub, the brother of Shuhah, conceived Mehir, who was the father of Eshton.
013	1CH	004	012	Then Eshton conceived Bethrapha, and Paseah, and Tehinnah, the father of the city of Nahash. These are the men of Recah.
013	1CH	004	013	Now the sons of Kenaz were Othniel and Seraiah. And the sons of Othniel were Hathath and Meonothai.
013	1CH	004	014	Meonothai conceived Ophrah, but Seraiah conceived Joab, the father of the Valley of Artisans. For indeed, there were artisans there.
013	1CH	004	015	Truly, the sons of Chelub, the son of Jephunneh, were Iru, and Elah, and Naam. And the sons of Elah: Kenaz.
013	1CH	004	016	Also, the sons of Jehallelel: Ziph and Ziphah, Tiria and Asarel.
013	1CH	004	017	And the sons of Ezrah: Jether, and Mered, and Epher, and Jalon; and he conceived Miriam, and Shammai, and Ishbah, the father of Eshtemoa.
013	1CH	004	018	And then his wife, Judaia, bore Jered, the father of Gedor, and Heber, the father of Soco, and Jekuthiel, the father of Zanoah. Now there were sons of Bithiah, the daughter of Pharaoh, whom Mered married,
013	1CH	004	019	and sons of his wife Hodiah, the sister of Naham, the father of Keilah the Garmite, and of Eshtemoa, who was from Maacathi.
013	1CH	004	020	And the sons of Shimon: Amnon, and Rinnah, son of Hanan, and Tilon. And the sons of Ishi: Zoheth and Benzoheth.
013	1CH	004	021	The sons of Shelah, the son of Judah: Er, the father of Lecah, and Laadah, the father of Mareshah, and the kindred of the house of the workers of fine linen in the house of the oath,
013	1CH	004	022	and he who caused the sun to stand still, and the men of Lying, and Secure, and Burning, who were leaders in Moab, and who returned into Lehem. Now these words are ancient.
013	1CH	004	023	These are the potters living in the Plantations and in the Hedges, with a king in his works, and they were dwelling there.
013	1CH	004	024	The sons of Simeon: Nemuel and Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, Shaul;
013	1CH	004	025	Shallum his son, Mibsam his son, Mishma his son.
013	1CH	004	026	The sons of Mishma: Hammuel his son, Zaccur his son, Shimei his son.
013	1CH	004	027	The sons of Shimei were sixteen, and there were six daughters. But his brothers did not have many sons, and the entire kindred was not equal to the sum of the sons of Judah.
013	1CH	004	028	Now they lived in Beersheba, and Moladah, and Hazarshual,
013	1CH	004	029	and in Bilhah, and in Ezem, and in Tolad,
013	1CH	004	030	and in Bethuel, and in Hormah, and in Ziklag,
013	1CH	004	031	and in Beth-marcaboth, and in Hazarsusim, and in Bethbiri, and in Shaaraim. These were their cities until king David.
013	1CH	004	032	And their towns were Etam, and Ain, Rimmon, and Tochen, and Ashan, five cities,
013	1CH	004	033	with all their villages, on every side of these cities, as far as Baal. This is their habitation and the distribution of the settlements.
013	1CH	004	034	And there were Meshobab and Jamlech, and Joshah, the son of Amaziah,
013	1CH	004	035	and Joel, and Jehu, the son of Joshibiah, the son of Seraiah, the son of Asiel,
013	1CH	004	036	and Elioenai, and Jaakobah, and Jeshohaiah, and Asaiah, and Adiel, and Jesimiel, and Benaiah,
013	1CH	004	037	as well as Ziza, the son of Shiphi, the son of Allon, the son of Jedaiah, the son of Shimri, the son of Shemaiah.
013	1CH	004	038	These were the names of the leaders in their kindred. And they were multiplied greatly within the houses of their marriages.
013	1CH	004	039	And they set out, so that they might enter into Gedor, as far as the eastern valley, and so that they might seek pastures for their flocks.
013	1CH	004	040	And they found fat and very good pastures, and a very wide and quiet and fruitful land, in which some from the stock of Ham had lived before.
013	1CH	004	041	So then, those whose names have been written above, went forth in the days of Hezekiah, the king of Judah. And they struck down the inhabitants who had been found there with their dwellings. And they wiped them out, even to the present day. And they lived in place of them, because they found very fat pastures there.
013	1CH	004	042	Also, some of the sons of Simeon, five hundred men, went away to mount Seir, having as leaders Pelatiah and Neariah and Rephaiah and Uzziel, the sons of Ishi.
013	1CH	004	043	And they struck down the remnant of the Amalekites, those who had been able to escape, and they lived there in place of them, even to this day.
013	1CH	005	001	Also, there were the sons of Reuben, the firstborn of Israel. For indeed, he was his firstborn, but when he had violated the bed of his father, his right as firstborn was given to the sons of Joseph, the son of Israel, and he was not reputed as firstborn.
013	1CH	005	002	Moreover, Judah, who was strongest among his brothers, from his stock leaders sprung up, but the right of firstborn was reputed to Joseph.
013	1CH	005	003	So then, the sons of Reuben, the firstborn of Israel, were Hanoch and Pallu, Hezron and Carmi.
013	1CH	005	004	The sons of Joel: Shemaiah his son, Gog his son, Shimei his son,
013	1CH	005	005	Micah his son, Reaiah his son, Baal his son,
013	1CH	005	006	Beerah his son, whom Tilgath-pilneser, the king of the Assyrians, led away captive, and he was a leader in the tribe of Reuben.
013	1CH	005	007	Now his brothers and all his kindred, when they were being numbered according to their families, had as leaders Jeiel and Zechariah.
013	1CH	005	008	Now Bela, the son of Azaz, the son of Shema, the son of Joel, lived in Aroer, as far as Nebo and Baalmeon.
013	1CH	005	009	And he lived toward the eastern region, as far as the entrance to the wilderness and the river Euphrates. For indeed, they possessed a great number of cattle in the land of Gilead.
013	1CH	005	010	Then, in the days of Saul, they battled against the Hagarites and put them to death. And they lived in place of them, in their dwellings, throughout the entire region that looks to the east of Gilead.
013	1CH	005	011	Truly, the sons of Gad lived in the opposite region from them, in the land of Bashan, as far as Salecah:
013	1CH	005	012	Joel the head, and Shapham the second, then Janai and Shaphat, in Bashan.
013	1CH	005	013	Truly, their brothers, according to the houses of their kindred, were: Michael, and Meshullam, and Sheba, and Jorai, and Jacan, and Zia, and Eber, seven.
013	1CH	005	014	These were the sons of Abihail, the son of Huri, the son of Jaroah, the son of Gilead, the son of Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the son of Jahdo, the son of Buz,
013	1CH	005	015	along with their brothers, the sons of Abdiel, the son of Guni, the leader of the house, in their families,
013	1CH	005	016	And they lived in Gilead, and in Bashan and its towns, and in all the suburbs of Sharon, as far as the borders.
013	1CH	005	017	All these were numbered in the days of Jotham, the king of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam, the king of Israel:
013	1CH	005	018	the sons of Reuben, and of Gad, and the one half tribe of Manasseh, men of war, carrying shields and swords, and bending the bow, and trained for battle, forty-four thousand and seven hundred sixty, advancing to the fight.
013	1CH	005	019	They struggled against the Hagarites, yet truly the Jetureans, and Naphish, and Nodab offered assistance to them.
013	1CH	005	020	And the Hagarites were delivered into their hands, and all who were with them. For they called upon God while they did battle. And he heeded them, because they had trusted in him.
013	1CH	005	021	And they seized all that they possessed, of camels fifty thousand, and of sheep two hundred fifty thousand, and of donkeys two thousand, and of men one hundred thousand lives.
013	1CH	005	022	And many fell down wounded. For it was a war of the Lord. And they lived in place of them, until the transmigration.
013	1CH	005	023	Also, the sons of the one half tribe of Manasseh possessed the land, from the parts of Bashan as far as Baal, Hermon, and Sanir, and Mount Hermon. For certainly, their number was immense.
013	1CH	005	024	And these were leaders of the house of their kindred: Epher, and Ishi, and Eliel, and Azriel, and Jeremiah, and Hodaviah, and Jahdiel, very valiant and powerful men, and renowned leaders in their families.
013	1CH	005	025	But they abandoned the God of their fathers, and they fornicated after the gods of the peoples of the land, whom God took away before them.
013	1CH	005	026	And so the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul, the king of the Assyrians, and the spirit of Tilgath-pilneser, the king of Assur. And he took away Reuben, and Gad, and the one half tribe of Manasseh. And he led them to Halah, and to Habor, and to Hara, and to the river of Gozan, even to this day.
013	1CH	006	001	The sons of Levi: Gershom, Kohath, and Merari.
013	1CH	006	002	The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel.
013	1CH	006	003	The sons of Amram: Aaron, Moses, and Miriam. The sons of Aaron: Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar.
013	1CH	006	004	Eleazar conceived Phinehas, and Phinehas conceived Abishua.
013	1CH	006	005	Truly, Abishua conceived Bukki, and Bukki conceived Uzzi.
013	1CH	006	006	Uzzi conceived Zerahiah, and Zerahiah conceived Meraioth.
013	1CH	006	007	Then Meraioth conceived Amariah, and Amariah conceived Ahitub.
013	1CH	006	008	Ahitub conceived Zadok, and Zadok conceived Ahimaaz.
013	1CH	006	009	Ahimaaz conceived Azariah; Azariah conceived Johanan.
013	1CH	006	010	Johanan conceived Azariah. He is the one who executed the priestly office in the house that Solomon built in Jerusalem.
013	1CH	006	011	Now Azariah conceived Amariah, and Amariah conceived Ahitub.
013	1CH	006	012	Ahitub conceived Zadok, and Zadok conceived Shallum.
013	1CH	006	013	Shallum conceived Hilkiah, and Hilkiah conceived Azariah.
013	1CH	006	014	Azariah conceived Seraiah, and Seraiah conceived Jehozadak.
013	1CH	006	015	Now Jehozadak departed, when the Lord took away Judah and Jerusalem, by the hands of Nebuchadnezzar.
013	1CH	006	016	So the sons of Levi were Gershom, Kohath, and Merari.
013	1CH	006	017	And these are the names of the sons of Gershom: Libni and Shimei.
013	1CH	006	018	The sons of Kohath: Amram, and Izhar, and Hebron, and Uzziel.
013	1CH	006	019	The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. And so these are the kindred of Levi, according to their families.
013	1CH	006	020	Of Gershom: Libni his son, Jahath his son, Zimmah his son,
013	1CH	006	021	Joah his son, Iddo his son, Zerah his son, Jeatherai his son.
013	1CH	006	022	The sons of Kohath: Amminadab his son, Korah his son, Assir his son,
013	1CH	006	023	Elkanah his son, Ebiasaph his son, Assir his son,
013	1CH	006	024	Tahath his son, Uriel his son, Uzziah his son, Shaul his son.
013	1CH	006	025	The sons of Elkanah: Amasai and Ahimoth
013	1CH	006	026	and Elkanah. The sons of Elkanah: Zophai his son, Nahath his son,
013	1CH	006	027	Eliab his son, Jeroham his son, Elkanah his son.
013	1CH	006	028	The sons of Samuel: Vasseni the firstborn, and Abijah.
013	1CH	006	029	Now the sons of Merari were: Mahli, Libni his son, Shimei his son, Uzzah his son,
013	1CH	006	030	Shimea his son, Haggiah his son, Asaiah his son.
013	1CH	006	031	These are the ones whom David appointed over the singing men in the house of the Lord, in the place where the ark was located.
013	1CH	006	032	And they ministered before the tabernacle of the testimony with singing, until Solomon built the house of the Lord in Jerusalem. And they would stand according to their order in the ministry.
013	1CH	006	033	Truly, these are the ones who were assisting, with their sons, from the sons of Kohath: the singer Heman, the son of Joel, the son of Samuel,
013	1CH	006	034	the son of Elkanah, the son of Jeroham, the son of Eliel, the son of Toah,
013	1CH	006	035	the son of Zuph, the son of Elkanah, the son of Mahath, the son of Amasai,
013	1CH	006	036	the son of Elkanah, the son of Joel, the son of Azariah, the son of Zephaniah,
013	1CH	006	037	the son of Tahath, the son of Assir, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah,
013	1CH	006	038	the son of Izhar, the son of Kohath, the son of Levi, the son of Israel.
013	1CH	006	039	And there was also his brother, Asaph, who was standing at his right, Asaph, the son of Berechiah, the son of Shimea,
013	1CH	006	040	the son of Michael, the son of Baaseiah, the son of Malchijah,
013	1CH	006	041	the son of Ethni, the son of Zerah, the son of Adaiah,
013	1CH	006	042	the son of Ethan, the son of Zimmah, the son of Shimei,
013	1CH	006	043	the son of Jahath, the son of Gershom, the son of Levi.
013	1CH	006	044	Now the sons of Merari, their brothers, were on the left: Ethan, the son of Kishi, the son of Abdi, the son of Malluch,
013	1CH	006	045	the son of Hashabiah, the son of Amaziah, the son of Hilkiah,
013	1CH	006	046	the son of Amzi, the son of Boni, the son of Shemer,
013	1CH	006	047	the son of Mahli, the son of Mushi, the son of Merari, the son of Levi.
013	1CH	006	048	There were also their brothers, Levites who were appointed for every ministry of the tabernacle of the house of the Lord.
013	1CH	006	049	Truly, Aaron and his sons were burning offerings upon the altar of holocausts and upon the altar of incense, for the entire work of the Holy of Holies, and to pray on behalf of Israel, in accord with all the things that Moses, the servant of God, had instructed.
013	1CH	006	050	Now these are the sons of Aaron: Eleazar his son, Phinehas his son, Abishua his son,
013	1CH	006	051	Bukki his son, Uzzi his son, Zerahiah his son,
013	1CH	006	052	Meraioth his son, Amariah his son, Ahitub his son,
013	1CH	006	053	Zadok his son, Ahimaaz his son.
013	1CH	006	054	And these are their habitations according to the villages and confines, specifically of the sons of Aaron, according to the kindred of the Kohathites. For it fell to them by lot.
013	1CH	006	055	And so, they gave Hebron, in the land of Judah, and its suburbs all around, to them,
013	1CH	006	056	but they gave the fields of the city, and the villages, to Caleb, the son of Jephunneh.
