013	1CH	010	012	each one of the valiant men rose up, and they took the bodies of Saul and of his sons. And they brought them to Jabesh. And they buried their bones under the oak that was in Jabesh. And they fasted for seven days.
013	1CH	010	013	Thus did Saul die for his iniquities, because he betrayed the commandment of the Lord which he had instructed, and did not keep it. And moreover, he even consulted a woman diviner;
013	1CH	010	014	for he did not trust in the Lord. Because of this, he caused his death, and he transferred his kingdom to David, the son of Jesse.
013	1CH	011	001	Then all of Israel was gathered to David at Hebron, saying: “We are your bone and your flesh.
013	1CH	011	002	Also, yesterday and the day before, when Saul still reigned, you were the one who led out and brought in Israel. For the Lord your God said to you: ‘You shall pasture my people Israel, and you shall be the leader over them.’”
013	1CH	011	003	Therefore, all those greater by birth of Israel went to the king at Hebron. And David formed a pact with them before the Lord. And they anointed him king over Israel, in accord with the word of the Lord, which he spoke by the hand of Samuel.
013	1CH	011	004	Then David and all of Israel went to Jerusalem. The same is Jebus, where the Jebusites, the inhabitants of the land, were.
013	1CH	011	005	And those who were living in Jebus said to David: “You shall not enter here.” But David seized the stronghold of Zion, which is the city of David.
013	1CH	011	006	And he said, “Whoever shall strike the Jebusites first, shall be ruler and commander.” And so Joab, the son of Zeruiah, ascended first, and he was made the leader.
013	1CH	011	007	Then David lived in the stronghold, and for this reason it was called the City of David.
013	1CH	011	008	And he built up the city all around, from Millo even to every side. But Joab built the rest of the city.
013	1CH	011	009	And David continued advancing and increasing, and the Lord of hosts was with him.
013	1CH	011	010	These are the leaders of the strong men of David, who assisted him, so that he would become king over all of Israel, in accord with the word of the Lord, which he spoke to Israel.
013	1CH	011	011	And this is the number of the robust of David: Jashobeam, the son of a Hachmonite, leader among the thirty. He lifted up his spear over three hundred, who were wounded at one time.
013	1CH	011	012	And after him, there was Eleazar, the son of his uncle, an Ahohite, who was among the three powerful ones.
013	1CH	011	013	He was with David in Pasdammim, when the Philistines were gathered to that place for battle. Now the field of that region was full of barley, but the people had fled from the face of the Philistines.
013	1CH	011	014	These men stood in the midst of the field, and they defended it. And when they had struck down the Philistines, the Lord gave a great salvation to his people.
013	1CH	011	015	Then three from the thirty leaders descended to the rock where David was, to the cave of Adullam, when the Philistines had made camp in the Valley of the Rephaim.
013	1CH	011	016	Now David was in a stronghold, and a garrison of the Philistines was in Bethlehem.
013	1CH	011	017	And then David desired and said, “O if only someone would give me water from the well of Bethlehem, which is at the gate!”
013	1CH	011	018	Therefore, these three broke through to the midst of the camp of the Philistines, and they drew water from the well of Bethlehem, which was at the gate. And they took it to David, so that he might drink. But he was not willing; and instead, he offered it as a libation to the Lord,
013	1CH	011	019	saying: “Far be it from me, that I would do this in the sight of my God, and that I would drink the blood of these men. For at the peril of their own lives, they brought the water to me.” And for this reason, he was not willing to drink. The three most powerful accomplished these things.
013	1CH	011	020	Also, Abishai, the brother of Joab, was the leader of the three, and he lifted up his spear against three hundred, who were wounded. And he was most renowned among the three,
013	1CH	011	021	and he was famous among the second three and their leader. Yet truly, he did not reach as far as the first three.
013	1CH	011	022	Benaiah, the son of Jehoiada, from Kabzeel, was a very mature man, who had accomplished many deeds. He struck down the two lions of God from Moab. And he descended and killed a lion in the middle of a pit, in the time of snow.
013	1CH	011	023	And he struck down an Egyptian man, whose stature was five cubits, and who had a spear like a weaver’s beam. And yet he descended to him with a staff. And he seized the spear that he was holding in his hand. And he killed him with his own spear.
013	1CH	011	024	These things were done by Benaiah, the son of Jehoiada, who was most renowned among the three robust ones,
013	1CH	011	025	the first among the thirty. Yet truly, he did not reach as far as the three. Then David placed him beside his ear.
013	1CH	011	026	Moreover, the strongest men of the army were Asahel, the brother of Joab; and Elhanan, the son of his uncle, from Bethlehem;
013	1CH	011	027	Shammoth, a Harorite; Helez, a Pelonite;
013	1CH	011	028	Ira, the son of Ikkesh, a Tekoite; Abiezer, an Anathothite;
013	1CH	011	029	Sibbecai, a Hushathite; Ilai, an Ahohite;
013	1CH	011	030	Maharai, a Netophathite; Heled, the son of Baanah, a Netophathite;
013	1CH	011	031	Ithai, the son of Ribai, from Gibeah, of the sons of Benjamin; Benaiah, a Pirathonite;
013	1CH	011	032	Hurai, from the torrent Gaash; Abiel, an Arbathite; Azmaveth, a Baharumite; Eliahba, a Shaalbonite.
013	1CH	011	033	The sons of Hashem, a Gizonite: Jonathan, the son of Shagee, a Hararite;
013	1CH	011	034	Ahiam, the son of Sachar, a Hararite;
013	1CH	011	035	Eliphal, the son of Ur;
013	1CH	011	036	Hepher, a Mecherathite; Ahijah, a Pelonite;
013	1CH	011	037	Hezro, a Carmelite; Naharai, the son of Ezbai;
013	1CH	011	038	Joel, the brother of Nathan; Mibhar, the son of Hagri;
013	1CH	011	039	Zelek, an Ammonite; Naarai, a Beerothite, the armor bearer of Joab, the son of Zeruiah;
013	1CH	011	040	Ira, an Ithrite; Gareb, an Ithrite;
013	1CH	011	041	Uriah, a Hittite; Zabad, the son of Ahlai;
013	1CH	011	042	Adina, the son of Shiza, a Reubenite, the leader of the Reubenites, and thirty who were with him;
013	1CH	011	043	Hanan, the son of Maacah; and Joshaphat, a Mithnite;
013	1CH	011	044	Uzzia, an Ashterathite; Shama and Jeiel, the sons of Hotham, an Aroerite;
013	1CH	011	045	Jediael, the son of Shimri; and Joha, his brother, a Tizite;
013	1CH	011	046	Eliel, a Mahavite; and Jeribai and Joshaviah, the sons of Elnaam; and Ithmah, a Moabite;
013	1CH	011	047	Eliel, and Obed, and Jaasiel from Mezobaite.
013	1CH	012	001	Also, these went to David at Ziklag, while he was still fleeing from Saul, the son of Kish. And they were very strong and distinguished fighters,
013	1CH	012	002	bending the bow, and using either hand in casting stones with slings, and shooting arrows. From the brothers of Saul, out of Benjamin:
013	1CH	012	003	the leader was Ahiezer, with Joash, sons of Shemaah from Gibeah, and Jeziel and Pelet, sons of Azmaveth, and Beracah and Jehu, from Anathoth.
013	1CH	012	004	Also, there was Ishmaiah, from Gibeon, the strongest among the thirty and over the thirty; Jeremiah, and Jahaziel, and Johanan, and Jozabad, from Gederah;
013	1CH	012	005	and Eluzai, and Jerimoth, and Bealiah, and Shemariah, and Shephatiah, the Haruphites;
013	1CH	012	006	Elkanah, and Isshiah, and Azarel, and Joezer, and Jashobeam, from Carehim;
013	1CH	012	007	and also Joelah and Zebadiah, sons of Jeroham, from Gedor.
013	1CH	012	008	Then too, from Gad, there went over to David, when he was hiding in the desert, very robust men, who were excellent fighters, taking hold of shield and spear; their faces were like the faces of a lion, and they were swift like the roe deer upon the mountains.
013	1CH	012	009	Ezer was the leader, Obadiah the second, Eliab the third,
013	1CH	012	010	Mishmannah the fourth, Jeremiah the fifth,
013	1CH	012	011	Attai the sixth, Eliel the seventh,
013	1CH	012	012	Johanan the eighth, Elzabad the ninth,
013	1CH	012	013	Jeremiah the tenth, Machbannai the eleventh.
013	1CH	012	014	These were from the sons of Gad, leaders of the army. The least was in charge of one hundred soldiers, and the greatest was in charge of one thousand.
013	1CH	012	015	These are the ones who crossed over the Jordan in the first month, when it is accustomed to overflow its banks. And they put to flight all those who were staying in the valleys, to the eastern region and to the west.
013	1CH	012	016	Then some from Benjamin and from Judah also arrived at the stronghold where David was staying.
013	1CH	012	017	And David went out to meet them, and he said: “If you have arrived peacefully, so as to be a help to me, may my heart be joined to you; but if to betray me to my adversaries, though I have no iniquity in my hands, may the God of our fathers see and judge.”
013	1CH	012	018	Truly, the Spirit clothed Amasai, the leader among the thirty, and he said: “O David, we are yours! O son of Jesse, we are for you! Peace, peace to you, and peace to your helpers. For your God helps you.” Therefore, David received them, and he appointed them as leaders of troops.
013	1CH	012	019	Moreover, some from Manasseh crossed over to David, when he went forth with the Philistines against Saul, so that he might fight. But he did not fight with them. For the leaders of the Philistines, taking counsel, sent him back, saying, “To the peril of our own heads, he will return to his lord, Saul.”
013	1CH	012	020	And so, when he returned to Ziklag, some fled over to him from Manasseh: Adnah, and Jozabad, and Jediael, and Michael, and Adnah, and Jozabad, and Elihu, and Zillethai, leaders of thousands in Manasseh.
013	1CH	012	021	These offered assistance to David against the robbers. For all were very strong men, and they became leaders in the army.
013	1CH	012	022	Then, too, some came to David throughout each day, in order to help him, until they became a great number, like the army of God.
013	1CH	012	023	Now this is the number of the leaders of the army who went to David when he was at Hebron, so that they might transfer the kingdom of Saul to him, in accord with the word of the Lord:
013	1CH	012	024	the sons of Judah, carrying shield and spear, six thousand eight hundred, equipped for battle;
013	1CH	012	025	from the sons of Simeon, very strong men for the fight, seven thousand one hundred;
013	1CH	012	026	from the sons of Levi, four thousand six hundred;
013	1CH	012	027	as well as Jehoiada, a leader from the stock of Aaron, and with him three thousand seven hundred;
013	1CH	012	028	and then Zadok, a youth of distinguished qualities, and the house of his father, twenty-two leaders;
013	1CH	012	029	and from the sons of Benjamin, brothers of Saul, three thousand, for still a great part of them were following the house of Saul.
013	1CH	012	030	Then from the sons of Ephraim, there were twenty thousand eight hundred, very strong and robust men, renowned among their kindred.
013	1CH	012	031	And out of the one half tribe of Manasseh, eighteen thousand, each by their names, went forth so that they might appoint David as king.
013	1CH	012	032	Also, from the sons of Issachar, there were learned men, who knew each of the times, in order to anticipate what Israel ought to do, two hundred leaders. And all the remainder of the tribe were following their counsel.
013	1CH	012	033	Then, from Zebulun, there were those who went forth to battle, and who were standing in a battle line, prepared with the weapons of warfare; these fifty thousand arrived to assist, without duplicity of heart.
013	1CH	012	034	And from Naphtali, there were one thousand leaders; and with them were thirty-seven thousand, prepared with shield and spear.
013	1CH	012	035	And then from Dan, there were twenty-eight thousand six hundred, ready for battle.
013	1CH	012	036	And from Asher, there were forty thousand, going forth to fight, and summoned to the battle line.
013	1CH	012	037	Then, across the Jordan, there were, from the sons of Reuben, and from Gad, and from the one half tribe of Manasseh, one hundred twenty thousand, prepared with the weapons of warfare.
013	1CH	012	038	All these men of war, equipped for the fight, went with a perfect heart to Hebron, so that they might appoint David as king over all of Israel. Then, too, all the remainder of Israel were of one heart, so that they might make David king.
013	1CH	012	039	And they were in that place with David for three days, eating and drinking. For their brothers had made preparations for them.
013	1CH	012	040	Moreover, those who were near to them, even as far as Issachar, and Zebulun, and Naphtali, were bringing, on donkeys and camels and mules and oxen, bread for their provisions, with grain, dried figs, dried grapes, wine, oil, and oxen and sheep, with all abundance. For indeed, there was joy in Israel.
013	1CH	013	001	Then David took counsel with the tribunes, and the centurions, and all the leaders.
013	1CH	013	002	And he said to the entire assembly of Israel: “If it pleases you, and if the words that I speak come from the Lord our God, let us send to the remainder of our brothers, in all the regions of Israel, and to the priests and Levites who live in the suburbs of the cities, so that they may gather to us.
013	1CH	013	003	And let us bring back the ark of our God to us. For we did not seek it during the days of Saul.”
013	1CH	013	004	And the entire multitude responded that it should be done. For the word had pleased all the people.
013	1CH	013	005	Therefore, David gathered all of Israel, from Shihor of Egypt even to the entrance of Hamath, so as to bring the ark of God from Kiriath-jearim.
013	1CH	013	006	And David ascended with all the men of Israel to the hill of Kiriath-jearim, which is in Judah, so that he might bring from there the ark of the Lord God, sitting upon the Cherubim, where his name is invoked.
013	1CH	013	007	And they placed the ark of God upon a new cart from the house of Abinadab. Then Uzzah and his brother drove the cart.
013	1CH	013	008	Now David and all of Israel were playing before God, with all of their ability, in songs, and with harps, and psalteries, and timbrels, and cymbals, and trumpets.
013	1CH	013	009	And when they had arrived at the threshing floor of Chidon, Uzzah reached out his hand, so that he might support the ark. For indeed, the ox being wanton had caused it to incline a little.
013	1CH	013	010	And so the Lord became angry against Uzzah. And he struck him down because he had touched the ark. And he died there before the Lord.
013	1CH	013	011	And David was greatly saddened because the Lord had divided Uzzah. And he called that place ‘the Division of Uzzah,’ even to the present day.
013	1CH	013	012	And then he feared God, at that time, saying: “How will I be able to bring in the ark of God to myself?”
013	1CH	013	013	And for this reason, he did not bring it to himself, that is, into the City of David. Instead, he turned aside to the house of Obededom, the Gittite.
013	1CH	013	014	Therefore, the ark of God dwelt in the house of Obededom for three months. And the Lord blessed his house and all that he had.
013	1CH	014	001	Also, Hiram, the king of Tyre, sent messengers to David, and cedar wood, and artisans of walls and of wood, so that they might build a house for him.
013	1CH	014	002	And David realized that the Lord had confirmed him as king over Israel, and that his kingdom had been lifted up over his people Israel.
013	1CH	014	003	Also, David took other wives in Jerusalem. And he conceived sons and daughters.
013	1CH	014	004	And these are the names of those who were born to him in Jerusalem: Shammua and Shobab, Nathan and Solomon,
013	1CH	014	005	Ibhar, and Elishua, and Elpelet,
013	1CH	014	006	as well as Nogah, and Nepheg, and Japhia,
013	1CH	014	007	Elishama, and Beeliada, and Eliphelet.
013	1CH	014	008	Then, hearing that David had been anointed as king over all of Israel, all the Philistines ascended so that they might seek him. But when David had heard of it, he went out to meet them.
013	1CH	014	009	Now the Philistines, arriving, spread out in the Valley of the Rephaim.
013	1CH	014	010	And so David consulted the Lord, saying, “Shall I ascend to the Philistines, and will you deliver them into my hand?” And the Lord said to him, “Ascend, and I will deliver them into your hand.”
013	1CH	014	011	And when they had ascended to Baal-perazim, David struck them there, and he said: “God has divided my enemies by my hand, just as waters are divided.” And therefore the name of that place was called Baal-perazim.
013	1CH	014	012	And they left behind their gods in that place, and so David ordered them to be burned.
013	1CH	014	013	And then, at another time, the Philistines invaded, and they spread out in the valley.
013	1CH	014	014	And again, David consulted God. And God said to him: “You shall not ascend after them. Draw away from them. And you shall come against them opposite the balsam trees.
013	1CH	014	015	And when you hear a sound approaching in the tops of the balsam trees, then you shall go forth to war. For God has gone forth before you, so that he may strike down the army of the Philistines.”
013	1CH	014	016	Therefore, David did just as God had instructed him. And he struck down the army of the Philistines, from Gibeon as far as Gazera.
013	1CH	014	017	And the name of David became well-known in all the regions. And the Lord placed the fear of him over all the nations.
013	1CH	015	001	Also, he made houses for himself in the City of David. And built a place for the ark of God, and he set up a tent for it.
013	1CH	015	002	Then David said: “It is illicit for anyone to carry the ark of God except the Levites, whom the Lord chose to carry it and to minister to himself, even unto eternity.”
013	1CH	015	003	And he gathered all of Israel in Jerusalem, so that the ark of God might be brought into its place, which he had prepared for it.
013	1CH	015	004	Certainly, there were both the sons of Aaron and the Levites:
013	1CH	015	005	From the sons of Kohath, Uriel was the leader, and his brothers were one hundred twenty.
013	1CH	015	006	From the sons of Merari: Asaiah was the leader, and his brothers were two hundred twenty.
013	1CH	015	007	From the sons of Gershom: Joel was the leader, and his brothers were one hundred thirty.
013	1CH	015	008	From the sons of Elizaphan: Shemaiah was the leader, and his brothers were two hundred.
013	1CH	015	009	From the sons of Hebron: Eliel was the leader, and his brothers were eighty.
013	1CH	015	010	From the sons of Uzziel: Amminadab was the leader, and his brothers were one hundred twelve.
013	1CH	015	011	And David summoned the priests, Zadok and Abiathar, and the Levites: Uriel, Asaiah, Joel, Shemaiah, Eliel, and Amminadab.
013	1CH	015	012	And he said to them: “You who are the leaders of the Levitical families, be sanctified with your brothers, and bring the ark of the Lord God of Israel to the place that has been prepared for it.
013	1CH	015	013	Otherwise, as it was before, when the Lord struck us because you were not present, so also it might be now, if we do what is illicit.”
013	1CH	015	014	Therefore, the priests and the Levites were sanctified, so that they might carry the ark of the Lord God of Israel.
013	1CH	015	015	And the sons of Levi took the ark of God, just as Moses had instructed, in accord with the word of the Lord, upon their shoulders by the bars.
013	1CH	015	016	And David spoke to the leaders of the Levites, so that they might appoint, from their brothers, singers with musical instruments, specifically, psalteries, and harps, and cymbals, so that a joyful noise might resound on high.
013	1CH	015	017	And they appointed from the Levites: Heman, the son of Joel; and from his brothers, Asaph, the son of Berechiah; and truly, from their brothers, the sons of Merari: Ethan, the son of Kushaiah.
013	1CH	015	018	And with them were their brothers in the second rank: Zechariah, and Ben, and Jaaziel, and Shemiramoth, and Jahiel, and Unni, and Eliab, and Benaiah, and Maaseiah, and Mattithiah, and Eliphelehu, and Mikneiah, and Obededom, and Jeiel, who were gatekeepers.
013	1CH	015	019	Now the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Ethan, were sounding out with cymbals of brass.
013	1CH	015	020	And Zechariah, and Aziel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Unni, and Eliab, and Maaseiah, and Benaiah were singing mysteries with the psalteries.
013	1CH	015	021	Then Mattithiah, and Eliphelehu, and Mikneiah and Obededom, and Jeiel and Azaziah were singing a song of victory with the harps, for the octave.
013	1CH	015	022	Now Chenaniah, the leader of the Levites, was foremost over the prophecies, in order to mark out in advance the melodies. For indeed, he was very skillful.
013	1CH	015	023	And Berechiah and Elkanah were porters of the ark.
013	1CH	015	024	And the priests, Shebaniah, and Joshaphat, and Nethanel, and Amasai, and Zechariah, and Benaiah, and Eliezer, were sounding the trumpets before the ark of God. And Obededom and Jehiah were porters of the ark.
013	1CH	015	025	Therefore, David, and all those greater by birth of Israel, and the tribunes, went to carry the ark of the covenant of the Lord from the house of Obededom with rejoicing.
013	1CH	015	026	And when God had assisted the Levites, who were carrying the ark of the covenant of the Lord, they immolated seven bulls and seven rams.
013	1CH	015	027	Now David was clothed with a robe of fine linen, as were all the Levites who were carrying the ark, and the singers, and Chenaniah, the leader of the prophecy among the singers. But David was also clothed with a linen ephod.
013	1CH	015	028	And all of Israel were leading back the ark of the covenant of the Lord with jubilation, sounding out with the noise of horns, and trumpets, and cymbals, and psalteries, and harps.
013	1CH	015	029	And when the ark of the covenant of the Lord had arrived in the City of David, Michal, the daughter of Saul, gazing through a window, saw king David dancing and playing, and she despised him in her heart.
013	1CH	016	001	And so they took the ark of God, and they set it in the midst of the tabernacle, which David had pitched for it. And they offered holocausts and peace offerings before God.
013	1CH	016	002	And when David had completed offering holocausts and peace offerings, he blessed the people in the name of the Lord.
013	1CH	016	003	And he divided to every single one, from men even to women, a twist of bread, and a piece of roasted beef, and fine wheat flour fried with oil.
013	1CH	016	004	And he appointed some from the Levites who would minister before the ark of the Lord, and commemorate his works, and glorify and praise the Lord, the God of Israel.
013	1CH	016	005	Asaph was the leader, and second to him was Zechariah. In addition, there were Jeiel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Mattithiah, and Eliab, and Benaiah, and Obededom. And Jeiel was over the instruments of the psaltery and the harps. But Asaph sounded out with the cymbals.
013	1CH	016	006	Truly, the priests, Benaiah and Jahaziel, were to sound the trumpet continually before the ark of the covenant of the Lord.
013	1CH	016	007	In that day, David made Asaph the leader, in order to confess to the Lord with his brothers:
013	1CH	016	008	“Confess to the Lord, and invoke his name. Make known his endeavors among the peoples.
013	1CH	016	009	Sing to him, and sing psalms to him, and describe all his miracles.
013	1CH	016	010	Praise his holy name! Let the heart of those who seek the Lord rejoice!
013	1CH	016	011	Seek the Lord and his virtue. Seek his face always.
013	1CH	016	012	Remember his miracles, which he has accomplished, his signs, and the judgments of his mouth.
013	1CH	016	013	O offspring of Israel, his servants! O sons of Jacob, his elect!
013	1CH	016	014	He is the Lord our God. His judgments are throughout all the earth.
013	1CH	016	015	Remember forever his covenant, the word that he instructed unto a thousand generations,
013	1CH	016	016	the covenant that he formed with Abraham, and his oath with Isaac.
013	1CH	016	017	And he appointed the same to Jacob as a precept, and to Israel as an everlasting pact,
013	1CH	016	018	saying: ‘To you, I will give the land of Canaan, the lot of your inheritance.’
013	1CH	016	019	At that time, they were small in number, they were few and were settlers there.
013	1CH	016	020	And they passed through, from nation to nation, and from one kingdom to another people.
013	1CH	016	021	He did not permit anyone to falsely accuse them. Instead, he reproved kings on their behalf:
013	1CH	016	022	‘Do not touch my Christ. And do not malign my prophets.’
013	1CH	016	023	Sing to the Lord, all the earth! Announce his salvation, from day to day.
013	1CH	016	024	Describe his glory among the Gentiles, his miracles among all the peoples.
013	1CH	016	025	For the Lord is great and exceedingly praiseworthy. And he is terrible, above all gods.
013	1CH	016	026	For all the gods of the peoples are idols. But the Lord made the heavens.
013	1CH	016	027	Confession and magnificence are before him. Strength and gladness are in his place.
013	1CH	016	028	Bring to the Lord, O families of the peoples, bring to the Lord glory and dominion.
013	1CH	016	029	Give glory to the Lord, to his name. Lift up sacrifice, and approach before his sight. And adore the Lord in holy attire.
013	1CH	016	030	Let all the earth be moved before his face. For he founded the globe immoveable.
013	1CH	016	031	Let the heavens rejoice, and let the earth exult. And let them say among the nations, ‘The Lord has reigned.’
013	1CH	016	032	Let the sea roar, with all its plenitude. Let the fields exult, with all that is in them.
013	1CH	016	033	Then the trees of the forest will give praise before the Lord. For he comes to judge the earth.
013	1CH	016	034	Confess to the Lord, for he is good. For his mercy is eternal.
013	1CH	016	035	And say: ‘Save us, O God our savior! And gather us together, and rescue us from the nations, so that we may confess to your holy name, and may exult in your songs.
013	1CH	016	036	Blessed be the Lord, the God of Israel, from eternity to eternity.’ And let all the people say, ‘Amen,’ and let them sing a hymn to the Lord.”
013	1CH	016	037	And so, there before the ark of the covenant of the Lord, he left Asaph and his brothers, so that they might minister in the sight of the ark continually, throughout each day, and in their turns.
013	1CH	016	038	Now Obededom and his brothers were sixty-eight. And he appointed Obededom, the son of Jeduthun, and Hosah to be porters.
013	1CH	016	039	But Zadok the priest, and his brothers the priests, were before the tabernacle of the Lord in the high place, which was in Gibeon,
013	1CH	016	040	so that they could offer holocausts to the Lord upon the altar of holocausts continually, morning and evening, according to all that was written in the law of the Lord, which he instructed to Israel.
013	1CH	016	041	And after him, Heman, and Jeduthun, and the remainder of the elect, each one by his name, were appointed to confess to the Lord: “For his mercy endures forever.”
013	1CH	016	042	Also Heman and Jeduthun sounded the trumpet, and they played upon the cymbals, and upon every kind of musical instrument, in order to sing praises to God. But the sons of Jeduthun he made to be porters.
013	1CH	016	043	And all the people returned to their houses, and David also, so that he might bless his own house too.
013	1CH	017	001	Now when David was living in his house, he said to the prophet Nathan: “Behold, I live in a house of cedar. But the ark of the covenant of the Lord is under tent skins.”
013	1CH	017	002	And Nathan said to David: “Do all that is in your heart. For God is with you.”
013	1CH	017	003	And yet, that night the word of God came to Nathan, saying:
013	1CH	017	004	“Go, and speak to my servant David: Thus says the Lord: You shall not build a house for me as a dwelling place.
013	1CH	017	005	For I have not stayed in a house from the time when I led out Israel, even to this day. Instead, I have been continually changing places, in a tabernacle and tent,
013	1CH	017	006	dwelling with all of Israel. When did I ever speak to any one at all, among the judges of Israel whom I placed in charge so that they might pasture my people, saying: ‘Why have you not built a house of cedar for me?’
013	1CH	017	007	And so, now you shall say this to my servant David: Thus says the Lord of hosts: I took you when you were following the flock in the pastures, so that you would be the leader of my people Israel.
013	1CH	017	008	And I have been with you wherever you have gone. And I have slain all your enemies before you, and I have made a name for you like one of the great ones who are celebrated upon the earth.
013	1CH	017	009	And I have given a place to my people Israel. They shall be planted, and they shall live in it, and they shall no longer be moved. Neither shall the sons of iniquity wear them away, as in the beginning,
013	1CH	017	010	from the days when I gave judges to my people Israel, and I humbled all your enemies. Therefore, I announce to you that the Lord will build a house for you.
013	1CH	017	011	And when you will have completed your days, so that you go to your fathers, I will raise up your offspring after you, who shall be from your sons. And I will establish his kingdom.
013	1CH	017	012	He shall build a house for me, and I will make firm his throne, even unto eternity.
013	1CH	017	013	I will be a father to him, and he shall be a son to me. And I will not take away my mercy from him, as I took it away from the one who was before you.
013	1CH	017	014	And I will station him in my house and in my kingdom, even forever. And his throne will be very firm, in perpetuity.”
013	1CH	017	015	According to all these words, and according to this entire vision, so did Nathan speak to David.
013	1CH	017	016	And when king David had departed, and had sat down before the Lord, he said: “Who am I, O Lord God, and what is my house, that you would grant such things to me?
013	1CH	017	017	But even this has seemed little in your sight, and therefore you have also spoken about the house of your servant even for the future. And you have made me a spectacle above all men, O Lord God.
013	1CH	017	018	What more can David add, since you have so glorified your servant, and have known him?
013	1CH	017	019	O Lord, because of your servant, in accord with your own heart, you have brought about all this magnificence, and you have willed all these great things to be known.
013	1CH	017	020	O Lord, there is no one like you. And there is no other God apart from you, out of all whom we have heard about with our ears.
013	1CH	017	021	For what other single nation upon earth is like your people Israel, to whom God reached out, so that he might free them, and might make a people for himself, and by his greatness and terribleness cast out the nations before the face of those whom he had freed from Egypt?
013	1CH	017	022	And you have set your people Israel to be your people, even unto eternity. And you, O Lord, have become their God.
013	1CH	017	023	Now therefore, O Lord, let the word that you have spoken to your servant, and over his house, be confirmed in perpetuity, and do just as you have spoken.
013	1CH	017	024	And may your name remain and be magnified even for all time. And let it be said: ‘The Lord of hosts is the God of Israel. And the house of his servant David remains forever before him.’
013	1CH	017	025	For you, O Lord my God, have revealed to the ear of your servant that you will build a house for him. And therefore your servant has found faith so that he might pray before you.
013	1CH	017	026	Now then, O Lord, you are God. And you have spoken to your servant such great benefits.
013	1CH	017	027	And you have begun to bless the house of your servant, so that it may be always before you. For since it is you who is blessing, O Lord, it shall be blessed forever.”
013	1CH	018	001	Now after these things, it happened that David struck the Philistines, and he humbled them, and he took Gath and her daughters from the hand of the Philistines.
013	1CH	018	002	And he struck Moab. And the Moabites became the servants of David, offering gifts to him.
013	1CH	018	003	In that time, David also struck Hadadezer, the king of Zobah, in the region of Hamath, when he went forth so that he might extend his dominion as far as the river Euphrates.
013	1CH	018	004	Then David seized one thousand of his four-horse chariots, and seven thousand horsemen, and twenty thousand men on foot. And he hamstrung all the chariot horses, except for one hundred four-horse chariots, which he reserved for himself.
013	1CH	018	005	Then the Syrians of Damascus also arrived, so that they might offer assistance to Hadadezer, the king of Zobah. And so, David then struck of them twenty-two thousand men.
013	1CH	018	006	And he stationed soldiers in Damascus, so that Syria also would serve him, and would offer gifts. And the Lord assisted him in all the things to which he went forth.
013	1CH	018	007	Also, David took the golden quivers, which the servants of Hadadezer had, and he brought them to Jerusalem.
013	1CH	018	008	In addition, from Tibhath and Cun, cities of Hadadezer, he brought very much brass, from which Solomon made the sea of brass, and the pillars, and the vessels of brass.
013	1CH	018	009	Now when Toi, the king of Hamath, had heard this, specifically that David had struck the entire army of Hadadezer, the king of Zobah,
013	1CH	018	010	he sent his son Hadoram to king David so that he might petition peace from him, and so that he might congratulate him that he had struck and defeated Hadadezer. For indeed, Toi was an adversary to Hadadezer.
013	1CH	018	011	Moreover, all the vessels of gold and silver and brass king David consecrated to the Lord, with the silver and gold that he had taken from all the nations, as much from Idumea, and Moab, and the sons of Ammon, as from the Philistines and Amalek.
013	1CH	018	012	Truly, Abishai, the son of Zeruiah, struck eighteen thousand of the Edomites in the Valley of the Salt Pits.
013	1CH	018	013	And he stationed a garrison in Edom, so that Idumea would serve David. And the Lord saved David in all the things to which he went forth.
013	1CH	018	014	Therefore, David reigned over all of Israel, and he executed judgment and justice among all his people.
013	1CH	018	015	Now Joab, the son of Zeruiah, was over the army, and Jehoshaphat, the son of Ahilud, was the keeper of records.
013	1CH	018	016	And Zadok, the son of Ahitub, and Ahimelech, the son of Abiathar, were the priests. And Shavsha was the scribe.
013	1CH	018	017	Also, Benaiah, the son of Jehoiada, was over the legions of the Cherethites and Pelethites. But the sons of David were first at the hand of the king.
013	1CH	019	001	Now it happened that Nahash, the king of the sons of Ammon, died, and his son reigned in his place.
013	1CH	019	002	And David said: “I will act with mercy toward Hanun, the son of Nahash. For his father was gracious to me.” And so David sent messengers to console him over the death of his father. But when they had reached the land of the sons of Ammon, so that they might console Hanun,
013	1CH	019	003	the leaders of the sons of Ammon said to Hanun: “Do you think that perhaps David has sent them to console you in order to honor your father? Have you not noticed that his servants came to you so that they might explore, and investigate, and examine your land?”
013	1CH	019	004	And so Hanun shaved the heads and beards of the servants of David, and he cut away their tunics from the buttocks to the feet, and he sent them away.
013	1CH	019	005	And when they had gone, and had sent word to David, (for they had suffered a great disgrace,) he sent to meet them, and he instructed them that they should remain at Jericho until their beards grew, and then they should return.
013	1CH	019	006	Then, when the sons of Ammon realized that they had committed an injury against David, both Hanun and the rest of the people sent one thousand talents of silver, so that they might hire for themselves chariots and horsemen from Mesopotamia, and from Syrian Maacah, and from Zobah.
013	1CH	019	007	And they hired thirty-two thousand chariots, and the king of Maacah with his people. When these had arrived, they made camp in the region opposite Medeba. Also, the sons of Ammon, gathering from their cities, went to war.
013	1CH	019	008	And when David had heard this, he sent Joab and the entire army of strong men.
013	1CH	019	009	And the sons of Ammon, going out, set up a battle line before the gate of the city. But the kings who had come to their aid stood separately in the field.
013	1CH	019	010	And so Joab, understanding the war to be set facing him and behind his back, chose the strongest men from all of Israel, and he went out against the Syrians.
013	1CH	019	011	But the remaining portion of the people he placed under the hand of his brother Abishai. And they went out against the sons of Ammon.
013	1CH	019	012	And he said: “If the Syrians prevail over me, then you shall be a help to me. But if the sons of Ammon prevail over you, I will be a safeguard for you.
013	1CH	019	013	Be strengthened, and let us act manfully on behalf of our people, and on behalf of the cities of our God. And the Lord will do what is good in his own sight.”
013	1CH	019	014	Therefore, Joab, and the people who were with him, went out to battle against the Syrians. And he put them to flight.
013	1CH	019	015	Then the sons of Ammon, seeing that the Syrians had fled, also themselves fled from Abishai, his brother, and they entered into the city. And now Joab returned to Jerusalem.
013	1CH	019	016	But the Syrians, seeing that they had fallen before Israel, sent messengers, and they brought the Syrians who were across the river. And Shophach, the leader of the military of Hadadezer, was their commander.
013	1CH	019	017	When this had been reported to David, he gathered together all of Israel, and he crossed the Jordan. And he rushed toward them. And he set up a battle line facing them. And they fought against him.
013	1CH	019	018	But the Syrians fled from Israel. And David killed of the Syrians seven thousand chariots, and forty thousand men on foot, and Shophach, the leader of the army.
013	1CH	019	019	Then the servants of Hadadezer, seeing themselves to be overwhelmed by Israel, crossed over to David, and they served him. And Syria was no longer willing to offer aid to the sons of Ammon.
013	1CH	020	001	Now it happened that, after the course of a year, in the time when kings usually go forth to war, Joab gathered an army with experienced soldiers, and he laid waste to the land of the sons of Ammon. And he continued on and besieged Rabbah. But David was staying in Jerusalem when Joab struck Rabbah and destroyed it.
013	1CH	020	002	Then David took the crown of Milcom from his head, and he found in it the weight of one talent of gold, and very precious gems. And he made for himself a diadem from it. Also, he took the best spoils of the city, which were very many.
013	1CH	020	003	Then he led away the people who were in it. And he caused plows, and sleds, and iron chariots to go over them, so much so that they were cut apart and crushed. So did David treat all the cities of the sons of Ammon. And he returned with all his people to Jerusalem.
013	1CH	020	004	After these things, a war was begun at Gezer against the Philistines, in which Sibbecai the Hushathite struck Sippai from the race of the Rephaim, and he humbled them.
013	1CH	020	005	Also, another war was undertaken against the Philistines, in which Adeodatus, a son of the forest, a Bethlehemite, struck the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the wood of whose spear was like a weaver’s beam.
013	1CH	020	006	Then too, another war occurred in Gath, in which there was a very tall man, having six digits, that is, all together twenty-four. This man too was born from the stock of the Rephaim.
013	1CH	020	007	He blasphemed Israel. And Jonathan, the son of Shimea, the brother of David, struck him down.
013	1CH	020	008	These were the sons of the Rephaim in Gath, who fell by the hand of David and his servants.
013	1CH	021	001	Now Satan rose up against Israel, and he incited David so that he would number Israel.
013	1CH	021	002	And David said to Joab and to the leaders of the people: “Go, and number Israel, from Beersheba even to Dan. And bring me the number, so that I may know it.”
013	1CH	021	003	And Joab responded: “May the Lord increase his people a hundred times more than they are. But, my lord the king, are they not all your servants? Why would my lord seek this thing, which may be imputed as a sin to Israel?”
013	1CH	021	004	But the word of the king prevailed instead. And Joab went away, and he traveled around, through all of Israel. And he returned to Jerusalem.
013	1CH	021	005	And he gave to David the number of those whom he had surveyed. And the entire number of Israel was found to be one million and one hundred thousand men who could draw the sword; but from Judah, there were four hundred and seventy thousand men of war.
013	1CH	021	006	But Levi and Benjamin he did not number. For Joab executed the orders of the king unwillingly.
013	1CH	021	007	Then God was displeased with what had been ordered, and so he struck Israel.
013	1CH	021	008	And David said to God: “I have sinned exceedingly in doing this. I beg you take away the iniquity of your servant. For I have acted unwisely.”
013	1CH	021	009	And the Lord spoke to Gad, the seer of David, saying:
013	1CH	021	010	“Go, and speak to David, and tell him: Thus says the Lord: I give to you the option of three things. Choose the one that you will want, and I will do it to you.”
013	1CH	021	011	And when Gad had gone to David, he said to him: “Thus says the Lord: Choose what you will want:
013	1CH	021	012	Either three years of famine, or three months for you to flee from your enemies, unable to escape from their sword, or three days for the sword of the Lord and a pestilence to turn within the land, with the Angel of the Lord killing in every part of Israel. Now therefore, see what I should respond to him who sent me.”
013	1CH	021	013	And David said to Gad: “There are difficulties pressing upon me from every side. But it is better for me to fall into the hands of the Lord, for his mercies are many, than into the hands of men.”
013	1CH	021	014	Therefore, the Lord sent a pestilence upon Israel. And there fell from Israel seventy thousand men.
013	1CH	021	015	Also, he sent an Angel to Jerusalem, so that he might strike it. And while he was striking, the Lord saw and took pity over the magnitude of the harm. And he commanded the Angel who was striking: “It is enough. Now let your hand cease.” And the Angel of the Lord was standing beside the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.
013	1CH	021	016	And David, lifting up his eyes, saw the Angel of the Lord, standing between heaven and earth with a drawn sword in his hand, turned toward Jerusalem. And both he and those greater by birth, being clothed in haircloth, fell prone upon the ground.
013	1CH	021	017	And David said to God: “Am I not the one who ordered that the people be numbered? It is I who sinned; it is I who did evil. This flock, what does it deserve? O Lord my God, I beg you to let your hand be turned against me and against the house of my father. But let not your people be struck down.”
013	1CH	021	018	Then the Angel of the Lord instructed Gad to tell David that he should ascend and build an altar to the Lord God on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite.
013	1CH	021	019	Therefore, David ascended, in accord with the word of Gad, which he had spoken to him in the name of the Lord.
013	1CH	021	020	Now when Ornan had looked up and seen the Angel, he and his four sons hid themselves. For at that time, he was threshing wheat upon the floor.
013	1CH	021	021	Then, as David was approaching Ornan, Ornan saw him, and he went out from the threshing floor to meet him. And he reverenced him prone on the ground.
013	1CH	021	022	And David said to him: “Give this place of your threshing floor to me, so that I may build an altar to the Lord upon it. And you shall accept from me as much money as it is worth, so that the plague may cease from the people.”
013	1CH	021	023	But Ornan said to David: “Take it, and may my lord the king do whatever pleases him. Moreover, I give the oxen also as a holocaust, and the plow for wood, and the wheat for a sacrifice. I will offer all freely.”
013	1CH	021	024	And king David said to him: “By no means shall it be so. Instead, I will give money to you, as much as it is worth. For I must not take it from you, and thereby offer to the Lord holocausts that cost nothing.”
013	1CH	021	025	Therefore, David gave Ornan, for the place, the very just weight of six hundred shekels of gold.
013	1CH	021	026	And he built an altar to the Lord there. And he offered holocausts and peace offerings, and he called upon the Lord. And he heeded him by sending fire from heaven upon the altar of the holocaust.
013	1CH	021	027	And the Lord instructed the Angel, and he turned his sword back into its sheath.
013	1CH	021	028	Then, seeing that the Lord had heeded him at the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite, David immediately immolated victims there.
013	1CH	021	029	But the tabernacle of the Lord, which Moses had made in the desert, and the altar of holocausts, were at that time on the high place of Gibeon.
013	1CH	021	030	And David was unable to go to the altar, so that he might pray to God there. For he had been struck with an exceedingly great fear, seeing the sword of the Angel of the Lord.
013	1CH	022	001	And David said, “This is the house of God, and this is the altar for the holocaust of Israel.”
013	1CH	022	002	And he instructed them to gather all the new converts from the land of Israel. And from these he appointed stoneworkers, to hew stones and to polish them, so that he might build the house of God.
013	1CH	022	003	Also, David prepared very much iron to use for the nails of the gates, and for the seams and joints, as well as an immeasurable weight of brass.
013	1CH	022	004	Also, the cedar trees, which the Sidonians and Tyrians had transported to David, were not able to be counted.
013	1CH	022	005	And David said: “My son Solomon is a young and tender boy. But the house that I desire to be built to the Lord ought to be so great that it is renowned in every region. Therefore, I will prepare what will be necessary for him.” And for this reason, before his death, he prepared all the expenses.
013	1CH	022	006	And he called for Solomon, his son. And he instructed him to build a house to the Lord, the God of Israel.
013	1CH	022	007	And David said to Solomon: “My son, it was my will that I build a house to the name of the Lord my God.
013	1CH	022	008	But the word of the Lord came to me, saying: ‘You have shed much blood, and you have battled in many wars. You are not able to build a house to my name, so great was the shedding of blood before me.
013	1CH	022	009	The son who shall be born to you will be a very quiet man. For I will cause him to have rest from all his enemies on every side. And for this reason, he shall be called Peaceful. And I will grant peace and tranquility to Israel during all his days.
013	1CH	022	010	He shall build a house to my name. And he shall be a son to me, and I will be a father to him. And I will establish the throne of his kingdom over Israel unto eternity.’
013	1CH	022	011	Now then, my son, may the Lord be with you, and may you prosper and build a house to the Lord your God, just as he has spoken concerning you.
013	1CH	022	012	Also, may the Lord give you prudence and understanding, so that you may be able to rule Israel and to guard the law of the Lord your God.
013	1CH	022	013	For then you will be able to advance, if you keep the commandments and judgments that the Lord instructed Moses to teach to Israel. Be strengthened and act manfully. You should not fear, and you should not dread.
013	1CH	022	014	Behold, in my poverty I have prepared the expenses for the house of the Lord: one hundred thousand talents of gold, and one million of talents of silver. Yet truly, there is no measuring the brass and the iron. For their magnitude is beyond numbering. And I have prepared the timber and the stones for the entire project.
013	1CH	022	015	Also, you have very many artisans: stoneworkers, and builders of walls, and craftsmen of wood, and those most prudent in doing the work of every art,
013	1CH	022	016	with gold and silver, and with brass and iron, of which there is no number. Therefore, rise up and act. And the Lord will be with you.”
013	1CH	022	017	Also, David instructed all the leaders of Israel, so that they would assist his son Solomon,
013	1CH	022	018	saying: “You discern that the Lord your God is with you, and that he has given you rest on all sides, and that he has delivered all your enemies into your hands, and that the land has been subdued before the Lord and before his people.
013	1CH	022	019	Therefore, offer your hearts and your souls, so that you seek the Lord your God. And rise up and build a sanctuary to the Lord God, so that the ark of the covenant of the Lord, and the vessels consecrated to the Lord, may be brought into the house that is built to the name of the Lord.”
013	1CH	023	001	Then David, being old and full of days, appointed his son Solomon as king over Israel.
013	1CH	023	002	And he gathered together all the leaders of Israel, with the priests as well as the Levites.
013	1CH	023	003	And the Levites were numbered from the age of thirty years and upward. And there were found thirty-eight thousand men.
013	1CH	023	004	Of these, twenty-four thousand were chosen and distributed to the ministry of the house of the Lord. Then six thousand were overseers and judges.
013	1CH	023	005	Moreover, four thousand were porters. And the same number were the singers of psalms to the Lord, with the musical instruments which he had made for the music.
013	1CH	023	006	And David distributed them into courses according to the sons of Levi, specifically, Gershom, and Kohath, and Merari.
013	1CH	023	007	The sons of Gershom: Ladan and Shimei.
013	1CH	023	008	The sons of Ladan: the leader Jahiel, and Zetham, and Joel, three.
013	1CH	023	009	The sons of Shimei: Shelomoth, and Haziel, and Haran, three. These were the leaders of the families of Ladan.
013	1CH	023	010	Then the sons of Shimei: Jahath, and Zizah, and Jeush, and Beriah. These were the sons of Shimei, four.
013	1CH	023	011	Now Jahath was first, Zizah second, but Jeush and Beriah did not have many sons, and for this reason they were reckoned as one family and one house.
013	1CH	023	012	The sons of Kohath: Amram and Izhar, Hebron and Uzziel, four.
013	1CH	023	013	The sons of Amram: Aaron and Moses. Now Aaron was separated so that he might minister in the Holy of Holies, he and his sons forever, and so that he might burn incense to the Lord, according to his rite, and so that he might bless his name in perpetuity.
013	1CH	023	014	The sons of Moses, the man of God, were also numbered in the tribe of Levi.
013	1CH	023	015	The sons of Moses: Gershom and Eliezer.
013	1CH	023	016	The sons of Gershom: Shebuel the first.
013	1CH	023	017	Now the sons of Eliezer were Rehabiah the first. And there were no other sons for Eliezer. But the sons of Rehabiah were multiplied exceedingly.
013	1CH	023	018	The sons of Izhar: Shelomith the first.
013	1CH	023	019	The sons of Hebron: Jeriah the first, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, Jekameam the fourth.
013	1CH	023	020	The sons of Uzziel: Micah the first, Isshiah the second.
013	1CH	023	021	The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The sons of Mahli: Eleazar and Kish.
013	1CH	023	022	Then Eleazar died, and had no sons, but only daughters. And so the sons of Kish, their brothers, married them.
013	1CH	023	023	The sons of Mushi: Mahli, and Eder, and Jeremoth, three.
013	1CH	023	024	These are the sons of Levi, in their kindred and families, leaders in turns, and the number of each of the heads who were doing the works of the ministry of the house of the Lord, from twenty years of age and upward.
013	1CH	023	025	For David said: “The Lord, the God of Israel, has given rest to his people, and a habitation in Jerusalem even unto eternity.
013	1CH	023	026	Neither shall it be the office of the Levites any more to carry the tabernacle with all its equipment for use in the ministry.”
013	1CH	023	027	Also, according to the last precepts of David, the sons of Levi shall be counted by number from twenty years of age and upward.
013	1CH	023	028	And they shall be under the hand of the sons of Aaron, in the care of the house of the Lord, in the vestibule, and in the chambers, and in the place of purification, and in the sanctuary, and in all the works of the ministry of the temple of the Lord.
013	1CH	023	029	But the priests shall be over the bread of the presence, and the sacrifice of fine wheat flour, and the unleavened cakes, and the frying pan, and the roasting, and over every weight and measure.
013	1CH	023	030	Yet truly, the Levites shall stand to confess and to sing to the Lord, in the morning, and similarly in the evening,
013	1CH	023	031	as much in the oblation of the holocausts of the Lord, as in the Sabbaths and new moons and other solemnities, according to the number and ceremonies for each and every matter, perpetually before the Lord.
013	1CH	023	032	And let them keep the observances of the tabernacle of the covenant, and the rituals of the sanctuary, and the observance of the sons of Aaron, their brothers, so that they may minister in the house of the Lord.
013	1CH	024	001	Now these were the divisions of the sons of Aaron. The sons of Aaron: Nadab, and Abihu, and Eleazar, and Ithamar.
013	1CH	024	002	But Nadab and Abihu died before their father, and without children. And so Eleazar and Ithamar exercised the priestly office.
013	1CH	024	003	And David distributed them, that is, Zadok of the sons of Eleazar, and Ahimelech of the sons of Ithamar, according to their courses and ministry.
013	1CH	024	004	And there were found many more of the sons of Eleazar among the leading men, than of the sons of Ithamar. Therefore, he divided them so that there were, of the sons of Eleazar, sixteen leaders by their families, and of the sons of Ithamar eight by their families and houses.
013	1CH	024	005	Then he divided among them, in both families, by lot. For there were leaders of the sanctuary and leaders of God, as much from the sons of Eleazar as from the sons of Ithamar.
013	1CH	024	006	And the scribe Shemaiah, the son of Nethanel, a Levite, wrote these down before the king and the leaders, with Zadok, the priest, and Ahimelech, the son of Abiathar, and also the leaders of the priestly and Levitical families. And there was one house, which was preeminent over the others, that of Eleazar; and there was another house, which had the others under it, that of Ithamar.
013	1CH	024	007	Now the first lot went forth to Jehoiarib, the second to Jedaiah,
013	1CH	024	008	the third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim,
013	1CH	024	009	the fifth to Malchijah, the sixth to Mijamin,
013	1CH	024	010	the seventh to Hakkoz, the eighth to Abijah,
013	1CH	024	011	the ninth to Jeshua, the tenth to Shecaniah,
013	1CH	024	012	the eleventh to Eliashib, the twelfth to Jakim,
013	1CH	024	013	the thirteenth to Huppah, the fourteenth to Jeshebeab,
013	1CH	024	014	the fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,
013	1CH	024	015	the seventeenth to Hezir, the eighteenth to Happizzez,
013	1CH	024	016	the nineteenth to Pethahiah, the twentieth to Jehezkel,
013	1CH	024	017	the twenty-first to Jachin, the twenty-second to Gamul,
013	1CH	024	018	the twenty-third to Delaiah, the twenty-fourth to Maaziah.
013	1CH	024	019	These were their courses according to their ministries, so that they would enter into the house of the Lord in accord with their practice, under the hand of Aaron, their father, just as the Lord, the God of Israel, had instructed.
013	1CH	024	020	Now of the sons of Levi who were remaining, there were Shubael, from the sons of Amram, and Jehdeiah, from the sons of Shubael.
013	1CH	024	021	Also, there were Isshiah, the leader from the sons of Rehabiah,
013	1CH	024	022	and truly Shelomoth, the son of Izhar, and Jahath, the son of Shelomoth,
013	1CH	024	023	and his son, Jeriah the first, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, Jekameam the fourth.
013	1CH	024	024	The son of Uzziel was Micah. The son of Micah was Shamir.
013	1CH	024	025	The brother of Micah was Isshiah. And the son of Isshiah was Zechariah.
013	1CH	024	026	The sons of Merari were Mahli and Mushi. The son of Uzziah was Beno.
013	1CH	024	027	Also, the son of Merari: Uzziah, and Shoham, and Zaccur, and Hebri.
013	1CH	024	028	In addition, the son of Mahli was Eleazar, who had no children.
013	1CH	024	029	Truly, the son of Kish was Jerahmeel.
013	1CH	024	030	The sons of Mushi were Mahli, Eder, and Jerimoth. These were the sons of Levi according to the houses of their families.
013	1CH	024	031	And they also cast lots concerning their brothers, the sons of Aaron, before David the king, and Zadok, and Ahimelech, and the leaders of the priestly and Levitical families, as much concerning the elder as the younger. The lot divided all things equitably.
013	1CH	025	001	Then David and the magistrates of the army set apart, for the ministry, the sons of Asaph, and of Heman, and of Jeduthun, who were to prophesy with harps and psalteries and cymbals, in accord with their number, having been dedicated to their appointed office.
013	1CH	025	002	From the sons of Asaph: Zaccur, and Joseph, and Nethaniah, and Asharelah, the sons of Asaph, under the hand of Asaph, prophesying beside the king.
013	1CH	025	003	Then of Jeduthun, the sons of Jeduthun: Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah, and Hashabiah, and Mattithiah, six, under the hand of their father Jeduthun, who was prophesying with stringed instruments, while confessing and praising the Lord.
013	1CH	025	004	Also, of Heman, the sons of Heman: Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Uzziel, Shebuel, and Jerimoth, Hananiah, Hanani, Eliathah, Giddalti, and Romamtiezer, and Joshbekashah, Mallothi, Hothir, Mahazioth.
013	1CH	025	005	All these were the sons of Heman, the seer of the king in the words of God, in order to lift up the horn. And God gave to Heman fourteen sons and three daughters.
013	1CH	025	006	All these, under their father’s hand, were distributed in order to sing in the temple of the Lord, with cymbals and psalteries and harps, in the ministry of the house of the Lord beside the king, specifically, Asaph, and Jeduthun, and Heman.
013	1CH	025	007	Now the number of these, with their brothers, who were instructing in the song of the Lord, all the teachers, were two hundred eighty-eight.
013	1CH	025	008	And they cast lots in their turns, the elder equally with the younger, the learned together with the unlearned.
013	1CH	025	009	And the first lot went forth to Joseph, who was of Asaph; the second went forth to Gedaliah, to him and his sons and his brothers, twelve.
013	1CH	025	010	The third went to Zaccur, to his sons and brothers, twelve.
013	1CH	025	011	The fourth went to Izri, to his sons and brothers, twelve.
013	1CH	025	012	The fifth went to Nethaniah, to his sons and brothers, twelve.
013	1CH	025	013	The sixth went to Bukkiah, to his sons and brothers, twelve.
