018	JOB	004	020	From morning all the way to evening, they will be cut down, and because no one understands, they will be destroyed without ceasing.
018	JOB	004	021	But those who are left behind will be taken away from them; they will die, and not in wisdom.
018	JOB	005	001	Therefore call, if there are any who will respond to you, and turn to one or another of the saints.
018	JOB	005	002	Truly, anger condemns the foolish to death, and envy kills the petty.
018	JOB	005	003	I have seen a fool with a strong root, and I have cursed his excellence without hesitation.
018	JOB	005	004	His sons will be far from prosperity and will be crushed at the gate, and there will be none who can rescue them.
018	JOB	005	005	Their harvest, the starving will eat. The armed man will rob him, and the thirsty will drink his resources.
018	JOB	005	006	Nothing on earth occurs without a reason, and sorrow does not rise from the earth.
018	JOB	005	007	Man is born to labor, and the bird to fly.
018	JOB	005	008	Therefore, because of this, I will beg the Lord, and place my eloquence before God.
018	JOB	005	009	He does great and unfathomable and miraculous things without number.
018	JOB	005	010	He gives rain over the face of the earth and irrigates all things with the waters.
018	JOB	005	011	He places the humble on high and encourages the grieving towards health.
018	JOB	005	012	He dispels the thoughts of the spiteful, lest their hands be able to complete what they had begun.
018	JOB	005	013	He catches the wise in their cleverness and dissipates the counsel of the perverse.
018	JOB	005	014	They will encounter darkness in the daytime, and they will grope at midday just as in the night.
018	JOB	005	015	Thereafter, he will act to save the needy from the sword of their mouth, and the poor from the hand of the violent.
018	JOB	005	016	And there will be hope for those in need, for iniquity will diminish its speech.
018	JOB	005	017	Blessed is the man whom God corrects; therefore, do not reject the chastisement of the Lord.
018	JOB	005	018	For he wounds and he cures; he strikes and his hands will heal.
018	JOB	005	019	He will deliver you into six tribulations, and in the seventh, evil will not touch you.
018	JOB	005	020	During famine, he will rescue you from death, and during war, from the hand of the sword.
018	JOB	005	021	You will be hidden from the scourge of the tongue, and you will not fear calamity when it arrives.
018	JOB	005	022	In desolation and in famine, you will laugh, and you will not dread the beasts of the earth.
018	JOB	005	023	For you are in harmony with the stones of the land, and the beasts of the earth will make peace with you.
018	JOB	005	024	And you will know that your home has peace, and, concerning your appearance, you will not sin.
018	JOB	005	025	Likewise, you will know that your offspring will be manifold and your progeny will be like the grass of the earth.
018	JOB	005	026	You will enter the grave with abundance, just as a crop of wheat is gathered in its time.
018	JOB	005	027	Behold, this is just as we have found it, which you have heard; walk it through your mind.
018	JOB	006	001	But Job, responding, said:
018	JOB	006	002	I wish that my sins, for which I deserve wrath, and the calamity that I endure, were weighed out on a balance.
018	JOB	006	003	Compared to the sand of the sea, they would appear heavier, and so my words are full of sorrow.
018	JOB	006	004	For the arrows of the Lord are in me, my spirit drinks of their indignation, and the terrors of the Lord are soldiers against me.
018	JOB	006	005	Will the wild ass bray when he has grass? Or will the ox bellow when he stands before a full manger?
018	JOB	006	006	Or can one eat bland food, which is not seasoned with salt? Or can anyone taste that which, if tasted, causes death?
018	JOB	006	007	The things that my soul was unwilling to touch before, now, because of anguish, are my foods.
018	JOB	006	008	Who will grant that my petition may arrive and that God may bestow on me what I expect,
018	JOB	006	009	and that he who, at first, had crushed me, will let loose his hand and cut me down?
018	JOB	006	010	And may this be my consolation, that in afflicting me with sorrow, although he might not be lenient with me, I still do not contradict the words of the Holy One.
018	JOB	006	011	For what is my strength, that I may continue? Or what is my goal, so that I may act patiently?
018	JOB	006	012	My strength is not the strength of stones, nor is my flesh made of bronze.
018	JOB	006	013	Behold, there is no help for me in myself, and my loved ones also have withdrawn from me.
018	JOB	006	014	He who takes away mercy from his friend, abandons the fear of the Lord.
018	JOB	006	015	My brethren have disregarded me, like a torrent that passes swiftly through the steep valleys.
018	JOB	006	016	Those who fear frost, snow will rush over them.
018	JOB	006	017	At that time, when they are scattered, they will perish, and when it becomes hot, they will be freed from their place.
018	JOB	006	018	The paths of their steps are entangled; they will walk in vain and will perish.
018	JOB	006	019	Consider the paths of Thema, the ways of Saba, and wait a little while.
018	JOB	006	020	They have been thrown into confusion, just as I had hoped; they have even come to me and are overwhelmed with shame.
018	JOB	006	021	Now you have arrived, and merely by seeing my affliction, you are afraid.
018	JOB	006	022	Did I say: “Bring to me and give to me from your necessities?”
018	JOB	006	023	or, “Free me from the hand of the enemy and rescue me from the hand of the strong?”
018	JOB	006	024	Teach me, and I will be silent, and if by chance I have been ignorant of anything, instruct me.
018	JOB	006	025	Why have you diminished the words of truth, when there is none of you who is able to offer proof against me?
018	JOB	006	026	You prepare speeches as so much noise, and you offer words into the wind.
018	JOB	006	027	You encroach upon the orphan, and you strive to undermine your friend.
018	JOB	006	028	Such is true, so finish what you have begun. Listen closely, and see if I lie.
018	JOB	006	029	Respond, I beg you, without contention, and, speaking what is just, pass judgment.
018	JOB	006	030	And you will not find iniquity on my tongue, nor will foolishness resound in my throat.
018	JOB	007	001	The life of a man on the earth is a battle, and his days are like the days of a hired hand.
018	JOB	007	002	Just as a servant desires the shade, and just as the hired hand looks forward to the end of his work,
018	JOB	007	003	so also have I had empty months and have counted my burdensome nights.
018	JOB	007	004	If I lie down to sleep, I will say, “When will I rise?” And next I will hope for the evening and will be filled with sorrows even until darkness.
018	JOB	007	005	My flesh is clothed with particles of rottenness and filth; my skin is dried up and tightened.
018	JOB	007	006	My days have passed by more quickly than threads are cut by a weaver, and they have been consumed without any hope.
018	JOB	007	007	Remember that my life is wind, and my eye will not return to see good things.
018	JOB	007	008	Neither will the sight of man gaze upon me; your eyes are upon me, and I will not endure.
018	JOB	007	009	Just as a cloud is consumed and passes away, so he who descends to hell will not ascend.
018	JOB	007	010	He will not return again to his house, nor will his own place know him any longer.
018	JOB	007	011	And because of this, I will not restrain my mouth. I will speak in the affliction of my spirit. I will converse from the bitterness of my soul.
018	JOB	007	012	Am I an ocean or a whale, that you have encircled me in a prison?
018	JOB	007	013	If I say, “My bed will comfort me, and I will find rest, speaking with myself on my blanket,”
018	JOB	007	014	then you will frighten me with dreams, and strike dread through visions,
018	JOB	007	015	so that, because of these things, my soul would choose hanging, and my bones, death.
018	JOB	007	016	I despair; by no means will I live any longer. Spare me, for my days are nothing.
018	JOB	007	017	What is man, that you should praise him? Or why do you place your heart near him?
018	JOB	007	018	You visit him at dawn, and you test him unexpectedly.
018	JOB	007	019	How long will you not spare me, nor release me to ingest my saliva?
018	JOB	007	020	I have sinned; what should I do for you, O keeper of men? Why have you set me against you, so that I have become burdensome even to myself?
018	JOB	007	021	Why do you not steal away my sin, and why do you not sweep away my iniquity? Behold, now I will sleep in the dust, and if you seek me in the morning, I will not remain.
018	JOB	008	001	But Baldad the Suhite, responding, said:
018	JOB	008	002	How long will you speak this way, so that the words of your mouth are like a changeable wind?
018	JOB	008	003	Does God supplant judgment, or does the Almighty subvert that which is just?
018	JOB	008	004	And if now your children have sinned against him, and he has dismissed them into the power of their iniquity,
018	JOB	008	005	even so, you should arise early to God, so as to beseech the Almighty.
018	JOB	008	006	If you approach with purity and honesty, he will quickly be attentive to you, and a peaceful life will repay your righteousness,
018	JOB	008	007	so much so that, if your former things were small, your latter things would be multiplied greatly.
018	JOB	008	008	For inquire of the earliest generation, and investigate diligently the history of the fathers,
018	JOB	008	009	(of course, we are but of yesterday and are ignorant that our days on earth are like a shadow,)
018	JOB	008	010	and they will teach you; they will speak with you and will offer you the eloquence of their hearts.
018	JOB	008	011	Can the marsh plant live without moisture? Or can sedges grow without water?
018	JOB	008	012	When it is still in flower, and has not been pulled up by hand, it withers before all other plants.
018	JOB	008	013	Just so are the ways of all who forget God, and the hope of the hypocrite will perish.
018	JOB	008	014	His frenzy will not please him, and his faith will be like a spider’s web.
018	JOB	008	015	He will lean on his house, and it will not stand; he will prop it up, but it will not rise.
018	JOB	008	016	He seems to have moisture before the sun arrives; and at sunrise, his sprout shoots forth.
018	JOB	008	017	His roots will crowd together over a heap of stones, and among the stones he will remain.
018	JOB	008	018	If someone is devoured right beside him, he will deny him and will say: “I do not know you.”
018	JOB	008	019	For this is the benefit of his way, that others in turn may spring up from the earth.
018	JOB	008	020	God will not discard the simple, nor will he extend his hand to the spiteful,
018	JOB	008	021	even until your mouth is filled with laughter and your lips with rejoicing.
018	JOB	008	022	Those who hate you, will be clothed with confusion, and the tabernacle of the impious will not continue.
018	JOB	009	001	And Job, responding, said:
018	JOB	009	002	Truly, I know that it is so, and that man cannot be justified compared with God.
018	JOB	009	003	If he chooses to contend with him, he is not able to respond to him once out of a thousand times.
018	JOB	009	004	He is understanding in heart and mighty in strength; who has resisted him and yet had peace?
018	JOB	009	005	He has moved mountains, and those whom he overthrew in his fury did not know it.
018	JOB	009	006	He shakes the earth out of its place and its pillars tremble.
018	JOB	009	007	He commands the sun and it does not rise, and he closes the stars as if under a seal.
018	JOB	009	008	He alone extends the heavens, and he walks upon the waves of the sea.
018	JOB	009	009	He fashions Arcturus, and Orion, and Hyades, and the interior of the south.
018	JOB	009	010	He accomplishes great and incomprehensible and miraculous things, which cannot be numbered.
018	JOB	009	011	If he approaches me, I will not see him; if he departs, I will not understand.
018	JOB	009	012	If he suddenly should question, who will answer him? Or who can say, “Why did you do so?”
018	JOB	009	013	God, whose wrath no one is able to resist, and under whom they bend who carry the world,
018	JOB	009	014	what am I then, that I should answer him and exchange words with him?
018	JOB	009	015	And if I now have any justice, I will not respond, but will beseech my judge.
018	JOB	009	016	And if he should listen to me when I call, I would not believe that he had heard my voice.
018	JOB	009	017	For he will crush me in a whirlwind and multiply my wounds, even without cause.
018	JOB	009	018	He does not permit my spirit to rest, and he fills me with bitterness.
018	JOB	009	019	If strength is sought, he is most strong; if equity in judgment, no one would dare to give testimony for me.
018	JOB	009	020	If I wanted to justify myself, my own mouth will condemn me; if I would reveal my innocence, he would prove me depraved.
018	JOB	009	021	And if I now became simple, my soul would be ignorant even of this, and my life would weary me.
018	JOB	009	022	There is one thing that I have said: both the innocent and the impious he consumes.
018	JOB	009	023	If he scourges, let him kill all at once, and not laugh at the punishment of the innocent.
018	JOB	009	024	Since the earth has been given into the hand of the impious, he covers the face of its judges; for if it is not him, then who is it?
018	JOB	009	025	My days have been swifter than a messenger; they have fled and have not seen goodness.
018	JOB	009	026	They have passed by like ships carrying fruits, just like an eagle flying to food.
018	JOB	009	027	If I say: “By no means will I speak this way.” I change my face and I am tortured with sorrow.
018	JOB	009	028	I have dreaded all my works, knowing that you did not spare the offender.
018	JOB	009	029	Yet, if I am also just as impious, why have I labored in vain?
018	JOB	009	030	If I had been washed with snow-like waters, and my hands were shining like the cleanest thing,
018	JOB	009	031	yet you would plunge me in filth, and my own garments would abhor me.
018	JOB	009	032	For even I would not answer a man who were like myself, nor one who could be heard with me equally in judgment.
018	JOB	009	033	There is no one who could both prevail in argument and in placing his hand between the two.
018	JOB	009	034	Let him take his staff away from me, and let not the fear of him terrify me.
018	JOB	009	035	I will speak and I will not fear him, for in fearfulness I am not able to respond.
018	JOB	010	001	My soul is weary of my life. I will release my words against myself. I will speak in the bitterness of my soul.
018	JOB	010	002	I will say to God: Do not be willing to condemn me. Reveal to me why you judge me this way.
018	JOB	010	003	Does it seem good to you, if you find fault with me and oppress me, the work of your own hands, and assist the counsel of the impious?
018	JOB	010	004	Do you have bodily eyes? Or, just as man sees, will you see?
018	JOB	010	005	Are your days just like the days of man, and are your years as the times of humans,
018	JOB	010	006	so that you would inquire about my iniquity and examine my sin?
018	JOB	010	007	And you know that I have done nothing impious, yet there is no one who can deliver from your hand.
018	JOB	010	008	Your hands have made me and formed me all around, and, in this way, do you suddenly throw me away?
018	JOB	010	009	Remember, I ask you, that you have fashioned me like clay, and you will reduce me to dust.
018	JOB	010	010	Have you not extracted me like milk and curdled me like cheese?
018	JOB	010	011	You have clothed me with skin and flesh. You have put me together with bones and nerves.
018	JOB	010	012	You have assigned to me life and mercy, and your visitation has preserved my spirit.
018	JOB	010	013	Though you may conceal this in your heart, yet I know that you remember everything.
018	JOB	010	014	If I have sinned, and you have spared me for an hour, why do you not endure me to be clean from my iniquity?
018	JOB	010	015	And if I should be impious, woe to me, and if I should be just, I will not lift up my head, being drenched with affliction and misery.
018	JOB	010	016	And because of pride, you will seize me like a lioness, and having returned, you torment me to an extraordinary degree.
018	JOB	010	017	You renew your testimony against me, and you multiply your wrath against me, and these punishments make war within me.
018	JOB	010	018	Why did you lead me out of the womb? If only I had been consumed, so that no eye would ever see me!
018	JOB	010	019	I should have been as if I had not been: transferred from the womb to the tomb.
018	JOB	010	020	Will not my few days be completed soon? Release me, therefore, so that I may lament my sorrows a little,
018	JOB	010	021	before I depart and return no more to a land that is dark and covered with the fog of death,
018	JOB	010	022	a land of misery and darkness, where the shadow of death, and nothing else but everlasting horror, dwells.
018	JOB	011	001	But Zophar the Naamathite, responding, said:
018	JOB	011	002	Will he who speaks much, not also listen? Or will a talkative man be justified?
018	JOB	011	003	Will men be silent only for you? And when you have mocked others, will no one refute you?
018	JOB	011	004	For you said: “My word is pure, and I am clean in your sight.”
018	JOB	011	005	Yet I wish that God would speak with you, and would open his lips to you,
018	JOB	011	006	so that he might reveal to you the secrets of wisdom, and how intricate his law is, and that you would understand how much less he requires of you than your iniquity deserves.
018	JOB	011	007	By chance, will you comprehend the footsteps of God and reach all the way to the perfection of the Almighty?
018	JOB	011	008	He is higher than heaven, and what will you do? He is deeper than hell, but how will you know?
018	JOB	011	009	His measure is longer than the earth and wider than the sea.
018	JOB	011	010	If he overturns all things, or packs them together, who will contradict him?
018	JOB	011	011	For he knows the vanity of men, and when he sees iniquity, does he not evaluate it?
018	JOB	011	012	A vain man is lifted up in arrogance, and he thinks that he is born free like a wild ass’s colt.
018	JOB	011	013	But you have fortified your heart and extended your hands to him.
018	JOB	011	014	If you would send away from you the iniquity that is in your hand, and not let injustice remain in your tabernacle,
018	JOB	011	015	then you would be able to lift up your face without blemish, and you would be steadfast and unafraid.
018	JOB	011	016	Misery, likewise, you would forget, or would remember only like waters that have passed by.
018	JOB	011	017	And brightness, like that of midday, will rise upon you until evening, and when you would think yourself consumed, you will rise up like the morning star.
018	JOB	011	018	And, when hope has been set before you, you will have faith, and, when buried, you will sleep secure.
018	JOB	011	019	You will rest, and there will be nothing to make you afraid, and many will make requests before your face.
018	JOB	011	020	But the eyes of the impious will fade away, and the path to escape will perish before them, for the abomination of the soul is their hope.
018	JOB	012	001	Then Job, answering, said:
018	JOB	012	002	Are you, therefore, alone among men, and will wisdom die with you?
018	JOB	012	003	And I have a heart just as you also do, and I am not inferior to you. For who is ignorant of these things, which you know?
018	JOB	012	004	He who is mocked by his friends as I am, will call upon God, and he will listen to him because it is the sincerity of the just that is being mocked.
018	JOB	012	005	The lamp that is despised in the thoughts of the rich is ready for the appointed time.
018	JOB	012	006	The tabernacles of robbers are numerous, and they provoke God boldly; whereas, it is he who has given all things into their hands.
018	JOB	012	007	In truth, ask the mules, and they will teach you, and the birds of the sky, and they will reveal to you.
018	JOB	012	008	Speak with the earth, and it will respond to you, and the fish of the sea will explain.
018	JOB	012	009	Who is ignorant that the hand of the Lord has made all these things?
018	JOB	012	010	In his hand is the soul of all the living and the spirit of all the flesh of mankind.
018	JOB	012	011	Does not the ear perceive words, and the palate, when eating, perceive flavor?
018	JOB	012	012	In old age is wisdom, and in length of days is prudence.
018	JOB	012	013	With him is wisdom and strength, he has counsel and understanding.
018	JOB	012	014	If he tears down, there is no one who can build up; if he encloses a man, there is no one who can open.
018	JOB	012	015	If he restrains the waters, everything will dry up; and if he sends them forth, they will subdue the land.
018	JOB	012	016	With him is strength and wisdom; he knows both the deceiver and he who is deceived.
018	JOB	012	017	He leads advisors to a foolish end and judges to stupidity.
018	JOB	012	018	He removes the belt of kings and encircles their waist with a rope.
018	JOB	012	019	He leads away priests in dishonor and displaces nobles,
018	JOB	012	020	altering the lips of those who speak the truth and sweeping away the teaching of the aged.
018	JOB	012	021	He pours disdain upon the leaders, relieving those who had been oppressed.
018	JOB	012	022	He reveals the depths of the darkness, and he brings the shadow of death into the light.
018	JOB	012	023	He multiplies peoples, and destroys them, and, having been overthrown, he restores them anew.
018	JOB	012	024	He transforms the heart of the leaders of the people on earth, and misleads those who in vain advance upon the inviolable.
018	JOB	012	025	They will grope as in the darkness, not the light, and he will make them stagger like drunkards.
018	JOB	013	001	Behold, my eye has seen all these things, and my ear has heard, and I have understood each one.
018	JOB	013	002	In conformity with your knowledge, I also know. I am not inferior to you.
018	JOB	013	003	Yet I speak this way to the Almighty, and I desire to argue with God,
018	JOB	013	004	having first shown that you fabricate lies and cultivate perverse teachings.
018	JOB	013	005	And I wish that you would remain silent, so that you would be counted among the wise.
018	JOB	013	006	Therefore, listen to my correction, and pay attention to the judgment of my lips.
018	JOB	013	007	Does God require your lie, so that you would speak deceitfully for him?
018	JOB	013	008	Have you taken his place, and do you struggle to give judgment in favor of God?
018	JOB	013	009	Or, will it please him, from whom nothing can be concealed? Or, will he be deceived, like a man, by your deceitfulness?
018	JOB	013	010	He will accuse you because in secret you have preempted his presence.
018	JOB	013	011	As soon as he moves himself, he will disturb you, and his dread will fall over you.
018	JOB	013	012	Your remembrance will be compared to ashes, and your necks will be reduced to clay.
018	JOB	013	013	Be silent for a little while, so that I may speak whatever my mind suggests to me.
018	JOB	013	014	Why do I wound my flesh with my teeth, and carry my soul in my hands?
018	JOB	013	015	And now, if he would kill me, I will hope in him; in this, truly, I will correct my ways in his sight.
018	JOB	013	016	And he will be my savior, for no hypocrite at all will approach in his sight.
018	JOB	013	017	Listen to my words, and perceive an enigma with your ears.
018	JOB	013	018	If I will be judged, I know that I will be found to be just.
018	JOB	013	019	Who is it that will go to judgment with me? Let him approach. Why should I be consumed in silence?
018	JOB	013	020	Do not do such things to me twice, and then I will not hide from your face.
018	JOB	013	021	Take your hand far away from me, and do not let your dread terrify me.
018	JOB	013	022	Call me, and I will answer you, or else I will speak, and you can answer me.
018	JOB	013	023	How many iniquities and sins do I have? Reveal my crimes and offenses to me.
018	JOB	013	024	Why do you conceal your face and consider me to be your enemy?
018	JOB	013	025	Against a leaf, which is carried away by the wind, you reveal your power, and you pursue dry straw.
018	JOB	013	026	For you write bitter things against me, and you want to consume me for the sins of my youth.
018	JOB	013	027	You have put my feet on a tether, and you have observed all my paths, and you have considered the steps of my feet.
018	JOB	013	028	I will be left to decay like something rotten and like a garment that is being eaten by moths.
018	JOB	014	001	Man, born of woman, living for a short time, is filled with many miseries.
018	JOB	014	002	He comes forth like a flower, and is crushed, and he flees, as if a shadow, and never remains in the same state.
018	JOB	014	003	And do you consider it fitting to look down with your eyes on someone in this way and to lead him into judgment with you?
018	JOB	014	004	Who can make him clean who is conceived of unclean seed? Are you not the only one who can?
018	JOB	014	005	The days of man are short, and the number of his months is with you; you have determined his limits, which cannot be surpassed.
018	JOB	014	006	Withdraw a little from him, so that he may rest, until his awaited day arrives, like that of the hired hand.
018	JOB	014	007	A tree has hope: if it has been cut, it turns green again, and its branches spring forth.
018	JOB	014	008	If its roots grow old in the earth, and its trunk passes into dust,
018	JOB	014	009	at the scent of water, it will sprout and bring forth leaves, as when it had first been planted.
018	JOB	014	010	Truly, when a man dies, and has been left unprotected, and has decayed, I ask you where is he?
018	JOB	014	011	It is as if the waters had receded from the sea and an emptied river had dried up;
018	JOB	014	012	just so, when a man is fallen asleep, he will not rise again, until the heavens are worn away; he will not awaken, nor rise from his sleep.
018	JOB	014	013	Who will grant this to me, that you will protect me in the underworld, and hide me until your fury passes by, and establish a time for me, in which you will remember me?
018	JOB	014	014	Do you suppose that a dead man will live again? On each of the days in which I now battle, I wait until my transformation occurs.
018	JOB	014	015	You will call me and I will answer you; to the work of your hands, you will extend your right hand.
018	JOB	014	016	Indeed, you have numbered my steps, but you have been lenient with my sins.
018	JOB	014	017	You have sealed up my offenses, as if in a purse, but you have cured my iniquity.
018	JOB	014	018	A falling mountain flows away, and a stone is transferred from its place.
018	JOB	014	019	Waters wear away stones, and with a flood the land is reduced little by little; and similarly, you will destroy man.
018	JOB	014	020	You have strengthened him for a little while, so that he may cross over into eternity. You will change his face and send him forth.
018	JOB	014	021	Whether his sons have been noble or ignoble, he will not understand.
018	JOB	014	022	And in this way his body, while he yet lives, will have grief, and his soul will mourn over himself.
018	JOB	015	001	But Eliphaz the Themanite, answering, said:
018	JOB	015	002	Will a wise man answer as if he were speaking wind, and will he fill his stomach with fire?
018	JOB	015	003	You rebuke with words he who is not equal to you, and you speak what is not expedient for you,
018	JOB	015	004	to such an extent that, within yourself, you have expelled reverence and have taken away prayers from the presence of God.
018	JOB	015	005	For your iniquity has mislead your mouth, and you imitate the tongue of blasphemers.
018	JOB	015	006	Your own mouth will condemn you, not I; and your own lips will answer you.
018	JOB	015	007	Are you the first man who was born, or were you formed before the hills?
018	JOB	015	008	Have you heard the intentions of God, and will his wisdom be inferior to you?
018	JOB	015	009	What do you know, about which we are ignorant? What do you understand that we do not know?
018	JOB	015	010	There are with us both aged and ancient men, even more senior than your fathers.
018	JOB	015	011	Is it so important that God should console you? But your own depraved words prevent this.
018	JOB	015	012	Why does your heart exalt you, and why do you gaze with your eyes, as if thinking great things?
018	JOB	015	013	Why does your spirit stir against God, so as to utter such speeches from your mouth?
018	JOB	015	014	What is man that he should be immaculate, and that he should appear just, having been born of woman?
018	JOB	015	015	Behold, among his holy ones not one is immutable, and even the heavens are not pure in his sight.
018	JOB	015	016	How much more abominable and useless is the man who drinks as if from the water of iniquity?
018	JOB	015	017	I will reveal to you, so listen to me; and I will explain to you what I have seen.
018	JOB	015	018	The wise acknowledge, and they do not leave behind, their fathers,
018	JOB	015	019	to whom alone the earth has been given, and no stranger passed among them.
018	JOB	015	020	The impious is arrogant for all his days, and the number of the years of his tyranny is uncertain.
018	JOB	015	021	The sound of terror is always in his ears; and when there is peace, he always suspects treason.
018	JOB	015	022	He does not believe that it is possible for him to be turned from darkness into the light, for he sees around him the sword on every side.
018	JOB	015	023	When he moves himself to seek bread, he knows that the day of darkness has been prepared for his hand.
018	JOB	015	024	Tribulation will terrify him, and anguish will prevail over him, like a king who is being prepared to go to battle.
018	JOB	015	025	For he has extended his hand against God, and he has strengthened himself against the Almighty.
018	JOB	015	026	He has rushed against him with his throat exposed, and he has been armed with a fat neck.
018	JOB	015	027	Thickness has covered his face, and lard hangs down from his sides.
018	JOB	015	028	He has lived in desolate cities and deserted houses, which have been turned into tombs.
018	JOB	015	029	He will not be enriched, nor will his basic necessities endure, nor will he establish his root in the earth.
018	JOB	015	030	He will not withdraw from the darkness; the flame will burn up his branches, and he will be defeated by the breath of his own mouth.
018	JOB	015	031	He will not believe, being vainly deceived by error, that he could be redeemed at any price.
018	JOB	015	032	Before his time is completed, he will pass into ruin and his hands will wither away.
018	JOB	015	033	He will be wounded like a grapevine, when its cluster is in first flower, and like an olive tree that casts off its flower.
018	JOB	015	034	For the congregation of the hypocrites is fruitless, and fire will devour the tabernacles of those who love to accept money.
018	JOB	015	035	He has conceived sorrow, and he has brought forth iniquity, and his womb prepares deceit.
018	JOB	016	001	Then Job, answering, said:
018	JOB	016	002	I have often heard such things; you are all aggravating comforters.
018	JOB	016	003	Will there be no end to windy words? Or is it at all a burden to you, if you speak?
018	JOB	016	004	I, too, can speak like you; and I also wish that your soul favored my soul. I would also comfort you with speeches and would wag my head over you.
018	JOB	016	005	I would strengthen you with my mouth, and would move my lips, as if being lenient to you.
018	JOB	016	006	But what can I do? When I am speaking, my grief will not be quiet; and if I am quiet, it will not withdraw from me.
018	JOB	016	007	But now my grief has crushed me, and all my limbs have been reduced to nothing.
018	JOB	016	008	My wrinkles bear witness against me, and a liar rises up against my face, contradicting me.
018	JOB	016	009	He has gathered together his fury towards me, and, threatening me, he has roared against me with his teeth; my enemy has beheld me with terrible eyes.
018	JOB	016	010	They have opened their mouths against me, and, reproaching me, they have struck me on the cheek; they are nourished by my sufferings.
018	JOB	016	011	God has confined me with the immoral, and he has delivered me into the hands of the impious.
018	JOB	016	012	I, who once was wealthy, am now crushed. He has grabbed me by my neck; he has broken me and has placed me before him as a sign.
018	JOB	016	013	He has surrounded me with his lances. He has severely wounded my lower back, he has not been lenient, and he has poured out my organs upon the earth.
018	JOB	016	014	He has cut me with wound after wound. He has rushed upon me like a giant.
018	JOB	016	015	I have sewn sackcloth over my skin, and I have covered my body with ashes.
018	JOB	016	016	My face is swollen from weeping, and my eyelids have dimmed my vision.
018	JOB	016	017	These things I have endured without iniquity in my hand, while I held pure prayers before God.
018	JOB	016	018	O earth, do not conceal my blood, nor let my outcry find a hiding place in you.
018	JOB	016	019	For behold, my witness is in heaven, and my confidante is on high.
018	JOB	016	020	My friends are full of words; my eye rains tears upon God.
018	JOB	016	021	And I wish that a man might be so judged before God, just as the son of man is judged with his assistant!
018	JOB	016	022	For behold, a few years pass by, and I am walking a path by which I will not return.
018	JOB	017	001	My spirit will be wasted, my days will be shortened, and only the grave will be left for me.
018	JOB	017	002	I have not sinned, yet my eye remains in bitterness.
018	JOB	017	003	Free me, O Lord, and set me beside you, and let the hand of anyone you wish fight against me.
018	JOB	017	004	You have set their heart far from discipline; therefore, they will not be praised.
018	JOB	017	005	He promises prey to his companions, but the eyes of his sons will grow faint.
018	JOB	017	006	He has posted me like a proverb to the people, and I am an example in their presence.
018	JOB	017	007	My eyesight has been clouded by indignation, and my limbs have been reduced, as if to nothing.
018	JOB	017	008	The just will be astounded over this, and the innocent will be stirred up against the hypocrite.
018	JOB	017	009	And the just will cling to his way, and clean hands will increase strength.
018	JOB	017	010	Therefore, be converted, all of you, and approach, for I do not find in you any wisdom.
018	JOB	017	011	My days have passed away; my thoughts have been scattered, tormenting my heart.
018	JOB	017	012	They have turned night into day, and I hope for light again after the darkness.
018	JOB	017	013	If I should wait, the underworld is my house, and in darkness I have spread out my bed.
018	JOB	017	014	I have said to decay and to worms: “You are my father, my mother, and my sister.”
018	JOB	017	015	Therefore, where is my expectation now, and who is it that considers my patience?
018	JOB	017	016	Everything of mine will descend into the deepest underworld; do you think that, in that place at least, there will be rest for me?
018	JOB	018	001	But Baldad the Suhite responded by saying:
018	JOB	018	002	How long will you throw around words? Understand first, and then let us speak.
018	JOB	018	003	Why have we been treated like mules, as if we were unworthy before you?
018	JOB	018	004	You, who ruins your own soul in your fury, will the earth be forsaken because of you, and will the cliffs be moved from their place?
018	JOB	018	005	Will not the light of the impious be put out, and the flame of his fire refuse to shine?
018	JOB	018	006	Light will become darkness in his tabernacle, and the lamp that is over him will be extinguished.
018	JOB	018	007	His strong steps will be constrained, and his own counsel will cast him down uncontrollably.
018	JOB	018	008	For he has caused his own feet to go into a net, and he has walked into its web.
018	JOB	018	009	His heel will be held in a snare, and thirst will rage against him.
018	JOB	018	010	A trap has been hidden for him in the earth, and a decoy, along his path.
018	JOB	018	011	Horrifying things will terrify him everywhere and will entangle his feet.
018	JOB	018	012	Let his strength be diminished by famine, and let starvation invade his ribs.
018	JOB	018	013	Let it devour the beauty of his skin; let the ancient death consume his arms.
018	JOB	018	014	Let his confidence be torn away from his tabernacle, and let ruin trample over him like a king.
018	JOB	018	015	Let the companions of he who is not, dwell in his tabernacle; let brimstone rain down upon his tabernacle.
018	JOB	018	016	Let his roots be dried up from beneath him, and his harvest be crushed from above.
018	JOB	018	017	Let the memory of him perish from the earth, and let not his name be celebrated in the streets.
018	JOB	018	018	He will expel him from light into darkness, and he will remove him from the world.
018	JOB	018	019	Neither his offspring, nor his descendants, will exist among his people, nor will there be any remnants in his country.
018	JOB	018	020	The last will be astonished at his day, and the first will be overcome with horror.
018	JOB	018	021	And so, these are the tabernacles of the sinful, and this the place of he who does not know God.
018	JOB	019	001	But Job answered by saying:
018	JOB	019	002	How long will you afflict my soul and wear me down with words?
018	JOB	019	003	So, ten times you confound me and are not ashamed to oppress me.
018	JOB	019	004	Now, of course, if I have been ignorant, my ignorance will be with me.
018	JOB	019	005	But you have risen up against me, and you accuse me to my disgrace.
018	JOB	019	006	At least now you should understand that God has not afflicted me with a balanced judgment, though he has encompassed me with his scourges.
018	JOB	019	007	Behold, I will cry out, enduring violence, and no one will hear. I will announce loudly, but there is no one who may judge.
018	JOB	019	008	He has hemmed in my path, and I cannot pass; he has added darkness to my difficult path.
018	JOB	019	009	He has plundered me of my glory, and he has stolen the crown from my head.
018	JOB	019	010	He has destroyed me on every side, and I am lost, and, like an uprooted tree, he has taken away my hope.
018	JOB	019	011	His fury has raged against me, and in this way he has treated me like his enemy.
018	JOB	019	012	His troops have gathered together, and they have made their way to me, and they have besieged my tabernacle all around.
018	JOB	019	013	He has put my brothers far from me, and my friends have withdrawn from me like strangers.
018	JOB	019	014	My kinsmen have forsaken me, and those who knew me, have forgotten me.
018	JOB	019	015	The inhabitants of my house and my maidservants treat me just as if I were a stranger, and I have been like a sojourner in their eyes.
018	JOB	019	016	I called my servant, and he did not respond; I pleaded with him with my own mouth.
018	JOB	019	017	My wife has shuddered at my breath, and I have begged the sons of my loins.
018	JOB	019	018	Even the foolish have looked down on me, and, when I withdrew from them, they spoke ill of me.
018	JOB	019	019	Those who were sometimes my counselors, treat me like an abomination; and he whom I valued the most has turned against me.
018	JOB	019	020	Since my flesh has been consumed, my bone adheres to my skin, and only my lips have been left around my teeth.
018	JOB	019	021	Have mercy on me, have compassion on me, at least you my friends, because the hand of the Lord has touched me.
018	JOB	019	022	Why do you pursue me just as God does, and satiate yourselves with my flesh?
018	JOB	019	023	Who will grant to me that my words may be written down? Who will grant to me that they may be inscribed in a book,
018	JOB	019	024	with an iron pen and a plate of lead, or else be carved in stone?
018	JOB	019	025	For I know that my Redeemer lives, and on the last day I will rise out of the earth.
018	JOB	019	026	And I will be enveloped again with my skin, and in my flesh I will see my God.
018	JOB	019	027	It is he whom I myself will see, and he whom my eyes will behold, and no other. This, my hope, has taken rest in my bosom.
018	JOB	019	028	Why then do you now say: “Let us pursue him, and let us find a basis to speak against him?”
018	JOB	019	029	So then, flee from the face of the sword, for the sword is the avenger of iniquities; but know this: there is to be a judgment.
018	JOB	020	001	Then Zophar the Naamathite answered by saying:
018	JOB	020	002	In response, various thoughts succeed one another in me, and my mind moves quickly through different ideas.
018	JOB	020	003	The teaching you use to admonish me, I will hear, and the spirit of my understanding will respond for me.
018	JOB	020	004	This, I know, is from the beginning, from the time that man was set over the earth:
018	JOB	020	005	that the praise of the impious shall be short, and the joy of the hypocrite lasts only a moment.
018	JOB	020	006	If his pride ascends even towards the heavens, and his head touches the clouds,
018	JOB	020	007	in the end, he will be destroyed like a trash heap, and those who had seen him will say: “Where is he?”
018	JOB	020	008	Like a dream that flies away, he will not be found; he will pass away like a nightmare.
018	JOB	020	009	The eyes that had seen him, will not see him; no longer will his own place admire him.
018	JOB	020	010	His sons will be worn away by poverty, and his own hands will deliver his grief to him.
018	JOB	020	011	His bones will be filled with the vices of his youth, and they will sleep with him in the dust.
018	JOB	020	012	For, when evil will be sweet in his mouth, he will hide it under his tongue.
018	JOB	020	013	He will permit it, and not abandon it, and he will conceal it in his throat.
018	JOB	020	014	His bread in his belly will be turned into the venom of snakes within him.
018	JOB	020	015	The riches that he devours, he will vomit up, and from his stomach God will draw them out.
018	JOB	020	016	He will suck the head of snakes, and the tongue of the viper will kill him.
018	JOB	020	017	(May he never see the streams of the river, the torrents of honey and butter.)
018	JOB	020	018	He will be repaid for all he has done, yet he will not be consumed; according to the multitude of his schemes, so also will he suffer.
018	JOB	020	019	For, having broken in, he stripped the poor. He has quickly stolen away a house he did not build.
018	JOB	020	020	And yet his stomach will not be satisfied, and when he has the things he desires, he will not be able to possess them.
018	JOB	020	021	Nothing remained of his portion, and, because of this, nothing will continue of his kind.
018	JOB	020	022	When he will be satisfied, he will be constrained; he will seethe, and all anguish will fall upon him.
018	JOB	020	023	May his stomach be filled, so that God may send forth the fury of his wrath to him and may rain down his battle upon him.
018	JOB	020	024	He will flee from weapons of iron, and he will fall in an arc of brass,
018	JOB	020	025	which had been drawn and had issued forth from its sheath, glittering in its bitterness: the horrible ones will go forth and approach over him.
018	JOB	020	026	All darkness has been hidden in his secrecy. A fire that has not been set will devour him; he will be thrown down and forsaken in his tabernacle.
018	JOB	020	027	The heavens will reveal his sinfulness, and the earth will rise up against him.
018	JOB	020	028	The offspring of his house will be exposed; he will be pulled down in the day of God’s wrath.
018	JOB	020	029	This is the portion of a wicked man from God, and the inheritance of his words from the Lord.
018	JOB	021	001	Then Job responded by saying:
018	JOB	021	002	I beseech you to hear my words and to do penance.
018	JOB	021	003	Permit me, and I will speak, and afterwards, if you see fit, you can laugh at my words.
018	JOB	021	004	Is my dispute against man, so that I would have no reason to be discouraged?
018	JOB	021	005	Listen to me and be astonished, and place a finger over your mouth.
018	JOB	021	006	As for me, when I think it over, I am afraid, and trembling convulses my body.
018	JOB	021	007	Why then do the impious live, having been lifted up and strengthened with riches?
018	JOB	021	008	They see their offspring continue before them: a commotion of close relatives and of children’s children in their sight.
018	JOB	021	009	Their houses have been secure and peaceable, and there is no staff of God over them.
018	JOB	021	010	Their cattle have conceived and have not miscarried; their cow has given birth and is not deprived of her newborn.
018	JOB	021	011	Their little ones go out like a flock, and their children jump around playfully.
018	JOB	021	012	They take up the timbrel and the lyre, and they rejoice at the sound of the organ.
018	JOB	021	013	Their days are prolonged in wealth, yet, in an instant, they descend into hell.
018	JOB	021	014	Who has said to God, “Depart from us, for we do not want the knowledge of your ways.
018	JOB	021	015	Who is the Almighty that we should serve him? And how is it helpful to us if we pray to him?”
018	JOB	021	016	It is true that their good things are not in their power. May the counsel of the impious be far from me!
018	JOB	021	017	How often will the lamp of the wicked be extinguished, and a deluge overtake them, and how often will he distribute the afflictions of his wrath?
018	JOB	021	018	They will be like chaff before the face of the wind, and like ashes that the whirlwind scatters.
018	JOB	021	019	God will preserve the grief of the father for his sons, and, when he repays, then he will understand.
018	JOB	021	020	His eyes will see his own destruction, and he will drink from the wrath of the Almighty.
018	JOB	021	021	For what does he care what happens to his house after him, or if the number of its months are reduced by half?
018	JOB	021	022	Can anyone teach holy knowledge to God, who judges the exalted?
018	JOB	021	023	This one dies strong and healthy, rich and happy.
018	JOB	021	024	His gut is full of fat and his bones are moistened with marrow.
018	JOB	021	025	In truth, another dies in bitterness of soul, without any resources.
018	JOB	021	026	And yet they will sleep together in the dust, and worms will cover them.
018	JOB	021	027	Surely, I know your thoughts and your sinful judgments against me.
018	JOB	021	028	For you say, “Where is the house of the ruler, and where are the tabernacles of the impious?”
018	JOB	021	029	Ask any passerby whom you wish, and you will realize that he understands these same things:
018	JOB	021	030	that the evil-doer is reserved for the day of destruction, and he will be led to the day of wrath.
018	JOB	021	031	Who will reprove his way to his face, and who will repay him for what he has done?
018	JOB	021	032	He will be led to the tomb, and he will remain awake in the chaos of the dead.
018	JOB	021	033	He has been found acceptable to the banks of the River of Lamentation, and he will draw any man towards him, and there are countless before him.
018	JOB	021	034	Therefore, how long will you console me in vain, when your answer is shown to be repugnant to truth?
018	JOB	022	001	Then Eliphaz the Themanite responded by saying:
018	JOB	022	002	Can man be compared with God, even if he were perfect in knowledge?
018	JOB	022	003	What advantage is it to God, if you were just? Or what do you provide for him, if your way should be immaculate?
018	JOB	022	004	Will he reprove you and take you to judgment for being afraid,
018	JOB	022	005	and not because of your many evil deeds and your infinite unfairness?
018	JOB	022	006	For you have taken away the collateral of your brothers without cause, and stripped them naked of their clothing.
018	JOB	022	007	You have not given water to the weary; you have taken bread away from the hungry.
018	JOB	022	008	By the strength of your arm, you took possession of the land, and you retain it by being the strongest.
018	JOB	022	009	You have sent widows away empty, and you have crushed the shoulders of orphans.
018	JOB	022	010	Because of this, you are surrounded by traps, and unexpected fears will disturb you.
018	JOB	022	011	And did you think that you would not see darkness and that you were not to be overwhelmed by the onrush of overflowing waters?
018	JOB	022	012	Have you not considered that God is higher than the heavens and is lifted above the height of the stars?
018	JOB	022	013	And you say: “Well, what does God know?” and, “He judges, as if through a fog,”
018	JOB	022	014	and, “The clouds are his hiding-place,” and, “He does not examine us closely,” and, “He makes his rounds at the limits of the heavens.”
018	JOB	022	015	Do you not want to tend the path of the ages, which wicked men have spurned?
018	JOB	022	016	These were taken away before their time, and a flood overthrew their foundation.
018	JOB	022	017	They said to God, “Withdraw from us,” and they treated the Almighty as if he could do nothing,
018	JOB	022	018	though he had filled their houses with good things. May their way of thinking be far from me.
018	JOB	022	019	The just will see and will rejoice, and the innocent will mock them.
018	JOB	022	020	Has not their haughtiness been cut down, and has not fire devoured the remnants of them?
018	JOB	022	021	So, repose yourself with him and be at peace, and, in this way, you will have the best fruits.
018	JOB	022	022	Accept the law from his mouth, and place his words in your heart.
018	JOB	022	023	If you will return to the Almighty, you will be rebuilt, and you will put sinfulness far from your tabernacle.
018	JOB	022	024	He will give you stone in place of dirt, and torrents of gold in place of stone.
018	JOB	022	025	And the Almighty will be against your enemies, and silver will be gathered together for you.
018	JOB	022	026	Then will you flock together in delight over the Almighty, and you will lift up your face to God.
018	JOB	022	027	You will plead with him, and he will listen to you, and you will pay your vows.
018	JOB	022	028	You will decide on something, and it will come to you, and the light will shine in your ways.
018	JOB	022	029	For he who had been humbled, will be in glory; and he who will lower his eyes, will be the one saved.
018	JOB	022	030	The innocent will be saved, and he will be saved with purity in his hands.
018	JOB	023	001	Then Job answered by saying:
018	JOB	023	002	Now again my conversation is in bitterness, and the force of my scourging weighs more heavily on me because of my mourning.
018	JOB	023	003	Who will grant me that I might know and find him, and that I may approach even to his throne?
018	JOB	023	004	I would place judgment before his eye, and my mouth would fill with criticism,
018	JOB	023	005	so that I may know the words that he will answer me and understand what he will say to me.
018	JOB	023	006	I do not want him to contend with me with much strength, nor to overwhelm me with the bulk of his greatness.
018	JOB	023	007	Let him show fairness in response to me, and let my judgment reach to victory.
018	JOB	023	008	If I go to the east, he does not appear; if I go to the west, I will not understand him.
018	JOB	023	009	If I turn to the left, what can I do? I will not take hold of him. If I turn myself to the right, I will not see him.
018	JOB	023	010	Truly, he knows my way and has tested me like gold that passes through fire.
018	JOB	023	011	My feet have been following his footsteps; I have kept to his way and have not strayed from it.
018	JOB	023	012	I have not withdrawn from the commands of his lips, and the words of his mouth I have hidden in my sinews.
018	JOB	023	013	For he is alone, and no one is able to disturb his intention; and whatever his spirit wills, that he accomplishes.
018	JOB	023	014	And when he fulfills his will in me, many other similar ones will also be present with him.
018	JOB	023	015	And, for this reason, I have been troubled at his presence, and, when I consider him, I am approached by fear.
018	JOB	023	016	God has weakened my heart, and the Almighty has confused me.
018	JOB	023	017	Yet I have not perished because of the threatening darkness, nor has gloom covered my face.
018	JOB	024	001	The times are not hidden from the Almighty; even those who know him, do not know his days.
018	JOB	024	002	Some have crossed the boundaries, plundered the flocks, and given them pasture.
018	JOB	024	003	They have driven away the donkey of orphans, and have taken the cow from the widow as collateral.
018	JOB	024	004	They have undermined the way of the poor, and have pressed together the meek of the earth.
018	JOB	024	005	Others, like wild asses in the desert, go forth to their work; by watching for prey, they obtain bread for their children.
018	JOB	024	006	They reap a field that is not their own, and they harvest a vineyard that they have taken by force.
018	JOB	024	007	They send men away naked, having taken the clothing of those who have no covering in the cold;
018	JOB	024	008	these are wet with the mountain rain, and, having no covering, they embrace the rocks.
018	JOB	024	009	They have used violence to deprive orphans, and they have robbed the poor common people.
018	JOB	024	010	From the naked and those who do not have enough clothing, and from the hungry, they have taken away sheaves of grain.
018	JOB	024	011	They take their midday rest among the stockpiles of those who, though they have trodden the winepresses, suffer thirst.
018	JOB	024	012	In the cities, they caused the men to groan and the spirit of the wounded to cry out, and so God does not allow this to go unpunished.
018	JOB	024	013	They have been rebellious against the light; they have not known his ways, nor have they returned by his paths.
