018	JOB	024	025	But, if this is not so, who is able to prove to me that I have lied and to place my words before God?
018	JOB	025	001	Then Baldad the Suhite answered by saying:
018	JOB	025	002	Power and terror are with him that makes a pact with those in high places.
018	JOB	025	003	Is there any limit to the number of his soldiers or to the number of those over whom his light rises?
018	JOB	025	004	Is it right for man to compare himself to God, or to appear pure though he is born of woman?
018	JOB	025	005	Behold, even the moon is not radiant, and the stars are not pure, in his sight.
