018	JOB	026	001	Then Job responded by saying:
018	JOB	026	002	Whose assistant are you? Is he weak-minded? And do you sustain the arm of him that is not strong?
018	JOB	026	003	To whom have you given advice? Perhaps it is to him that has no wisdom or prudence that you have revealed your many ideas.
018	JOB	026	004	Who is it that you wanted to teach? Was it not him that created the breath of life?
018	JOB	026	005	Behold, giant things groan under the waters, and they dwell with them.
018	JOB	026	006	The underworld is naked before him, and there is no covering for perdition.
018	JOB	026	007	He stretched out the North over emptiness, and he suspended the land over nothing.
018	JOB	026	008	He secures the waters in his clouds, so that they do not burst forth downward all at once.
018	JOB	026	009	He holds back the face of his throne, and he stretches his cloud over it.
018	JOB	026	010	He has set limits around the waters, until light and darkness shall reach their limit.
018	JOB	026	011	The pillars of heaven tremble and are frightened at his nod.
018	JOB	026	012	By his strength, the seas suddenly gather together, and his foresight has struck the arrogant.
018	JOB	026	013	His spirit has adorned the heavens, and his birthing hand has brought forth the winding serpent.
018	JOB	026	014	Behold, these things have been said about his ways in part, and, since we barely have heard a small drop of his word, who will be able to gaze upon the thunder of his greatness?
018	JOB	027	001	Job also added to this, using figures of speech, and he said:
018	JOB	027	002	As God lives, who has taken away my judgment, and the Almighty, who has led my soul to bitterness,
