018	JOB	028	011	The depths of rivers he has also examined, and he has brought hidden things into the light.
018	JOB	028	012	But, in truth, where is wisdom to be found, and where is the place of understanding?
018	JOB	028	013	Man does not know its price, nor is it found in the land of those who live in sweetness.
018	JOB	028	014	The abyss declares, “It is not in me.” And the sea says, “It is not with me.”
018	JOB	028	015	The finest gold will not be paid for it, nor will silver be weighed in exchange for it.
018	JOB	028	016	It will not be compared with the dyed colors of India, nor with the very costly stone sardonyx, nor with the sapphire.
018	JOB	028	017	Neither gold nor crystal will be its equal; neither will vessels of gold be fitted for it.
018	JOB	028	018	The exalted and the eminent will not be remembered in comparison with it. Yet wisdom is drawn out of concealment.
018	JOB	028	019	The topaz of Ethiopia will not be equal to it, nor will it be compared to the purest dyes.
