018	JOB	031	026	if I gazed upon the sun when it shined and the moon advancing brightly,
018	JOB	031	027	so that my heart rejoiced in secret and I kissed my hand with my mouth,
018	JOB	031	028	which is a very great iniquity and a denial against the most high God;
018	JOB	031	029	if I have been glad at the ruin of him who hated me and have exulted that evil found him,
018	JOB	031	030	for I have not been given my throat to sin by asking for a curse on his soul;
018	JOB	031	031	if the men around my tabernacle have not said: “He might give us some of his food, so that we will be filled,”
