018	JOB	034	012	For truly, God will not condemn in vain, nor will the Almighty repudiate judgment.
018	JOB	034	013	What other is established over the earth? Or whom has he placed over the world, which he made?
018	JOB	034	014	But, if he directs his heart towards him, he will draw his spirit and breath to himself.
018	JOB	034	015	All flesh will fail together, and man will return to ashes.
018	JOB	034	016	Therefore, if you have understanding, hear what is said, and heed the sound of my eloquence.
018	JOB	034	017	Is he that does not love judgment able to be corrected? And how can you so greatly condemn him who is just?
018	JOB	034	018	He says to the king, “You are an apostate.” He calls commanders impious.
018	JOB	034	019	He does not accept the reputation of leaders; nor does he recognize the tyrant as he contends against the poor. For all are the work of his hands.
018	JOB	034	020	They will die suddenly, and the people will be troubled in the middle of the night, but they will pass through it, and the violent will be taken away without a hand.
018	JOB	034	021	For his eyes are upon the ways of men, and he examines all of their steps.
018	JOB	034	022	There is no darkness and no shadow of death, where those who work iniquity may be hidden.
018	JOB	034	023	For it is no longer within the power of man to enter into judgment with God.
018	JOB	034	024	He will break into many innumerable pieces, and he will cause others to stand up in their place.
018	JOB	034	025	For he knows their works, and, as a result, he will bring the night, and they will be crushed.
018	JOB	034	026	Just as the impious do, he has struck them in a place where they can be seen.
018	JOB	034	027	They, as if with great diligence, have withdrawn from him, and they refused to understand all his ways,
018	JOB	034	028	so that they caused the outcry of the needy to reach him, and he heard the voice of the poor.
018	JOB	034	029	For, when he grants peace, who is there that can condemn? When he hides his face, who is there that can contemplate him, either among the nations, or among all men?
018	JOB	034	030	He causes a hypocritical man to reign because of the sins of the people.
018	JOB	034	031	Therefore, since I have been speaking about God, I will not prevent you from doing the same.
018	JOB	034	032	If I have erred, you may teach me; if I have spoken unfairly, I will add no more.
018	JOB	034	033	Does God require this of you because it is displeasing to you? For you were the first to speak, and not I. But if you know something better, speak.
018	JOB	034	034	Let men of understanding speak to me, and let a wise man listen to me.
018	JOB	034	035	But Job has been speaking foolishly, and his words contain unsound teaching.
018	JOB	034	036	My father, let Job be tested even to the end; may you not retreat from a man of iniquity.
018	JOB	034	037	For he adds blasphemy on top of his sins; nevertheless, let him be constrained to be among us, and then let him provoke God to judgment with his speeches.
018	JOB	035	001	After this, Eliu again spoke in this way:
018	JOB	035	002	Does it seem right to you in your thoughts, that you should say, “I am more just than God?”
018	JOB	035	003	For you said, “Having done what is right does not please you,” and, “How will it benefit you, if I sin?”
018	JOB	035	004	And so, I will respond to your words, and to your friends who are with you.
018	JOB	035	005	Look up towards heaven and consider; also, think about the sky, which is higher than you.
018	JOB	035	006	If you sin, how will it hurt him? And if your iniquities are multiplied, what will you do against him?
018	JOB	035	007	Furthermore, if you act justly, what will you give him, or what will he receive from your hand?
018	JOB	035	008	Your impiety may hurt a man who is like you, though your justice may help the son of the man.
018	JOB	035	009	Because of the multitude of false accusers, they will cry out; and they will lament because of the strong arm of the tyrants.
018	JOB	035	010	Yet he has not said: “Where is God, who made me, who has given songs in the night,
018	JOB	035	011	who teaches us in addition to the beasts of the earth, and who educates us along with the birds of the air?”
018	JOB	035	012	There they will cry, and he will not heed them, because of the arrogance of the wicked.
018	JOB	035	013	Therefore, God does not hear in vain, and the Almighty will look into each and every case.
018	JOB	035	014	And so, when you say, “He does not examine,” be judged before him, but wait for him.
018	JOB	035	015	For, at the present time, he does not bring forth his fury, nor does he punish sin exceedingly.
018	JOB	035	016	Therefore, Job has opened his mouth in vain and has multiplied words without knowledge.
018	JOB	036	001	Continuing in a similar manner, Eliu had this to say:
018	JOB	036	002	Bear with me for a little while and I will show you; for I have still more to say in favor of God.
018	JOB	036	003	I will review my knowledge from the beginning, and I will prove my Maker to be just.
018	JOB	036	004	For truly my words are without any falsehood and perfect knowledge will be proven to you.
018	JOB	036	005	God does not abandon the powerful, for he himself is also powerful.
018	JOB	036	006	But he does not save the impious, though he grants judgment to the poor.
018	JOB	036	007	He will not take his eyes away from the just, and he continually establishes kings on their throne, and they are exalted.
018	JOB	036	008	And, if they are in captivity, or are bound with the chains of poverty,
018	JOB	036	009	he will reveal to them their works, as well as their sinfulness, in that they were violent.
018	JOB	036	010	Likewise, he will open their ears to his correction, and he will speak to them, so that they may return from iniquity.
018	JOB	036	011	If they listen and obey, they will fill their days with goodness and complete their years in glory.
018	JOB	036	012	But if they will not listen, they will pass away by the sword and will be consumed by foolishness.
018	JOB	036	013	The false and the crafty provoke the wrath of God, yet they do not cry out to him when they are chained.
018	JOB	036	014	Their soul will die in a storm, and their life, among the unmanly.
018	JOB	036	015	He will rescue the poor from his anguish, and he will open his ear during tribulation.
018	JOB	036	016	Therefore, he will save you from the narrow mouth very widely, even though it has no foundation under it. Moreover, your respite at table will be full of fatness.
018	JOB	036	017	Your case has been judged like that of the impious; you will withdraw your plea and your judgment.
018	JOB	036	018	Therefore, do not let anger overwhelm you so that you oppress another; neither should you allow a multitude of gifts to influence you.
018	JOB	036	019	Lay down your greatness without distress, and put aside all of your power with courage.
018	JOB	036	020	Do not prolong the night, even if people rise on their behalf.
018	JOB	036	021	Be careful that you do not turn to iniquity; for, after your misery, you have begun to follow this.
018	JOB	036	022	Behold, God is exalted in his strength, and there is no one like him among the law-givers.
018	JOB	036	023	Who is able to investigate his ways? And who can say, “You have done iniquity,” to him?
018	JOB	036	024	Remember that you are ignorant of his work, yet men have sung its praises.
018	JOB	036	025	All men consider him; and each one ponders from a distance.
018	JOB	036	026	Behold, God is great, defeating our knowledge; the number of his years is inestimable.
018	JOB	036	027	He carries away the drops of rain, and he sends forth showers like a raging whirlpool;
018	JOB	036	028	they flow from the clouds that are woven above everything.
018	JOB	036	029	If he wills it, he extends the clouds as his tent
018	JOB	036	030	and shines with his light from above; likewise, he covers the oceans within his tent.
018	JOB	036	031	For he judges the people by these things, and he gives food to a multitude of mortals.
018	JOB	036	032	Within his hands, he hides the light, and he commands it to come forth again.
018	JOB	036	033	He announces it to his friend, for it is his possession and he is able to reach out to it.
018	JOB	037	001	At this, my heart became frightened, and it has been moved from its place.
018	JOB	037	002	Pay close attention to the alarm of his voice and to the sound that proceeds from his mouth.
018	JOB	037	003	He beholds everything under the heavens, and his light reaches beyond the ends of the earth.
018	JOB	037	004	After this, a noise will sound; he will thunder with the voice of his greatness, and it will not be tracked down, yet his voice will be obeyed.
018	JOB	037	005	God will thunder with his voice miraculously, for he performs great and unsearchable things.
018	JOB	037	006	He commands the snow to descend on earth, and the winter rains, and the shower of his strength.
018	JOB	037	007	He signs the hand of all men, so that each one may know his works.
018	JOB	037	008	The beast will enter his hiding-place, and he will remain in his cave.
018	JOB	037	009	From the interior, a storm will come forth, and a cold winter from the north.
018	JOB	037	010	As God breathes out, frost forms, and the waters are poured forth very widely again.
018	JOB	037	011	Crops desire clouds, and the clouds scatter their light.
018	JOB	037	012	It shines all around, wherever the will of him that governs them will lead, to anywhere he will command, over the whole face of the earth,
018	JOB	037	013	whether in one tribe, or in his own region, or in whatever place of his mercy that he will order them to be found.
018	JOB	037	014	Listen to these things, Job. Stand up and consider the wonders of God.
018	JOB	037	015	Do you know when God ordered the rains, so as to show the light of his clouds?
018	JOB	037	016	Do you know the great paths of the clouds, and the perfect sciences?
018	JOB	037	017	Are not your garments hot, when the south wind blows across the land?
018	JOB	037	018	Perhaps you have made the heavens with him, which are very solid, as if they had been cast from brass.
018	JOB	037	019	Reveal to us what we should say to him, for, of course, we are wrapped in darkness.
018	JOB	037	020	Who will explain to him the things that I am saying? Even while a man is still speaking, he will be devoured.
018	JOB	037	021	Although they do not see the light, the air will be thickened suddenly into clouds, and the wind, passing by, will drive them away.
018	JOB	037	022	Riches arrive from the north, and fearful praise reaches out to God.
018	JOB	037	023	We are not worthy to be able to find him. Great in strength, great in judgment, great in justice: he is indescribable.
018	JOB	037	024	Therefore, men will fear him, and all those who seem to themselves to be wise, will not dare to contemplate him.
018	JOB	038	001	But the Lord, responding to Job from a whirlwind, said:
018	JOB	038	002	Who is this that wraps sentences in unskilled words?
018	JOB	038	003	Gird your waist like a man. I will question you, and you must answer me.
018	JOB	038	004	Where were you, when I set the foundations of the earth? Tell me, if you have understanding.
018	JOB	038	005	Who set its measurements, if you know, or who stretched a line over it?
018	JOB	038	006	Upon what have its bases been grounded, and who set forth its cornerstone,
018	JOB	038	007	when the morning stars praised me together, and all the sons of God made a joyful noise?
018	JOB	038	008	Who enclosed the sea with doors, when it broke forth as if issuing from the womb,
018	JOB	038	009	when I stationed a cloud as its garment and wrapped it in a mist as if swaddling an infant?
018	JOB	038	010	I encircled it with my limits, and I positioned its bars and doors.
018	JOB	038	011	And I said: “This far you will approach, and you will proceed no further, and here you will break your swelling waves.”
018	JOB	038	012	Did you, after your birth, command the birth of the sun and show the sunrise its place?
018	JOB	038	013	And did you hold the extremities of the earth, shaking them, and have you shaken the impious out of it?
018	JOB	038	014	The seal will be restored like clay, and it will remain in place like a garment.
018	JOB	038	015	From the impious, the light will be taken away, and the exalted arm will be broken.
018	JOB	038	016	Have you entered the depths of the sea, and have you taken a walk in the uttermost parts of the abyss?
018	JOB	038	017	Have the gates of death been opened to you, and have you seen the doors of darkness?
018	JOB	038	018	Have you considered the breadth of the earth? If you know all things, reveal them to me.
018	JOB	038	019	Which is the way that holds the light, and which is the place of darkness?
018	JOB	038	020	In this way, you might lead each thing to its final place, and understand the paths of its house.
018	JOB	038	021	So then, did you know when you were to be born? And did you know the number of your days?
018	JOB	038	022	Have you been admitted into the storehouses of the snows, and have you gazed upon the stockpile of the brimstone,
018	JOB	038	023	which I have prepared for the time of the enemy, for the day of the battle and the war?
018	JOB	038	024	In what way is the light scattered, and the heat distributed, over the earth?
018	JOB	038	025	Who gave a course to the rainstorms, and a path to the resounding thunder,
018	JOB	038	026	so that it would rain on the earth far from man, in the wilderness where no mortal lingers,
018	JOB	038	027	so that it would fill impassable and desolate places, and would bring forth green plants?
018	JOB	038	028	Who is the father of rain, or who conceived the drops of dew?
018	JOB	038	029	From whose womb did the ice proceed, and who created the frost from the air?
018	JOB	038	030	The waters are hardened to become like stone, and the surface of the abyss freezes over.
018	JOB	038	031	Will you have the strength to join together the sparkling stars of the Pleiades, or are you able to disperse the circling of Arcturus?
018	JOB	038	032	Can you bring forth the morning star, in its time, and make the evening star rise over the sons of the earth?
018	JOB	038	033	Do you know the order of heaven, and can you explain its rules here on the earth?
018	JOB	038	034	Can you lift up your voice to the clouds, so that an onslaught of waters will cover you?
018	JOB	038	035	Can you send forth lightning bolts, and will they go, and on returning, say to you: “Here we are?”
018	JOB	038	036	Who placed discernment in the guts of man, or who gave the rooster intelligence?
018	JOB	038	037	Who can describe the rules of the heavens, or who can put to rest the harmony of heaven?
018	JOB	038	038	When was the dust cast to become the earth, and when were its clods fastened together?
018	JOB	038	039	Will you seize prey for the lioness, and will you sustain the lives of her young,
018	JOB	038	040	as they rest in their dens or lie in wait in pits?
018	JOB	038	041	Who provides the raven with its meal, when her chicks cry out to God, as they wander around because they have no food?
018	JOB	039	001	Do you know at what time the wild goats have given birth among the rocks, or do you observe the deer when they go into labor?
018	JOB	039	002	Have you numbered the months since their conception, and do you know at what time they gave birth?
018	JOB	039	003	They bend themselves for their offspring, and they give birth, and they emit roars.
018	JOB	039	004	Their young are weaned and go out to feed; they depart and do not return to them.
018	JOB	039	005	Who has set the wild ass free, and who has released his bonds?
018	JOB	039	006	I have given a house in solitude to him, and his tabernacle is in the salted land.
018	JOB	039	007	He despises the crowded city; he does not pay attention to the bellow of the tax collector.
018	JOB	039	008	He looks around the mountains of his pasture, and he searches everywhere for green plants.
018	JOB	039	009	Will the rhinoceros be willing to serve you, and will he remain in your stall?
018	JOB	039	010	Can you detain the rhinoceros with your harness to plough for you, and will he loosen the soil of the furrows behind you?
018	JOB	039	011	Will you put your faith in his great strength, and delegate your labors to him?
018	JOB	039	012	Will you trust him to return to you the seed, and to gather it on your drying floor?
018	JOB	039	013	The wing of the ostrich is like the wings of the heron, and of the hawk.
018	JOB	039	014	When she leaves eggs behind in the earth, will you perhaps warm them in the dust?
018	JOB	039	015	She forgets that feet may trample them, or that the beasts of the field may shatter them.
018	JOB	039	016	She is hardened against her young, as if they were not hers; she has labored in vain, with no fear compelling her.
018	JOB	039	017	For God has deprived her of wisdom; neither has he given her understanding.
018	JOB	039	018	Yet, when the time is right, she raises her wings on high; she ridicules the horse and his rider.
018	JOB	039	019	Will you supply strength to the horse, or envelope his throat with neighing?
018	JOB	039	020	Will you alarm him as the locusts do? His panic is revealed by the display of his nostrils.
018	JOB	039	021	He digs at the earth with his hoof; he jumps around boldly; he advances to meet armed men.
018	JOB	039	022	He despises fear; he does not turn away from the sword.
018	JOB	039	023	Above him, the quiver rattles, the spear and the shield shake.
018	JOB	039	024	Seething and raging, he drinks up the earth; neither does he pause when the blast of the trumpet sounds.
018	JOB	039	025	When he hears the bugle, he says, “Ha!” He smells the battle from a distance, the exhortation of the officers, and the battle cry of the soldiers.
018	JOB	039	026	Does the hawk grow feathers by means of your wisdom, spreading her wings towards the south?
018	JOB	039	027	Will the eagle lift herself up at your command and make her nest in steep places?
018	JOB	039	028	She dwells among the rocks, and she lingers among broken boulders and inaccessible cliffs.
018	JOB	039	029	From there, she looks for food, and her eyes catch sight of it from far away.
018	JOB	039	030	Her young will drink blood, and wherever the carcass will be, she is there immediately.
018	JOB	040	001	And the Lord continued, and he said to Job:
018	JOB	040	002	Will he who contends with God be so easily silenced? Certainly, he who argues with God must also respond to him.
018	JOB	040	003	Then Job answered the Lord, saying:
018	JOB	040	004	What could I possibly answer, since I have been speaking thoughtlessly? I will place my hand over my mouth.
018	JOB	040	005	One thing I have spoken, which I wish I had not said; and another, to which I will add no more.
018	JOB	040	006	But the Lord, answering Job out of the whirlwind, said:
018	JOB	040	007	Gird your waist like a man. I will question you, and you must answer me.
018	JOB	040	008	Will you make my judgment null and void; and will you condemn me so that you may be justified?
018	JOB	040	009	And do you have an arm like God, or a voice like thunder?
018	JOB	040	010	Envelop yourself with splendor, and raise yourself up on high, and be glorious, and put on splendid garments.
018	JOB	040	011	Scatter the arrogant with your wrath, and, when you see all the arrogant, humble them.
018	JOB	040	012	Look down upon each of the arrogant and confound them, and crush the impious in their place.
018	JOB	040	013	Hide them in the dust together and plunge their faces into the pit.
018	JOB	040	014	Then I will confess that your right hand is able to save you.
018	JOB	040	015	Behold, the behemoth, whom I created along with you, eats hay like an ox.
018	JOB	040	016	His strength is in his lower back, and his power is in the center of his abdomen.
018	JOB	040	017	He draws up his tail like a cedar; the sinews of his thighs have been drawn together.
018	JOB	040	018	His bones are like pipes of brass; his cartilage is like plates of iron.
018	JOB	040	019	He is the beginning of the ways of God, who made him; he will use him as his sword.
018	JOB	040	020	The mountains bring forth grass for him; all the beasts of the field will play there.
018	JOB	040	021	He sleeps in the shadows, under the cover of branches, and in moist places.
018	JOB	040	022	The shadows cover his shadow; the willows of the brook will encircle him.
018	JOB	040	023	Behold, he will drink a river and not be amazed, and he has confidence that the Jordan could flow into his mouth.
018	JOB	040	024	He will seize him through his eyes, as if with a hook, and he will bore through his nostrils, as if with stakes.
018	JOB	041	001	Can you draw out the leviathan with a hook, and can you bind his tongue with a cord?
018	JOB	041	002	Can you place a ring in his nose, or bore through his jaw with an arm band?
018	JOB	041	003	Will he offer many prayers to you, or speak to you quietly?
018	JOB	041	004	Will he form a covenant with you, and will you accept him as a servant forever?
018	JOB	041	005	Will you play with him as with a bird, or tether him for your handmaids?
018	JOB	041	006	Will your friends cut him into pieces, will dealers distribute him?
018	JOB	041	007	Will you fill up bags with his hide, and let his head be used as a home for fishes?
018	JOB	041	008	Place your hand upon him; remember the battle and speak no more.
018	JOB	041	009	Behold, his hope will fail him, and in the sight of all, he will be thrown down.
018	JOB	041	010	I will not rouse him, as the cruel would do, for who is able to withstand my countenance?
018	JOB	041	011	Who has given to me beforehand, so that I should repay him? All things that are under heaven are mine.
018	JOB	041	012	I will not spare him, nor his powerful words and counterfeit attempts at supplication.
018	JOB	041	013	Who can reveal the beauty of his garment? And who can enter the middle of his mouth?
018	JOB	041	014	Who can open the doors of his face? I gave fear to the circle of his teeth.
018	JOB	041	015	His body is like shields fused together, like dense scales pressed over one another.
018	JOB	041	016	One is joined to another, and not even air can pass between them.
018	JOB	041	017	They adhere to one another, and they hold themselves in place and will not be separated.
018	JOB	041	018	His sneezing has the brilliance of fire, and his eyes are like the eyelids of the morning.
018	JOB	041	019	Lamps proceed from his mouth, like torches of fire burning brightly.
018	JOB	041	020	Smoke passes out of his nostrils, like a pot that is heated and boiling.
018	JOB	041	021	His breath causes coal to burn, and a flame comes forth from his mouth.
018	JOB	041	022	Strength dwells in his neck, and destitution goes before his presence.
018	JOB	041	023	The parts of his body work in harmony together. He will send lightning bolts against him, and they will not be carried to another place.
018	JOB	041	024	His heart will be as hard as a stone and as dense as a blacksmith’s anvil.
018	JOB	041	025	When he will be raised up, the angels will be afraid, and, because they are terrified, they will purify themselves.
018	JOB	041	026	When a sword catches up with him, it will not be able to settle in, nor a spear, nor a breastplate.
018	JOB	041	027	For he will consider iron as if it were chaff, and brass as if it were rotten wood.
018	JOB	041	028	The archer will not cause him to flee; the stones of the sling have been turned into stubble for him.
018	JOB	041	029	He will treat the hammer as if it were stubble, and he will ridicule those who brandish the spear.
018	JOB	041	030	The beams of the sun will be under him, and he will dispense gold to them as if it were clay.
018	JOB	041	031	He will make the depths of the sea boil like a pot, and he will set it to bubble just as ointments do.
018	JOB	041	032	A path will shine after him; he will esteem the abyss as if it were weakening with age.
018	JOB	041	033	There is no power on the earth that is being compared to him, who has been made so that he fears no one.
018	JOB	041	034	He sees every prominent thing; he is king over all the sons of arrogance.
018	JOB	042	001	Then Job, responding to the Lord, said:
018	JOB	042	002	I know that you are able to do all things, and that no thoughts are hidden from you.
018	JOB	042	003	So, who is it that would disguise a lack of knowledge as counsel? Therefore, I have been speaking foolishly, about things whose measure exceeds my knowledge.
018	JOB	042	004	Listen, and I will speak. I will question you, and you may answer me.
018	JOB	042	005	By paying attention with the ear, I have heard you, but now my eye sees you.
018	JOB	042	006	Therefore, I find myself reprehensible, and I will do penance in embers and ashes.
018	JOB	042	007	But after the Lord had finished speaking these words to Job, he said to Eliphaz the Themanite: My wrath has been kindled against you, and against your two friends, because you have not been speaking correctly in my eyes, as my servant Job has done.
018	JOB	042	008	Therefore, have seven bulls and seven rams brought to you, and go to my servant Job, and offer these as a holocaust for yourselves. But also, my servant Job will pray for you; I will accept his face, so that foolishness will not be imputed to you. For you have not been speaking correctly about me, as my servant Job has done.
018	JOB	042	009	So Eliphaz the Themanite, and Baldad the Suhite, and Zophar the Naamathite departed, and they did just as the Lord had spoken to them, and the Lord accepted the face of Job.
018	JOB	042	010	Likewise, the Lord was moved by the repentance of Job, when he prayed for his friends. And the Lord gave to Job twice as much as he had before.
018	JOB	042	011	Yet all his brethren came to him, and all his sisters, and everyone who had known him before, and they ate bread with him in his house. They also shook their heads over him and comforted him, because of all the bad things that God had inflicted on him. And each one of them gave him one female sheep, and one earring of gold.
018	JOB	042	012	And the Lord blessed the latter end of Job even more than his beginning. And he had fourteen thousand sheep, and six thousand camels, and a thousand pairs of oxen, and a thousand she-donkeys.
018	JOB	042	013	And he had seven sons and three daughters.
018	JOB	042	014	And he called the name of one, Daylight, and the name of the second, Cinnamon, and the name of the third, Horn of Cosmetics.
018	JOB	042	015	And, in the whole world, there were not found women so beautiful as the daughters of Job. And so their father gave them an inheritance along with their brothers.
018	JOB	042	016	But Job lived long after these events, for a hundred and forty years, and he saw his children, and his children’s children, all the way to the fourth generation,
018	JOB	042	017	and he died an old man and full of days.
