# BOOK	019	PSA	Psalms	Psalms
019	PSA	001	001	Blessed is the man who has not followed the counsel of the impious, and has not remained in the way of sinners, and has not sat in the chair of pestilence.
019	PSA	001	002	But his will is with the law of the Lord, and he will meditate on his law, day and night.
019	PSA	001	003	And he will be like a tree that has been planted beside running waters, which will provide its fruit in its time, and its leaf will not fall away, and all things whatsoever that he does will prosper.
019	PSA	001	004	Not so the impious, not so. For they are like the dust that the wind casts along the face of the earth.
019	PSA	001	005	Therefore, the impious will not prevail again in judgment, nor sinners in the council of the just.
019	PSA	001	006	For the Lord knows the way of the just. And the path of the impious will pass away.
019	PSA	002	001	Why have the Gentiles been seething, and why have the people been pondering nonsense?
019	PSA	002	002	The kings of the earth have stood up, and the leaders have joined together as one, against the Lord and against his Christ:
019	PSA	002	003	“Let us shatter their chains and cast their yoke away from us.”
019	PSA	002	004	He who dwells in heaven will ridicule them, and the Lord will mock them.
019	PSA	002	005	Then will he speak to them in his anger and trouble them with his fury.
019	PSA	002	006	Yet I have been appointed king by him over Zion, his holy mountain, preaching his precepts.
019	PSA	002	007	The Lord has said to me: You are my son, this day have I begotten you.
019	PSA	002	008	Ask of me and I will give to you: the Gentiles for your inheritance, and the ends of the earth for your possession.
019	PSA	002	009	You will rule them with an iron rod, and you will shatter them like a potter’s vessel.
019	PSA	002	010	And now, O kings, understand. Receive instruction, you who judge the earth.
019	PSA	002	011	Serve the Lord in fear, and exult in him with trembling.
019	PSA	002	012	Embrace discipline, lest at any time the Lord might become angry, and you would perish from the way of the just. Though his wrath can flare up in a short time, blessed are all those who trust in him.
019	PSA	003	001	A Psalm of David. When he fled from the face of his son, Absalom. Lord, why have those who trouble me been multiplied? Many rise up against me.
019	PSA	003	002	Many say to my soul, “There is no salvation for him in his God.” (Pause)
019	PSA	003	003	But you, Lord, are my supporter, my glory, and the one who raises up my head.
019	PSA	003	004	I have cried out to the Lord with my voice, and he has heard me from his holy mountain. (Pause)
019	PSA	003	005	I have slept, and I have been stupefied. But I awakened because the Lord has taken me up.
019	PSA	003	006	I will not fear the thousands of people surrounding me. Rise up, Lord. Save me, my God.
019	PSA	003	007	For you have struck all those who oppose me without cause. You have broken the teeth of sinners.
019	PSA	003	008	Salvation is of the Lord, and your blessing is upon your people. (Pause)
019	PSA	004	001	In parts according to verses. A Psalm of David. When I called upon him, the God of my justice heeded me. In tribulation, you have enlarged me. Have mercy on me, and heed my prayer.
019	PSA	004	002	Sons of men, how long will you be dull in heart, so that whatever you love is in vain, and whatever you seek is false? (Pause)
019	PSA	004	003	And know this: the Lord has made wondrous his holy one. The Lord will heed me when I cry out to him.
019	PSA	004	004	Be angry, and do not be willing to sin. The things that you say in your hearts: be sorry for them on your beds. (Pause)
019	PSA	004	005	Offer the sacrifice of justice, and hope in the Lord. Many say, “Who reveals to us what is good?”
019	PSA	004	006	The light of your countenance, Lord, has been sealed upon us. You have given joy to my heart.
019	PSA	004	007	By the fruit of their grain, wine, and oil, they have been multiplied.
019	PSA	004	008	In peace itself, I will sleep and I will rest. For you, O Lord, have established me singularly in hope.
019	PSA	005	001	Unto the end. For her who pursues the inheritance. A Psalm of David. O Lord, listen closely to my words. Understand my outcry.
019	PSA	005	002	Attend to the voice of my prayer, my King and my God.
019	PSA	005	003	For to you, I will pray. In the morning, Lord, you will hear my voice.
019	PSA	005	004	In the morning, I will stand before you, and I will see. For you are not a God who wills iniquity.
019	PSA	005	005	And the malicious will not dwell close to you, nor will the unjust endure before your eyes.
019	PSA	005	006	You hate all who work iniquity. You will destroy all who speak a lie. The bloody and deceitful man, the Lord will abominate.
019	PSA	005	007	But I am in the multitude of your mercy. I will enter your house. I will show adoration toward your holy temple, in your fear.
019	PSA	005	008	Lord, lead me in your justice. Because of my enemies, direct my way in your sight.
019	PSA	005	009	For there is no truth in their mouth: their heart is vain.
019	PSA	005	010	Their throat is an open sepulcher. They have acted deceitfully with their tongues. Judge them, O God. Let them fall by their own intentions: according to the multitude of their impiety, expel them. For they have provoked you, O Lord.
019	PSA	005	011	But let all those who hope in you rejoice. They will exult in eternity, and you will dwell in them. And all those who love your name will glory in you.
019	PSA	005	012	For you will bless the just. You have crowned us, O Lord, as if with a shield of your good will.
019	PSA	006	001	In parts according to verses. A Psalm of David. For the octave. O Lord, do not rebuke me in your fury, nor chastise me in your anger.
019	PSA	006	002	Have mercy on me, Lord, for I am weak. Heal me, Lord, for my bones have become disturbed,
019	PSA	006	003	and my soul has been very troubled. But as for you, Lord, when?
019	PSA	006	004	Turn to me, Lord, and rescue my soul. Save me because of your mercy.
019	PSA	006	005	For there is no one in death who would be mindful of you. And who will confess to you in Hell?
019	PSA	006	006	I have labored in my groaning. Every night, with my tears, I will wash my bed and drench my blanket.
019	PSA	006	007	My eye has been troubled by rage. I have grown old among all my enemies.
019	PSA	006	008	Scatter before me, all you who work iniquity, for the Lord has heard the voice of my weeping.
019	PSA	006	009	The Lord has heard my supplication. The Lord has accepted my prayer.
019	PSA	006	010	Let all my enemies be ashamed and together be greatly troubled. May they be converted and become ashamed very quickly.
019	PSA	007	001	A Psalm of David, which he sang to the Lord because of the words of Cush, the son of Jemini. O Lord, my God, in you I have hoped. Save me from all those who persecute me, and free me:
019	PSA	007	002	lest at any time, like a lion, he might seize my soul, while there is no one to redeem me, nor any who can save.
019	PSA	007	003	O Lord, my God, if there is iniquity in my hands, if I have done this:
019	PSA	007	004	if I have repaid those who rendered evils to me, may I deservedly fall away empty before my enemies:
019	PSA	007	005	let the enemy pursue my soul, and take hold of it, and trample my life into the earth, and drag down my glory into the dust. (Pause)
019	PSA	007	006	Rise up, Lord, in your anger. And be exalted to the borders of my enemies. And rise up, O Lord my God, according to the precept that you commanded,
019	PSA	007	007	and a congregation of people will surround you. And, because of this, return on high.
019	PSA	007	008	The Lord judges the people. Judge me, O Lord, according to my justice and according to my innocence within me.
019	PSA	007	009	The wickedness of sinners will be consumed, and you will direct the just: the examiner of hearts and temperaments is God.
019	PSA	007	010	Just is my help from the Lord, who saves the upright of heart.
019	PSA	007	011	God is a just judge, strong and patient. How could he be angry throughout every day?
019	PSA	007	012	Unless you will be converted, he will brandish his sword. He has extended his bow and made it ready.
019	PSA	007	013	And with it, he has prepared instruments of death. He has produced his arrows for those on fire.
019	PSA	007	014	Behold him who has given birth to injustice: he has conceived sorrow and has begotten iniquity.
019	PSA	007	015	He has opened a pit and enlarged it. And he has fallen into the hole that he made.
019	PSA	007	016	His sorrow will be turned upon his own head, and his iniquity will descend upon his highest point.
019	PSA	007	017	I will confess to the Lord according to his justice, and I will sing a psalm to the name of the Lord Most High.
019	PSA	008	001	Unto the end. For the oil and wine presses. A Psalm of David. O Lord, our Lord, how admirable is your name throughout all the earth! For your magnificence is elevated above the heavens.
019	PSA	008	002	Out of the mouths of babes and infants, you have perfected praise, because of your enemies, so that you may destroy the enemy and the revenger.
019	PSA	008	003	For I will behold your heavens, the works of your fingers: the moon and the stars, which you have founded.
019	PSA	008	004	What is man, that you are mindful of him, or the son of man, that you visit him?
019	PSA	008	005	You reduced him to a little less than the Angels; you have crowned him with glory and honor,
019	PSA	008	006	and you have set him over the works of your hands.
019	PSA	008	007	You have subjected all things under his feet, all sheep and oxen, and in addition: the beasts of the field,
019	PSA	008	008	the birds of the air, and the fish of the sea, which pass through the paths of the sea.
019	PSA	008	009	O Lord, our Lord, how admirable is your name throughout all the earth!
019	PSA	009	001	Unto the end. For the secrets of the Son. A Psalm of David. I will confess to you, Lord, with my whole heart. I will recount all your wonders.
019	PSA	009	002	I will rejoice and exult in you. I will sing a psalm to your name, O Most High.
019	PSA	009	003	For my enemy will be turned back. They will be weakened and perish before your face.
019	PSA	009	004	For you have accomplished my judgment and my cause. You have sat upon the throne that judges justice.
019	PSA	009	005	You have rebuked the Gentiles, and the impious one has perished. You have deleted their name in eternity and for all generations.
019	PSA	009	006	The spears of the enemy have failed in the end, and their cities, you have destroyed. Their memory has perished with a loud noise.
019	PSA	009	007	But the Lord remains in eternity. He has prepared his throne in judgment.
019	PSA	009	008	And he will judge the whole world in equity. He will judge the people in justice.
019	PSA	009	009	And the Lord has become a refuge for the poor, a helper in opportunity, in tribulation.
019	PSA	009	010	And may they hope in you, who know your name. For you have not abandoned those seeking you, Lord.
019	PSA	009	011	Sing a psalm to the Lord, who dwells in Zion. Announce his study among the Gentiles.
019	PSA	009	012	Because of those who yearned for their blood, he has remembered them. He has not forgotten the cry of the poor.
019	PSA	009	013	Have mercy on me, Lord. See my humiliation from my enemies.
019	PSA	009	014	You lift me up from the gates of death, so that I may announce all your praises at the gates of the daughter of Zion.
019	PSA	009	015	I will exult in your salvation. The Gentiles have become trapped in the ruin that they made. Their foot has been caught in the same snare that they themselves had hidden.
019	PSA	009	016	The Lord will be recognized when making judgments. The sinner has been caught in the works of his own hands. (Pause)
019	PSA	009	017	The sinners will be turned into Hell: all the Gentiles who have forgotten God.
019	PSA	009	018	For the poor will not be forgotten in the end. The patience of the poor will not perish in the end.
019	PSA	009	019	Rise up, Lord: do not let man be strengthened. Let the Gentiles be judged in your sight.
019	PSA	009	020	O Lord, establish a lawgiver over them, so that the Gentiles may know that they are only men. (Pause)
019	PSA	010	001	So then, why, O Lord, have you withdrawn far away? Why have you overlooked us in opportunity, in tribulation?
019	PSA	010	002	While the impious is arrogant, the poor is enflamed. They are held by the counsels that they devise.
019	PSA	010	003	For the sinner is praised by the desires of his soul, and the iniquitous is blessed.
019	PSA	010	004	The sinner has provoked the Lord; according to the multitude of his wrath, he will not seek him.
019	PSA	010	005	God is not before his sight. His ways are stained at all times. Your judgments are removed from his face. He will be master of all his enemies.
019	PSA	010	006	For he has said in his heart, “I will not be disturbed: from generation to generation without evil.”
019	PSA	010	007	His mouth is full of curses, and bitterness, and deceit. Under his tongue are hardship and sorrow.
019	PSA	010	008	He sits in ambush, with resources in hidden places, so that he may execute the innocent.
019	PSA	010	009	His eyes catch sight of the poor. He lies in ambush, in hiding like a lion in his den. He lies in ambush, so that he may seize the poor, to seize the poor as he draws him in.
019	PSA	010	010	With his snare, he will bring him down. He will crouch down and pounce, when he has power over the poor.
019	PSA	010	011	For he has said in his heart, “God has forgotten, he has turned away his face, lest he see to the end.”
019	PSA	010	012	O Lord God, rise up. Let your hand be exalted. Do not forget the poor.
019	PSA	010	013	How has the impious one provoked God? For he has said in his heart, “He will not inquire.”
019	PSA	010	014	You do see, for you examine hardship and sorrow, so that you may deliver them into your hands. The poor one has been abandoned to you. You will be a helper to the orphan.
019	PSA	010	015	Break the arm of the sinner and the malicious. His sin will be sought, and it will not be found.
019	PSA	010	016	The Lord shall reign in eternity, even forever and ever. You will perish the Gentiles from his land.
019	PSA	010	017	The Lord has heeded the desire of the poor. Your ear has listened to the preparation of their heart,
019	PSA	010	018	so as to judge for the orphan and the humble, so that man may no longer presume to magnify himself upon the earth.
019	PSA	011	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. I trust in the Lord. How can you say to my soul, “Sojourn to the mountain, like a sparrow.”
019	PSA	011	002	For behold, the sinners have bent their bow. They have prepared their arrows in the quiver, so as to shoot arrows in the dark at the upright of heart.
019	PSA	011	003	For they have destroyed the things that you have completed. But what has the just one done?
019	PSA	011	004	The Lord is in his holy temple. The Lord’s throne is in heaven. His eyes look upon the poor. His eyelids question the sons of men.
019	PSA	011	005	The Lord questions the just and the impious. Yet he who loves iniquity, hates his own soul.
019	PSA	011	006	He will rain down snares upon sinners. Fire and brimstone and windstorms will be the portion of their cup.
019	PSA	011	007	For the Lord is just, and he has chosen justice. His countenance has beheld equity.
019	PSA	012	001	Unto the end. For the octave. A Psalm of David. Save me, O Lord, because holiness has passed away, because truths have been diminished, before the sons of men.
019	PSA	012	002	They have been speaking emptiness, each one to his neighbor; they have been speaking with deceitful lips and a duplicitous heart.
019	PSA	012	003	May the Lord scatter all deceitful lips, along with the tongue that speaks malice.
019	PSA	012	004	They have said: “We will magnify our tongue; our lips belong to us. What is Lord to us?”
019	PSA	012	005	Because of the misery of the destitute and the groaning of the poor, now I will arise, says the Lord. I will place him in safety. I will act faithfully toward him.
019	PSA	012	006	The eloquence of the Lord is pure eloquence, silver tested by fire, purged from the earth, refined seven times.
019	PSA	012	007	You, O Lord, will preserve us, and you will guard us from this generation into eternity.
019	PSA	012	008	The impious wander aimlessly. According to your loftiness, you have multiplied the sons of men.
019	PSA	013	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. How long, O Lord? Will you forget me until the end? How long will you turn your face away from me?
019	PSA	013	002	How long can I take counsel in my soul, sorrowing in my heart throughout the day?
019	PSA	013	003	How long will my enemy be exalted over me?
019	PSA	013	004	Look upon me and listen to me, O Lord my God. Enlighten my eyes, lest I fall asleep forever in death,
019	PSA	013	005	lest at any time my enemy may say, “I have prevailed against him.” Those who trouble me will exult, if I have been disturbed.
019	PSA	013	006	But I have hoped in your mercy. My heart will exult in your salvation. I will sing to the Lord, who assigns good things to me. And I will sing psalms to the name of the Lord Most High.
019	PSA	014	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. The fool has said in his heart, “There is no God.” They were corrupted, and they have become abominable in their studies. There is no one who does good; there is not even one.
019	PSA	014	002	The Lord has looked down from heaven upon the sons of men, to see if there were any who were considering or seeking God.
019	PSA	014	003	They have all gone astray; together they have become useless. There is no one who does good; there is not even one. Their throat is an open sepulcher. With their tongues, they have been acting deceitfully; the venom of asps is under their lips. Their mouth is full of curses and bitterness. Their feet are swift to shed blood. Grief and unhappiness are in their ways; and the way of peace, they have not known. There is no fear of God before their eyes.
019	PSA	014	004	Will they never learn: all those who work iniquity, who devour my people like a meal of bread?
019	PSA	014	005	They have not called upon the Lord. There, they have trembled in fear, where there was no fear.
019	PSA	014	006	For the Lord is with the just generation. You have confounded the counsel of the needy because the Lord is his hope.
019	PSA	014	007	Who will grant the salvation of Israel from Zion? When the Lord turns away the captivity of his people, Jacob will exult, and Israel will rejoice.
019	PSA	015	001	A Psalm of David. O Lord, who will dwell in your tabernacle? Or who will rest on your holy mountain?
019	PSA	015	002	He who walks without blemish and who works justice.
019	PSA	015	003	He who speaks the truth in his heart, who has not acted deceitfully with his tongue, and has not done evil to his neighbor, and has not taken up a reproach against his neighbors.
019	PSA	015	004	In his sight, the malicious one has been reduced to nothing, but he glorifies those who fear the Lord. He who swears to his neighbor and does not deceive.
019	PSA	015	005	He who has not given his money in usury, nor accepted bribes against the innocent. He who does these things will be undisturbed for eternity.
019	PSA	016	001	The inscription of a title: of David himself. Preserve me, O Lord, because I have hoped in you.
019	PSA	016	002	I have said to the Lord: “You are my God, so you have no need of my goodness.”
019	PSA	016	003	As for the saints, who are in his land: he has made all my desires wonderful in them.
019	PSA	016	004	Their infirmities have been multiplied; after this, they acted more quickly. I will not gather for their convocations of blood, nor will I remember their names with my lips.
019	PSA	016	005	The Lord is the portion of my inheritance and my cup. It is you who will restore my inheritance to me.
019	PSA	016	006	The lots have fallen upon me with clarity. And, indeed, my inheritance has been very clear to me.
019	PSA	016	007	I will bless the Lord, who has bestowed understanding upon me. Moreover, my temperament has also corrected me, even through the night.
019	PSA	016	008	I have made provision for the Lord always in my sight. For he is at my right hand, so that I may not be disturbed.
019	PSA	016	009	Because of this, my heart has been joyful, and my tongue has exulted. Moreover, even my body will rest in hope.
019	PSA	016	010	For you will not abandon my soul to Hell, nor will you allow your holy one to see corruption.
019	PSA	016	011	You have made known to me the ways of life; you will fill me with joy by your countenance. At your right hand are delights, even to the end.
019	PSA	017	001	A Prayer of David. Lord, listen to my justice, attend to my supplication. Pay attention to my prayer, which is not from deceitful lips.
019	PSA	017	002	Let my judgment proceed from your presence. Let your eyes behold fairness.
019	PSA	017	003	You have tested my heart and visited it by night. You have examined me by fire, and iniquity has not been found in me.
019	PSA	017	004	Therefore, may my mouth not speak the works of men. I have kept to difficult ways because of the words of your lips.
019	PSA	017	005	Perfect my steps in your paths, so that my footsteps may not be disturbed.
019	PSA	017	006	I have cried out because you, O God, have listened to me. Incline your ear to me and heed my words.
019	PSA	017	007	Make your mercies wonderful, for you save those who hope in you.
019	PSA	017	008	From those who resist your right hand, preserve me like the pupil of your eye. Protect me under the shadow of your wings,
019	PSA	017	009	from the face of the impious who have afflicted me. My enemies have surrounded my soul.
019	PSA	017	010	They have concealed their fatness; their mouth has been speaking arrogantly.
019	PSA	017	011	They have cast me out, and now they have surrounded me. They have cast their eyes down to the earth.
019	PSA	017	012	They have taken me, like a lion ready for the prey, and like a young lion dwelling in hiding.
019	PSA	017	013	Rise up, O Lord, arrive before him and displace him. Deliver my soul from the impious one: your spear from the enemies of your hand.
019	PSA	017	014	Lord, divide them from the few of the earth in their life. Their gut has been filled from your hidden stores. They have been filled with sons, and they have bequeathed to their little ones the remainder.
019	PSA	017	015	But as for me, I will appear before your sight in justice. I will be satisfied when your glory appears.
019	PSA	018	001	Unto the end. For David, the servant of the Lord, who spoke the words of this canticle to the Lord, in the day that the Lord delivered him from the hand of all his enemies and from the hand of Saul. And he said: I will love you, O Lord my strength.
019	PSA	018	002	The Lord is my firmament, my refuge, and my liberator. My God is my helper, and I hope in him: my protector, and the horn of my salvation, and my support.
019	PSA	018	003	Praising, I will call upon the Lord. And I will be saved from my enemies.
019	PSA	018	004	The sorrows of death surrounded me, and the torrents of iniquity dismayed me.
019	PSA	018	005	The sorrows of Hell encompassed me, and the snares of death intercepted me.
019	PSA	018	006	In my tribulation, I called upon the Lord, and I cried out to my God. And he listened to my voice from his holy temple. And my cry in his presence entered into his ears.
019	PSA	018	007	The earth was shaken, and it trembled. The foundations of the mountains were disturbed, and they were shaken, because he was angry with them.
019	PSA	018	008	A smoke ascended by his wrath, and a fire flared up from his face: coals were kindled by it.
019	PSA	018	009	He bent the heavens, and they descended. And darkness was under his feet.
019	PSA	018	010	And he ascended upon the cherubim, and he flew: he flew upon the feathers of the winds.
019	PSA	018	011	And he set darkness as his hiding place, with his tabernacle all around him: dark waters in the clouds of the air.
019	PSA	018	012	At the brightness that was before his sight, the clouds crossed by, with hail and coals of fire.
019	PSA	018	013	And the Lord thundered from heaven, and the Most High uttered his voice: hail and coals of fire.
019	PSA	018	014	And he sent forth his arrows and scattered them. He multiplied lightnings, and he set them in disarray.
019	PSA	018	015	Then the fountains of waters appeared, and the foundations of the world were revealed, by your rebuke, O Lord, by the inspiration of the Spirit of your wrath.
019	PSA	018	016	He sent from on high, and he accepted me. And he took me up, out of many waters.
019	PSA	018	017	He rescued me from my strongest enemies, and from those who hated me. For they had been too strong for me.
019	PSA	018	018	They intercepted me in the day of my affliction, and the Lord became my protector.
019	PSA	018	019	And he led me out, into a wide place. He accomplished my salvation, because he willed me.
019	PSA	018	020	And the Lord will reward me according to my justice, and he will repay me according to the purity of my hands.
019	PSA	018	021	For I have preserved the ways of the Lord, and I have not behaved impiously before my God.
019	PSA	018	022	For all his judgments are in my sight, and his justice, I have not pushed away from me.
019	PSA	018	023	And I will be immaculate together with him, and I will keep myself from my iniquity.
019	PSA	018	024	And the Lord will reward me according to my justice and according to the purity of my hands before his eyes.
019	PSA	018	025	With the holy, you will be holy, and with the innocent, you will be innocent,
019	PSA	018	026	and with the elect, you will be elect, and with the perverse, you will be perverse.
019	PSA	018	027	For you will save the humble people, but you will bring down the eyes of the arrogant.
019	PSA	018	028	For you illuminate my lamp, O Lord. My God, enlighten my darkness.
019	PSA	018	029	For in you, I will be delivered from temptation; and with my God, I will climb over a wall.
019	PSA	018	030	As for my God, his way is undefiled. The eloquence of the Lord has been examined by fire. He is the protector of all who hope in him.
019	PSA	018	031	For who is God, except the Lord? And who is God, except our God?
019	PSA	018	032	It is God who has wrapped me with virtue and made my way immaculate.
019	PSA	018	033	It is he who has perfected my feet, like the feet of deer, and who stations me upon the heights.
019	PSA	018	034	It is he who trains my hands for battle. And you have set my arms like a bow of brass.
019	PSA	018	035	And you have given me the protection of your salvation. And your right hand sustains me. And your discipline has corrected me unto the end. And your discipline itself will teach me.
019	PSA	018	036	You have expanded my footsteps under me, and my tracks have not been weakened.
019	PSA	018	037	I will pursue my enemies and apprehend them. And I will not turn back until they have failed.
019	PSA	018	038	I will break them, and they will not be able to stand. They will fall under my feet.
019	PSA	018	039	And you have wrapped me with virtue for the battle. And those rising up against me, you have subdued under me.
019	PSA	018	040	And you have given the back of my enemies to me, and you have destroyed those who hated me.
019	PSA	018	041	They cried out, but there was none to save them, to the Lord, but he did not heed them.
019	PSA	018	042	And I will crush them into dust before the face of the wind, so that I will obliterate them like the mud in the streets.
019	PSA	018	043	You will rescue me from the contradictions of the people. You will set me at the head of the Gentiles.
019	PSA	018	044	A people I did not know has served me. As soon as their ears heard, they were obedient to me.
019	PSA	018	045	The sons of foreigners have been deceitful to me, the sons of foreigners have grown weak with time, and they have wavered from their paths.
019	PSA	018	046	The Lord lives, and blessed is my God, and may the God of my salvation be exalted:
019	PSA	018	047	O God, who vindicates me and who subdues the people under me, my liberator from my enraged enemies.
019	PSA	018	048	And you will exalt me above those who rise up against me. From the iniquitous man, you will rescue me.
019	PSA	018	049	Because of this, O Lord, I will confess to you among the nations, and I will compose a psalm to your name:
019	PSA	018	050	magnifying the salvation of his king, and showing mercy to David, his Christ, and to his offspring, even for all time.
019	PSA	019	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. The heavens describe the glory of God, and the firmament announces the work of his hands.
019	PSA	019	002	Day proclaims the word to day, and night to night imparts knowledge.
019	PSA	019	003	There are no speeches or conversations, where their voices are not being heard.
019	PSA	019	004	Their sound has gone forth through all the earth, and their words to the ends of the world.
019	PSA	019	005	He has placed his tabernacle in the sun, and he is like a bridegroom coming out of his bedroom. He has exulted like a giant running along the way;
019	PSA	019	006	his departure is from the summit of heaven. And his course reaches all the way to its summit. Neither is there anyone who can hide himself from his heat.
019	PSA	019	007	The law of the Lord is immaculate, converting souls. The testimony of the Lord is faithful, providing wisdom to little ones.
019	PSA	019	008	The justice of the Lord is right, rejoicing hearts. The precepts of the Lord are brilliant, enlightening the eyes.
019	PSA	019	009	The fear of the Lord is holy, enduring for all generations. The judgments of the Lord are true, justified in themselves:
019	PSA	019	010	desirable beyond gold and many precious stones, and sweeter than honey and the honeycomb.
019	PSA	019	011	For, indeed, your servant keeps them, and in keeping them, there are many rewards.
019	PSA	019	012	Who can understand transgression? From my hidden faults, cleanse me, O Lord,
019	PSA	019	013	and from those of others, spare your servant. If they will have no dominion over me, then I will be immaculate, and I will be cleansed from the greatest transgression.
019	PSA	019	014	And the eloquence of my mouth will be so as to please, along with the meditation of my heart, in your sight, forever, O Lord, my helper and my redeemer.
019	PSA	020	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. May the Lord hear you in the day of tribulation. May the name of the God of Jacob protect you.
019	PSA	020	002	May he send you help from the sanctuary and watch over you from Zion.
019	PSA	020	003	May he be mindful of all your sacrifices, and may your burnt-offerings be fat.
019	PSA	020	004	May he grant to you according to your heart, and confirm all your counsels.
019	PSA	020	005	We will rejoice in your salvation, and in the name of our God, we will be magnified.
019	PSA	020	006	May the Lord fulfill all your petitions. Now I know that the Lord has saved his Christ. He will hear him from his holy heaven. The salvation of his right hand is in his power.
019	PSA	020	007	Some trust in chariots, and some in horses, but we will call upon the name of the Lord our God.
019	PSA	020	008	They have been bound, and they have fallen. But we have risen up, and we have been set upright.
019	PSA	020	009	O Lord, save the king, and hear us on the day that we will call upon you.
019	PSA	021	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. In your virtue, Lord, the king will rejoice, and over your salvation, he will exult exceedingly.
019	PSA	021	002	You have granted him the desire of his heart, and you have not cheated him of the wish of his lips.
019	PSA	021	003	For you have gone ahead of him with blessings of sweetness. You have placed a crown of precious stones on his head.
019	PSA	021	004	He petitioned you for life, and you have granted him length of days, in the present time, and forever and ever.
019	PSA	021	005	Great is his glory in your salvation. Glory and great adornment, you will lay upon him.
019	PSA	021	006	For you will give him as a blessing forever and ever. You will make him rejoice with gladness in your presence.
019	PSA	021	007	Because the king hopes in the Lord, and in the mercy of the Most High, he will not be disturbed.
019	PSA	021	008	May your hand be found by all your enemies. May your right hand discover all those who hate you.
019	PSA	021	009	You will make them like an oven of fire, in the time of your presence. The Lord will stir them up with his wrath, and fire will devour them.
019	PSA	021	010	You will destroy their fruit from the earth and their offspring from the sons of men.
019	PSA	021	011	For they have turned evils upon you; they have devised plans, which they have not been able to accomplish.
019	PSA	021	012	For you will make them turn their back; with your remnants, you will prepare their countenance.
019	PSA	021	013	Be exalted, Lord, by your own power. We will play music and sing psalms to your virtues.
019	PSA	022	001	Unto the end. For the tasks of early morning. A Psalm of David. O God, my God, look upon me. Why have you forsaken me? Far from my salvation are the words of my offenses.
019	PSA	022	002	My God, I will cry out by day, and you will not heed, and by night, and it will not be foolishness for me.
019	PSA	022	003	But you dwell in holiness, O Praise of Israel.
019	PSA	022	004	In you, our fathers have hoped. They hoped, and you freed them.
019	PSA	022	005	They cried out to you, and they were saved. In you, they hoped and were not confounded.
019	PSA	022	006	But I am a worm and not a man: a disgrace among men, and an outcast of the people.
019	PSA	022	007	All those who saw me have derided me. They have spoken with the lips and shook the head.
019	PSA	022	008	He has hoped in the Lord, let him rescue him. Let him save him because he chooses him.
019	PSA	022	009	For you are the one who has drawn me out of the womb, my hope from the breasts of my mother.
019	PSA	022	010	I have been thrown upon you from the womb; from the womb of my mother, you are my God.
019	PSA	022	011	Do not depart from me. For tribulation is near, since there is no one who may help me.
019	PSA	022	012	Many calves have surrounded me; fat bulls have besieged me.
019	PSA	022	013	They have opened their mouths over me, just like a lion seizing and roaring.
019	PSA	022	014	And so, I have been poured out like water, and all my bones have been scattered. My heart has become like wax, melting in the midst of my chest.
019	PSA	022	015	My strength has dried up like clay, and my tongue has adhered to my jaws. And you have pulled me down, into the dust of death.
019	PSA	022	016	For many dogs have surrounded me. The council of the malicious has besieged me. They have pierced my hands and feet.
019	PSA	022	017	They have numbered all my bones. And they have examined me and stared at me.
019	PSA	022	018	They divided my garments among them, and over my vestment, they cast lots.
019	PSA	022	019	But you, O Lord, do not take your help far from me; be attentive to my defense.
019	PSA	022	020	O God, rescue my soul from the spear, and my only one from the hand of the dog.
019	PSA	022	021	Save me from the mouth of the lion, and my humility from the horns of the single-horned beast.
019	PSA	022	022	I will declare your name to my brothers. In the midst of the Church, I will praise you.
019	PSA	022	023	You who fear the Lord, praise him. All the offspring of Jacob, glorify him.
019	PSA	022	024	May all the offspring of Israel fear him. For he has neither spurned nor despised the pleas of the poor. Neither has he turned his face away from me. And when I cried out to him, he heeded me.
019	PSA	022	025	My praise is with you, within a great church. I will pay my vows in the sight of those who fear him.
019	PSA	022	026	The poor will eat and be satisfied, and those who yearn for the Lord will praise him. Their hearts will live forever and ever.
019	PSA	022	027	All the ends of the earth will remember, and they will be converted to the Lord. And all the families of the Gentiles will adore in his sight.
019	PSA	022	028	For the kingdom belongs to the Lord, and he will have dominion over the Gentiles.
019	PSA	022	029	All the fat of the earth have gnashed their teeth, and they have adored. In his sight, they will fall down, all those who descend to the ground.
019	PSA	022	030	And my soul will live for him, and my offspring will serve him.
019	PSA	022	031	There will be announced for the Lord a future generation, and the heavens will announce his justice to a people who will be born, whom the Lord has made.
019	PSA	023	001	A Psalm of David. The Lord directs me, and nothing will be lacking to me.
019	PSA	023	002	He has settled me here, in a place of pasture. He has led me out to the water of refreshment.
019	PSA	023	003	He has converted my soul. He has led me away on the paths of justice, for the sake of his name.
019	PSA	023	004	For, even if I should walk in the midst of the shadow of death, I will fear no evils. For you are with me. Your rod and your staff, they have given me consolation.
019	PSA	023	005	You have prepared a table in my sight, opposite those who trouble me. You have anointed my head with oil, and my cup, which inebriates me, how brilliant it is!
019	PSA	023	006	And your mercy will follow me all the days of my life, and so may I dwell in the house of the Lord for length of days.
019	PSA	024	001	For the First Sabbath. A Psalm of David. The earth and all its fullness belong to the Lord: the whole world and all that dwells in it.
019	PSA	024	002	For he has founded it upon the seas, and he has prepared it upon the rivers.
019	PSA	024	003	Who will ascend to the mountain of the Lord? And who will stand in his holy place?
019	PSA	024	004	The innocent of hands and the clean of heart, who has not received his soul in vain, nor sworn deceitfully to his neighbor.
019	PSA	024	005	He will receive a blessing from the Lord, and mercy from God, his Savior.
019	PSA	024	006	This is the generation that seeks him, that seeks the face of the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	024	007	Lift up your gates, you princes, and be lifted up, eternal gates. And the King of Glory shall enter.
019	PSA	024	008	Who is this King of Glory? The Lord who is strong and powerful; the Lord powerful in battle.
019	PSA	024	009	Lift up your gates, you princes, and be lifted up, eternal gates. And the King of Glory shall enter.
019	PSA	024	010	Who is this King of Glory? The Lord of virtue. He himself is the King of Glory.
019	PSA	025	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. To you, Lord, I have lifted up my soul.
019	PSA	025	002	In you, my God, I trust. Let me not be put to shame.
019	PSA	025	003	And do not let my enemies laugh at me. For all who remain with you will not be confounded.
019	PSA	025	004	May all those who act unjustly over nothing be confounded. O Lord, demonstrate your ways to me, and teach me your paths.
019	PSA	025	005	Direct me in your truth, and teach me. For you are God, my Savior, and I remain with you all day long.
019	PSA	025	006	O Lord, remember your compassion and your mercies, which are from ages past.
019	PSA	025	007	Do not remember the offenses of my youth and my ignorances. Remember me according to your mercy, because of your goodness, O Lord.
019	PSA	025	008	The Lord is sweet and righteous. Because of this, he will grant a law to those who fall short in the way.
019	PSA	025	009	He will direct the mild in judgment. He will teach the meek his ways.
019	PSA	025	010	All the ways of the Lord are mercy and truth, to those who yearn for his covenant and his testimonies.
019	PSA	025	011	Because of your name, O Lord, you will pardon my sin, for it is great.
019	PSA	025	012	Which is the man who fears the Lord? He has established a law for him, on the way that he has chosen.
019	PSA	025	013	His soul will dwell upon good things, and his offspring will inherit the earth.
019	PSA	025	014	The Lord is a firmament to those who fear him, and his covenant will be made manifest to them.
019	PSA	025	015	My eyes are ever toward the Lord, for he will pull my feet from the snare.
019	PSA	025	016	Look upon me and have mercy on me; for I am alone and poor.
019	PSA	025	017	The troubles of my heart have been multiplied. Deliver me from my needfulness.
019	PSA	025	018	See my lowliness and my hardship, and release all my offenses.
019	PSA	025	019	Consider my enemies, for they have been multiplied, and they have hated me with an unjust hatred.
019	PSA	025	020	Preserve my soul and rescue me. I will not be ashamed, for I have hoped in you.
019	PSA	025	021	The innocent and the righteous have adhered to me, because I have remained with you.
019	PSA	025	022	Free Israel, O God, from all his tribulations.
019	PSA	026	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. Judge me, Lord, for I have been walking in my innocence, and by hoping in the Lord, I will not be weakened.
019	PSA	026	002	Examine me, Lord, and test me: enkindle my temperament and my heart.
019	PSA	026	003	For your mercy is before my eyes, and I am serene in your truth.
019	PSA	026	004	I have not sat with the council of emptiness, and I will not enter with those who carry out injustice.
019	PSA	026	005	I have hated the assembly of the malicious; and I will not sit with the impious.
019	PSA	026	006	I will wash my hands among the innocent, and I will surround your altar, O Lord,
019	PSA	026	007	so that I may hear the voice of your praise and describe all your wonders.
019	PSA	026	008	O Lord, I have loved the beauty of your house and the dwelling place of your glory.
019	PSA	026	009	O God, do not let my soul perish with the impious, nor my life with the men of blood,
019	PSA	026	010	in whose hands are iniquities: their right hand has been filled by bribes.
019	PSA	026	011	But as for me, I have been walking in my innocence. Redeem me, and have mercy on me.
019	PSA	026	012	My foot has stood firm in the straight path. In the churches, I will bless you, O Lord.
019	PSA	027	001	A Psalm of David, before he was sealed. The Lord is my light and my salvation, whom shall I fear? The Lord is the protector of my life, of whom shall I be afraid?
019	PSA	027	002	Meanwhile, the guilty draw near to me, so as to eat my flesh. Those who trouble me, my enemies, have themselves been weakened and have fallen.
019	PSA	027	003	If entrenched armies were to stand together against me, my heart would not fear. If a battle were to rise up against me, I would have hope in this.
019	PSA	027	004	One thing I have asked of the Lord, this I will seek: that I may dwell in the house of the Lord all the days of my life, so that I may behold the delight of the Lord, and may visit his temple.
019	PSA	027	005	For he has hidden me in his tabernacle. In the day of evils, he has protected me in the hidden place of his tabernacle.
019	PSA	027	006	He has exalted me upon the rock, and now he has exalted my head above my enemies. I have circled around and offered a sacrifice of loud exclamation in his tabernacle. I will sing, and I will compose a psalm, to the Lord.
019	PSA	027	007	Hear my voice, O Lord, with which I have cried out to you. Have mercy on me, and hear me.
019	PSA	027	008	My heart has spoken to you; my face has sought you. I yearn for your face, O Lord.
019	PSA	027	009	Do not turn your face away from me. In your wrath, do not turn aside from your servant. Be my helper. Do not abandon me, and do not despise me, O God, my Savior.
019	PSA	027	010	For my father and my mother have left me behind, but the Lord has taken me up.
019	PSA	027	011	O Lord, establish a law for me in your way, and direct me in the right path, because of my enemies.
019	PSA	027	012	Do not surrender me to the souls of those who trouble me. For unjust witnesses have risen up against me, and iniquity has lied to itself.
019	PSA	027	013	I believe that I shall see the good things of the Lord in the land of the living.
019	PSA	027	014	Wait for the Lord, act manfully; and let your heart be strengthened, and remain with the Lord.
019	PSA	028	001	A Psalm of David himself. To you, Lord, I will cry out. My God, do not be silent toward me. For if you remain silent toward me, I will become like those who descend into the pit.
019	PSA	028	002	Hear, O Lord, the voice of my supplication, when I pray to you, when I lift up my hands toward your holy temple.
019	PSA	028	003	Do not draw me away together with sinners; and let me not perish with those who work iniquity, who speak peacefully to their neighbor, yet evils are in their hearts.
019	PSA	028	004	Give to them according to their works and according to the wickedness of their inventions. Assign to them according to the works of their hands. Repay them with their own retribution.
019	PSA	028	005	Since they have not understood the works of the Lord and the works of his hands, you will destroy them, and you will not build them up.
019	PSA	028	006	Blessed is the Lord, for he has heard the voice of my supplication.
019	PSA	028	007	The Lord is my helper and my protector. In him, my heart has hoped and I have been helped. And my flesh has flourished again. And from my will, I shall confess to him.
019	PSA	028	008	The Lord is the strength of his people and the protector of the salvation of his Christ.
019	PSA	028	009	O Lord, save your people and bless your inheritance, and reign over them and exalt them, even unto eternity.
019	PSA	029	001	A Psalm of David, at the completion of the tabernacle. Bring to the Lord, O sons of God, bring to the Lord the sons of rams.
019	PSA	029	002	Bring to the Lord, glory and honor. Bring to the Lord, glory for his name. Adore the Lord in his holy court.
019	PSA	029	003	The voice of the Lord is over the waters. The God of majesty has thundered. The Lord is over many waters.
019	PSA	029	004	The voice of the Lord is in virtue. The voice of the Lord is in magnificence.
019	PSA	029	005	The voice of the Lord shatters the cedars. And the Lord will shatter the cedars of Lebanon.
019	PSA	029	006	And it will break them into pieces, like a calf of Lebanon, and in the same way as the beloved son of the single-horned beast.
019	PSA	029	007	The voice of the Lord cuts through the flame of fire.
019	PSA	029	008	The voice of the Lord shakes the desert. And the Lord will quake the desert of Kadesh.
019	PSA	029	009	The voice of the Lord is preparing the stags, and he will reveal the dense woods. And in his temple, all will speak his glory.
019	PSA	029	010	The Lord causes the great flood to dwell. And the Lord will sit as King in eternity.
019	PSA	029	011	The Lord will give virtue to his people. The Lord will bless his people in peace.
019	PSA	030	001	A Canticle Psalm. In dedication to the house of David. I will extol you, Lord, for you have sustained me, and you have not allowed my enemies to delight over me.
019	PSA	030	002	O Lord my God, I have cried out to you, and you have healed me.
019	PSA	030	003	Lord, you led my soul away from Hell. You have saved me from those who descend into the pit.
019	PSA	030	004	Sing a psalm to the Lord, you his saints, and confess with remembrance of his holiness.
019	PSA	030	005	For wrath is in his indignation, and life is in his will. Toward evening, weeping will linger, and toward morning, gladness.
019	PSA	030	006	But I have said in my abundance: “I will never be disturbed.”
019	PSA	030	007	O Lord, in your will, you made virtue preferable to beauty for me. You turned your face away from me, and I became disturbed.
019	PSA	030	008	To you, Lord, I will cry out. And I will make supplication to my God.
019	PSA	030	009	What use would there be in my blood, if I descend into corruption? Will dust confess to you or announce your truth?
019	PSA	030	010	The Lord has heard, and he has been merciful to me. The Lord has become my helper.
019	PSA	030	011	You have turned my mourning into gladness for me. You have cut off my sackcloth, and you have surrounded me with joy.
019	PSA	030	012	So then, may my glory sing to you, and may I not regret it. O Lord, my God, I will confess to you for eternity.
019	PSA	031	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David according to an ecstasy. In you, Lord, I have hoped; let me never be confounded. In your justice, deliver me.
019	PSA	031	002	Incline your ear to me. Hasten to rescue me. Be for me a protector God and a house of refuge, so as to accomplish my salvation.
019	PSA	031	003	For you are my strength and my refuge; and for the sake of your name, you will lead me and nourish me.
019	PSA	031	004	You will lead me out of this snare, which they have hidden for me. For you are my protector.
019	PSA	031	005	Into your hands, I commend my spirit. You have redeemed me, O Lord, God of truth.
019	PSA	031	006	You have hated those who practice emptiness to no purpose. But I have hoped in the Lord.
019	PSA	031	007	I will exult and rejoice in your mercy. For you have looked upon my humility; you have saved my soul from needfulness.
019	PSA	031	008	And you have not enclosed me in the hands of the enemy. You have set my feet in a spacious place.
019	PSA	031	009	Have mercy on me, Lord, for I am troubled. My eye has been disturbed by wrath, along with my soul and my gut.
019	PSA	031	010	For my life has fallen into sorrow, and my years into sighing. My virtue has been weakened in poverty, and my bones have been disturbed.
019	PSA	031	011	I have become a disgrace among all my enemies, and even more so to my neighbors, and a dread to my acquaintances. Those who catch sight of me, flee away from me.
019	PSA	031	012	I have become forgotten, like one dead to the heart. I have become like a damaged utensil.
019	PSA	031	013	For I have heard the harsh criticism of many who linger in the area. While assembled together against me in that place, they deliberated on how to take away my life.
019	PSA	031	014	But I have hoped in you, O Lord. I said, “You are my God.”
019	PSA	031	015	My fate is in your hands. Rescue me from the hand of my enemies and from those who are persecuting me.
019	PSA	031	016	Shine your face upon your servant. Save me in your mercy.
019	PSA	031	017	Do not let me be confounded, Lord, for I have called upon you. Let the impious be ashamed and be drawn down into Hell.
019	PSA	031	018	May deceitful lips be silenced: those that speak iniquity against the just, in arrogance and in abusiveness.
019	PSA	031	019	How great is the multitude of your sweetness, O Lord, which you keep hidden for those who fear you, which you have perfected for those who hope in you, in the sight of the sons of men.
019	PSA	031	020	You hide them in the concealment of your face, from the disturbance of men. You protect them in your tabernacle, from the contradiction of tongues.
019	PSA	031	021	Blessed is the Lord. For he has shown his wonderful mercy to me, in a fortified city.
019	PSA	031	022	But I said in the excess of my mind: “I have been cast away from the glance of your eyes.” And so, you heeded the voice of my prayer, while I was still crying out to you.
019	PSA	031	023	Love the Lord, all you his saints. For the Lord will require truth, and he will abundantly repay those who act with arrogance.
019	PSA	031	024	Act manfully, and let your heart be strengthened, all you who hope in the Lord.
019	PSA	032	001	The understanding of David himself. Blessed are they whose iniquities have been forgiven and whose sins have been covered.
019	PSA	032	002	Blessed is the man to whom the Lord has not imputed sin, and in whose spirit there is no deceit.
019	PSA	032	003	Because I was silent, my bones grew old, while still I cried out all day long.
019	PSA	032	004	For, day and night, your hand was heavy upon me. I have been converted in my anguish, while still the thorn is piercing.
019	PSA	032	005	I have acknowledged my offense to you, and I have not concealed my injustice. I said, “I will confess against myself, my injustice to the Lord,” and you forgave the impiety of my sin.
019	PSA	032	006	For this, everyone who is holy will pray to you in due time. Yet truly, in a flood of many waters, they will not draw near to him.
019	PSA	032	007	You are my refuge from the tribulation that has surrounded me. You are my exultation: rescue me from those who are surrounding me.
019	PSA	032	008	I will give you understanding, and I will instruct you in this way, in which you will walk. I will fix my eyes upon you.
019	PSA	032	009	Do not become like the horse and the mule, which have no understanding. Their jaws are constrained with bit and bridle, so as not to draw near to you.
019	PSA	032	010	Many are the scourges of the sinner, but mercy will surround him that hopes in the Lord.
019	PSA	032	011	Rejoice in the Lord and exult, you just ones, and glory, all you upright of heart.
019	PSA	033	001	A Psalm of David. Exult in the Lord, you just ones; together praise the upright.
019	PSA	033	002	Confess to the Lord with stringed instruments; sing psalms to him with the psaltery, the instrument of ten strings.
019	PSA	033	003	Sing to him a new song. Sing psalms to him skillfully, with loud exclamation.
019	PSA	033	004	For the word of the Lord is upright, and all his works are in faith.
019	PSA	033	005	He loves mercy and judgment. The earth is full of the mercy of the Lord.
019	PSA	033	006	By the word of the Lord, the heavens were established, and all their power, by the Spirit of his mouth:
019	PSA	033	007	gathering together the waters of the sea, as if in a container, placing the depths in storage.
019	PSA	033	008	Let all the earth fear the Lord, and may all the inhabitants of the world quake before him.
019	PSA	033	009	For he spoke, and they became. He commanded, and they were created.
019	PSA	033	010	The Lord scatters the counsels of the nations. Moreover, he reproves the thoughts of the people, and he rejects the counsels of the leaders.
019	PSA	033	011	But the counsel of the Lord remains for eternity, the thoughts of his heart from generation to generation.
019	PSA	033	012	Blessed is the nation whose God is the Lord, the people whom he has chosen as his inheritance.
019	PSA	033	013	The Lord has looked down from heaven. He has seen all the sons of men.
019	PSA	033	014	From his well-prepared dwelling place, he has gazed upon all who dwell on the earth.
019	PSA	033	015	He has formed the hearts of each one of them; he understands all their works.
019	PSA	033	016	The king is not saved by great power, nor will the giant be saved by his many powers.
019	PSA	033	017	The horse is false safety; for he will not be saved by the abundance of his powers.
019	PSA	033	018	Behold, the eyes of the Lord are on those who fear him and on those who hope in his mercy,
019	PSA	033	019	so as to rescue their souls from death and to feed them during famine.
019	PSA	033	020	Our soul remains with the Lord. For he is our helper and protector.
019	PSA	033	021	For in him, our heart will rejoice, and in his holy name, we have hoped.
019	PSA	033	022	Let your mercy be upon us, O Lord, just as we have hoped in you.
019	PSA	034	001	To David, when he changed his appearance in the sight of Abimelech, and so he dismissed him, and he went away. I will bless the Lord at all times. His praise will be ever in my mouth.
019	PSA	034	002	In the Lord, my soul will be praised. May the meek listen and rejoice.
019	PSA	034	003	Magnify the Lord with me, and let us extol his name in itself.
019	PSA	034	004	I sought the Lord, and he heeded me, and he carried me away from all my tribulations.
019	PSA	034	005	Approach him and be enlightened, and your faces will not be confounded.
019	PSA	034	006	This poor one cried out, and the Lord heeded him, and he saved him from all his tribulations.
019	PSA	034	007	The Angel of the Lord will encamp around those who fear him, and he will rescue them.
019	PSA	034	008	Taste and see that the Lord is sweet. Blessed is the man who hopes in him.
019	PSA	034	009	Fear the Lord, all you his saints. For there is no destitution for those who fear him.
019	PSA	034	010	The rich have been needy and hungry, but those who seek the Lord will not be deprived of any good thing.
019	PSA	034	011	Come forward, sons. Listen to me. I will teach you the fear of the Lord.
019	PSA	034	012	Which is the man who wills life, who chooses to see good days?
019	PSA	034	013	Prohibit your tongue from evil and your lips from speaking deceit.
019	PSA	034	014	Turn away from evil, and do good. Inquire about peace, and pursue it.
019	PSA	034	015	The eyes of the Lord are on the just, and his ears are with their prayers.
019	PSA	034	016	But the countenance of the Lord is upon those who do evil, to perish the remembrance of them from the earth.
019	PSA	034	017	The just cried out, and the Lord heard them, and he freed them from all their tribulations.
019	PSA	034	018	The Lord is near to those who are troubled in heart, and he will save the humble in spirit.
019	PSA	034	019	Many are the afflictions of the just, but from them all the Lord will free them.
019	PSA	034	020	The Lord preserves all of their bones, not one of them shall be broken.
019	PSA	034	021	The death of a sinner is very harmful, and those who hate the just will fare badly.
019	PSA	034	022	The Lord will redeem the souls of his servants, and none of those who hope in him will fare badly.
019	PSA	035	001	Of David himself. O Lord, judge those who harm me; assail those who attack me.
019	PSA	035	002	Take hold of weapons and a shield, and rise up in assistance to me.
019	PSA	035	003	Bring forth the spear, and close in on those who persecute me. Say to my soul, “I am your salvation.”
019	PSA	035	004	Let them be confounded and in awe, who pursue my soul. Let them be turned back and be confounded, who think up evil against me.
019	PSA	035	005	May they become like dust before the face of the wind, and let the Angel of the Lord hem them in.
019	PSA	035	006	May their way become dark and slippery, and may the Angel of the Lord pursue them.
019	PSA	035	007	For, without cause, they have concealed their snare for me unto destruction. Over nothing, they have rebuked my soul.
019	PSA	035	008	Let the snare, of which he is ignorant, come upon him, and let the deception, which he has hidden, take hold of him: and may he fall into that very snare.
019	PSA	035	009	But my soul will exult in the Lord and delight over his salvation.
019	PSA	035	010	All my bones will say, “Lord, who is like you?” He rescues the needy from the hand of the stronger one, the indigent and the poor from those who plunder him.
019	PSA	035	011	Unfair witnesses have risen up, interrogating me about things of which I am ignorant.
019	PSA	035	012	They repaid me evil for good, to the deprivation of my soul.
019	PSA	035	013	But as for me, when they were harassing me, I was clothed with haircloth. I humbled my soul with fasting, and my prayer will become my sinews.
019	PSA	035	014	Like a neighbor, and like our brother, so did I please; like one mourning and contrite, so was I humbled.
019	PSA	035	015	And they have been joyful against me, and they joined together. Scourges have been gathered over me, and I was ignorant of it.
019	PSA	035	016	They have been scattered, yet they were unremorseful. They have tested me. They scoffed at me with scorn. They gnashed their teeth over me.
019	PSA	035	017	Lord, when will you look down upon me? Restore my soul from before their malice, my only one from before the lions.
019	PSA	035	018	I will confess to you in a great Church. I will praise you among a weighty people.
019	PSA	035	019	May those who are my unjust adversaries not be glad over me: those who have hated me without cause, and who nod agreement with their eyes.
019	PSA	035	020	For indeed, they spoke peacefully to me; and speaking with passion to the earth, they intended deceit.
019	PSA	035	021	And they opened their mouth wide over me. They said, “Well, well, our eyes have seen.”
019	PSA	035	022	You have seen, O Lord, do not be silent. Lord, do not depart from me.
019	PSA	035	023	Rise up and be attentive to my judgment, to my cause, my God and my Lord.
019	PSA	035	024	Judge me according to your justice, O Lord, my God, and do not let them be glad over me.
019	PSA	035	025	Do not let them say in their hearts, “Well, well, to our soul.” Neither let them say, “We have devoured him.”
019	PSA	035	026	Let them blush and be in awe together, those who congratulate at my misfortunes. Let them be clothed with confusion and awe, who speak great things against me.
019	PSA	035	027	Let them exult and rejoice, who wish my justice, and let them ever say, “The Lord be magnified,” who will the peace of his servant.
019	PSA	035	028	And so my tongue will express your justice: your praise all day long.
019	PSA	036	001	Unto the end. To the servant of the Lord, David himself. The unjust one has said within himself that he would commit offenses. There is no fear of God before his eyes.
019	PSA	036	002	For he has acted deceitfully in his sight, such that his iniquity will be found to be hatred.
019	PSA	036	003	The words of his mouth are iniquity and deceit. He is unwilling to understand, so that he may act well.
019	PSA	036	004	He has been considering iniquity on his bed. He has set himself on every way that is not good; moreover, he has not hated evil.
019	PSA	036	005	Lord, your mercy is in heaven, and your truth is even to the clouds.
019	PSA	036	006	Your justice is like the mountains of God. Your judgments are a great abyss. Men and beasts, you will save, O Lord.
019	PSA	036	007	How you have multiplied your mercy, O God! And so the sons of men will hope under the cover of your wings.
019	PSA	036	008	They will be inebriated with the fruitfulness of your house, and you will give them to drink from the torrent of your enjoyment.
019	PSA	036	009	For with you is the fountain of life; and within your light, we will see the light.
019	PSA	036	010	Extend your mercy before those who know you, and your justice to these, who are upright in heart.
019	PSA	036	011	May arrogant feet not approach me, and may the hand of the sinner not disturb me.
019	PSA	036	012	In that place, those who work iniquity have fallen. They have been expelled; they were not able to stand.
019	PSA	037	001	A Psalm of David himself. Do not choose to imitate the malicious; neither should you envy those who work iniquity.
019	PSA	037	002	For they will quickly wither away like dry grass, and in like manner to kitchen herbs, they will soon droop.
019	PSA	037	003	Hope in the Lord and do good, and dwell in the land, and so you shall be pastured with its riches.
019	PSA	037	004	Delight in the Lord, and he will grant to you the petitions of your heart.
019	PSA	037	005	Reveal your way to the Lord, and hope in him, and he will accomplish it.
019	PSA	037	006	And he will bring forth your justice like the light, and your judgment like the midday.
019	PSA	037	007	Be subject to the Lord and pray to him. Do not choose to compete with him who prospers in his way, with the man who does injustice.
019	PSA	037	008	Cease from wrath and leave behind rage. Do not choose to imitate the malicious.
019	PSA	037	009	For those who are malicious will be exterminated. But those who remain with the Lord, these will inherit the land.
019	PSA	037	010	Yet still a little while, and the sinner will not be. And you will search his place and find nothing.
019	PSA	037	011	But the meek shall inherit the earth, and they will delight in the multitude of peace.
019	PSA	037	012	The sinner will observe the just, and he will gnash his teeth over him.
019	PSA	037	013	But the Lord will laugh at him: for he knows in advance that his day will come.
019	PSA	037	014	The sinners have drawn the sword, they have bent their bow, so as to cast down the poor and the needy, so as to massacre the upright of heart.
019	PSA	037	015	Let their sword enter into their own hearts, and let their bow be broken.
019	PSA	037	016	A little is better to the just than the many riches of sinners.
019	PSA	037	017	For the arms of sinners will be crushed, but the Lord confirms the just.
019	PSA	037	018	The Lord knows the days of the immaculate, and their inheritance will be in eternity.
019	PSA	037	019	They will not be confounded in an evil time; and in days of famine, they will be satisfied:
019	PSA	037	020	for sinners will perish. Truly, the adversaries of the Lord, soon after they have been honored and exalted, will fade away, in the same way that smoke fades away.
019	PSA	037	021	The sinner will lend and not release, but the just one shows compassion and donates.
019	PSA	037	022	For those who bless him will inherit the earth, but those who curse him will perish.
019	PSA	037	023	The steps of a man will be directed by the Lord, and he will choose his way.
019	PSA	037	024	When he falls, he will not be harmed, because the Lord places his hand under him.
019	PSA	037	025	I have been young, and now I am old; and I have not seen the just forsaken, nor his offspring seeking bread.
019	PSA	037	026	He shows compassion and lends, all day long, and his offspring will be in blessing.
019	PSA	037	027	Turn away from evil and do good, and dwell forever and ever.
019	PSA	037	028	For the Lord loves judgment, and he will not abandon his saints. They will be kept safe in eternity. The unjust will be punished, and the offspring of the impious will perish.
019	PSA	037	029	But the just will inherit the earth, and they will dwell upon it forever and ever.
019	PSA	037	030	The mouth of the just one will express wisdom, and his tongue will speak judgment.
019	PSA	037	031	The law of his God is in his heart, and his steps shall not be supplanted.
019	PSA	037	032	The sinner considers the just one and seeks to put him to death.
019	PSA	037	033	But the Lord will not abandon him into his hands, nor condemn him, when he will be judged.
019	PSA	037	034	Wait for the Lord, and keep to his way. And he will exalt you, so as to inherit the land that you may seize. When the sinners will have passed away, then you shall see.
019	PSA	037	035	I have seen the impious over-exalted, and lifted up like the cedars of Lebanon.
019	PSA	037	036	And I passed by, and behold, he was not. And I sought him, and his place was not found.
019	PSA	037	037	Keep to innocence, and gaze upon fairness: because there are allotments for the peaceful man.
019	PSA	037	038	But the unjust will be destroyed together: the allotments of the impious will pass away.
019	PSA	037	039	But the salvation of the just is from the Lord, and he is their protector in time of tribulation.
019	PSA	037	040	And the Lord will help them and free them. And he will rescue them from sinners and save them, because they have hoped in him.
019	PSA	038	001	A Psalm of David, in commemoration of the Sabbath. O Lord, do not rebuke me in your fury, nor chastise me in your wrath.
019	PSA	038	002	For your arrows have been driven into me, and your hand has been confirmed over me.
019	PSA	038	003	There is no health in my flesh before the face of your wrath. There is no peace for my bones before the face of my sins.
019	PSA	038	004	For my iniquities have walked over my head, and they have been like a heavy burden weighing upon me.
019	PSA	038	005	My sores have putrefied and been corrupted before the face of my foolishness.
019	PSA	038	006	I have become miserable, and I have been bent down, even to the end. I have walked with contrition all day long.
019	PSA	038	007	For my loins have been filled with illusions, and there is no health in my flesh.
019	PSA	038	008	I have been afflicted and greatly humbled. I bellowed from the groaning of my heart.
019	PSA	038	009	O Lord, all my desire is before you, and my groaning before you has not been hidden.
019	PSA	038	010	My heart has been disturbed. My strength has abandoned me, and the light of my eyes has abandoned me, and it is not with me.
019	PSA	038	011	My friends and my neighbors have drawn near and stood against me. And those who were next to me stood far apart. And those who sought my soul used violence.
019	PSA	038	012	And those who sought evil accusations against me were speaking emptiness. And they practiced deceitfulness all day long.
019	PSA	038	013	But, like someone deaf, I did not hear. And I was like someone mute, not opening his mouth.
019	PSA	038	014	And I became like a man who does not hear, and who has no reproofs in his mouth.
019	PSA	038	015	For in you, Lord, I have hoped. You will listen to me, O Lord my God.
019	PSA	038	016	For I said, “Lest at any time, my enemies might rejoice over me,” and, “While my feet are being shaken, they have spoken great things against me.”
019	PSA	038	017	For I have been prepared for scourges, and my sorrow is ever before me.
019	PSA	038	018	For I will announce my iniquity, and I will think about my sin.
019	PSA	038	019	But my enemies live, and they have been stronger than me. And those who have wrongfully hated me have been multiplied.
019	PSA	038	020	Those who render evil for good have dragged me down, because I followed goodness.
019	PSA	038	021	Do not forsake me, O Lord my God. Do not depart from me.
019	PSA	038	022	Be attentive to my help, O Lord, the God of my salvation.
019	PSA	039	001	Unto the end. For Jeduthun himself. A Canticle of David. I said, “I will keep to my ways, so that I will not offend with my tongue.” I posted a guard at my mouth, when a sinner took up a position against me.
019	PSA	039	002	I was silenced and humbled, and I was quiet before good things, and my sorrow was renewed.
019	PSA	039	003	My heart grew hot within me, and, during my (meditation) a fire would flare up.
019	PSA	039	004	I spoke with my tongue, “O Lord, make me know my end, and what the number of my days will be, so that I may know what is lacking to me.”
019	PSA	039	005	Behold, you have made my days measurable, and, before you, my substance is as nothing. Yet truly, all things are vanity: every living man.
019	PSA	039	006	So then, truly man passes by like an image; even so, he is disquieted in vain. He stores up, and he knows not for whom he will gather these things.
019	PSA	039	007	And now, what is it that awaits me? Is it not the Lord? And my substance is with you.
019	PSA	039	008	Rescue me from all my iniquities. You have handed me over as a reproach to the foolish.
019	PSA	039	009	I was silenced, and I did not open my mouth, because it was you who acted.
019	PSA	039	010	Remove your scourges from me.
019	PSA	039	011	I fall short at corrections from the strength of your hand. For you have chastised man for iniquity. And you have made his soul shrink away like a spider. Nevertheless, it is in vain that any man be disquieted.
019	PSA	039	012	O Lord, heed my prayer and my supplication. Pay attention to my tears. Do not be silent. For I am a newcomer with you, and a sojourner, just as all my fathers were.
019	PSA	039	013	Forgive me, so that I may be refreshed, before I will go forth and be no more.
019	PSA	040	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David himself. I have waited expectantly for the Lord, and he was attentive to me.
019	PSA	040	002	And he heard my prayers and he led me out of the pit of misery and the quagmire. And he stationed my feet upon a rock, and he directed my steps.
019	PSA	040	003	And he sent a new canticle into my mouth, a song to our God. Many will see, and they will fear; and they will hope in the Lord.
019	PSA	040	004	Blessed is the man whose hope is in the name of the Lord, and who has no respect for vanities and absurd falsehoods.
019	PSA	040	005	You have accomplished your many wonders, O Lord my God, and there is no one similar to you in your thoughts. I have announced and I have spoken: they are multiplied beyond number.
019	PSA	040	006	Sacrifice and oblation, you did not want. But you have perfected ears for me. Holocaust and sin offering, you did not require.
019	PSA	040	007	Then I said, “Behold, I draw near.” At the head of the book, it has been written of me:
019	PSA	040	008	that I should do your will. My God, I have willed it. And your law is in the midst of my heart.
019	PSA	040	009	I have announced your justice in a great Church: behold, I will not restrain my lips. O Lord, you have known it.
019	PSA	040	010	I have not concealed your justice within my heart. I have spoken your truth and your salvation. I have not concealed your mercy and your truth from a great assembly.
019	PSA	040	011	O Lord, do not take your tender mercies far from me. Your mercy and your truth ever sustain me.
019	PSA	040	012	For evils without number have surrounded me. My iniquities have taken hold of me, and I was not able to see. They have been multiplied beyond the hairs of my head. And my heart has forsaken me.
019	PSA	040	013	Be pleased, O Lord, to rescue me. Look down, O Lord, to help me.
019	PSA	040	014	Let them together be confounded and awed, who seek after my soul to steal it away. Let them be turned back and be in awe, who wish evils upon me.
019	PSA	040	015	Let them bear their confusion all at once, who say to me, “Well, well.”
019	PSA	040	016	Let all who seek you exult and rejoice over you. And let those who love your salvation always say, “May the Lord be magnified.”
019	PSA	040	017	But I am a beggar and poor. The Lord has been concerned about me. You are my helper and my protector. My God, do not delay.
019	PSA	041	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David himself. Blessed is he who shows understanding toward the needy and the poor. The Lord will deliver him in the evil day.
019	PSA	041	002	May the Lord preserve him and give him life, and make him blessed upon the earth. And may he not hand him over to the will of his adversaries.
019	PSA	041	003	May the Lord bring him help on his bed of sorrow. In his infirmity, you have changed his entire covering.
019	PSA	041	004	I said, “O Lord, be merciful to me. Heal my soul, because I have sinned against you.”
019	PSA	041	005	My enemies have spoken evils against me. When will he die and his name perish?
019	PSA	041	006	And when he came in to see me, he was speaking emptiness. His heart gathered iniquity to itself. He went outside, and he was speaking in the same way.
019	PSA	041	007	All my enemies were whispering against me. They were thinking up evils against me.
019	PSA	041	008	They established an unjust word against me. Will he that sleeps no longer rise again?
019	PSA	041	009	For even the man of my peace, in whom I hoped, who ate my bread, has greatly supplanted me.
019	PSA	041	010	But you, O Lord, have mercy on me, and raise me up again. And I will requite them.
019	PSA	041	011	By this, I knew that you preferred me: because my adversary will not rejoice over me.
019	PSA	041	012	But you have sustained me, because of my innocence, and you have confirmed me in your sight in eternity.
019	PSA	041	013	Blessed is the Lord God of Israel, for all generations and even forever. Amen. Amen.
019	PSA	042	001	Unto the end. The understanding of the sons of Korah. As the deer longs for fountains of water, so my soul longs for you, O God.
019	PSA	042	002	My soul has thirsted for the strong living God. When will I draw close and appear before the face of God?
019	PSA	042	003	My tears have been my bread, day and night. Meanwhile, it is said to me daily: “Where is your God?”
019	PSA	042	004	These things I have remembered; and my soul within me, I have poured out. For I will cross into the place of the wonderful tabernacle, all the way to the house of God, with a voice of exultation and confession, the sound of feasting.
019	PSA	042	005	Why are you sad, my soul? And why do you disquiet me? Hope in God, for I will still confess to him: the salvation of my countenance,
019	PSA	042	006	and my God. My soul has been troubled within myself. Because of this, I will remember you from the land of the Jordan and from Hermon, from the little mountain.
019	PSA	042	007	Abyss calls upon abyss, with the voice of your floodgate. All your heights and your waves have passed over me.
019	PSA	042	008	In the daylight, the Lord has ordered his mercy; and in the night, a canticle to him. With me is a prayer to the God of my life.
019	PSA	042	009	I will say to God, “You are my supporter. Why have you forgotten me? And why do I walk in mourning, while my adversary afflicts me?”
019	PSA	042	010	While my bones are being broken, my enemies, who trouble me, have reproached me. Meanwhile, they say to me every single day, “Where is your God?”
019	PSA	042	011	My soul, why are you saddened? And why do you disquiet me? Hope in God, for I will still confess to him: the salvation of my countenance and my God.
019	PSA	043	001	A Psalm of David. Judge me, O God, and discern my cause from that of a nation not holy; rescue me from a man unjust and deceitful.
019	PSA	043	002	For you are God, my strength. Why have you rejected me? And why do I walk in sadness, while the adversary afflicts me?
019	PSA	043	003	Send forth your light and your truth. They have guided me and led me, to your holy mountain and into your tabernacles.
019	PSA	043	004	And I will enter, up to the altar of God, to God who enlivens my youthfulness. To you, O God, my God, I will confess upon a stringed instrument.
019	PSA	043	005	Why are you sad, my soul? And why do you disquiet me? Hope in God, for I will still give praise to him: the salvation of my countenance and my God.
019	PSA	044	001	Unto the end. To the sons of Korah, toward understanding. We have heard, O God, with our own ears. Our fathers have announced to us the work that you wrought in their days and in the days of antiquity.
019	PSA	044	002	Your hand dispersed the Gentiles, and you transplanted them. You afflicted a people, and you expelled them.
019	PSA	044	003	For they did not take possession of the land by their sword, and their own arm did not save them. But your right hand and your arm, and the light of your countenance did so, because you were pleased with them.
019	PSA	044	004	You yourself are my king and my God, who commands the salvation of Jacob.
019	PSA	044	005	With you, we will brandish a horn before our enemies; and in your name, we will spurn those rising up against us.
019	PSA	044	006	For I will not hope in my bow, and my sword will not save me.
019	PSA	044	007	For you have saved us from those who afflict us, and you have bewildered those who hate us.
019	PSA	044	008	In God, we will give praise all day long; and in your name, we will confess forever.
019	PSA	044	009	But now, you have rejected and bewildered us, and you will not go forth with our armies, O God.
019	PSA	044	010	You have turned our back to our enemies, and those who hated us have plundered for themselves.
019	PSA	044	011	You have given us over like sheep for food. You have scattered us among the Gentiles.
019	PSA	044	012	You have sold your people without a price, and no great number was exchanged for them.
019	PSA	044	013	You have set us as a disgrace to our neighbors, a scoff and a derision to those who are around us.
019	PSA	044	014	You have set us as a parable among the Gentiles, a shaking of the head among the peoples.
019	PSA	044	015	All day long my shame is before me, and the confusion of my face has covered me,
019	PSA	044	016	before the voice of the reproacher and the commentator, before the face of the adversary and the pursuer.
019	PSA	044	017	All these things have come upon us, yet we have not forgotten you, and we have not acted unjustly in your covenant.
019	PSA	044	018	And our heart has not turned back. And you have not diverted our steps from your way.
019	PSA	044	019	For you humbled us in a place of affliction, and the shadow of death has covered us.
019	PSA	044	020	If we have forgotten the name of our God, and if we have extended our hands to a foreign god,
019	PSA	044	021	will not God find this out? For he knows the secrets of the heart.
019	PSA	044	022	For, because of you, we are being killed all day long. We are considered as sheep for the slaughter.
019	PSA	044	023	Rise up. Why do you fall asleep, O Lord? Rise up, and do not reject us in the end.
019	PSA	044	024	Why do you turn your face away, and why do you forget our needfulness and our tribulation?
019	PSA	044	025	For our soul has been humbled into the dust. Our belly has been bound to the earth.
019	PSA	044	026	Rise up, O Lord. Help us and redeem us, because of your name.
019	PSA	045	001	Unto the end. For those who will be changed. To the sons of Korah, toward understanding. A Canticle for the Beloved. My heart has uttered a good word. I speak of my works to the king. My tongue is like the pen of a scribe who writes quickly.
019	PSA	045	002	You are a brilliant form before the sons of men. Grace has been poured freely into your lips. Because of this, God has blessed you in eternity.
019	PSA	045	003	Fasten your sword to your thigh, O most powerful one.
019	PSA	045	004	With your splendor and your excellence extended, proceed prosperously, and reign for the sake of truth and meekness and justice, and so will your right hand lead you wondrously.
019	PSA	045	005	Your arrows are sharp; the people will fall under you, with the hearts of the enemies of the king.
019	PSA	045	006	Your throne, O God, is forever and ever. The scepter of your kingdom is a scepter of true aim.
019	PSA	045	007	You have loved justice and hated iniquity. Because of this, God, your God, has anointed you, before your co-heirs, with the oil of gladness.
019	PSA	045	008	Myrrh and balsam and cinnamon perfume your garments, from the houses of ivory. From these, they have delighted you:
019	PSA	045	009	the daughters of kings in your honor. The queen assisted at your right hand, in clothing of gold, encircled with diversity.
019	PSA	045	010	Listen, daughter, and see, and incline your ear. And forget your people and your father’s house.
019	PSA	045	011	And the king will desire your beauty. For he is the Lord your God, and they will adore him.
019	PSA	045	012	And the daughters of Tyre will entreat your countenance with gifts: all the rich men of the people.
019	PSA	045	013	All the glory of the daughter of its king is inside, in golden fringes,
019	PSA	045	014	clothed all around with diversities. After her, virgins will be led to the king. Her neighbors will be brought to you.
019	PSA	045	015	They will be brought with gladness and exultation. They will be led into the temple of the king.
019	PSA	045	016	For your fathers, sons have been born to you. You will establish them as leaders over all the earth.
019	PSA	045	017	They will remember your name always, for generation after generation. Because of this, people will confess to you in eternity, even forever and ever.
019	PSA	046	001	Unto the end. To the sons of Korah, for confidants. A Psalm. Our God is our refuge and strength, a helper in the tribulations that have greatly overwhelmed us.
019	PSA	046	002	Because of this, we will not be afraid when the earth will be turbulent and the mountains will be transferred into the heart of the sea.
019	PSA	046	003	They thundered, and the waters were stirred up among them; the mountains have been disturbed by his strength.
019	PSA	046	004	The frenzy of the river rejoices the city of God. The Most High has sanctified his tabernacle.
019	PSA	046	005	God is in its midst; it will not be shaken. God will assist it in the early morning.
019	PSA	046	006	The peoples have been disturbed, and the kingdoms have been bowed down. He uttered his voice: the earth has been moved.
019	PSA	046	007	The Lord of hosts is with us. The God of Jacob is our supporter.
019	PSA	046	008	Draw near and behold the works of the Lord: what portents he has set upon the earth,
019	PSA	046	009	carrying away wars even to the end of the earth. He will crush the bow and break the weapons, and he will burn the shield with fire.
019	PSA	046	010	Be empty, and see that I am God. I will be exalted among the peoples, and I will be exalted upon the earth.
019	PSA	046	011	The Lord of hosts is with us. The God of Jacob is our supporter.
019	PSA	047	001	Unto the end. A Psalm for the sons of Korah. All nations, clap your hands. Shout joyfully to God with a voice of exultation.
019	PSA	047	002	For the Lord is exalted and terrible: a great King over all the earth.
019	PSA	047	003	He has subjected the peoples to us and subdued the nations under our feet.
019	PSA	047	004	He has chosen us for his inheritance: the splendor of Jacob, whom he has loved.
019	PSA	047	005	God ascends with jubilation, and the Lord with the voice of the trumpet.
019	PSA	047	006	Sing psalms to our God, sing psalms. Sing psalms to our King, sing psalms.
019	PSA	047	007	For God is the King of all the earth. Sing psalms wisely.
019	PSA	047	008	God will reign over the peoples. God sits upon his holy throne.
019	PSA	047	009	The leaders of the peoples have been gathered together by the God of Abraham. For the strong gods of the earth have been exceedingly exalted.
019	PSA	048	001	A Canticle Psalm. To the sons of Korah, on the second Sabbath. The Lord is great and exceedingly praiseworthy, in the city of our God, on his holy mountain.
019	PSA	048	002	Mount Zion is being founded with the exultation of the whole earth, on the north side, the city of the great king.
019	PSA	048	003	In her houses, God will be known, since he will support her.
019	PSA	048	004	For behold, the kings of the earth have been gathered together; they have convened as one.
019	PSA	048	005	Such did they see, and they were astonished: they were disturbed, they were moved.
019	PSA	048	006	Trembling took hold of them. In that place, their pains were that of a woman in labor.
019	PSA	048	007	With a vehement spirit, you will crush the ships of Tarshish.
019	PSA	048	008	As we have heard, so we have seen, in the city of the Lord of hosts, in the city of our God. God has founded it in eternity.
019	PSA	048	009	We have received your mercy, O God, in the midst of your temple.
019	PSA	048	010	According to your name, O God, so does your praise reach to the ends of the earth. Your right hand is full of justice.
019	PSA	048	011	Let mount Zion rejoice, and let the daughters of Judah exult, because of your judgments, O Lord.
019	PSA	048	012	Encircle Zion and embrace her. Discourse in her towers.
019	PSA	048	013	Set your hearts on her virtue. And distribute her houses, so that you may discourse of it in another generation.
019	PSA	048	014	For this is God, our God, in eternity and forever and ever. He will rule us forever.
019	PSA	049	001	Unto the end. A Psalm to the sons of Korah. Hear these things, all nations. Pay attention, all inhabitants of the world:
019	PSA	049	002	whoever is earth-born, you sons of men, together as one, the rich and the poor.
019	PSA	049	003	My mouth will speak wisdom, and the meditation of my heart will speak prudence.
019	PSA	049	004	I will incline my ear to a parable. I will open my case with the psaltery.
019	PSA	049	005	Why should I fear in the evil day? The iniquity at my heel will surround me.
019	PSA	049	006	Those who trust in their own strength and who glory in the multitude of their riches,
019	PSA	049	007	no brother redeems, nor will man buy back. He will not give to God his appeasement,
019	PSA	049	008	nor the price for the redemption of his soul. And he will labor continuously,
019	PSA	049	009	and he will still live, until the end.
019	PSA	049	010	He will not see death, when he sees the wise dying: the foolish and the senseless will perish together. And they will leave their riches to strangers.
019	PSA	049	011	And their sepulchers will be their houses forever, their tabernacles from generation to generation. They have called their names in their own lands.
019	PSA	049	012	And man, when he was held in honor, did not understand. He has been compared to the senseless beasts, and he has become like them.
019	PSA	049	013	This way of theirs is a scandal to them. And afterwards, they will delight in their mouth.
019	PSA	049	014	They have been placed in Hell like sheep. Death will feed on them. And the just will have dominion over them in the morning. And their help will grow old in Hell for their glory.
019	PSA	049	015	Even so, truly God will redeem my soul from the hand of Hell, when he will receive me.
019	PSA	049	016	Do not be afraid, when a man will have been made rich, and when the glory of his house will have been multiplied.
019	PSA	049	017	For when he dies, he will take nothing away, and his glory will not descend with him.
019	PSA	049	018	For his soul will be blessed in his lifetime, and he will admit to you when you do good to him.
019	PSA	049	019	He will even enter with the progeny of his fathers, but, even in eternity, he will not see the light.
019	PSA	049	020	Man, when he was in honor, did not understand. He has been compared to the senseless beasts, and he has become like them.
019	PSA	050	001	A Psalm of Asaph. The God of gods, the Lord has spoken, and he has called the earth, from the rising of the sun even to its setting,
019	PSA	050	002	from Zion, the brilliance of his beauty.
019	PSA	050	003	God will arrive manifestly. Our God also will not keep silence. A fire will flare up in his sight, and a mighty tempest will surround him.
019	PSA	050	004	He will call to heaven from above, and to the earth, to discern his people.
019	PSA	050	005	Gather his holy ones to him, you who order his covenant above sacrifices.
019	PSA	050	006	And the heavens will announce his justice. For God is the judge.
019	PSA	050	007	Listen, my people, and I will speak. Listen, Israel, and I will testify for you. I am God, your God.
019	PSA	050	008	I will not reprove you for your sacrifices. Moreover, your holocausts are ever in my sight.
019	PSA	050	009	I will not accept calves from your house, nor he-goats from your flocks.
019	PSA	050	010	For all the wild beasts of the forest are mine: the cattle on the hills and the oxen.
019	PSA	050	011	I know all the flying things of the air, and the beauty of the field is with me.
019	PSA	050	012	If I should be hungry, I would not tell you: for the whole world is mine, and all its plentitude.
019	PSA	050	013	Shall I gnaw on the flesh of bulls? Or would I drink the blood of goats?
019	PSA	050	014	Offer to God the sacrifice of praise, and pay your vows to the Most High.
019	PSA	050	015	And call upon me in the day of tribulation. I will rescue you, and you will honor me.
019	PSA	050	016	But to the sinner, God has said: Why do you discourse on my justices, and take up my covenant through your mouth?
019	PSA	050	017	Truly, you have hated discipline, and you have cast my sermons behind you.
019	PSA	050	018	If you saw a thief, you ran with him, and you have placed your portion with adulterers.
019	PSA	050	019	Your mouth has abounded with malice, and your tongue has concocted deceits.
019	PSA	050	020	Sitting, you spoke against your brother, and you set up a scandal against your mother’s son.
019	PSA	050	021	These things you have done, and I was silent. You thought, unjustly, that I ought to be like you. But I will reprove you, and I will set myself against your face.
019	PSA	050	022	Understand these things, you who forget God; lest at any time, he might quickly take you away, and there would be no one to rescue you.
019	PSA	050	023	The sacrifice of praise will honor me. And in that place is the journey by which I will reveal to him the salvation of God.
019	PSA	051	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David, when Nathan the prophet came to him, after he went to Bathsheba. Be merciful to me, O God, according to your great mercy. And, according to the plentitude of your compassion, wipe out my iniquity.
019	PSA	051	002	Wash me once again from my iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin.
019	PSA	051	003	For I know my iniquity, and my sin is ever before me.
019	PSA	051	004	Against you only have I sinned, and I have done evil before your eyes. And so, you are justified in your words, and you will prevail when you give judgment.
019	PSA	051	005	For behold, I was conceived in iniquities, and in sinfulness did my mother conceive me.
019	PSA	051	006	For behold, you have loved truth. The obscure and hidden things of your wisdom, you have manifested to me.
019	PSA	051	007	You will sprinkle me with hyssop, and I will be cleansed. You will wash me, and I will be made whiter than snow.
019	PSA	051	008	In my hearing, you will grant gladness and rejoicing. And the bones that have been humbled will exult.
019	PSA	051	009	Turn your face away from my sins, and erase all my iniquities.
019	PSA	051	010	Create a clean heart in me, O God. And renew an upright spirit within my inmost being.
019	PSA	051	011	Do not cast me away from your face; and do not take your Holy Spirit from me.
019	PSA	051	012	Restore to me the joy of your salvation, and confirm me with an unsurpassed spirit.
019	PSA	051	013	I will teach the unjust your ways, and the impious will be converted to you.
019	PSA	051	014	Free me from blood, O God, the God of my salvation, and my tongue will extol your justice.
019	PSA	051	015	O Lord, you will open my lips, and my mouth will announce your praise.
019	PSA	051	016	For if you had desired sacrifice, I would certainly have given it, but with holocausts, you will not be delighted.
019	PSA	051	017	A crushed spirit is a sacrifice to God. A contrite and humbled heart, O God, you will not spurn.
019	PSA	051	018	Act kindly, Lord, in your good will toward Zion, so that the walls of Jerusalem may be built up.
019	PSA	051	019	Then you will accept the sacrifice of justice, oblations, and holocausts. Then they will lay calves upon your altar.
019	PSA	052	001	Unto the end. The understanding of David. When Doeg the Edomite came and reported to Saul, David went to the house of Ahimelech. Why do you glory in malice, you who are powerful in iniquity?
019	PSA	052	002	All day long your tongue thinks up injustice. Like a sharp razor, you have wrought deceit.
019	PSA	052	003	You have loved malice above goodness, and iniquity more than speaking righteousness.
019	PSA	052	004	You have loved all precipitous words, you deceitful tongue.
019	PSA	052	005	Because of this, God will destroy you in the end. He will pull you up, and he will remove you from your tabernacle and your root from the land of the living.
019	PSA	052	006	The just will see and be afraid, and they will laugh over him, and say:
019	PSA	052	007	“Behold the man who did not set God as his helper. But he hoped in the multitude of his riches, and so he prevailed in his emptiness.”
019	PSA	052	008	But I, like a fruitful olive tree in the house of God, have hoped in the mercy of God unto eternity, and forever and ever.
019	PSA	052	009	I will confess to you forever, because you have accomplished it. And I will wait on your name, for it is good in the sight of your saints.
019	PSA	053	001	Unto the end. For Mahalath: the thoughts of David. The fool has said in his heart, “There is no God.” They were corrupted, and they became abominable with iniquities. There is no one who does good.
019	PSA	053	002	God gazed down from heaven on the sons of men, to see if there were any who were considering or seeking God.
019	PSA	053	003	All have gone astray; together they have become useless. There is no one who does good; there is not even one.
019	PSA	053	004	Will they never learn: all those who work iniquity, who devour my people like a meal of bread?
019	PSA	053	005	They have not called upon God. In that place, they have trembled in fear, where there was no fear. For God has scattered the bones of those who please men. They have been confounded, because God has spurned them.
019	PSA	053	006	Who will grant from Zion the salvation of Israel? Jacob will exult, when God will convert the captivity of his people; and Israel will rejoice.
019	PSA	054	001	Unto the end. In verses, the understanding of David, when the Ziphites had arrived and they said to Saul, “Has not David been hidden with us?” Save me, O God, by your name, and judge me in your virtue.
019	PSA	054	002	O God, listen to my prayer. Pay attention to the words of my mouth.
019	PSA	054	003	For strangers have risen up against me, and the strong have sought my soul. And they have not set God before their eyes.
019	PSA	054	004	For behold, God is my helper, and the Lord is the protector of my soul.
019	PSA	054	005	Turn back the evils upon my adversaries, and ruin them by your truth.
019	PSA	054	006	I will freely sacrifice to you, and I will confess your name, O God, because it is good.
019	PSA	054	007	For you have quickly rescued me from all tribulation, and my eye has looked down upon my enemies.
019	PSA	055	001	Unto the end. In verses, the understanding of David. Listen to my prayer, O God, and despise not my supplication.
019	PSA	055	002	Be attentive to me, and heed me. I have been grieved in my training, and I have been disturbed
019	PSA	055	003	at the voice of the adversary and at the tribulation of the sinner. For they have diverted iniquities toward me, and they have been harassing me with rage.
019	PSA	055	004	My heart has become disturbed within me, and the dread of death has fallen over me.
019	PSA	055	005	Fear and trembling have overwhelmed me, and darkness has buried me.
019	PSA	055	006	And I said, “Who will give me wings like the dove, so that I may fly away and take rest?”
019	PSA	055	007	Behold, I have fled far away, and I linger in solitude.
019	PSA	055	008	I waited for him who saved me from a weak-minded spirit and from a tempest.
019	PSA	055	009	Cast them down, O Lord, and divide their tongues. For I have seen iniquity and contradiction in the city.
019	PSA	055	010	Day and night, iniquity will surround it upon its walls, and hardship is in its midst,
019	PSA	055	011	with injustice. And usury and deceit have not fallen away from its streets.
019	PSA	055	012	For if my enemy had spoken evil about me, certainly, I would have sustained it. And if he who hated me had been speaking great things against me, I would perhaps have hidden myself from him.
019	PSA	055	013	Truly, you are a man of one mind: my leader and my acquaintance,
019	PSA	055	014	who took sweet food together with me. In the house of God, we walked side-by-side.
019	PSA	055	015	Let death come upon them, and let them descend alive into Hellfire. For there is wickedness in their dwellings, in their midst.
019	PSA	055	016	But I have cried out to God, and the Lord will save me.
019	PSA	055	017	Evening and morning and midday, I will discourse and announce, and he will heed my voice.
019	PSA	055	018	He will redeem my soul in peace from those who draw near to me. For, among the many, they were with me.
019	PSA	055	019	God will hear, and He who is before time will humble them. For there is no change with them, and they have not feared God.
019	PSA	055	020	He has stretched forth his hand in retribution. They have contaminated his covenant.
019	PSA	055	021	They were divided by the wrath of his countenance, and his heart has drawn near. His words are smoother than oil, and they are arrows.
019	PSA	055	022	Cast your cares upon the Lord, and he will nurture you. He will not allow the just to be tossed about forever.
019	PSA	055	023	Truly, O God, you will lead them away into the well of death. Bloody and deceitful men will not divide their days in half. But I will hope in you, O Lord.
019	PSA	056	001	Unto the end. For the people who have become far removed from the Sacred. Of David, with the inscription of a title, when the Philistines held him in Gath. Have mercy on me, O God, because man has trampled over me. All day long, he has afflicted me by fighting against me.
019	PSA	056	002	My enemies have trampled over me all day long. For those who make war against me are many.
019	PSA	056	003	From the height of the day, I will be afraid. But truly, I will hope in you.
019	PSA	056	004	In God, I will praise my words. In God, I have put my trust. I will not fear what flesh can do to me.
019	PSA	056	005	All day long, they curse my words. All their intentions are for evil against me.
019	PSA	056	006	They will dwell and hide themselves. They will watch my heel, just as they waited for my soul;
019	PSA	056	007	because of this, nothing will save them. In your anger, you will crush the people.
019	PSA	056	008	O God, I have announced my life to you. You have placed my tears in your sight, and even in your promise.
019	PSA	056	009	Then my enemies will be turned back. On whatever day that I call upon you, behold, I know that you are my God.
019	PSA	056	010	In God, I will praise the word. In the Lord, I will praise his speech.
019	PSA	056	011	In God, I have hoped. I will not fear what man can do to me.
019	PSA	056	012	My vows to you, O God, are in me. I will repay them. Praises be to you.
019	PSA	056	013	For you have rescued my soul from death and my feet from slipping, so that I may be pleasing in the sight of God, in the light of the living.
019	PSA	057	001	Unto the end. May you not destroy. Of David, with the inscription of a title, when he fled from Saul into a cave. Be merciful to me, O God, be merciful to me. For my soul trusts in you. And I will hope in the shadow of your wings, until iniquity passes away.
019	PSA	057	002	I will cry out to God Most High, to God who has been kind to me.
019	PSA	057	003	He sent from heaven and freed me. He has surrendered into disgrace those who trampled me. God has sent his mercy and his truth.
019	PSA	057	004	And he has rescued my soul from the midst of the young lions. I slept troubled. The sons of men: their teeth are weapons and arrows, and their tongue is a sharp sword.
019	PSA	057	005	Be exalted above the heavens, O God, and your glory above all the earth.
019	PSA	057	006	They prepared a snare for my feet, and they bowed down my soul. They dug a pit before my face, yet they have fallen into it.
019	PSA	057	007	My heart is prepared, O God, my heart is prepared. I will sing, and I will compose a psalm.
019	PSA	057	008	Rise up, my glory. Rise up, psaltery and harp. I will arise in early morning.
019	PSA	057	009	I will confess to you, O Lord, among the peoples. I will compose a psalm to you among the nations.
019	PSA	057	010	For your mercy has been magnified, even to the heavens, and your truth, even to the clouds.
019	PSA	057	011	Be exalted above the heavens, O God, and your glory above all the earth.
019	PSA	058	001	Unto the end. May you not destroy. Of David, with the inscription of a title. If, truly and certainly, you speak justice, then judge what is right, you sons of men.
019	PSA	058	002	For, even in your heart, you work iniquity. Your hands construct injustice on the earth.
019	PSA	058	003	Sinners have become foreigners from the womb; they have gone astray from conception. They have been speaking falsehoods.
019	PSA	058	004	Their fury is similar to that of a serpent; it is like a deaf asp, who even blocks her ears,
019	PSA	058	005	who will not listen to the voice of charmers, nor even to the enchanter who chants wisely.
019	PSA	058	006	God will crush their teeth within their own mouth. The Lord will break the molars of the lions.
019	PSA	058	007	They will come to nothing, like water flowing away. He has aimed his bow, while they are being weakened.
019	PSA	058	008	Like wax that flows, they will be carried away. Fire has fallen upon them, and they will not see the sun.
019	PSA	058	009	Before your thorns could know the brier, he consumes them alive, as if in rage.
019	PSA	058	010	The just one will rejoice when he sees vindication. He will wash his hands in the blood of the sinner.
019	PSA	058	011	And man will say, “If the just one is fruitful, then, truly, there is a God judging them on earth.”
019	PSA	059	001	Unto the end. May you not destroy. Of David, with the inscription of a title, when Saul sent and watched his house, in order to execute him. Rescue me from my enemies, my God, and free me from those who rise up against me.
019	PSA	059	002	Rescue me from those who work iniquity, and save me from men of blood.
019	PSA	059	003	For behold, they have seized my soul. The strong have rushed upon me.
019	PSA	059	004	And it is neither my iniquity, nor my sin, O Lord. I have run and gone directly, without iniquity.
019	PSA	059	005	Rise up to meet me, and see: even you, O Lord, the God of hosts, the God of Israel. Reach out to visit all nations. Do not take pity on all those who work iniquity.
019	PSA	059	006	They will return toward evening, and they will suffer hunger like dogs, and they will wander around the city.
019	PSA	059	007	Behold, they will speak with their mouth, and a sword is in their lips: “For who has heard us?”
019	PSA	059	008	And you, O Lord, will laugh at them. You will lead all the Gentiles to nothing.
019	PSA	059	009	I will guard my strength toward you, for you are God, my supporter.
019	PSA	059	010	My God, his mercy will precede me.
019	PSA	059	011	God will oversee my enemies for me. Do not slay them, lest at times my people may forget them. Scatter them by your virtue. And depose them, O Lord, my protector,
019	PSA	059	012	by the offense of their mouth and by the speech of their lips. And may they be caught in their arrogance. And, for their cursing and lying, they will be made known
019	PSA	059	013	at the consummation, in the fury of the consummation, and so they will be no more. And they will know that God will rule over Jacob, even to the ends of the earth.
019	PSA	059	014	They will return toward evening, and they will suffer hunger like dogs, and they will wander around the city.
019	PSA	059	015	They will be dispersed in order to gnaw, and truly, when they will not have been satisfied, they will murmur.
019	PSA	059	016	But I will sing your strength, and I will extol your mercy, in the morning. For you have been my supporter and my refuge in the day of my tribulation.
019	PSA	059	017	To you, my helper, I will sing psalms. For you are God, my supporter. My God is my mercy.
019	PSA	060	001	Unto the end. For those who will be changed, with the inscription of a title, of David himself, for instruction: when he set fire to Mesopotamia of Syria and Sobal, and Joab turned back and struck Idumea, in the valley of the salt pits, twelve thousand men. O God, you have rejected us, and you have ruined us. You became angry, and yet you have been merciful to us.
019	PSA	060	002	You have moved the earth, and you have disturbed it. Heal its breaches, for it has been moved.
019	PSA	060	003	You have revealed to your people difficulties. You have made us drink the wine of remorse.
019	PSA	060	004	You have given a warning sign to those who fear you, so that they may flee from before the face of the bow, so that your beloved may be delivered.
019	PSA	060	005	Save me with your right hand, and hear me.
019	PSA	060	006	God has spoken in his holy place: I will rejoice, and I will divide Shechem, and I will measure the steep valley of the tabernacles.
019	PSA	060	007	Gilead is mine, and Manasseh is mine. And Ephraim is the strength of my head. Judah is my king.
019	PSA	060	008	Moab is the cooking pot of my hope. Into Idumea, I will extend my shoe. To me, the foreigners have been made subject.
019	PSA	060	009	Who will lead me into the fortified city? Who will lead me all the way to Idumea?
019	PSA	060	010	Will not you, O God, who has rejected us? And will not you, O God, go out with our armies?
019	PSA	060	011	Grant us help from tribulation. For salvation from man is empty.
019	PSA	060	012	In God, we will act virtuously. And those who trouble us, he will lead to nothing.
019	PSA	061	001	Unto the end. With hymns, of David. O God, pay attention to my supplication. Be attentive to my prayer.
019	PSA	061	002	I cried out to you from the ends of the earth. When my heart was in anguish, you exalted me on a rock. You have led me,
019	PSA	061	003	for you have been my hope, a tower of strength before the face of the enemy.
019	PSA	061	004	I will dwell in your tabernacle forever. I will be protected under the cover of your wings.
019	PSA	061	005	For you, my God, have listened to my prayer. You have granted an inheritance to those who fear your name.
019	PSA	061	006	You will add days to the days of the king, to his years, even to the time of generation after generation.
019	PSA	061	007	He remains in eternity, in the sight of God. Who will long for his mercy and truth?
019	PSA	061	008	So I will compose a psalm to your name, forever and ever, so that I may repay my vows from day to day.
019	PSA	062	001	Unto the end. For Jeduthun. A Psalm of David. Will my soul not be subject to God? For from him is my salvation.
019	PSA	062	002	Yes, he himself is my God and my salvation. He is my supporter; I will be moved no more.
019	PSA	062	003	How is it that you rush against a man? Every one of you puts to death, as if you were pulling down a ruined wall, leaning over and falling apart.
019	PSA	062	004	So, truly, they intended to reject my price. I ran in thirst. They blessed with their mouth and cursed with their heart.
019	PSA	062	005	Yet, truly, my soul will be subject to God. For from him is my patience.
019	PSA	062	006	For he is my God and my Savior. He is my helper; I will not be expelled.
019	PSA	062	007	In God is my salvation and my glory. He is the God of my help, and my hope is in God.
019	PSA	062	008	All peoples gathered together: trust in him. Pour out your hearts in his sight. God is our helper for eternity.
019	PSA	062	009	So, truly, the sons of men are untrustworthy. The sons of men are liars in the scales, so that, by emptiness, they may deceive among themselves.
019	PSA	062	010	Do not trust in iniquity, and do not desire plunder. If riches flow toward you, do not be willing to set your heart on them.
019	PSA	062	011	God has spoken once. I have heard two things: that power belongs to God,
019	PSA	062	012	and that mercy belongs to you, O Lord. For you will repay each one according to his works.
019	PSA	063	001	A Psalm of David, when he was in the desert of Idumea. O God, my God: to you, I keep vigil until first light. For you, my soul has thirsted, to you my body, in so many ways.
019	PSA	063	002	By a deserted land, both inaccessible and waterless, so I have appeared in the sanctuary before you, in order to behold your virtue and your glory.
019	PSA	063	003	For your mercy is better than life itself. It is you my lips will praise.
019	PSA	063	004	So will I bless you in my life, and I will lift up my hands in your name.
019	PSA	063	005	Let my soul be filled, as if with marrow and fatness; and my mouth will give praise with exultant lips.
019	PSA	063	006	When I have remembered you on my bed in the morning, I will meditate on you.
019	PSA	063	007	For you have been my helper. And I will exult under the cover of your wings.
019	PSA	063	008	My soul has clung close to you. Your right hand has supported me.
019	PSA	063	009	Truly, these ones have sought my soul in vain. They will enter into the lower parts of the earth.
019	PSA	063	010	They will be delivered into the hand of the sword. They will be the portions of foxes.
019	PSA	063	011	Truly, the king will rejoice in God: all those who swear by him will be praised, because the mouth of those who speak iniquity has been blocked.
019	PSA	064	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. Hear, O God, my prayer of supplication. Rescue my soul from the fear of the enemy.
019	PSA	064	002	You have protected me from the assembly of the malignant, from a multitude of workers of iniquity.
019	PSA	064	003	For they have sharpened their tongues like a sword; they have formed their bow into a bitter thing,
019	PSA	064	004	so that they may shoot arrows from hiding at the immaculate.
019	PSA	064	005	They will suddenly shoot arrows at him, and they will not be afraid. They are resolute in their wicked talk. They have discussed hidden snares. They have said, “Who will see them?”
019	PSA	064	006	They have been searching carefully for iniquities. Their exhaustive search has failed. Man will approach with a deep heart,
019	PSA	064	007	and God will be exalted. The arrows of the little ones have become their wounds,
019	PSA	064	008	and their tongues have been weakened against them. All those who saw them have been troubled;
019	PSA	064	009	and every man was afraid. And they announced the works of God, and they understood his acts.
019	PSA	064	010	The just will rejoice in the Lord, and they will hope in him. And all the upright of heart will be praised.
019	PSA	065	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. A Canticle of Jeremiah and Ezekiel to the people of the captivity, when they began to go into exile. O God, a hymn adorns you in Zion, and a vow will be repaid to you in Jerusalem.
019	PSA	065	002	Hear my prayer: all flesh will come to you.
019	PSA	065	003	Words of iniquity have prevailed over us. And you will pardon our impieties.
019	PSA	065	004	Blessed is he whom you have chosen and taken up. He will dwell in your courts. We will be filled with the good things of your house. Holy is your temple:
019	PSA	065	005	wonderful in equity. Hear us, O God our Savior, the hope of all the ends of the earth and of a sea far away.
019	PSA	065	006	You prepare the mountains in your virtue, wrapped with power.
019	PSA	065	007	You stir up the depths of the sea, the noise of its waves. The nations will be troubled,
019	PSA	065	008	and those who dwell at the limits will be afraid, before your signs. You will make the passing of morning and evening enjoyable.
019	PSA	065	009	You have visited the earth, and you have saturated it. You have enriched it in so many ways. The river of God has been filled with water. You have prepared their food. For thus is its preparation.
019	PSA	065	010	Drench its streams, multiply its fruits; it will spring up and rejoice in its showers.
019	PSA	065	011	You will bless the crown of the year with your kindness, and your fields will be filled with abundance.
019	PSA	065	012	The beauty of the desert will fatten, and the hills will be wrapped with exultation.
019	PSA	065	013	The rams of the sheep have been clothed, and the valleys will abound with grain. They will cry out; yes, they will even utter a hymn.
019	PSA	066	001	Unto the end. A Canticle Psalm of the Resurrection. Shout joyfully to God, all the earth.
019	PSA	066	002	Proclaim a psalm to his name. Give glory to his praise.
019	PSA	066	003	Exclaim to God, “How terrible are your works, O Lord!” According to the fullness of your virtue, your enemies will speak lies about you.
019	PSA	066	004	Let all the earth adore you and sing psalms to you. May it sing a psalm to your name.
019	PSA	066	005	Draw near and see the works of God, who is terrible in his counsels over the sons of men.
019	PSA	066	006	He converts the sea into dry land. They will cross the river on foot. There, we will rejoice in him.
019	PSA	066	007	He rules by his virtue for eternity. His eyes gaze upon the nations. May those who exasperate him, not be exalted in themselves.
019	PSA	066	008	Bless our God, you Gentiles, and make the voice of his praise be heard.
019	PSA	066	009	He has set my soul toward life, and he has granted that my feet may not be shaken.
019	PSA	066	010	For you, O God, have tested us. You have examined us by fire, just as silver is examined.
019	PSA	066	011	You have led us into a snare. You have placed tribulations on our back.
019	PSA	066	012	You have set men over our heads. We have crossed through fire and water. And you have led us out to refreshment.
019	PSA	066	013	I will enter your house with holocausts. I will repay my vows to you,
019	PSA	066	014	which my lips discerned and my mouth spoke, in my tribulation.
019	PSA	066	015	I will offer to you holocausts full of marrow, with the burnt offerings of rams. I will offer to you bulls as well as goats.
019	PSA	066	016	Draw near and listen, all you who fear God, and I will describe to you how much he has done for my soul.
019	PSA	066	017	I cried out to him with my mouth, and I extolled him under my breath.
019	PSA	066	018	If I have seen iniquity in my heart, the Lord would not heed me.
019	PSA	066	019	And yet, God has heeded me and he has attended to the voice of my supplication.
019	PSA	066	020	Blessed is God, who has not removed my prayer, nor his mercy, from me.
019	PSA	067	001	Unto the end. With hymns, a Canticle Psalm of David. May God have mercy on us and bless us. May he shine his countenance upon us, and may he have mercy on us.
019	PSA	067	002	So may we know your way upon the earth, your salvation among all nations.
019	PSA	067	003	Let the peoples confess to you, O God. Let all the peoples confess to you.
019	PSA	067	004	May the nations rejoice and exult. For you judge the peoples with equity, and you direct the nations on earth.
019	PSA	067	005	Let the peoples confess to you, O God. Let all the peoples confess to you.
019	PSA	067	006	The earth has provided her fruit. May God, our God, bless us.
019	PSA	067	007	May God bless us, and may all the ends of the earth fear him.
019	PSA	068	001	Unto the end. A Canticle Psalm of David himself. May God rise up, and may his enemies be scattered, and may those who hate him flee from before his face.
019	PSA	068	002	Just as smoke vanishes, so may they vanish. Just as wax flows away before the face of fire, so may sinners pass away before the face of God.
019	PSA	068	003	And so, let the just feast, and let them exult in the sight of God and be delighted in gladness.
019	PSA	068	004	Sing to God, sing a psalm to his name. Make a path for him, who ascends over the west. The Lord is his name. Exult in his sight; they will be stirred up before his face,
019	PSA	068	005	the father of orphans and the judge of widows. God is in his holy place.
019	PSA	068	006	It is God who makes men dwell in a house under one custom. He leads out those who are strongly bound, and similarly, those who exasperate, who dwell in sepulchers.
019	PSA	068	007	O God, when you departed in the sight of your people, when you passed through the desert,
019	PSA	068	008	the earth was moved, for the heavens rained down before the face of the God of Sinai, before the face of the God of Israel.
019	PSA	068	009	You will set aside for your inheritance, O God, a willing rain. And though it was weak, truly, you have made it perfect.
019	PSA	068	010	Your animals will dwell in it. O God, in your sweetness, you have provided for the poor.
019	PSA	068	011	The Lord will give the word to evangelizers, along with great virtue.
019	PSA	068	012	The King of virtue is beloved among the beloved. And the beauty of the house will divide spoils.
019	PSA	068	013	If you take your rest in the midst of the clergy, you will be like a dove whose wings are covered with fine silver and edged with pale gold.
019	PSA	068	014	When heaven discerns kings to be over her, they will be whitened with the snows of Zalmon.
019	PSA	068	015	The mountain of God is a fat mountain, a dense mountain, a thick mountain.
019	PSA	068	016	So then, why are you distrustful of dense mountains? The mountain on which God is well pleased to dwell, even there, the Lord will dwell until the end.
019	PSA	068	017	The chariot of God is ten thousand fold: thousands rejoice. The Lord is with them in Sinai, in the holy place.
019	PSA	068	018	You have ascended on high; you have taken captivity captive. You have accepted gifts among men. For even those who do not believe dwell with the Lord God.
019	PSA	068	019	Blessed is the Lord, day after day. The God of our salvation will make our journey prosper for us.
019	PSA	068	020	Our God is the God who will bring about our salvation, and our Lord is the Lord who has brought an end to death.
019	PSA	068	021	So then, truly, God will break the heads of his enemies, the hairy skull of those who wander around in their offenses.
019	PSA	068	022	The Lord said: I will turn them away from Bashan, I will turn them into the depths of the sea,
019	PSA	068	023	so that your feet may be soaked in the blood of your enemies, so that the tongue of your dogs may be soaked with the same.
019	PSA	068	024	O God, they have seen your arrival, the arrival of my God, of my king who is in a holy place.
019	PSA	068	025	The leaders went ahead, united with the singers of psalms, in the midst of girls playing on timbrels.
019	PSA	068	026	In the churches, bless the Lord God from the fountains of Israel.
019	PSA	068	027	In that place, Benjamin is a youth in ecstasy of mind. The leaders of Judah are their governors: the leaders of Zebulun, the leaders of Naphtali.
019	PSA	068	028	Command by your virtue, O God. Confirm in this place, O God, what you have wrought in us.
019	PSA	068	029	Before your temple in Jerusalem, kings will offer gifts to you.
019	PSA	068	030	Rebuke the wild beasts of the reeds, a congregation of bulls with the cows of the people, for they seek to exclude those who have been tested like silver. Scatter the nations that are pleased by wars.
019	PSA	068	031	Ambassadors will come out of Egypt. Ethiopia will offer in advance her hands to God.
019	PSA	068	032	Sing to God, O kingdoms of the earth. Sing psalms to the Lord. Sing psalms to God.
019	PSA	068	033	He ascends, up to the heaven of the heavens, toward the east. Behold, he will utter his voice, the voice of virtue.
019	PSA	068	034	Give glory to God beyond Israel. His magnificence and his virtue is in the clouds.
019	PSA	068	035	God is wonderful in his saints. The God of Israel himself will give virtue and strength to his people. Blessed is God.
019	PSA	069	001	Unto the end. For those who will be changed: of David. Save me, O God, for the waters have entered, even to my soul.
019	PSA	069	002	I have become stuck in a deep quagmire, and there is no firm footing. I have arrived at the height of the sea, and a tempest has overwhelmed me.
019	PSA	069	003	I have endured hardships, while crying out. My jaws have become hoarse; my eyes have failed. Meanwhile, I hope in my God.
019	PSA	069	004	Those who hate me without cause have been multiplied beyond the hairs of my head. My enemies, who persecuted me unjustly, have been strengthened. Then I was required to pay for what I did not take.
019	PSA	069	005	O God, you know my foolishness, and my offenses have not been hidden from you.
019	PSA	069	006	Let those who wait for you, O Lord, the Lord of hosts, not be shamed in me. Let those who seek you, O God of Israel, not be confounded over me.
019	PSA	069	007	For because of you, I have endured reproach; confusion has covered my face.
019	PSA	069	008	I have become a stranger to my brothers and a sojourner to the sons of my mother.
019	PSA	069	009	For zeal for your house has consumed me, and the reproaches of those who reproached you have fallen upon me.
019	PSA	069	010	And I covered my soul with fasting, and it has become a reproach to me.
019	PSA	069	011	And I put on a haircloth as my garment, and I became a parable to them.
019	PSA	069	012	Those who sat at the gate spoke against me, and those who drank wine made me their song.
019	PSA	069	013	But as for me, truly, my prayer is to you, O Lord. This time has pleased you well, O God. In the multitude of your mercy, in the truth of your salvation, hear me.
019	PSA	069	014	Rescue me from the quagmire, so that I may not become trapped. Free me from those who hate me and from deep waters.
019	PSA	069	015	Do not allow the tempest of water to submerge me, nor the deep to absorb me. And do not allow the well to close in on me.
019	PSA	069	016	Hear me, O Lord, for your mercy is kind. Look upon me, according to the fullness of your compassion.
019	PSA	069	017	And do not turn your face away from your servant, for I am in trouble: heed me quickly.
019	PSA	069	018	Attend to my soul, and free it. Rescue me, because of my enemies.
019	PSA	069	019	You know my reproach, and my confusion, and my reverence.
019	PSA	069	020	All those who trouble me are in your sight; my heart has anticipated reproach and misery. And I sought for one who might grieve together with me, but there was no one, and for one who might console me, and I found no one.
019	PSA	069	021	And they gave me gall for my food. And in my thirst, they gave me vinegar to drink.
019	PSA	069	022	Let their table be a snare before them, and a retribution, and a scandal.
019	PSA	069	023	Let their eyes be darkened, so that they may not see, and may their back always be crooked.
019	PSA	069	024	Pour out your indignation upon them, and may the fury of your anger take hold of them.
019	PSA	069	025	May their dwelling place be deserted, and may there be no one who dwells in their tabernacles.
019	PSA	069	026	For they persecuted whomever you struck. And they have added to the grief of my wounds.
019	PSA	069	027	Assign an iniquity upon their iniquity, and may they not enter into your justice.
019	PSA	069	028	Delete them from the Book of the Living, and let them not be written down with the just.
019	PSA	069	029	I am poor and sorrowful, but your salvation, O God, has taken me up.
019	PSA	069	030	I will praise the name of God with a canticle, and I will magnify him with praise.
019	PSA	069	031	And it will please God more than a new calf producing horns and hoofs.
019	PSA	069	032	Let the poor see and rejoice. Seek God, and your soul will live.
019	PSA	069	033	For the Lord has heard the poor, and he has not despised his prisoners.
019	PSA	069	034	Let the heavens and the earth praise him: the sea, and everything that crawls in it.
019	PSA	069	035	For God will save Zion, and the cities of Judah will be built up. And they will dwell there, and they will acquire it by inheritance.
019	PSA	069	036	And the offspring of his servants will possess it; and those who love his name will dwell in it.
019	PSA	070	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David, in remembrance that the Lord had saved him. O God, reach out to help me. O Lord, hasten to assist me.
019	PSA	070	002	May those who seek my soul be confounded and awed.
019	PSA	070	003	May those who wish evils upon me be turned back and blush with shame. May they be turned away immediately, blushing with shame, who say to me: “Well, well.”
019	PSA	070	004	Let all who seek you exult and rejoice in you, and let those who love your salvation forever say: “The Lord be magnified.”
019	PSA	070	005	I am truly destitute and poor. O God, assist me. You are my helper and my deliverer. O Lord, do not delay.
019	PSA	071	001	A Psalm of David. Of the sons of Jonadab and the former captives. In you, O Lord, I have hoped; do not let me be brought to ruin forever.
019	PSA	071	002	Free me by your justice, and rescue me. Incline your ear to me, and save me.
019	PSA	071	003	Be a God of protection and a place of strength for me, so that you may accomplish my salvation. For you are my firmament and my refuge.
019	PSA	071	004	Rescue me, O my God, from the hand of the sinner, and from the hand of the unjust and those who act against the law.
019	PSA	071	005	For you, O Lord, are my patience: my hope from my youth, O Lord.
019	PSA	071	006	In you, I have been confirmed from conception. From my mother’s womb, you are my protector. In you, I will sing forever.
019	PSA	071	007	I have become to many as if I were a portent, but you are a strong helper.
019	PSA	071	008	Let my mouth be filled with praise, so that I may sing your glory, your greatness all day long.
019	PSA	071	009	Do not cast me off in the time of old age. Do not abandon me when my strength will fail.
019	PSA	071	010	For my enemies have spoken against me. And those who watched for my soul have taken counsel as one,
019	PSA	071	011	saying: “God has abandoned him. Pursue and overtake him. For there is no one to rescue him.”
019	PSA	071	012	O God, do not be far from me. O my God, provide for my assistance.
019	PSA	071	013	May they be confounded, and may they fail, who drag down my soul. Let them be covered with confusion and shame, who seek evils for me.
019	PSA	071	014	But I will always have hope. And I will add more to all your praise.
019	PSA	071	015	My mouth will announce your justice, your salvation all day long. For I have not known letters.
019	PSA	071	016	I will enter into the powers of the Lord. I will be mindful of your justice alone, O Lord.
019	PSA	071	017	You have taught me from my youth, O God. And so I will declare your wonders continuously,
019	PSA	071	018	even in old age and with grey hairs. Do not abandon me, O God, while I announce your arm to every future generation: your power
019	PSA	071	019	and your justice, O God, even to the highest great things that you have done. O God, who is like you?
019	PSA	071	020	How great is the tribulation that you have revealed to me: very great and evil. And so, turning back, you have brought me to life, and you have led me back again from the abyss of the earth.
019	PSA	071	021	You have multiplied your magnificence. And so, turning back to me, you have consoled me.
019	PSA	071	022	Therefore, I will confess your truth to you, with the instruments of the Psalter. O God, I will sing psalms to you with stringed instruments, O Holy One of Israel.
019	PSA	071	023	My lips will exult, when I sing to you, and also my soul, which you have redeemed.
019	PSA	071	024	And even my tongue will meditate on your justice all day long, when those who seek evils for me have been confounded and set in awe.
019	PSA	072	001	A Psalm according to Solomon.
019	PSA	072	002	Give your judgment, O God, to the king, and your justice to the king’s son, to judge your people with justice and your poor with judgment.
019	PSA	072	003	Let the mountains take up peace for the people, and the hills, justice.
019	PSA	072	004	He will judge the poor of the people, and he will bring salvation to the sons of the poor. And he will humble the false accuser.
019	PSA	072	005	And he will remain, with the sun and before the moon, from generation to generation.
019	PSA	072	006	He will descend like rain upon fleece, and like showers showering upon the earth.
019	PSA	072	007	In his days, justice will rise like the sun, with abundance of peace, until the moon is taken away.
019	PSA	072	008	And he will rule from sea to sea and from the river to the limits of the whole world.
019	PSA	072	009	In his sight, the Ethiopians will fall prostrate, and his enemies will lick the ground.
019	PSA	072	010	The kings of Tarshish and the islands will offer gifts. The kings of Arabia and of Seba will bring gifts.
019	PSA	072	011	And all the kings of the earth shall adore him. All nations will serve him.
019	PSA	072	012	For he will free the poor from the powerful, and the poor one who has no helper.
019	PSA	072	013	He will spare the poor and the indigent, and he will bring salvation to the souls of the poor.
019	PSA	072	014	He will redeem their souls from usuries and from iniquity, and their names shall be honorable in his sight.
019	PSA	072	015	And he will live, and to him will be given from the gold of Arabia, and by him they will always adore. They will bless him all day long.
019	PSA	072	016	And there will be a firmament on earth, at the summits of mountains: its fruits will be extolled above Lebanon, and those of the city will flourish like the grass of the earth.
019	PSA	072	017	May his name be blessed forever; may his name remain before the sun. And all the tribes of the earth will be blessed in him. All nations will magnify him.
019	PSA	072	018	Blessed is the Lord, God of Israel, who alone does wondrous things.
019	PSA	072	019	And blessed is the name of his majesty in eternity. And all the earth will be filled with his majesty. Amen. Amen.
019	PSA	072	020	The praises of David, the son of Jesse, have reached an end.
019	PSA	073	001	A Psalm of Asaph. How good is God to Israel, to those who are upright in heart.
019	PSA	073	002	But my feet were nearly moved; my steps had nearly slipped.
019	PSA	073	003	For I was zealous over the iniquitous, seeing the peacefulness of sinners.
019	PSA	073	004	For they have no respect for their death, nor do they have support in their wounds.
019	PSA	073	005	They are not with the hardships of men, nor will they be scourged with men.
019	PSA	073	006	Therefore, arrogance has held on to them. They have been covered with their iniquity and impiety.
019	PSA	073	007	Their iniquity has proceeded, as if from fat. They have parted from the affection of the heart.
019	PSA	073	008	They have thought and spoken wickedness. They have spoken iniquity in high places.
019	PSA	073	009	They have set their mouth against heaven, and their tongue has traversed the earth.
019	PSA	073	010	Therefore, my people will be converted here, and fullness of days will be found in them.
019	PSA	073	011	And they said, “How would God know?” and, “Isn’t there knowledge in high places?”
019	PSA	073	012	Behold, these are sinners, and, abounding in this age, they have obtained riches.
019	PSA	073	013	And I said: So then, it is without purpose that I have justified my heart and washed my hands among the innocent.
019	PSA	073	014	And I have been scourged all day long, and I have received my chastisement in the mornings.
019	PSA	073	015	If I were to say that I would explain this: Behold, I would condemn this nation of your sons.
019	PSA	073	016	I considered, so that I might know this. It is a hardship before me,
019	PSA	073	017	until I may enter into the Sanctuary of God, and understand it to its last part.
019	PSA	073	018	So, because of deceitfulness, truly, you have placed it before them. While they were being lifted up, you were casting them down.
019	PSA	073	019	How have they been brought to desolation? They have suddenly failed. They have perished because of their iniquity.
019	PSA	073	020	As a dream is to those who awaken, O Lord, so will you reduce their image to nothing in your city.
019	PSA	073	021	For my heart has been inflamed, and my temperament has been changed.
019	PSA	073	022	And so, I have been reduced to nothing, and I did not know it.
019	PSA	073	023	I have become like a beast of burden to you, and I am always with you.
019	PSA	073	024	You have held my right hand. And in your will, you have conducted me, and with your glory, you have taken me up.
019	PSA	073	025	For what is there for me in heaven? And what do I wish for on earth before you?
019	PSA	073	026	My body has failed, and my heart: O God of my heart, and God my portion, into eternity.
019	PSA	073	027	For behold, those who put themselves far from you will perish. You have perished all those who fornicate away from you.
019	PSA	073	028	But it is good for me to adhere to God, to put my hope in the Lord God, so that I may announce all your prophecies, at the gates of the daughter of Zion.
019	PSA	074	001	The understanding of Asaph. O God, why have you rejected us to the end. Why has your fury become enraged over the sheep of your pasture?
019	PSA	074	002	Be mindful of your congregation, which you have possessed from the beginning. You redeemed the scepter of your inheritance, mount Zion, in which you have dwelt.
019	PSA	074	003	Lift up your hands against their arrogance in the end. How great the malice of the enemy has been in the sanctuary!
019	PSA	074	004	And those who hate you have been glorified, in the midst of your solemnity. They have set up their own signs as a proof,
019	PSA	074	005	as if it had been issued from on high; yet they did not understand. As in a forest of chopped wood,
019	PSA	074	006	they have cut down the entrances themselves. With axe and hatchet, they have brought it down.
019	PSA	074	007	They have set fire to your Sanctuary. They have polluted the tabernacle of your name on earth.
019	PSA	074	008	They have said in their heart, the whole group of them together: “Let us cause all the feast days of God to cease from the land.
019	PSA	074	009	We have not seen our proof; there is now no prophet. And he will no longer know us.”
019	PSA	074	010	How long, O God, will the enemy place blame? Is the adversary to provoke your name until the end?
019	PSA	074	011	Why do you turn your hand away, even your right hand, from the midst of your sinews, until the end?
019	PSA	074	012	But God is our king before all ages. He has wrought salvation in the midst of the earth.
019	PSA	074	013	In your virtue, you confirmed the sea. You crushed the heads of the serpents in the waters.
019	PSA	074	014	You have broken the heads of the serpent. You have given him as food for the people of the Ethiopians.
019	PSA	074	015	You have disrupted the fountains and the torrents. You have dried up the rivers of Ethan.
019	PSA	074	016	Yours is the day, and yours is the night. You have made the morning light and the sun.
019	PSA	074	017	You have made all the limits of the earth. The summer and the spring were formed by you.
019	PSA	074	018	Be mindful of this: the enemy placed blame against the Lord, and a foolish people has incited against your name.
019	PSA	074	019	Do not hand over to beasts the souls that confess to you; and do not forget the souls of your poor until the end.
019	PSA	074	020	Consider your covenant. For those who have been darkened upon the earth have been filled by the iniquity of the houses.
019	PSA	074	021	Do not allow the humble to be turned away in confusion. The poor and the needy will praise your name.
019	PSA	074	022	Rise up, O God, judge your own case. Call to mind the accusations against you, which are made by the foolish all day long.
019	PSA	074	023	Do not forget the voices of your adversaries. The arrogance of those who hate you rises up continually.
019	PSA	075	001	Unto the end. May you not be corrupted. A Canticle Psalm of Asaph. We will confess to you, O God. We will confess, and we will call upon your name. We will describe your wonders.
019	PSA	075	002	While I have time, I will judge justices.
019	PSA	075	003	The earth has been dissolved, with all who dwell in it. I have confirmed its pillars.
019	PSA	075	004	I said to the iniquitous: “Do not act unjustly,” and to the offenders: “Do not exalt the horn.”
019	PSA	075	005	Do not exalt your horn on high. Do not speak iniquity against God.
019	PSA	075	006	For it is neither from the east, nor from the west, nor before the desert mountains.
019	PSA	075	007	For God is judge. This one he humbles and that one he exalts.
019	PSA	075	008	For, in the hand of the Lord, there is a cup of undiluted wine, full of consternation. And he has tipped it from here to there. So, truly, its dregs have not been emptied. All the sinners of the earth will drink.
019	PSA	075	009	But I will announce it in every age. I will sing to the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	075	010	And I will break all the horns of sinners. And the horns of the just will be exalted.
019	PSA	076	001	Unto the end. With Praises. A Psalm of Asaph. A Canticle to the Assyrians. In Judea, God is known. In Israel, his name is great.
019	PSA	076	002	And his place has been formed with peace. And his dwelling place is in Zion.
019	PSA	076	003	In that place, he has broken the powers of the bows, the shield, the sword, and the battle.
019	PSA	076	004	You illuminate wondrously from the mountains of eternity.
019	PSA	076	005	All the foolish of heart have been disturbed. They have slept their sleep, and all the men of riches have found nothing in their hands.
019	PSA	076	006	At your rebuke, O God of Jacob, those who were mounted on horseback have fallen asleep.
019	PSA	076	007	You are terrible, and so, who can withstand you? From thence is your wrath.
019	PSA	076	008	You have caused judgment to be heard from heaven. The earth trembled and was quieted,
019	PSA	076	009	when God rose up in judgment in order to bring salvation to all the meek of the earth.
019	PSA	076	010	For the thinking of man will confess to you, and the legacy of his thinking will keep a feast day to you.
019	PSA	076	011	Make vows and pay them to the Lord, your God. All you who surround him bring gifts: to him who is terrible,
019	PSA	076	012	even to him who takes away the spirit of leaders, to him who is terrible with the kings of the earth.
019	PSA	077	001	Unto the end. For Jeduthun. A Psalm of Asaph. I cried out to the Lord with my voice, to God with my voice, and he attended to me.
019	PSA	077	002	In the days of my tribulation, I sought God, with my hands opposite him in the night, and I was not deceived. My soul refused to be consoled.
019	PSA	077	003	I was mindful of God, and I was delighted, and I was distressed, and my spirit fell away.
019	PSA	077	004	My eyes anticipated the vigils. I was disturbed, and I did not speak.
019	PSA	077	005	I considered the days of antiquity, and I held the years of eternity in my mind.
019	PSA	077	006	And I meditated in the night with my heart, and I was distressed, and I examined my spirit.
019	PSA	077	007	So then, will God reject for eternity? Will he not continue to allow himself to show favor?
019	PSA	077	008	Or, will he cut off his mercy in the end, from generation to generation?
019	PSA	077	009	And would God ever forget to be merciful? Or, would he, in his wrath, restrict his mercies?
019	PSA	077	010	And I said, “Now I have begun. This change is from the right hand of the Most High.”
019	PSA	077	011	I was mindful of the works of the Lord. For I will be mindful from the beginning of your wonders,
019	PSA	077	012	and I will meditate on all your works. And I will take part in your intentions.
019	PSA	077	013	Your way, O God, is in what is holy. Which God is great like our God?
019	PSA	077	014	You are the God who performs miracles. You have made your virtue known among the peoples.
019	PSA	077	015	With your arm, you have redeemed your people, the sons of Jacob and of Joseph.
019	PSA	077	016	The waters saw you, O God, the waters saw you, and they were afraid, and the depths were stirred up.
019	PSA	077	017	Great was the sound of the waters. The clouds uttered a voice. For your arrows also pass by.
019	PSA	077	018	The voice of your thunder is like a wheel. Your flashes have illuminated the whole world. The earth has quaked and trembled.
019	PSA	077	019	Your way is through the sea, and your paths are through many waters. And your traces will not be known.
019	PSA	077	020	You have conducted your people like sheep, by the hand of Moses and Aaron.
019	PSA	078	001	The understanding of Asaph. O my people, attend to my law. Incline your ears to the words of my mouth.
019	PSA	078	002	I will open my mouth in parables. I will speak about concepts that are from the beginning.
019	PSA	078	003	We have heard and known such great things, as our fathers have described to us.
019	PSA	078	004	These things have not been hidden from their sons in any generation: declaring the praises of the Lord, and his virtues, and the wonders that he has done.
019	PSA	078	005	And he has received testimony with Jacob, and he has set a law within Israel. Such great things, he has commanded our fathers, so as to make these things known to their sons,
019	PSA	078	006	so that another generation might know them, and so that the sons, who will be born and who will grow up, shall describe them to their sons.
019	PSA	078	007	So then, may they put their hope in God, and may they not forget the works of God, and may they seek his commandments.
019	PSA	078	008	May they not become like their fathers, a perverse and exasperating generation: a generation that does not straighten their heart and whose spirit is not trustworthy with God.
019	PSA	078	009	The sons of Ephraim, who bend and shoot the bow, have been turned back in the day of battle.
019	PSA	078	010	They have not kept the covenant of God. And they were not willing to walk in his law.
019	PSA	078	011	And they have been forgetful of his benefits, and of his miracle, which he revealed to them.
019	PSA	078	012	He performed miracles in the sight of their fathers, in the land of Egypt, in the field of Tanis.
019	PSA	078	013	He broke the sea and he led them through. And he stationed the waters, as if in a vessel.
019	PSA	078	014	And he led them with a cloud by day, and with illumination by fire throughout the night.
019	PSA	078	015	He broke through the rock in the wasteland, and he gave them to drink, as if from the great abyss.
019	PSA	078	016	He brought forth water from the rock, and he conducted the waters, as if they were rivers.
019	PSA	078	017	And yet, they continued to sin against him. In a waterless place, they provoked the Most High with resentment.
019	PSA	078	018	And they tempted God in their hearts, by asking for food according to their desires.
019	PSA	078	019	And they spoke badly about God. They said, “Would God be able to prepare a table in the desert?
019	PSA	078	020	He struck the rock, and so waters flowed and the torrents flooded, but would even he be able to provide bread, or provide a table, for his people?”
019	PSA	078	021	Therefore, the Lord heard, and he was dismayed, and a fire was kindled within Jacob, and an anger ascended into Israel.
019	PSA	078	022	For they neither put their trust in God, nor did they hope in his salvation.
019	PSA	078	023	And he commanded the clouds from above, and he opened the doors of heaven.
019	PSA	078	024	And he rained down manna upon them to eat, and he gave them the bread of heaven.
019	PSA	078	025	Man ate the bread of Angels. He sent them provisions in abundance.
019	PSA	078	026	He transferred the south wind from heaven, and, in his virtue, he brought in the Southwest wind.
019	PSA	078	027	And he rained down flesh upon them, as if it were dust, and feathered birds, as if they were the sand of the sea.
019	PSA	078	028	And they fell down in the midst of their camp, encircling their tabernacles.
019	PSA	078	029	And they ate until they were greatly satisfied, and he brought to them according to their desires.
019	PSA	078	030	They were not cheated out of what they wanted. Their food was still in their mouth,
019	PSA	078	031	and then the wrath of God came upon them. And he slew the fat ones among them, and he impeded the elect of Israel.
019	PSA	078	032	In all these things, they continued to sin, and they were not trustworthy with his miracles.
019	PSA	078	033	And their days faded away into vanity, and their years with haste.
019	PSA	078	034	When he slew them, then they sought him. And they returned, and they drew near to him in the early morning.
019	PSA	078	035	And they were mindful that God is their helper and that the Most High God is their redeemer.
019	PSA	078	036	And they chose him with their mouth, and then they lied to him with their tongue.
019	PSA	078	037	For their heart was not upright with him, nor have they been living faithfully in his covenant.
019	PSA	078	038	Yet he is merciful, and he will pardon their sins. And he will not destroy them. And he has abundantly turned aside his own wrath. And he did not enflame his wrath entirely.
019	PSA	078	039	And he remembered that they are flesh: with a spirit that goes forth and does not return.
019	PSA	078	040	How often did they provoke him in the desert and stir him to wrath in a waterless place?
019	PSA	078	041	And they turned back and tempted God, and they exasperated the Holy One of Israel.
019	PSA	078	042	They did not remember his hand, in the day that he redeemed them from the hand of the one troubling them.
019	PSA	078	043	Thus, he positioned his signs in Egypt and his wonders in the field of Tanis.
019	PSA	078	044	And he turned their rivers into blood, along with their rain showers, so that they could not drink.
019	PSA	078	045	He sent among them the common fly, and it devoured them, and the frog, and it scattered them.
019	PSA	078	046	And he gave up their fruits to mold and their labors to the locust.
019	PSA	078	047	And he slew their vineyards with hail and their mulberry trees with severe frost.
019	PSA	078	048	And he delivered their cattle to the hail and their possessions to fire.
019	PSA	078	049	And he sent the wrath of his indignation among them: indignation and wrath and tribulation, sent forth by evil angels.
019	PSA	078	050	He made way for the path of his anger. He did not spare their souls from death. And he enclosed their beasts of burden in death.
019	PSA	078	051	And he struck all the first-born in the land of Egypt: the first-fruits of all their labor in the tabernacles of Ham.
019	PSA	078	052	And he took away his own people like sheep, and he led them through the wilderness like a flock.
019	PSA	078	053	And he led them out in hope, and they did not fear. And the sea covered their enemies.
019	PSA	078	054	And he led them to the mountain of his sanctification: the mountain that his right hand had acquired. And he cast out the Gentiles before their face. And he divided their land by lot to them, with a line of distribution.
019	PSA	078	055	And he caused the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tabernacles.
019	PSA	078	056	Yet they tempted and aggravated God Most High, and they did not keep his testaments.
019	PSA	078	057	And they turned themselves aside, and they did not serve the covenant. In the same manner as their fathers, they were turned backwards, like a crooked bow.
019	PSA	078	058	They impelled him to anger on their hills, and they provoked him to rivalry with their graven images.
019	PSA	078	059	God listened, and he spurned them, and he reduced Israel greatly, almost to nothing.
019	PSA	078	060	And he rejected the tabernacle of Shiloh, his tabernacle where he had dwelt among men.
019	PSA	078	061	And he delivered their virtue into captivity, and their beauty into the hands of the enemy.
019	PSA	078	062	And he enclosed his people with the sword, and he spurned his inheritance.
019	PSA	078	063	Fire consumed their young men, and their virgins were not lamented.
019	PSA	078	064	Their priests fell by the sword, and their widows did not weep.
019	PSA	078	065	And the Lord was awakened, as if out of sleep, and like a powerful man impaired by wine.
019	PSA	078	066	And he struck his enemies on the back. He gave them over to everlasting disgrace.
019	PSA	078	067	And he rejected the tabernacle of Joseph, and he did not choose the tribe of Ephraim.
019	PSA	078	068	But he chose the tribe of Judah: mount Zion, which he loved.
019	PSA	078	069	And he built up his sanctuary, like a single-horned beast, in the land that he founded for all ages.
019	PSA	078	070	And he chose his servant David, and he took him from the flocks of the sheep: he received him from following the ewes with their young,
019	PSA	078	071	in order to pasture Jacob his servant and Israel his inheritance.
019	PSA	078	072	And he fed them with the innocence of his heart. And he led them with the understanding of his hands.
019	PSA	079	001	A Psalm of Asaph. O God, the Gentiles have entered into your inheritance; they have polluted your holy temple. They have set Jerusalem as a place to tend fruit trees.
019	PSA	079	002	They have placed the dead bodies of your servants as food for the birds of the sky, the flesh of your saints for the beasts of the earth.
019	PSA	079	003	They have poured out their blood like water all around Jerusalem, and there was no one who would bury them.
019	PSA	079	004	We have become a disgrace to our neighbors, an object of ridicule and mockery to those who are around us.
019	PSA	079	005	How long, O Lord? Will you be angry until the end? Will your zeal be kindled like a fire?
019	PSA	079	006	Pour out your wrath among the Gentiles, who have not known you, and upon the kingdoms that have not invoked your name.
019	PSA	079	007	For they have devoured Jacob, and they have desolated his place.
019	PSA	079	008	Do not remember our iniquities of the past. May your mercies quickly intercept us, for we have become exceedingly poor.
019	PSA	079	009	Help us, O God, our Savior. And free us, Lord, for the glory of your name. And forgive us our sins for the sake of your name.
019	PSA	079	010	Let them not say among the Gentiles, “Where is their God?” And may your name become known among the nations before our eyes. For the retribution of your servants’ blood, which has been poured out:
019	PSA	079	011	may the groans of the shackled enter before you. According to the greatness of your arm, take possession of the sons of those who have been killed.
019	PSA	079	012	And repay our neighbors sevenfold within their sinews. It is the reproach of the same ones who brought reproach against you, O Lord.
019	PSA	079	013	But we are your people and the sheep of your pasture: we will give thanks to you in all ages. From generation to generation, we will announce your praise.
019	PSA	080	001	Unto the end. For those who will be changed. The testimony of Asaph. A Psalm. The One who reigns over Israel: Be attentive. For you lead Joseph like a sheep. The One who sits upon the cherubim: Shine forth
019	PSA	080	002	in the presence of Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasseh. Awaken your power and draw near, so as to accomplish our salvation.
019	PSA	080	003	Convert us, O God. And reveal your face, and we will be saved.
019	PSA	080	004	O Lord, God of hosts, how long will you be angry over the prayer of your servant?
019	PSA	080	005	How long will you feed us the bread of tears, and give us to drink a full measure of tears?
019	PSA	080	006	You have set us as a contradiction to our neighbors. And our enemies have ridiculed us.
019	PSA	080	007	O God of hosts, convert us. And reveal your face, and we will be saved.
019	PSA	080	008	You have transferred a vineyard from Egypt. You have cast out the Gentiles, and planted it.
019	PSA	080	009	You were the leader of the journey in its sight. You planted its roots, and it filled the earth.
019	PSA	080	010	Its shadow covered the hills, and its branches covered the cedars of God.
019	PSA	080	011	It extended its new branches even to the sea, and its new seedlings even to the river.
019	PSA	080	012	So then, why have you destroyed its walls, so that all those who pass by the way gather its grapes?
019	PSA	080	013	The wild boar of the forest has trampled it, and a single wild beast has laid waste to it.
019	PSA	080	014	Turn back, O God of hosts. Look down from heaven, and see, and visit this vineyard;
019	PSA	080	015	and complete what your right hand has planted, and look upon the son of man, whom you have confirmed for yourself.
019	PSA	080	016	Whatever has been set on fire and dug under will perish at the rebuke of your countenance.
019	PSA	080	017	Let your hand be over the man on your right, and over the son of man, whom you have confirmed for yourself.
019	PSA	080	018	For we do not depart from you, and you will revive us. And we will invoke your name.
019	PSA	080	019	O Lord, God of hosts, convert us. And reveal your face, and we will be saved.
019	PSA	081	001	Unto the end. For the wine and oil presses. A Psalm of Asaph himself. Exult before God our helper. Sing joyfully to the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	081	002	Take up a psalm, and bring forth the timbrel: a pleasing Psalter with stringed instruments.
019	PSA	081	003	Sound the trumpet at the new moon, on the noteworthy day of your solemnity,
019	PSA	081	004	for it is a precept in Israel and a judgment for the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	081	005	He set it as a testimony with Joseph, when he went out of the land of Egypt. He heard a tongue that he did not know.
019	PSA	081	006	He turned the burdens away from his back. His hands had been a slave to baskets.
019	PSA	081	007	You called upon me in tribulation, and I freed you. I heard you within the hidden tempest. I tested you with waters of contradiction.
019	PSA	081	008	My people, listen and I will call you to testify. If, O Israel, you will pay heed to me,
019	PSA	081	009	then there will be no new god among you, nor will you adore a foreign god.
019	PSA	081	010	For I am the Lord your God, who led you out of the land of Egypt. Widen your mouth, and I will fill it.
019	PSA	081	011	But my people did not hear my voice, and Israel was not attentive to me.
019	PSA	081	012	And so, I sent them away, according to the desires of their heart. They will go forth according to their own inventions.
019	PSA	081	013	If my people had heard me, if Israel had walked in my ways,
019	PSA	081	014	I would have humbled their enemies, as if it were nothing, and I would have sent my hand upon those who troubled them.
019	PSA	081	015	The enemies of the Lord have lied to him, and their time will come, in every age.
019	PSA	081	016	And he fed them from the fat of the grain, and he saturated them with honey from the rock.
019	PSA	082	001	A Psalm of Asaph. God has stood in the synagogue of gods, but, in their midst, he decides between gods.
019	PSA	082	002	How long will you judge unjustly and favor the faces of sinners?
019	PSA	082	003	Judge for the indigent and the orphan. Do justice to the humble and the poor.
019	PSA	082	004	Rescue the poor, and free the needy from the hand of the sinner.
019	PSA	082	005	They did not know and did not understand. They wander in darkness. All the foundations of the earth will be moved.
019	PSA	082	006	I said: You are gods, and all of you are sons of the Most High.
019	PSA	082	007	But you will die like men, and you will fall just like one of the princes.
019	PSA	082	008	Rise up, O God. Judge the earth. For you will inherit it with all the nations.
019	PSA	083	001	A Canticle Psalm of Asaph. O God, who will ever be like you? Do not be silent, and do not be unmoved, O God.
019	PSA	083	002	For behold, your enemies have sounded off, and those who hate you have carried out a head.
019	PSA	083	003	They have acted with malice in counsel over your people, and they have plotted against your holy ones.
019	PSA	083	004	They have said, “Come, let us scatter them from the nations and not allow the name of Israel to be remembered any longer.”
019	PSA	083	005	For they plotted unanimously. Joined together against you, they ordained a covenant:
019	PSA	083	006	the tabernacle of Edomites and Ishmaelites, and Moab and the Hagarites,
019	PSA	083	007	and Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek, the foreigners among the inhabitants of Tyre.
019	PSA	083	008	For even Assur comes with them. They have become the helpers of the sons of Lot.
019	PSA	083	009	Do to them as you did to Midian and Sisera, just as to Jabin at the torrent of Kishon.
019	PSA	083	010	They perished at Endor, and they became like the dung of the earth.
019	PSA	083	011	Set their leaders to be like Oreb and Zeeb, and Zebah and Zalmunna: all their leaders
019	PSA	083	012	who said, “Let us possess the Sanctuary of God for an inheritance.”
019	PSA	083	013	My God, set them like a wheel, and like stubble before the face of the wind.
019	PSA	083	014	Set them like a fire burning up the forest, and like a flame burning up the mountains.
019	PSA	083	015	So will you pursue them in your tempest, and disturb them in your wrath.
019	PSA	083	016	Fill their faces with shame, and they will seek your name, O Lord.
019	PSA	083	017	Let them be ashamed and troubled, from age to age, and let them be confounded and perish.
019	PSA	083	018	And let them know that the Lord is your name. You alone are the Most High in all the earth.
019	PSA	084	001	Unto the end. For the wine and oil presses. A Psalm to the sons of Korah. How beloved are your tabernacles, O Lord of hosts!
019	PSA	084	002	My soul longs and faints for the courts of the Lord. My heart and my flesh have exulted in the living God.
019	PSA	084	003	For even the sparrow has found a home for himself, and the turtle-dove a nest for herself, where she may lay her young: your altars, O Lord of hosts, my king and my God.
019	PSA	084	004	Blessed are those who dwell in your house, O Lord. They will praise you from age to age.
019	PSA	084	005	Blessed is the man whose help is from you. In his heart, he is disposed to ascend
019	PSA	084	006	from the valley of tears, from the place which he has determined.
019	PSA	084	007	For even the lawgiver will provide a blessing; they will go from virtue to virtue. The God of gods will be seen in Zion.
019	PSA	084	008	O Lord, God of hosts, hear my prayer. Pay attention, O God of Jacob.
019	PSA	084	009	O God, gaze upon our protector, and look upon the face of your Christ.
019	PSA	084	010	For one day in your courts is better than thousands elsewhere. I have chosen to be lowly in the house of my God, rather than to dwell in the tabernacles of sinners.
019	PSA	084	011	For God loves mercy and truth. The Lord will give grace and glory.
019	PSA	084	012	He will not withhold good things from those who walk in innocence. O Lord of hosts, blessed is the man who hopes in you.
019	PSA	085	001	Unto the end. A Psalm to the sons of Korah. O Lord, you have blessed your land. You have turned aside the captivity of Jacob.
019	PSA	085	002	You have released the iniquity of your people. You have covered all their sins.
019	PSA	085	003	You have mitigated all your wrath. You have turned aside from the wrath of your indignation.
019	PSA	085	004	Convert us, O God, our Savior, and turn your anger away from us.
019	PSA	085	005	Will you be angry with us forever? And will you extend your wrath from generation to generation?
019	PSA	085	006	O God, you will turn back and revive us. And your people will rejoice in you.
019	PSA	085	007	O Lord, reveal to us your mercy, and grant to us your salvation.
019	PSA	085	008	I will listen to what the Lord God may be saying to me. For he will speak peace to his people, and to his saints, and to those who are being converted to the heart.
019	PSA	085	009	So then, truly his salvation is near to those who fear him, so that glory may inhabit our land.
019	PSA	085	010	Mercy and truth have met each other. Justice and peace have kissed.
019	PSA	085	011	Truth has risen from the earth, and justice has gazed down from heaven.
019	PSA	085	012	For so will the Lord give goodness, and our earth will give her fruit.
019	PSA	085	013	Justice will walk before him, and he will set his steps upon the way.
019	PSA	086	001	A Prayer of David himself. Incline your ear, O Lord, and hear me. For I am needy and poor.
019	PSA	086	002	Preserve my soul, for I am holy. My God, bring salvation to your servant who hopes in you.
019	PSA	086	003	O Lord, be merciful to me, for I have cried out to you all day long.
019	PSA	086	004	Give joy to the soul of your servant, for I have lifted up my soul to you, Lord.
019	PSA	086	005	For you are sweet and mild, Lord, and plentiful in mercy to all who call upon you.
019	PSA	086	006	Pay attention, Lord, to my prayer, and attend to the voice of my supplication.
019	PSA	086	007	In the day of my tribulation, I cried out to you, because you heeded me.
019	PSA	086	008	There is no one like you among the gods, O Lord, and there is no one like you in your works.
019	PSA	086	009	All the nations, which you have made, will draw near and adore in your presence, O Lord. And they will glorify your name.
019	PSA	086	010	For you are great, and you perform wonders. You alone are God.
019	PSA	086	011	Lead me, O Lord, in your way, and I will walk in your truth. May my heart rejoice, so that it will fear your name.
019	PSA	086	012	I will confess to you, O Lord my God, with my whole heart. And I will glorify your name in eternity.
019	PSA	086	013	For your mercy toward me is great, and you have rescued my soul from the lower part of Hell.
019	PSA	086	014	O God, the iniquitous have risen up against me, and the synagogue of the powerful have sought my soul, and they have not placed you in their sight.
019	PSA	086	015	And you, Lord God, are compassionate and merciful, being patient and full of mercy and truthful.
019	PSA	086	016	Look down upon me and have mercy on me. Grant your authority to your servant, and bring salvation to the son of your handmaid.
019	PSA	086	017	Make me a sign of what is good, so that those who hate me, may look and be confounded. For you, O Lord, have helped me and consoled me.
019	PSA	087	001	A Canticle Psalm to the sons of Korah. Its foundations are in the holy mountains:
019	PSA	087	002	the Lord loves the gates of Zion above all the tabernacles of Jacob.
019	PSA	087	003	Glorious things are being said of you, O City of God.
019	PSA	087	004	I will be mindful of Rahab and of Babylon knowing me. Behold, the foreigners, and Tyre, and the people of the Ethiopians: these have been there.
019	PSA	087	005	Will not Zion say that this man and that man were born in her? And the Most High himself has founded her.
019	PSA	087	006	The Lord will explain, in the writings of peoples and of leaders, about those who have been in her.
019	PSA	087	007	For so the dwelling place within you is with all rejoicing.
019	PSA	088	001	A Canticle Psalm to the sons of Korah. Unto the end. For Mahalath, to answer the understanding of Heman the Ezrahite. O Lord, God of my salvation: I have cried out, day and night, in your presence.
019	PSA	088	002	Let my prayer enter in your sight. Incline your ear to my petition.
019	PSA	088	003	For my soul has been filled with evils, and my life has drawn near to Hell.
019	PSA	088	004	I am considered to be among those who will descend into the pit. I have become like a man without assistance,
019	PSA	088	005	idle among the dead. I am like the wounded sleeping in sepulchers, whom you no longer remember, and who have been repelled by your hand.
019	PSA	088	006	They have lain me in the lower pit: in dark places and in the shadow of death.
019	PSA	088	007	Your fury has been confirmed over me. And you have brought all your waves upon me.
019	PSA	088	008	You have sent my acquaintances far from me. They have set me as an abomination to themselves. I was handed over, yet I did not depart.
019	PSA	088	009	My eyes languished before destitution. All day long, I cried out to you, O Lord. I stretched out my hands to you.
019	PSA	088	010	Will you perform wonders for the dead? Or will physicians raise to life, and so confess to you?
019	PSA	088	011	Could anyone declare your mercy in the sepulcher, or your truth from within perdition?
019	PSA	088	012	Will your wonders be known in the darkness, or your justice in the land of oblivion?
019	PSA	088	013	And I have cried out to you, O Lord, and in early morning, my prayer will come before you.
019	PSA	088	014	Lord, why do you reject my prayer? Why do you turn your face away from me?
019	PSA	088	015	I am poor, and I have been amid hardships from my youth. And, though I have been exalted, I am humbled and disturbed.
019	PSA	088	016	Your wrath has crossed into me, and your terrors have disturbed me.
019	PSA	088	017	They have surrounded me like water, all day long. They have surrounded me, all at once.
019	PSA	088	018	Friend and neighbor, and my acquaintances, you have sent far away from me, away from misery.
019	PSA	089	001	The understanding of Ethan the Ezrahite. I will sing the mercies of the Lord in eternity. I will announce your truth with my mouth, from generation to generation.
019	PSA	089	002	For you have said: Mercy will be built in the heavens, unto eternity. Your truth will be prepared there.
019	PSA	089	003	I have set up a covenant with my elect. I have sworn to David my servant:
019	PSA	089	004	I will prepare your offspring, even in eternity. And I will build up your throne, from generation to generation.
019	PSA	089	005	The heavens will confess your miracles, Lord, and also your truth, in the Church of the saints.
019	PSA	089	006	For who among the clouds is equal to the Lord? Who among the sons of God is like God?
019	PSA	089	007	God is glorified by the counsel of the saints. He is great and terrible above all those who are around him.
019	PSA	089	008	O Lord, God of hosts, who is like you? You are powerful, Lord, and your truth is all around you.
019	PSA	089	009	You rule over the power of the sea, and you even mitigate the movement of its waves.
019	PSA	089	010	You have humbled the arrogant one, like one who has been wounded. You have scattered your enemies with the arm of your strength.
019	PSA	089	011	Yours are the heavens, and yours is the earth. You founded the whole world in all its fullness.
019	PSA	089	012	You created the north and the sea. Tabor and Hermon will exult in your name.
019	PSA	089	013	Your arm acts with power. Let your hand be strengthened, and let your right hand be exalted.
019	PSA	089	014	Justice and judgment are the preparation of your throne. Mercy and truth will precede your face.
019	PSA	089	015	Blessed is the people that knows jubilation. They will walk in the light of your countenance, O Lord,
019	PSA	089	016	and they will exult in your name all day long, and they will be exalted in your justice.
019	PSA	089	017	For you are the glory of their virtue, and in your goodness, our horn will be exalted.
019	PSA	089	018	For our assumption is of the Lord, and it is of our king, the holy one of Israel.
019	PSA	089	019	Then you spoke in a vision to your holy ones, and you said: I have stationed help with the powerful one, and I have exalted the elect one from my people.
019	PSA	089	020	I have found my servant David. I have anointed him with my holy oil.
019	PSA	089	021	For my hand will assist him, and my arm will fortify him.
019	PSA	089	022	The enemy will have no advantage over him, nor will the son of iniquity be positioned to harm him.
019	PSA	089	023	And I will cut down his enemies before his face. And those who hate him, I will turn to flight.
019	PSA	089	024	And my truth and my mercy will be with him. And his horn will be exalted in my name.
019	PSA	089	025	And I will place his hand on the sea and his right hand on the rivers.
019	PSA	089	026	He will invoke me: “You are my father, my God, and the support of my salvation.”
019	PSA	089	027	And I will make him the first-born, preeminent before the kings of the earth.
019	PSA	089	028	I will preserve my mercy for him eternally, and my covenant for him faithfully.
019	PSA	089	029	And I will set his offspring from generation to generation, and his throne like the days of heaven.
019	PSA	089	030	But if his sons abandon my law, and if they do not walk in my judgments,
019	PSA	089	031	if they profane my justices, and if they do not keep my commandments:
019	PSA	089	032	I will visit their iniquities with a rod, and their sins with a beating.
019	PSA	089	033	But I will not scatter my mercy from him, and I will not do harm to my truth.
019	PSA	089	034	And I will not profane my covenant, and I will not make void that which proceeds from my lips.
019	PSA	089	035	I have sworn by my holiness one time: I will not lie to David,
019	PSA	089	036	his offspring will remain for eternity. And his throne will be like the sun in my sight,
019	PSA	089	037	and, like the moon, it is perfected in eternity, and it is a faithful witness in heaven.
019	PSA	089	038	Yet, truly, you have rejected and despised, you have pushed away, my Christ.
019	PSA	089	039	You have overthrown the covenant of your servant. You have profaned his sanctuary on earth.
019	PSA	089	040	You have destroyed all his fences. You have made his territory dreadful.
019	PSA	089	041	All who pass by the way have plundered him. He has become a disgrace to his neighbors.
019	PSA	089	042	You have exalted the right hand of those who oppress him. You have brought joy to all his enemies.
019	PSA	089	043	You have diverted the help of his sword, and you have not assisted him in battle.
019	PSA	089	044	You have torn him away from cleansing, and you have smashed his throne down to the ground.
019	PSA	089	045	You have reduced the days of his time. You have flooded him with confusion.
019	PSA	089	046	How long, O Lord? Will you turn away unto the end? Will your wrath flare up like a fire?
019	PSA	089	047	Remember what my substance is. For could you really have appointed all the sons of men in vain?
019	PSA	089	048	Who is the man that will live, and yet not see death? Who will rescue his own soul from the hand of the underworld?
019	PSA	089	049	O Lord, where are your mercies of antiquity, just as you swore to David in your truth?
019	PSA	089	050	Be mindful, O Lord, of the disgrace of your servants (which I have sustained in my sinews) among many nations.
019	PSA	089	051	With these, your enemies have reproached you, O Lord; with these, they have reproached the commutation of your Christ.
019	PSA	089	052	Blessed is the Lord for all eternity. Amen. Amen.
019	PSA	090	001	A prayer of Moses, the man of God. O Lord, you have been our refuge from generation to generation.
019	PSA	090	002	Before the mountains became, or the land was formed along with the world: from ages past, even to all ages, you are God.
019	PSA	090	003	And, lest man be turned aside in humiliation, you have said: Be converted, O sons of men.
019	PSA	090	004	For a thousand years before your eyes are like the days of yesterday, which have passed by, and they are like a watch of the night,
019	PSA	090	005	which was held for nothing: so their years shall be.
019	PSA	090	006	In the morning, he may pass away like grass; in the morning, he may flower and pass away. In the evening, he will fall, and harden, and become dry.
019	PSA	090	007	For, at your wrath, we have withered away, and we have been disturbed by your fury.
019	PSA	090	008	You have placed our iniquities in your sight, our age in the illumination of your countenance.
019	PSA	090	009	For all our days have faded away, and at your wrath, we have fainted. Our years will be considered to be like a spider’s web.
019	PSA	090	010	The days of our years in them are seventy years. But in the powerful, they are eighty years, and more of these are with hardship and sorrow. For mildness has overwhelmed us, and we shall be corrected.
019	PSA	090	011	Who knows the power of your wrath? And, before fear, can your wrath
019	PSA	090	012	be numbered? So make known your right hand, along with men learned in heart, in wisdom.
019	PSA	090	013	Return, O Lord, how long? And may you be persuaded on behalf of your servants.
019	PSA	090	014	We were filled in the morning with your mercy, and we exulted and delighted all our days.
019	PSA	090	015	We have been rejoicing, because of the days in which you humbled us, because of the years in which we saw evils.
019	PSA	090	016	Look down upon your servants and upon their works, and direct their sons.
019	PSA	090	017	And may the splendor of the Lord our God be upon us. And so, direct the works of our hands over us; direct even the work of our hands.
019	PSA	091	001	The Praise of a Canticle, of David. Whoever dwells with the assistance of the Most High will abide in the protection of the God of heaven.
019	PSA	091	002	He will say to the Lord, “You are my supporter and my refuge.” My God, I will hope in him.
019	PSA	091	003	For he has freed me from the snare of those who go hunting, and from the harsh word.
019	PSA	091	004	He will overshadow you with his shoulders, and you will hope under his wings.
019	PSA	091	005	His truth will surround you with a shield. You will not be afraid: before the terror of the night,
019	PSA	091	006	before the arrow flying in the day, before the troubles that wander in the darkness, nor of invasion and the midday demon.
019	PSA	091	007	A thousand will fall before your side and ten thousand before your right hand. Yet it will not draw near you.
019	PSA	091	008	So then, truly, you will consider with your eyes, and you will see the retribution of sinners.
019	PSA	091	009	For you, O Lord, are my hope. You have set the Most High as your refuge.
019	PSA	091	010	Disaster will not draw near to you, and the scourge will not approach your tabernacle.
019	PSA	091	011	For he has given his Angels charge over you, so as to preserve you in all your ways.
019	PSA	091	012	With their hands, they will carry you, lest you hurt your foot against a stone.
019	PSA	091	013	You will walk over the asp and the king serpent, and you will trample the lion and the dragon.
019	PSA	091	014	Because he has hoped in me, I will free him. I will protect him because he has known my name.
019	PSA	091	015	He will cry out to me, and I will heed him. I am with him in tribulation. I will rescue him, and I will glorify him.
019	PSA	091	016	I will fill him with length of days. And I will reveal to him my salvation.
019	PSA	092	001	A Canticle Psalm. On the day of the Sabbath. It is good to confess to the Lord and to sing psalms to your name, O Most High:
019	PSA	092	002	to announce your mercy in the morning, and your truth throughout the night,
019	PSA	092	003	upon the ten strings, upon the psaltery, with a canticle, upon stringed instruments.
019	PSA	092	004	For you, O Lord, have delighted me with your doings, and I will exult in the works of your hands.
019	PSA	092	005	How great are your works, O Lord! Your thoughts have been made exceedingly deep.
019	PSA	092	006	A foolish man will not know these things, and a senseless one will not understand:
019	PSA	092	007	when sinners will have risen up like grass, and when all those who work iniquity will have appeared, that they shall pass away, age after age.
019	PSA	092	008	But you, O Lord, are the Most High for all eternity.
019	PSA	092	009	For behold your enemies, O Lord, for behold your enemies will perish, and all those who work iniquity will be dispersed.
019	PSA	092	010	And my horn will be exalted like that of the single-horned beast, and my old age will be exalted in fruitful mercy.
019	PSA	092	011	And my eye has looked down upon my enemies, and my ear will hear of the malignant rising up against me.
019	PSA	092	012	The just one will flourish like the palm tree. He will be multiplied like the cedar of Lebanon.
019	PSA	092	013	Those planted in the house of the Lord will flourish in the courts of the house of our God.
019	PSA	092	014	They will still be multiplied in a fruitful old age, and they will endure well,
019	PSA	092	015	so that they may announce that the Lord our God is righteous and that there is no iniquity in him.
019	PSA	093	001	The Praise of a Canticle, of David himself. In the time before the Sabbath, when the earth was founded. The Lord has reigned. He has been clothed with beauty. The Lord has been clothed with strength, and he has girded himself. Yet he has also confirmed the world, which will not be moved.
019	PSA	093	002	My throne is prepared from of old. You are from everlasting.
019	PSA	093	003	The floods have lifted up, O Lord, the floods have lifted up their voice. The floods have lifted up their waves,
019	PSA	093	004	before the noise of many waters. Wondrous are the surges of the sea; wondrous is the Lord on high.
019	PSA	093	005	Your testimonies have been made exceedingly trustworthy. Sanctity befits your house, O Lord, with length of days.
019	PSA	094	001	A Psalm of David himself. The Fourth Sabbath. The Lord is the God of retribution. The God of retribution acts in order to deliver.
019	PSA	094	002	Lift yourself up, for you judge the earth. Repay the arrogant with retribution.
019	PSA	094	003	How long will sinners, O Lord, how long will sinners glory?
019	PSA	094	004	How long will they utter and speak iniquity? How long will all who work injustice speak out?
019	PSA	094	005	They have humiliated your people, O Lord, and they have harassed your inheritance.
019	PSA	094	006	They have executed the widow and the new arrival, and they have slaughtered the orphan.
019	PSA	094	007	And they have said, “The Lord will not see, nor will the God of Jacob understand.”
019	PSA	094	008	Understand, you senseless ones among the people. And be wise at last, you foolish ones.
019	PSA	094	009	He who formed the ear, will he not hear? And he who forged the eye, does he not look closely?
019	PSA	094	010	He who chastises nations, he who teaches man knowledge, will he not rebuke?
019	PSA	094	011	The Lord knows the thoughts of men: that these are in vain.
019	PSA	094	012	Blessed is the man whom you will instruct, O Lord. And you will teach him from your law.
019	PSA	094	013	So may you soothe him from the evil days, until a pit may be dug for sinners.
019	PSA	094	014	For the Lord will not drive away his people, and he will not abandon his inheritance,
019	PSA	094	015	even until the time when justice is being converted into judgment, and when those who are close to justice are all those who are upright of heart.
019	PSA	094	016	Who will rise up with me against the malignant? Or who will stand with me against the workers of iniquity?
019	PSA	094	017	Except that the Lord assisted me, my soul almost would have dwelt in Hell.
019	PSA	094	018	If ever I said, “My foot is slipping,” then your mercy, O Lord, assisted me.
019	PSA	094	019	According to the multitude of my sorrows in my heart, your consolations have given joy to my soul.
019	PSA	094	020	Does the seat of iniquity adhere to you, you who contrive hardship within a commandment?
019	PSA	094	021	They will hunt down the soul of the just, and they will condemn innocent blood.
019	PSA	094	022	And the Lord has been made into a refuge for me, and my God into the assistance of my hope.
019	PSA	094	023	And he will repay them their iniquity, and he will destroy them in their malice. The Lord our God will utterly destroy them.
019	PSA	095	001	The Praise of a Canticle, of David himself. Come, let us exult in the Lord. Let us shout joyfully to God, our Savior.
019	PSA	095	002	Let us anticipate his presence with confession, and let us sing joyfully to him with psalms.
019	PSA	095	003	For the Lord is a great God and a great King over all gods.
019	PSA	095	004	For in his hand are all the limits of the earth, and the heights of the mountains are his.
019	PSA	095	005	For the sea is his, and he made it, and his hands formed the dry land.
019	PSA	095	006	Come, let us adore and fall prostrate, and let us weep before the Lord who made us.
019	PSA	095	007	For he is the Lord our God, and we are the people of his pasture and the sheep of his hand.
019	PSA	095	008	If today you hear his voice, harden not your hearts:
019	PSA	095	009	as in the provocation, according to the day of temptation in the wilderness, where your fathers tempted me; they tested me, though they had seen my works.
019	PSA	095	010	For forty years, I was offended by that generation, and I said: These have always strayed in heart.
019	PSA	095	011	And these have not known my ways. So I swore in my wrath: They shall not enter into my rest.
019	PSA	096	001	A Canticle of David himself, when the house was built after the captivity. Sing to the Lord a new song. Sing to the Lord, all the earth.
019	PSA	096	002	Sing to the Lord and bless his name. Announce his salvation from day to day.
019	PSA	096	003	Announce his glory among the Gentiles, his miracles among all peoples.
019	PSA	096	004	For the Lord is great and greatly to be praised. He is terrible, beyond all gods.
019	PSA	096	005	For all the gods of the Gentiles are demons, but the Lord made the heavens.
019	PSA	096	006	Confession and beauty are in his sight. Sanctity and magnificence are in his sanctuary.
019	PSA	096	007	Bring to the Lord, you natives of the nations, bring to the Lord glory and honor.
019	PSA	096	008	Bring to the Lord glory for his name. Lift up sacrifices, and enter into his courts.
019	PSA	096	009	Adore the Lord in his holy court. Let the entire earth be shaken before his face.
019	PSA	096	010	Say among the Gentiles: The Lord has reigned. For he has even corrected the whole world, which will not be shaken. He will judge the peoples with fairness.
019	PSA	096	011	Let the heavens rejoice, and let the earth exult; let the sea and all its fullness be moved.
019	PSA	096	012	The fields and all the things that are in them will be glad. Then all the trees of the forest will rejoice
019	PSA	096	013	before the face of the Lord: for he arrives. For he arrives to judge the earth. He will judge the whole world with fairness and the peoples with his truth.
019	PSA	097	001	This is to David, when his land was restored to him. The Lord has reigned, let the earth exult. Let the many islands rejoice.
019	PSA	097	002	Clouds and mist are all around him. Justice and judgment are corrections from his throne.
019	PSA	097	003	A fire will precede him, and it will enflame his enemies all around.
019	PSA	097	004	His lightnings have enlightened the whole world. The earth saw, and it was shaken.
019	PSA	097	005	The mountains flowed like wax before the face of the Lord, before the face of the Lord of all the earth.
019	PSA	097	006	The heavens announced his justice, and all peoples saw his glory.
019	PSA	097	007	May all those who adore graven images be confounded, along with those who glory in their false images. All you his Angels: Adore him.
019	PSA	097	008	Zion heard, and was glad. And the daughters of Judah exulted because of your judgments, O Lord.
019	PSA	097	009	For you are the Most High Lord over all the earth. You are greatly exalted above all gods.
019	PSA	097	010	You who love the Lord: hate evil. The Lord watches over the souls of his holy ones. He will free them from the hand of the sinner.
019	PSA	097	011	The light has risen for the just, and joy for the upright of heart.
019	PSA	097	012	Rejoice in the Lord, you just ones, and confess to the memory of his sanctuary.
019	PSA	098	001	A Psalm of David himself. Sing to the Lord a new song, for he has performed wonders. His right hand has accomplished salvation for him, with his holy arm.
019	PSA	098	002	The Lord has made known his salvation. He has revealed his justice in the sight of the nations.
019	PSA	098	003	He has remembered his mercy and his truth toward the house of Israel. All the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.
019	PSA	098	004	Sing joyfully to God, all the earth. Sing and exult, and sing psalms.
019	PSA	098	005	Sing psalms to the Lord with stringed instruments, with strings and the voice of a psalmist,
019	PSA	098	006	with subtle wind instruments and the voice of woodwinds. Make a joyful noise before the Lord our king.
019	PSA	098	007	Let the sea be moved and all its fullness, the whole world and all who dwell in it.
019	PSA	098	008	The rivers will clap their hands, the mountains will exult together,
019	PSA	098	009	before the presence of the Lord. For he comes to judge the earth. He will judge the whole world with justice, and the peoples with fairness.
019	PSA	099	001	A Psalm of David himself. The Lord has reigned: let the peoples be angry. He sits upon the cherubim: let the earth be moved.
019	PSA	099	002	The Lord is great in Zion, and he is high above all peoples.
019	PSA	099	003	May they confess to your great name, for it is terrible and holy.
019	PSA	099	004	And the honor of the king loves judgment. You have prepared guidance. You have accomplished judgment and justice in Jacob.
019	PSA	099	005	Exalt the Lord our God, and adore the footstool of his feet, for it is holy.
019	PSA	099	006	Moses and Aaron are among his priests, and Samuel is among those who call upon his name. They called upon the Lord, and he heeded them.
019	PSA	099	007	He spoke to them in the pillar of the cloud. They kept his testimonies and the precept that he gave them.
019	PSA	099	008	You heeded them, O Lord our God. You were a forgiving God to them, though taking vengeance on all their inventions.
019	PSA	099	009	Exalt the Lord our God, and adore on his holy mountain. For the Lord our God is holy.
019	PSA	100	001	A Psalm of Confession.
019	PSA	100	002	Shout joyfully to God, all the earth. Serve the Lord with rejoicing. Enter into his sight in exultation.
019	PSA	100	003	Know that the Lord himself is God. He made us, and we ourselves did not. We are his people and the sheep of his pasture.
019	PSA	100	004	Enter his gates with confession, his courts with hymns, and acknowledge him. Praise his name.
019	PSA	100	005	For the Lord is sweet, his mercy is in eternity, and his truth is from generation to generation.
019	PSA	101	001	A Psalm of David himself. I will sing mercy and judgment to you, O Lord. I will sing psalms.
019	PSA	101	002	And I will have understanding within the immaculate way, when you will draw near to me. I wandered about in the innocence of my heart, in the midst of my house.
019	PSA	101	003	I will not display any unjust thing before my eyes. I have hated those carrying out betrayals.
019	PSA	101	004	The perverse heart did not adhere to me. And the malignant, who turned away before me, I would not recognize.
019	PSA	101	005	The one who secretly detracted his neighbor, this one I pursued. The one with an arrogant eye and an insatiable heart, with that one I would not eat.
019	PSA	101	006	My eyes looked toward the faithful of the earth, to sit with me. The one walking in the immaculate way, this one ministered to me.
019	PSA	101	007	He who has acted arrogantly will not dwell in the midst of my house. He who has spoken iniquity was not guided with the sight of my eyes.
019	PSA	101	008	In the morning, I executed all the sinners of the earth, so that I might scatter all the workers of iniquity from the city of the Lord.
019	PSA	102	001	The prayer of the pauper, when he was anxious, and so he poured out his petition in the sight of the Lord. O Lord, hear my prayer, and let my outcry reach you.
019	PSA	102	002	Do not turn your face away from me. In whatever day that I am in trouble, incline your ear to me. In whatever day that I will call upon you, heed me quickly.
019	PSA	102	003	For my days have faded away like smoke, and my bones have dried out like firewood.
019	PSA	102	004	I have been cut down like hay, and my heart has withered, for I had forgotten to eat my bread.
019	PSA	102	005	Before the voice of my groaning, my bone has adhered to my flesh.
019	PSA	102	006	I have become like a pelican in solitude. I have become like a night raven in a house.
019	PSA	102	007	I have kept vigil, and I have become like a solitary sparrow on a roof.
019	PSA	102	008	All day long my enemies reproached me, and those who praised me swore oaths against me.
019	PSA	102	009	For I chewed on ashes like bread, and I mixed weeping into my drink.
019	PSA	102	010	By the face of your anger and indignation, you lifted me up and threw me down.
019	PSA	102	011	My days have declined like a shadow, and I have dried out like hay.
019	PSA	102	012	But you, O Lord, endure for eternity, and your memorial is from generation to generation.
019	PSA	102	013	You will rise up and take pity on Zion, for it is time for its mercy, for the time has come.
019	PSA	102	014	For its stones have pleased your servants, and they will take pity on its land.
019	PSA	102	015	And the Gentiles will fear your name, O Lord, and all the kings of the earth your glory.
019	PSA	102	016	For the Lord has built up Zion, and he will be seen in his glory.
019	PSA	102	017	He has noticed the prayer of the humble, and he has not despised their petition.
019	PSA	102	018	Let these things be written in another generation, and the people who will be created will praise the Lord.
019	PSA	102	019	For he has gazed from his high sanctuary. From heaven, the Lord has beheld the earth.
019	PSA	102	020	So may he hear the groans of those in shackles, in order that he may release the sons of the slain.
019	PSA	102	021	So may they announce the name of the Lord in Zion and his praise in Jerusalem:
019	PSA	102	022	while the people convene, along with kings, in order that they may serve the Lord.
019	PSA	102	023	He responded to him in the way of his virtue: Declare to me the brevity of my days.
019	PSA	102	024	Do not call me back in the middle of my days: your years are from generation to generation.
019	PSA	102	025	In the beginning, O Lord, you founded the earth. And the heavens are the work of your hands.
019	PSA	102	026	They will perish, but you remain. And all will grow old like a garment. And, like a blanket, you will change them, and they will be changed.
019	PSA	102	027	Yet you are ever yourself, and your years will not decline.
019	PSA	102	028	The sons of your servants will live, and their offspring will be guided aright in every age.
019	PSA	103	001	To David himself. Bless the Lord, O my soul, and bless his holy name, all that is within me.
019	PSA	103	002	Bless the Lord, O my soul, and do not forget all his recompenses.
019	PSA	103	003	He forgives all your iniquities. He heals all your infirmities.
019	PSA	103	004	He redeems your life from destruction. He crowns you with mercy and compassion.
019	PSA	103	005	He satisfies your desire with good things. Your youth will be renewed like that of the eagle.
019	PSA	103	006	The Lord accomplishes mercies, and his judgment is for all who patiently endure injuries.
019	PSA	103	007	He has made his ways known to Moses, his will to the sons of Israel.
019	PSA	103	008	The Lord is compassionate and merciful, patient and full of mercy.
019	PSA	103	009	He will not be angry forever, and he will not threaten for eternity.
019	PSA	103	010	He has not dealt with us according to our sins, and he has not repaid us according to our iniquities.
019	PSA	103	011	For according to the height of the heavens above the earth, so has he reinforced his mercy toward those who fear him.
019	PSA	103	012	As far as the east is from the west, so far has he removed our iniquities from us.
019	PSA	103	013	As a father is compassionate to his sons, so has the Lord been compassionate to those who fear him.
019	PSA	103	014	For he knows our form. He has called to mind that we are dust.
019	PSA	103	015	Man: his days are like hay. Like the flower of the field, so will he flourish.
019	PSA	103	016	For the spirit in him will pass away, and it will not remain, and he will know his place no longer.
019	PSA	103	017	But the mercy of the Lord is from eternity, and even unto eternity, upon those who fear him. And his justice is with the sons of the sons,
019	PSA	103	018	with those who serve his covenant and have been mindful of his commandments by doing them.
019	PSA	103	019	The Lord has prepared his throne in heaven, and his kingdom will rule over all.
019	PSA	103	020	Bless the Lord, all you his Angels: powerful in virtue, doing his word, in order to heed the voice of his discourse.
019	PSA	103	021	Bless the Lord, all his hosts: his ministers who do his will.
019	PSA	103	022	Bless the Lord, all his works: in every place of his dominion. Bless the Lord, O my soul.
019	PSA	104	001	To David himself. Bless the Lord, O my soul. O Lord my God, you are exceedingly great. You have clothed yourself with confession and beauty;
019	PSA	104	002	you are dressed with light like a garment, while you stretch out heaven like a tent.
019	PSA	104	003	You cover its heights with water. You set the clouds as your stairs. You walk upon the wings of the winds.
019	PSA	104	004	You make your Angels a breath of life, and your ministers a burning fire.
019	PSA	104	005	You founded the earth upon its stable base. It will not be bent from age to age.
019	PSA	104	006	The abyss, like a garment, is its clothing. The waters will remain standing above the mountains.
019	PSA	104	007	At your rebuke, they will flee. At the voice of your thunder, they will dread.
019	PSA	104	008	The mountains ascend, and the plains descend, to the place which you have founded for them.
019	PSA	104	009	You have set a limit that they will not cross. And they will not return to cover the earth.
019	PSA	104	010	You spring forth fountains in steep valleys. The waters will cross through the midst of the mountains.
019	PSA	104	011	All the wild beasts of the field will drink. The wild donkeys will anticipate in their thirst.
019	PSA	104	012	Above them, the flying things of the air will dwell. From the midst of the rocks, they will utter voices.
019	PSA	104	013	You irrigate the mountains from your heights. The earth will be satiated from the fruit of your works,
019	PSA	104	014	producing grass for cattle and herbs for the service of men. So may you draw bread from the earth,
019	PSA	104	015	and wine, in order to cheer the heart of man. Then he may gladden his face with oil, and bread will confirm the heart of man.
019	PSA	104	016	The trees of the field will be saturated, along with the cedars of Lebanon, which he planted.
019	PSA	104	017	There, the sparrows will make their nests. The leader of them is the house of the heron.
019	PSA	104	018	The heights of the hills are for the deer; the rock is a refuge for the hedgehog.
019	PSA	104	019	He has made the moon for seasons; the sun knows its setting.
019	PSA	104	020	You appointed darkness, and it has become night; all the beasts of the forest will cross through it.
019	PSA	104	021	The young lions will roar, while searching for and seizing their meal from God.
019	PSA	104	022	The sun arose, and they were gathered together; and in their dens, they will lie down together.
019	PSA	104	023	Man will go forth to his work and to his activities, until the evening.
019	PSA	104	024	How great are your works, O Lord! You have made all things in wisdom. The earth has been filled with your possessions.
019	PSA	104	025	This sea is great and its hands are spacious. There are creeping things without number: the small animals with the great.
019	PSA	104	026	There, the ships will pass by this sea-serpent that you have formed to mock them.
019	PSA	104	027	All these expect you to give them food in due time.
019	PSA	104	028	What you give to them, they will gather. When you open your hand, they will all be filled with goodness.
019	PSA	104	029	But if you turn your face away, they will be disturbed. You will take away their breath, and they will fail, and they will return to their dust.
019	PSA	104	030	You will send forth your Spirit, and they will be created. And you will renew the face of the earth.
019	PSA	104	031	May the glory of the Lord be for all ages. The Lord will rejoice in his works.
019	PSA	104	032	He considers the earth, and he makes it tremble. He touches the mountains, and they smoke.
019	PSA	104	033	I will sing to the Lord with my life. I will sing psalms to my God, as long as I am.
019	PSA	104	034	May my speech be pleasing to him. Truly, I will take delight in the Lord.
019	PSA	104	035	Let sinners fade away from the earth, along with the unjust, so that they may not be. Bless the Lord, O my soul.
019	PSA	105	001	Alleluia. Confess to the Lord, and invoke his name. Announce his works among the nations.
019	PSA	105	002	Sing to him, and sing psalms to him. Describe all his wonders.
019	PSA	105	003	Be praised in his holy name. Let the heart of those who seek the Lord rejoice.
019	PSA	105	004	Seek the Lord, and be confirmed. Seek his face always.
019	PSA	105	005	Remember his miracles, which he has done, his portents and the judgments of his mouth:
019	PSA	105	006	you offspring of Abraham his servant, you sons of Jacob his elect.
019	PSA	105	007	He is the Lord our God. His judgments are throughout the entire earth.
019	PSA	105	008	He has remembered his covenant for all ages: the word that he entrusted to a thousand generations,
019	PSA	105	009	which he assigned to Abraham, and his oath to Isaac.
019	PSA	105	010	And he stationed the same for Jacob with a precept, and for Israel with an eternal testament,
019	PSA	105	011	saying: To you, I will give the land of Canaan, the allotment of your inheritance.
019	PSA	105	012	Though they may have been but a small number, very few and foreigners there,
019	PSA	105	013	and though they passed from nation to nation, and from one kingdom to another people,
019	PSA	105	014	he allowed no man to harm them, and he reproved kings on their behalf.
019	PSA	105	015	Do not be willing to touch my Christ, and do not be willing to malign my prophets.
019	PSA	105	016	And he called a famine upon the land, and he crushed every foundation of the bread.
019	PSA	105	017	He sent a man before them: Joseph, who had been sold as a slave.
019	PSA	105	018	They humbled his feet in shackles; the iron pierced his soul,
019	PSA	105	019	until his word arrived. The eloquence of the Lord inflamed him.
019	PSA	105	020	The king sent and released him; he was the ruler of the people, and he dismissed him.
019	PSA	105	021	He established him as master of his house and ruler of all his possessions,
019	PSA	105	022	so that he might instruct his princes as himself, and teach his elders prudence.
019	PSA	105	023	And Israel entered into Egypt, and Jacob became a sojourner in the land of Ham.
019	PSA	105	024	And he helped his people greatly, and he strengthened them over their enemies.
019	PSA	105	025	He turned their heart to hate his people, and to deal deceitfully with his servants.
019	PSA	105	026	He sent Moses, his servant, and Aaron, the one whom he chose.
019	PSA	105	027	He placed with them signs of his word, and portents in the land of Ham.
019	PSA	105	028	He sent darkness and made it conceal, and he did not afflict them with his speech.
019	PSA	105	029	He turned their waters into blood, and he slaughtered their fish.
019	PSA	105	030	Their land brought forth frogs, even in the inner chambers of their kings.
019	PSA	105	031	He spoke, and there came forth common flies and gnats, in every region.
019	PSA	105	032	He gave them a shower of hail and a burning fire, in the same land.
019	PSA	105	033	And he struck their vineyards and their fig trees, and he crushed the trees of their region.
019	PSA	105	034	He spoke, and the locust came forth, and the caterpillar, of which there was no number.
019	PSA	105	035	And it devoured all the grass in their land, and it consumed all the fruit of their land.
019	PSA	105	036	And he struck all the first-born in their land, the first-fruits of all their labor.
019	PSA	105	037	And he led them out with silver and gold, and there was not an infirm one among their tribes.
019	PSA	105	038	Egypt was joyful at their departure, for the fear of them lay heavy upon them.
019	PSA	105	039	He spread a cloud for their protection, and a fire, to give them light through the night.
019	PSA	105	040	They petitioned, and the quail came; and he satisfied them with the bread of heaven.
019	PSA	105	041	He ruptured the rock and the waters flowed: rivers gushed in the dry land.
019	PSA	105	042	For he had called to mind his holy word, which he kept near to his servant Abraham.
019	PSA	105	043	And he led forth his people in exultation, and his elect in rejoicing.
019	PSA	105	044	And he gave them the regions of the Gentiles, and they possessed the labors of the peoples,
019	PSA	105	045	so that they might observe his justifications, and inquire about his law.
019	PSA	106	001	Alleluia. Confess to the Lord, for he is good, for his mercy is with every generation.
019	PSA	106	002	Who will declare the powers of the Lord? Who make a hearing for all his praises?
019	PSA	106	003	Blessed are those who keep judgment and who do justice at all times.
019	PSA	106	004	Remember us, O Lord, with good will for your people. Visit us with your salvation,
019	PSA	106	005	so that we may see the goodness of your elect, so that we may rejoice in the joy of your nation, so that you may be praised along with your inheritance.
019	PSA	106	006	We have sinned, as have our fathers. We have acted unjustly; we have wrought iniquity.
019	PSA	106	007	Our fathers did not understand your miracles in Egypt. They did not remember the multitude of your mercies. And they provoked you, while going up to the sea, even the Red Sea.
019	PSA	106	008	And he saved them for the sake of his name, so that he might make known his power.
019	PSA	106	009	And he rebuked the Red Sea, and it dried up. And he led them into the abyss, as if into a desert.
019	PSA	106	010	And he saved them from the hand of those who hated them. And he redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.
019	PSA	106	011	And the water covered those who troubled them. Not one of them remained.
019	PSA	106	012	And they believed his words, and they sang his praises.
019	PSA	106	013	As soon as they had finished, they forgot his works, and they would not endure his counsel.
019	PSA	106	014	And they coveted their desire in the desert, and they tempted God in a waterless place.
019	PSA	106	015	And he granted to them their request, and he sent abundance into their souls.
019	PSA	106	016	And they provoked Moses in the camp, and Aaron, the holy one of the Lord.
019	PSA	106	017	The earth opened and swallowed Dathan, and it covered the congregation of Abiram.
019	PSA	106	018	And a fire broke out in their congregation. A flame burned up the sinners.
019	PSA	106	019	And they fashioned a calf at Horeb, and they adored a graven image.
019	PSA	106	020	And they exchanged their glory for the likeness of a calf that eats hay.
019	PSA	106	021	They forgot God, who saved them, who did great things in Egypt:
019	PSA	106	022	miracles in the land of Ham, terrible things at the Red Sea.
019	PSA	106	023	And he said that he would destroy them, yet Moses, his elect, stood firm before him in the breach, in order to avert his wrath, lest he destroy them.
019	PSA	106	024	And they held the desirable land to be nothing. They did not trust in his word.
019	PSA	106	025	And they murmured in their tabernacles. They did not heed the voice of the Lord.
019	PSA	106	026	And he lifted up his hand over them, in order to prostrate them in the desert,
019	PSA	106	027	and in order to cast their offspring among the nations, and to scatter them among the regions.
019	PSA	106	028	And they were initiated into Baal of Peor, and they ate the sacrifices of the dead.
019	PSA	106	029	And they provoked him with their inventions, and ruination was multiplied in them.
019	PSA	106	030	Then Phinehas stood up and placated him: and so the violent disturbance ceased.
019	PSA	106	031	And it was reputed to him unto justice, from generation to generation, even forever.
019	PSA	106	032	And they provoked him at the Waters of Contradiction, and Moses was afflicted because of them,
019	PSA	106	033	for they exasperated his spirit. And so he divided them with his lips.
019	PSA	106	034	They did not destroy the nations, about which the Lord had spoken to them.
019	PSA	106	035	And they were mixed among the Gentiles. And they learned their works,
019	PSA	106	036	and they served their graven images, and it became a scandal to them.
019	PSA	106	037	And they sacrificed their sons and their daughters to demons.
019	PSA	106	038	And they shed innocent blood: the blood of their sons and of their daughters, which they sacrificed to the graven images of Canaan. And the land was infected with bloodshed,
019	PSA	106	039	and was contaminated with their works. And they fornicated according to their own inventions.
019	PSA	106	040	And the Lord became furiously angry with his people, and he abhorred his inheritance.
019	PSA	106	041	And he delivered them into the hands of the nations. And those who hated them became rulers over them.
019	PSA	106	042	And their enemies afflicted them, and they were humbled under their hands.
019	PSA	106	043	Many times, he delivered them. Yet they provoked him with their counsel, and they were brought low by their iniquities.
019	PSA	106	044	And he saw that they were in tribulation, and he heard their prayer.
019	PSA	106	045	And he was mindful of his covenant, and he repented according to the multitude of his mercies.
019	PSA	106	046	And he provided for them with mercies, in the sight of all those who had seized them.
019	PSA	106	047	Save us, O Lord our God, and gather us from the nations, so that we may confess your holy name and glory in your praise.
019	PSA	106	048	Blessed is the Lord God of Israel, from ages past, even to all ages. And let all the people say: Amen. Amen.
019	PSA	107	001	Alleluia. Confess to the Lord, for he is good, for his mercy is with every generation.
019	PSA	107	002	Let those who have been redeemed by the Lord say so: those whom he redeemed from the hand of the enemy and gathered from the regions,
019	PSA	107	003	from the rising of the sun and its setting, from the north and from the sea.
019	PSA	107	004	They wandered into solitude in a waterless place. They did not find the way of the city to be their dwelling place.
019	PSA	107	005	They were hungry, and they were thirsty. Their soul fainted within them.
019	PSA	107	006	And they cried out to the Lord in tribulation, and he rescued them in their necessity.
019	PSA	107	007	And he led them in the right way, so that they might go forth to a city of habitation.
019	PSA	107	008	Let his mercies confess to the Lord, and let his miracles confess to the sons of men.
019	PSA	107	009	For he has satisfied the empty soul, and he has satisfied the hungry soul with good things:
019	PSA	107	010	those sitting in darkness and in the shadow of death, shackled by extreme poverty and by iron.
019	PSA	107	011	For they exasperated the eloquence of God, and they irritated the deliberation of the Most High.
019	PSA	107	012	And their heart was brought low with hardships. They were weakened, and there was no one to help them.
019	PSA	107	013	And they cried out to the Lord in their tribulation, and he freed them from their distress.
019	PSA	107	014	And he led them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and he broke apart their chains.
019	PSA	107	015	Let his mercies confess to the Lord, and let his miracles confess to the sons of men.
019	PSA	107	016	For he has crushed the gates of brass and broken the iron bars.
019	PSA	107	017	He has taken them up, from the way of their iniquity. For they were brought low, because of their injustices.
019	PSA	107	018	Their soul abhorred all food, and they drew near even to the gates of death.
019	PSA	107	019	And they cried out to the Lord in their tribulation, and he delivered them in their necessity.
019	PSA	107	020	He sent his word, and he healed them, and he rescued them from their utter destruction.
019	PSA	107	021	Let his mercies confess to the Lord, and let his miracles confess to the sons of men.
019	PSA	107	022	And let them offer sacrifice with the sacrifice of praise, and let them announce his works in exultation.
019	PSA	107	023	Those who descend to the sea in ships, making their livelihood in the great waters:
019	PSA	107	024	these have seen the works of the Lord and his wonders in the deep.
019	PSA	107	025	He spoke: and a windstorm stood up, and its waves were exalted.
019	PSA	107	026	They ascend even to the heavens, and they descend even to the abyss. Their soul will waste away in distress.
019	PSA	107	027	They were troubled, and they moved like a drunkard, and all their wisdom was consumed.
019	PSA	107	028	And they cried out to the Lord in their tribulation, and he led them out of their distress.
019	PSA	107	029	And he replaced the storm with a breeze, and its waves were stilled.
019	PSA	107	030	And they were joyful that it was stilled, and he led them into the haven that they desired.
019	PSA	107	031	Let his mercies confess to the Lord, and let his miracles confess to the sons of men.
019	PSA	107	032	And let them exalt him in the Church of the people, and praise him in the chair of the elders.
019	PSA	107	033	He has placed rivers in the desert and sources of water in dry places,
019	PSA	107	034	a fruit-bearing land in the midst of brine, before the malice of those who dwell in it.
019	PSA	107	035	He has placed a desert in the midst of pools of waters, and a land without water in the midst of sources of water.
019	PSA	107	036	And he has gathered the hungry together there, and they constructed a city of habitation.
019	PSA	107	037	And they sowed fields and planted vineyards, and they produced the fruit of nativity.
019	PSA	107	038	And he blessed them, and they were multiplied exceedingly. And he did not diminish their beasts of burden.
019	PSA	107	039	And they became few, and they were afflicted by the tribulation of evils and of sorrow.
019	PSA	107	040	Contempt was poured over their leaders, and he caused them to wander in an impassable place, and not on the way.
019	PSA	107	041	And he helped the poor out of destitution, and he stationed families like sheep.
019	PSA	107	042	The upright will see, and they will rejoice. And every iniquity will block its mouth.
019	PSA	107	043	Who is wise and will keep these things? And who will understand the mercies of the Lord?
019	PSA	108	001	A Canticle Psalm, of David himself. My heart is prepared, O God, my heart is prepared. I will sing songs, and I will sing psalms in my glory.
019	PSA	108	002	Rise up, my glory. Rise up, Psalter and harp. I will arise in early morning.
019	PSA	108	003	I will confess to you, O Lord, among the peoples. And I will sing psalms to you among the nations.
019	PSA	108	004	For your mercy is great, beyond the heavens, and your truth, even to the clouds.
019	PSA	108	005	Be exalted, O God, beyond the heavens, and your glory, beyond all the earth,
019	PSA	108	006	so that your beloved may be freed. Save with your right hand, and heed me.
019	PSA	108	007	God has spoken in his holiness. I will exult, and I will divide Shechem, and I will divide by measure the steep valley of tabernacles.
019	PSA	108	008	Gilead is mine, and Manasseh is mine, and Ephraim is the supporter of my head. Judah is my king.
019	PSA	108	009	Moab is the cooking pot of my hope. I will extend my shoe in Idumea; the foreigners have become my friends.
019	PSA	108	010	Who will lead me into the fortified city? Who will lead me, even into Idumea?
019	PSA	108	011	Will not you, O God, who had rejected us? And will not you, O God, go out with our armies?
019	PSA	108	012	Grant us help from tribulation, for vain is the help of man.
019	PSA	108	013	In God, we will act virtuously, and he will bring our enemies to nothing.
019	PSA	109	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David.
019	PSA	109	002	O God, do not be silent toward my praise, for the mouth of the sinner and the mouth of the deceitful one have been opened against me.
019	PSA	109	003	They have spoken against me with deceitful tongues, and they have surrounded me with hateful words, and they fought against me over nothing.
019	PSA	109	004	Instead of choosing to act on my behalf, they detracted me. But I gave myself to prayer.
019	PSA	109	005	And they set evil against me, instead of good, and hatred, in return for my love.
019	PSA	109	006	Establish the sinner over him, and let the devil stand at his right hand.
019	PSA	109	007	When he is judged, may he go forth in condemnation, and may his prayer be counted as sin.
019	PSA	109	008	May his days be few, and let another take his episcopate.
019	PSA	109	009	May his sons be orphans, and his wife a widow.
019	PSA	109	010	May his sons be carried by those who walk unsteadily, and may they go begging. And may they be cast out of their dwelling places.
019	PSA	109	011	May the money lenders scrutinize all his belongings, and let foreigners plunder his labors.
019	PSA	109	012	May there be no one to assist him, nor anyone to be compassionate to his orphaned children.
019	PSA	109	013	May his posterity be in utter ruin. In one generation, may his name be wiped away.
019	PSA	109	014	May the iniquity of his fathers return in memory before the sight of the Lord, and do not let the sin of his mother be wiped away.
019	PSA	109	015	May these be opposite the Lord always, but let their memory perish from the earth.
019	PSA	109	016	For certain things are not remembered about them, in order to be merciful.
019	PSA	109	017	And so the destitute man was pursued, with the beggar and the remorseful in heart, so as to be put to death.
019	PSA	109	018	And he loved a curse, and it came to him. And he was unwilling to have a blessing, and it went far from him. And he clothed himself with curses like a garment, and it entered his inner self like water, and it entered his bones like oil.
019	PSA	109	019	May it be to him like a garment that covers him, and like a belt that always cinches him.
019	PSA	109	020	This is the work of those who detract me with the Lord and who speak evils against my soul.
019	PSA	109	021	But as for you, Lord, O Lord: act on my behalf for your name’s sake. For your mercy is sweet.
019	PSA	109	022	Free me, for I am destitute and poor, and my heart has been disquieted within me.
019	PSA	109	023	I have been taken away like a shadow when it declines, and I have been shaken off like locusts.
019	PSA	109	024	My knees have been weakened by fasting, and my flesh has been replaced by oil.
019	PSA	109	025	And I have become a disgrace to them. They saw me, and they shook their heads.
019	PSA	109	026	Help me, O Lord, my God. Save me according to your mercy.
019	PSA	109	027	And let them know that this is your hand, and that you, O Lord, have done this.
019	PSA	109	028	They will curse, and you will bless. May those who rise up against me be confounded. But your servant will rejoice.
019	PSA	109	029	May those who detract me be clothed with shame, and may they be covered with their confusion, as if with a double cloak.
019	PSA	109	030	I will confess exceedingly to the Lord with my mouth. And I will praise him in the midst of the multitude.
019	PSA	109	031	For he stands at the right hand of the poor, in order to save my soul from persecutors.
019	PSA	110	001	A Psalm of David. The Lord said to my Lord, “Sit at my right hand, until I make your enemies your footstool.”
019	PSA	110	002	The Lord will send forth the scepter of your virtue from Zion. Rule in the midst of your enemies.
019	PSA	110	003	It is with you from the beginning, in the day of your virtue, in the splendor of the saints. From conception, before the light-bearer, I begot you.
019	PSA	110	004	The Lord has sworn, and he will not repent: “You are a priest forever, according to the order of Melchizedek.”
019	PSA	110	005	The Lord is at your right hand. He has broken kings in the day of his wrath.
019	PSA	110	006	He will judge between the nations; he will fill up ruination. He will shatter heads in the land of the many.
019	PSA	110	007	He will drink from the torrent on the way. Because of this, he will exalt the head.
019	PSA	111	001	Alleluia. I will confess to you, O Lord, with my whole heart, in the council of the just and in the congregation.
019	PSA	111	002	Great are the works of the Lord, exquisite in all his intentions.
019	PSA	111	003	Confession and magnificence are his work. And his justice remains from age to age.
019	PSA	111	004	He has created a memorial to his wonders; he is a merciful and compassionate Lord.
019	PSA	111	005	He has given food to those who fear him. He will be mindful of his covenant in every age.
019	PSA	111	006	He will announce the virtue of his works to his people,
019	PSA	111	007	so that he may give them the inheritance of the nations. The works of his hands are truth and judgment.
019	PSA	111	008	All his commands are faithful: confirmed from age to age, created in truth and fairness.
019	PSA	111	009	He has sent redemption upon his people. He has commanded his covenant for all eternity. Holy and terrible is his name.
019	PSA	111	010	The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom. A good understanding is for all who do it. His praise remains from age to age.
019	PSA	112	001	Alleluia. Of the return of Haggai and Zachariah. Blessed is the man who fears the Lord. He will prefer his commandments exceedingly.
019	PSA	112	002	His offspring will be powerful on the earth. The generation of the upright will be blessed.
019	PSA	112	003	Glory and wealth will be in his house, and his justice shall remain from age to age.
019	PSA	112	004	For the upright, a light has risen up in the darkness. He is merciful and compassionate and just.
019	PSA	112	005	Pleasing is the man who shows mercy and lends. He will order his words with judgment.
019	PSA	112	006	For he will not be disturbed in eternity.
019	PSA	112	007	The just one will be an everlasting memorial. He will not fear a report of disasters. His heart is prepared to hope in the Lord.
019	PSA	112	008	His heart has been confirmed. He will not be disturbed, until he looks down upon his enemies.
019	PSA	112	009	He has distributed, he has given to the poor. His justice shall remain from age to age. His horn shall be exalted in glory.
019	PSA	112	010	The sinner will see and become angry. He will gnash his teeth and waste away. The desire of sinners will perish.
019	PSA	113	001	Alleluia. Praise the Lord, children. Praise the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	113	002	Blessed is the name of the Lord, from this time forward and even forever.
019	PSA	113	003	From the rising of the sun, even to its setting, praiseworthy is the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	113	004	The Lord is high above all nations, and his glory is high above the heavens.
019	PSA	113	005	Who is like the Lord, our God, who dwells on high,
019	PSA	113	006	and who gazes upon the humble things in heaven and on earth?
019	PSA	113	007	He lifts up the needy from the ground, and he urges the poor away from filth,
019	PSA	113	008	so that he may place him with the leaders, with the leaders of his people.
019	PSA	113	009	He causes a barren woman to live in a house, as the joyful mother of sons.
019	PSA	114	001	Alleluia. At the departure of Israel from Egypt, the house of Jacob from a barbarous people:
019	PSA	114	002	Judea was made his sanctuary; Israel was made his power.
019	PSA	114	003	The sea looked, and it fled. The Jordan was turned back again.
019	PSA	114	004	The mountains exulted like rams, and the hills like lambs among the sheep.
019	PSA	114	005	What happened to you, O sea, so that you fled, and to you, O Jordan, so that you were turned back again?
019	PSA	114	006	What happened to you, O mountains, so that you exulted like rams, and to you, O hills, so that you exulted like lambs among the sheep?
019	PSA	114	007	Before the face of the Lord, the earth was moved, before the face of the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	114	008	He converted the rock into pools of water, and the cliff into fountains of waters.
019	PSA	115	001	Not to us, O Lord, not to us, but to your name give glory.
019	PSA	115	002	Give glory to your mercy and your truth, lest the Gentiles should say, “Where is their God?”
019	PSA	115	003	But our God is in heaven. All things whatsoever that he has willed, he has done.
019	PSA	115	004	The idols of the nations are silver and gold, the works of the hands of men.
019	PSA	115	005	They have mouths, and do not speak; they have eyes, and do not see.
019	PSA	115	006	They have ears, and do not hear; they have noses, and do not smell.
019	PSA	115	007	They have hands, and do not feel; they have feet, and do not walk. Neither will they cry out with their throat.
019	PSA	115	008	Let those who make them become like them, along with all who trust in them.
019	PSA	115	009	The house of Israel has hoped in the Lord. He is their helper and their protector.
019	PSA	115	010	The house of Aaron has hoped in the Lord. He is their helper and their protector.
019	PSA	115	011	Those who fear the Lord have hoped in the Lord. He is their helper and their protector.
019	PSA	115	012	The Lord has been mindful of us, and he has blessed us. He has blessed the house of Israel. He has blessed the house of Aaron.
019	PSA	115	013	He has blessed all who fear the Lord, the small with the great.
019	PSA	115	014	May the Lord add blessings upon you: upon you, and upon your sons.
019	PSA	115	015	Blessed are you by the Lord, who made heaven and earth.
019	PSA	115	016	The heaven of heaven is for the Lord, but the earth he has given to the sons of men.
019	PSA	115	017	The dead will not praise you, Lord, and neither will all those who descend into Hell.
019	PSA	115	018	But we who live will bless the Lord, from this time forward, and even forever.
019	PSA	116	001	Alleluia. I have loved: therefore, the Lord will heed the voice of my prayer.
019	PSA	116	002	For he has inclined his ear to me. And in my days, I will call upon him.
019	PSA	116	003	The sorrows of death have surrounded me, and the perils of Hell have found me. I have found tribulation and sorrow.
019	PSA	116	004	And so, I called upon the name of the Lord. O Lord, free my soul.
019	PSA	116	005	Merciful is the Lord, and just. And our God is compassionate.
019	PSA	116	006	The Lord is the keeper of little ones. I was humbled, and he freed me.
019	PSA	116	007	Turn again, my soul, to your rest. For the Lord has done good to you.
019	PSA	116	008	For he has rescued my soul from death, my eyes from tears, my feet from slipping.
019	PSA	116	009	I will please the Lord in the land of the living.
019	PSA	116	010	Alleluia. I had confidence, because of what I was saying, but then I was greatly humbled.
019	PSA	116	011	I said in my excess, “Every man is a liar.”
019	PSA	116	012	What shall I repay to the Lord, for all the things that he has repaid to me?
019	PSA	116	013	I will take up the cup of salvation, and I will call upon the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	116	014	I will repay my vows to the Lord, in the sight of all his people.
019	PSA	116	015	Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of his holy ones.
019	PSA	116	016	O Lord, because I am your servant, your servant and the son of your handmaid, you have broken my bonds.
019	PSA	116	017	I will sacrifice to you the sacrifice of praise, and I will invoke the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	116	018	I will repay my vows to the Lord in the sight of all his people,
019	PSA	116	019	in the courts of the house of the Lord, in your midst, O Jerusalem.
019	PSA	117	001	Alleluia. All nations, praise the Lord. All peoples, praise him.
019	PSA	117	002	For his mercy has been confirmed over us. And the truth of the Lord remains for all eternity.
019	PSA	118	001	Alleluia. Confess to the Lord, for he is good, for his mercy is forever.
019	PSA	118	002	Let Israel now say: For he is good, for his mercy is forever.
019	PSA	118	003	Let the house of Aaron now say: For his mercy is forever.
019	PSA	118	004	Let those who fear the Lord now say: For his mercy is forever.
019	PSA	118	005	In my tribulation, I called upon the Lord. And the Lord heeded me with generosity.
019	PSA	118	006	The Lord is my helper. I will not fear what man can do to me.
019	PSA	118	007	The Lord is my helper. And I will look down upon my enemies.
019	PSA	118	008	It is good to trust in the Lord, rather than to trust in man.
019	PSA	118	009	It is good to hope in the Lord, rather than to hope in leaders.
019	PSA	118	010	All the nations have surrounded me. And, in the name of the Lord, I have been avenged over them.
019	PSA	118	011	Surrounding me, they closed in on me. And, in the name of the Lord, I have been avenged over them.
019	PSA	118	012	They surrounded me like a swarm, and they burned like fire among the thorns. And, in the name of the Lord, I have been avenged over them.
019	PSA	118	013	Having been pushed, I was overturned so as to fall. But the Lord took me up.
019	PSA	118	014	The Lord is my strength and my praise. And he has become my salvation.
019	PSA	118	015	A voice of exultation and salvation is in the tabernacles of the just.
019	PSA	118	016	The right hand of the Lord has wrought virtue. The right hand of the Lord has exalted me. The right hand of the Lord has wrought virtue.
019	PSA	118	017	I will not die, but I will live. And I will declare the works of the Lord.
019	PSA	118	018	When chastising, the Lord chastised me. But he has not delivered me over to death.
019	PSA	118	019	Open the gates of justice to me. I will enter them, and I will confess to the Lord.
019	PSA	118	020	This is the gate of the Lord. The just will enter by it.
019	PSA	118	021	I will confess to you because you have heard me. And you have become my salvation.
019	PSA	118	022	The stone which the builders have rejected, this has become the head of the corner.
019	PSA	118	023	By the Lord has this been done, and it is a wonder before our eyes.
019	PSA	118	024	This is the day that the Lord has made. Let us exult and rejoice in it.
019	PSA	118	025	O Lord, grant salvation to me. O Lord, grant good prosperity.
019	PSA	118	026	Blessed is he who arrives in the name of the Lord. We have blessed you from the house of the Lord.
019	PSA	118	027	The Lord is God, and he has enlightened us. Establish a solemn day amid a dense crowd, even to the horn of the altar.
019	PSA	118	028	You are my God, and I will confess to you. You are my God, and I will exalt you. I will confess to you, for you have heeded me. And you have become my salvation.
019	PSA	118	029	Confess to the Lord, for he is good, for his mercy is forever.
019	PSA	119	001	Alleluia. Blessed are the immaculate in the way, who walk in the law of the Lord.
019	PSA	119	002	Blessed are those who examine his testimonies. They seek him with their whole heart.
019	PSA	119	003	For those who work iniquity have not walked in his ways.
019	PSA	119	004	You have ordered your commandments to be kept most diligently.
019	PSA	119	005	I wish that my ways may be directed so as to keep your justifications.
019	PSA	119	006	Then I will not be confounded, when I will look into all your commandments.
019	PSA	119	007	I will confess to you with honesty of heart. In this way, I have learned the judgments of your justice.
019	PSA	119	008	I will keep your justifications. Do not utterly abandon me.
019	PSA	119	009	By what does an adolescent correct his way? By keeping to your words.
019	PSA	119	010	With my whole heart, I have sought you. Do not let me be driven away from your commandments.
019	PSA	119	011	I have hidden your eloquence in my heart, so that I may not sin against you.
019	PSA	119	012	Blessed are you, O Lord. Teach me your justifications.
019	PSA	119	013	With my lips, I have pronounced all the judgments of your mouth.
019	PSA	119	014	I have been delighted in the way of your testimonies, as if in all riches.
019	PSA	119	015	I will be trained in your commandments, and I will consider your ways.
019	PSA	119	016	I will meditate on your justifications. I will not forget your words.
019	PSA	119	017	Repay your servant, revive me; and I will keep your words.
019	PSA	119	018	Reveal to my eyes, and I will consider the wonders of your law.
019	PSA	119	019	I am a sojourner on the earth. Do not hide your commandments from me.
019	PSA	119	020	My soul has longed to desire your justifications at all times.
019	PSA	119	021	You have rebuked the arrogant. Those who decline from your commandments are accursed.
019	PSA	119	022	Take me away from disgrace and contempt, for I have sought your testimonies.
019	PSA	119	023	For even the leaders sat and spoke against me. But your servant has been trained in your justifications.
019	PSA	119	024	For your testimonies are also my (meditation) and your justifications are my counsel.
019	PSA	119	025	My soul has adhered to the pavement. Revive me according to your word.
019	PSA	119	026	I have declared my ways, and you have heeded me. Teach me your justifications.
019	PSA	119	027	Instruct me in the way of your justifications, and I will be trained in your wonders.
019	PSA	119	028	My soul has slumbered because of weariness. Confirm me in your words.
019	PSA	119	029	Remove the way of iniquity from me, and have mercy on me by your law.
019	PSA	119	030	I have chosen the way of truth. I have not forgotten your judgments.
019	PSA	119	031	I have adhered to your testimonies, O Lord. Do not be willing to confound me.
019	PSA	119	032	I have run by way of your commandments, when you enlarged my heart.
019	PSA	119	033	O Lord, place the law before me, the way of your justifications, and I will always inquire into it.
019	PSA	119	034	Give me understanding, and I will examine your law. And I will keep it with my whole heart.
019	PSA	119	035	Lead me according to the path of your commandments, for I have desired this.
019	PSA	119	036	Bend my heart with your testimonies, and not with avarice.
019	PSA	119	037	Turn my eyes away, lest they see what is vain. Revive me in your way.
019	PSA	119	038	Station your eloquence with your servant, along with your fear.
019	PSA	119	039	Cut off my disgrace, which I have taken up, for your judgments are delightful.
019	PSA	119	040	Behold, I have longed for your commandments. Revive me in your fairness.
019	PSA	119	041	And let your mercy overwhelm me, O Lord: your salvation according to your eloquence.
019	PSA	119	042	And I will respond to those who reproach me by word, for I have hoped in your words.
019	PSA	119	043	And do not utterly take away the word of truth from my mouth. For in your judgments, I have hoped beyond hope.
019	PSA	119	044	And I will always keep your law, in this age and forever and ever.
019	PSA	119	045	And I have wandered far and wide, because I was seeking your commandments.
019	PSA	119	046	And I spoke of your testimonies in the sight of kings, and I was not confounded.
019	PSA	119	047	And I meditated on your commandments, which I loved.
019	PSA	119	048	And I lifted up my hands to your commandments, which I loved. And I was trained in your justifications.
019	PSA	119	049	Be mindful of your word to your servant, by which you have given me hope.
019	PSA	119	050	This has consoled me in my humiliation, for your word has revived me.
019	PSA	119	051	The arrogant act altogether iniquitously, but I have not turned aside from your law.
019	PSA	119	052	I called to mind your judgments of antiquity, O Lord, and I was consoled.
019	PSA	119	053	Faintness has taken hold of me, because of the sinners, those who abandon your law.
019	PSA	119	054	Your justifications were the subject of my worthy singing, in the place of my pilgrimage.
019	PSA	119	055	During the night, I remembered your name, O Lord, and I kept your law.
019	PSA	119	056	This has happened to me because I sought your justifications.
019	PSA	119	057	O Lord, my portion, I have said that I would keep your law.
019	PSA	119	058	I have beseeched your face with my whole heart. Be merciful to me according to your word.
019	PSA	119	059	I have considered my ways, and I have turned my feet toward your testimonies.
019	PSA	119	060	I have been prepared, and I have not been disturbed, so that I may keep your commandments.
019	PSA	119	061	The ropes of the impious have encircled me, and I have not forgotten your law.
019	PSA	119	062	I arose in the middle of the night to confess to you, over the judgments of your justification.
019	PSA	119	063	I am a partaker with all those who fear you and who keep your commandments.
019	PSA	119	064	The earth, O Lord, is full of your mercy. Teach me your justifications.
019	PSA	119	065	You have done well with your servant, O Lord, according to your word.
019	PSA	119	066	Teach me goodness and discipline and knowledge, for I have trusted your commandments.
019	PSA	119	067	Before I was humbled, I committed offenses; because of this, I have kept to your word.
019	PSA	119	068	You are good, so in your goodness teach me your justifications.
019	PSA	119	069	The iniquity of the arrogant has been multiplied over me. Yet I will examine your commandments with all my heart.
019	PSA	119	070	Their heart has been curdled like milk. Truly, I have meditated on your law.
019	PSA	119	071	It is good for me that you humbled me, so that I may learn your justifications.
019	PSA	119	072	The law of your mouth is good for me, beyond thousands of gold and silver pieces.
019	PSA	119	073	Your hands have created me and formed me. Give me understanding, and I will learn your commandments.
019	PSA	119	074	Those who fear you will see me, and they will rejoice. For I have greatly hoped in your words.
019	PSA	119	075	I know, O Lord, that your judgments are fairness. And in your truth, you have humbled me.
019	PSA	119	076	Let it be your mercy that consoles me, according to your eloquence to your servant.
019	PSA	119	077	Let your compassion draw near to me, and I will live. For your law is my (meditation)
019	PSA	119	078	Let the arrogant be confounded, for unjustly they have done iniquity to me. But I will be trained in your commandments.
019	PSA	119	079	Let those who fear you turn to me, along with those who know your testimonies.
019	PSA	119	080	Let my heart be immaculate in your justifications, so that I may not be confounded.
019	PSA	119	081	My soul has faltered in your salvation, yet in your word, I have hoped beyond hope.
019	PSA	119	082	My eyes have failed in your eloquence, saying, “When will you console me?”
019	PSA	119	083	For I have become like a wineskin in the frost. I have not forgotten your justifications.
019	PSA	119	084	How many are the days of your servant? When will you bring judgment against those who persecute me?
019	PSA	119	085	The iniquitous have spoken fables to me. But these are unlike your law.
019	PSA	119	086	All your commandments are truth. They have been persecuting me unjustly: assist me.
019	PSA	119	087	They have nearly consumed me on earth. Yet I have not forsaken your commandments.
019	PSA	119	088	Revive me according to your mercy. And I will keep the testimonies of your mouth.
019	PSA	119	089	O Lord, your word remains firm in heaven, for all eternity.
019	PSA	119	090	Your truth is from generation to generation. You have founded the earth, and it remains firm.
019	PSA	119	091	By your ordinance, the day perseveres. For all things are in service to you.
019	PSA	119	092	If your law had not been my (meditation) then perhaps I would have perished in my humiliation.
019	PSA	119	093	I will not forget your justifications, for eternity. For by them, you have enlivened me.
019	PSA	119	094	I am yours. Accomplish my salvation. For I have inquired into your justifications.
019	PSA	119	095	The sinners have waited for me, in order to destroy me. I have understood your testimonies.
019	PSA	119	096	I have seen the end of the consummation of all things. Your commandment is exceedingly broad.
019	PSA	119	097	How have I loved your law, O Lord? It is my meditation all day long.
019	PSA	119	098	By your commandment, you have made me able to see far, beyond my enemies. For it is with me for eternity.
019	PSA	119	099	I have understood beyond all my teachers. For your testimonies are my (meditation)
019	PSA	119	100	I have understood beyond the elders. For I have searched your commandments.
019	PSA	119	101	I have prohibited my feet from every evil way, so that I may keep your words.
019	PSA	119	102	I have not declined from your judgments, because you have stationed a law for me.
019	PSA	119	103	How sweet is your eloquence to my palate, more so than honey to my mouth!
019	PSA	119	104	I obtained understanding by your commandments. Because of this, I have hated every way of iniquity.
019	PSA	119	105	Your word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my paths.
019	PSA	119	106	I have sworn it, and so I am determined to keep the judgments of your justice.
019	PSA	119	107	I have been altogether humbled, Lord. Revive me according to your word.
019	PSA	119	108	Make the willing offerings of my mouth well pleasing, Lord, and teach me your judgments.
019	PSA	119	109	My soul is always in my hands, and I have not forgotten your law.
019	PSA	119	110	Sinners have set a snare for me, yet I have not strayed from your commandments.
019	PSA	119	111	I have acquired your testimonies as an inheritance unto eternity, because they are the exultation of my heart.
019	PSA	119	112	I have inclined my heart to do your justifications for eternity, as a recompense.
019	PSA	119	113	I have hated the iniquitous, and I have loved your law.
019	PSA	119	114	You are my helper and my supporter. And in your word, I have greatly hoped.
019	PSA	119	115	Turn away from me, you malignant ones. And I will examine the commandments of my God.
019	PSA	119	116	Uphold me according to your eloquence, and I will live. And let me not be confounded in my expectation.
019	PSA	119	117	Help me, and I will be saved. And I will meditate always on your justifications.
019	PSA	119	118	You have despised all those who fell away from your judgments. For their intention is unjust.
019	PSA	119	119	I have considered all the sinners of the earth to be transgressors. Therefore, I have loved your testimonies.
019	PSA	119	120	Pierce my flesh with your fear, for I am afraid of your judgments.
019	PSA	119	121	I have accomplished judgment and justice. Do not hand me over to those who slander me.
019	PSA	119	122	Uphold your servant in what is good. And do not allow the arrogant to slander me.
019	PSA	119	123	My eyes have failed in your salvation and in the eloquence of your justice.
019	PSA	119	124	Deal with your servant according to your mercy, and teach me your justifications.
019	PSA	119	125	I am your servant. Give me understanding, so that I may know your testimonies.
019	PSA	119	126	It is time to act, O Lord. They have dissipated your law.
019	PSA	119	127	Therefore, I have loved your commandments beyond gold and topaz.
019	PSA	119	128	Because of this, I was directed toward all your commandments. I held hatred for every iniquitous way.
019	PSA	119	129	Your testimonies are wonderful. Therefore, my soul has been examined by them.
019	PSA	119	130	The declaration of your words illuminates, and it gives understanding to little ones.
019	PSA	119	131	I opened my mouth and drew breath, for I desired your commandments.
019	PSA	119	132	Gaze upon me and be merciful to me, according to the judgment of those who love your name.
019	PSA	119	133	Direct my steps according to your eloquence, and let no injustice rule over me.
019	PSA	119	134	Redeem me from the slanders of men, so that I may keep your commandments.
019	PSA	119	135	Make your face shine upon your servant, and teach me your justifications.
019	PSA	119	136	My eyes have gushed like springs of water, because they have not kept your law.
019	PSA	119	137	You are just, O Lord, and your judgment is right.
019	PSA	119	138	You have commanded justice: your testimonies and your truth even more so.
019	PSA	119	139	My zeal has caused me to pine away, because my enemies have forgotten your words.
019	PSA	119	140	Your eloquence has been greatly enflamed, and your servant has loved it.
019	PSA	119	141	I am young and treated with contempt. But I have not forgotten your justifications.
019	PSA	119	142	Your justice is justice for all eternity, and your law is truth.
019	PSA	119	143	Tribulation and anguish have found me. Your commandments are my (meditation)
019	PSA	119	144	Your testimonies are fairness unto eternity. Give me understanding, and I will live.
019	PSA	119	145	I cried out with my whole heart. Heed me, O Lord. I will ask for your justifications.
019	PSA	119	146	I cried out to you. Save me, so that I may keep your commandments.
019	PSA	119	147	I arrived first in maturity, and so I cried out. For in your words, I have hoped beyond hope.
019	PSA	119	148	My eyes preceded the dawn for you, so that I might meditate on your eloquence.
019	PSA	119	149	Hear my voice according to your mercy, O Lord. And revive me according to your judgment.
019	PSA	119	150	Those who persecute me have drawn near to iniquity, but they have been brought far from your law.
019	PSA	119	151	You are near, O Lord, and all your ways are truth.
019	PSA	119	152	I have known from the beginning about your testimonies. For you founded them in eternity.
019	PSA	119	153	See my humiliation and rescue me, for I have not forgotten your law.
019	PSA	119	154	Judge my judgment and redeem me. Revive me because of your eloquence.
019	PSA	119	155	Salvation is far from sinners, because they have not inquired about your justifications.
019	PSA	119	156	Many are your mercies, O Lord. Enliven me according to your judgment.
019	PSA	119	157	Many are those who persecute me and who trouble me. I have not turned away from your testimonies.
019	PSA	119	158	I saw the prevaricators, and I pine away. For they have not kept your word.
019	PSA	119	159	O Lord, see how I have loved your commandments. Revive me in your mercy.
019	PSA	119	160	The beginning of your words is truth. All the judgments of your justice are for eternity.
019	PSA	119	161	The leaders have persecuted me without cause. And my heart has been awed by your words.
019	PSA	119	162	I will rejoice over your eloquence, like one who has found many spoils.
019	PSA	119	163	I have held hatred for iniquity, and I have abhorred it. Yet I have loved your law.
019	PSA	119	164	Seven times a day, I uttered praise to you about the judgments of your justice.
019	PSA	119	165	Those who love your law have great peace, and there is no scandal for them.
019	PSA	119	166	I have waited for your salvation, O Lord. And I have loved your commandments.
019	PSA	119	167	My soul has kept to your testimonies and has loved them exceedingly.
019	PSA	119	168	I have served your commandments and your testimonies. For all my ways are before your sight.
019	PSA	119	169	O Lord, let my supplication draw near in your sight. Grant understanding to me according to your eloquence.
019	PSA	119	170	Let my petition enter before you. Rescue me according to your word.
019	PSA	119	171	A hymn will burst forth from my lips, when you will teach me your justifications.
019	PSA	119	172	My tongue will pronounce your eloquence. For all your commandments are fairness.
019	PSA	119	173	Let it be your hand that saves me. For I have chosen your commandments.
019	PSA	119	174	O Lord, I have longed for your salvation, and your law is my (meditation)
019	PSA	119	175	My soul will live and will praise you, and your judgments will assist me.
019	PSA	119	176	I have gone astray like a sheep that is lost. Seek out your servant, for I have not forgotten your commandments.
019	PSA	120	001	A Canticle in steps. When troubled, I cried out to the Lord, and he heard me.
019	PSA	120	002	O Lord, free my soul from lips of iniquity and from the deceitful tongue.
019	PSA	120	003	What will be given to you, or what will be added to you, for a deceitful tongue?:
019	PSA	120	004	the sharp arrows of the powerful, along with the burning coals of desolation.
019	PSA	120	005	Woe to me, for my sojourning has been prolonged. I have lived with the inhabitants of Kedar.
019	PSA	120	006	My soul has long been a sojourner.
019	PSA	120	007	With those who hated peace, I was peaceful. When I spoke to them, they fought against me without cause.
019	PSA	121	001	A Canticle in steps. I have lifted up my eyes to the mountains; from thence help will come to me.
019	PSA	121	002	My help is from the Lord, who made heaven and earth.
019	PSA	121	003	May he not allow your foot to be moved, and may he not slumber, who guards you.
019	PSA	121	004	Behold, he who guards Israel will neither sleep, nor slumber.
019	PSA	121	005	The Lord is your keeper, the Lord is your protection, above your right hand.
019	PSA	121	006	The sun will not burn you by day, nor the moon by night.
019	PSA	121	007	The Lord guards you from all evil. May the Lord guard your soul.
019	PSA	121	008	May the Lord guard your entrance and your exit, from this time forward and even forever.
019	PSA	122	001	A Canticle in steps. I rejoiced in the things that were said to me: “We shall go into the house of the Lord.”
019	PSA	122	002	Our feet were standing in your courts, O Jerusalem.
019	PSA	122	003	Jerusalem has been built as a city, whose participation is unto itself.
019	PSA	122	004	For to that place, the tribes ascended, the tribes of the Lord: the testimony of Israel, to confess to the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	122	005	For in that place, seats have sat down in judgment, seats above the house of David.
019	PSA	122	006	Petition for the things that are for the peace of Jerusalem, and for abundance for those who love you.
019	PSA	122	007	Let peace be in your virtue, and abundance in your towers.
019	PSA	122	008	For the sake of my brothers and my neighbors, I spoke peace about you.
019	PSA	122	009	For the sake of the house of the Lord our God, I sought good things for you.
019	PSA	123	001	A Canticle in steps. I have lifted up my eyes to you, who dwells in the heavens.
019	PSA	123	002	Behold, as the eyes of the servants are on the hands of their masters, as the eyes of the handmaid are on the hands of her mistress, so our eyes are upon the Lord our God, until he may be merciful to us.
019	PSA	123	003	Have mercy on us, O Lord, have mercy on us. For we have been filled with utter disdain.
019	PSA	123	004	For our soul has been greatly filled. We are the disgrace of those who have abundance and the disdain of the arrogant.
019	PSA	124	001	A Canticle in steps. If the Lord had not been with us, let Israel now say it:
019	PSA	124	002	if the Lord had not been with us, when men rose up against us,
019	PSA	124	003	perhaps they would have swallowed us alive. When their fury was enraged against us,
019	PSA	124	004	perhaps the waters would have engulfed us.
019	PSA	124	005	Our soul has passed through a torrent. Perhaps, our soul had even passed through intolerable water.
019	PSA	124	006	Blessed is the Lord, who has not given us into the harm of their teeth.
019	PSA	124	007	Our soul has been snatched away like a sparrow from the snare of the hunters. The snare has been broken, and we have been freed.
019	PSA	124	008	Our help is in the name of the Lord, who made heaven and earth.
019	PSA	125	001	A Canticle in steps. Those who trust in the Lord will be like the mountain of Zion. He will not be disturbed for eternity, who dwells
019	PSA	125	002	in Jerusalem. Mountains surround it. And the Lord surrounds his people, from this time forward and even forever.
019	PSA	125	003	For the Lord will not allow the rod of sinners to remain over the lot of the just, so that the just may not extend their hands toward iniquity.
019	PSA	125	004	Do good, O Lord, to the good and to the upright of heart.
019	PSA	125	005	But those who turn away into obligation, the Lord will lead away with the workers of iniquity. Peace be upon Israel.
019	PSA	126	001	A Canticle in steps. When the Lord turned back the captivity of Zion, we became like those who are consoled.
019	PSA	126	002	Then our mouth was filled with gladness and our tongue with exultation. Then they will say among the nations: “The Lord has done great things for them.”
019	PSA	126	003	The Lord has done great things for us. We have become joyful.
019	PSA	126	004	Convert our captivity, O Lord, like a torrent in the south.
019	PSA	126	005	Those who sow in tears shall reap in exultation.
019	PSA	126	006	When departing, they went forth and wept, sowing their seeds. But when returning, they will arrive with exultation, carrying their sheaves.
019	PSA	127	001	A Canticle in steps: of Solomon. Unless the Lord has built the house, those who build it have labored in vain. Unless the Lord has guarded the city, he who guards it watches in vain.
019	PSA	127	002	It is in vain that you rise before daylight, that you rise up after you have sat down, you who chew the bread of sorrow. Whereas, to his beloved, he will give sleep.
019	PSA	127	003	Behold, the inheritance of the Lord is sons, the reward is the fruit of the womb.
019	PSA	127	004	Like arrows in the hand of the powerful, so are the sons of those who have been cast out.
019	PSA	127	005	Blessed is the man who has filled his desire from these things. He will not be confounded when he speaks to his enemies at the gate.
019	PSA	128	001	A Canticle in steps. Blessed are all those who fear the Lord, who walk in his ways.
019	PSA	128	002	For you will eat by the labors of your hands. Blessed are you, and it will be well with you.
019	PSA	128	003	Your wife is like an abundant vine on the sides of your house. Your sons are like young olive trees surrounding your table.
019	PSA	128	004	Behold, so will the man be blessed who fears the Lord.
019	PSA	128	005	May the Lord bless you from Zion, and may you see the good things of Jerusalem, all the days of your life.
019	PSA	128	006	And may you see the sons of your sons. Peace be upon Israel.
019	PSA	129	001	A Canticle in steps. They have often fought against me from my youth, let Israel now say:
019	PSA	129	002	they have often fought against me from my youth, yet they could not prevail over me.
019	PSA	129	003	The sinners have made fabrications behind my back. They have prolonged their iniquity.
019	PSA	129	004	The just Lord will cut the necks of sinners.
019	PSA	129	005	Let all those who hate Zion be confounded and turned backwards.
019	PSA	129	006	Let them be like grass on the rooftops, which withers before it can be pulled up:
019	PSA	129	007	with it, he who reaps does not fill his hand and he who gathers sheaves does not fill his bosom.
019	PSA	129	008	And those who were passing by have not said to them: “The blessing of the Lord be upon you. We have blessed you in the name of the Lord.”
019	PSA	130	001	A Canticle in steps. From the depths, I have cried out to you, O Lord.
019	PSA	130	002	O Lord, hear my voice. Let your ears be attentive to the voice of my supplication.
019	PSA	130	003	If you, O Lord, were to heed iniquities, who, O Lord, could persevere?
019	PSA	130	004	For with you, there is forgiveness, and because of your law, I persevered with you, Lord. My soul has persevered in his word.
019	PSA	130	005	My soul has hoped in the Lord.
019	PSA	130	006	From the morning watch, even until night, let Israel hope in the Lord.
019	PSA	130	007	For with the Lord there is mercy, and with him there is bountiful redemption.
019	PSA	130	008	And he will redeem Israel from all his iniquities.
019	PSA	131	001	A Canticle in steps: of David. O Lord, my heart has not been exalted, and my eyes have not been raised up. Neither have I walked in greatness, nor in wonders beyond me.
019	PSA	131	002	When I was not humble in thought, then I lifted up my soul. Like one who has been weaned from his mother, so was I recompensed in my soul.
019	PSA	131	003	Let Israel hope in the Lord, from this time forward and even forever.
019	PSA	132	001	A Canticle in steps. O Lord, remember David and all his meekness,
019	PSA	132	002	how he swore to the Lord, how he made a vow to the God of Jacob:
019	PSA	132	003	I shall not enter into the tabernacle of my house, nor climb into the bed where I lie down;
019	PSA	132	004	I shall not give sleep to my eyes, nor slumber to my eyelids
019	PSA	132	005	and rest to my temples, until I find a place for the Lord, a tabernacle for the God of Jacob.
019	PSA	132	006	Behold, we heard of it in Ephrathah. We discovered it in the fields of the forest.
019	PSA	132	007	We will enter into his tabernacle. We will adore in the place where his feet stood.
019	PSA	132	008	Rise up, O Lord, into your resting place. You and the ark of your sanctification.
019	PSA	132	009	Let your priests be clothed with justice, and let your saints exult.
019	PSA	132	010	For the sake of your servant David, do not turn away the face of your Christ.
019	PSA	132	011	The Lord has sworn the truth to David, and he will not disappoint: I will set upon your throne from the fruit of your lineage.
019	PSA	132	012	If your sons will keep my covenant and these, my testimonies, which I will teach to them, then their sons will sit upon your throne even forever.
019	PSA	132	013	For the Lord has chosen Zion. He has chosen it as his dwelling place.
019	PSA	132	014	This is my resting place, forever and ever. Here I will dwell, for I have chosen it.
019	PSA	132	015	When blessing, I will bless her widow. I will satisfy her poor with bread.
019	PSA	132	016	I will clothe her priests with salvation, and her saints will rejoice with great joy.
019	PSA	132	017	There, I will produce a horn to David. There, I have prepared a lamp for my Christ.
019	PSA	132	018	I will clothe his enemies with confusion. But my sanctification will flourish over him.
019	PSA	133	001	A Canticle in steps: of David. Behold, how good and how pleasing it is for brothers to dwell in unity.
019	PSA	133	002	It is like the ointment on the head that descended to the beard, the beard of Aaron, which descended to the hem of his garment.
019	PSA	133	003	It is like the dew of Hermon, which descended from mount Zion. For in that place, the Lord has commanded a blessing, and life, even unto eternity.
019	PSA	134	001	A Canticle in steps. Behold, bless the Lord now, all you servants of the Lord, who stand in the house of the Lord, in the courts of the house of our God.
019	PSA	134	002	In the nights, lift up your hands in sanctity, and bless the Lord.
019	PSA	134	003	May the Lord, who made heaven and earth, bless you from Zion.
019	PSA	135	001	Alleluia. Praise the name of the Lord. You servants, praise the Lord.
019	PSA	135	002	You who stand in the house of the Lord, in the courts of the house of our God:
019	PSA	135	003	praise the Lord, for the Lord is good. Sing psalms to his name, for it is sweet.
019	PSA	135	004	For the Lord has chosen Jacob for himself, Israel for his own possession.
019	PSA	135	005	For I have known that the Lord is great, and our God is before all gods.
019	PSA	135	006	All things whatsoever that he willed, the Lord did: in heaven, on earth, in the sea, and in all the deep places.
019	PSA	135	007	He leads clouds from the ends of the earth. He has created lightnings in the rain. He has produced winds from his storehouses.
019	PSA	135	008	He struck the first-born of Egypt, from man even to cattle.
019	PSA	135	009	He sent signs and wonders into your midst, O Egypt: upon Pharaoh and upon all his servants.
019	PSA	135	010	He has struck many nations, and he has slaughtered strong kings:
019	PSA	135	011	Sihon, king of the Amorites, and Og, king of Bashan, and all the kingdoms of Canaan.
019	PSA	135	012	And he gave their land as an inheritance, as an inheritance for his people Israel.
019	PSA	135	013	Your name, O Lord, is in eternity. Your memorial, O Lord, is from generation to generation.
019	PSA	135	014	For the Lord will judge his people, and he will be petitioned by his servants.
019	PSA	135	015	The idols of the Gentiles are silver and gold, the works of the hands of men.
019	PSA	135	016	They have a mouth, and do not speak. They have eyes, and do not see.
019	PSA	135	017	They have ears, and do not hear. For neither is there any breath in their mouths.
019	PSA	135	018	Let those who make them become like them, along with all who trust in them.
019	PSA	135	019	Bless the Lord, O house of Israel. Bless the Lord, O house of Aaron.
019	PSA	135	020	Bless the Lord, O house of Levi. You who fear the Lord, bless the Lord.
019	PSA	135	021	The Lord is blessed from Zion, by those who dwell in Jerusalem.
019	PSA	136	001	Alleluia. Confess to the Lord, for he is good: for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	002	Confess to the God of gods, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	003	Confess to the Lord of lords, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	004	He alone performs great miracles, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	005	He made the heavens with understanding, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	006	He established the earth above the waters, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	007	He made the great lights, for his mercy is eternal:
019	PSA	136	008	the sun to rule the day, for his mercy is eternal:
019	PSA	136	009	the moon and the stars to rule the night, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	010	He struck Egypt along with their first-born, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	011	He led Israel away from their midst, for his mercy is eternal:
019	PSA	136	012	with a powerful hand and an outstretched arm, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	013	He divided the Red Sea into separate parts, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	014	And he led out Israel through the middle of it, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	015	And he shook off Pharaoh and his army in the Red Sea, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	016	He led his people through the desert, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	017	He has struck great kings, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	018	And he has slaughtered strong kings, for his mercy is eternal:
019	PSA	136	019	Sihon, king of the Amorites, for his mercy is eternal:
019	PSA	136	020	and Og, king of Bashan, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	021	And he granted their land as an inheritance, for his mercy is eternal:
019	PSA	136	022	as an inheritance for his servant Israel, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	023	For he was mindful of us in our humiliation, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	024	And he redeemed us from our enemies, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	025	He gives food to all flesh, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	136	026	Confess to the God of heaven, for his mercy is eternal. Confess to the Lord of lords, for his mercy is eternal.
019	PSA	137	001	A Psalm of David: to Jeremiah. Above the rivers of Babylon, there we sat and wept, while we remembered Zion.
019	PSA	137	002	By the willow trees, in their midst, we hung up our instruments.
019	PSA	137	003	For, in that place, those who led us into captivity questioned us about the words of the songs. And those who carried us away said: “Sing us a hymn from the songs of Zion.”
019	PSA	137	004	How can we sing a song of the Lord in a foreign land?
019	PSA	137	005	If I ever forget you, Jerusalem, let my right hand be forgotten.
019	PSA	137	006	May my tongue adhere to my jaws, if I do not remember you, if I do not set Jerusalem first, as the beginning of my joy.
019	PSA	137	007	O Lord, call to mind the sons of Edom, in the day of Jerusalem, who say: “Despoil it, despoil it, even to its foundation.”
019	PSA	137	008	O daughter of Babylon, have pity. Blessed is he who will repay you with your payment, which you have paid to us.
019	PSA	137	009	Blessed is he who will take hold of your little ones and dash them against the rock.
019	PSA	138	001	Of David himself. O Lord, I will confess to you with my whole heart, for you have heard the words of my mouth. I will sing psalms to you in the sight of the Angels.
019	PSA	138	002	I will adore before your holy temple, and I will confess your name: it is above your mercy and your truth. For you have magnified your holy name above all.
019	PSA	138	003	On whatever day that I will call upon you: hear me. You will multiply virtue in my soul.
019	PSA	138	004	May all the kings of the earth confess to you, O Lord. For they have heard all the words of your mouth.
019	PSA	138	005	And let them sing in accordance with the ways of the Lord. For great is the glory of the Lord.
019	PSA	138	006	For the Lord is exalted, and he looks with favor on the humble. But the lofty he knows from a distance.
019	PSA	138	007	If I wander into the midst of tribulation, you will revive me. For you extended your hand against the wrath of my enemies. And your right hand has accomplished my salvation.
019	PSA	138	008	The Lord will provide retribution on my behalf. O Lord, your mercy is forever. Do not disdain the works of your hands.
019	PSA	139	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. O Lord, you have examined me, and you have known me.
019	PSA	139	002	You have known my sitting down and my rising up again.
019	PSA	139	003	You have understood my thoughts from afar. My path and my fate, you have investigated.
019	PSA	139	004	And you have foreseen all my ways. For there is no word in my tongue.
019	PSA	139	005	Behold, O Lord, you have known all things: the newest and the very old. You have formed me, and you have placed your hand over me.
019	PSA	139	006	Your knowledge has become a wonder to me. It has been reinforced, and I am not able to prevail against it.
019	PSA	139	007	Where will I go from your Spirit? And where will I flee from your face?
019	PSA	139	008	If I ascend into heaven, you are there. If I descend into Hell, you are near.
019	PSA	139	009	If I assume my feathers in early morning, and dwell in the utmost parts of the sea,
019	PSA	139	010	even there, your hand will lead me forth, and your right hand will hold me.
019	PSA	139	011	And I said: Perhaps darkness will overwhelm me, and the night will be my illumination, to my delight.
019	PSA	139	012	But darkness will not be impenetrable to you, and night will illuminate like the day: for just as its darkness is, so also is its light.
019	PSA	139	013	For you have possessed my temperament. You have supported me from the womb of my mother.
019	PSA	139	014	I will confess to you, for you have been magnified terribly. Your works are miraculous, as my soul knows exceedingly well.
019	PSA	139	015	My bone, which you have made in secret, has not been hidden from you, and my substance is in accord with the lower parts of the earth.
019	PSA	139	016	Your eyes saw my imperfection, and all this shall be written in your book. Days will be formed, and no one shall be in them.
019	PSA	139	017	But to me, O God, your friends have been greatly honored. Their first ruler has been exceedingly strengthened.
019	PSA	139	018	I will number them, and they will be more numerous than the sand. I rose up, and I am still with you.
019	PSA	139	019	O God, if only you would cut down sinners. You men of blood: depart from me.
019	PSA	139	020	For you say in thought: They will accept your cities in vain.
019	PSA	139	021	Have I not hated those who hated you, Lord, and wasted away because of your enemies?
019	PSA	139	022	I have hated them with a perfect hatred, and they have become enemies to me.
019	PSA	139	023	Examine me, O God, and know my heart. Question me, and know my paths.
019	PSA	139	024	And see if there might be in me the way of iniquity, and lead me in the way of eternity.
019	PSA	140	001	Unto the end. A Psalm of David. Rescue me, O Lord, from the evil man. Rescue me from the iniquitous leader.
019	PSA	140	002	Those who have devised iniquities in their hearts: all day long they constructed conflicts.
019	PSA	140	003	They have sharpened their tongues like a serpent. The venom of asps is under their lips.
019	PSA	140	004	Preserve me, O Lord, from the hand of the sinner, and rescue me from men of iniquity. They have decided to supplant my steps.
019	PSA	140	005	The arrogant have hidden a snare for me. And they have stretched out cords for a snare. They have placed a stumbling block for me near the road.
019	PSA	140	006	I said to the Lord: You are my God. O Lord, heed the voice of my supplication.
019	PSA	140	007	Lord, O Lord, the strength of my salvation: you have overshadowed my head in the day of war.
019	PSA	140	008	O Lord, do not hand me over to the sinner by my desire. They have plotted against me. Do not abandon me, lest they should triumph.
019	PSA	140	009	The head of those who encompass me, the labor of their lips, will overwhelm them.
019	PSA	140	010	Burning coals will fall upon them. You will cast them down into the fire, into miseries that they will not be able to withstand.
019	PSA	140	011	A talkative man will not be guided aright upon the earth. Evils will drag the unjust man unto utter ruin.
019	PSA	140	012	I know that the Lord will accomplish justice for the needy and vindication for the poor.
019	PSA	140	013	So then, truly, the just will confess your name, and the upright will dwell with your countenance.
019	PSA	141	001	A Psalm of David. O Lord, I have cried out to you, hear me. Attend to my voice, when I cry out to you.
019	PSA	141	002	Let my prayer be guided like incense in your sight: the lifting up of my hands, like the evening sacrifice.
019	PSA	141	003	O Lord, station a guard over my mouth and a door enclosing my lips.
019	PSA	141	004	Do not turn aside my heart to words of malice, to making excuses for sins, with men who work iniquity; and I will not communicate, even with the best of them.
019	PSA	141	005	The just one will correct me with mercy, and he will rebuke me. But do not allow the oil of the sinner to fatten my head. For my prayer will still be toward their good will.
019	PSA	141	006	Their judges have been engulfed, joined to the rocks. They will hear my words, which have prevailed,
019	PSA	141	007	as when the lava of the earth has erupted above ground. Our bones have been scattered beside Hell.
019	PSA	141	008	For Lord, O Lord, my eyes look to you. In you, I have hoped. Do not take away my soul.
019	PSA	141	009	Protect me from the snare that they have set up for me and from the scandals of those who work iniquity.
019	PSA	141	010	The sinners will fall into his net. I am alone, until I pass over.
019	PSA	142	001	The understanding of David. A prayer, when he was in the cave. With my voice, I cried out to the Lord. With my voice, I made supplication to the Lord.
019	PSA	142	002	In his sight, I pour out my prayer, and before him, I declare my tribulation.
019	PSA	142	003	Though my spirit may become faint within me, even then, you have known my paths. Along this way, which I have been walking, they have hidden a snare for me.
019	PSA	142	004	I considered toward the right, and I looked, but there was no one who would know me. Flight has perished before me, and there is no one who has concern for my soul.
019	PSA	142	005	I cried out to you, O Lord. I said: You are my hope, my portion in the land of the living.
019	PSA	142	006	Attend to my supplication. For I have been humbled exceedingly. Free me from my persecutors, for they have been fortified against me.
019	PSA	142	007	Lead my soul out of confinement in order to confess your name. The just are waiting for me, until you repay me.
019	PSA	143	001	A Psalm of David, when his son Absalom was pursuing him. O Lord, hear my prayer. Incline your ear to my supplication in your truth. Heed me according to your justice.
019	PSA	143	002	And do not enter into judgment with your servant. For all the living will not be justified in your sight.
019	PSA	143	003	For the enemy has pursued my soul. He has lowered my life to the earth. He has stationed me in darkness, like the dead of ages past.
019	PSA	143	004	And my spirit has been in anguish over me. My heart within me has been disturbed.
019	PSA	143	005	I have called to mind the days of antiquity. I have been meditating on all your works. I have meditated on the workings of your hands.
019	PSA	143	006	I have extended my hands to you. My soul is like a land without water before you.
019	PSA	143	007	O Lord, heed me quickly. My spirit has grown faint. Do not turn your face away from me, lest I become like those who descend into the pit.
019	PSA	143	008	Make me hear your mercy in the morning. For I have hoped in you. Make known to me the way that I should walk. For I have lifted up my soul to you.
019	PSA	143	009	O Lord, rescue me from my enemies. I have fled to you.
019	PSA	143	010	Teach me to do your will. For you are my God. Your good Spirit will lead me into the righteous land.
019	PSA	143	011	For the sake of your name, O Lord, you will revive me in your fairness. You will lead my soul out of tribulation.
019	PSA	143	012	And you will scatter my enemies in your mercy. And you will destroy all those who afflict my soul. For I am your servant.
019	PSA	144	001	A Psalm of David versus Goliath. Blessed is the Lord, my God, who trains my hands for the battle and my fingers for the war.
019	PSA	144	002	My mercy and my refuge, my supporter and my deliverer, my protector and him in whom I have hoped: he subdues my people under me.
019	PSA	144	003	O Lord, what is man that you have become known to him? Or the son of man that you consider him?
019	PSA	144	004	Man has been made similar to vanity. His days pass by like a shadow.
019	PSA	144	005	O Lord, incline your heavens and descend. Touch the mountains, and they will smoke.
019	PSA	144	006	Send a flash of lightning, and you will scatter them. Shoot your arrows, and you will set them in disarray.
019	PSA	144	007	Send forth your hand from on high: rescue me, and free me from many waters, from the hand of the sons of foreigners.
019	PSA	144	008	Their mouth has been speaking vain things, and their right hand is the right hand of iniquity.
019	PSA	144	009	To you, O God, I will sing a new song. On the psaltery, with an instrument of ten strings, I will sing psalms to you.
019	PSA	144	010	He gives salvation to kings. He has redeemed your servant David from the malignant sword.
019	PSA	144	011	Rescue me, and deliver me from the hand of the sons of foreigners. Their mouth has been speaking vain things, and their right hand is the right hand of iniquity.
019	PSA	144	012	Their sons are like new plantings in their youth. Their daughters are dressed up: adorned all around like the idols of a temple.
019	PSA	144	013	Their cupboards are full: overflowing from one thing into another. Their sheep bear young, brought forth in abundance.
019	PSA	144	014	Their cattle are fat. There is no ruined wall or passage, nor anyone crying out in their streets.
019	PSA	144	015	They have called the people that has these things: blessed. But blessed is the people whose God is the Lord.
019	PSA	145	001	The Praise of David himself. I will extol you, O God, my king. And I will bless your name, in this time and forever and ever.
019	PSA	145	002	Throughout every single day, I will bless you. And I will praise your name, in this time and forever and ever.
019	PSA	145	003	The Lord is great and exceedingly praiseworthy. And there is no end to his greatness.
019	PSA	145	004	Generation after generation will praise your works, and they will declare your power.
019	PSA	145	005	They will tell of the magnificent glory of your sanctity. And they will discourse of your wonders.
019	PSA	145	006	And they will talk about the virtue of your terrible acts. And they will describe your greatness.
019	PSA	145	007	They will shout about the memory of your abundant sweetness. And they will exult in your justice.
019	PSA	145	008	The Lord is compassionate and merciful, patient and full of mercy.
019	PSA	145	009	The Lord is sweet to all things, and his compassion is upon all his works.
019	PSA	145	010	O Lord, may all your works confess to you, and let your holy ones bless you.
019	PSA	145	011	They will speak of the glory of your kingdom, and they will declare your power,
019	PSA	145	012	so as to make known to the sons of men your power and the glory of your magnificent kingdom.
019	PSA	145	013	Your kingdom is a kingdom for all ages, and your dominion is with all, from generation to generation. The Lord is faithful in all his words and holy in all his works.
019	PSA	145	014	The Lord lifts up all who have fallen down, and he sets upright all who have been thrown down.
019	PSA	145	015	O Lord, all eyes hope in you, and you provide their food in due time.
019	PSA	145	016	You open your hand, and you fill every kind of animal with a blessing.
019	PSA	145	017	The Lord is just in all his ways and holy in all his works.
019	PSA	145	018	The Lord is near to all who call upon him, to all who call upon him in truth.
019	PSA	145	019	He will do the will of those who fear him, and he will heed their supplication and accomplish their salvation.
019	PSA	145	020	The Lord watches over all who love him. And he will destroy all sinners.
019	PSA	145	021	My mouth will speak the praise of the Lord, and may all flesh bless his holy name, in this time and forever and ever.
019	PSA	146	001	Alleluia. Of Haggai and Zachariah.
019	PSA	146	002	Praise the Lord, O my soul. I will praise the Lord with my life. I will sing psalms to my God as long as I shall be. Do not trust in the leaders,
019	PSA	146	003	in the sons of men, in whom there is no salvation.
019	PSA	146	004	His spirit will depart, and he will return to his earth. In that day, all their thoughts will perish.
019	PSA	146	005	Blessed is he whose help is the God of Jacob: his hope is in the Lord God himself,
019	PSA	146	006	who made heaven and earth, the sea, and all the things that are in them.
019	PSA	146	007	He preserves the truth forever. He executes judgment for those who suffer injury. He provides food for the hungry. The Lord releases those who are bound.
019	PSA	146	008	The Lord enlightens the blind. The Lord sets upright those who have been thrown down. The Lord loves the just.
019	PSA	146	009	The Lord watches over new arrivals. He will support the orphan and the widow. And he will destroy the ways of sinners.
019	PSA	146	010	The Lord shall reign forever: your God, O Zion, from generation to generation.
019	PSA	147	001	Alleluia. Praise the Lord, because the psalm is good. Delightful and beautiful praise shall be for our God.
019	PSA	147	002	The Lord builds up Jerusalem. He will gather together the dispersed of Israel.
019	PSA	147	003	He heals the contrite of heart, and he binds up their sorrows.
019	PSA	147	004	He numbers the multitude of the stars, and he calls them all by their names.
019	PSA	147	005	Great is our Lord, and great is his virtue. And of his wisdom, there is no number.
019	PSA	147	006	The Lord lifts up the meek, but he brings down the sinner, even to the ground.
019	PSA	147	007	Sing before the Lord with confession. Play psalms to our God on a stringed instrument.
019	PSA	147	008	He covers heaven with clouds, and he prepares rain for the earth. He produces grass on the mountains and herbs for the service of men.
019	PSA	147	009	He gives their food to beasts of burden and to young ravens that call upon him.
019	PSA	147	010	He will not have good will for the strength of the horse, nor will he be well pleased with the legs of a man.
019	PSA	147	011	The Lord is well pleased with those who fear him and with those who hope in his mercy.
019	PSA	147	012	Alleluia. Praise the Lord, O Jerusalem. Praise your God, O Zion.
019	PSA	147	013	For he has reinforced the bars of your gates. He has blessed your sons within you.
019	PSA	147	014	He has stationed peace at your borders, and he has satisfied you with the fat of the grain.
019	PSA	147	015	He sends forth his eloquence to the earth. His word runs swiftly.
019	PSA	147	016	He provides snow like wool. He strews clouds like ashes.
019	PSA	147	017	He sends his ice crystals like morsels. Who can stand firm before the face of his cold?
019	PSA	147	018	He will send forth his word, and it will melt them. His Spirit will breathe out, and the waters will flow.
019	PSA	147	019	He announces his word to Jacob, his justices and his judgments to Israel.
019	PSA	147	020	He has not done so much for every nation, and he has not made his judgments manifest to them. Alleluia.
019	PSA	148	001	Alleluia. Praise the Lord from the heavens. Praise him on the heights.
019	PSA	148	002	Praise him, all his Angels. Praise him, all his hosts.
019	PSA	148	003	Praise him, sun and moon. Praise him, all stars and light.
019	PSA	148	004	Praise him, heavens of the heavens. And let all the waters that are above the heavens
019	PSA	148	005	praise the name of the Lord. For he spoke, and they became. He commanded, and they were created.
019	PSA	148	006	He has stationed them in eternity, and for age after age. He has established a precept, and it will not pass away.
019	PSA	148	007	Praise the Lord from the earth: you dragons and all deep places,
019	PSA	148	008	fire, hail, snow, ice, windstorms, which do his word,
019	PSA	148	009	mountains and all hills, fruitful trees and all cedars,
019	PSA	148	010	wild beasts and all cattle, serpents and feathered flying things,
019	PSA	148	011	kings of the earth and all peoples, leaders and all judges of the earth,
019	PSA	148	012	young men and virgins. Let the older men with the younger men, praise the name of the Lord.
019	PSA	148	013	For his name alone is exalted.
019	PSA	148	014	Confession of him is beyond heaven and earth, and he has exalted the horn of his people. A hymn to all his holy ones, to the sons of Israel, to a people close to him. Alleluia.
019	PSA	149	001	Alleluia. Sing to the Lord a new song. His praise is in the Church of the saints.
019	PSA	149	002	Let Israel rejoice in him who made them, and let the sons of Zion exult in their king.
019	PSA	149	003	Let them praise his name in chorus. Let them sing psalms to him with the timbrel and the psaltery.
019	PSA	149	004	For the Lord is well pleased with his people, and he will exalt the meek unto salvation.
019	PSA	149	005	The saints will exult in glory. They will rejoice upon their couches.
019	PSA	149	006	The exultations of God will be in their throat, and two-edged swords will be in their hands:
019	PSA	149	007	to obtain vindication among the nations, chastisements among the peoples,
019	PSA	149	008	to bind their kings with shackles and their nobles with manacles of iron,
019	PSA	149	009	to obtain judgment over them, as it has been written. This is glory for all his saints. Alleluia.
019	PSA	150	001	Alleluia. Praise the Lord in his holy places. Praise him in the firmament of his power.
019	PSA	150	002	Praise him for his virtues. Praise him according to the multitude of his greatness.
019	PSA	150	003	Praise him with the sound of the trumpet. Praise him with psaltery and stringed instrument.
019	PSA	150	004	Praise him with timbrel and choir. Praise him with strings and organ.
019	PSA	150	005	Praise him with sweet-sounding cymbals. Praise him with cymbals of jubilation.
019	PSA	150	006	Let every spirit praise the Lord. Alleluia.
#
# BOOK	020	PRO	Proverbs	Proverbs
020	PRO	001	001	The parables of Solomon, son of David, king of Israel,
020	PRO	001	002	in order to know wisdom and discipline,
020	PRO	001	003	to understand words of prudence, and to accept the instruction of doctrine, justice and judgment, and equity,
020	PRO	001	004	so as to give discernment to little ones, knowledge and understanding to adolescents.
020	PRO	001	005	By listening, the wise shall become wiser and the intelligent shall possess governments.
020	PRO	001	006	He shall turn his soul to a parable and to its interpretation, to the words of the wise and their enigmas.
020	PRO	001	007	The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom. The foolish despise wisdom as well as doctrine.
020	PRO	001	008	Listen, my son, to the discipline of your father, and forsake not the law of your mother,
020	PRO	001	009	so that grace may be added to your head and a collar to your neck.
020	PRO	001	010	My son, if sinners should entice you, do not consent to them.
020	PRO	001	011	If they should say: “Come with us. We will lie in wait for blood. We will lay traps against the innocent, without cause.
020	PRO	001	012	Let us swallow him alive, like Hell, and whole, like one descending into the pit.
020	PRO	001	013	We will discover every precious substance. We will fill our houses with spoils.
020	PRO	001	014	Cast your lot with us. One purse will be for us all.”
020	PRO	001	015	My son, do not walk with them. Preclude your feet from their paths.
020	PRO	001	016	For their feet rush to evil, and they hurry to shed blood.
020	PRO	001	017	But a net is thrown in vain before the eyes of those who have wings.
020	PRO	001	018	Likewise, they lie in ambush against their own blood, and they undertake deceits against their own souls.
020	PRO	001	019	Thus, the ways of all those who are greedy seize the souls of those who possess.
020	PRO	001	020	Wisdom forewarns far and wide; she bestows her voice in the streets.
020	PRO	001	021	She cries out at the head of crowds; at the entrance of the gates of the city, she offers her words, saying:
020	PRO	001	022	“Little ones, how long will you choose to be childish, and how long will the foolish desire what is harmful to themselves, and how long will the imprudent hate knowledge?
020	PRO	001	023	Be converted by my correction. Lo, I will offer my spirit to you, and I will reveal my words to you.
020	PRO	001	024	For I called, and you refused. I extended my hand, and there was no one who watched.
020	PRO	001	025	You have despised all my counsels, and you have neglected my rebukes.
020	PRO	001	026	Similarly, I will ridicule you at your demise, and I will mock you, when that which you feared shall overcome you.
020	PRO	001	027	When sudden calamity rushes upon you, and your demise advances like a tempest, when tribulation and anguish overcome you,
020	PRO	001	028	then they will call to me, and I will not heed, they will arise in the morning, and not find me.
020	PRO	001	029	For they held hatred for discipline, and they would not accept the fear of the Lord;
020	PRO	001	030	they would not consent to my counsel, but they detracted from all of my corrections.
020	PRO	001	031	Therefore, they shall eat the fruit of their way, and they shall have their fill of their own counsels.
020	PRO	001	032	The loathing of the little ones shall destroy them, and the prosperity of the foolish shall perish them.
020	PRO	001	033	But whoever will listen to me shall rest without terror, and shall have full enjoyment of abundance, without fear of evils.”
020	PRO	002	001	My son, if you would accept my words, and conceal my commandments within you,
020	PRO	002	002	so that your ears may listen to wisdom, then bend your heart in order to know prudence.
020	PRO	002	003	For if you would call upon wisdom and bend your heart to prudence,
020	PRO	002	004	if you will seek her like money, and dig for her as if for treasure,
020	PRO	002	005	then you will understand the fear of the Lord, and you will discover the knowledge of God.
020	PRO	002	006	For the Lord bestows wisdom, and out of his mouth, prudence and knowledge.
020	PRO	002	007	He will preserve the salvation of the righteous, and he will protect those who walk in simplicity:
020	PRO	002	008	serving the paths of justice, and guarding the ways of sanctity.
020	PRO	002	009	Then you shall understand justice and judgment, and equity, and every good path.
020	PRO	002	010	If wisdom is to enter into your heart, and if knowledge is to become pleasing to your soul,
020	PRO	002	011	then counsel must guard you, and prudence must serve you,
020	PRO	002	012	so that you may be rescued from the evil way, and from the man who speaks perversities,
020	PRO	002	013	from those who leave the straight path to walk in dark ways,
020	PRO	002	014	who rejoice when they have done evil, and who exult in the most wicked things.
020	PRO	002	015	Their ways are perverse, and their steps are infamous.
020	PRO	002	016	So may you be rescued from the foreign woman, and from the outsider, who softens her speech,
020	PRO	002	017	and who leaves behind the Guide of her youth,
020	PRO	002	018	and who has forgotten the covenant of her God. For her household inclines toward death, and her paths toward Hell.
020	PRO	002	019	All those who enter to her will not return again, nor will they take hold of the paths of life.
020	PRO	002	020	So may you walk in the good way, and keep to the difficult paths of the just.
020	PRO	002	021	For those who are upright shall live upon the earth, and the simple shall continue upon it.
020	PRO	002	022	Yet truly, the impious shall perish from the earth, and those who act unjustly shall be taken away from it.
020	PRO	003	001	My son, do not forget my law, but let your heart guard my precepts.
020	PRO	003	002	For they shall set before you length of days, and years of life, and peace.
020	PRO	003	003	Let not mercy and truth abandon you: encircle them around your throat, and inscribe them on the tablets of your heart.
020	PRO	003	004	And so shall you discover grace and good discipline, in the sight of God and men.
020	PRO	003	005	Have confidence in the Lord with all your heart, and do not depend upon your own prudence.
020	PRO	003	006	In all your ways, consider him, and he himself will direct your steps.
020	PRO	003	007	Do not seem wise to yourself. Fear God, and withdraw from evil.
020	PRO	003	008	Certainly, it shall be health to your navel, and refreshment to your bones.
020	PRO	003	009	Honor the Lord with your substance, and give to him from the first of all your fruits,
020	PRO	003	010	and then your storehouses will be filled with abundance, and your presses shall overflow with wine.
020	PRO	003	011	My son, do not discard the discipline of the Lord, and do not fall away when you are corrected by him.
020	PRO	003	012	For whomever the Lord loves, he corrects, and just as a father does with a son, he wins him over.
020	PRO	003	013	Blessed is the man who finds wisdom and who advances to prudence.
020	PRO	003	014	Her acquisition is better than trading in silver, and her fruit is better than the first and purest gold.
020	PRO	003	015	She is more precious than all riches, and all that can be desired cannot prevail in comparison to her.
020	PRO	003	016	Length of days is at her right hand, and at her left hand is wealth and glory.
020	PRO	003	017	Her ways are beautiful ways, and all her paths are peaceful.
020	PRO	003	018	She is a tree of life to those who overtake her, and he who shall take hold of her is blessed.
020	PRO	003	019	The Lord founded the earth on wisdom. He secured the heavens with prudence.
020	PRO	003	020	By his wisdom, the abyss erupted and the clouds increased with dew.
020	PRO	003	021	My son, let not these things move away from your eyes. Preserve law as well as counsel.
020	PRO	003	022	And so shall there be life in your soul and grace in your voice.
020	PRO	003	023	Then you shall walk confidently in your way, and your feet will not stumble.
020	PRO	003	024	When you slumber, you shall not fear. When you rest, your sleep also will be sweet.
020	PRO	003	025	Do not fear unexpected terror, nor the power of the impious falling upon you.
020	PRO	003	026	For the Lord will be at your side, and he will guard your feet, so that you may not be seized.
020	PRO	003	027	Do not prevent him who is able from doing good. When you are able, do good yourself too.
020	PRO	003	028	Do not say to your friend: “Go away, and then return. Tomorrow I will give to you.” When you are able to do so, give in the present.
020	PRO	003	029	Do not undertake evil against your friend, even though he has trust in you.
020	PRO	003	030	Do not contend against a man without cause, even though he has done no evil to you.
020	PRO	003	031	Do not rival an unjust man, and do not imitate his ways.
020	PRO	003	032	For everyone who ridicules is an abomination to the Lord, and his communication is for the simple.
020	PRO	003	033	Destitution in the house of the impious is from the Lord. But the habitations of the just shall be blessed.
020	PRO	003	034	He will ridicule those who ridicule, but he will bestow grace upon the mild.
020	PRO	003	035	The wise will possess glory. The exaltation of the foolish is disgraceful.
020	PRO	004	001	Listen, sons, to the discipline of a father, and pay attention, so that you may know prudence.
020	PRO	004	002	I will bestow upon you a good gift. Do not relinquish my law.
020	PRO	004	003	For I, too, was the son of my father, tender and an only son in the sight of my mother.
020	PRO	004	004	And he taught me, and he also said: “Let your heart accept my words. Keep my precepts, and you shall live.
020	PRO	004	005	Obtain wisdom, obtain prudence. May you neither forget, nor turn away from, the words of my mouth.
020	PRO	004	006	Do not send her away, and she will guard you. Love her, and she will preserve you.
020	PRO	004	007	The beginning of wisdom is to obtain wisdom, and, with all that you possess, to acquire prudence.
020	PRO	004	008	Grasp her, and she will exalt you. You will be glorified by her, when you have embraced her.
020	PRO	004	009	She will bestow upon your head an increase in graces, and she will protect you with a noble crown.
020	PRO	004	010	Listen, my son, and accept my words, so that years of life may be multiplied for you.
020	PRO	004	011	I will demonstrate to you the way of wisdom. I will lead you along the paths of equity.
020	PRO	004	012	When you have entered by these, your steps will not be constrained, and when running, you will have no obstacle.
020	PRO	004	013	Take hold of discipline. Do not dismiss it. Guard it, for it is your life.
020	PRO	004	014	Do not delight in the paths of the impious, nor permit the way of evil-doers to please you.
020	PRO	004	015	Take flight from it. Do not pass close to it. Turn away and abandon it.
020	PRO	004	016	For they do not sleep, unless they have done evil. And their sleep is quickly taken away from them, unless they have overthrown.
020	PRO	004	017	They eat the bread of impiety, and they drink the wine of iniquity.
020	PRO	004	018	But the path of the just is like a shining light: it advances and increases, even to the day of completion.
020	PRO	004	019	The way of the impious is darkened. They do not know where they may fall.
020	PRO	004	020	My son, pay attention to my sermons, and incline your ear to my eloquent words.
020	PRO	004	021	Let them not recede from your eyes. Keep them in the midst of your heart.
020	PRO	004	022	For they are life to those who find them and health to all that is flesh.
020	PRO	004	023	Preserve your heart with all watchfulness, for life proceeds from this.
020	PRO	004	024	Remove from yourself a corrupt mouth, and let detracting lips be far from you.
020	PRO	004	025	Let your eyes look straight ahead, and let your eyelids precede your steps.
020	PRO	004	026	Direct the path of your feet, and all your ways shall be secure.
020	PRO	004	027	Turn aside, neither to the right, nor to the left; yet turn your foot away from evil. For the Lord knows the ways that are on the right, and truly, those that are on the left are perverse. But he himself will make your courses straight. Then your journey will advance in peace.
020	PRO	005	001	My son, pay attention to my wisdom, and incline your ear to my prudence,
020	PRO	005	002	so that you may guard your thinking, and so that your lips may preserve discipline. Do not pay attention to the deceit of a woman.
020	PRO	005	003	For the lips of a loose woman are like a dripping honeycomb, and her voice is smoother than oil.
020	PRO	005	004	But in the end, she is as bitter as wormwood, and as sharp as a two-edged sword.
020	PRO	005	005	Her feet descend into death, and her steps reach even to Hell.
020	PRO	005	006	They do not walk along the path of life; her steps are wandering and untraceable.
020	PRO	005	007	Therefore, my son, listen to me now, and do not withdraw from the words of my mouth.
020	PRO	005	008	Make your way at a distance from her, and do not approach the doors of her house.
020	PRO	005	009	Do not give your honor to foreigners, and your years to the cruel.
020	PRO	005	010	Otherwise, outsiders may be filled with your strength, and your labors may be in a foreign house,
020	PRO	005	011	and you may mourn in the end, when you will have consumed your flesh and your body. And so you may say:
020	PRO	005	012	“Why have I detested discipline, and why has my heart not been quieted by correction?
020	PRO	005	013	And why have I not listened to the voice of those who guided me? And why has my ear not inclined to my teachers?
020	PRO	005	014	I have almost been with all evil in the midst of the church and of the assembly.”
020	PRO	005	015	Drink water from your own cistern and from the springs of your own well.
020	PRO	005	016	Let your fountains be diverted far and wide, and divide your waters in the streets.
020	PRO	005	017	Hold them for yourself alone, and do not let strangers be partakers with you.
020	PRO	005	018	Let your spring be blessed, and rejoice with the wife of your youth:
020	PRO	005	019	a beloved doe and most pleasing fawn. Let her breasts inebriate you at all times. Be delighted continually by her love.
020	PRO	005	020	Why are you seduced, my son, by a strange woman, and why are you kept warm by the bosom of another?
020	PRO	005	021	The Lord beholds the ways of man, and he considers all his steps.
020	PRO	005	022	His own iniquities take hold of the impious, and he is bound by the cords of his own sins.
020	PRO	005	023	He shall die, for he has not held to discipline. And by the multitude of his foolishness, he shall be deceived.
020	PRO	006	001	My son, if you have taken a pledge on behalf of your friend, then you have bound your hand to an outsider,
020	PRO	006	002	then you are ensnared by the words of your own mouth, and taken captive by your own words.
020	PRO	006	003	Therefore, my son, do what I say, and free yourself, for you have fallen into the hand of your neighbor. Run, hurry, awaken your friend.
020	PRO	006	004	Do not grant sleep to your eyes, nor let your eyelids slumber.
020	PRO	006	005	Rescue yourself like a gazelle from the hand, and like a bird from the hand of the fowler.
020	PRO	006	006	Go to the ant, you lazy one, and consider her ways, and so learn wisdom.
020	PRO	006	007	For though she has no ruler, nor instructor, nor leader,
020	PRO	006	008	she provides meals for herself in the summer, and she gathers at the harvest what she may eat.
020	PRO	006	009	How long will you slumber, you lazy one? When will you rise up from your sleep?
020	PRO	006	010	You will sleep a little, you will slumber a little, you will fold your hands a little to sleep,
020	PRO	006	011	and then destitution will meet with you, like a traveler, and poverty, like an armed man. Yet truly, if you would be diligent, then your harvest will arrive like a fountain, and destitution will flee far from you.
020	PRO	006	012	An apostate man, a harmful man, walks with a perverse mouth;
020	PRO	006	013	he winks with the eyes, touches with the foot, speaks with the finger.
020	PRO	006	014	With a depraved heart he devises evil, and at all times he sows conflict.
020	PRO	006	015	To this one, his perdition will arrive promptly, and he shall be crushed suddenly: he will no longer have any remedy.
020	PRO	006	016	Six things there are that the Lord hates, and the seventh, his soul detests:
020	PRO	006	017	haughty eyes, a lying tongue, hands that shed innocent blood,
020	PRO	006	018	a heart that devises the most wicked thoughts, feet running swiftly unto evil,
020	PRO	006	019	a deceitful witness bringing forth lies, and he who sows discord among brothers.
020	PRO	006	020	My son, preserve the precepts of your father, and do not dismiss the law of your mother.
020	PRO	006	021	Bind them to your heart unceasingly, and encircle them around your throat.
020	PRO	006	022	When you walk, let them keep step with you. When you sleep, let them guard you. And when you keep watch, speak with them.
020	PRO	006	023	For commandment is a lamp, and law is a light, and the reproofs of discipline are the way of life.
020	PRO	006	024	So may they guard you from an evil woman, and from the flattering tongue of the outsider.
020	PRO	006	025	Let not your heart desire her beauty; do not be captivated by her winks.
020	PRO	006	026	For the price of a prostitute is only one loaf. Yet the woman seizes the precious soul of a man.
020	PRO	006	027	Would a man be able to conceal fire in his bosom, so that his garments would not burn?
020	PRO	006	028	Or could he walk over burning coals, so that his feet would not be burned?
020	PRO	006	029	So also, he who enters to the wife of his neighbor shall not be clean when he touches her.
020	PRO	006	030	Not so great is the fault when someone has stolen. For he steals so as to satisfy a hungry soul.
020	PRO	006	031	Also, if he is apprehended, he shall repay sevenfold and hand over all the substance of his house.
020	PRO	006	032	But whoever is an adulterer, because of the emptiness of his heart, will destroy his own soul.
020	PRO	006	033	He gathers shame and dishonor to himself, and his disgrace will not be wiped away.
020	PRO	006	034	For the jealousy and fury of the husband will not spare him on the day of vindication,
020	PRO	006	035	nor will he agree to the pleadings of anyone, nor will he accept, as repayment, a multitude of gifts.
020	PRO	007	001	My son, guard my words and conceal my precepts within you.
020	PRO	007	002	Son, preserve my commandments, and you shall live. And keep my law as the pupil of your eye.
020	PRO	007	003	Bind it with your fingers; write it on the tablets of your heart.
020	PRO	007	004	Say to wisdom, “You are my sister,” and call prudence your friend.
020	PRO	007	005	So may she guard you from the woman who is an outsider, and from the stranger who sweetens her words.
020	PRO	007	006	For I gaze from the window of my house, through the lattice,
020	PRO	007	007	and I see little ones. I consider a frenzied youth,
020	PRO	007	008	who crosses the street at the corner and close to the way of that house.
020	PRO	007	009	He steps into shadows, as day becomes evening, into the darkness and gloom of the night.
020	PRO	007	010	And behold, a woman meets him, dressed like a harlot, prepared to captivate souls: chattering and rambling,
020	PRO	007	011	unwilling to bear silence, unable to keep her feet at home,
020	PRO	007	012	now outside, now in the streets, now lying in ambush near the corners.
020	PRO	007	013	And overtaking the youth, she kisses him, and with a provocative face, she flatters him, saying:
020	PRO	007	014	“I vowed sacrifices for well-being. Today I have repaid my vows.
020	PRO	007	015	Because of this, I have gone out to meet you, desiring to see you, and I have found you.
020	PRO	007	016	I have woven my bed with cords. I have strewn it with embroidered tapestries from Egypt.
020	PRO	007	017	I have sprinkled my bed with myrrh, aloe, and cinnamon.
020	PRO	007	018	Come, let us be inebriated in abundance, and let us delight in the embraces of desire, until the day begins to dawn.
020	PRO	007	019	For my husband is not in his house. He has gone away on a very long journey.
020	PRO	007	020	He took with him a bag of money. He will return to his house on the day of the full moon.”
020	PRO	007	021	She enmeshed him with many words, and she drew him forward with the flattery of her lips.
020	PRO	007	022	Immediately, he follows her, like an ox being led to the sacrifice, and like a lamb acting lasciviously, and not knowing that he is being drawn foolishly into chains,
020	PRO	007	023	until the arrow pierces his liver. It is just as if a bird were to hurry into the snare. And he does not know that his actions endanger his own soul.
020	PRO	007	024	Therefore, my son, hear me now, and attend to the words of my mouth.
020	PRO	007	025	Do not let your mind be pulled into her ways. And do not be deceived by her paths.
020	PRO	007	026	For she has tossed aside many wounded, and some of those who were very strong have been slain by her.
020	PRO	007	027	Her household is the way to Hell, reaching even to the inner places of death.
020	PRO	008	001	Does not wisdom call out, and prudence bestow her voice?
020	PRO	008	002	At the summits and the tops of exalted places, standing above the ways, in the midst of the paths,
020	PRO	008	003	beside the gates of the city, at the very doors, she speaks, saying:
020	PRO	008	004	“O men, to you I call out, and my voice is to the sons of men.
020	PRO	008	005	O little ones, understand discernment. And you who are unwise, turn your souls.
020	PRO	008	006	Listen, for I will speak about great things, and my lips will be opened, so as to foretell what is right.
020	PRO	008	007	My throat shall practice truth, and my lips shall detest the impious.
020	PRO	008	008	All my words are just. There is no depravity in them, and no perversity.
020	PRO	008	009	They are upright to those who understand, and equitable to those who discover knowledge.
020	PRO	008	010	Accept my discipline, and not money. Choose the doctrine that is greater than gold.
020	PRO	008	011	For wisdom is better than all that is most precious, and everything that is desirable cannot compare to her.
020	PRO	008	012	I, wisdom, dwell in counsel, and I am inside learned thoughts.
020	PRO	008	013	The fear of the Lord hates evil. I detest arrogance, and pride, and every wicked way, and a mouth with a double tongue.
020	PRO	008	014	Counsel is mine, and equity. Prudence is mine. Strength is mine.
020	PRO	008	015	Through me, kings reign and legislators decree just conditions.
020	PRO	008	016	Through me, princes rule and the powerful decree justice.
020	PRO	008	017	I love those who love me. And those who stand watch for me until morning shall discover me.
020	PRO	008	018	With me, are wealth and glory, superb riches and justice.
020	PRO	008	019	For my fruit is better than gold and precious stones, and my progeny better than choice silver.
020	PRO	008	020	I walk in the way of justice, in the midst of the paths of judgment,
020	PRO	008	021	so that I may enrich those who love me, and thus complete their treasures.
020	PRO	008	022	The Lord possessed me in the beginning of his ways, before he made anything, from the beginning.
020	PRO	008	023	I was ordained from eternity, and out of antiquity, before the earth was formed.
020	PRO	008	024	The abyss did not yet exist, and I was already conceived; neither had the fountains of waters yet erupted.
020	PRO	008	025	The mountains, with their great mass, had not yet been established. Before the hills, I was brought forth.
020	PRO	008	026	Still he had not made the earth, and the rivers, and the poles of the globe of the earth.
020	PRO	008	027	I was already present: when he prepared the heavens; when, with a certain law and a circuit, he fortified the abyss;
020	PRO	008	028	when he made firm the sky above, and set free the fountains of waters;
020	PRO	008	029	when he encompassed the sea within its limits, and laid down a law for the waters, lest they transgress their limits; when he weighed the foundations of the earth.
020	PRO	008	030	I was with him in composing all things. And I was delighted, throughout every day, by playing in his sight at all times,
020	PRO	008	031	playing in globe of the earth. And my delight was to be with the sons of men.
020	PRO	008	032	Therefore, sons, hear me now. Blessed are those who preserve my ways.
020	PRO	008	033	Listen to discipline, and become wise, and do not be willing to cast it aside.
020	PRO	008	034	Blessed is the man who listens to me, and who stands watch at my gates every day, and who observes at the posts of my doors.
020	PRO	008	035	He who finds me, finds life, and he will draw salvation from the Lord.
020	PRO	008	036	But he who sins against me will wound his own soul. All who hate me love death.”
020	PRO	009	001	Wisdom has built a house for herself. She has hewn seven columns.
020	PRO	009	002	She has immolated her victims. She has mixed her wine and set forth her table.
020	PRO	009	003	She has sent her maids to call out to the tower and to the fortified walls of the city,
020	PRO	009	004	“If anyone is little, let him come to me.” And to the unwise, she has said:
020	PRO	009	005	“Approach. Eat my bread, and drink the wine that I have mixed for you.
020	PRO	009	006	Leave behind childishness. And live and walk by the ways of prudence.”
020	PRO	009	007	Whoever teaches a mocker causes injury to himself. And whoever argues with the impious produces a blemish on himself.
020	PRO	009	008	Do not be willing to argue with a mocker, lest he hate you. Dispute with the wise, and he will love you.
020	PRO	009	009	Present an opportunity to the wise, and wisdom shall be added to him. Teach the just, and he will hurry to receive it.
020	PRO	009	010	The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom, and knowledge of holiness is prudence.
020	PRO	009	011	For by me, your days will be multiplied and years of life will be added to you.
020	PRO	009	012	If you would be wise, you will be so for yourself. But if you would be one who ridicules, you alone shall carry the evil.
020	PRO	009	013	A foolish and loud woman, who is full of enticements and who knows nothing at all,
020	PRO	009	014	sat at the entrance of her house on a seat, in a high place of the city,
020	PRO	009	015	so as to call to those who were passing by the way and continuing on their journey:
020	PRO	009	016	“Whoever is little, let him turn aside to me.” And to the frenzied, she said,
020	PRO	009	017	“Stolen waters are more soothing, and secret bread is more pleasant.”
020	PRO	009	018	And he did not know that giants are there, and that her companions are in the depths of Hell.
020	PRO	010	001	A wise son gladdens the father. Yet truly, a foolish son is the grief of his mother.
020	PRO	010	002	Treasures of impiety will profit nothing. Truly, justice shall liberate from death.
020	PRO	010	003	The Lord will not afflict with famine the soul of the just, and he will overthrow the treacheries of the impious.
020	PRO	010	004	The neglectful hand has wrought destitution. But the hand of the steadfast prepares riches. He who advances by lies, this one feeds on the wind. For he is the same as one who runs after flying birds.
020	PRO	010	005	He who gathers the harvest is a wise son. But he who snores in warm weather is a son of confusion.
020	PRO	010	006	The blessing of the Lord is on the head of the just. But iniquity covers the mouth of the impious.
020	PRO	010	007	The remembrance of the just is with praises. And the name of the impious shall decay.
020	PRO	010	008	The wise of heart accept precepts. The foolish are cut down by the lips.
020	PRO	010	009	He who walks in simplicity walks in confidence. But he who corrupts his ways shall be discovered.
020	PRO	010	010	He who winks with the eye gives sorrow. And the foolish in lips shall be beaten.
020	PRO	010	011	The mouth of the just is a vein of life. And the mouth of the impious covers iniquity.
020	PRO	010	012	Hatred rises up from disputes. And charity covers all offenses.
020	PRO	010	013	In the lips of the wise, wisdom is discovered. And a rod is for the back of one who lacks heart.
020	PRO	010	014	The wise store away knowledge. But the mouth of the foolish is a neighbor to confusion.
020	PRO	010	015	The substance of the rich is the city of his strength. The fear of the poor is their destitution.
020	PRO	010	016	The work of the just is unto life. But the fruit of the impious is unto sin.
020	PRO	010	017	The way of life is for those who observe discipline. But whoever abandons correction wanders astray.
020	PRO	010	018	Lying lips conceal hatred; whoever brings forth contempt is unwise.
020	PRO	010	019	In a multitude of speaking, sin will not be lacking. But whoever tempers his lips is most prudent.
020	PRO	010	020	The tongue of the just is choice silver. But the heart of the impious is exchanged for nothing.
020	PRO	010	021	The lips of the just instruct many. But those who are unlearned shall die in destitution of heart.
020	PRO	010	022	The blessing of the Lord causes riches. Affliction will not be a companion to them.
020	PRO	010	023	The foolish work wickedness as if in jest. But wisdom is prudence to a man.
020	PRO	010	024	What the impious fear will overwhelm them. The just shall be given their desire.
020	PRO	010	025	Like a passing tempest, so the impious one will be no more. But the just one is like an everlasting foundation.
020	PRO	010	026	Like vinegar to the teeth, and smoke to the eyes, so is a lazy one to those who sent him.
020	PRO	010	027	The fear of the Lord adds days. And the years of the impious will be shortened.
020	PRO	010	028	The expectation of the just is rejoicing. But the hope of the impious will perish.
020	PRO	010	029	The strength of the simple is the way of the Lord, and it is fear to those who work evil.
020	PRO	010	030	The just in eternity shall not be moved. But the impious will not live upon the earth.
020	PRO	010	031	The mouth of the just shall bring forth wisdom. The tongue of the depraved will perish.
020	PRO	010	032	The lips of the just consider what is acceptable. And the mouth of the impious considers perversities.
020	PRO	011	001	A deceitful scale is an abomination with the Lord, and a fair weighing is his will.
020	PRO	011	002	Wherever arrogance may be, there too is insult. But wherever humility is, there too is wisdom.
020	PRO	011	003	The simplicity of the just shall direct them, and the rebellion of the perverse will devastate them.
020	PRO	011	004	Wealth will not profit in the day of vengeance. But justice shall liberate from death.
020	PRO	011	005	The justice of the simple shall direct his way. And the impious will fall in his impiety.
020	PRO	011	006	The justice of the upright shall free them. And the iniquitous will be seized by their own treachery.
020	PRO	011	007	When the impious man is dead, there will no longer be any hope. And the expectation of the anxious will perish.
020	PRO	011	008	The just one is freed from anguish. And the impious one will be handed over instead of him.
020	PRO	011	009	The pretender deceives his friend by mouth. But the just shall be freed by knowledge.
020	PRO	011	010	In the good of the just, the city shall exult. And in the perdition of the impious, there shall be praise.
020	PRO	011	011	By the blessing of the just, the city shall be exalted. And by the mouth of the impious, it will be subverted.
020	PRO	011	012	Whoever despises his friend is destitute in heart. But the prudent man will remain silent.
020	PRO	011	013	Whoever walks dishonestly reveals secrets. But whoever is of a faithful soul conceals what is confided by a friend.
020	PRO	011	014	Where there is no governor, the people shall fall. But where there is much counsel, well-being shall be.
020	PRO	011	015	He will be afflicted with evil, who provides a guarantee for an outsider. But whoever is wary of traps shall be secure.
020	PRO	011	016	A gracious woman shall discover glory. And the robust will have wealth.
020	PRO	011	017	A merciful man benefits his own soul. But whoever is cruel casts out even his close relatives.
020	PRO	011	018	The impious does work with inconstancy. But for the sower of justice, there is the reward of faithfulness.
020	PRO	011	019	Clemency prepares life. And the pursuit of evils prepares death.
020	PRO	011	020	A depraved heart is abominable to the Lord. And his will is with those who walk in simplicity.
020	PRO	011	021	Hand in hand, the evil shall not be innocent. But the offspring of the just shall be saved.
020	PRO	011	022	A beautiful and senseless woman is like a gold ring in the snout of a swine.
020	PRO	011	023	The desire of the just is entirely good. The anticipation of the impious is fury.
020	PRO	011	024	Some distribute their own goods, and they become wealthier. Others seize what is not their own, and they are always in need.
020	PRO	011	025	The soul that blesses shall be made fat. And whoever inebriates will likewise be inebriated himself.
020	PRO	011	026	Whoever hides away grain shall be cursed among the people. But a blessing is upon the head of those who sell it.
020	PRO	011	027	He does well to rise early, who seeks what is good. But whoever is a seeker of evils shall be oppressed by them.
020	PRO	011	028	Whoever trusts in his riches will fall. But the just shall spring up like a green leaf.
020	PRO	011	029	Whoever troubles his own house will possess the winds. And whoever is foolish will serve the wise.
020	PRO	011	030	The fruit of the just one is the tree of life. And whoever receives souls is wise.
020	PRO	011	031	If the just are repaid upon the earth, how much more the impious and the sinner!
020	PRO	012	001	Whoever loves discipline loves knowledge. But whoever hates correction is unwise.
020	PRO	012	002	Whoever is good shall draw grace from the Lord. But whoever trusts in his own thoughts acts impiously.
020	PRO	012	003	Man will not be made strong from impiety. And the root of the just shall not be moved.
020	PRO	012	004	A diligent woman is a crown to her husband. And she who acts with confusion as to which things are worthy is decay to his bones.
020	PRO	012	005	The thoughts of the just are judgments. And the counsels of the impious are dishonest.
020	PRO	012	006	The words of the impious lie in wait for blood. The mouth of the just shall free them.
020	PRO	012	007	Turn from the impious, and they will not be. But the house of the just shall stand firm.
020	PRO	012	008	A man will be known by his doctrine. But whoever is vain and heartless will suffer contempt.
020	PRO	012	009	Better is a pauper who has what he needs, than someone glorious and in need of bread.
020	PRO	012	010	The just one knows the lives of his beasts. But the inner most parts of the impious are cruel.
020	PRO	012	011	Whoever works his land shall be satisfied with bread. But whoever continually pursues leisure is most foolish. Whoever is soothed by lingering over wine leaves behind contempt in his strongholds.
020	PRO	012	012	The desire of the impious is the fortification of what is most wicked. But the root of the just shall prosper.
020	PRO	012	013	For the sins of the lips draw ruin to the evil. But the just shall escape from distress.
020	PRO	012	014	By the fruit of his own mouth, each one shall be filled with good things, and according to the works of his own hands, it will be distributed to him.
020	PRO	012	015	The way of the foolish is right in his own eyes. But whoever is wise listens to counsels.
020	PRO	012	016	The senseless immediately reveals his anger. But whoever ignores injuries is clever.
020	PRO	012	017	He is a sign of justice, who speaks what he knows. But whoever deceives is a dishonest witness.
020	PRO	012	018	He who makes promises is also jabbed, as if with a sword, in conscience. But the tongue of the wise is reasonable.
020	PRO	012	019	The lips of truth shall be steadfast forever. But a hasty witness readies a lying tongue.
020	PRO	012	020	Deceit is in the heart of those who devise evils. But gladness follows those who take up counsels of peace.
020	PRO	012	021	Whatever may befall the just, it will not discourage him. But the impious will be filled with disasters.
020	PRO	012	022	Lying lips are an abomination to the Lord. But whoever acts faithfully pleases him.
020	PRO	012	023	A resourceful man conceals knowledge. And the heart of the unwise provokes foolishness.
020	PRO	012	024	The hand of the strong will rule. But anyone who is neglectful will pay tribute.
020	PRO	012	025	Grief in the heart of a man humbles him. And with a good word he shall be made glad.
020	PRO	012	026	He who ignores a loss for the sake of a friend is just. But the way of the impious will deceive them.
020	PRO	012	027	The dishonest will not discover gain. But the substance of a man will be like precious gold.
020	PRO	012	028	In the path of justice, there is life. But the devious way leads to death.
020	PRO	013	001	A wise son is the doctrine of his father. But he who ridicules does not listen when he is reproved.
020	PRO	013	002	From the fruit of his own mouth, a man shall be satisfied with good things. But the soul of betrayers is iniquity.
020	PRO	013	003	Whoever guards his mouth guards his soul. But whoever gives no consideration to his speech shall experience misfortunes.
020	PRO	013	004	The lazy one is willing and then not willing. But the soul of he who labors shall be made fat.
020	PRO	013	005	The just shall detest a lying word. But the impious confound and will be confounded.
020	PRO	013	006	Justice guards the way of the innocent. But impiety undermines the sinner.
020	PRO	013	007	One is like the rich, though he has nothing. And another is like the poor, though he has many riches.
020	PRO	013	008	The redemption of a man’s life is his riches. But he who is poor cannot tolerate correction.
020	PRO	013	009	The light of the just enriches. But the lamp of the impious will be extinguished.
020	PRO	013	010	Among the arrogant, there are always conflicts. But those who do everything with counsel are ruled by wisdom.
020	PRO	013	011	Substance obtained in haste will be diminished. But what is collected by hand, little by little, shall be multiplied.
020	PRO	013	012	Hope, when it is delayed, afflicts the soul. The arrival of the desired is a tree of life.
020	PRO	013	013	Whoever denounces something obligates himself for the future. But whoever fears a lesson shall turn away in peace. Deceitful souls wander into sins. The just are merciful and compassionate.
020	PRO	013	014	The law of the wise is a fountain of life, so that he may turn aside from the ruin of death.
020	PRO	013	015	Good doctrine bestows grace. In the way of the contemptuous, there is a chasm.
020	PRO	013	016	The discerning do everything with counsel. But whoever is senseless discloses his stupidity.
020	PRO	013	017	The messenger of the impious will fall into evil. But a faithful ambassador shall prosper.
020	PRO	013	018	Destitution and disgrace are for those who abandon discipline. But whoever agrees with a reproof shall be glorified.
020	PRO	013	019	The desired, when perfected, shall delight the soul. The foolish detest those who flee from evils.
020	PRO	013	020	Whoever keeps step with the wise shall be wise. A friend of the foolish will become like them.
020	PRO	013	021	Evil pursues sinners. And good things shall be distributed to the just.
020	PRO	013	022	The good leave behind heirs: children and grandchildren. And the substance of the sinner is preserved for the just.
020	PRO	013	023	Much nourishment is in the fallow land of the fathers. But for others, it is gathered without judgment.
020	PRO	013	024	He who spares the rod hates his son. But he who loves him urgently instructs him.
020	PRO	013	025	The just eats and fills his soul. But the belly of the impious is never satisfied.
020	PRO	014	001	A wise woman builds up her household. But a foolish one will pull down with her own hands what has been built up.
020	PRO	014	002	One who walks on a virtuous journey, and who fears God, is despised by him who advances along a disreputable way.
020	PRO	014	003	In the mouth of the foolish, there is a rod of arrogance. But the lips of the wise guard them.
020	PRO	014	004	Where there are no oxen, the feeding trough is empty. But where there are many crops, there the strength of the ox is manifest.
020	PRO	014	005	A faithful witness will not lie. But a deceitful witness offers a lie.
020	PRO	014	006	A mocker seeks wisdom and does not find it. The doctrine of the prudent is accessible.
020	PRO	014	007	Go against a foolish man, and he does not acknowledge lips of prudence.
020	PRO	014	008	The wisdom of a discerning man is to understand his way. And the imprudence of the foolish is to be wandering astray.
020	PRO	014	009	The foolish will speak mockingly of sin. But grace lingers among the just.
020	PRO	014	010	The heart that knows the bitterness of its own soul, in its gladness the outsider shall not meddle.
020	PRO	014	011	The house of the impious will be wiped away. Yet truly, the tabernacles of the just shall spring forth.
020	PRO	014	012	There is a way which seems just to a man, but its conclusion leads to death.
020	PRO	014	013	Laughter shall be mingled with sorrow, and mourning occupies the limits of joy.
020	PRO	014	014	The foolish will be filled up by his own ways. And the good man shall be above him.
020	PRO	014	015	The innocent trust every word. The astute one considers his own steps. Nothing good will be for the deceitful son. But the wise servant shall act prosperously and his way will be set in order.
020	PRO	014	016	The wise fear, and so turn away from evil. The foolish leap ahead with confidence.
020	PRO	014	017	The impatient will work foolishness. And a resourceful man is hated.
020	PRO	014	018	The childish will possess foolishness, and the discerning will anticipate knowledge.
020	PRO	014	019	The evil will fall down before the good. And the impious will fall down before the gates of the just.
020	PRO	014	020	The pauper will be hated, even by his own neighbor. Yet truly, the friends of the wealthy are many.
020	PRO	014	021	Whoever despises his neighbor, sins. But whoever pities the poor shall be blessed. Whoever trusts in the Lord loves mercy.
020	PRO	014	022	They wander astray who work evil. But mercy and truth prepare good things.
020	PRO	014	023	In every work, there shall be abundance. But where there are many words, there is often need.
020	PRO	014	024	The crown of the wise is their wealth. The senselessness of the foolish is imprudence.
020	PRO	014	025	A faithful witness frees souls. And the chameleon utters lies.
020	PRO	014	026	In the fear of the Lord is the faithfulness of strength, and there shall be hope for his sons.
020	PRO	014	027	The fear of the Lord is a fountain of life, so as to turn aside from the ruin of death.
020	PRO	014	028	In a multitude of people, there is dignity for the king. And in a paucity of people, there is disgrace for the prince.
020	PRO	014	029	Whoever is patient is governed by much prudence. But whoever is impatient exalts his foolishness.
020	PRO	014	030	The well-being of the heart is life for the flesh. But envy is decay for the bones.
020	PRO	014	031	Whoever slanders the indigent argues against his Maker. But he who has compassion on the poor honors his Maker.
020	PRO	014	032	The impious will be expelled in his malice. But the just finds hope even in his own death.
020	PRO	014	033	In the heart of the prudent, wisdom finds rest. And so shall he instruct all the uneducated.
020	PRO	014	034	Justice elevates a nation. But sin makes the peoples miserable.
020	PRO	014	035	An intelligent minister is acceptable to the king. Whoever is useless shall bear his wrath.
020	PRO	015	001	A mild response shatters anger. But a harsh word stirs up fury.
020	PRO	015	002	The tongue of the wise adorns knowledge. But the mouth of the senseless gushes with foolishness.
020	PRO	015	003	In every place, the eyes of the Lord consider good and evil.
020	PRO	015	004	A peaceful tongue is a tree of life. But that which is immoderate will crush the spirit.
020	PRO	015	005	A fool laughs at the discipline of his father. But whoever preserves rebukes will become astute. In abundant justice, there is very great virtue. But the intentions of the impious will be eradicated.
020	PRO	015	006	The house of the just has very great strength. And in the fruits of the impious, there is disorder.
020	PRO	015	007	The lips of the wise shall disseminate knowledge. The heart of the foolish will be dissimilar.
020	PRO	015	008	The sacrifices of the impious are abominable to the Lord. The vows of the just are appeasing.
020	PRO	015	009	The way of the impious is an abomination to the Lord. Whoever pursues justice is loved by him.
020	PRO	015	010	Doctrine is evil to those who abandon the way of life. Whoever hates correction shall die.
020	PRO	015	011	Hell and perdition are in the sight of the Lord. How much more the hearts of the sons of men!
020	PRO	015	012	He who corrupts himself does not love the one who afflicts him, nor will he step toward the wise.
020	PRO	015	013	A rejoicing heart gladdens the face. But by the grief of the soul, the spirit is cast down.
020	PRO	015	014	The heart of the wise seeks doctrine. And the mouth of the foolish feeds on ignorance.
020	PRO	015	015	All the days of the poor are evil. A secure mind is like a continual feast.
020	PRO	015	016	Better is a little with the fear of the Lord, than great treasures and dissatisfaction.
020	PRO	015	017	It is better to be called to vegetables with charity, than to a fatted calf with hatred.
020	PRO	015	018	A short-tempered man provokes conflicts. Whoever is patient tempers those who are stirred up.
020	PRO	015	019	The way of the slothful is like a hedge of thorns. The way of the just is without offense.
020	PRO	015	020	A wise son gladdens the father. But the foolish man despises his mother.
020	PRO	015	021	Folly is gladness to the foolish. And the prudent man sets his own steps in order.
020	PRO	015	022	Intentions dissipate where there is no counsel. Yet truly, they are confirmed where there are many counselors.
020	PRO	015	023	A man rejoices in the verdict of his own mouth. And a word at the right time is best.
020	PRO	015	024	The path of life is for the wise above, so that he may turn away from the end of Hell.
020	PRO	015	025	The Lord will demolish the house of the arrogant. And He will make firm the borders of the widow.
020	PRO	015	026	Evil intentions are an abomination to the Lord. And pure conversation, most beautiful, shall be confirmed by him.
020	PRO	015	027	Whoever pursues avarice disturbs his own house. But whoever hates bribes shall live. Through mercy and faith, sins are purged. But through the fear of the Lord, each one turns aside from evil.
020	PRO	015	028	The mind of the just meditates on obedience. The mouth of the impious overflows with evils.
020	PRO	015	029	The Lord is distant from the impious. And he will heed the prayers of the just.
020	PRO	015	030	The light of the eyes rejoices the soul. A good reputation fattens the bones.
020	PRO	015	031	The ear that listens to the reproofs of life shall abide in the midst of the wise.
020	PRO	015	032	Whoever rejects discipline despises his own soul. But whoever agrees to correction is a possessor of the heart.
020	PRO	015	033	The fear of the Lord is the discipline of wisdom. And humility precedes glory.
020	PRO	016	001	It is for man to prepare the soul, and for the Lord to govern the tongue.
020	PRO	016	002	All the ways of a man are open to his eyes; the Lord is the one who weighs spirits.
020	PRO	016	003	Open your works to the Lord, and your intentions will be set in order.
020	PRO	016	004	The Lord has wrought all things because of himself. Likewise the impious is for the evil day.
020	PRO	016	005	All the arrogant are an abomination to the Lord. Even if hand will be joined to hand, he is not innocent. The beginning of a good way is to do justice. And this is more acceptable with God than to immolate sacrifices.
020	PRO	016	006	By mercy and truth, iniquity is redeemed. And by the fear of the Lord, one turns away from evil.
020	PRO	016	007	When the ways of man will please the Lord, he will convert even his enemies to peace.
020	PRO	016	008	Better is a little with justice, than many fruits with iniquity.
020	PRO	016	009	The heart of man disposes his way. But it is for Lord to direct his steps.
020	PRO	016	010	Foreknowledge is in the lips of the king. His mouth shall not err in judgment.
020	PRO	016	011	Weights and scales are judgments of the Lord. And all the stones in the bag are his work.
020	PRO	016	012	Those who act impiously are abominable to the king. For the throne is made firm by justice.
020	PRO	016	013	Just lips are the will of kings. He who speaks honestly shall be loved.
020	PRO	016	014	The indignation of a king is a herald of death. And the wise man will appease it.
020	PRO	016	015	In the cheerfulness of the king’s countenance, there is life. And his clemency is like belated rain.
020	PRO	016	016	Possess wisdom, for it is better than gold. And acquire prudence, for it is more precious than silver.
020	PRO	016	017	The path of the just turns away from evils. He who guards his soul preserves his way.
020	PRO	016	018	Arrogance precedes destruction. And the spirit is exalted before a fall.
020	PRO	016	019	It is better to be humbled with the meek, than to divide spoils with the arrogant.
020	PRO	016	020	The learned in word shall find good things. And whoever hopes in the Lord is blessed.
020	PRO	016	021	Whoever is wise in heart shall be called prudent. And whoever is sweet in eloquence shall attain to what is greater.
020	PRO	016	022	Learning is a fountain of life to one who possesses it. The doctrine of the foolish is senseless.
020	PRO	016	023	The heart of the wise shall instruct his mouth and add grace to his lips.
020	PRO	016	024	Careful words are a honeycomb: sweet to the soul and healthful to the bones.
020	PRO	016	025	There is a way which seems right to a man, and its end result leads to death.
020	PRO	016	026	The soul of the laborer labors for himself, because his mouth has driven him to it.
020	PRO	016	027	The impious man digs up evil, and in his lips is a burning fire.
020	PRO	016	028	A perverse man stirs up lawsuits. And one who is verbose divides leaders.
020	PRO	016	029	A man of iniquity entices his friend, and he leads him along a way that is not good.
020	PRO	016	030	Whoever, with astonished eyes, thinks up depravities, biting his lips, accomplishes evil.
020	PRO	016	031	Old age is a crown of dignity, when it is found in the ways of justice.
020	PRO	016	032	A patient man is better than a strong one. And whoever rules his soul is better than one who assaults cities.
020	PRO	016	033	Lots are cast into the lap, but they are tempered by the Lord.
020	PRO	017	001	A dry morsel with gladness is better than a house full of sacrifices along with conflict.
020	PRO	017	002	A wise servant shall rule over foolish sons, and he will divide the inheritance among brothers.
020	PRO	017	003	Just as silver is tested by fire, and gold is tested in the furnace, so also does the Lord test hearts.
020	PRO	017	004	The evil obey an unjust tongue. And the false are submissive to lying lips.
020	PRO	017	005	Whoever despises the poor rebukes his Maker. And whoever rejoices in the ruin of another will not go unpunished.
020	PRO	017	006	Sons of sons are the crown of old age. And the glory of sons is their fathers.
020	PRO	017	007	Well-chosen words are not fitting for the foolish, nor are lying lips fitting for a leader.
020	PRO	017	008	The expectation of those who stand ready is a most pleasing jewel. Whichever way he turns himself, he understands prudently.
020	PRO	017	009	Whoever conceals an offense seeks friendships. Whoever repeats the words of another separates allies.
020	PRO	017	010	A correction benefits more with a wise man, than a hundred stripes with a fool.
020	PRO	017	011	The evil one continually seeks conflicts. But a cruel Angel shall be sent against him.
020	PRO	017	012	It is more expedient to meet a bear robbed of her young, than the foolish trusting in his own folly.
020	PRO	017	013	Whoever repays evil for good, evil shall not withdraw from his house.
020	PRO	017	014	Whoever releases the water is the head of the conflict. And just before he suffers contempt, he abandons judgment.
020	PRO	017	015	Those who justify the impious, and those who condemn the just, both are abominable with God.
020	PRO	017	016	What does it profit the foolish to have riches, when he is not able to buy wisdom? Whoever makes his house high seeks ruin. And whoever shuns learning shall fall into evils.
020	PRO	017	017	Whoever is a friend loves at all times. And a brother is proved by distress.
020	PRO	017	018	A foolish man will clap his hands, when he makes a pledge for his friend.
020	PRO	017	019	Whoever dwells on discord loves disputes. And whoever exalts his door seeks ruin.
020	PRO	017	020	Whoever is of a perverse heart shall not find good. And whoever turns his tongue shall fall into evil.
020	PRO	017	021	A foolish one is born into his own disgrace. But his father will not rejoice in one who is senseless.
020	PRO	017	022	A joyful soul makes a lifetime flourish. A gloomy spirit dries out the bones.
020	PRO	017	023	The impious receives gifts from the bosom, so that he may pervert the paths of judgment.
020	PRO	017	024	Prudence shines from the face of the wise. The eyes of the foolish are on the ends of the earth.
020	PRO	017	025	A foolish son is the anger of the father and the grief of the mother who conceived him.
020	PRO	017	026	It is not good to inflict damage on the just, nor to strike the leader who judges uprightly.
020	PRO	017	027	Whoever moderates his words is learned and prudent. And a man of learning has a precious spirit.
020	PRO	017	028	If he would remain silent, even the foolish would be considered wise, and if he closes his lips, intelligent.
020	PRO	018	001	Whoever has a will to withdraw from a friend, seeks occasions; he shall be reproached at all times.
020	PRO	018	002	The foolish do not accept words of prudence, unless you say what is already turning in his heart.
020	PRO	018	003	The impious, when he has arrived within the depths of sin, thinks little of it. But ill repute and disgrace follow him.
020	PRO	018	004	Words from the mouth of a man are deep waters. And the fountain of wisdom is a torrent overflowing.
020	PRO	018	005	It is not good to accept the character of the impious, so as to turn away from true judgment.
020	PRO	018	006	The lips of the foolish meddle in disputes. And his mouth provokes conflicts.
020	PRO	018	007	The mouth of the foolish is his destruction, and his own lips are the ruin of his soul.
020	PRO	018	008	The words of the double-tongued seem simple. And they reach even to the interior of the gut. Fear casts down the lazy, but the souls of the effeminate shall go hungry.
020	PRO	018	009	Whoever is dissolute and slack in his work is the brother of him who wastes his own works.
020	PRO	018	010	The name of the Lord is a very strong tower. The just one rushes to it, and he shall be exalted.
020	PRO	018	011	The substance of the wealthy is the city of his strength, and it is like a strong wall encircling him.
020	PRO	018	012	The heart of a man is exalted before it is crushed and humbled before it is glorified.
020	PRO	018	013	Whoever responds before he listens, demonstrates himself to be foolish and deserving of confusion.
020	PRO	018	014	The spirit of a man sustains his weakness. Yet who can sustain a spirit that is easily angered?
020	PRO	018	015	A prudent heart shall possess knowledge. And the ear of the wise seeks doctrine.
020	PRO	018	016	A man’s gift expands his way and makes space for him before leaders.
020	PRO	018	017	The just is the first accuser of himself; his friend arrives and shall investigate him.
020	PRO	018	018	Casting a lot suppresses contentions and passes judgment, even among the powerful.
020	PRO	018	019	A brother who is helped by a brother is like a reinforced city, and judgments are like the bars of cities.
020	PRO	018	020	From the fruit of a man’s mouth shall his belly be filled. And the harvest of his own lips shall satisfy him.
020	PRO	018	021	Death and life are in the power of the tongue. Whoever values it shall eat from its fruits.
020	PRO	018	022	He who has found a good wife has found goodness, and he shall draw contentment from the Lord. He who expels a good wife expels goodness. But he who holds on to an adulteress is foolish and impious.
020	PRO	018	023	The poor will speak with supplications. And the rich will express themselves roughly.
020	PRO	018	024	A man amiable to society shall be more friendly than a brother.
020	PRO	019	001	Better is the poor who walks in his simplicity, than the rich who twists his lips and is unwise.
020	PRO	019	002	Where there is no knowledge of the soul, there is no good. And whoever hurries with his feet will stumble.
020	PRO	019	003	The foolishness of a man undermines his steps. And then he seethes in his soul against God.
020	PRO	019	004	Riches add many friends. But from the pauper, even those whom he had become separated.
020	PRO	019	005	A false witness shall not go unpunished. And whoever speaks lies will not escape.
020	PRO	019	006	Many honor the character of one who is powerful, and there are friends for a giver of gifts.
020	PRO	019	007	The brothers of the poor man hate him. Moreover, even his friends have withdrawn far from him. Whoever pursues only words shall have nothing.
020	PRO	019	008	But whoever possesses reason loves his own soul. And one who guards prudence shall discover good things.
020	PRO	019	009	A false witness shall not go unpunished. And whoever speaks lies will perish.
020	PRO	019	010	Fine things are not fitting for the foolish, nor is it fitting for a servant to rule over princes.
020	PRO	019	011	The doctrine of a man is known through patience. And his glory is to pass beyond iniquities.
020	PRO	019	012	Like the roaring of a lion, so also is the wrath of a king. And his cheerfulness is like the dew upon the grass.
020	PRO	019	013	A foolish son is the grief of his father. And an argumentative wife is like a roof that is continually leaking.
020	PRO	019	014	A house and its riches are given by parents. But a prudent wife is particularly from the Lord.
020	PRO	019	015	Laziness sends one into a deep sleep, and a dissolute soul will go hungry.
020	PRO	019	016	Whoever guards a commandment guards his own soul. But whoever neglects his own way will die.
020	PRO	019	017	Whoever is merciful to the poor lends to the Lord. And he will repay him for his efforts.
020	PRO	019	018	Teach your son; do not despair. But do not set your soul toward putting him to death.
020	PRO	019	019	Whoever is impatient will sustain damage. And when it has been taken away, he will set up another.
020	PRO	019	020	Listen to counsel and take up discipline, so that you may be wise in your latter days.
020	PRO	019	021	There are many intentions in the heart of a man. But the will of the Lord shall stand firm.
020	PRO	019	022	An indigent man is merciful. And a pauper is better than a deceitful man.
020	PRO	019	023	The fear of the Lord is unto life. And he shall linger in plentitude, without being visited by disaster.
020	PRO	019	024	The lazy conceals his hand under his arm, and he will not so much as bring it to his mouth.
020	PRO	019	025	When the pestilent are scourged, the foolish will become wiser. But if you chastise the wise, he will understand discipline.
020	PRO	019	026	Whoever afflicts his father and flees from his mother is disreputable and unhappy.
020	PRO	019	027	Son, do not cease listening to doctrine, and do not be ignorant of the sermons of knowledge.
020	PRO	019	028	An unjust witness ridicules judgment. And the mouth of the impious devours iniquity.
020	PRO	019	029	Judgments are prepared for those who ridicule. And striking hammers are prepared for the bodies of the foolish.
020	PRO	020	001	It is a luxurious thing, wine, and inebriation is tumultuous. Anyone who is delighted by this will not be wise.
020	PRO	020	002	Just like the roaring of a lion, so also is the dread of a king. Whoever provokes him sins in his own soul.
020	PRO	020	003	Honor is for the man who separates himself from contentions. But all the foolish meddle in altercations.
020	PRO	020	004	Because of the cold, the lazy one was not willing to plough. Therefore, in the summer, he will beg, and it will not be given to him.
020	PRO	020	005	Counsel in the heart of a man is like deep waters. But a wise man will draw it out.
020	PRO	020	006	Many men are called merciful. But who will find a faithful man?
020	PRO	020	007	The just who walks in his simplicity shall leave behind him blessed sons.
020	PRO	020	008	The king who sits on the throne of judgment scatters all evil with his gaze.
020	PRO	020	009	Who is able to say: “My heart is clean. I am pure from sin?”
020	PRO	020	010	Diverse weights, diverse measures: both are abominable with God.
020	PRO	020	011	A child may be understood by his interests: whether his works may be clean and upright.
020	PRO	020	012	The hearing ear and the seeing eye: the Lord has made them both.
020	PRO	020	013	Do not love sleep, lest deprivation oppress you. Open your eyes and be satisfied with bread.
020	PRO	020	014	“It is bad, it is bad,” says every buyer; and when he has withdrawn, then he will boast.
020	PRO	020	015	There is gold, and there are a multitude of jewels. But lips of knowledge are a precious vessel.
020	PRO	020	016	Take away the vestments of him who stands up to vouch for a stranger, and take a pledge from him instead of from outsiders.
020	PRO	020	017	The bread of lies is sweet to a man. But afterwards, his mouth will be filled with pebbles.
020	PRO	020	018	Plans are strengthened by counsels. And wars are to be handled by governments.
020	PRO	020	019	Do not become involved with him who reveals mysteries, and who walks deceitfully, and who enlarges his lips.
020	PRO	020	020	Whoever curses his father and mother, his lamp will be extinguished in the midst of darkness.
020	PRO	020	021	When an inheritance is obtained hastily in the beginning, in the end it will be without a blessing.
020	PRO	020	022	Do not say, “I will repay evil.” Wait for the Lord, and he will free you.
020	PRO	020	023	Diverse weights are an abomination with the Lord. A deceitful balance is not good.
020	PRO	020	024	The steps of men are directed by the Lord. But who is the man able to understand his own way?
020	PRO	020	025	It is ruin for a man to devour what is holy, or, after making vows, to retract them.
020	PRO	020	026	A wise king scatters the impious and bends an archway over them.
020	PRO	020	027	The spirit of a man is a lamp to the Lord, which investigates all the secrets of the inner self.
020	PRO	020	028	Mercy and truth guard the king, and his throne is strengthened by clemency.
020	PRO	020	029	The joy of youths is their strength. And the dignity of old men is their grey hairs.
020	PRO	020	030	The bruise of a wound, as well as scourges, shall wipe away evils in the more secret places of the inner self.
020	PRO	021	001	Just as with the dividing of the waters, so also is the heart of the king in the hand of the Lord. He shall bend it whichever way he wills.
020	PRO	021	002	Every way of a man seems right to himself. But the Lord weighs hearts.
020	PRO	021	003	To do mercy and judgment is more pleasing to the Lord than sacrifices.
020	PRO	021	004	To lift up the eyes is to enlarge the heart. The lamp of the impious is sin.
020	PRO	021	005	The intentions of the robust continually bring forth abundance. But all the lazy are continually in need.
020	PRO	021	006	Whoever gathers treasures by a lying tongue is vain and heartless. And he will stumble into the snares of death.
020	PRO	021	007	The robberies of the impious will drag them down, because they were not willing to do judgment.
020	PRO	021	008	The perverse way of a man is foreign. But whoever is pure: his work is upright.
020	PRO	021	009	It is better to sit in a corner of the attic, than with a contentious woman and in a shared house.
020	PRO	021	010	The soul of the impious desires evil; he will not take pity on his neighbor.
020	PRO	021	011	When the pestilent is punished, a little one will become wiser. And if he pursues what is wise, he will receive knowledge.
020	PRO	021	012	The just thinks carefully about the house of the impious, so that he may draw the impious away from evil.
020	PRO	021	013	Whoever blocks his ears to the outcry of the poor shall also cry out himself, and he will not be heeded.
020	PRO	021	014	A surprise gift extinguishes anger. And a gift concealed in the bosom extinguishes the greatest indignation.
020	PRO	021	015	It is gladness for the just to do judgment; and it is dread for those who work iniquity.
020	PRO	021	016	A man who wanders astray from the way of doctrine will linger in the company of the giants.
020	PRO	021	017	Whoever loves a feast will be in deprivation. Whoever loves wine and fatness will not be enriched.
020	PRO	021	018	The impious is given over instead of the just, and the iniquitous is given over in place of the upright.
020	PRO	021	019	It is better to live in a deserted land, than with a quarrelsome and emotional woman.
020	PRO	021	020	There is desirable treasure, as well as oil, in the habitations of the just. And the imprudent man will waste it.
020	PRO	021	021	Whoever follows justice and mercy shall discover life, justice, and glory.
020	PRO	021	022	The wise has ascended the city of the strong, and he has torn down the bulwark of its confidence.
020	PRO	021	023	Whoever guards his mouth and his tongue guards his soul from anguish.
020	PRO	021	024	A proud and arrogant one is also called ignorant, if he, in anger, acts according to pride.
020	PRO	021	025	Desires kill the lazy, for his hands are not willing to work at all.
020	PRO	021	026	He covets and desires all day long. But whoever is just shall distribute and shall not cease.
020	PRO	021	027	The sacrifices of the impious are abominable, because they are offered out of wickedness.
020	PRO	021	028	A lying witness will perish. An obedient man shall speak of victory.
020	PRO	021	029	The impious man insolently hardens his face. But whoever is upright corrects his own way.
020	PRO	021	030	There is no wisdom, there is no prudence, there is no counsel, which is against the Lord.
020	PRO	021	031	The horse is prepared for the day of battle. But the Lord bestows salvation.
020	PRO	022	001	A good name is better than many riches. And good esteem is above silver and gold.
020	PRO	022	002	The rich and poor have met one another. The Lord is the maker of them both.
020	PRO	022	003	The clever saw evil and hid himself. The innocent continued on and was afflicted with damage.
020	PRO	022	004	The end of moderation is the fear of the Lord, riches and glory and life.
020	PRO	022	005	Weapons and swords are on the way of the perverse. But he who guards his own soul withdraws far from them.
020	PRO	022	006	The proverb is: A youth is close to his way; even when he is old, he will not withdraw from it.
020	PRO	022	007	The rich rule over the poor. And the borrower is servant to the lender.
020	PRO	022	008	Whoever sows iniquity will reap evils, and by the rod of his own wrath he will be consumed.
020	PRO	022	009	Whoever is inclined to mercy shall be blessed, for from his bread he has given to the poor. Whoever gives gifts will acquire victory and honor. But he carries away the soul of the receiver.
020	PRO	022	010	Cast out the one who ridicules, and conflict will go out with him, and accusations and insults will cease.
020	PRO	022	011	Whoever loves cleanness of heart, because of the grace of his lips, will have the king as his friend.
020	PRO	022	012	The eyes of the Lord watch over knowledge. And the words of the iniquitous are supplanted.
020	PRO	022	013	The lazy one says: “There is a lion outside. I might be slain in the midst of the streets.”
020	PRO	022	014	The mouth of a foreign woman is a deep pit; the Lord was angry with him who will fall into it.
020	PRO	022	015	Foolishness has been bound to the heart of a child, and a rod of discipline shall cause it to flee.
020	PRO	022	016	Whoever slanders the poor, so as to augment his own riches, will give it away to one who is richer, and will be in need.
020	PRO	022	017	Incline your ear, and listen to the words of the wise. Then apply your heart to my doctrine.
020	PRO	022	018	It shall be beautiful to you, if you preserve it in your inner self, and it shall overflow from your lips,
020	PRO	022	019	so that your confidence may be in the Lord. Therefore, I also have revealed it to you this day.
020	PRO	022	020	Behold, I have written it for you in three ways, and with meditations and knowledge,
020	PRO	022	021	so that I might reveal to you, firmly and with words of truth, in order to respond about these things to those who sent you.
020	PRO	022	022	Do not act with violence toward the pauper because he is poor. And do not weary the needy at the gate.
020	PRO	022	023	For the Lord will judge his case, and he will pierce those who have pierced his soul.
020	PRO	022	024	Do not be willing to be a friend to an angry man, and do not walk with a furious man,
020	PRO	022	025	lest perhaps you learn his ways, and take up a stumbling block to your soul.
020	PRO	022	026	Do not be willing to be with those who certify with their hands, and who offer themselves as a guarantee against debts.
020	PRO	022	027	For if you do not have the means to restore, what reason should there be for him to take the covering from your bed?
020	PRO	022	028	Do not cross beyond the ancient limits that your fathers have set.
020	PRO	022	029	Have you seen a man swift in his work? He shall stand in the sight of kings, and not before those who are disreputable.
020	PRO	023	001	When you sit down to eat with a leader, pay close attention to what has been set before your face,
020	PRO	023	002	and put a knife to your throat, if, in such a way, you could hold your soul in your own power.
020	PRO	023	003	Do not desire his foods, in which is the bread of deceit.
020	PRO	023	004	Do not be willing to labor so that you may be enriched. But set limits by your prudence.
020	PRO	023	005	Do not raise your eyes toward wealth that you are not able to have. For they will make themselves wings, like those of an eagle, and they will fly in the sky.
020	PRO	023	006	Do not eat with an envious man, and do not desire his foods.
020	PRO	023	007	For, like a seer and an interpreter of dreams, he presumes what he does not know. “Eat and drink,” he will say to you; and his mind is not with you.
020	PRO	023	008	The foods that you had eaten, you will vomit up. And you will lose the beauty in your words.
020	PRO	023	009	Do not speak into the ears of the unwise. They will despise the doctrine of your eloquence.
020	PRO	023	010	Do not touch the boundaries of little ones, and do not enter into the field of the fatherless.
020	PRO	023	011	For their close relative is strong, and he will judge their case against you.
020	PRO	023	012	Let your heart enter into doctrine, and let your ears enter into words of knowledge.
020	PRO	023	013	Do not be willing to take away discipline from a child. For if you strike him with the rod, he will not die.
020	PRO	023	014	You will strike him with the rod, and so shall you deliver his soul from Hell.
020	PRO	023	015	My son, if your soul will become wise, my heart will be glad with you.
020	PRO	023	016	And my temperament will exult, when your lips will have spoken what is upright.
020	PRO	023	017	Let not your heart compete with sinners. But be in the fear of the Lord all day long.
020	PRO	023	018	For you will have hope in the end, and your expectation will not be taken away.
020	PRO	023	019	Listen, my son, and be wise, and direct your soul along the way.
020	PRO	023	020	Do not be willing to be in the feasts of great drinkers, nor in the carousings of those who gather to feed on flesh.
020	PRO	023	021	For those who waste time drinking, and who surrender themselves to symbols, will be consumed. And those who sleep will be clothed in rags.
020	PRO	023	022	Listen to your father, who conceived you. And do not despise your mother, when she is old.
020	PRO	023	023	Purchase truth, and do not sell wisdom, or doctrine, or understanding.
020	PRO	023	024	The father of the just exults in gladness; he who has conceived the wise will rejoice in him.
020	PRO	023	025	Let your father and your mother be joyful, and may she who conceived you exult.
020	PRO	023	026	My son, offer me your heart, and let your eyes keep to my ways.
020	PRO	023	027	For a loose woman is a deep pit, and a foreign woman is a constricted well.
020	PRO	023	028	She lies in wait along the way like a robber. And the incautious one whom she sees, she will put to death.
020	PRO	023	029	Who has woe? Whose father has woe? Who has quarrels? Who falls into pits? Who has wounds without cause? Who has watery eyes?
020	PRO	023	030	Is it not those who linger over wine, and who strive to be drinking from their cups?
020	PRO	023	031	Do not gaze into the wine when it turns gold, when its color shines in the glass. It enters pleasantly,
020	PRO	023	032	but in the end, it will bite like a snake, and it will spread poison like a king of snakes.
020	PRO	023	033	Your eyes will see women who are outsiders, and your heart will utter perversities.
020	PRO	023	034	And you will be like someone sleeping in the middle of the sea, and like a pilot, fast asleep, who has lost his hold on the helm.
020	PRO	023	035	And you will say: “They have beaten me, but I did not feel pain. They have dragged me, and I did not realize it. When will I awaken and find more wine?”
020	PRO	024	001	Do not imitate evil men, nor desire to be among them.
020	PRO	024	002	For their mind meditates on robberies, and their lips speak deceptions.
020	PRO	024	003	By wisdom shall a house be built, and by prudence shall it be strengthened.
020	PRO	024	004	By doctrine, the storerooms shall be filled with every substance that is precious and most beautiful.
020	PRO	024	005	A wise man is strong, and a well-taught man is robust and valiant.
020	PRO	024	006	For war is undertaken in an orderly manner, and safety shall be where there are many counsels.
020	PRO	024	007	Wisdom is beyond the foolish; at the gate he will not open his mouth.
020	PRO	024	008	Whoever intends to do evil shall be called foolish.
020	PRO	024	009	The intention of the foolish is sin. And the detractor is an abomination among men.
020	PRO	024	010	If you despair, being weary in the day of anguish, your strength will be diminished.
020	PRO	024	011	Rescue those who are led away to death. And do not cease from delivering those who are dragged away to a violent death.
020	PRO	024	012	If you would say: “I do not have sufficient strength.” He who inspects the heart, the same one understands, and nothing slips past the one who preserves your soul. And he shall repay a man according to his works.
020	PRO	024	013	My son, eat honey, because it is good, and the honeycomb, because it is so sweet to your throat.
020	PRO	024	014	So, too, is the doctrine of wisdom to your soul. When you have found it, you will have hope in the end, and your hope shall not perish.
020	PRO	024	015	Do not lie in wait, and do not seek impiety in the house of the just, nor spoil his rest.
020	PRO	024	016	For the just one will fall seven times, and he shall rise again. But the impious will fall into evil.
020	PRO	024	017	When your enemy will fall, do not be glad, and do not let your heart exult in his ruin,
020	PRO	024	018	lest perhaps the Lord see, and it displease him, and he may take away his wrath from him.
020	PRO	024	019	Do not contend with the most wicked, and do not be a rival to the impious.
020	PRO	024	020	For the evil hold no hope in the future, and the lamp of the impious will be extinguished.
020	PRO	024	021	My son, fear the Lord, as well as the king. And do not mingle with detractors.
020	PRO	024	022	For their perdition shall rise up suddenly. And who knows what ruin will be for each of them?
020	PRO	024	023	Likewise, these things are for the wise. It is not good to base judgment on knowledge of character.
020	PRO	024	024	Those who say to the impious, “You are just,” shall be cursed by the people, and the tribes shall detest them.
020	PRO	024	025	Those who argue against the impious shall be praised, and a blessing shall come upon them.
020	PRO	024	026	He shall kiss the lips, who responds with upright words.
020	PRO	024	027	Prepare your outdoor work, and diligently cultivate your field, so that afterward, you may build your house.
020	PRO	024	028	Do not be a witness without cause against your neighbor. And do not mislead anyone with your lips.
020	PRO	024	029	Do not say, “I will do to him as he has done to me.” I will repay each one according to his work.
020	PRO	024	030	I passed by the field of a lazy man, and by the vineyard of a foolish man,
020	PRO	024	031	and behold, it was entirely filled with nettles, and thorns had covered its surface, and the stonewall was destroyed.
020	PRO	024	032	When I had seen this, I laid it up in my heart, and by this example, I received discipline.
020	PRO	024	033	You will sleep a little,” I said. “You will slumber briefly. You will fold your hands a little, so as to rest.
020	PRO	024	034	And destitution will overtake you like a runner, and begging will overtake you like an armed man.”
020	PRO	025	001	These, too, are parables of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah, king of Judah, transferred.
020	PRO	025	002	It is to the glory of God to conceal a word, and it is to the glory of kings to investigate speech.
020	PRO	025	003	Heaven above, and earth below, and the heart of kings are each unsearchable.
020	PRO	025	004	Take away the tarnish from silver, and a most pure vessel will go forth.
020	PRO	025	005	Take away impiety from the face of the king, and his throne shall be made firm by justice.
020	PRO	025	006	Do not appear glorious before the king, and do not stand in the place of the great.
020	PRO	025	007	For it is better that it should be said to you, “Ascend to here,” than that you should be humbled before the prince.
020	PRO	025	008	The things that your eyes have seen, do not offer hastily in a quarrel, lest afterward you may not be able to make amends, when you have dishonored your friend.
020	PRO	025	009	Argue your case with your friend, and do not reveal the secret to an outsider,
020	PRO	025	010	lest perhaps he may insult you, when he has heard it, and he might not cease to reproach you. Grace and friendship free a man; preserve these for yourself, lest you fall under reproach.
020	PRO	025	011	Whoever speaks a word at an opportune time is like apples of gold on beds of silver.
020	PRO	025	012	Whoever reproves the wise and obedient ear is like an earring of gold with a shining pearl.
020	PRO	025	013	Just like the cold of snow in a time of harvest, so also is a faithful messenger to him who sent him: he causes his soul to rest.
020	PRO	025	014	A man who boasts and does not fulfill his promises is like clouds and wind, when rain does not follow.
020	PRO	025	015	By patience, a leader shall be appeased, and a soft tongue shall break hardness.
020	PRO	025	016	You have discovered honey; eat what is sufficient for you, lest perhaps, being filled up, you may vomit it.
020	PRO	025	017	Withdraw your feet from the house of your neighbor, lest, when he has had his fill, he may hate you.
020	PRO	025	018	A man who speaks false testimony against his neighbor is like a dart and a sword and a sharp arrow.
020	PRO	025	019	Whoever sets his hopes on the unfaithful in a day of anguish is like a rotten tooth and weary foot,
020	PRO	025	020	and like one who loosens his garment in cold weather. Whoever sings verses to a wicked heart is like vinegar on baking soda. Just like a moth to a garment, and a worm to wood, so too does the sadness of a man do harm to the heart.
020	PRO	025	021	If your enemy is hungry, feed him. If he is thirsty, give him water to drink.
020	PRO	025	022	For you will gather hot coals upon his head, and the Lord will repay you.
020	PRO	025	023	The north wind brings forth the rain, and a sorrowful face brings forth a detracting tongue.
020	PRO	025	024	It is better to sit in a corner of the attic, than with an argumentative woman and in a shared house.
020	PRO	025	025	Like cold water to a thirsty soul, so too are good reports from a far away land.
020	PRO	025	026	The just falling down before the impious is like a fountain stirred up by feet and like a corrupted spring.
020	PRO	025	027	Just as whoever eats too much honey, it is not good for him, so also whoever is an investigator of what is majestic will be overwhelmed by glory.
020	PRO	025	028	Just like a city lying in the open and without surrounding walls, so also is a man who is unable to restrain his own spirit in speaking.
020	PRO	026	001	In the manner of snow in the summer, and rain at the harvest, so also is glory unfit for the foolish.
020	PRO	026	002	Like a bird flying away to another place, and like a sparrow that hurries away freely, so also a curse uttered against someone without cause will pass away.
020	PRO	026	003	A whip is for a horse, and a muzzle is for donkey, and a rod is for the back of the imprudent.
020	PRO	026	004	Do not respond to the foolish according to his folly, lest you become like him.
020	PRO	026	005	Respond to the foolish according to his folly, lest he imagine himself to be wise.
020	PRO	026	006	Whoever sends words by a foolish messenger has lame feet and drinks iniquity.
020	PRO	026	007	In the manner of a lame man who has beautiful legs to no purpose, so also is a parable unfit for the mouth of the foolish.
020	PRO	026	008	Just like one who casts a stone into the pile of Mercury, so also is he who gives honor to the foolish.
020	PRO	026	009	In the manner of a thorn, if it were to spring up from the hand of a drunkard, so also is a parable in the mouth of the foolish.
020	PRO	026	010	Judgment determines cases. And whoever imposes silence on the foolish mitigates anger.
020	PRO	026	011	Like a dog that returns to his vomit, so also is the imprudent who repeats his foolishness.
020	PRO	026	012	Have you seen a man who seems wise to himself? There will be greater hope held for the unwise than for him.
020	PRO	026	013	The lazy one says, “There is a lion along the way, and a lioness in the roads.”
020	PRO	026	014	Just as a door turns upon its hinges, so also does the lazy one turn upon his bed.
020	PRO	026	015	The lazy one conceals his hand under his arms, and it is a labor for him to move it to his mouth.
020	PRO	026	016	The lazy one seems wiser to himself than seven men speaking judgments.
020	PRO	026	017	Just like one who takes hold of a dog by the ears, so also is he who crosses impatiently and meddles in the quarrels of another.
020	PRO	026	018	Just as he is guilty who let loose the arrows and the lances unto death,
020	PRO	026	019	so also is the man who harms his friend by deceitfulness. And when he has been apprehended, he says, “I did it jokingly.”
020	PRO	026	020	When the wood fails, the fire will be extinguished. And when the gossiper is taken away, conflicts will be quelled.
020	PRO	026	021	Just as charcoals are to burning coals, and wood is to fire, so also is an angry man who stirs up quarrels.
020	PRO	026	022	The words of a whisperer seem simple, but they penetrate to the innermost parts of the self.
020	PRO	026	023	In the same manner as an earthen vessel, if it were adorned with impure silver, conceited lips are allied with a wicked heart.
020	PRO	026	024	An enemy is known by his lips, though it is from his heart that he draws out deceit.
020	PRO	026	025	When he will have lowered his voice, do not believe him, for there are seven vices in his heart.
020	PRO	026	026	Whoever covers hatred with deceit, his malice shall be revealed in the assembly.
020	PRO	026	027	Whoever digs a pit will fall into it. And whoever rolls a stone, it will roll back to him.
020	PRO	026	028	A false tongue does not love truth. And a slippery mouth works ruin.
020	PRO	027	001	Do not boast about tomorrow, for you do not know what the future day may bring.
020	PRO	027	002	Let another praise you, and not your own mouth: an outsider, and not your own lips.
020	PRO	027	003	A stone is weighty, and sand is burdensome; but the wrath of the foolish is heavier than both.
020	PRO	027	004	Anger holds no mercy, nor does fury when it erupts. And who can bear the assault of one who has been provoked?
020	PRO	027	005	An open rebuke is better than hidden love.
020	PRO	027	006	The wounds of a loved one are better than the deceitful kisses of a hateful one.
020	PRO	027	007	A sated soul will trample the honeycomb. And a hungry soul will accept even bitter in place of sweet.
020	PRO	027	008	Just like a bird migrating from her nest, so also is a man who abandons his place.
020	PRO	027	009	Ointment and various perfumes delight the heart. And the good advice of a friend is sweet to the soul.
020	PRO	027	010	Do not dismiss your friend or your father’s friend. And do not enter your brother’s house in the day of your affliction. A close neighbor is better than a distant brother.
020	PRO	027	011	My son, study wisdom, and rejoice my heart, so that you may be able to respond to the one who reproaches.
020	PRO	027	012	The discerning man, seeing evil, hides himself. The little ones, continuing on, sustain losses.
020	PRO	027	013	Take away the garment of him who has vouched for an outsider. And take a pledge from him on behalf of foreigners.
020	PRO	027	014	Whoever blesses his neighbor with a grand voice, rising in the night, shall be like one who curses.
020	PRO	027	015	A roof leaking on a cold day, and an argumentative woman, are comparable.
020	PRO	027	016	He who would restrain her, he is like one who would grasp the wind, or who would gather together oil with his right hand.
020	PRO	027	017	Iron sharpens iron, and a man sharpens the countenance of his friend.
020	PRO	027	018	Whoever maintains the fig tree shall eat its fruit. And whoever is the keeper of his master shall be glorified.
020	PRO	027	019	In the manner of faces looking into shining water, so are the hearts of men made manifest to the prudent.
020	PRO	027	020	Hell and perdition are never filled; similarly the eyes of men are insatiable.
020	PRO	027	021	In the manner of silver being tested in the refinery, and gold in the furnace, so also is a man tested by the mouth of one who praises. The heart of the iniquitous inquires after evils, but the heart of the righteous inquires after knowledge.
020	PRO	027	022	Even if you were to crush the foolish with a mortar, as when a pestle strikes over pearled barley, his foolishness would not be taken from him.
020	PRO	027	023	Be diligent to know the countenance of your cattle, and consider your own flocks,
020	PRO	027	024	for you will not always hold this power. But a crown shall be awarded from generation to generation.
020	PRO	027	025	The meadows are open, and the green plants have appeared, and the hay has been collected from the mountains.
020	PRO	027	026	Lambs are for your clothing, and goats are for the price of a field.
020	PRO	027	027	Let the milk of goats be sufficient for your food, and for the necessities of your household, and for the provisions of your handmaids.
020	PRO	028	001	The impious flees, though no one pursues. But the just, like a confident lion, shall be without dread.
020	PRO	028	002	Because of the sins of the land, it has many princes. And because of the wisdom of a man, and the knowledge of those things that are said, the life of the leader shall be prolonged.
020	PRO	028	003	A poor man slandering the poor is like a violent rainstorm in advance of a famine.
020	PRO	028	004	Those who abandon the law praise the impious. Those who guard it are inflamed against him.
020	PRO	028	005	Evil men do not intend judgment. But those who inquire after the Lord turn their souls toward all things.
020	PRO	028	006	Better is the pauper walking in his simplicity, than the rich walking in ways of depravity.
020	PRO	028	007	Whoever keeps the law is a wise son. But whoever feeds gluttons brings shame to his father.
020	PRO	028	008	Whoever piles up riches by usury and profit gathers them for him who will give freely to the poor.
020	PRO	028	009	Whoever turns away his ears from listening to the law: his prayer will be detestable.
020	PRO	028	010	Whoever deceives the just in a malicious way will fall into his own perdition. And the simple shall possess his goods.
020	PRO	028	011	The rich one seems wise to himself. But the poor one, being prudent, shall evaluate him.
020	PRO	028	012	In the exultation of the just, there is great glory. When the impious reign, men are brought to ruin.
020	PRO	028	013	Whoever hides his crimes will not be guided. But whoever will have confessed and abandoned them shall overtake mercy.
020	PRO	028	014	Blessed is the man who is ever fearful. Yet truly, whoever is hardened in mind will fall into evil.
020	PRO	028	015	An impious leader over a poor people is like a roaring lion and a hungry bear.
020	PRO	028	016	A leader destitute of prudence will oppress many through false accusations. But whoever hates avarice shall prolong his days.
020	PRO	028	017	A man who slanders the blood of a life, even if he flees to the pit, no one will tolerate him.
020	PRO	028	018	Whoever walks simply shall be saved. Whoever is perverse in his steps will fall all at once.
020	PRO	028	019	Whoever works his land shall be satisfied with bread. But whoever pursues leisure will be filled with need.
020	PRO	028	020	A faithful man shall be greatly praised. But whoever rushes to become rich will not be innocent.
020	PRO	028	021	Whoever shows favoritism in judgment does not do well; even if it is for a morsel of bread, he forsakes the truth.
020	PRO	028	022	A man who hurries to become rich, and who envies others, does not know that destitution will overwhelm him.
020	PRO	028	023	Whoever corrects a man, afterward he shall find favor with him, more so than he who deceives him with a flattering tongue.
020	PRO	028	024	Whoever takes away anything from his father or mother, and who says, “This is not a sin,” is the associate of a murderer.
020	PRO	028	025	Whoever boasts and enlarges himself stirs up conflicts. Yet truly, whoever trusts in the Lord will be healed.
020	PRO	028	026	Whoever trusts in his own heart is a fool. But whoever treads wisely, the same shall be saved.
020	PRO	028	027	Whoever gives to the poor shall not be in need. Whoever despises his petition will suffer scarcity.
020	PRO	028	028	When the impious rise up, men will hide themselves. When they perish, the just shall be multiplied.
020	PRO	029	001	The man who, with a stiff neck, treats the one who corrects him with contempt will be suddenly overwhelmed to his own destruction, and reason shall not follow him.
020	PRO	029	002	When just men are multiplied, the common people shall rejoice. When the impious take up the leadership, the people shall mourn.
020	PRO	029	003	The man who loves wisdom rejoices his father. But whoever nurtures promiscuous women will lose his substance.
020	PRO	029	004	A just king guides the land. A man of avarice will destroy it.
020	PRO	029	005	A man who speaks to his friend with flattering and feigned words spreads a net for his own feet.
020	PRO	029	006	A snare will entangle the iniquitous when he sins. And the just shall praise and be glad.
020	PRO	029	007	The just knows the case of the poor. The impious is ignorant of knowledge.
020	PRO	029	008	Pestilent men squander a city. Yet truly, the wise avert fury.
020	PRO	029	009	A wise man, if he were to contend with the foolish, whether in anger or in laughter, would find no rest.
020	PRO	029	010	Bloodthirsty men hate the simple one; but the just seek out his soul.
020	PRO	029	011	A foolish one offers everything on his mind. A wise one reserves and defers until later.
020	PRO	029	012	A leader who freely listens to lying words has only impious servants.
020	PRO	029	013	The pauper and the creditor have met one another. The Lord is the illuminator of them both.
020	PRO	029	014	The king who judges the poor in truth, his throne shall be secured in eternity.
020	PRO	029	015	The rod and its correction distribute wisdom. But the child who is left to his own will, brings shame to his mother.
020	PRO	029	016	When the impious are multiplied, crimes will be multiplied. But the just shall see their ruin.
020	PRO	029	017	Teach your son, and he will refresh you, and he will give delight to your soul.
020	PRO	029	018	When prophecy fails, the people will be scattered. Yet truly, whoever guards the law is blessed.
020	PRO	029	019	A servant cannot be taught by words, because he understands what you say, but he disdains to respond.
020	PRO	029	020	Have you seen a man rushing to speak? Foolishness has more hope than his correction.
020	PRO	029	021	Whoever nurtures his servant delicately from childhood, afterwards will find him defiant.
020	PRO	029	022	A short-tempered man provokes quarrels. And whoever is easily angered is more likely to sin.
020	PRO	029	023	Humiliation follows the arrogant. And glory shall uphold the humble in spirit.
020	PRO	029	024	Whoever participates with a thief hates his own soul; for he listens to his oath and does not denounce him.
020	PRO	029	025	Whoever fears man will quickly fall. Whoever hopes in the Lord shall be lifted up.
020	PRO	029	026	Many demand the face of the leader. But the judgment of each one proceeds from the Lord.
020	PRO	029	027	The just abhor an impious man. And the impious abhor those who are on the right way. By keeping the word, the son shall be free from perdition.
020	PRO	030	001	The words of the Gatherer, the son of the Vomiter. The vision that the man spoke. God is with him, and he, being strengthened by God and abiding with him, said:
020	PRO	030	002	“I am the most foolish among men, and the wisdom of men is not with me.
020	PRO	030	003	I have not learned wisdom, and I have not known the knowledge of sanctity.
020	PRO	030	004	Who has ascended to heaven and also descended? Who has grasped the wind in his hands? Who has tied the waters together, as with a garment? Who has raised all the limits of the earth? What is his name, and what is the name of his son, if you know?
020	PRO	030	005	Every word of God is fire-tested. He is a bronze shield to those who hope in him.
020	PRO	030	006	Do not add anything to his words, lest you be reproved and be discovered to be a liar.
020	PRO	030	007	Two things I have asked of you; do not deny them to me before I die.
020	PRO	030	008	Remove, far from me, vanity and lying words. Give me neither begging, nor wealth. Apportion to me only the necessities of my life,
020	PRO	030	009	lest perhaps, being filled, I might be enticed into denial, and say: ‘Who is the Lord?’ Or, being compelled by destitution, I might steal, and then perjure myself in the name of my God.
020	PRO	030	010	Do not accuse a servant to his lord, lest he curse you, and you fall.
020	PRO	030	011	There is a generation which curses their father, and which does not bless their mother.
020	PRO	030	012	There is a generation which seems pure to themselves, and yet they are not even washed from their filthiness.
020	PRO	030	013	There is a generation, whose eyes have been elevated, and their eyelids are lifted on high.
020	PRO	030	014	There is a generation which has swords in place of teeth, and which commands their molars to devour the indigent from the earth and the poor from among men.
020	PRO	030	015	The leech has two daughters, who say, ‘Bring, bring.’ Three things are insatiable, and a fourth never says ‘Enough’:
020	PRO	030	016	Hell, and the mouth of the womb, and a land that is not filled with water. And truly, fire never says, ‘Enough.’
020	PRO	030	017	The eye of one who mocks his father and who despises the childbearing of his mother, let the ravens of the torrent tear it out, and let the sons of the eagles consume it.
020	PRO	030	018	Three things are difficult for me, and about a fourth, I am nearly ignorant:
020	PRO	030	019	the way of an eagle in the sky, the way of a serpent on a rock, the way of a ship in the middle of the sea, and the way of a man in adolescence.
020	PRO	030	020	Such is the way also of an adulterous woman, who eats, and wiping her mouth, says: “I have done no evil.”
020	PRO	030	021	By three things, the earth is moved, and a fourth it is not able to sustain:
020	PRO	030	022	by a slave when he reigns, by the foolish when he has been filled with food,
020	PRO	030	023	by a hateful woman when she has been taken in matrimony, and by a handmaid when she has been heir to her mistress.
020	PRO	030	024	Four things are least upon the earth, and they are wiser than the wise:
020	PRO	030	025	the ants, an infirm people who provide food for themselves at the harvest,
020	PRO	030	026	the rabbit, a sickened people who make their bed upon the rock.
020	PRO	030	027	The locust has no king, but they all depart by their troops.
020	PRO	030	028	The lizard supports itself on hands and dwells in the buildings of kings.
020	PRO	030	029	There are three things that advance well, and a fourth that marches happily on:
020	PRO	030	030	a lion, the strongest of beasts, who fears nothing that he meets,
020	PRO	030	031	a rooster prepared at the loins, likewise a ram, and a king, whom none can resist.
020	PRO	030	032	There is one who has appeared foolish, after he was lifted up on high; for if he had understood, he would have placed his hand over his mouth.
020	PRO	030	033	But whoever strongly squeezes the udder to bring out the milk, presses out butter. And whoever violently blows his nose, brings out blood. And whoever provokes wrath, brings forth discord.”
020	PRO	031	001	The words of king Lamuel. The vision by which his mother instructed him:
020	PRO	031	002	“What, O my beloved? What, O beloved of my womb? What, O beloved of my vows?
020	PRO	031	003	Do not give your substance to women, or your riches to overthrow kings.
020	PRO	031	004	Not to kings, O Lamuel, not to kings give wine. For there are no secrets where drunkenness reigns.
020	PRO	031	005	And perhaps they may drink and forget judgments, and alter the case of the sons of the poor.
020	PRO	031	006	Give strong drink to the grieving, and wine to those who are bitter in soul.
020	PRO	031	007	Let them drink, and forget their needs, and remember their sorrow no more.
020	PRO	031	008	Open your mouth for the mute and for all the cases of the sons who are passing through.
020	PRO	031	009	Open your mouth, declare what is just, and do justice to the indigent and the poor.
020	PRO	031	010	Who shall find a strong woman? Far away, and from the furthest parts, is her price.
020	PRO	031	011	The heart of her husband confides in her, and he will not be deprived of spoils.
020	PRO	031	012	She will repay him with good, and not evil, all the days of her life.
020	PRO	031	013	She has sought wool and flax, and she has worked these by the counsel of her hands.
020	PRO	031	014	She has become like a merchant’s ship, bringing her bread from far away.
020	PRO	031	015	And she has risen in the night, and given a prey to her household, and provisions to her maids.
020	PRO	031	016	She has considered a field and bought it. From the fruit of her own hands, she has planted a vineyard.
020	PRO	031	017	She has wrapped her waist with fortitude, and she has strengthened her arm.
020	PRO	031	018	She has tasted and seen that her tasks are good; her lamp shall not be extinguished at night.
020	PRO	031	019	She has put her hand to strong things, and her fingers have taken hold of the spindle.
020	PRO	031	020	She has opened her hand to the needy, and she has extended her hands to the poor.
020	PRO	031	021	She shall not fear, in the cold of snow, for her household. For all those of her household have been clothed two-fold.
020	PRO	031	022	She has made embroidered clothing for herself. Fine linen and purple is her garment.
020	PRO	031	023	Her husband is noble at the gates, when he sits among the senators of the land.
020	PRO	031	024	She has made finely woven cloth and sold it, and she has delivered a waistband to the Canaanite.
020	PRO	031	025	Strength and elegance are her clothing, and she will laugh in the final days.
020	PRO	031	026	She has opened her mouth to wisdom, and the law of clemency is on her tongue.
020	PRO	031	027	She has considered the paths of her household, and she has not eaten her bread in idleness.
020	PRO	031	028	Her sons rose up and predicted great happiness; her husband rose up and praised her.
020	PRO	031	029	Many daughters have gathered together riches; you have surpassed them all.
020	PRO	031	030	Charm is false, and beauty is vain. The woman who fears the Lord, the same shall be praised.
020	PRO	031	031	Give to her from the fruit of her own hands. And let her works praise her at the gates.
#
# BOOK	021	ECC	Ecclesiastes	Ecclesiastes
021	ECC	001	001	The words of Ecclesiastes, the son of David, the king of Jerusalem.
021	ECC	001	002	Ecclesiastes said: Vanity of vanities! Vanity of vanities, and all is vanity!
021	ECC	001	003	What more does a man have from all his labor, as he labors under the sun?
021	ECC	001	004	A generation passes away, and a generation arrives. But the earth stands forever.
021	ECC	001	005	The sun rises and sets; it returns to its place, and from there, being born again,
021	ECC	001	006	it circles through the south, and arcs toward the north. The spirit continues on, illuminating everything in its circuit, and turning again in its cycle.
021	ECC	001	007	All rivers enter into the sea, and the sea does not overflow. To the place from which the rivers go out, they return, so that they may flow again.
021	ECC	001	008	Such things are difficult; man is not able to explain them with words. The eye is not satisfied by seeing, nor is the ear fulfilled by hearing.
021	ECC	001	009	What is it that has existed? The same shall exist in the future. What is it that has been done? The same shall continue to be done.
021	ECC	001	010	There is nothing new under the sun. Neither is anyone able to say: “Behold, this is new!” For it has already been brought forth in the ages that were before us.
021	ECC	001	011	There is no remembrance of the former things. Indeed, neither shall there be any record of past things in the future, for those who will exist at the very end.
021	ECC	001	012	I, Ecclesiastes, was king of Israel at Jerusalem.
021	ECC	001	013	And I was determined in my mind to seek and to investigate wisely, concerning all that is done under the sun. God has given this very difficult task to the sons of men, so that they may be occupied by it.
021	ECC	001	014	I have seen all that is done under the sun, and behold: all is emptiness and an affliction of the spirit.
021	ECC	001	015	The perverse are unwilling to be corrected, and the number of the foolish is boundless.
021	ECC	001	016	I have spoken in my heart, saying: “Behold, I have achieved greatness, and I have surpassed all the wise who were before me in Jerusalem.” And my mind has contemplated many things wisely, and I have learned.
021	ECC	001	017	And I have dedicated my heart, so that I may know prudence and doctrine, and also error and foolishness. Yet I recognize that, in these things also, there is hardship, and affliction of the spirit.
021	ECC	001	018	Because of this, with much wisdom there is also much anger. And whoever adds knowledge, also adds hardship.
021	ECC	002	001	I said in my heart: “I will go forth and overflow with delights, and I will enjoy good things.” And I saw that this, too, is emptiness.
021	ECC	002	002	Laughter, I considered an error. And to rejoicing, I said: “Why are you being deceived, to no purpose?”
021	ECC	002	003	I decided in my heart to withdraw my flesh from wine, so that I might bring my mind to wisdom, and turn away from foolishness, until I see what is useful for the sons of men, and what they ought to do under the sun, during the number of the days of their life.
021	ECC	002	004	I magnified my works. I built houses for myself, and I planted vineyards.
021	ECC	002	005	I made gardens and orchards. And I planted them with trees of every kind.
021	ECC	002	006	And I dug out fishponds of water, so that I might irrigate the forest of growing trees.
021	ECC	002	007	I obtained men and women servants, and I had a great family, as well as herds of cattle and great flocks of sheep, beyond all who were before me in Jerusalem.
021	ECC	002	008	I amassed for myself silver and gold, and the wealth of kings and governors. I chose men and women singers, and the delights of the sons of men, bowls and pitchers for the purpose of pouring wine.
021	ECC	002	009	And I surpassed in opulence all who were before me in Jerusalem. My wisdom also persevered with me.
021	ECC	002	010	And all that my eyes desired, I did not refuse them. Neither did I prohibit my heart from enjoying every pleasure, and from amusing itself in the things that I had prepared. And I regarded this as my share, as if I were making use of my own labors.
021	ECC	002	011	But when I turned myself toward all the works that my hands had made, and to the labors in which I had perspired to no purpose, I saw emptiness and affliction of the soul in all things, and that nothing is permanent under the sun.
021	ECC	002	012	I continued on, so as to contemplate wisdom, as well as error and foolishness. “What is man,” I said, “that he would be able to follow his Maker, the King?”
021	ECC	002	013	And I saw that wisdom surpasses foolishness, so much so that they differ as much as light from darkness.
021	ECC	002	014	The eyes of a wise man are in his head. A foolish man walks in darkness. Yet I learned that one would pass away like the other.
021	ECC	002	015	And I said in my heart: “If the death of both the foolish and myself will be one, how does it benefit me, if I have given myself more thoroughly to the work of wisdom?” And as I was speaking within my own mind, I perceived that this, too, is emptiness.
021	ECC	002	016	For there will not be a remembrance in perpetuity of the wise, nor of the foolish. And the future times will cover everything together, with oblivion. The learned die in a manner similar to the unlearned.
021	ECC	002	017	And, because of this, my life wearied me, since I saw that everything under the sun is evil, and everything is empty and an affliction of the spirit.
021	ECC	002	018	Again, I detested all my efforts, by which I had earnestly labored under the sun, to be taken up by an heir after me,
021	ECC	002	019	though I know not whether he will be wise or foolish. And yet he will have power over my labors, in which I have toiled and been anxious. And is there anything else so empty?
021	ECC	002	020	Therefore, I ceased, and my heart renounced further laboring under the sun.
021	ECC	002	021	For when someone labors in wisdom, and doctrine, and prudence, he leaves behind what he has obtained to one who is idle. So this, too, is emptiness and a great burden.
021	ECC	002	022	For how can a man benefit from all his labor and affliction of spirit, by which he has been tormented under the sun?
021	ECC	002	023	All his days have been filled with sorrows and hardships; neither does he rest his mind, even in the night. And is this not emptiness?
021	ECC	002	024	Is it not better to eat and drink, and to show his soul the good things of his labors? And this is from the hand of God.
021	ECC	002	025	So who will feast and overflow with delights as much as I have?
021	ECC	002	026	God has given, to the man who is good in his sight, wisdom, and knowledge, and rejoicing. But to the sinner, he has given affliction and needless worrying, so as to add, and to gather, and to deliver, to him who has pleased God. But this, too, is emptiness and a hollow worrying of the mind.
021	ECC	003	001	All things have their time, and all things under heaven continue during their interval.
021	ECC	003	002	A time to be born, and a time to die. A time to plant, and a time to pull up what was planted.
021	ECC	003	003	A time to kill, and a time to heal. A time to tear down, and a time to build up.
021	ECC	003	004	A time to weep, and a time to laugh. A time to mourn, and a time to dance.
021	ECC	003	005	A time to scatter stones, and a time to gather. A time to embrace, and a time to be far from embraces.
021	ECC	003	006	A time to gain, and a time to lose. A time to keep, and a time to cast away.
021	ECC	003	007	A time to rend, and a time to sew. A time to be silent, and a time to speak.
021	ECC	003	008	A time of love, and a time of hatred. A time of war, and a time of peace.
021	ECC	003	009	What more does a man have from his labor?
021	ECC	003	010	I have seen the affliction that God has given to the sons of men, in order that they may be occupied by it.
021	ECC	003	011	He has made all things good in their time, and he has handed over the world to their disputes, so that man may not discover the work which God made from the beginning, even until the end.
021	ECC	003	012	And I realize that there is nothing better than to rejoice, and to do well in this life.
021	ECC	003	013	For this is a gift from God: when each man eats and drinks, and sees the good results of his labor.
021	ECC	003	014	I have learned that all the works which God has made continue on, in perpetuity. We are not able to add anything, nor to take anything away, from those things which God has made in order that he may be feared.
021	ECC	003	015	What has been made, the same continues. What is in the future, has already existed. And God restores what has passed away.
021	ECC	003	016	I saw under the sun: instead of judgment, impiety, and instead of justice, iniquity.
021	ECC	003	017	And I said in my heart: “God will judge the just and the impious, and then the time for each matter shall be.”
021	ECC	003	018	I said in my heart, about the sons of men, that God would test them, and reveal them to be like wild animals.
021	ECC	003	019	For this reason, the passing away of man and of beasts is one, and the condition of both is equal. For as a man dies, so also do they die. All things breathe similarly, and man has nothing more than beast; for all these are subject to vanity.
021	ECC	003	020	And all things continue on to one place; for from the earth they were made, and unto the earth they shall return together.
021	ECC	003	021	Who knows if the spirit of the sons of Adam ascend upward, and if the spirit of the beasts descend downward?
021	ECC	003	022	And I have discovered nothing to be better than for a man to rejoice in his work: for this is his portion. And who shall add to him, so that he may know the things that will occur after him?
021	ECC	004	001	I turned myself to other things, and I saw the false accusations which are carried out under the sun, and the tears of the innocent, and that there was no one to console them; and that they were not able to withstand their violence, being destitute of all help.
021	ECC	004	002	And so, I praised the dead more than the living.
021	ECC	004	003	And happier than both of these, I judged him to be, who has not yet been born, and who has not yet seen the evils which are done under the sun.
021	ECC	004	004	Again, I was contemplating all the labors of men. And I took notice that their endeavors are open to the envy of their neighbor. And so, in this, too, there is emptiness and superfluous anxiety.
021	ECC	004	005	The foolish man folds his hands together, and he consumes his own flesh, saying:
021	ECC	004	006	“A handful with rest is better than both hands filled with labors and with affliction of the soul.”
021	ECC	004	007	While considering this, I also discovered another vanity under the sun.
021	ECC	004	008	He is one, and he does not have a second: no son, no brother. And yet he does not cease to labor, nor are his eyes satisfied with wealth, nor does he reflect, saying: “For whom do I labor and cheat my soul of good things?” In this, too, is emptiness and a most burdensome affliction.
021	ECC	004	009	Therefore, it is better for two to be together, than for one to be alone. For they have the advantage of their companionship.
021	ECC	004	010	If one falls, he shall be supported by the other. Woe to one who is alone. For when he falls, he has no one to lift him up.
021	ECC	004	011	And if two are sleeping, they warm one another. How can one person alone be warmed?
021	ECC	004	012	And if a man can prevail against one, two may withstand him, and a threefold cord is broken with difficulty.
021	ECC	004	013	Better is a boy, poor and wise, than a king, old and foolish, who does not know to look ahead for the sake of posterity.
021	ECC	004	014	For sometimes, one goes forth from prison and chains, to a kingdom, while another, born to kingly power, is consumed by need.
021	ECC	004	015	I saw all the living who are walking under the sun, and I saw the next generation, who shall rise up in their places.
021	ECC	004	016	The number of people, out of all who existed before these, is boundless. And those who will exist afterwards shall not rejoice in them. But this, too, is emptiness and an affliction of the spirit.
021	ECC	005	001	Guard your foot, when you step into the house of God, and draw near, so that you may listen. For obedience is much better than the sacrifices of the foolish, who do not know the evil that they are doing.
021	ECC	005	002	You should not speak anything rashly, nor should your heart be hasty to present a word before God. For God is in heaven, and you are on earth. For this reason, let your words be few.
021	ECC	005	003	Dreams follow many worries, and in many words foolishness will be found.
021	ECC	005	004	If you have vowed anything to God, you should not delay to repay it. And whatever you have vowed, render it. But an unfaithful and foolish promise displeases him.
021	ECC	005	005	And it is much better not to make a vow, than, after a vow, not to fulfill what was promised.
021	ECC	005	006	You should not use your mouth so as to cause your flesh to sin. And you should not say, in the sight of an Angel, “There is no Providence.” For God, being angry at your words, may scatter all the works of your hands.
021	ECC	005	007	Where there are many dreams, there are many vanities and innumerable words. Yet truly, you must fear God.
021	ECC	005	008	If you see false accusations against the indigent, and violent judgments, and subverted justice in the government, do not be surprised over this situation. For those in high places have others who are higher, and there are still others, more eminent, over these.
021	ECC	005	009	But finally, there is the King who rules over the entire earth, which is subject to him.
021	ECC	005	010	A greedy man will not be satisfied by money. And whoever loves wealth will reap no fruit from it. Therefore, this, too, is emptiness.
021	ECC	005	011	Where there are many riches, there will also be many to consume these things. And how does it benefit the one who possesses, except that he discerns the wealth with his own eyes?
021	ECC	005	012	Sleep is sweet to one who works, whether he consumes little or much. But the satiation of a wealthy man will not permit him to sleep.
021	ECC	005	013	There is even another most burdensome infirmity, which I have seen under the sun: wealth kept to the harm of the owner.
021	ECC	005	014	For they are lost in a most grievous affliction. He has produced a son, who will be in the utmost destitution.
021	ECC	005	015	Just as he went forth naked from his mother’s womb, so shall he return, and he shall take nothing with him from his labors.
021	ECC	005	016	It is an utterly miserable infirmity that, in the same manner as he has arrived, so shall he return. How then does it benefit him, since he has labored for the wind?
021	ECC	005	017	All the days of his life he consumes: in darkness, and with many worries, and in distress as well as sadness.
021	ECC	005	018	And so, this has seemed good to me: that a person should eat and drink, and should enjoy the fruits of his labor, in which he has toiled under the sun, for the number of the days of his life that God has given him. For this is his portion.
021	ECC	005	019	And this is a gift from God: that every man to whom God has given wealth and resources, and to whom he has granted the ability to consume these, may enjoy his portion, and may find joy in his labors.
021	ECC	005	020	And then he will not fully remember the days of his life, because God occupies his heart with delights.
021	ECC	006	001	There is also another evil, which I have seen under the sun, and, indeed, it is frequent among men.
021	ECC	006	002	It is a man to whom God has given wealth, and resources, and honor; and out of all that he desires, nothing is lacking to his life; yet God does not grant him the ability to consume these things, but instead a man who is a stranger will devour them. This is emptiness and a great misfortune.
021	ECC	006	003	If a man were to produce one hundred children, and to live for many years, and to attain to an age of many days, and if his soul were to make no use of the goods of his resources, and if he were lacking even a burial: concerning such a man, I declare that a miscarried child is better than he.
021	ECC	006	004	For he arrives without a purpose and he continues on into darkness, and his name shall be wiped away, into oblivion.
021	ECC	006	005	He has not seen the sun, nor recognized the difference between good and evil.
021	ECC	006	006	Even if he were to live for two thousand years, and yet not thoroughly enjoy what is good, does not each one hurry on to the same place?
021	ECC	006	007	Every labor of man is for his mouth, but his soul will not be filled.
021	ECC	006	008	What do the wise have which is more than the foolish? And what does the pauper have, except to continue on to that place, where there is life?
021	ECC	006	009	It is better to see what you desire, than to desire what you cannot know. But this, too, is emptiness and a presumption of spirit.
021	ECC	006	010	Whoever shall be in the future, his name has already been called. And it is known that he is a man and that he is not able to contend in judgment against one who is stronger than himself.
021	ECC	006	011	There are many words, and many of these, in disputes, hold much emptiness.
021	ECC	006	012	Why is it necessary for a man to seek things that are greater than himself, when he does not know what is advantageous for himself in his life, during the number of the days of his sojourn, and while time passes by like a shadow? Or who will be able to tell him what will be in the future after him under the sun?
021	ECC	007	001	A good name is better than precious ointments, and a day of death is better than a day of birth.
021	ECC	007	002	It is better to go to a house of mourning, than to a house of feasting. For in the former, we are admonished about the end of all things, so that the living consider what may be in the future.
021	ECC	007	003	Anger is better than laughter. For through the sadness of the countenance, the soul of one who offends may be corrected.
021	ECC	007	004	The heart of the wise is a place of mourning, and the heart of the foolish is a place of rejoicing.
021	ECC	007	005	It is better to be corrected by a wise man, than to be deceived by the false praise of the foolish.
021	ECC	007	006	For, like the crackling of thorns burning under a pot, so is the laughter of the foolish. But this, too, is emptiness.
021	ECC	007	007	A false accusation troubles the wise man and saps the strength of his heart.
021	ECC	007	008	The end of a speech is better than the beginning. Patience is better than arrogance.
021	ECC	007	009	Do not be quickly moved to anger. For anger resides in the sinews of the foolish.
021	ECC	007	010	You should not say: “What do you think is the reason that the former times were better than they are now?” For this type of question is foolish.
021	ECC	007	011	Wisdom with riches is more useful and more advantageous, for those who see the sun.
021	ECC	007	012	For as wisdom protects, so also does money protect. But learning and wisdom have this much more: that they grant life to one who possesses them.
021	ECC	007	013	Consider the works of God, that no one is able to correct whomever he has despised.
021	ECC	007	014	In good times, enjoy good things, but beware of an evil time. For just as God has established the one, so also the other, in order that man may not find any just complaint against him.
021	ECC	007	015	I also saw this, in the days of my vanity: a just man perishing in his justice, and an impious man living a long time in his malice.
021	ECC	007	016	Do not try to be overly just, and do not try to be more wise than is necessary, lest you become stupid.
021	ECC	007	017	Do not act with great impiety, and do not choose to be foolish, lest you die before your time.
021	ECC	007	018	It is good for you to support a just man. Furthermore, you should not withdraw your hand from him, for whoever fears God, neglects nothing.
021	ECC	007	019	Wisdom has strengthened the wise more than ten princes of a city.
021	ECC	007	020	But there is no just man on earth, who does good and does not sin.
021	ECC	007	021	So then, do not attach your heart to every word that is spoken, lest perhaps you may hear your servant speaking ill of you.
021	ECC	007	022	For your conscience knows that you, too, have repeatedly spoken evil of others.
021	ECC	007	023	I have tested everything in wisdom. I have said: “I will be wise.” And wisdom withdrew farther from me,
021	ECC	007	024	so much more than it was before. Wisdom is very profound, so who shall reveal her?
021	ECC	007	025	I have examined all things in my soul, so that I may know, and consider, and seek out wisdom and reason, and so that I may recognize the impiety of the foolish, and the error of the imprudent.
021	ECC	007	026	And I have discovered a woman more bitter than death: she who is like the snare of a hunter, and whose heart is like a net, and whose hands are like chains. Whoever pleases God shall flee from her. But whoever is a sinner shall be seized by her.
021	ECC	007	027	Behold, Ecclesiastes said, I have discovered these things, one after another, in order that I might discover the explanation
021	ECC	007	028	which my soul still seeks and has not found. One man among a thousand, I have found; a woman among them all, I have not found.
021	ECC	007	029	This alone have I discovered: that God made man righteous, and yet he has adulterated himself with innumerable questions. Who is so great as the wise? And who has understood the meaning of the word?
021	ECC	008	001	The wisdom of a man shines in his countenance, and even the expression of a most powerful man will change.
021	ECC	008	002	I heed the mouth of the king, and the commandment of an oath to God.
021	ECC	008	003	You should not hastily withdraw from his presence, nor should you remain in an evil work. For all that pleases him, he will do.
021	ECC	008	004	And his word is filled with authority. Neither is anyone able to say to him: “Why are you acting this way?”
021	ECC	008	005	Whoever keeps the commandment will not experience evil. The heart of a wise man understands the time to respond.
021	ECC	008	006	For every matter, there is a time and an opportunity, as well as many difficulties, for man.
021	ECC	008	007	For he is ignorant of the past, and he is able to know nothing of the future by means of a messenger.
021	ECC	008	008	It is not in the power of a man to prohibit the spirit, nor does he have authority over the day of death, nor is he permitted to rest when war breaks out, and neither will impiety save the impious.
021	ECC	008	009	I have considered all these things, and I have applied my heart to all the works which are being done under the sun. Sometimes one man rules over another to his own harm.
021	ECC	008	010	I have seen the impious buried. These same, while they were still living, were in the holy place, and they were praised in the city as workers of justice. But this, too, is emptiness.
021	ECC	008	011	For the sons of men perpetrate evils without any fear, because judgment is not pronounced quickly against the evil.
021	ECC	008	012	But although a sinner may do evil of himself one hundred times, and by patience still endure, I realize that it will be well with those who fear God, who revere his face.
021	ECC	008	013	So, may it not go well with the impious, and may his days not be prolonged. And let those who do not fear the face of the Lord pass away like a shadow.
021	ECC	008	014	There is also another vanity, which is done upon the earth. There are the just, to whom evils happen, as though they had done the works of the impious. And there are the impious, who are very secure, as though they possess the deeds of the just. But this, too, I judge to be a very great vanity.
021	ECC	008	015	And so, I praised rejoicing, because there was no good for a man under the sun, except to eat and drink, and to be cheerful, and because he may take nothing with him from his labor in the days of his life, which God has given to him under the sun.
021	ECC	008	016	And I applied my heart, so that I might know wisdom, and so that I might understand a disturbance that turns upon the earth: it is a man, who takes no sleep with his eyes, day and night.
021	ECC	008	017	And I understood that man is able to find no explanation for all those works of God which are done under the sun. And so, the more that he labors to seek, so much the less does he find. Yes, even if a wise man were to claim that he knows, he would not be able to discover it.
021	ECC	009	001	I have drawn all these things through my heart, so that I might carefully understand. There are just men as well as wise men, and their works are in the hand of God. And yet a man does not know so much as whether he is worthy of love or of hatred.
021	ECC	009	002	But all things in the future remain uncertain, because all things happen equally to the just and to the impious, to the good and to the bad, to the pure and to the impure, to those who offer sacrifices and to those who despise sacrifices. As the good are, so also are sinners. As those who commit perjury are, so also are those who swear to the truth.
021	ECC	009	003	This is a very great burden among all things that are done under the sun: that the same things happen to everyone. And when the hearts of the sons of men are filled with malice and contempt in their lives, afterwards they shall be dragged down to hell.
021	ECC	009	004	There is no one who lives forever, or who even has confidence in this regard. A living dog is better than a dead lion.
021	ECC	009	005	For the living know that they themselves will die, yet truly the dead know nothing anymore, nor do they have any recompense. For the memory of them is forgotten.
021	ECC	009	006	Likewise, love and hatred and envy have all perished together, nor have they any place in this age and in the work which is done under the sun.
021	ECC	009	007	So then, go and eat your bread with rejoicing, and drink your wine with gladness. For your works are pleasing to God.
021	ECC	009	008	Let your garments be white at all times, and let not oil be absent from your head.
021	ECC	009	009	Enjoy life with the wife whom you love, all the days of your uncertain life which have been given to you under the sun, during all the time of your vanity. For this is your portion in life and in your labor, with which you labor under the sun.
021	ECC	009	010	Whatever your hand is able to do, do it earnestly. For neither work, nor reason, nor wisdom, nor knowledge will exist in death, toward which you are hurrying.
021	ECC	009	011	I turned myself toward another thing, and I saw that under the sun, the race is not to the swift, nor the battle to the strong, nor bread to the wise, nor wealth to the learned, nor grace to the skillful: but there is a time and an end for all these things.
021	ECC	009	012	Man does not know his own end. But, just as fish are caught with a hook, and birds are captured with a snare, so are men seized in the evil time, when it will suddenly overwhelm them.
021	ECC	009	013	This wisdom, likewise, I have seen under the sun, and I have examined it intensely.
021	ECC	009	014	There was a small city, with a few men in it. There came against it a great king, who surrounded it, and built fortifications all around it, and the blockade was completed.
021	ECC	009	015	And there was found within it, a poor and wise man, and he freed the city through his wisdom, and nothing was recorded afterward of that poor man.
021	ECC	009	016	And so, I declared that wisdom is better than strength. But how is it, then, that the wisdom of the poor man is treated with contempt, and his words are not heeded?
021	ECC	009	017	The words of the wise are heard in silence, more so than the outcry of a prince among the foolish.
021	ECC	009	018	Wisdom is better than weapons of war. And whoever offends in one thing, shall lose many good things.
021	ECC	010	001	Dying flies ruin the sweetness of the ointment. Wisdom and glory is more precious than a brief and limited foolishness.
021	ECC	010	002	The heart of a wise man is in his right hand, and the heart of a foolish man is in his left hand.
021	ECC	010	003	Moreover, as a foolish man is walking along the way, even though he himself is unwise, he considers everyone to be foolish.
021	ECC	010	004	If the spirit of one who holds authority rises over you, do not leave your place, because attentiveness will cause the greatest sins to cease.
021	ECC	010	005	There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, proceeding from the presence of a prince, as if by mistake:
021	ECC	010	006	a foolish man appointed to a high dignity, and the rich sitting beneath him.
021	ECC	010	007	I have seen servants on horses, and princes walking on the ground like servants.
021	ECC	010	008	Whoever digs a pit will fall into it. And whoever tears apart a hedge, a snake will bite him.
021	ECC	010	009	Whoever carries away stones will be harmed by them. And whoever cuts down trees will be wounded by them.
021	ECC	010	010	If the iron is dull, and if it was not that way before, but has been made dull by much labor, then it will be sharpened. And wisdom will follow after diligence.
021	ECC	010	011	Whoever slanders in secret is nothing less than a snake that bites silently.
021	ECC	010	012	Words from the mouth of a wise man are graceful, but the lips of a foolish man will throw him down with violence.
021	ECC	010	013	At the beginning of his words is foolishness, and at the end of his talk is a most grievous error.
021	ECC	010	014	The fool multiplies his words. A man does not know what has been before him, and who is able to reveal to him what will be in the future after him?
021	ECC	010	015	The hardship of the foolish will afflict those who do not know to go into the city.
021	ECC	010	016	Woe to you, the land whose king is a boy, and whose princes consume in the morning.
021	ECC	010	017	Blessed is the land whose king is noble, and whose princes eat at the proper time, for refreshment and not for self-indulgence.
021	ECC	010	018	By laziness, a framework shall be brought down, and by the weakness of hands, a house shall collapse through.
021	ECC	010	019	While laughing, they make bread and wine, so that the living may feast. And all things are obedient to money.
021	ECC	010	020	You should not slander the king, even in your thoughts, and you should not speak evil of a wealthy man, even in your private chamber. For even the birds of the air will carry your voice, and whatever has wings will announce your opinion.
021	ECC	011	001	Cast your bread over running waters. For, after a long time, you shall find it again.
021	ECC	011	002	Give a portion to seven, and indeed even to eight. For you do not know what evil may be upon the earth in the future.
021	ECC	011	003	If the clouds have been filled, they will pour forth rain upon the earth. If a tree falls to the south, or to the north, or to whatever direction it may fall, there it shall remain.
021	ECC	011	004	Whoever heeds the wind will not sow. And whoever considers the clouds will never reap.
021	ECC	011	005	In the same manner that you do not know the way of the spirit, nor the way that bones are joined together in the womb of a pregnant woman, so you do not know the works of God, who is the Maker of all.
021	ECC	011	006	In the morning, sow your seed, and in the evening, do not let your hand cease. For you do not know which of these may rise up, the one or the other. But if both rise up together, so much the better.
021	ECC	011	007	Light is pleasant, and it is delightful for the eyes to see the sun.
021	ECC	011	008	If a man lives for many years, and if he has rejoiced in all of these, he must remember the many days of the dark times, which, when they will have arrived, will accuse the past of vanity.
021	ECC	011	009	So then, rejoice, O young man, in your youth, and let your heart remain in what is good during the days of your youth. And walk in the ways of your heart, and with the perception of your eyes. And know that, concerning all these things, God will bring you to judgment.
021	ECC	011	010	Remove anger from your heart, and set aside evil from your flesh. For youth and pleasure are empty.
021	ECC	012	001	Remember your Creator in the days of your youth, before the time of affliction arrives and the years draw near, about which you will say, “These do not please me.”
021	ECC	012	002	Before the sun, and the light, and the moon, and the stars are darkened and the clouds return after the rain,
021	ECC	012	003	when the guardians of the house will tremble, and the strongest men will waver, and those who grind grain will be idle, except for a small number, and those who look through the keyholes will be darkened.
021	ECC	012	004	And they will close the doors to the street, when the voice of he who grinds the grain will be humbled, and they will be disturbed at the sound of a flying thing, and all the daughters of song shall become deaf.
021	ECC	012	005	Likewise, they will fear the things above them, and they will dread the way. The almond tree will flourish; the locust will be fattened; and the caper plant will be scattered, because man shall go into the house of his eternity, and the mourners shall wander around in the street.
021	ECC	012	006	Before the silver cord is broken, and the golden band pulls away, and the pitcher is crushed over the fountain, and the wheel is broken above the cistern,
021	ECC	012	007	and the dust returns to its earth, from which it was, and the spirit returns to God, who granted it.
021	ECC	012	008	Vanity of vanities, said Ecclesiastes, and all is vanity!
021	ECC	012	009	And since Ecclesiastes was very wise, he taught the people, and he described what he had accomplished. And while searching, he composed many parables.
021	ECC	012	010	He sought useful words, and he wrote most righteous words, which were full of truth.
021	ECC	012	011	The words of the wise are like a goad, and like nails deeply fastened, which, through the counsel of teachers, are set forth by one pastor.
021	ECC	012	012	You should require no more than this, my son. For there is no end to the making of many books. And excessive study is an affliction to the flesh.
021	ECC	012	013	Let us all listen together to the end of the discourse. Fear God, and observe his commandments. This is everything for man.
021	ECC	012	014	And so, for all that is done and for each error, God will bring judgment: whether it was good or evil.
