# BOOK	023	ISA	Isaiah	Isaiah
023	ISA	001	001	The vision of Isaiah, the son of Amoz, which he saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem, in the days of Uzziah, Joatham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah.
023	ISA	001	002	Listen, O heavens, and pay attention, O earth, for the Lord has spoken. I have nurtured and raised children, but they have spurned me.
023	ISA	001	003	An ox knows his owner, and a donkey knows the manger of his lord, but Israel has not known me, and my people have not understood.
023	ISA	001	004	Woe to a sinful nation, a people burdened by iniquity, a wicked offspring, accursed children. They have abandoned the Lord. They have blasphemed the Holy One of Israel. They been taken away backwards.
023	ISA	001	005	For what reason shall I continue to strike you, as you increase transgressions? The entire head is feeble, and the entire heart is grieving.
023	ISA	001	006	From the sole of the foot, even to the top of the head, there is no soundness within. Wounds and bruises and swelling sores: these are not bandaged, nor treated with medicine, nor soothed with oil.
023	ISA	001	007	Your land is desolate. Your cities have been set ablaze. Foreigners devour your countryside in your sight, and it will become desolate, as if devastated by enemies.
023	ISA	001	008	And the daughter of Zion will be left behind, like an arbor in a vineyard, and like a shelter in a cucumber field, and like a city being laid to waste.
023	ISA	001	009	If the Lord of hosts had not bequeathed us offspring, we would have been like Sodom, and we would have been comparable to Gomorrah.
023	ISA	001	010	Listen to the Word of the Lord, you leaders of the people of Sodom. Listen closely to the law of our God, O people of Gomorrah.
023	ISA	001	011	The multitude of your sacrifices, what is that to me, says the Lord? I am full. I do not desire holocausts of rams, nor the fat of fatlings, nor the blood of calves and of lambs and of he-goats.
023	ISA	001	012	When you approach before my sight, who is it that requires these things from your hands, so that you would walk in my courts?
023	ISA	001	013	You should no longer offer sacrifice in vain. Incense is an abomination to me. The new moons and the Sabbaths and the other feast days, I will not receive. Your gatherings are iniquitous.
023	ISA	001	014	My soul hates your days of proclamation and your solemnities. They have become bothersome to me. I labor to endure them.
023	ISA	001	015	And so, when you extend your hands, I will avert my eyes from you. And when you multiply your prayers, I will not heed you. For your hands are full of blood.
023	ISA	001	016	Wash, become clean, take away the evil of your intentions from my eyes. Cease to act perversely.
023	ISA	001	017	Learn to do good. Seek judgment, support the oppressed, judge for the orphan, defend the widow.
023	ISA	001	018	And then approach and accuse me, says the Lord. Then, if your sins are like scarlet, they shall be made white like snow; and if they are red like vermillion, they shall become white like wool.
023	ISA	001	019	If you are willing, and you listen to me, then you will eat the good things of the land.
023	ISA	001	020	But if you are not willing, and you provoke me to anger, then the sword will devour you. For the mouth of the Lord has spoken.
023	ISA	001	021	How has the faithful city, full of judgment, become a harlot? Justice lived in her, but now murderers.
023	ISA	001	022	Your silver has turned into dross. Your wine has been mixed with water.
023	ISA	001	023	Your leaders are unfaithful, the associates of thieves. They all love gifts; they pursue rewards. They do not judge for orphans, and the widow’s case is not brought before them.
023	ISA	001	024	Because of this, the Lord God of hosts, the Strength of Israel, says: Ah! I will be consoled over my enemies, and I will be vindicated from my adversaries.
023	ISA	001	025	And I will turn my hand to you. And I will temper your dross unto purity, and I will take away all your tin.
023	ISA	001	026	And I will restore your judges, so that they will be as before, and your counselors as in times long past. After this, you shall be called the City of the Just, the Faithful City.
023	ISA	001	027	Zion will be redeemed in judgment, and they will lead her back to justice.
023	ISA	001	028	And he shall crush the accursed and sinners together. And those who have abandoned the Lord will be consumed.
023	ISA	001	029	For they shall be confounded because of the idols, to which they have sacrificed. And you shall be ashamed over the gardens that you chose,
023	ISA	001	030	when you were like an oak with falling leaves, and like a garden without water.
023	ISA	001	031	And your strength will be like the embers from stubble, and your work will be like a spark, and both will burn together, and there will be no one to extinguish it.
023	ISA	002	001	The word that Isaiah, the son of Amoz, saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem.
023	ISA	002	002	And in the last days, the mountain of the house of the Lord will be prepared at the summit of the mountains, and it will be exalted above the hills, and all the nations shall flow to it.
023	ISA	002	003	And many peoples will go, and they will say: “Let us approach and ascend to the mountain of the Lord, and to the house of the God of Jacob. And he will teach us his ways, and we will walk in his paths.” For the law will go forth from Zion, and the Word of the Lord from Jerusalem.
023	ISA	002	004	And he will judge the nations, and he will rebuke many peoples. And they shall forge their swords into plowshares, and their spears into sickles. Nation will not lift up sword against nation, neither will they continue to train for battle.
023	ISA	002	005	O house of Jacob, let us approach and walk in the light of the Lord.
023	ISA	002	006	For you have cast aside your people, the house of Jacob, because they have been filled up, as in past times, and because they have had soothsayers as the Philistines have, and because they have joined themselves to foreign servants.
023	ISA	002	007	Their land has been filled with silver and gold. And there is no end to their storehouses.
023	ISA	002	008	And their land has been filled with horses. And their four-horse chariots are innumerable. And their land has been filled with idols. They have adored the work of their hands, which their own fingers have made.
023	ISA	002	009	And man has bowed himself down, and so man has become debased. Therefore, you should not forgive them.
023	ISA	002	010	Enter into the rock, and hide in a ditch in the soil, from the presence of the fear of the Lord, and from the glory of his majesty.
023	ISA	002	011	The lofty eyes of man have been humbled, and the haughtiness of men will be bowed down. Then the Lord alone shall be exalted, in that day.
023	ISA	002	012	For the day of the Lord of hosts will prevail over all the proud and self-exalted, and over all the arrogant, and each one shall be humbled,
023	ISA	002	013	and over all the straight and tall cedars of Lebanon, and over all the oaks of Bashan;
023	ISA	002	014	and over all the lofty mountains, and over all the elevated hills;
023	ISA	002	015	and over every lofty tower, and over every fortified wall;
023	ISA	002	016	and over all the ships of Tarshish, and over all the beauty that may be seen.
023	ISA	002	017	And the loftiness of men will be bowed down, and the haughtiness of men will be brought low. And the Lord alone shall be exalted, in that day.
023	ISA	002	018	And idols will be thoroughly crushed.
