023	ISA	003	018	In that day, the Lord will take away their decorative shoes,
023	ISA	003	019	and the little moons and chains, and the necklaces and bracelets, and the hats,
023	ISA	003	020	and the ornaments for their hair, and the anklets, and the touches of myrrh and little bottles of perfumes, and the earrings,
023	ISA	003	021	and the rings, and the jewels hanging on their foreheads,
023	ISA	003	022	and the continual changes in appearance, and the short skirts, and the fine linens and embroidered cloths,
023	ISA	003	023	and the mirrors, and scarves, and ribbons, and their sparse clothing.
023	ISA	003	024	And in place of a sweet fragrance, there will be stench. And in place of a belt, there will be a rope. And in place of stylish hair, there will be baldness. And in place of a blouse, there will be haircloth.
