023	ISA	005	001	I will sing to my beloved the canticle of my paternal cousin, about his vineyard. A vineyard was made for my beloved, at the horn in the son of oil.
023	ISA	005	002	And he fenced it in, and he picked the stones out of it, and he planted it with the best vines, and he built a tower in the middle of it, and he set up a winepress within it. And he expected it to produce grapes, but it produced wild vines.
023	ISA	005	003	Now then, inhabitants of Jerusalem and men of Judah: judge between me and my vineyard.
023	ISA	005	004	What more should I have done for my vineyard that I did not do for it? Should I not have expected it to produce grapes, though it produced wild vines?
023	ISA	005	005	And now, I will reveal to you what I will do to my vineyard. I will take away its fence, and it will be plundered. I will pull down its wall, and it will be trampled.
023	ISA	005	006	And I will make it desolate. It will not be pruned, and it will not be dug. And briers and thorns will rise up. And I will command the clouds not to rain upon it.
023	ISA	005	007	For the vineyard of the Lord of hosts is the house of Israel. And the man of Judah is his delightful seedling. And I expected that he would do judgment, and behold iniquity, and that he would do justice, and behold an outcry.
023	ISA	005	008	Woe to you who join house to house, and who combine field to field, even to the limits of the place! Do you intend to live alone in the midst of the earth?
023	ISA	005	009	These things are in my ears, says the Lord of hosts. Otherwise, many houses, great and beautiful, will become desolate, without an inhabitant.
023	ISA	005	010	Then ten acres of vineyard will produce one small bottle of wine, and thirty measures of seed will produce three measures of grain.
023	ISA	005	011	Woe to you who rise up in the morning to pursue drunkenness, and to drink even until evening, so as to be inflamed with wine.
023	ISA	005	012	Harp and lyre and timbrel and pipe, as well as wine, are at your feasts. But you do not respect the work of the Lord, nor do you consider the works of his hands.
023	ISA	005	013	Because of this, my people have been led away as captives, for they did not have knowledge, and their nobles have passed away from famine, and their multitudes have dried up from thirst.
023	ISA	005	014	For this reason, Hell has expanded its soul, and has opened its mouth without any limits. And their strong ones, and their people, and their exalted and glorious ones will descend into it.
023	ISA	005	015	And man will be bowed down, and man will be humbled, and the eyes of the exalted will be brought low.
023	ISA	005	016	And the Lord of hosts will be exalted in judgment, and the holy God will be sanctified in justice.
023	ISA	005	017	And the lambs will pasture in proper order, and new arrivals will eat from the deserts turned into fertile lands.
023	ISA	005	018	Woe to you who draw iniquity with cords of vanity, and who draw sin as if with the rope of a cart,
023	ISA	005	019	and who say: “Let him hurry, and let his work arrive soon, so that we may see it. And let the plan of the Holy One of Israel approach and arrive, so that we may know it.”
023	ISA	005	020	Woe to you who call evil good, and good evil; who substitute darkness for light, and light for darkness; who exchange bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!
023	ISA	005	021	Woe to you who are wise in your own eyes, and prudent in your own sight!
023	ISA	005	022	Woe to you who are powerful at drinking wine, who are strong men in contriving inebriation!
023	ISA	005	023	For you justify an impious man in exchange for bribes, and you carry away the justice of a just man from him.
023	ISA	005	024	Because of this, as the tongue of fire devours stubble, and as the heat of a flame burns it completely, so will their root become like glowing embers, and so will their offshoot ascend like dust. For they have cast aside the law of the Lord of hosts, and they have blasphemed the eloquence of the Holy One of Israel.
023	ISA	005	025	For this reason, the fury of the Lord has been enraged against his people, and he has extended his hand over them, and he has struck them. And the mountains were disturbed. And their carcasses became like dung in the midst of the streets. After all this, his fury was not turned away; instead, his hand was still extended.
023	ISA	005	026	And he will lift up a sign to nations far away, and he will whistle to them from the ends of the earth. And behold, they will rush forward speedily.
023	ISA	005	027	There is no one weak or struggling among them. They will not become drowsy, and they will not sleep. Neither will the belt around their waist be loosened, nor the laces of their boots be broken.
023	ISA	005	028	Their arrows are sharp, and all their bows are taut. The hoofs of their horses are like flint, and their wheels are like the force of a tempest.
023	ISA	005	029	Their roaring is like the lion; they will roar like young lions. They will both roar and seize their prey. And they will wrap themselves around it, and there will be no one who can rescue it.
023	ISA	005	030	And in that day, they will make a noise over it, like the sound of the sea. We will gaze out toward the land, and behold, the darkness of the tribulation, and even the light has been darkened by its gloom.
023	ISA	006	001	In the year in which king Uzziah died, I saw the Lord sitting on a throne, sublime and exalted, and the things that were under him filled the temple.
023	ISA	006	002	The Seraphim were standing above the throne. One had six wings, and the other had six wings: with two they were covering his face, and with two they were covering his feet, and with two they were flying.
023	ISA	006	003	And they were crying out to one another, and saying: “Holy, holy, holy is the Lord God of hosts! All the earth is filled with his glory!”
023	ISA	006	004	And the lintels above the hinges were shaken at the voice of the one crying out. And the house was filled with smoke.
023	ISA	006	005	And I said: “Woe to me! For I have remained silent. For I am a man of unclean lips, and I live in the midst of a people having unclean lips, and I have seen with my eyes the King, the Lord of hosts!”
023	ISA	006	006	And one of the Seraphim flew to me, and in his hand was a burning coal, which he had taken with tongs from the altar.
023	ISA	006	007	And he touched my mouth, and he said, “Behold, this has touched your lips, and so your iniquities will be taken away, and your sin will be cleansed.”
023	ISA	006	008	And I heard the voice of the Lord, saying: “Whom shall I send?” and, “Who will go for us?” And I said: “Here I am. Send me.”
023	ISA	006	009	And he said: “Go forth! And you shall say to this people: ‘When you listen, you will hear and not understand. And when you see a vision, you will not comprehend.’
023	ISA	006	010	Blind the heart of this people. Make their ears heavy and close their eyes, lest they see with their eyes, and hear with their ears, and understand with their heart, and be converted, and then I would heal them.”
023	ISA	006	011	And I said, “For how long, O Lord?” And he said, “Until the cities are desolate, without an inhabitant, and the houses are without a man, and the land will be left behind, deserted.”
