023	ISA	053	005	But he himself was wounded because of our iniquities. He was bruised because of our wickedness. The discipline of our peace was upon him. And by his wounds, we are healed.
023	ISA	053	006	We have all gone astray like sheep; each one has turned aside to his own way. And the Lord has placed all our iniquity upon him.
023	ISA	053	007	He was offered up, because it was his own will. And he did not open his mouth. He will be led like a sheep to the slaughter. And he will be mute like a lamb before his shearer. For he will not open his mouth.
023	ISA	053	008	He was lifted up from anguish and judgment. Who will describe his life? For he has been cut off from the land of the living. Because of the wickedness of my people, I have struck him down.
023	ISA	053	009	And he will be given a place with the impious for his burial, and with the rich for his death, though he has done no iniquity, nor was deceit in his mouth.
023	ISA	053	010	But it was the will of the Lord to crush him with infirmity. If he lays down his life because of sin, he will see offspring with long lives, and the will of the Lord will be directed by his hand.
023	ISA	053	011	Because his soul has labored, he will see and be satisfied. By his knowledge, my just servant will himself justify many, and he himself will carry their iniquities.
023	ISA	053	012	Therefore, I will allot to him a great number. And he will divide the spoils of the strong. For he has handed over his life to death, and he was reputed among criminals. And he has taken away the sins of many, and he has prayed for the transgressors.
023	ISA	054	001	Give praise, you who are barren and unable to conceive. Sing praise and make a joyful noise, you who have not given birth. For many are the children of the desolate, more so than of her who has a husband, says the Lord.
023	ISA	054	002	Enlarge the place of your tent and extend the skins of your tabernacles, unsparingly. Lengthen your cords, and strengthen your stakes.
023	ISA	054	003	For you shall extend to the right and to the left. And your offspring shall inherit the nations, and you shall inhabit the desolate cities.
023	ISA	054	004	Do not be afraid! For you will not be confounded, and you will not blush. And you will not be put to shame, because you shall forget the confusion of your youth, and you shall no longer remember the disgrace of your widowhood.
023	ISA	054	005	For the One who made you will rule over you. The Lord of hosts is his name. And your Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel, will be called the God of all the earth.
023	ISA	054	006	For the Lord has called you, like a woman forsaken and mourning in spirit, and like a wife rejected in her youth, said your God.
023	ISA	054	007	For a brief moment, I have forsaken you, and with great pities, I will gather you.
023	ISA	054	008	In a moment of indignation, I have hidden my face from you, for a little while. But with everlasting mercy, I have taken pity on you, said your Redeemer, the Lord.
023	ISA	054	009	For me, it is just as in the days of Noah, to whom I swore that I would no longer bring in the waters of Noah over the earth. Thus have I sworn not to be angry with you, and not to rebuke you.
023	ISA	054	010	For the mountains will be moved, and the hills will tremble. But my mercy will not depart from you, and the covenant of my peace will not be shaken, said the Lord, who has compassion on you.
023	ISA	054	011	O poor little ones, convulsed by the tempest, away from any consolation! Behold, I will set your stones in order, and I will lay your foundation with sapphires,
023	ISA	054	012	and I will make your ramparts out of jasper, and your gates out of sculpted stones, and all your borders out of desirable stones.
023	ISA	054	013	All your children will be taught by the Lord. And great will be the peace of your children.
023	ISA	054	014	And you will be founded in justice. Depart far from oppression, for you will not be afraid. And depart from terror, for it will not approach you.
023	ISA	054	015	Behold, a settler will arrive, who was not with me, a certain new arrival will be joined to you.
023	ISA	054	016	Behold, I created the smith who fans the coals of the fire and produces an object by his work, and I have created the slayer who destroys.
023	ISA	054	017	No object which has been formed to use against you will succeed. And every tongue that resists you in judgment, you shall judge. This is the inheritance of the servants of the Lord, and this is their justice with me, says the Lord.
023	ISA	055	001	All you who thirst, come to the waters. And you who have no money: hurry, buy and eat. Approach, buy wine and milk, without money and without barter.
023	ISA	055	002	Why do you spend money for what is not bread, and expend your labor for what does not satisfy? Listen very closely to me, and eat what is good, and then your soul will be delighted by a full measure.
023	ISA	055	003	Incline your ear and draw near to me. Listen, and your soul will live. And I will make an everlasting covenant with you, by the faithful mercies of David.
