# BOOK	024	JER	Jeremiah	Jeremiah
024	JER	001	001	The words of Jeremiah, the son of Hilkiah of the priests who were in Anathoth in the land of Benjamin.
024	JER	001	002	The word of the Lord, which came to him in the days of Josiah, the son of Amon, king of Judah, in the thirteenth year of his reign,
024	JER	001	003	and which came to him in the days of Jehoiakim, the son of Josiah, king of Judah, even until the completion of the eleventh year of Zedekiah, the son of Josiah, king of Judah, even until the transmigration of Jerusalem in the fifth month.
024	JER	001	004	And the word of the Lord came to me, saying:
024	JER	001	005	“Before I formed you in the womb, I knew you. And before you went forth from the womb, I sanctified you. And I made you a prophet to the nations.”
024	JER	001	006	And I said: “Alas, alas, alas, Lord God! Behold, I do not know how to speak, for I am a boy.”
024	JER	001	007	And the Lord said to me: “Do not choose to say, ‘I am a boy.’ For you shall go forth to everyone to whom I will send you. And you shall speak all that I will command you.
024	JER	001	008	You should not be afraid before their face. For I am with you, so that I may deliver you,” says the Lord.
024	JER	001	009	And the Lord put forth his hand, and he touched my mouth. And the Lord said to me: “Behold, I have placed my words in your mouth.
024	JER	001	010	Behold, today I have appointed you over nations and over kingdoms, so that you may root up, and pull down, and destroy, and scatter, and so that you may build and plant.”
024	JER	001	011	And the word of the Lord came to me, saying, “What do you see, Jeremiah?” And I said, “I see a staff, keeping watch.”
024	JER	001	012	And the Lord said to me: “You have seen well. For I will keep watch over my word, so that I may accomplish it.”
024	JER	001	013	And the word of the Lord came to me a second time, saying, “What do you see?” And I said, “I see a cooking pot upon a fire, and its face is before the face of the north.”
024	JER	001	014	And the Lord said to me: “From the north, an evil will spread over all the inhabitants of the earth.
024	JER	001	015	For behold, I will call together all the close associates of the kingdoms of the north, says the Lord. And they will arrive, and each one of them will place his throne at the entrance to the gates of Jerusalem, and over all its surrounding walls, and over all the cities of Judah.
024	JER	001	016	And I will speak my judgments with them, concerning all the wickedness of those who have forsaken me, and who have offered libations to strange gods, and who have adored the work of their own hands.
024	JER	001	017	Therefore, you should gird your waist, and rise up, and speak to them everything that I instruct you. You should not have dread before their face. For I will cause you to be unafraid of their countenance.
024	JER	001	018	For certainly, this day, I have made you like a fortified city, and an iron pillar, and a brass wall, over all the land, to the kings of Judah, to its leaders, and to the priests, and to the people of the land.
024	JER	001	019	And they will make war against you, but they will not prevail. For I am with you, says the Lord, so that I may free you.”
024	JER	002	001	And the word of the Lord came to me, saying:
024	JER	002	002	“Go, and cry out to the ears of Jerusalem, saying: Thus says the Lord: I have remembered you, taking pity on your youth and on the charity of your betrothal, when you followed me into the desert, into a land which is not sown.
024	JER	002	003	Israel is holy to the Lord, the first of his fruits. All those who devour him commit an offense. Evils will overwhelm them, says the Lord.”
024	JER	002	004	Listen to the word of the Lord, O house of Jacob, and all you families of the house of Israel.
024	JER	002	005	Thus says the Lord: “What iniquity have your fathers found in me, that they would draw far away from me, and would walk after emptiness, and would become empty?
024	JER	002	006	And they have not said: ‘Where is the Lord, who caused us to ascend from the land of Egypt; who led us through the desert, through an uninhabited and impassable land, through a land of drought and of the image of death, through a land in which no one walked and in which no man lived?’
024	JER	002	007	And I led you into the land of Carmel, so that you would eat from its fruit and from its excellence. And having entered it, you defiled my land, and you turned my inheritance into an abomination.
024	JER	002	008	The priests have not said: ‘Where is the Lord?’ And those who held the law did not know me. And the pastors betrayed me. And the prophets prophesied in Baal and followed idols.
024	JER	002	009	Because of this, I will still contend in judgment against you, says the Lord, and I will dispute with your sons.
024	JER	002	010	Cross over to the isles of Kittim, and gaze. And send to Kedar, and consider diligently. And see if anything like this has ever been done.
024	JER	002	011	See if a nation has ever changed their gods, though certainly those are not gods. Yet truly, my people have exchanged their glory for an idol.
024	JER	002	012	Be astonished at this, O heavens, and be utterly desolate, O gates of heaven, says the Lord.
024	JER	002	013	For my people have done two evils. They have forsaken me, the Fountain of living water, and they have dug for themselves cisterns, broken cisterns that are unable to hold water.
024	JER	002	014	Is Israel a servant, or one born into slavery? Then why has he become a prey?
024	JER	002	015	The lions have roared over him, and they have uttered their voice. They have set his land in solitude; his cities have been burned up, and there is no one who lives in them.
024	JER	002	016	Likewise, the sons of Memphis and of Tahpanhes have defiled you, even to the top of the head.
024	JER	002	017	Has this not been done to you because you abandoned the Lord your God, in that time when he was leading you by the way?
024	JER	002	018	And now what do you want from the way of Egypt, but to drink their turbid water? And what do you want from the way of the Assyrians, but to drink the water of their river?
024	JER	002	019	Your own malice will reprove you, and your own apostasy will rebuke you! But know and perceive this: it is an evil and bitter thing for you to forsake the Lord your God, and to be without my fear within you, says the Lord, the God of hosts.
024	JER	002	020	From ancient times, you have broken my yoke; you have torn apart my bonds, and you have said, ‘I will not serve.’ For on every high hill, and under every leafy tree, you have been debased, O harlot.
024	JER	002	021	Yet I planted you as an elect vineyard, with only true seed. Then how have you been turned away from me, toward that which is depraved, O strange vineyard?
024	JER	002	022	Even if you wash yourself with soap, and increase your use of herbal soaps, you are still stained by your iniquity in my sight, says the Lord God.
024	JER	002	023	How can you say: ‘I have not been polluted. I have not walked after Baal?’ Consider your ways in the steep valley. Acknowledge what you have done, so that you may be like a swift runner, following his course.
024	JER	002	024	A wild donkey accustomed to solitude, out of the desire in his soul, caught the scent of his lover. Now nothing will turn him away from her. All those who seek her will not cease. But they will find her in her menstruation.
024	JER	002	025	You should keep your foot from being naked, and your throat from being thirsty. But you have said: ‘I have lost hope. I will not do it. For certainly, I have loved strangers, and I will walk after them.’
024	JER	002	026	In the same way that a thief is confounded when he has been apprehended, so the house of Israel has been confounded, they and their kings, their leaders and priests and prophets.
024	JER	002	027	For they say to a piece of wood, ‘You are my father,’ and to a stone, ‘You have conceived me.’ They have turned their back to me, and not their face. But in the time of their affliction, they will say: ‘Rise up and deliver us.’
024	JER	002	028	Where are your gods that you made for yourselves? Let them rise up and deliver you in the time of your affliction. For certainly, your gods were like the number of your cities, O Judah.
024	JER	002	029	Why do you want to contend against me in judgment? You have all forsaken me, says the Lord.
024	JER	002	030	I have struck your children to no effect; they have not accepted discipline. Your own sword has devoured your prophets. Your generation is like a raging lion.
024	JER	002	031	Consider the word of the Lord. Have I become like a wilderness to Israel, or like a land late to bear fruit? Then why have my people said, ‘We are withdrawing; we will no longer approach you’?
024	JER	002	032	Can a virgin forget her ornament, or a bride the covering across her breast? Yet truly, my people have forgotten me, for innumerable days.
