024	JER	051	038	They will roar together, like lions, they will shake their manes, like young lions.
024	JER	051	039	In their heat, I will give them a drink, and I will inebriate them, so that they become drowsy, and sleep an everlasting sleep, and do not rise up, says the Lord.
024	JER	051	040	I will lead them away, like lambs to the slaughter, and like rams with young goats.
024	JER	051	041	How was Sesac captured, and how was the renowned one of all the earth seized? How has Babylon become an astonishment among the nations?
024	JER	051	042	The sea has ascended over Babylon; she has been covered by the multitude of its waves.
024	JER	051	043	Her cities have become an astonishment, an uninhabited and desolate land, a land in which no one may live, nor may a son of man pass through it.
024	JER	051	044	And I will visit against Bel in Babylon, and I will cast from his mouth what he has swallowed. And the nations will no longer flow together before him. For even the wall of Babylon will also fall.
024	JER	051	045	Go forth from her midst, my people, so that each one may save his life from the wrath of the fury of the Lord.
024	JER	051	046	For otherwise, your heart may faint, and you may be afraid at the news that is heard in the land. And the news will arrive within a year, and after that year more news will arrive. And iniquity will be in the land, and one ruler will be over another ruler.
024	JER	051	047	Because of this, behold, the days are approaching, when I will visit against the graven images of Babylon. And her entire land will be confounded, and all her slain will fall in her midst.
024	JER	051	048	And the heavens and the earth, and all the things that are in them, will give praise over Babylon. For despoilers will approach her from the north, says the Lord.
024	JER	051	049	And in the manner that Babylon has caused the slain to fall in Israel, so the slain of Babylon will fall over the entire earth.
024	JER	051	050	You who have fled from the sword, approach, do not stand still. Remember from afar the Lord, and let Jerusalem rise up in your heart.
024	JER	051	051	We have been confounded, for we heard reproach. Shame has covered our faces, for strangers have overwhelmed the holiness of the house of the Lord.
024	JER	051	052	Because of this, behold, the days are approaching, says the Lord, when I will visit against her graven images, and within all her land the wounded will groan.
024	JER	051	053	If Babylon were to ascend to heaven, and establish her strength on high, her despoilers would go forth from me, says the Lord.”
024	JER	051	054	A voice of outcry from Babylon, and great destruction from the land of the Chaldeans!
024	JER	051	055	For the Lord has despoiled Babylon, and he has perished the great voice from her. And their wave will make a sound like many waters. Their voice has uttered a noise.
024	JER	051	056	For the despoiler has overwhelmed her, that is, Babylon, and her strong ones have been apprehended, and their bow has been weakened. For the Lord, the powerful revenger, will certainly repay.
024	JER	051	057	“And I will inebriate her leaders, and her wise ones, and her military rulers, and her civil rulers, and her strong ones. And they will sleep an everlasting sleep, and they will not awaken,” says the King: the Lord of hosts is his name.
024	JER	051	058	Thus says the Lord of hosts: “That very wide wall of Babylon will be utterly overturned, and her exalted gates will be burned with fire, and the labors of the people will be as nothing, and the labors of the nations will be sent into the fire and will perish.”
024	JER	051	059	The word that Jeremiah, the prophet, instructed to Seraiah, the son of Neriah, the son of Mahseiah, when he traveled with king Zedekiah into Babylon, in the fourth year of his reign. Now Seraiah was the leader of the prophets.
024	JER	051	060	And Jeremiah wrote in one book all the evil that was to overwhelm Babylon; all these words were written against Babylon.
024	JER	051	061	And Jeremiah said to Seraiah: “When you will enter into Babylon, and you will see and read all these words,
024	JER	051	062	you will say: ‘O Lord, you have spoken against this place so that you may destroy it, so that there would not be anyone, from man even to beast, who may live in it, and so that it may be desolate forever.’
024	JER	051	063	And when you will have completed reading this book, you will tie a stone to it, and you will cast it into the midst of the Euphrates.
024	JER	051	064	And you will say: ‘So shall Babylon be submerged! And she will not rise up before the face of the affliction that I will lead over her. And she will be broken.’” The words of Jeremiah thus far.
024	JER	052	001	Zedekiah was a son of twenty-one years when he first began to reign. And he reigned for eleven years in Jerusalem. And the name of his mother was Hamutal, the daughter of Jeremiah from Libnah.
024	JER	052	002	And he did what was evil in the eyes of the Lord, in accord with all that Jehoiakim had done.
024	JER	052	003	And so the fury of the Lord was toward Jerusalem, and toward Judah, even until he cast them away from his face. And Zedekiah drew away from the king of Babylon.
024	JER	052	004	And it happened that, in the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, on the tenth of the month, Nebuchadnezzar, the king of Babylon, he and his entire army, came against Jerusalem. And they besieged it, and they built fortifications against it, on every side.
024	JER	052	005	And the city was besieged, until the eleventh year of king Zedekiah.
024	JER	052	006	Then, in the fourth month, on the ninth of the month, a famine gripped the city. And there was no nourishment for the people of the land.
024	JER	052	007	And the city was broken, and all the men of war fled, and they departed from the city at night by way of the gate which is between the two walls, and which leads to the king’s garden, while the Chaldeans were besieging the city all around, and they went away by the road that leads to the wilderness.
024	JER	052	008	But the army of the Chaldeans pursued the king. And they overtook Zedekiah in the desert which is near Jericho. And all of his companions fled away from him.
024	JER	052	009	And when they had captured the king, they led him away to the king of Babylon at Riblah, which is in the land of Hamath. And he spoke a judgment against him.
024	JER	052	010	And the king of Babylon cut the throats of the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes, and he also killed all the leaders of Judah at Riblah.
024	JER	052	011	And he plucked out the eyes of Zedekiah, and he bound him with shackles, and the king of Babylon led him away to Babylon, and he placed him in the prison house, even until the day of his death.
024	JER	052	012	Then, in the fifth month, on the tenth of the month, which is the nineteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar, the king of Babylon, Nebuzaradan, the leader of the military, arrived. And he was standing before the king of Babylon at Jerusalem.
024	JER	052	013	And he set fire to the house of the Lord, and to the house of the king, and to all the houses of Jerusalem. And every great house he burned with fire.
024	JER	052	014	And the entire army of the Chaldeans, who were with the chief of the military, destroyed the entire wall all around Jerusalem.
024	JER	052	015	Then Nebuzaradan, the leader of the military, took away some of the poor people, and some of the rest of the common people, who had remained in the city, and some of the fugitives, who had fled over to the king of Babylon, and the rest of the multitude.
024	JER	052	016	Yet truly, some of the poor of the land, Nebuzaradan, the leader of the military, left behind as vinedressers and farmers.
024	JER	052	017	The Chaldeans also broke apart the bronze pillars that were in the house of the Lord, and the bases, and the sea of brass that was in the house of the Lord. And they took all the brass of these things to Babylon.
024	JER	052	018	And they took the cooking pots, and the hooks, and the psalteries, and the bowls, and the little mortars, and all the bronze vessels that had been used in the ministry.
024	JER	052	019	And the chief of the military took the water pots, and the censers, and the pitchers, and the basins, and the lampstands, and the mortars, and the little cups, whatever was gold, for the gold, and whatever was silver, for the silver,
024	JER	052	020	as well as the two pillars, and the one brass sea, and the twelve oxen of brass that were under the bases, which king Solomon had made in the house of the Lord. There was no weight of brass left behind out of all these vessels.
024	JER	052	021	Now concerning the pillars, one pillar was eighteen cubits high, and a cord of twelve cubits encircled it. Moreover, its thickness was four fingers, and the interior was hollow.
024	JER	052	022	And heads of brass were upon both. And the height of one head was five cubits. And little nets with pomegranates were upon the heads all around, all of brass. The second pillar was similar, and the pomegranates.
024	JER	052	023	And there were ninety-six pomegranates hanging down; and there were one hundred pomegranates in all, surrounded by the little nets.
024	JER	052	024	And the chief of the military took Seraiah, the first priest, and Zephaniah, the second priest, and the three keepers of the vestibule.
024	JER	052	025	He also took from the city one eunuch who was in charge of the men of war, and seven men among those who served before the face of the king, who were found in the city, and a scribe, a leader of the military, who tested the new recruits, and sixty men from the people of the land, who were found in the midst of the city.
024	JER	052	026	Then Nebuzaradan, the chief of the military, took them, and he led them to the king of Babylon at Riblah.
024	JER	052	027	And the king of Babylon struck them and put them to death at Riblah, in the land of Hamath. And Judah was carried away from his land.
024	JER	052	028	This is the people whom Nebuchadnezzar carried away: in the seventh year, three thousand and twenty-three Jews;
024	JER	052	029	in the eighteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar, eight hundred thirty-two souls from Jerusalem;
024	JER	052	030	in the twenty-third year of Nebuchadnezzar, Nebuzaradan, the chief of the military, carried away of the Jews seven hundred forty-five souls. Therefore, all the souls were four thousand six hundred.
024	JER	052	031	And it happened that, in the thirty-seventh year of the transmigration of Jehoiachin, the king of Judah, in the twelfth month, on the twenty-fifth of the month, Evilmerodach, the king of Babylon, in the very first year of his reign, lifted up the head of Jehoiachin, the king of Judah, and he brought him out of the prison house.
024	JER	052	032	And he spoke with him for good, and he set his throne above the thrones of the kings who were after him in Babylon.
024	JER	052	033	And he changed his prison garments, and he ate bread in his sight always, all the days of his life.
024	JER	052	034	And for his meals, a continual provision was allotted to him by the king of Babylon, a measure for every single day, until the day of his death, all the days of his life.
#
# BOOK	025	LAM	Lamentations	Lamentations
025	LAM	001	001	ALEPH. O how a city once filled with people now sits alone! The Governess of the Gentiles has become like a widow. The Prince of the provinces has been placed under tribute.
025	LAM	001	002	BETH. Weeping, she has wept through the night, and her tears are on her cheeks. There is no one to be a comfort to her and to all her beloved. All her friends have spurned her, and they have become her enemies.
025	LAM	001	003	GHIMEL. Judah has migrated because of affliction and great servitude. She has lived among the nations and not found rest. All of her persecutors have apprehended her, amid torments.
025	LAM	001	004	DALETH. The pathways of Zion mourn, because there are none who approach for the solemnity. All her gates are destroyed. Her priests groan. Her virgins are filthy. And she is overwhelmed with bitterness.
025	LAM	001	005	HE. Her enemies have been made her leaders; her adversaries have been enriched. For the Lord has spoken against her, because of the multitude of her iniquities. Her little ones have been led into captivity before the face of the tribulator.
025	LAM	001	006	VAU. And all her elegance has departed, from the daughter of Zion. Her leaders have become like rams that cannot find pasture, and they have gone away without strength before the face of the pursuer.
025	LAM	001	007	ZAIN. Jerusalem has remembered the days of her affliction and the betrayal of all her desirable ones, whom she held from the days of antiquity, when her people fell into the hand of the enemy, and there was no one to be a helper. The enemies have looked upon her and mocked her Sabbaths.
025	LAM	001	008	HETH. Jerusalem has sinned a grievous sinz. Because of this, she has become unstable. All who glorified her have spurned her, because they have looked upon her disgrace. Then she groaned and turned away again.
025	LAM	001	009	TETH. Her filth is on her feet, and her end has not been remembered. She has been vehemently put down, having no consolation. O Lord, look upon my affliction, for the adversary has been lifted up.
025	LAM	001	010	JOD. The enemy has sent his hand against all her desirable ones. For she has watched the Gentiles enter her sanctuary, even though you instructed that they should not enter into your church.
025	LAM	001	011	CAPH. All her people are groaning and seeking bread. They have given up whatever was precious in exchange for food, so as to remain alive. See, O Lord, and consider, for I have become vile.
025	LAM	001	012	LAMED. O all you who pass by the way, attend, and see if there is any sorrow like my sorrow. For he has made me a vintage, just as the Lord has spoken in the day of his furious anger.
025	LAM	001	013	MEM. From on high, he has sent fire into my bones, and he has educated me. He has spread a net for my feet; he has turned me back. He has placed me in desolation, consumed by grief, all day long.
025	LAM	001	014	NUN. Vigilant is the yoke of my iniquities. They have been folded together in his hand and imposed on my neck. My virtue has been weakened. The Lord has given me into a hand, out of which I am not able to rise.
025	LAM	001	015	SAMECH. The Lord has taken away all of my great ones from my midst. He has called forth time against me, so as to crush my elect ones. The Lord has trampled the winepress, which was for the virgin daughter of Judah.
025	LAM	001	016	AIN. For this I weep, and my eyes bring forth water. For the consoler has been far away from me, changing my soul. My sons have become lost, because the enemy has prevailed.
025	LAM	001	017	PHE. Zion has reached out her hands; there is no one to console her. The Lord has given orders against Jacob; his enemies are all around him. Jerusalem among them is like a woman made unclean by menstruation.
025	LAM	001	018	SADE. The Lord is just, for it is I who has provoked his mouth to wrath. I beg all people to listen and to see my sorrow. My virgins and my youths have gone into captivity.
025	LAM	001	019	COPH. I called for my friends, but they deceived me. My priests and my elders have been consumed in the city. For they were seeking their food, so as to revive their life.
025	LAM	001	020	RES. See, O Lord, that I am in tribulation. My bowels have been disturbed, my heart has been subverted within me, for I am filled with bitterness. Outside, the sword puts to death, and at home there is a similar death.
025	LAM	001	021	SIN. They have heard that I groan and that there is no one to console me. All my enemies have heard of my misfortune; they have rejoiced that you caused it. You have brought in a day of consolation, and so they shall become like me.
025	LAM	001	022	THAU. Let all their evil enter before you. And make vintage of them, just as you made vintage of me, because of all my iniquities. For my sighs are many, and my heart is grieving.
025	LAM	002	001	ALEPH. O how the Lord has covered the daughter of Zion with gloom in his fury! O how he has thrown down from heaven to earth the famous one of Israel, and he has not remembered his footstool in the day of his fury.
025	LAM	002	002	BETH. The Lord has cast down, and he has not been lenient, with all the beauties of Jacob. In his fury, he has destroyed the fortifications of the virgin of Judah, and he has thrown them down to the ground. He has polluted the kingdom and its leaders.
025	LAM	002	003	GHIMEL. In the anger of his fury, he has broken the entire horn of Israel. He has drawn back his right hand before the face of the enemy. And he has kindled within Jacob a flaming fire, devouring all around.
025	LAM	002	004	DALETH. He has bent his bow like an enemy. He has fixed his right hand like an adversary. And he has cut down all that was beautiful to behold in the tabernacle of the daughter of Zion. He has poured out his indignation like fire.
025	LAM	002	005	HE. The Lord has become like an enemy. He has thrown down Israel. He has thrown down all of his defenses. He has torn apart his fortifications. And he has filled the daughter of Judah with humbled men and humbled women.
025	LAM	002	006	VAU. And he has torn apart her tent like a garden. He has demolished her tabernacle. In Zion, the Lord has delivered feast and Sabbath into oblivion, and king and priest into disgrace, and into the indignation of his fury.
025	LAM	002	007	ZAIN. The Lord has pushed away his own altar. He has cursed his own sanctuary. He has delivered the walls of its towers into the hand of the enemy. They have made a noise in the house of the Lord, as if on the day of a solemnity.
025	LAM	002	008	HETH. The Lord has decided to tear down the wall of the daughter of Zion. He has stretched out his measuring line, and he has not turned away his hand from perdition. And the rampart has mourned, and with the wall it has been torn apart.
025	LAM	002	009	TETH. Her gates have been buried in the ground. He has ruined and crushed its bars. Her king and her princes are with the Gentiles. There is no law, and her prophets have found no vision from the Lord.
025	LAM	002	010	JOD. The elders of the daughter of Zion have become idle; they sit on the ground. They have sprinkled their heads with ashes. They have been wrapped with haircloth. The virgins of Jerusalem have cast their heads down to the ground.
025	LAM	002	011	CAPH. My eyes have exhausted their tears. My internal organs have become disturbed. My liver has been poured out on the earth, over the grief of the daughter of my people, when the little ones and the infants passed away in the streets of the town.
025	LAM	002	012	LAMED. They said to their mothers, “Where is the wheat and the wine?” when they fell like the wounded in the streets of the city, when they breathed out their lives into the bosoms of their mothers.
025	LAM	002	013	MEM. To what shall I compare you, or to what shall I liken you, O daughter of Jerusalem? To what shall I equate you, so as to console you, O virgin daughter of Zion? For your destruction is as great as the sea. Who will cure you?
025	LAM	002	014	NUN. Your prophets have seen false and foolish things for you. And they have not laid open your iniquity, so as to provoke you to repentance. Yet they have seen for you false revelations and banishments.
025	LAM	002	015	SAMECH. All those who passed by the way have clapped their hands over you. They have hissed and shook their heads over the daughter of Jerusalem, saying, “Is this the city of perfect dignity, the joy of all the earth?”
025	LAM	002	016	PHE. All your enemies have opened their mouth over you. They have hissed and gnashed their teeth, and they said: “We will devour her. Yes, this is the day we waited for. We have found it, we have seen it.”
025	LAM	002	017	AIN. The Lord has done what he decided to do. He has fulfilled his word, which he instructed since the days of antiquity. He has destroyed, and he has not been lenient, and he has caused the enemy to rejoice over you, and he has exalted the horn of your adversaries.
025	LAM	002	018	SADE. Their heart cried out to the Lord from the walls of the daughter of Zion. Let tears run down like a torrent throughout the day and the night. Do not give rest to yourself, and do not allow the pupil of your eye to cease.
025	LAM	002	019	COPH. Rise up. Give praise in the night, in the first of the watches. Pour out your heart like water before the sight of the Lord. Lift up your hands to him on behalf of the souls of your little ones, who have passed away from famine at the head of all the crossroads.
025	LAM	002	020	RES. O Lord, see and consider those whom you have made into such a vintage. So then, shall women eat their own fruit, little ones measured by the palm of the hand? Shall priest and prophet be killed in the sanctuary of the Lord?
025	LAM	002	021	SIN. The boy and the old man lie down on the ground outside. My virgins and my youths have fallen by the sword. You have slain them in the day of your fury. You have struck down, and you have not shown pity.
025	LAM	002	022	THAU. You have called, as if to a day of solemnity, those who would terrify me all around. And there was no one, in the day of the fury of the Lord, who escaped or was left behind. Those whom I educated and nourished, my enemy has consumed.
025	LAM	003	001	ALEPH. I am a man watching my own poverty by the rod of his indignation.
025	LAM	003	002	ALEPH. He has driven me and led me into darkness, and not into light.
025	LAM	003	003	ALEPH. Against me only, he has turned and turned again his hand, all day long.
025	LAM	003	004	BETH. My skin and my flesh, he has made old; he has crushed my bones.
025	LAM	003	005	BETH. He has built all around me, and he has encircled me with gall and hardship.
025	LAM	003	006	BETH. He has gathered me into darkness, like those who are forever dead.
025	LAM	003	007	GHIMEL. He has built against me all around, so that I may not depart. He has increased the burden of my confinement.
025	LAM	003	008	GHIMEL. Yet even when I cry out and beg, he excludes my prayer.
025	LAM	003	009	GHIMEL. He has enclosed my ways with square stones; he has subverted my paths.
025	LAM	003	010	DALETH. He has become to me like a bear lying in ambush, like a lion in hiding.
025	LAM	003	011	DALETH. He has subverted my paths, and he has broken me. He has placed me in desolation.
025	LAM	003	012	DALETH. He has bent his bow, and he has positioned me like a target for his arrows.
025	LAM	003	013	HE. He has shot into my kidneys the daughters of his quiver.
025	LAM	003	014	HE. I have become a derision to all my people, their song throughout the day.
025	LAM	003	015	HE. He has filled me with bitterness; he has inebriated me with wormwood.
025	LAM	003	016	VAU. And he has broken each one of my teeth; he has fed me with ashes.
025	LAM	003	017	VAU. And my soul has been driven away from peace; I have forgotten what is good.
025	LAM	003	018	VAU. And I said, “My end and my hope from the Lord has perished.”
025	LAM	003	019	ZAIN. Remember my poverty and my transgression, the wormwood and the gall.
025	LAM	003	020	ZAIN. I will call to mind the past, and my soul shall languish within me.
025	LAM	003	021	ZAIN. These recollections are in my heart; therefore, I shall hope.
025	LAM	003	022	HETH. By the mercies of the Lord, we are not consumed. For his compassion has not passed away.
025	LAM	003	023	HETH. I know it at first light; great is your faithfulness.
025	LAM	003	024	HETH. “The Lord is my portion,” said my soul. Because of this, I will wait for him.
025	LAM	003	025	TETH. The Lord is good to those who hope in him, to the soul that seeks him.
025	LAM	003	026	TETH. It is good to stand ready in silence for the salvation of God.
025	LAM	003	027	TETH. It is good for a man, when he has carried the yoke from his youth.
025	LAM	003	028	JOD. He shall sit solitary and silent. For he has lifted it upon himself.
025	LAM	003	029	JOD. He shall place his mouth in the dirt, if perhaps there may be hope.
025	LAM	003	030	JOD. He shall give his cheek to those who strike him; he shall be saturated with reproaches.
025	LAM	003	031	CAPH. For the Lord will not rebuke forever.
025	LAM	003	032	CAPH. For, if he has cast down, he will also have compassion, according to the multitude of his mercies.
025	LAM	003	033	CAPH. For he has not humiliated from his heart, nor has he thrown aside the sons of men,
025	LAM	003	034	LAMED. as if to crush under his feet all the prisoners of the land,
025	LAM	003	035	LAMED. as if to turn aside the judgment of a man in the sight of the presence of the Most High,
025	LAM	003	036	LAMED. as if to pervert a man in his judgment: the Lord does not do this.
025	LAM	003	037	MEM. Who is this, who said to do what the Lord did not command?
025	LAM	003	038	MEM. Does not both misfortune and good proceed from the mouth of the Most High?
025	LAM	003	039	MEM. Why has a living man murmured, a man suffering for his sins?
025	LAM	003	040	NUN. Let us examine our ways, and seek out, and return to the Lord.
025	LAM	003	041	NUN. Let us lift up our hearts, with our hands, toward the Lord in the heavens.
025	LAM	003	042	NUN. We have acted sinfully, and we have provoked to wrath. About this, you are relentless.
025	LAM	003	043	SAMECH. You have covered us in your fury, and you have struck us. You have killed, and have not spared.
025	LAM	003	044	SAMECH. You have set a cloud opposite you, lest our prayer pass through.
025	LAM	003	045	SAMECH. In the midst of the peoples, you have uprooted me and cast me out.
025	LAM	003	046	PHE. All our enemies have opened their mouths over us.
025	LAM	003	047	PHE. Prediction has become for us a dread, and a snare, and a grief.
025	LAM	003	048	PHE. My eye has brought forth streams of water at the contrition of the daughter of my people.
025	LAM	003	049	AIN. My eye has been afflicted, and it has not been quieted, because there would be no rest
025	LAM	003	050	AIN. until the Lord looked down and saw from the heavens.
025	LAM	003	051	AIN. My eye has exhausted my soul over every one of the daughters of my city.
025	LAM	003	052	SADE. My enemies have chased me, and they have caught me like a bird, without reason.
025	LAM	003	053	SADE. My life has fallen into a pit, and they have placed a stone over me.
025	LAM	003	054	SADE. The waters have flooded over my head. I said, “I am lost.”
025	LAM	003	055	COPH. I called upon your name, O Lord, from the furthest pit.
025	LAM	003	056	COPH. You have heard my voice. Do not turn away your ear from my sobbing and my cries.
025	LAM	003	057	COPH. You drew near in the daytime, when I called upon you. You said, “Fear not.”
025	LAM	003	058	RES. You have judged, O Lord, the case of my soul. You are the Redeemer of my life.
025	LAM	003	059	RES. You have seen, O Lord, their iniquity against me. Judge my case.
025	LAM	003	060	RES. You have seen all their fury, every one of their thoughts is against me.
025	LAM	003	061	SIN. You have heard their reproach, O Lord, all their thoughts are against me.
025	LAM	003	062	SIN. The lips of those who rise up against me, and their meditations, are against me all day long.
025	LAM	003	063	SIN. Watch their sitting down and their rising up: I am their psalm.
025	LAM	003	064	THAU. You shall pay a recompense to them, O Lord, according to the works of their hands.
025	LAM	003	065	THAU. You shall give them a heavy shield of the heart: your hardship.
025	LAM	003	066	THAU. You shall pursue them in fury, and you shall destroy them under the heavens, O Lord.
025	LAM	004	001	ALEPH. O how the gold has become dulled, the finest color has been altered, the stones of the sanctuary have been scattered at the head of every street.
025	LAM	004	002	BETH. The famous sons of Zion, and those clothed with the foremost gold: how they have become like earthen vessels, the work of the hands of a potter.
025	LAM	004	003	GHIMEL. Yet even savages expose their breast and give milk to their young. But the daughter of my people is cruel, like the ostrich in the desert.
025	LAM	004	004	DALETH. The tongue of the infant adheres to his palate out of thirst. The little ones have asked for bread, and there was no one to break it for them.
025	LAM	004	005	HE. Those who were fed indulgently have passed away in the roads. Those who were nourished with saffron have welcomed filth.
025	LAM	004	006	VAU. And the iniquity of the daughter of my people has been made greater than the sin of Sodom, which was overthrown in a moment, and yet hands did not take captives in her.
025	LAM	004	007	ZAIN. Her Nazirites were whiter than snow, shinier than milk, more ruddy than ancient ivory, more beautiful than sapphire.
025	LAM	004	008	HETH. Their face has been blacked more than coals, and they are not recognized in the streets. Their skin has adhered to their bones; it dried out and became like wood.
025	LAM	004	009	TETH. It was better for those slain by the sword, than for those put to death by famine. For these waste away, being consumed by the sterility of the land.
025	LAM	004	010	JOD. The hands of pitiable women have boiled their sons. They became their food in the grief of the daughter of my people.
025	LAM	004	011	CAPH. The Lord has completed his fury; he has poured out the wrath of his indignation. And he has kindled a fire in Zion, and it has devoured its foundations.
025	LAM	004	012	LAMED. The kings of the earth, and all the inhabitants of the world, did not believe that the adversary and the enemy would enter through the gates of Jerusalem.
025	LAM	004	013	MEM. It is because of the sins of her prophets, and the iniquities of her priests, who have shed the blood of the just in her midst.
025	LAM	004	014	NUN. They have wandered in the streets like the blind; they have been defiled with blood. And when they were not able, they held their garments.
025	LAM	004	015	SAMECH. “Go back, you polluted ones!” they cried out to them. “Go back, go away, do not touch!” Of course, they argued, and being removed, they said among the Gentiles, “He will no longer dwell among them.”
025	LAM	004	016	PHE. The face of the Lord has divided them. He will no longer respect them. They were not ashamed before the faces of the priests, nor did they take pity on the elderly.
025	LAM	004	017	AIN. While we were still standing, our eyes failed, expecting help for us in vain, when we looked attentively toward a nation that was not able to save.
025	LAM	004	018	SADE. Our footsteps have slipped on the paths of our own streets. Our end draws near. Our days have been completed, for our end has arrived.
025	LAM	004	019	COPH. Our persecutors have been swifter than the eagles of the sky. They have been pursuing us above the mountains; they have lain in wait for us in the desert.
025	LAM	004	020	RES. The spirit of our mouth, Christ the Lord, has been captured by our sins; to him, we said, “In your shadow, we will live among the Gentiles.”
025	LAM	004	021	SIN. Be glad and rejoice, O daughter of Edom, who dwells in the Land of Uz. The cup will also pass to you; you will be inebriated as well as naked.
025	LAM	004	022	THAU. Your iniquity has been completed, O daughter of Zion. He will no longer send you away to captivity. He has visited your iniquity, O daughter of Edom; he has uncovered your sins.
025	LAM	005	001	Remember, O Lord, what has befallen us. Consider and look kindly upon our disgrace.
025	LAM	005	002	Our inheritance has been turned over to foreigners; our houses to outsiders.
025	LAM	005	003	We have become orphans without a father; our mothers are like widows.
025	LAM	005	004	We paid for our drinking water. We acquired our wood for a price.
025	LAM	005	005	We were dragged by our necks. Being weary, no rest was given to us.
025	LAM	005	006	We have given our hand to Egypt and to the Assyrians, so that we may be satisfied with bread.
025	LAM	005	007	Our fathers have sinned, and are not. And we have carried their iniquities.
025	LAM	005	008	Servants have become rulers over us. There was no one to redeem us from their hand.
025	LAM	005	009	We obtained our bread at the risk of our lives, before the face of the sword, in the wilderness.
025	LAM	005	010	Our skin was burned, as if by an oven, before the face of the tempest of the famine.
025	LAM	005	011	They humiliated the women in Zion and the virgins in the cities of Judah.
025	LAM	005	012	The leaders were suspended by their hand. They were not ashamed before the faces of the elders.
025	LAM	005	013	They have sexually abused the adolescents, and the children were corrupted in the wood.
025	LAM	005	014	The elders have ceased from the gates, the youths from the choir of the psalms.
025	LAM	005	015	The gladness of our heart has failed, our singing has been turned into mourning.
025	LAM	005	016	The crown has fallen from our head. Woe to us, for we have sinned.
025	LAM	005	017	Because of this, our heart became gloomy; for this reason, our eyes have been darkened:
025	LAM	005	018	because of mount Zion, because it was ruined. Foxes have wandered upon it.
025	LAM	005	019	But you, O Lord, shall remain for eternity, your throne from generation to generation.
025	LAM	005	020	Why would you forget us forever? Why would you forsake us for a long time?
025	LAM	005	021	Convert us, O Lord, to you, and we shall be converted. Renew our days, as from the beginning.
025	LAM	005	022	But you have utterly rejected us; you are vehemently angry against us.
