033	MIC	007	004	Whoever is best among them is like a thorny plant, and he who is righteous is like a thorny hedge. The day of your inspection, your visitation, arrives. Now will be their ruination.
033	MIC	007	005	Do not be willing to believe a friend. And do not be willing to confide in a commander. From her, who sleeps in your bosom, keep the doors of your mouth closed.
033	MIC	007	006	For the son acts with contempt for the father, and the daughter rises up against her mother, the daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law, and a man’s enemies are those of his own household.
033	MIC	007	007	But I will look towards the Lord. I will wait for God, my Savior. My God will hear me.
033	MIC	007	008	You, my enemy, should not rejoice over me because I have fallen. I will rise up, when I sit in darkness. The Lord is my light.
033	MIC	007	009	I will carry the wrath of the Lord, because I have sinned against him, until he may judge my case and execute judgment for me. He will lead me into the light. I will behold his justice.
033	MIC	007	010	And my enemy will look, and she will be covered with confusion, she who says to me, “Where is the Lord your God?” My eyes will look upon her. Now she will be trampled underfoot like the mud of the streets.
033	MIC	007	011	The day that your walls will be rebuilt, in that day the law will be far away.
033	MIC	007	012	In that day also, they will come towards you even from Assur, and even to the fortified cities, and from the fortified cities even to the river, and from sea to sea, and from mountain to mountain.
033	MIC	007	013	And the land will be in desolation, because of its inhabitants and because of the fruit of their intentions.
033	MIC	007	014	With your rod, pasture your people, the flock of your inheritance, living alone in the narrow forest, in the midst of Carmel. They will graze in Bashan and Gilead, as in the ancient days.
033	MIC	007	015	As in the days of your departure from the land of Egypt, I will reveal miracles to him.
033	MIC	007	016	The nations will look, and they will be confounded at the strength of them all. They will place hand over mouth; their ears will be deaf.
033	MIC	007	017	They will lick the dust like serpents, and, like the creeping things of the earth, they will be disturbed in their houses. They will dread the Lord our God, and they will fear you.
033	MIC	007	018	What God is like you, who takes away iniquity and passes over the sin of the remnant of your inheritance? No longer will he send forth his fury, because he is willing to be merciful.
033	MIC	007	019	He will turn back and have mercy on us. He will put away our iniquities, and he will cast all our sins into the depths of the sea.
033	MIC	007	020	You will give the truth to Jacob, mercy to Abraham, which you swore to our fathers from the ancient days.
