035	HAB	003	001	A Prayer of Habakkuk the Prophet on Behalf of Those Who Are Ignorant.
035	HAB	003	002	Lord, I heard what has been said about you, and I was afraid. Lord, your work, in the midst of years, revive it. In the midst of years, you will make it known. When you have become angry, you will remember mercy.
035	HAB	003	003	God will come from the south, and the Holy One from mount Pharan. His glory has covered the heavens, and the earth is full of his praise.
035	HAB	003	004	His brightness shall be like the light; horns are in his hands. There, his strength has been hidden.
035	HAB	003	005	Death will go forth before his face. And the devil shall depart before his feet.
035	HAB	003	006	He stood, and measured the earth. He looked, and dissolved the Gentiles. And the mountains of ages past have been shattered. The hills of the world became curved by the journeys of his eternity.
035	HAB	003	007	I saw the tents of Ethiopia for their iniquity; the tent-skins of the land of Midian will be thrown into confusion.
035	HAB	003	008	Could you have been angry with the rivers, Lord? Or was your fury within the rivers, or your indignation in the sea? He will ascend upon your horses, and your four-horse chariots are salvation.
035	HAB	003	009	Being stirred up, you will take up your bow, the oaths you have spoken to the tribes. You will split apart the Rivers of the earth.
035	HAB	003	010	They saw you, and the mountains grieved. The great body of waters crossed over. The abyss uttered its voice. The pinnacle lifted up its hands.
035	HAB	003	011	The sun and the moon have stood firm in their dwelling place; with the light of your arrows, they shall go forth in the splendor of your flashing spear.
035	HAB	003	012	With a roar, you will trample the earth. In your fury, you will cause the nations to be stupefied.
035	HAB	003	013	You have gone forth for the salvation of your people, for salvation with your Christ. You struck the head of the house of the impious. You have laid bare his foundation all the way to the neck.
035	HAB	003	014	You have cursed his scepters, the head of his warriors, those who approached like a whirlwind so as to scatter me. Their exultation was like one who devours the poor in secret.
035	HAB	003	015	You made a way in the sea for your horses, in the mud of great waters.
035	HAB	003	016	I heard, and my stomach became troubled. My lips trembled at the voice. Let decay enter into my bones and gush forth from within me. Then I may rest in the day of tribulation, so that I may ascend to our people well-prepared.
035	HAB	003	017	For the fig tree will not flower, and there will be no bud on the vines. The labor of the olive tree will be misleading, and the farmland will produce no food. The sheep will be cut off from the sheepfold, and there will be no herd at the manger.
035	HAB	003	018	But I will rejoice in the Lord; and I will exult in God my Jesus.
