036	ZEP	003	001	Woe to the provocatrix and the redeemed city, the dove.
036	ZEP	003	002	She has not heeded the voice, nor has she accepted discipline. She has not trusted in the Lord; she did not draw near to her God.
036	ZEP	003	003	Her leaders are in her midst like roaring lions. Her judges are evening wolves; they leave nothing for the morning.
036	ZEP	003	004	Her prophets are crazed; men without faith. Her priests have polluted what is holy; they have acted unjustly against the law.
036	ZEP	003	005	The just Lord is in their midst; he will not do iniquity. In the morning, in the morning, he will bring his judgment into the light, and it will not be hidden. But the impious one has not known shame.
036	ZEP	003	006	I have dispersed the nations, and their towers have been torn down. I have made their ways deserts, until there were none who passed through. Their cities have become desolate, with no man remaining, nor any inhabitant.
