040	MAT	006	013	And lead us not into temptation. But free us from evil. Amen.
040	MAT	006	014	For if you will forgive men their sins, your heavenly Father also will forgive you your offenses.
040	MAT	006	015	But if you will not forgive men, neither will your Father forgive you your sins.
040	MAT	006	016	And when you fast, do not choose to become gloomy, like the hypocrites. For they alter their faces, so that their fasting may be apparent to men. Amen I say to you, that they have received their reward.
040	MAT	006	017	But as for you, when you fast, anoint your head and wash your face,
040	MAT	006	018	so that your fasting will not be apparent to men, but to your Father, who is in secret. And your Father, who sees in secret, will repay you.
040	MAT	006	019	Do not choose to store up for yourselves treasures on earth: where rust and moth consume, and where thieves break in and steal.
040	MAT	006	020	Instead, store up for yourselves treasures in heaven: where neither rust nor moth consumes, and where thieves do not break in and steal.
040	MAT	006	021	For where your treasure is, there also is your heart.
040	MAT	006	022	The lamp of your body is your eye. If your eye is wholesome, your entire body will be filled with light.
040	MAT	006	023	But if your eye has been corrupted, your entire body will be darkened. If then the light that is in you is darkness, how great will that darkness be!
040	MAT	006	024	No one is able to serve two masters. For either he will have hatred for the one, and love the other, or he will persevere with the one, and despise the other. You cannot serve God and wealth.
040	MAT	006	025	And so I say to you, do not be anxious about your life, as to what you will eat, nor about your body, as to what you will wear. Is not life more than food, and the body more than clothing?
040	MAT	006	026	Consider the birds of the air, how they neither sow, nor reap, nor gather into barns, and yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not of much greater value than they are?
040	MAT	006	027	And which of you, by thinking, is able to add one cubit to his stature?
040	MAT	006	028	And as for clothing, why are you anxious? Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow; they neither work nor weave.
040	MAT	006	029	But I say to you, that not even Solomon, in all his glory, was arrayed like one of these.
040	MAT	006	030	So if God so clothes the grass of the field, which is here today, and cast into the oven tomorrow, how much more will he care for you, O little in faith?
040	MAT	006	031	Therefore, do not choose to be anxious, saying: ‘What shall we eat, and what shall we drink, and with what shall we be clothed?’
040	MAT	006	032	For the Gentiles seek all these things. Yet your Father knows that you need all these things.
040	MAT	006	033	Therefore, seek first the kingdom of God and his justice, and all these things shall be added to you as well.
