040	MAT	024	051	And he shall separate him, and he shall place his portion with the hypocrites, where there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.”
040	MAT	025	001	“Then the kingdom of heaven shall be like ten virgins, who, taking their lamps, went out to meet the groom and the bride.
040	MAT	025	002	But five of them were foolish, and five were prudent.
040	MAT	025	003	For the five foolish, having brought their lamps, did not take oil with them.
040	MAT	025	004	Yet truly, the prudent ones brought the oil, in their containers, with the lamps.
040	MAT	025	005	Since the bridegroom was delayed, they all fell asleep, and they were sleeping.
040	MAT	025	006	But in the middle of the night, a cry went out: ‘Behold, the groom is arriving. Go out to meet him.’
040	MAT	025	007	Then all those virgins rose up and trimmed their lamps.
040	MAT	025	008	But the foolish ones said to the wise, ‘Give to us from your oil, for our lamps are being extinguished.’
040	MAT	025	009	The prudent responded by saying, ‘Lest perhaps there may not be enough for us and for you, it would be better for you to go to the vendors and buy some for yourselves.’
040	MAT	025	010	But while they were going to buy it, the groom arrived. And those who were prepared entered with him to the wedding, and the door was closed.
040	MAT	025	011	Yet truly, at the very end, the remaining virgins also arrived, saying, ‘Lord, Lord, open to us.’
040	MAT	025	012	But he responded by saying, ‘Amen I say to you, I do not know you.’
040	MAT	025	013	And so you must be vigilant, because you do not know the day or the hour.
040	MAT	025	014	For it is like a man setting out on a long journey, who called his servants and delivered to them his goods.
040	MAT	025	015	And to one he gave five talents, and to another two, yet to another he gave one, to each according to his own ability. And promptly, he set out.
040	MAT	025	016	Then he who had received five talents went out, and he made use of these, and he gained another five.
040	MAT	025	017	And similarly, he who had received two gained another two.
040	MAT	025	018	But he who had received one, going out, dug into the earth, and he hid the money of his lord.
040	MAT	025	019	Yet truly, after a long time, the lord of those servants returned and he settled accounts with them.
040	MAT	025	020	And when he who had received five talents approached, he brought another five talents, saying: ‘Lord, you delivered five talents to me. Behold, I have increased it by another five.’
040	MAT	025	021	His lord said to him: ‘Well done, good and faithful servant. Since you have been faithful over a few things, I will appoint you over many things. Enter into the gladness of your lord.’
040	MAT	025	022	Then he who had received two talents also approached, and he said: ‘Lord, you delivered two talents to me. Behold, I have gained another two.’
040	MAT	025	023	His lord said to him: ‘Well done, good and faithful servant. Since you have been faithful over a few things, I will appoint you over many things. Enter into the gladness of your lord.’
040	MAT	025	024	Then he who had received one talent, approaching, said: ‘Lord, I know that you are a hard man. You reap where you have not sown, and gather where you have not scattered.
040	MAT	025	025	And so, being afraid, I went out and hid your talent in the earth. Behold, you have what is yours.’
040	MAT	025	026	But his lord said to him in response: ‘You evil and lazy servant! You knew that I reap where I have not sown, and gather where I have not scattered.
040	MAT	025	027	Therefore, you should have deposited my money with the bankers, and then, at my arrival, at least I would have received what is mine with interest.
040	MAT	025	028	And so, take the talent away from him and give it to the one who has ten talents.
040	MAT	025	029	For to everyone who has, more shall be given, and he shall have in abundance. But from him who has not, even what he seems to have, shall be taken away.
040	MAT	025	030	And cast that useless servant into the outer darkness, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.’
040	MAT	025	031	But when the Son of man will have arrived in his majesty, and all the Angels with him, then he will sit upon the seat of his majesty.
040	MAT	025	032	And all the nations shall be gathered together before him. And he shall separate them from one another, just as a shepherd separates the sheep from the goats.
040	MAT	025	033	And he shall station the sheep, indeed, on his right, but the goats on his left.
040	MAT	025	034	Then the King shall say to those who will be on his right: ‘Come, you blessed of my Father. Possess the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world.
040	MAT	025	035	For I was hungry, and you gave me to eat; I was thirsty, and you gave me to drink; I was a stranger, and you took me in;
040	MAT	025	036	naked, and you covered me; sick, and you visited me; I was in prison, and you came to me.’
040	MAT	025	037	Then the just will answer him, saying: ‘Lord, when have we seen you hungry, and fed you; thirsty, and given you drink?
040	MAT	025	038	And when have we seen you a stranger, and taken you in? Or naked, and covered you?
040	MAT	025	039	Or when did we see you sick, or in prison, and visit to you?’
040	MAT	025	040	And in response, the King shall say to them, ‘Amen I say to you, whenever you did this for one of these, the least of my brothers, you did it for me.’
040	MAT	025	041	Then he shall also say, to those who will be on his left: ‘Depart from me, you accursed ones, into the eternal fire, which was prepared for the devil and his angels.
