041	MAR	015	015	Then Pilate, wishing to satisfy the people, released Barabbas to them, and he delivered Jesus, having severely scourged him, to be crucified.
041	MAR	015	016	Then the soldiers led him away to the court of the praetorium. And they called together the entire cohort.
041	MAR	015	017	And they clothed him with purple. And platting a crown of thorns, they placed it on him.
041	MAR	015	018	And they began to salute him: “Hail, king of the Jews.”
041	MAR	015	019	And they struck his head with a reed, and they spit on him. And kneeling down, they reverenced him.
