041	MAR	015	021	And they compelled a certain passerby, Simon the Cyrenian, who was arriving from the countryside, the father of Alexander and Rufus, to take up his cross.
041	MAR	015	022	And they led him through to the place called Golgotha, which means, ‘the Place of Calvary.’
041	MAR	015	023	And they gave him wine with myrrh to drink. But he did not accept it.
