# BOOK	043	JOH	John	John
043	JOH	001	001	In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and God was the Word.
043	JOH	001	002	He was with God in the beginning.
043	JOH	001	003	All things were made through Him, and nothing that was made was made without Him.
043	JOH	001	004	Life was in Him, and Life was the light of men.
043	JOH	001	005	And the light shines in the darkness, and the darkness did not comprehend it.
043	JOH	001	006	There was a man sent by God, whose name was John.
043	JOH	001	007	He arrived as a witness to offer testimony about the Light, so that all would believe through him.
043	JOH	001	008	He was not the Light, but he was to offer testimony about the Light.
043	JOH	001	009	The true Light, which illuminates every man, was coming into this world.
043	JOH	001	010	He was in the world, and the world was made through him, and the world did not recognize him.
043	JOH	001	011	He went to his own, and his own did not accept him.
043	JOH	001	012	Yet whoever did accept him, those who believed in his name, he gave them the power to become the sons of God.
043	JOH	001	013	These are born, not of blood, nor of the will of flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God.
043	JOH	001	014	And the Word became flesh, and he lived among us, and we saw his glory, glory like that of an only-begotten Son from the Father, full of grace and truth.
043	JOH	001	015	John offers testimony about him, and he cries out, saying: “This is the one about whom I said: ‘He who is to come after me, has been placed ahead of me, because he existed before me.’”
043	JOH	001	016	And from his fullness, we all have received, even grace for grace.
043	JOH	001	017	For the law was given through Moses, but grace and truth came through Jesus Christ.
043	JOH	001	018	No one ever saw God; the only-begotten Son, who is in the bosom of the Father, he himself has described him.
043	JOH	001	019	And this is the testimony of John, when the Jews sent priests and Levites from Jerusalem to him, so that they might ask him, “Who are you?”
043	JOH	001	020	And he confessed it and did not deny it; and what he confessed was: “I am not the Christ.”
043	JOH	001	021	And they questioned him: “Then what are you? Are you Elijah?” And he said, “I am not.” “Are you the Prophet?” And he answered, “No.”
043	JOH	001	022	Therefore, they said to him: “Who are you, so that we may give an answer to those who sent us? What do you say about yourself?”
043	JOH	001	023	He said, “I am a voice crying out in the desert, ‘Make straight the way of the Lord,’ just as the prophet Isaiah said.”
043	JOH	001	024	And some of those who had been sent were from among the Pharisees.
043	JOH	001	025	And they questioned him and said to him, “Then why do you baptize, if you are not the Christ, and not Elijah, and not the Prophet?”
043	JOH	001	026	John answered them by saying: “I baptize with water. But in your midst stands one, whom you do not know.
043	JOH	001	027	The same is he who is to come after me, who has been placed ahead of me, the laces of whose shoes I am not worthy to loosen.”
043	JOH	001	028	These things happened in Bethania, across the Jordan, where John was baptizing.
043	JOH	001	029	On the next day, John saw Jesus coming toward him, and so he said: “Behold, the Lamb of God. Behold, he who takes away the sin of the world.
043	JOH	001	030	This is the one about whom I said, ‘After me arrives a man, who has been placed ahead of me, because he existed before me.’
043	JOH	001	031	And I did not know him. Yet it is for this reason that I come baptizing with water: so that he may be made manifest in Israel.”
043	JOH	001	032	And John offered testimony, saying: “For I saw the Spirit descending from heaven like a dove; and he remained upon him.
043	JOH	001	033	And I did not know him. But he who sent me to baptize with water said to me: ‘He over whom you will see the Spirit descending and remaining upon him, this is the one who baptizes with the Holy Spirit.’
043	JOH	001	034	And I saw, and I gave testimony: that this one is the Son of God.”
043	JOH	001	035	The next day again, John was standing with two of his disciples.
043	JOH	001	036	And catching sight of Jesus walking, he said, “Behold, the Lamb of God.”
043	JOH	001	037	And two disciples were listening to him speaking. And they followed Jesus.
043	JOH	001	038	Then Jesus, turning around and seeing them following him, said to them, “What are you seeking?” And they said to him, “Rabbi (which means in translation, Teacher), where do you live?”
043	JOH	001	039	He said to them, “Come and see.” They went and saw where he was staying, and they stayed with him that day. Now it was about the tenth hour.
043	JOH	001	040	And Andrew, the brother of Simon Peter, was one of the two who had heard about him from John and had followed him.
043	JOH	001	041	First, he found his brother Simon, and he said to him, “We have found the Messiah,” (which is translated as the Christ).
043	JOH	001	042	And he led him to Jesus. And Jesus, gazing at him, said: “You are Simon, son of Jonah. You shall be called Cephas,” (which is translated as Peter).
043	JOH	001	043	On the next day, he wanted to go into Galilee, and he found Philip. And Jesus said to him, “Follow me.”
043	JOH	001	044	Now Philip was from Bethsaida, the city of Andrew and Peter.
043	JOH	001	045	Philip found Nathanael, and he said to him, “We have found the one about whom Moses wrote in the Law and the Prophets: Jesus, the son of Joseph, from Nazareth.”
043	JOH	001	046	And Nathanael said to him, “Can anything good be from Nazareth?” Philip said to him, “Come and see.”
043	JOH	001	047	Jesus saw Nathanael coming toward him, and he said about him, “Behold, an Israelite in whom truly there is no deceit.”
043	JOH	001	048	Nathanael said to him, “From where do you know me?” Jesus responded and said to him, “Before Philip called you, when you were under the fig tree, I saw you.”
043	JOH	001	049	Nathanael answered him and said: “Rabbi, you are the Son of God. You are the King of Israel.”
043	JOH	001	050	Jesus responded and said to him: “Because I told you that I saw you under the fig tree, you believe. Greater things than these, you will see.”
043	JOH	001	051	And he said to him, “Amen, amen, I say to you, you will see heaven opened, and the Angels of God ascending and descending over the Son of man.”
043	JOH	002	001	And on the third day, a wedding was held in Cana of Galilee, and the mother of Jesus was there.
043	JOH	002	002	Now Jesus was also invited to the wedding, with his disciples.
043	JOH	002	003	And when the wine was failing, the mother of Jesus said to him, “They have no wine.”
043	JOH	002	004	And Jesus said to her: “What is that to me and to you, woman? My hour has not yet arrived.”
043	JOH	002	005	His mother said to the servants, “Do whatever he tells you.”
043	JOH	002	006	Now in that place, there were six stone water jars, for the purification ritual of the Jews, containing two or three measures each.
043	JOH	002	007	Jesus said to them, “Fill the water jars with water.” And they filled them to the very top.
043	JOH	002	008	And Jesus said to them, “Now draw from it, and carry it to the chief steward of the feast.” And they took it to him.
043	JOH	002	009	Then, when the chief steward had tasted the water made into wine, since he did not know where it was from, for only the servants who had drawn the water knew, the chief steward called the groom,
043	JOH	002	010	and he said to him: “Every man offers the good wine first, and then, when they have become inebriated, he offers what is worse. But you have kept the good wine until now.”
043	JOH	002	011	This was the beginning of the signs that Jesus accomplished in Cana of Galilee, and it manifested his glory, and his disciples believed in him.
043	JOH	002	012	After this, he descended to Capernaum, with his mother and his brothers and his disciples, but they did not remain there for many days.
043	JOH	002	013	And the Passover of the Jews was near, and so Jesus ascended to Jerusalem.
043	JOH	002	014	And he found, sitting in the temple, sellers of oxen and sheep and doves, and the moneychangers.
043	JOH	002	015	And when he had made something like a whip out of little cords, he drove them all out of the temple, including the sheep and the oxen. And he poured out the brass coins of the moneychangers, and he overturned their tables.
043	JOH	002	016	And to those who were selling doves, he said: “Take these things out of here, and do not make my Father’s house into a house of commerce.”
043	JOH	002	017	And truly, his disciples were reminded that it is written: “Zeal for your house consumes me.”
043	JOH	002	018	Then the Jews responded and said to him, “What sign can you show to us, that you may do these things?”
043	JOH	002	019	Jesus responded and said to them, “Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up.”
043	JOH	002	020	Then the Jews said, “This temple has been built up over forty-six years, and you will raise it up in three days?”
043	JOH	002	021	Yet he was speaking about the Temple of his body.
043	JOH	002	022	Therefore, when he had resurrected from the dead, his disciples were reminded that he had said this, and they believed in the Scriptures and in the word that Jesus had spoken.
043	JOH	002	023	Now while he was at Jerusalem during the Passover, on the day of the feast, many trusted in his name, seeing his signs that he was accomplishing.
043	JOH	002	024	But Jesus did not trust himself to them, because he himself had knowledge of all persons,
043	JOH	002	025	and because he had no need of anyone to offer testimony about a man. For he knew what was within a man.
043	JOH	003	001	Now there was a man among the Pharisees, named Nicodemus, a leader of the Jews.
043	JOH	003	002	He went to Jesus at night, and he said to him: “Rabbi, we know that you have arrived as a teacher from God. For no one would be able to accomplish these signs, which you accomplish, unless God were with him.”
043	JOH	003	003	Jesus responded and said to him, “Amen, amen, I say to you, unless one has been reborn anew, he is not able to see the kingdom of God.”
043	JOH	003	004	Nicodemus said to him: “How could a man be born when he is old? Surely, he cannot enter a second time into his mother’s womb to be reborn?”
043	JOH	003	005	Jesus responded: “Amen, amen, I say to you, unless one has been reborn by water and the Holy Spirit, he is not able to enter into the kingdom of God.
043	JOH	003	006	What is born of the flesh is flesh, and what is born of the Spirit is spirit.
043	JOH	003	007	You should not be amazed that I said to you: You must be born anew.
043	JOH	003	008	The Spirit inspires where he wills. And you hear his voice, but you do not know where he comes from, or where he is going. So it is with all who are born of the Spirit.”
043	JOH	003	009	Nicodemus responded and said to him, “How are these things able to be accomplished?”
043	JOH	003	010	Jesus responded and said to him: “You are a teacher in Israel, and you are ignorant of these things?
043	JOH	003	011	Amen, amen, I say to you, that we speak about what we know, and we testify about what we have seen. But you do not accept our testimony.
043	JOH	003	012	If I have spoken to you about earthly things, and you have not believed, then how will you believe, if I will speak to you about heavenly things?
043	JOH	003	013	And no one has ascended to heaven, except the one who descended from heaven: the Son of man who is in heaven.
043	JOH	003	014	And just as Moses lifted up the serpent in the desert, so also must the Son of man be lifted up,
043	JOH	003	015	so that whoever believes in him may not perish, but may have eternal life.
043	JOH	003	016	For God so loved the world that he gave his only-begotten Son, so that all who believe in him may not perish, but may have eternal life.
043	JOH	003	017	For God did not send his Son into the world, in order to judge the world, but in order that the world may be saved through him.
043	JOH	003	018	Whoever believes in him is not judged. But whoever does not believe is already judged, because he does not believe in the name of the only-begotten Son of God.
043	JOH	003	019	And this is the judgment: that the Light has come into the world, and men loved darkness more than light. For their works were evil.
043	JOH	003	020	For everyone who does evil hates the Light and does not go toward the Light, so that his works may not be corrected.
043	JOH	003	021	But whoever acts in truth goes toward the Light, so that his works may be manifested, because they have been accomplished in God.”
043	JOH	003	022	After these things, Jesus and his disciples went into the land of Judea. And he was living there with them and baptizing.
043	JOH	003	023	Now John was also baptizing, at Aenon near Salim, because there was much water in that place. And they were arriving and being baptized.
043	JOH	003	024	For John had not yet been cast into prison.
043	JOH	003	025	Then a dispute occurred between the disciples of John and the Jews, about purification.
043	JOH	003	026	And they went to John and said to him: “Rabbi, the one who was with you across the Jordan, about whom you offered testimony: behold, he is baptizing and everyone is going to him.”
043	JOH	003	027	John responded and said: “A man is not able to receive anything, unless it has been given to him from heaven.
043	JOH	003	028	You yourselves offer testimony for me that I said, ‘I am not the Christ,’ but that I have been sent before him.
043	JOH	003	029	He who holds the bride is the groom. But the friend of the groom, who stands and listens to Him, rejoices joyfully at the voice of the groom. And so, this, my joy, has been fulfilled.
043	JOH	003	030	He must increase, while I must decrease.
043	JOH	003	031	He who comes from above, is above everything. He who is from below, is of the earth, and he speaks about the earth. He who comes from heaven is above everything.
043	JOH	003	032	And what he has seen and heard, about this he testifies. And no one accepts his testimony.
043	JOH	003	033	Whoever has accepted his testimony has certified that God is truthful.
043	JOH	003	034	For he whom God has sent speaks the words of God. For God does not give the Spirit by measure.
043	JOH	003	035	The Father loves the Son, and he has given everything into his hand.
043	JOH	003	036	Whoever believes in the Son has eternal life. But whoever is unbelieving toward the Son shall not see life; instead the wrath of God remains upon him.”
043	JOH	004	001	And so, when Jesus realized that the Pharisees had heard that Jesus made more disciples and baptized more than John,
043	JOH	004	002	(though Jesus himself was not baptizing, but only his disciples)
043	JOH	004	003	he left behind Judea, and he traveled again to Galilee.
043	JOH	004	004	Now he needed to cross through Samaria.
043	JOH	004	005	Therefore, he went into a city of Samaria which is called Sychar, near the estate which Jacob gave to his son Joseph.
043	JOH	004	006	And Jacob’s well was there. And so Jesus, being tired from the journey, was sitting in a certain way on the well. It was about the sixth hour.
043	JOH	004	007	A woman of Samaria arrived to draw water. Jesus said to her, “Give me to drink.”
043	JOH	004	008	For his disciples had gone into the city in order to buy food.
043	JOH	004	009	And so, that Samaritan woman said to him, “How is it that you, being a Jew, are requesting a drink from me, though I am a Samaritan woman?” For the Jews do not associate with the Samaritans.
043	JOH	004	010	Jesus responded and said to her: “If you knew the gift of God, and who it is who is saying to you, ‘Give me to drink,’ perhaps you would have made a request of him, and he would have given you living water.”
043	JOH	004	011	The woman said to him: “Lord, you do not have anything with which to draw water, and the well is deep. From where, then, do you have living water?
043	JOH	004	012	Surely, you are not greater than our father Jacob, who gave us the well and who drank from it, with his sons and his cattle?”
043	JOH	004	013	Jesus responded and said to her: “All who drink from this water will thirst again.
043	JOH	004	014	But whoever shall drink from the water that I will give to him will not thirst for eternity. Instead, the water that I will give to him will become in him a fountain of water, springing up into eternal life.”
043	JOH	004	015	The woman said to him, “Lord, give me this water, so that I may not thirst and may not come here to draw water.”
043	JOH	004	016	Jesus said to her, “Go, call your husband, and return here.”
043	JOH	004	017	The woman responded and said, “I have no husband.” Jesus said to her: “You have spoken well, in saying, ‘I have no husband.’
043	JOH	004	018	For you have had five husbands, but he whom you have now is not your husband. You have spoken this in truth.”
043	JOH	004	019	The woman said to him: “Lord, I see that you are a Prophet.
043	JOH	004	020	Our fathers worshipped on this mountain, but you say that Jerusalem is the place where one ought to worship.”
043	JOH	004	021	Jesus said to her: “Woman, believe me, the hour is coming when you shall worship the Father, neither on this mountain, nor in Jerusalem.
043	JOH	004	022	You worship what you do not know; we worship what we do know. For salvation is from the Jews.
043	JOH	004	023	But the hour is coming, and it is now, when true worshippers shall worship the Father in spirit and in truth. For the Father also seeks such persons who may worship him.
043	JOH	004	024	God is Spirit. And so, those who worship him must worship in spirit and in truth.”
043	JOH	004	025	The woman said to him: “I know that the Messiah is coming (who is called the Christ). And then, when he will have arrived, he will announce everything to us.”
043	JOH	004	026	Jesus said to her: “I am he, the one who is speaking with you.”
043	JOH	004	027	And then his disciples arrived. And they wondered that he was speaking with the woman. Yet no one said: “What are you seeking?” or, “Why are you talking with her?”
043	JOH	004	028	And so the woman left behind her water jar and went into the city. And she said to the men there:
043	JOH	004	029	“Come and see a man who has told me all the things that I have done. Is he not the Christ?”
043	JOH	004	030	Therefore, they went out of the city and came to him.
043	JOH	004	031	Meanwhile, the disciples petitioned him, saying, “Rabbi, eat.”
043	JOH	004	032	But he said to them, “I have food to eat which you do not know.”
043	JOH	004	033	Therefore, the disciples said to one another, “Could someone have brought him something to eat?”
043	JOH	004	034	Jesus said to them: “My food is to do the will of the One who sent me, so that I may perfect his work.
043	JOH	004	035	Do you not say, ‘There are still four months, and then the harvest arrives?’ Behold, I say to you: Lift up your eyes and look at the countryside; for it is already ripe for the harvest.
043	JOH	004	036	For he who reaps, receives wages and gathers fruit unto eternal life, so that both he who sows and he who reaps may rejoice together.
043	JOH	004	037	For in this the word is true: that it is one who sows, and it is another who reaps.
043	JOH	004	038	I have sent you to reap that for which you did not labor. Others have labored, and you have entered into their labors.”
043	JOH	004	039	Now many of the Samaritans from that city believed in him, because of the word of the woman who was offering testimony: “For he told me all the things that I have done.”
043	JOH	004	040	Therefore, when the Samaritans had come to him, they petitioned him to lodge there. And he lodged there for two days.
043	JOH	004	041	And many more believed in him, because of his own word.
043	JOH	004	042	And they said to the woman: “Now we believe, not because of your speech, but because we ourselves have heard him, and so we know that he is truly the Savior of the world.”
043	JOH	004	043	Then, after two days, he departed from there, and he traveled into Galilee.
043	JOH	004	044	For Jesus himself offered testimony that a Prophet has no honor in his own country.
043	JOH	004	045	And so, when he had arrived in Galilee, the Galileans received him, because they had seen all that he had done at Jerusalem, in the day of the feast. For they also went to the feast day.
043	JOH	004	046	Then he went again into Cana of Galilee, where he made water into wine. And there was a certain ruler, whose son was sick at Capernaum.
043	JOH	004	047	Since he had heard that Jesus came to Galilee from Judea, he sent to him and begged him to come down and heal his son. For he was beginning to die.
043	JOH	004	048	Therefore, Jesus said to him, “Unless you have seen signs and wonders, you do not believe.”
043	JOH	004	049	The ruler said to him, “Lord, come down before my son dies.”
043	JOH	004	050	Jesus said to him, “Go, your son lives.” The man believed the word that Jesus spoke to him, and so he went away.
043	JOH	004	051	Then, as he was going down, his servants met him. And they reported to him, saying that his son was alive.
043	JOH	004	052	Therefore, he asked them at which hour he had become better. And they said to him, “Yesterday, at the seventh hour, the fever left him.”
043	JOH	004	053	Then the father realized that it was at the same hour that Jesus said to him, “Your son lives.” And both he and his entire household believed.
