043	JOH	005	001	After these things, there was a feast day of the Jews, and so Jesus ascended to Jerusalem.
043	JOH	005	002	Now at Jerusalem is the Pool of Evidence, which in Hebrew is known as the Place of Mercy; it has five porticos.
043	JOH	005	003	Along these lay a great multitude of the sick, the blind, the lame, and the withered, waiting for the movement of the water.
043	JOH	005	004	Now at times an Angel of the Lord would descend into the pool, and so the water was moved. And whoever descended first into the pool, after the motion of the water, he was healed of whatever infirmity held him.
043	JOH	005	005	And there was a certain man in that place, having been in his infirmity for thirty-eight years.
043	JOH	005	006	Then, when Jesus had seen him reclining, and when he realized that he had been afflicted for a long time, he said to him, “Do you want to be healed?”
043	JOH	005	007	The invalid answered him: “Lord, I do not have any man to put me in the pool, when the water has been stirred. For as I am going, another descends ahead of me.”
043	JOH	005	008	Jesus said to him, “Rise, take up your stretcher, and walk.”
043	JOH	005	009	And immediately the man was healed. And he took up his stretcher and walked. Now this day was the Sabbath.
043	JOH	005	010	Therefore, the Jews said to the one who had been healed: “It is the Sabbath. It is not lawful for you to take up your stretcher.”
043	JOH	005	011	He answered them, “The one who healed me, he said to me, ‘Take up your stretcher and walk.’”
043	JOH	005	012	Therefore, they questioned him, “Who is that man, who said to you, ‘Take up your bed and walk?’”
043	JOH	005	013	But the one who had been given health did not know who it was. For Jesus had turned aside from the crowd gathered in that place.
043	JOH	005	014	Afterwards, Jesus found him in the temple, and he said to him: “Behold, you have been healed. Do not choose to sin further, otherwise something worse may happen to you.”
043	JOH	005	015	This man went away, and he reported to the Jews that it was Jesus who had given him health.
043	JOH	005	016	Because of this, the Jews were persecuting Jesus, for he was doing these things on the Sabbath.
043	JOH	005	017	But Jesus answered them, “Even now, my Father is working, and I am working.”
043	JOH	005	018	And so, because of this, the Jews were seeking to kill him even more so. For not only did he break the Sabbath, but he even said that God was his Father, making himself equal to God.
043	JOH	005	019	Then Jesus responded and said to them: “Amen, amen, I say to you, the Son is not able to do anything of himself, but only what he has seen the Father doing. For whatever he does, even this does the Son do, similarly.
043	JOH	005	020	For the Father loves the Son, and he shows him all that he himself does. And greater works than these will he show him, so much so that you shall wonder.
043	JOH	005	021	For just as the Father raises the dead and gives life, so also does the Son give life to whomever he wills.
043	JOH	005	022	For the Father does not judge anyone. But he has given all judgment to the Son,
043	JOH	005	023	so that all may honor the Son, just as they honor the Father. Whoever does not honor the Son, does not honor the Father who sent him.
043	JOH	005	024	Amen, amen, I say to you, that whoever hears my word, and believes in him who sent me, has eternal life, and he does not go into judgment, but instead he crosses from death into life.
043	JOH	005	025	Amen, amen, I say to you, that the hour is coming, and it is now, when the dead shall hear the voice of the Son of God; and those who hear it shall live.
043	JOH	005	026	For just as the Father has life in himself, so also has he granted to the Son to have life in himself.
043	JOH	005	027	And he has given him the authority to accomplish judgment. For he is the Son of man.
043	JOH	005	028	Do not be amazed at this. For the hour is coming in which all who are in the grave shall hear the voice of the Son of God.
043	JOH	005	029	And those who have done good shall go forth to the resurrection of life. Yet truly, those who have done evil shall go to the resurrection of judgment.
043	JOH	005	030	I am not able to do anything of myself. As I hear, so do I judge. And my judgment is just. For I do not seek my own will, but the will of him who sent me.
043	JOH	005	031	If I offer testimony about myself, my testimony is not true.
043	JOH	005	032	There is another who offers testimony about me, and I know that the testimony which he offers about me is true.
043	JOH	005	033	You sent to John, and he offered testimony to the truth.
043	JOH	005	034	But I do not accept testimony from man. Instead, I say these things, so that you may be saved.
043	JOH	005	035	He was a burning and shining light. So you were willing, at the time, to exult in his light.
043	JOH	005	036	But I hold a greater testimony than that of John. For the works which the Father has given to me, so that I may complete them, these works themselves that I do, offer testimony about me: that the Father has sent me.
043	JOH	005	037	And the Father who has sent me has himself offered testimony about me. And you have never heard his voice, nor have you beheld his appearance.
043	JOH	005	038	And you do not have his word abiding in you. For the one whom he sent, the same you would not believe.
043	JOH	005	039	Study the Scriptures. For you think that in them you have eternal life. And yet they also offer testimony about me.
043	JOH	005	040	And you are not willing to come to me, so that you may have life.
043	JOH	005	041	I do not accept glory from men.
043	JOH	005	042	But I know you, that you do not have the love of God within you.
043	JOH	005	043	I have come in the name of my Father, and you do not accept me. If another will arrive in his own name, him you will accept.
043	JOH	005	044	How are you able to believe, you who accept glory from one another and yet do not seek the glory that is from God alone?
043	JOH	005	045	Do not consider that I might accuse you with the Father. There is one who accuses you, Moses, in whom you hope.
043	JOH	005	046	For if you were believing in Moses, perhaps you would believe in me also. For he wrote about me.
043	JOH	005	047	But if you do not believe by his writings, how will you believe by my words?”
043	JOH	006	001	After these things, Jesus traveled across the sea of Galilee, which is the Sea of Tiberias.
043	JOH	006	002	And a great multitude was following him, for they saw the signs that he was accomplishing toward those who were infirm.
043	JOH	006	003	Therefore, Jesus went onto a mountain, and he sat down there with his disciples.
043	JOH	006	004	Now the Passover, the feast day of the Jews, was near.
043	JOH	006	005	And so, when Jesus had lifted up his eyes and had seen that a very great multitude came to him, he said to Philip, “From where should we buy bread, so that these may eat?”
043	JOH	006	006	But he said this to test him. For he himself knew what he would do.
043	JOH	006	007	Philip answered him, “Two hundred denarii of bread would not be sufficient for each of them to receive even a little.”
043	JOH	006	008	One of his disciples, Andrew, the brother of Simon Peter, said to him:
