# BOOK	045	ROM	Romans	Romans
045	ROM	001	001	Paul, a servant of Jesus Christ, called as an Apostle, separated for the Gospel of God,
045	ROM	001	002	which he had promised beforehand, through his Prophets, in the Holy Scriptures,
045	ROM	001	003	about his Son, who was made for him from the offspring of David according to the flesh,
045	ROM	001	004	the Son of God, who was predestined in virtue according to the Spirit of sanctification from the resurrection of the dead, our Lord Jesus Christ,
045	ROM	001	005	through whom we have received grace and Apostleship, for the sake of his name, for the obedience of faith among all the Gentiles,
045	ROM	001	006	from whom you also have been called by Jesus Christ:
045	ROM	001	007	To all who are at Rome, the beloved of God, called as saints. Grace to you, and peace, from God our Father and from the Lord Jesus Christ.
045	ROM	001	008	Certainly, I give thanks to my God, through Jesus Christ, first for all of you, because your faith is being announced throughout the entire world.
045	ROM	001	009	For God is my witness, whom I serve in my spirit by the Gospel of his Son, that without ceasing I have kept a remembrance of you
045	ROM	001	010	always in my prayers, pleading that in some way, at some time, I may have a prosperous journey, within the will of God, to come to you.
045	ROM	001	011	For I long to see you, so that I may impart to you a certain spiritual grace to strengthen you,
045	ROM	001	012	specifically, to be consoled together with you through that which is mutual: your faith and mine.
045	ROM	001	013	But I want you to know, brothers, that I have often intended to come to you, (though I have been hindered even to the present time) so that I might obtain some fruit among you also, just as also among the other Gentiles.
045	ROM	001	014	To the Greeks and to the uncivilized, to the wise and to the foolish, I am in debt.
045	ROM	001	015	So within me there is a prompting to evangelize to you also who are at Rome.
045	ROM	001	016	For I am not ashamed of the Gospel. For it is the power of God unto salvation for all believers, the Jew first, and the Greek.
045	ROM	001	017	For the justice of God is revealed within it, by faith unto faith, just as it was written: “For the just one lives by faith.”
045	ROM	001	018	For the wrath of God is revealed from heaven over every impiety and injustice among those men who fend off the truth of God with injustice.
045	ROM	001	019	For what is known about God is manifest in them. For God has manifested it to them.
045	ROM	001	020	For unseen things about him have been made conspicuous, since the creation of the world, being understood by the things that were made; likewise his everlasting virtue and divinity, so much so that they have no excuse.
045	ROM	001	021	For although they had known God, they did not glorify God, nor give thanks. Instead, they became weakened in their thoughts, and their foolish heart was obscured.
045	ROM	001	022	For, while proclaiming themselves to be wise, they became foolish.
045	ROM	001	023	And they exchanged the glory of the incorruptible God for the likeness of an image of corruptible man, and of flying things, and of four-legged beasts, and of serpents.
045	ROM	001	024	For this reason, God handed them over to the desires of their own heart for impurity, so that they afflicted their own bodies with indignities among themselves.
045	ROM	001	025	And they exchanged the truth of God for a lie. And they worshipped and served the creature, rather than the Creator, who is blessed for all eternity. Amen.
045	ROM	001	026	Because of this, God handed them over to shameful passions. For example, their females have exchanged the natural use of the body for a use which is against nature.
045	ROM	001	027	And similarly, the males also, abandoning the natural use of females, have burned in their desires for one another: males doing with males what is disgraceful, and receiving within themselves the recompense that necessarily results from their error.
045	ROM	001	028	And since they did not prove to have God by knowledge, God handed them over to a morally depraved way of thinking, so that they might do those things which are not fitting:
045	ROM	001	029	having been completely filled with all iniquity, malice, fornication, avarice, wickedness; full of envy, murder, contention, deceit, spite, gossiping;
045	ROM	001	030	slanderous, hateful toward God, abusive, arrogant, self-exalting, devisers of evil, disobedient to parents,
045	ROM	001	031	foolish, disorderly; without affection, without fidelity, without mercy.
045	ROM	001	032	And these, though they had known the justice of God, did not understand that those who act in such a manner are deserving of death, and not only those who do these things, but also those who consent to what is done.
045	ROM	002	001	For this reason, O man, each one of you who judges is inexcusable. For by that which you judge another, you condemn yourself. For you do the same things that you judge.
045	ROM	002	002	For we know that the judgment of God is in accord with truth against those who do such things.
045	ROM	002	003	But, O man, when you judge those who do such things as you yourself also do, do you think that you will escape the judgment of God?
045	ROM	002	004	Or do you despise the riches of his goodness and patience and forbearance? Do you not know that the kindness of God is calling you to repentance?
045	ROM	002	005	But in accord with your hard and impenitent heart, you store up wrath for yourself, unto the day of wrath and of revelation by the just judgment of God.
045	ROM	002	006	For he will render to each one according to his works:
045	ROM	002	007	To those who, in accord with patient good works, seek glory and honor and incorruption, certainly, he will render eternal life.
045	ROM	002	008	But to those who are contentious and who do not acquiesce to the truth, but instead trust in iniquity, he will render wrath and indignation.
045	ROM	002	009	Tribulation and anguish are upon every soul of man that works evil: the Jew first, and also the Greek.
045	ROM	002	010	But glory and honor and peace are for all who do what is good: the Jew first, and also the Greek.
045	ROM	002	011	For there is no favoritism with God.
045	ROM	002	012	For whoever had sinned without the law, will perish without the law. And whoever had sinned in the law, will be judged by the law.
045	ROM	002	013	For it is not the hearers of the law who are just before God, but rather it is the doers of the law who shall be justified.
045	ROM	002	014	For when the Gentiles, who do not have the law, do by nature those things which are of the law, such persons, not having the law, are a law unto themselves.
045	ROM	002	015	For they reveal the work of the law written in their hearts, while their conscience renders testimony about them, and their thoughts within themselves also accuse or even defend them,
045	ROM	002	016	unto the day when God shall judge the hidden things of men, through Jesus Christ, according to my Gospel.
045	ROM	002	017	But if you are called by name a Jew, and you rest upon the law, and you find glory in God,
045	ROM	002	018	and you have known his will, and you demonstrate the more useful things, having been instructed by the law:
045	ROM	002	019	you become confident within yourself that you are a guide to the blind, a light to those who are in darkness,
045	ROM	002	020	an instructor to the foolish, a teacher to children, because you have a type of knowledge and truth in the law.
045	ROM	002	021	As a result, you teach others, but you do not teach yourself. You preach that men should not steal, but you yourself steal.
045	ROM	002	022	You speak against adultery, but you commit adultery. You abominate idols, but you commit sacrilege.
045	ROM	002	023	You would glory in the law, but through a betrayal of the law you dishonor God.
