045	ROM	003	005	But if even our injustice points to the justice of God, what shall we say? Could God be unfair for inflicting wrath?
045	ROM	003	006	(I am speaking in human terms.) Let it not be so! Otherwise, how would God judge this world?
045	ROM	003	007	For if the truth of God has abounded, through my falseness, unto his glory, why should I still be judged as such a sinner?
045	ROM	003	008	And should we not do evil, so that good may result? For so we have been slandered, and so some have claimed we said; their condemnation is just.
045	ROM	003	009	What is next? Should we try to excel ahead of them? By no means! For we have accused all Jews and Greeks to be under sin,
045	ROM	003	010	just as it was written: “There is no one who is just.
