045	ROM	005	011	And not only that, but we also glory in God through our Lord Jesus Christ, through whom we have now received reconciliation.
045	ROM	005	012	Therefore, just as through one man sin entered into this world, and through sin, death; so also death was transferred to all men, to all who have sinned.
045	ROM	005	013	For even before the law, sin was in the world, but sin was not imputed while the law did not exist.
045	ROM	005	014	Yet death reigned from Adam until Moses, even in those who have not sinned, in the likeness of the transgression of Adam, who is a figure of him who was to come.
045	ROM	005	015	But the gift is not entirely like the offense. For though by the offense of one, many died, yet much more so, by the grace of one man, Jesus Christ, has the grace and gift of God abounded to many.
045	ROM	005	016	And the sin through one is not entirely like the gift. For certainly, the judgment of one was unto condemnation, but the grace toward many offenses is unto justification.
045	ROM	005	017	For though, by the one offense, death reigned through one, yet so much more so shall those who receive an abundance of grace, both of the gift and of justice, reign in life through the one Jesus Christ.
045	ROM	005	018	Therefore, just as through the offense of one, all men fell under condemnation, so also through the justice of one, all men fall under justification unto life.
045	ROM	005	019	For, just as through the disobedience of one man, many were established as sinners, so also through the obedience of one man, many shall be established as just.
045	ROM	005	020	Now the law entered in such a way that offenses would abound. But where offenses were abundant, grace was superabundant.
045	ROM	005	021	So then, just as sin has reigned unto death, so also may grace reign through justice unto eternal life, through Jesus Christ our Lord.
045	ROM	006	001	So what shall we say? Should we remain in sin, so that grace may abound?
045	ROM	006	002	Let it not be so! For how can we who have died to sin still live in sin?
045	ROM	006	003	Do you not know that those of us who have been baptized in Christ Jesus have been baptized into his death?
045	ROM	006	004	For through baptism we have been buried with him into death, so that, in the manner that Christ rose from the dead, by the glory of the Father, so may we also walk in the newness of life.
045	ROM	006	005	For if we have been planted together, in the likeness of his death, so shall we also be, in the likeness of his resurrection.
045	ROM	006	006	For we know this: that our former selves have been crucified together with him, so that the body which is of sin may be destroyed, and moreover, so that we may no longer serve sin.
045	ROM	006	007	For he who has died has been justified from sin.
045	ROM	006	008	Now if we have died with Christ, we believe that we shall also live together with Christ.
045	ROM	006	009	For we know that Christ, in rising up from the dead, can no longer die: death no longer has dominion over him.
045	ROM	006	010	For in as much as he died for sin, he died once. But in as much as he lives, he lives for God.
045	ROM	006	011	And so, you should consider yourselves to be certainly dead to sin, and to be living for God in Christ Jesus our Lord.
045	ROM	006	012	Therefore, let not sin reign in your mortal body, such that you would obey its desires.
045	ROM	006	013	Nor should you offer the parts of your body as instruments of iniquity for sin. Instead, offer yourselves to God, as if you were living after death, and offer the parts of your body as instruments of justice for God.
045	ROM	006	014	For sin should not have dominion over you. For you are not under the law, but under grace.
045	ROM	006	015	What is next? Should we sin because we are not under the law, but under grace? Let it not be so!
045	ROM	006	016	Do you not know to whom you are offering yourselves as servants under obedience? You are the servants of whomever you obey: whether of sin, unto death, or of obedience, unto justice.
045	ROM	006	017	But thanks be to God that, though you used to be the servants of sin, now you have been obedient from the heart to the very form of the doctrine into which you have been received.
045	ROM	006	018	And having been freed from sin, we have become servants of justice.
045	ROM	006	019	I am speaking in human terms because of the infirmity of your flesh. For just as you offered the parts of your body to serve impurity and iniquity, for the sake of iniquity, so also have you now yielded the parts of your body to serve justice, for the sake of sanctification.
045	ROM	006	020	For though you were once the servants of sin, you have become the children of justice.
045	ROM	006	021	But what fruit did you hold at that time, in those things about which you are now ashamed? For the end of those things is death.
045	ROM	006	022	Yet truly, having been freed now from sin, and having been made servants of God, you hold your fruit in sanctification, and truly its end is eternal life.
045	ROM	006	023	For the wages of sin is death. But the free gift of God is eternal life in Christ Jesus our Lord.
045	ROM	007	001	Or do you not know, brothers, (now I am speaking to those who know the law) that the law has dominion over a man only so long as he lives?
045	ROM	007	002	For example, a woman who is subject to a husband is obligated by the law while her husband lives. But when her husband has died, she is released from the law of her husband.
045	ROM	007	003	Therefore, while her husband lives, if she has been with another man, she should be called an adulteress. But when her husband has died, she is freed from the law of her husband, such that, if she has been with another man, she is not an adulteress.
045	ROM	007	004	And so, my brothers, you also have become dead to the law, through the body of Christ, so that you may be another one who has risen from the dead, in order that we may bear fruit for God.
045	ROM	007	005	For when we were in the flesh, the passions of sins, which were under the law, operated within our bodies, so as to bear fruit unto death.
045	ROM	007	006	But now we have been released from the law of death, by which we were being held, so that now we may serve with a renewed spirit, and not in the old way, by the letter.
045	ROM	007	007	What should we say next? Is the law sin? Let it not be so! But I do not know sin, except through the law. For example, I would not have known about coveting, unless the law said: “You shall not covet.”
045	ROM	007	008	But sin, receiving an opportunity through the commandment, wrought in me all manner of coveting. For apart from the law, sin was dead.
045	ROM	007	009	Now I lived for some time apart from the law. But when the commandment had arrived, sin was revived,
045	ROM	007	010	and I died. And the commandment, which was unto life, was itself found to be unto death for me.
045	ROM	007	011	For sin, receiving an opportunity through the commandment, seduced me, and, through the law, sin killed me.
045	ROM	007	012	And so, the law itself is indeed holy, and the commandment is holy and just and good.
045	ROM	007	013	Then was what is good made into death for me? Let it not be so! But rather sin, in order that it might be known as sin by what is good, wrought death in me; so that sin, through the commandment, might become sinful beyond measure.
045	ROM	007	014	For we know that the law is spiritual. But I am carnal, having been sold under sin.
045	ROM	007	015	For I do things that I do not understand. For I do not do the good that I want to do. But the evil that I hate is what I do.
045	ROM	007	016	So, when I do what I do not want to do, I am in agreement with the law, that the law is good.
045	ROM	007	017	But I am then acting not according to the law, but according to the sin which lives within me.
045	ROM	007	018	For I know that what is good does not live within me, that is, within my flesh. For the willingness to do good lies close to me, but the carrying out of that good, I cannot reach.
045	ROM	007	019	For I do not do the good that I want to do. But instead, I do the evil that I do not want to do.
045	ROM	007	020	Now if I do what I am not willing to do, it is no longer I who am doing it, but the sin which lives within me.
045	ROM	007	021	And so, I discover the law, by wanting to do good within myself, though evil lies close beside me.
045	ROM	007	022	For I am delighted with the law of God, according to the inner man.
045	ROM	007	023	But I perceive another law within my body, fighting against the law of my mind, and captivating me with the law of sin which is in my body.
045	ROM	007	024	Unhappy man that I am, who will free me from this body of death?
045	ROM	007	025	The grace of God, by Jesus Christ our Lord! Therefore, I serve the law of God with my own mind; but with the flesh, the law of sin.
045	ROM	008	001	Therefore, there is now no condemnation for those who are in Christ Jesus, who are not walking according to the flesh.
045	ROM	008	002	For the law of the Spirit of life in Christ Jesus has freed me from the law of sin and death.
045	ROM	008	003	For though this was impossible under the law, because it was weakened by the flesh, God sent his own Son in the likeness of sinful flesh and because of sin, in order to condemn sin in the flesh,
045	ROM	008	004	so that the justification of the law might be fulfilled in us. For we are not walking according to the flesh, but according to the spirit.
045	ROM	008	005	For those who are in agreement with the flesh are mindful of the things of the flesh. But those who are in agreement with the spirit are mindful of the things of the spirit.
045	ROM	008	006	For the prudence of the flesh is death. But the prudence of the spirit is life and peace.
045	ROM	008	007	And the wisdom of the flesh is inimical to God. For it is not subject to the law of God, nor can it be.
045	ROM	008	008	So those who are in the flesh are not able to please God.
045	ROM	008	009	And you are not in the flesh, but in the spirit, if it is true that the Spirit of God lives within you. But if anyone does not have the Spirit of Christ, he does not belong to him.
045	ROM	008	010	But if Christ is within you, then the body is indeed dead, concerning sin, but the spirit truly lives, because of justification.
045	ROM	008	011	But if the Spirit of him who raised up Jesus from the dead lives within you, then he who raised up Jesus Christ from the dead shall also enliven your mortal bodies, by means of his Spirit living within you.
045	ROM	008	012	Therefore, brothers, we are not debtors to the flesh, so as to live according to the flesh.
045	ROM	008	013	For if you live according to the flesh, you will die. But if, by the Spirit, you mortify the deeds of the flesh, you shall live.
045	ROM	008	014	For all those who are led by the Spirit of God are the sons of God.
045	ROM	008	015	And you have not received, again, a spirit of servitude in fear, but you have received the Spirit of the adoption of sons, in whom we cry out: “Abba, Father!”
045	ROM	008	016	For the Spirit himself renders testimony to our spirit that we are the sons of God.
045	ROM	008	017	But if we are sons, then we are also heirs: certainly heirs of God, but also co-heirs with Christ, yet in such a way that, if we suffer with him, we shall also be glorified with him.
045	ROM	008	018	For I consider that the sufferings of this time are not worthy to be compared with that future glory which shall be revealed in us.
045	ROM	008	019	For the anticipation of the creature anticipates the revelation of the sons of God.
045	ROM	008	020	For the creature was made subject to emptiness, not willingly, but for the sake of the One who made it subject, unto hope.
045	ROM	008	021	For the creature itself shall also be delivered from the servitude of corruption, into the liberty of the glory of the sons of God.
045	ROM	008	022	For we know that every creature groans inwardly, as if giving birth, even until now;
045	ROM	008	023	and not only these, but also ourselves, since we hold the first-fruits of the Spirit. For we also groan within ourselves, anticipating our adoption as the sons of God, and the redemption of our body.
045	ROM	008	024	For we have been saved by hope. But a hope which is seen is not hope. For when a man sees something, why would he hope?
045	ROM	008	025	But since we hope for what we do not see, we wait with patience.
045	ROM	008	026	And similarly, the Spirit also helps our weakness. For we do not know how to pray as we ought, but the Spirit himself asks on our behalf with ineffable sighing.
045	ROM	008	027	And he who examines hearts knows what the Spirit seeks, because he asks on behalf of the saints in accordance with God.
045	ROM	008	028	And we know that, for those who love God, all things work together unto good, for those who, in accordance with his purpose, are called to be saints.
045	ROM	008	029	For those whom he foreknew, he also predestined, in conformity with the image of his Son, so that he might be the Firstborn among many brothers.
045	ROM	008	030	And those whom he predestined, he also called. And those whom he called, he also justified. And those whom he justified, he also glorified.
045	ROM	008	031	So, what should we say about these things? If God is for us, who is against us?
045	ROM	008	032	He who did not spare even his own Son, but handed him over for the sake of us all, how could he not also, with him, have given us all things?
045	ROM	008	033	Who will make an accusation against the elect of God? God is the One who justifies;
045	ROM	008	034	who is the one who condemns? Christ Jesus who has died, and who has indeed also risen again, is at the right hand of God, and even now he intercedes for us.
045	ROM	008	035	Then who will separate us from the love of Christ? Tribulation? Or anguish? Or famine? Or nakedness? Or peril? Or persecution? Or the sword?
045	ROM	008	036	For it is as it has been written: “For your sake, we are being put to death all day long. We are being treated like sheep for the slaughter.”
045	ROM	008	037	But in all these things we overcome, because of him who has loved us.
045	ROM	008	038	For I am certain that neither death, nor life, nor Angels, nor Principalities, nor Powers, nor the present things, nor the future things, nor strength,
045	ROM	008	039	nor the heights, nor the depths, nor any other created thing, will be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord.
045	ROM	009	001	I am speaking the truth in Christ; I am not lying. My conscience offers testimony to me in the Holy Spirit,
045	ROM	009	002	because the sadness within me is great, and there is a continuous sorrow in my heart.
045	ROM	009	003	For I was desiring that I myself might be anathemized from Christ, for the sake of my brothers, who are my kinsmen according to the flesh.
045	ROM	009	004	These are the Israelites, to whom belongs adoption as sons, and the glory and the testament, and the giving and following of the law, and the promises.
045	ROM	009	005	Theirs are the fathers, and from them, according to the flesh, is the Christ, who is over all things, blessed God, for all eternity. Amen.
045	ROM	009	006	But it is not that the Word of God has perished. For not all those who are Israelites are of Israel.
045	ROM	009	007	And not all sons are the offspring of Abraham: “For your offspring will be invoked in Isaac.”
045	ROM	009	008	In other words, those who are the sons of God are not those who are sons of the flesh, but those who are sons of the Promise; these are considered to be the offspring.
045	ROM	009	009	For the word of promise is this: “I will return at the proper time. And there shall be a son for Sarah.”
045	ROM	009	010	And she was not alone. For Rebecca also, having conceived by Isaac our father, from one act,
045	ROM	009	011	when the children had not yet been born, and had not yet done anything good or bad (such that the purpose of God might be based on their choice),
045	ROM	009	012	and not because of deeds, but because of a calling, it was said to her: “The elder shall serve the younger.”
045	ROM	009	013	So also it was written: “I have loved Jacob, but I have hated Esau.”
045	ROM	009	014	What should we say next? Is there unfairness with God? Let it not be so!
045	ROM	009	015	For to Moses he says: “I will pity whomever I pity. And I will offer mercy to whomever I will pity.”
045	ROM	009	016	Therefore, it is not based on those who choose, nor on those who excel, but on God who takes pity.
045	ROM	009	017	For Scripture says to the Pharaoh: “I have raised you up for this purpose, so that I may reveal my power by you, and so that my name may be announced to all the earth.”
045	ROM	009	018	Therefore, he takes pity on whomever he wills, and he hardens whomever he wills.
045	ROM	009	019	And so, you would say to me: “Then why does he still find fault? For who can resist his will?”
045	ROM	009	020	O man, who are you to question God? How can the thing that has been formed say to the One who formed him: “Why have you made me this way?”
045	ROM	009	021	And does not the potter have the authority over the clay to make, from the same material, indeed, one vessel unto honor, yet truly another unto disgrace?
045	ROM	009	022	What if God, wanting to reveal his wrath and to make his power known, endured, with much patience, vessels deserving wrath, fit to be destroyed,
045	ROM	009	023	so that he might reveal the wealth of his glory, within these vessels of mercy, which he has prepared unto glory?
045	ROM	009	024	And so it is with those of us whom he has also called, not only from among the Jews, but even from among the Gentiles,
045	ROM	009	025	just as he says in Hosea: “I will call those who were not my people, ‘my people,’ and she who was not beloved, ‘beloved,’ and she who had not obtained mercy, ‘one who has obtained mercy.’
045	ROM	009	026	And this shall be: in the place where it was said to them, ‘You are not my people,’ there they shall be called the sons of the living God.”
045	ROM	009	027	And Isaiah cried out on behalf of Israel: “When the number of the sons of Israel is like the sand of the sea, a remnant shall be saved.
045	ROM	009	028	For he shall complete his word, while abbreviating it out of equity. For the Lord shall accomplish a brief word upon the earth.”
045	ROM	009	029	And it is just as Isaiah predicted: “Unless the Lord of hosts had bequeathed offspring, we would have become like Sodom, and we would have been made similar to Gomorrah.”
045	ROM	009	030	What should we say next? That the Gentiles who did not follow justice have attained justice, even the justice that is of faith.
045	ROM	009	031	Yet truly, Israel, though following the law of justice, has not arrived at the law of justice.
045	ROM	009	032	Why is this? Because they did not seek it from faith, but as if it were from works. For they stumbled over a stumbling block,
045	ROM	009	033	just as it was written: “Behold, I am placing a stumbling block in Zion, and a rock of scandal. But whoever believes in him shall not be confounded.”
045	ROM	010	001	Brothers, certainly the will of my heart, and my prayer to God, is for them unto salvation.
045	ROM	010	002	For I offer testimony to them, that they have a zeal for God, but not according to knowledge.
045	ROM	010	003	For, being ignorant of the justice of God, and seeking to establish their own justice, they have not subjected themselves to the justice of God.
045	ROM	010	004	For the end of the law, Christ, is unto justice for all who believe.
045	ROM	010	005	And Moses wrote, about the justice that is of the law, that the man who will have done justice shall live by justice.
045	ROM	010	006	But the justice that is of faith speaks in this way: Do not say in your heart: “Who shall ascend into heaven?” (that is, to bring Christ down);
045	ROM	010	007	“Or who shall descend into the abyss?” (that is, to call back Christ from the dead).
045	ROM	010	008	But what does Scripture say? “The word is near, in your mouth and in your heart.” This is the word of faith, which we are preaching.
045	ROM	010	009	For if you confess with your mouth the Lord Jesus, and if you believe in your heart that God has raised him up from the dead, you shall be saved.
045	ROM	010	010	For with the heart, we believe unto justice; but with the mouth, confession is unto salvation.
045	ROM	010	011	For Scripture says: “All those who believe in him shall not be confounded.”
045	ROM	010	012	For there is no distinction between Jew and Greek. For the same Lord is over all, richly in all who call upon him.
045	ROM	010	013	For all those who have called upon the name of the Lord shall be saved.
045	ROM	010	014	Then in what way will those who have not believed in him call upon him? Or in what way will those who have not heard of him believe in him? And in what way will they hear of him without preaching?
045	ROM	010	015	And truly, in what way will they preach, unless they have been sent, just as it has been written: “How beautiful are the feet of those who evangelize peace, of those who evangelize what is good!”
045	ROM	010	016	But not all are obedient to the Gospel. For Isaiah says: “Lord, who has believed our report?”
045	ROM	010	017	Therefore, faith is from hearing, and hearing is through the Word of Christ.
045	ROM	010	018	But I say: Have they not heard? For certainly: “Their sound has gone forth throughout all the earth, and their words unto the limits of the whole world.”
045	ROM	010	019	But I say: Has Israel not known? First, Moses says: “I will lead you into a rivalry with those who are not a nation; in the midst of a foolish nation, I will send you into wrath.”
045	ROM	010	020	And Isaiah dares to say: “I was discovered by those who were not seeking me. I appeared openly to those who were not asking about me.”
045	ROM	010	021	Then to Israel he says: “All day long I have stretched out my hands to a people who do not believe and who contradict me.”
045	ROM	011	001	Therefore, I say: Has God driven away his people? Let it not be so! For I, too, am an Israelite of the offspring of Abraham, from the tribe of Benjamin.
045	ROM	011	002	God has not driven away his people, whom he foreknew. And do you not know what Scripture says in Elijah, how he calls upon God against Israel?
045	ROM	011	003	“Lord, they have slain your Prophets. They have overturned your altars. And I alone remain, and they are seeking my life.”
045	ROM	011	004	But what is the Divine response to him? “I have retained for myself seven thousand men, who have not bent their knees before Baal.”
045	ROM	011	005	Therefore, in the same way, again in this time, there is a remnant that has been saved in accord with the choice of grace.
045	ROM	011	006	And if it is by grace, then it is not now by works; otherwise grace is no longer free.
045	ROM	011	007	What is next? What Israel was seeking, he has not obtained. But the elect have obtained it. And truly, these others have been blinded,
045	ROM	011	008	just as it was written: “God has given them a spirit of reluctance: eyes that do not perceive, and ears that do not hear, even until this very day.”
045	ROM	011	009	And David says: “Let their table become like a snare, and a deception, and a scandal, and a retribution for them.
045	ROM	011	010	Let their eyes be obscured, so that they may not see, and so that they may bow down their backs always.”
045	ROM	011	011	Therefore, I say: Have they stumbled in such a way that they should fall? Let it not be so! Instead, by their offense, salvation is with the Gentiles, so that they may be a rival to them.
045	ROM	011	012	Now if their offense is the riches of the world, and if their diminution is the riches of the Gentiles, how much more is their fullness?
045	ROM	011	013	For I say to you Gentiles: Certainly, as long as I am an Apostle to the Gentiles, I will honor my ministry,
045	ROM	011	014	in such a way that I might provoke to rivalry those who are my own flesh, and so that I may save some of them.
045	ROM	011	015	For if their loss is for the reconciliation of the world, what could their return be for, except life out of death?
045	ROM	011	016	For if the first-fruit has been sanctified, so also has the whole. And if the root is holy, so also are the branches.
045	ROM	011	017	And if some of the branches are broken, and if you, being a wild olive branch, are grafted on to them, and you become a partaker of the root and of the fatness of the olive tree,
045	ROM	011	018	do not glorify yourself above the branches. For though you glory, you do not support the root, but the root supports you.
045	ROM	011	019	Therefore, you would say: The branches were broken off, so that I might be grafted on.
045	ROM	011	020	Well enough. They were broken off because of unbelief. But you stand on faith. So do not choose to savor what is exalted, but instead be afraid.
045	ROM	011	021	For if God has not spared the natural branches, perhaps also he might not spare you.
045	ROM	011	022	So then, notice the goodness and the severity of God. Certainly, toward those who have fallen, there is severity; but toward you, there is the goodness of God, if you remain in goodness. Otherwise, you also will be cut off.
045	ROM	011	023	Moreover, if they do not remain in unbelief, they will be grafted on. For God is able to graft them on again.
045	ROM	011	024	So if you have been cut off from the wild olive tree, which is natural to you, and, contrary to nature, you are grafted on to the good olive tree, how much more shall those who are the natural branches be grafted on to their own olive tree?
045	ROM	011	025	For I do not want you to be ignorant, brothers, of this mystery (lest you seem wise only to yourselves) that a certain blindness has occurred in Israel, until the fullness of the Gentiles has arrived.
