045	ROM	011	030	And just as you also, in times past, did not believe in God, but now you have obtained mercy because of their unbelief,
045	ROM	011	031	so also have these now not believed, for your mercy, so that they might obtain mercy also.
045	ROM	011	032	For God has enclosed everyone in unbelief, so that he may have mercy on everyone.
045	ROM	011	033	Oh, the depths of the richness of the wisdom and knowledge of God! How incomprehensible are his judgments, and how unsearchable are his ways!
045	ROM	011	034	For who has known the mind of the Lord? Or who has been his counselor?
045	ROM	011	035	Or who first gave to him, so that repayment would be owed?
045	ROM	011	036	For from him, and through him, and in him are all things. To him is glory, for all eternity. Amen.
045	ROM	012	001	And so, I beg you, brothers, by the mercy of God, that you offer your bodies as a living sacrifice, holy and pleasing to God, with the subservience of your mind.
045	ROM	012	002	And do not choose to be conformed to this age, but instead choose to be reformed in the newness of your mind, so that you may demonstrate what is the will of God: what is good, and what is well-pleasing, and what is perfect.
045	ROM	012	003	For I say, through the grace that has been given to me, to all who are among you: Taste no more than it is necessary to taste, but taste unto sobriety and just as God has distributed a share of the faith to each one.
045	ROM	012	004	For just as, within one body, we have many parts, though all the parts do not have the same role,
045	ROM	012	005	so also we, being many, are one body in Christ, and each one is a part, the one of the other.
045	ROM	012	006	And we each have different gifts, according to the grace that has been given to us: whether prophecy, in agreement with the reasonableness of faith;
045	ROM	012	007	or ministry, in ministering; or he who teaches, in doctrine;
045	ROM	012	008	he who exhorts, in exhortation; he who gives, in simplicity; he who governs, in solicitude; he who shows mercy, in cheerfulness.
045	ROM	012	009	Let love be without falseness: hating evil, clinging to what is good,
045	ROM	012	010	loving one another with fraternal charity, surpassing one another in honor:
045	ROM	012	011	in solicitude, not lazy; in spirit, fervent; serving the Lord;
045	ROM	012	012	in hope, rejoicing; in tribulation, enduring; in prayer, ever-willing;
045	ROM	012	013	in the difficulties of the saints, sharing; in hospitality, attentive.
045	ROM	012	014	Bless those who are persecuting you: bless, and do not curse.
045	ROM	012	015	Rejoice with those who are rejoicing. Weep with those who are weeping.
045	ROM	012	016	Be of the same mind toward one another: not savoring what is exalted, but consenting in humility. Do not choose to seem wise to yourself.
045	ROM	012	017	Render to no one harm for harm. Provide good things, not only in the sight of God, but also in the sight of all men.
045	ROM	012	018	If it is possible, in so far as you are able, be at peace with all men.
045	ROM	012	019	Do not defend yourselves, dearest ones. Instead, step aside from wrath. For it is written: “Vengeance is mine. I shall give retribution, says the Lord.”
045	ROM	012	020	So if an enemy is hungry, feed him; if he is thirsty, give him a drink. For in doing so, you will heap burning coals upon his head.
045	ROM	012	021	Do not allow evil to prevail, instead prevail over evil by means of goodness.
045	ROM	013	001	Let every soul be subject to higher authorities. For there is no authority except from God and those who have been ordained by God.
045	ROM	013	002	And so, whoever resists authority, resists what has been ordained by God. And those who resist are acquiring damnation for themselves.
045	ROM	013	003	For leaders are not a source of fear to those who work good, but to those who work evil. And would you prefer not to be afraid of authority? Then do what is good, and you shall have praise from them.
045	ROM	013	004	For he is a minister of God for you unto good. But if you do what is evil, be afraid. For it is not without reason that he carries a sword. For he is a minister of God; an avenger to execute wrath upon whomever does evil.
045	ROM	013	005	For this reason, it is necessary to be subject, not solely because of wrath, but also because of conscience.
045	ROM	013	006	Therefore, you must also offer tribute. For they are the ministers of God, serving him in this.
045	ROM	013	007	Therefore, render to all whatever is owed. Taxes, to whom taxes is due; revenue, to whom revenue is due; fear, to whom fear is due; honor, to whom honor is due.
045	ROM	013	008	You should owe nothing to anyone, except so as to love one another. For whoever loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law.
045	ROM	013	009	For example: You shall not commit adultery. You shall not kill. You shall not steal. You shall not speak false testimony. You shall not covet. And if there is any other commandment, it is summed up in this word: You shall love your neighbor as yourself.
045	ROM	013	010	The love of neighbor does no harm. Therefore, love is the plenitude of the law.
045	ROM	013	011	And we know the present time, that now is the hour for us to rise up from sleep. For already our salvation is closer than when we first believed.
045	ROM	013	012	The night has passed, and the day draws near. Therefore, let us cast aside the works of darkness, and be clothed with the armor of light.
045	ROM	013	013	Let us walk honestly, as in the daylight, not in carousing and drunkenness, not in promiscuity and sexual immorality, not in contention and envy.
045	ROM	013	014	Instead, be clothed with the Lord Jesus Christ, and make no provision for the flesh in its desires.
045	ROM	014	001	But accept those who are weak in faith, without disputing about ideas.
045	ROM	014	002	For one person believes that he may eat all things, but if another is weak, let him eat plants.
045	ROM	014	003	He who eats should not despise him who does not eat. And he who does not eat should not judge him who eats. For God has accepted him.
045	ROM	014	004	Who are you to judge the servant of another? He stands or falls by his own Lord. But he shall stand. For God is able to make him stand.
045	ROM	014	005	For one person discerns one age from the next. But another discerns unto every age. Let each one increase according to his own mind.
045	ROM	014	006	He who understands the age, understands for the Lord. And he who eats, eats for the Lord; for he gives thanks to God. And he who does not eat, does not eat for the Lord, and he gives thanks to God.
045	ROM	014	007	For none of us lives for himself, and none of us dies for himself.
045	ROM	014	008	For if we live, we live for the Lord, and if we die, we die for the Lord. Therefore, whether we live or die, we belong to the Lord.
045	ROM	014	009	For Christ died and rose again for this purpose: that he might be the ruler of both the dead and the living.
045	ROM	014	010	So then, why do you judge your brother? Or why do you despise your brother? For we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Christ.
045	ROM	014	011	For it is written: “As I live, says the Lord, every knee shall bend to me, and every tongue shall confess to God.”
045	ROM	014	012	And so, each one of us shall offer an explanation of himself to God.
045	ROM	014	013	Therefore, we should no longer judge one another. Instead, judge this to a greater extent: that you should not place an obstacle before your brother, nor lead him astray.
045	ROM	014	014	I know, with confidence in the Lord Jesus, that nothing is unclean in and of itself. But to him who considers anything to be unclean, it is unclean to him.
045	ROM	014	015	For if your brother is grieved because of your food, you are not now walking according to love. Do not allow your food to destroy him for whom Christ died.
045	ROM	014	016	Therefore, what is good for us should not be a cause of blasphemy.
045	ROM	014	017	For the kingdom of God is not food and drink, but rather justice and peace and joy, in the Holy Spirit.
045	ROM	014	018	For he who serves Christ in this, pleases God and is proven before men.
045	ROM	014	019	And so, let us pursue the things that are of peace, and let us keep to the things that are for the edification of one another.
045	ROM	014	020	Do not be willing to destroy the work of God because of food. Certainly, all things are clean. But there is harm for a man who offends by eating.
045	ROM	014	021	It is good to refrain from eating meat and from drinking wine, and from anything by which your brother is offended, or led astray, or weakened.
045	ROM	014	022	Do you have faith? It belongs to you, so hold it before God. Blessed is he who does not judge himself in that by which he is tested.
045	ROM	014	023	But he who discerns, if he eats, is condemned, because it is not of faith. For all that is not of faith is sin.
045	ROM	015	001	But we who are stronger must bear with the feebleness of the weak, and not so as to please ourselves.
045	ROM	015	002	Each one of you should please his neighbor unto good, for edification.
045	ROM	015	003	For even Christ did not please himself, but as it was written: “The reproaches of those who reproached you fell upon me.”
045	ROM	015	004	For whatever was written, was written to teach us, so that, through patience and the consolation of the Scriptures, we might have hope.
045	ROM	015	005	So may the God of patience and solace grant you to be of one mind toward one another, in accord with Jesus Christ,
045	ROM	015	006	so that, together with one mouth, you may glorify the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.
045	ROM	015	007	For this reason, accept one another, just as Christ also has accepted you, in the honor of God.
045	ROM	015	008	For I declare that Christ Jesus was the minister of circumcision because of the truth of God, so as to confirm the promises to the fathers,
045	ROM	015	009	and that the Gentiles are to honor God because of his mercy, just as it was written: “Because of this, I will confess you among the Gentiles, O Lord, and I will sing to your name.”
045	ROM	015	010	And again, he says: “Rejoice, O Gentiles, along with his people.”
045	ROM	015	011	And again: “All Gentiles, praise the Lord; and all peoples, magnify him.”
045	ROM	015	012	And again, Isaiah says: “There shall be a root of Jesse, and he shall rise up to rule the Gentiles, and in him the Gentiles shall hope.”
045	ROM	015	013	So may the God of hope fill you with every joy and with peace in believing, so that you may abound in hope and in the virtue of the Holy Spirit.
045	ROM	015	014	But I am also certain about you, my brothers, that you also have been filled with love, completed with all knowledge, so that you are able to admonish one another.
045	ROM	015	015	But I have written to you, brothers, more boldly than to the others, as if calling you to mind again, because of the grace which has been given to me from God,
045	ROM	015	016	so that I may be a minister of Christ Jesus among the Gentiles, sanctifying the Gospel of God, in order that the oblation of the Gentiles may be made acceptable and may be sanctified in the Holy Spirit.
045	ROM	015	017	Therefore, I have glory in Christ Jesus before God.
045	ROM	015	018	So I dare not speak of any of those things which Christ does not effect through me, unto the obedience of the Gentiles, in word and deed,
045	ROM	015	019	with the power of signs and wonders, by power of the Holy Spirit. For in this way, from Jerusalem, throughout its surroundings, as far as Illyricum, I have replenished the Gospel of Christ.
045	ROM	015	020	And so I have preached this Gospel, not where Christ was known by name, lest I build upon the foundation of another,
045	ROM	015	021	but just as it was written: “Those to whom he was not announced shall perceive, and those who have not heard shall understand.”
045	ROM	015	022	Because of this also, I was greatly hindered in coming to you, and I have been prevented until the present time.
045	ROM	015	023	Yet truly now, having no other destination in these regions, and having already had a great desire to come to you over the past many years,
045	ROM	015	024	when I begin to set out on my journey to Spain, I hope that, as I pass by, I may see you, and I may be guided from there by you, after first having borne some fruit among you.
045	ROM	015	025	But next I will set out for Jerusalem, to minister to the saints.
045	ROM	015	026	For those of Macedonia and Achaia have decided to make a collection for those of the poor among the saints who are at Jerusalem.
045	ROM	015	027	And this has pleased them, because they are in their debt. For, since the Gentiles have become partakers of their spiritual things, they also ought to minister to them in worldly things.
045	ROM	015	028	Therefore, when I have completed this task, and have consigned to them this fruit, I shall set out, by way of you, to Spain.
045	ROM	015	029	And I know that when I come to you I shall arrive with an abundance of the blessings of the Gospel of Christ.
045	ROM	015	030	Therefore, I beg you, brothers, through our Lord Jesus Christ and through the love of the Holy Spirit, that you assist me with your prayers to God on my behalf,
045	ROM	015	031	so that I may be freed from the unfaithful who are in Judea, and so that the oblation of my service may be acceptable to the saints in Jerusalem.
045	ROM	015	032	So may I come to you with joy, through the will of God, and so may I be refreshed with you.
045	ROM	015	033	And may the God of peace be with you all. Amen.
045	ROM	016	001	Now I commend to you our sister Phoebe, who is in the ministry of the church, which is at Cenchreae,
045	ROM	016	002	so that you may receive her in the Lord with the worthiness of the saints, and so that you may be of assistance to her in whatever task she will have need of you. For she herself has also assisted many, and myself also.
045	ROM	016	003	Greet Prisca and Aquila, my helpers in Christ Jesus,
045	ROM	016	004	who have risked their own necks on behalf of my life, for whom I give thanks, not I alone, but also all the churches of the Gentiles;
045	ROM	016	005	and greet the church at their house. Greet Epaenetus, my beloved, who is among the first-fruits of Asia in Christ.
045	ROM	016	006	Greet Mary, who has labored much among you.
045	ROM	016	007	Greet Andronicus and Junias, my kinsmen and fellow captives, who are noble among the Apostles, and who were in Christ prior to me.
045	ROM	016	008	Greet Ampliatus, most beloved to me in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	009	Greet Urbanus, our helper in Christ Jesus, and Stachys, my beloved.
045	ROM	016	010	Greet Apelles, who has been tested in Christ.
045	ROM	016	011	Greet those who are from the household of Aristobulus. Greet Herodian, my kinsman. Greet those who are of the household of Narcissus, who are in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	012	Greet Tryphaena and Tryphosa, who labor in the Lord. Greet Persis, most beloved, who has labored much in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	013	Greet Rufus, elect in the Lord, and his mother and mine.
045	ROM	016	014	Greet Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermas, Patrobas, Hermes, and the brothers who are with them.
045	ROM	016	015	Greet Philologus and Julia, Nereus and his sister, and Olympas, and all the saints who are with them.
045	ROM	016	016	Greet one another with a holy kiss. All the churches of Christ greet you.
045	ROM	016	017	But I beg you, brothers, to take note of those who cause dissensions and offenses contrary to the doctrine that you have learned, and to turn away from them.
045	ROM	016	018	For ones such as these do not serve Christ our Lord, but their inner selves, and, through pleasing words and skillful speaking, they seduce the hearts of the innocent.
045	ROM	016	019	But your obedience has been made known in every place. And so, I rejoice in you. But I want you to be wise in what is good, and simple in what is evil.
045	ROM	016	020	And may the God of peace quickly crush Satan under your feet. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.
045	ROM	016	021	Timothy, my fellow laborer, greets you, and Lucius and Jason and Sosipater, my kinsmen.
045	ROM	016	022	I, Tertius, who wrote this epistle, greet you in the Lord.
045	ROM	016	023	Gaius, my host, and the entire church, greets you. Erastus, the treasurer of the city, greets you, and Quartus, a brother.
045	ROM	016	024	The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all. Amen.
045	ROM	016	025	But to him who is able to confirm you according to my Gospel and the preaching of Jesus Christ, in accord with the revelation of the mystery which has been hidden from time immemorial,
045	ROM	016	026	(which now has been made clear through the Scriptures of the Prophets, in accord with the precept of the eternal God, unto the obedience of faith) which has been made known among all the Gentiles:
045	ROM	016	027	to God, who alone is wise, through Jesus Christ, to him be honor and glory forever and ever. Amen.
#
# BOOK	046	1CO	1 Corinthians	1 Corinthians
046	1CO	001	001	Paul, called as an Apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God; and Sosthenes, a brother:
046	1CO	001	002	to the Church of God which is at Corinth, to those sanctified in Christ Jesus, called to be saints with all who are invoking the name of our Lord Jesus Christ in every place of theirs and of ours.
046	1CO	001	003	Grace and peace to you from God our Father and from the Lord Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	001	004	I give thanks to my God continuously for you because of the grace of God that has been given to you in Christ Jesus.
046	1CO	001	005	By that grace, in all things, you have become wealthy in him, in every word and in all knowledge.
046	1CO	001	006	And so, the testimony of Christ has been strengthened in you.
046	1CO	001	007	In this way, nothing is lacking to you in any grace, as you await the revelation of our Lord Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	001	008	And he, too, will strengthen you, even until the end, without guilt, until the day of the advent of our Lord Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	001	009	God is faithful. Through him, you have been called into the fellowship of his Son, Jesus Christ our Lord.
046	1CO	001	010	And so, I beg you, brothers, by the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that every one of you speak in the same way, and that there be no schisms among you. So may you become perfect, with the same mind and with the same judgment.
046	1CO	001	011	For it has been indicated to me, about you, my brothers, by those who are with Chloes, that there are contentions among you.
046	1CO	001	012	Now I say this because each of you is saying: “Certainly, I am of Paul;” “But I am of Apollo;” “Truly, I am of Cephas;” as well as: “I am of Christ.”
046	1CO	001	013	Has Christ been divided? Was Paul crucified for you? Or were you baptized in the name of Paul?
046	1CO	001	014	I give thanks to God that I have baptized none of you, except Crispus and Gaius,
046	1CO	001	015	lest anyone say that you have been baptized in my name.
046	1CO	001	016	And I also baptized the household of Stephanus. Other than these, I do not recall if I baptized any others.
046	1CO	001	017	For Christ did not send me to baptize, but to evangelize: not through the wisdom of words, lest the cross of Christ become empty.
046	1CO	001	018	For the Word of the Cross is certainly foolishness to those who are perishing. But to those who have been saved, that is, to us, it is the power of God.
046	1CO	001	019	For it has been written: “I will perish the wisdom of the wise, and I will reject the discernment of the prudent.”
046	1CO	001	020	Where are the wise? Where are the scribes? Where are the truth-seekers of this age? Has not God made the wisdom of this world into foolishness?
046	1CO	001	021	For the world did not know God through wisdom, and so, in the wisdom of God, it pleased God to accomplish the salvation of believers, through the foolishness of our preaching.
046	1CO	001	022	For the Jews ask for signs, and the Greeks seek wisdom.
046	1CO	001	023	But we are preaching Christ crucified. Certainly, to the Jews, this is a scandal, and to the Gentiles, this is foolishness.
046	1CO	001	024	But to those who have been called, Jews as well as Greeks, the Christ is the virtue of God and the wisdom of God.
046	1CO	001	025	For what is foolishness to God is considered wise by men, and that which is weakness to God is considered strong by men.
046	1CO	001	026	So take care of your vocation, brothers. For not many are wise according to the flesh, not many are powerful, not many are noble.
046	1CO	001	027	But God has chosen the foolish of the world, so that he may confound the wise. And God has chosen the weak of the world, so that he may confound the strong.
046	1CO	001	028	And God has chosen the ignoble and contemptible of the world, those who are nothing, so that he may reduce to nothing those who are something.
046	1CO	001	029	So then, nothing that is of the flesh should glory in his sight.
046	1CO	001	030	But you are of him in Christ Jesus, who was made by God to be our wisdom and justice and sanctification and redemption.
046	1CO	001	031	And so, in the same way, it was written: “Whoever glories, should glory in the Lord.”
046	1CO	002	001	And so, brothers, when I came to you, announcing to you the testimony of Christ, I did not bring exalted words or lofty wisdom.
046	1CO	002	002	For I did not judge myself to know anything among you, except Jesus Christ, and him crucified.
046	1CO	002	003	And I was with you in weakness, and in fear, and with much trembling.
046	1CO	002	004	And my words and preaching were not the persuasive words of human wisdom, but were a manifestation of the Spirit and of virtue,
046	1CO	002	005	so that your faith would not be based on the wisdom of men, but on the virtue of God.
046	1CO	002	006	Now, we do speak wisdom among the perfect, yet truly, this is not the wisdom of this age, nor that of the leaders of this age, which shall be reduced to nothing.
046	1CO	002	007	Instead, we speak of the wisdom of God in a mystery which has been hidden, which God predestined before this age for our glory,
046	1CO	002	008	something that none of the leaders of this world have known. For if they had known it, they would never have crucified the Lord of glory.
046	1CO	002	009	But this is just as it has been written: “The eye has not seen, and the ear has not heard, nor has it entered into the heart of man, what things God has prepared for those who love him.”
046	1CO	002	010	But God has revealed these things to us through his Spirit. For the Spirit searches all things, even the depths of God.
046	1CO	002	011	And who can know the things that are of a man, except the spirit which is within that man? So also, no one knows the things which are of God, except the Spirit of God.
046	1CO	002	012	But we have not received the spirit of this world, but the Spirit who is of God, so that we may understand the things that have been given to us by God.
046	1CO	002	013	And we are also speaking of these things, not in the learned words of human wisdom, but in the doctrine of the Spirit, bringing spiritual things together with spiritual things.
046	1CO	002	014	But the animal nature of man does not perceive these things that are of the Spirit of God. For it is foolishness to him, and he is not able to understand it, because it must be examined spiritually.
046	1CO	002	015	But the spiritual nature of man judges all things, and he himself may be judged by no man.
046	1CO	002	016	For who has known the mind of the Lord, so that he may instruct him? But we have the mind of Christ.
046	1CO	003	001	And so, brothers, I was not able to speak to you as if to those who are spiritual, but rather as if to those who are carnal. For you are like infants in Christ.
046	1CO	003	002	I gave you milk to drink, not solid food. For you were not yet able. And indeed, even now, you are not able; for you are still carnal.
046	1CO	003	003	And since there is still envy and contention among you, are you not carnal, and are you not walking according to man?
046	1CO	003	004	For if one says, “Certainly, I am of Paul,” while another says, “I am of Apollo,” are you not men? But what is Apollo, and what is Paul?
046	1CO	003	005	We are only the ministers of him in whom you have believed, just as the Lord has granted to each of you.
046	1CO	003	006	I planted, Apollo watered, but God provided the growth.
046	1CO	003	007	And so, neither he who plants, nor he who waters, is anything, but only God, who provides the growth.
046	1CO	003	008	Now he who plants, and he who waters, are one. But each shall receive his proper reward, according to his labors.
046	1CO	003	009	For we are God’s assistants. You are God’s cultivation; you are God’s construction.
046	1CO	003	010	According to the grace of God, which has been given to me, I have laid the foundation like a wise architect. But another builds upon it. So then, let each one be careful how he builds upon it.
046	1CO	003	011	For no one is able to lay any other foundation, in place of that which has been laid, which is Christ Jesus.
046	1CO	003	012	But if anyone builds upon this foundation, whether gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, or stubble,
046	1CO	003	013	each one’s work shall be made manifest. For the day of the Lord shall declare it, because it will be revealed by fire. And this fire will test each one’s work, as to what kind it is.
046	1CO	003	014	If anyone’s work, which he has built upon it, remains, then he will receive a reward.
046	1CO	003	015	If anyone’s work is burned up, he will suffer its loss, but he himself will still be saved, but only as through fire.
046	1CO	003	016	Do you not know that you are the Temple of God, and that the Spirit of God lives within you?
046	1CO	003	017	But if anyone violates the Temple of God, God will destroy him. For the Temple of God is holy, and you are that Temple.
046	1CO	003	018	Let no one deceive himself. If anyone among you seems to be wise in this age, let him become foolish, so that he may be truly wise.
046	1CO	003	019	For the wisdom of this world is foolishness with God. And so it has been written: “I will catch the wise in their own astuteness.”
046	1CO	003	020	And again: “The Lord knows the thoughts of the wise, that they are vain.”
046	1CO	003	021	And so, let no one glory in men.
046	1CO	003	022	For all is yours: whether Paul, or Apollo, or Cephas, or the world, or life, or death, or the present, or the future. Yes, all is yours.
046	1CO	003	023	But you are Christ’s, and Christ is God’s.
046	1CO	004	001	Accordingly, let man consider us to be ministers of Christ and attendants of the mysteries of God.
046	1CO	004	002	Here and now, it is required of attendants that each one be found to be faithful.
046	1CO	004	003	But as for me, it is such a small thing to be judged by you, or by the age of mankind. And neither do I judge myself.
046	1CO	004	004	For I have nothing on my conscience. But I am not justified by this. For the Lord is the One who judges me.
046	1CO	004	005	And so, do not choose to judge before the time, until the Lord returns. He will illuminate the hidden things of the darkness, and he will make manifest the decisions of hearts. And then each one shall have praise from God.
046	1CO	004	006	And so, brothers, I have presented these things in myself and in Apollo, for your sakes, so that you may learn, through us, that no one should be inflated against one person and for another, not beyond what has been written.
046	1CO	004	007	For what distinguishes you from another? And what do you have that you have not received? But if you have received it, why do you glory, as if you had not received it?
046	1CO	004	008	So, now you have been filled, and now you have been made wealthy, as if to reign without us? But I wish that you would reign, so that we, too, might reign with you!
046	1CO	004	009	For I think that God has presented us as the last Apostles, as those destined for death. For we have been made into a spectacle for the world, and for Angels, and for men.
046	1CO	004	010	So we are fools because of Christ, but you are discerning in Christ? We are weak, but you are strong? You are noble, but we are ignoble?
046	1CO	004	011	Even to this very hour, we hunger and thirst, and we are naked and repeatedly beaten, and we are unsteady.
046	1CO	004	012	And we labor, working with our own hands. We are slandered, and so we bless. We suffer and endure persecution.
046	1CO	004	013	We are cursed, and so we pray. We have become like the refuse of this world, like the reside of everything, even until now.
046	1CO	004	014	I am not writing these things in order to confound you, but in order to admonish you, as my dearest sons.
046	1CO	004	015	For you might have ten thousand instructors in Christ, but not so many fathers. For in Christ Jesus, through the Gospel, I have begotten you.
046	1CO	004	016	Therefore, I beg you, be imitators of me, just as I am of Christ.
046	1CO	004	017	For this reason, I have sent you Timothy, who is my dearest son, and who is faithful in the Lord. He will remind you of my ways, which are in Christ Jesus, just as I teach everywhere, in every church.
046	1CO	004	018	Certain persons have become inflated in thinking that I would not return to you.
046	1CO	004	019	But I will return to you soon, if the Lord is willing. And I will consider, not the words of those who are inflated, but the virtue.
046	1CO	004	020	For the kingdom of God is not in words, but in virtue.
046	1CO	004	021	What would you prefer? Should I return to you with a rod, or with charity and a spirit of meekness?
046	1CO	005	001	Above all else, it is being said that there is fornication among you, even fornication of a such kind that is not among the Gentiles, so that someone would have the wife of his father.
046	1CO	005	002	And yet you are inflated, and you have not instead been grieved, so that he who has done this thing would be taken away from your midst.
046	1CO	005	003	Certainly, though absent in body, I am present in spirit. Thus, I have already judged, as if I were present, him who has done this.
046	1CO	005	004	In the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, you have been gathered together with my spirit, in the power of our Lord Jesus,
046	1CO	005	005	to hand over such a one as this to Satan, for the destruction of the flesh, so that the spirit may be saved in the day of our Lord Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	005	006	It is not good for you to glory. Do you not know that a little leaven corrupts the entire mass?
046	1CO	005	007	Purge the old leaven, so that you may become the new bread, for you are unleavened. For Christ, our Passover, has now been immolated.
046	1CO	005	008	And so, let us feast, not with the old leaven, not with the leaven of malice and wickedness, but with the unleavened bread of sincerity and truth.
046	1CO	005	009	As I have written to you in an epistle: “Do not associate with fornicators,”
046	1CO	005	010	certainly not with the fornicators of this world, nor with the greedy, nor with robbers, nor with the servants of idolatry. Otherwise, you ought to depart from this world.
046	1CO	005	011	But now I have written to you: do not associate with anyone who is called a brother and yet is a fornicator, or greedy, or a servant of idolatry, or a slanderer, or inebriated, or a robber. With such a one as this, do not even take food.
046	1CO	005	012	For what have I to do with judging those who are outside? But do not even you yourselves judge those who are inside?
046	1CO	005	013	For those who are outside, God will judge. But send this evil person away from yourselves.
046	1CO	006	001	How is it that anyone of you, having a dispute against another, would dare to be judged before the iniquitous, and not before the saints?
046	1CO	006	002	Or do you not know that the saints from this age shall judge it? And if the world is to be judged by you, are you unworthy, then, to judge even the smallest matters?
046	1CO	006	003	Do you not know that we shall judge angels? How much more the things of this age?
046	1CO	006	004	Therefore, if you have matters to judge concerning this age, why not appoint those who are most contemptible in the Church to judge these things!
046	1CO	006	005	But I am speaking so as to shame you. Is there no one among you wise enough, so that he might be able to judge between his brothers?
046	1CO	006	006	Instead, brother contends against brother in court, and this before the unfaithful!
046	1CO	006	007	Now there is certainly an offense among you, beyond everything else, when you have court cases against one another. Should you not accept injury instead? Should you not endure being cheated instead?
046	1CO	006	008	But you are doing the injuring and the cheating, and this toward brothers!
046	1CO	006	009	Do you not know that the iniquitous will not possess the kingdom of God? Do not choose to wander astray. For neither fornicators, nor servants of idolatry, nor adulterers,
046	1CO	006	010	nor the effeminate, nor males who sleep with males, nor thieves, nor the avaricious, nor the inebriated, nor slanderers, nor the rapacious shall possess the kingdom of God.
046	1CO	006	011	And some of you were like this. But you have been absolved, but you have been sanctified, but you have been justified: all in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ and in the Spirit of our God.
046	1CO	006	012	All is lawful to me, but not all is expedient. All is lawful to me, but I will not be driven back by the authority of anyone.
046	1CO	006	013	Food is for the stomach, and the stomach is for food. But God shall destroy both the stomach and food. And the body is not for fornication, but rather for the Lord; and the Lord is for the body.
046	1CO	006	014	Truly, God has raised up the Lord, and he will raise us up by his power.
046	1CO	006	015	Do you not know that your bodies are a part of Christ? So then, should I take a part of Christ and make it a part of a harlot? Let it not be so!
046	1CO	006	016	And do you not know that whoever is joined to a harlot becomes one body? “For the two,” he said, “shall be as one flesh.”
046	1CO	006	017	But whoever is joined to the Lord is one spirit.
046	1CO	006	018	Flee from fornication. Every sin whatsoever that a man commits is outside of the body, but whoever fornicates, sins against his own body.
046	1CO	006	019	Or do you not know that your bodies are the Temple of the Holy Spirit, who is in you, whom you have from God, and that you are not your own?
046	1CO	006	020	For you have been bought at a great price. Glorify and carry God in your body.
046	1CO	007	001	Now concerning the things about which you wrote to me: It is good for a man not to touch a woman.
046	1CO	007	002	But, because of fornication, let each man have his own wife, and let each woman have her own husband.
046	1CO	007	003	A husband should fulfill his obligation to his wife, and a wife should also act similarly toward her husband.
046	1CO	007	004	It is not the wife, but the husband, who has power over her body. But, similarly also, it is not the husband, but the wife, who has power over his body.
046	1CO	007	005	So, do not fail in your obligations to one another, except perhaps by consent, for a limited time, so that you may empty yourselves for prayer. And then, return together again, lest Satan tempt you by means of your abstinence.
046	1CO	007	006	But I am saying this, neither as an indulgence, nor as a commandment.
046	1CO	007	007	For I would prefer it if you were all like myself. But each person has his proper gift from God: one in this way, yet another in that way.
046	1CO	007	008	But I say to the unmarried and to widows: It is good for them, if they would remain as they are, just as I also am.
046	1CO	007	009	But if they cannot restrain themselves, they should marry. For it is better to marry, than to be burned.
046	1CO	007	010	But to those who have been joined in matrimony, it is not I who commands you, but the Lord: a wife is not to separate from her husband.
046	1CO	007	011	But if she has separated from him, she must remain unmarried, or be reconciled to her husband. And a husband should not divorce his wife.
046	1CO	007	012	Concerning the rest, I am speaking, not the Lord. If any brother has an unbelieving wife, and she consents to live with him, he should not divorce her.
046	1CO	007	013	And if any woman has an unbelieving husband, and he consents to live with her, she should not divorce her husband.
046	1CO	007	014	For the unbelieving husband has been sanctified through the believing wife, and the unbelieving wife has been sanctified through the believing husband. Otherwise, your children would be unclean, whereas instead they are holy.
046	1CO	007	015	But if the unbeliever departs, let him depart. For a brother or sister cannot be made subject to servitude in this way. For God has called us to peace.
046	1CO	007	016	And how do you know, wife, whether you will save your husband? Or how do you know, husband, whether you will save your wife?
046	1CO	007	017	However, let each one walk just as the Lord has distributed to him, each one just as God has called him. And thus do I teach in all the churches.
046	1CO	007	018	Has any circumcised man been called? Let him not cover his circumcision. Has any uncircumcised man been called? Let him not be circumcised.
046	1CO	007	019	Circumcision is nothing, and uncircumcision is nothing; there is only the observance of the commandments of God.
046	1CO	007	020	Let each and every one remain in the same calling to which he was called.
046	1CO	007	021	Are you a servant who has been called? Do not be concerned about it. But if you ever have the ability to be free, make use of it.
046	1CO	007	022	For any servant who has been called in the Lord is free in the Lord. Similarly, any free person who has been called is a servant in Christ.
046	1CO	007	023	You have been bought with a price. Do not be willing to become the servants of men.
046	1CO	007	024	Brothers, let each one, in whatever state he was called, remain in that state with God.
046	1CO	007	025	Now, concerning virgins, I have no commandment from the Lord. But I give counsel, as one who has obtained the mercy of the Lord, so as to be faithful.
046	1CO	007	026	Therefore, I consider this to be good, because of the present necessity: that it is good for a man to be such as I am.
046	1CO	007	027	Are you bound to a wife? Do not seek to be freed. Are you free of a wife? Do not seek a wife.
046	1CO	007	028	But if you take a wife, you have not sinned. And if a virgin has married, she has not sinned. Even so, such as these will have the tribulation of the flesh. But I would spare you from this.
046	1CO	007	029	And so, this is what I say, brothers: The time is short. What remains of it is such that: those who have wives should be as if they had none;
046	1CO	007	030	and those who weep, as though they were not weeping; and those who rejoice, as if they were not rejoicing; and those who buy, as if they possessed nothing;
046	1CO	007	031	and those who use the things of this world, as if they were not using them. For the figure of this world is passing away.
046	1CO	007	032	But I would prefer you to be without worry. Whoever is without a wife is worried about the things of the Lord, as to how he may please God.
046	1CO	007	033	But whoever is with a wife is worried about the things of the world, as to how he may please his wife. And so, he is divided.
046	1CO	007	034	And the unmarried woman and the virgin think about the things that are of the Lord, so that she may be holy in body and in spirit. But she who is married thinks about the things that are of the world, as to how she may please her husband.
046	1CO	007	035	Furthermore, I am saying this for your own benefit, not in order to cast a snare over you, but toward whatever is honest and whatever may provide you with the ability to be without hindrance, so as to worship the Lord.
046	1CO	007	036	But if any man considers himself to seem dishonorable, concerning a virgin who is of adult age, and so it ought to be, he may do as he wills. If he marries her, he does not sin.
046	1CO	007	037	But if he has decided firmly in his heart, and he does not have any obligation, but only the power of his free will, and if he has judged this in his heart, to let her remain a virgin, he does well.
046	1CO	007	038	And so, he who joins with his virgin in matrimony does well, and he who does not join with her does better.
046	1CO	007	039	A woman is bound under the law for as long as her husband lives. But if her husband has died, she is free. She may marry whomever she wishes, but only in the Lord.
046	1CO	007	040	But she will be more blessed, if she remains in this state, in accord with my counsel. And I think that I, too, have the Spirit of God.
046	1CO	008	001	Now concerning those things that are sacrificed to idols: we know that we all have knowledge. Knowledge puffs up, but charity builds up.
046	1CO	008	002	But if anyone considers himself to know anything, he does not yet know in the way that he ought to know.
046	1CO	008	003	For if anyone loves God, he is known by him.
046	1CO	008	004	But as to the foods that are immolated to idols, we know that an idol in the world is nothing, and that no one is God, except One.
046	1CO	008	005	For although there are things that are called gods, whether in heaven or on earth, (if one even considers there to be many gods and many lords)
046	1CO	008	006	yet we know that there is only one God, the Father, from whom all things are, and in whom we are, and one Lord Jesus Christ, through whom all things are, and by whom we are.
046	1CO	008	007	But knowledge is not in everyone. For some persons, even now, with consent to an idol, eat what has been sacrificed to an idol. And their conscience, being infirm, becomes polluted.
046	1CO	008	008	Yet food does not commend us to God. For if we eat, we will not have more, and if we do not eat, we will not have less.
046	1CO	008	009	But be careful not to let your liberty become a cause of sin to those who are weak.
046	1CO	008	010	For if anyone sees someone with knowledge sitting down to eat in idolatry, will not his own conscience, being infirm, be emboldened to eat what has been sacrificed to idols?
046	1CO	008	011	And should an infirm brother perish by your knowledge, even though Christ died for him?
046	1CO	008	012	So when you sin in this way against the brothers, and you harm their weakened conscience, then you sin against Christ.
046	1CO	008	013	Because of this, if food leads my brother to sin, I will never eat meat, lest I lead my brother to sin.
046	1CO	009	001	Am I not free? Am I not an Apostle? Have I not seen Christ Jesus our Lord? Are you not my work in the Lord?
046	1CO	009	002	And if I am not an Apostle to others, yet still I am to you. For you are the seal of my Apostleship in the Lord.
046	1CO	009	003	My defense with those who question me is this:
046	1CO	009	004	Do we not have the authority to eat and to drink?
046	1CO	009	005	Do we not have the authority to travel around with a woman who is a sister, just as do the other Apostles, and the brothers of the Lord, and Cephas?
046	1CO	009	006	Or is it only myself and Barnabas who do not have the authority to act in this way?
046	1CO	009	007	Who has ever served as a soldier and paid his own stipend? Who plants a vineyard and does not eat from its produce? Who pastures a flock and does not drink from the milk of the flock?
046	1CO	009	008	Am I saying these things according to man? Or does the law not also say these things?
046	1CO	009	009	For it is written in the law of Moses: “You shall not bind the mouth of an ox, while it is treading out the grain.” Is God here concerned with the oxen?
046	1CO	009	010	Or is he saying this, indeed, for our sake? These things were written specifically for us, because he who plows, ought to plow in hope, and he who threshes, too, in hope of receiving the produce.
046	1CO	009	011	If we have sown spiritual things in you, is it important if we harvest from your worldly things?
046	1CO	009	012	If others are sharers in this authority over you, why are we not more entitled? And yet we have not used this authority. Instead, we bear all things, lest we give any hindrance to the Gospel of Christ.
046	1CO	009	013	Do you not know that those who work in the holy place eat the things that are for the holy place, and that those who serve at the altar also share with the altar?
046	1CO	009	014	So, too, has the Lord ordained that those who announce the Gospel should live by the Gospel.
046	1CO	009	015	Yet I have used none of these things. And I have not written so that these things may be done for me. For it is better for me to die, rather than to let anyone empty out my glory.
046	1CO	009	016	For if I preach the Gospel, it is not glory for me. For an obligation has been laid upon me. And woe to me, if I do not preach the Gospel.
046	1CO	009	017	For if I do this willingly, I have a reward. But if I do this reluctantly, a dispensation is granted to me.
046	1CO	009	018	And what, then, would be my reward? So, when preaching the Gospel, I should give the Gospel without taking, so that I may not misuse my authority in the Gospel.
046	1CO	009	019	For when I was a free man to all, I made myself the servant of all, so that I might gain all the more.
046	1CO	009	020	And so, to the Jews, I became like a Jew, so that I might gain the Jews.
046	1CO	009	021	To those who are under the law, I became as if I were under the law, (though I was not under the law) so that I might gain those who were under the law. To those who were without the law, I became as if I were without the law, (though I was not without the law of God, being in the law of Christ) so that I might gain those who were without the law.
046	1CO	009	022	To the weak, I became weak, so that I might gain the weak. To all, I became all, so that I might save all.
046	1CO	009	023	And I do everything for the sake of the Gospel, so that I may become its partner.
046	1CO	009	024	Do you not know that, of those who run in a race, all of them, certainly, are runners, but only one achieves the prize. Similarly, you must run, so that you may achieve.
046	1CO	009	025	And one who competes in a contest abstains from all things. And they do this, of course, so that they may achieve a corruptible crown. But we do this, so that we may achieve what is incorruptible.
046	1CO	009	026	And so I run, but not with uncertainty. And so I fight, but not by flailing in the air.
046	1CO	009	027	Instead, I chastise my body, so as to redirect it into servitude. Otherwise, I might preach to others, but become myself an outcast.
046	1CO	010	001	For I do not want you to be ignorant, brothers, that our fathers were all under the cloud, and they all went across the sea.
046	1CO	010	002	And in Moses, they all were baptized, in the cloud and in the sea.
046	1CO	010	003	And they all ate of the same spiritual food.
046	1CO	010	004	And they all drank of the same spiritual drink. And so, they all were drinking of the spiritual rock seeking to obtain them; and that rock was Christ.
046	1CO	010	005	But with most of them, God was not well-pleased. For they were struck down in the desert.
046	1CO	010	006	Now these things were done as an example for us, so that we might not desire evil things, just as they desired.
046	1CO	010	007	And so, do not take part in idolatry, as some of them did, just as it was written: “The people sat down to eat and to drink, and then they rose up to amuse themselves.”
046	1CO	010	008	And let us not commit fornication, as some of them fornicated, and so twenty-three thousand fell on one day.
046	1CO	010	009	And let us not tempt Christ, as some of them tempted, and so they perished by serpents.
046	1CO	010	010	And you should not murmur, as some of them murmured, and so they perished by the destroyer.
046	1CO	010	011	Now all of these things happened to them as an example, and so they have been written for our correction, because the final age has fallen upon us.
046	1CO	010	012	And so, whosoever considers himself to be standing, let him be careful not to fall.
046	1CO	010	013	Temptation should not take hold of you, except what is human. For God is faithful, and he will not permit you to be tempted beyond your ability. Instead, he will effect his Providence, even during temptation, so that you may be able to bear it.
046	1CO	010	014	Because of this, most beloved of mine, flee from the worship of idols.
046	1CO	010	015	Since I am speaking to those who are prudent, judge what I say for yourselves.
046	1CO	010	016	The cup of benediction that we bless, is it not a communion in the Blood of Christ? And the bread that we break, is it not a participation in the Body of the Lord?
046	1CO	010	017	Through the one bread, we, though many, are one body: all of us who are partakers of the one bread.
046	1CO	010	018	Consider Israel, according to the flesh. Are not those who eat from the sacrifices partakers of the altar?
046	1CO	010	019	What is next? Should I say that what is immolated to idols is anything? Or that the idol is anything?
046	1CO	010	020	But the things that the Gentiles immolate, they immolate to demons, and not to God. And I do not want you to become partakers with demons.
046	1CO	010	021	You cannot drink the cup of the Lord, and the cup of demons. You cannot be partakers of the table of the Lord, and partakers of the table of demons.
046	1CO	010	022	Or should we provoke the Lord to jealousy? Are we stronger than he is? All is lawful to me, but not all is expedient.
046	1CO	010	023	All is lawful to me, but not all is edifying.
046	1CO	010	024	Let no one seek for himself, but for others.
046	1CO	010	025	Whatever is sold in the market, you may eat, without asking questions for the sake of conscience.
046	1CO	010	026	“The earth and all its fullness belong to the Lord.”
046	1CO	010	027	If you are invited by any unbelievers, and you are willing to go, you may eat whatever is set before you, without asking questions for the sake of conscience.
046	1CO	010	028	But if anyone says, “This has been sacrificed to idols,” do not eat it, for the sake of the one who told you, and for the sake of conscience.
046	1CO	010	029	But I am referring to the conscience of the other person, not to yours. For why should my liberty be judged by the conscience of another?
046	1CO	010	030	If I partake with thanksgiving, why should I be slandered over that for which I give thanks?
046	1CO	010	031	Therefore, whether you eat or drink, or whatever else you may do, do everything for the glory of God.
046	1CO	010	032	Be without offense toward the Jews, and toward the Gentiles, and toward the Church of God,
046	1CO	010	033	just as I also, in all things, please everyone, not seeking what is best for myself, but what is best for many others, so that they may be saved.
046	1CO	011	001	Be imitators of me, as I also am of Christ.
046	1CO	011	002	Now I praise you, brothers, because you are mindful of me in everything, in such a way as to hold to my precepts as I have handed them down to you.
046	1CO	011	003	So I want you to know that the head of every man is Christ. But the head of woman is man. Yet truly, the head of Christ is God.
046	1CO	011	004	Every man praying or prophesying with his head covered disgraces his head.
046	1CO	011	005	But every woman praying or prophesying with her head not covered disgraces her head. For it is the same as if her head were shaven.
046	1CO	011	006	So if a woman is not veiled, let her hair be cut off. Truly then, if it is a disgrace for a woman to have her hair cut off, or to have her head shaven, then she should cover her head.
046	1CO	011	007	Certainly, a man ought not to cover his head, for he is the image and glory of God. But woman is the glory of man.
046	1CO	011	008	For man is not of woman, but woman is of man.
046	1CO	011	009	And indeed, man was not created for woman, but woman was created for man.
046	1CO	011	010	Therefore, a woman ought to have a sign of authority on her head, because of the Angels.
046	1CO	011	011	Yet truly, man would not exist without woman, nor would woman exist without man, in the Lord.
046	1CO	011	012	For just as woman came into existence from man, so also does man exist through woman. But all things are from God.
046	1CO	011	013	Judge for yourselves. Is it proper for a woman to pray to God unveiled?
046	1CO	011	014	Does not even nature herself teach you that, indeed, if a man grows his hair long, it is a disgrace for him?
046	1CO	011	015	Yet truly, if a woman grows her hair long, it is a glory for her, because her hair has been given to her as a covering.
046	1CO	011	016	But if anyone has a mind to be contentious, we have no such custom, nor does the Church of God.
046	1CO	011	017	Now I caution you, without praising, about this: that you assemble together, and not for better, but for worse.
046	1CO	011	018	First of all, indeed, I hear that when you assemble together in the church, there are schisms among you. And I believe this, in part.
046	1CO	011	019	For there must also be heresies, so that those who have been tested may be made manifest among you.
046	1CO	011	020	And so, when you assemble together as one, it is no longer in order to eat the Lord’s supper.
046	1CO	011	021	For each one first takes his own supper to eat. And as a result, one person is hungry, while another is inebriated.
046	1CO	011	022	Do you not have houses, in which to eat and drink? Or do you have such contempt for the Church of God that you would confound those who do not have such contempt? What should I say to you? Should I praise you? I am not praising you in this.
046	1CO	011	023	For I have received from the Lord what I have also delivered to you: that the Lord Jesus, on the same night that he was handed over, took bread,
046	1CO	011	024	and giving thanks, he broke it, and said: “Take and eat. This is my body, which shall be given up for you. Do this in remembrance of me.”
046	1CO	011	025	Similarly also, the cup, after he had eaten supper, saying: “This cup is the new covenant in my blood. Do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of me.”
046	1CO	011	026	For whenever you eat this bread and drink this cup, you proclaim the death of the Lord, until he returns.
046	1CO	011	027	And so, whoever eats this bread, or drinks from the cup of the Lord, unworthily, shall be liable of the body and blood of the Lord.
046	1CO	011	028	But let a man examine himself, and, in this way, let him eat from that bread, and drink from that cup.
046	1CO	011	029	For whoever eats and drinks unworthily, eats and drinks a sentence against himself, not discerning it to be the body of the Lord.
046	1CO	011	030	As a result, many are weak and sick among you, and many have fallen asleep.
046	1CO	011	031	But if we ourselves were discerning, then certainly we would not be judged.
046	1CO	011	032	Yet when we are judged, we are being corrected by the Lord, so that we might not be condemned along with this world.
046	1CO	011	033	And so, my brothers, when you assemble together to eat, be attentive to one another.
046	1CO	011	034	If anyone is hungry, let him eat at home, so that you may not assemble together unto judgment. As for the rest, I will set it in order when I arrive.
046	1CO	012	001	Now concerning spiritual things, I do not want you to be ignorant, brothers.
046	1CO	012	002	You know that when you were Gentiles, you approached mute idols, doing what you were led to do.
046	1CO	012	003	Because of this, I would have you know that no one speaking in the Spirit of God utters a curse against Jesus. And no one is able to say that Jesus is Lord, except in the Holy Spirit.
046	1CO	012	004	Truly, there are diverse graces, but the same Spirit.
046	1CO	012	005	And there are diverse ministries, but the same Lord.
046	1CO	012	006	And there are diverse works, but the same God, who works everything in everyone.
046	1CO	012	007	However, the manifestation of the Spirit is given to each one toward what is beneficial.
046	1CO	012	008	Certainly, to one, through the Spirit, is given words of wisdom; but to another, according to the same Spirit, words of knowledge;
046	1CO	012	009	to another, in the same Spirit, faith; to another, in the one Spirit, the gift of healing;
046	1CO	012	010	to another, miraculous works; to another, prophecy; to another, the discernment of spirits; to another, different kinds of languages; to another, the interpretation of words.
046	1CO	012	011	But one and the same Spirit works all these things, distributing to each one according to his will.
046	1CO	012	012	For just as the body is one, and yet has many parts, so all the parts of the body, though they are many, are only one body. So also is Christ.
046	1CO	012	013	And indeed, in one Spirit, we were all baptized into one body, whether Jews or Gentiles, whether servant or free. And we all drank in the one Spirit.
046	1CO	012	014	For the body, too, is not one part, but many.
046	1CO	012	015	If the foot were to say, “Because I am not the hand, I am not of the body,” would it then not be of the body?
046	1CO	012	016	And if the ear were to say, “Because I am not the eye, I am not of the body,” would it then not be of the body?
046	1CO	012	017	If the whole body were the eye, how would it hear? If the whole were hearing, how would it smell?
046	1CO	012	018	But instead, God has placed the parts, each one of them, in the body, just as it has pleased him.
046	1CO	012	019	So if they were all one part, how would it be a body?
046	1CO	012	020	But instead, there are many parts, indeed, yet one body.
046	1CO	012	021	And the eye cannot say to the hand, “I have no need for your works.” And again, the head cannot say to the feet, “You are of no use to me.”
046	1CO	012	022	In fact, so much more necessary are those parts of the body which seem to be weaker.
046	1CO	012	023	And though we consider certain parts of the body to be less noble, we surround these with more abundant dignity, and so, those parts which are less presentable end up with more abundant respect.
046	1CO	012	024	However, our presentable parts have no such need, since God has tempered the body together, distributing the more abundant honor to that which has the need,
046	1CO	012	025	so that there might be no schism in the body, but instead the parts themselves might take care of one another.
046	1CO	012	026	And so, if one part suffers anything, all the parts suffer with it. Or, if one part finds glory, all the parts rejoice with it.
046	1CO	012	027	Now you are the body of Christ, and parts like any part.
046	1CO	012	028	And indeed, God has established a certain order in the Church: first Apostles, second Prophets, third Teachers, next miracle-workers, and then the grace of healing, of helping others, of governing, of different kinds of languages, and of the interpretation of words.
046	1CO	012	029	Are all Apostles? Are all Prophets? Are all Teachers?
046	1CO	012	030	Are all workers of miracles? Do all have the grace of healing? Do all speak in tongues? Do all interpret?
046	1CO	012	031	But be zealous for the better charisms. And I reveal to you a yet more excellent way.
046	1CO	013	001	If I were to speak in the language of men, or of Angels, yet not have charity, I would be like a clanging bell or a crashing cymbal.
046	1CO	013	002	And if I have prophecy, and learn every mystery, and obtain all knowledge, and possess all faith, so that I could move mountains, yet not have charity, then I am nothing.
046	1CO	013	003	And if I distribute all my goods in order to feed the poor, and if I hand over my body to be burned, yet not have charity, it offers me nothing.
046	1CO	013	004	Charity is patient, is kind. Charity does not envy, does not act wrongly, is not inflated.
046	1CO	013	005	Charity is not ambitious, does not seek for itself, is not provoked to anger, devises no evil.
046	1CO	013	006	Charity does not rejoice over iniquity, but rejoices in truth.
046	1CO	013	007	Charity suffers all, believes all, hopes all, endures all.
046	1CO	013	008	Charity is never torn away, even if prophecies pass away, or languages cease, or knowledge is destroyed.
046	1CO	013	009	For we know only in part, and we prophesy only in part.
046	1CO	013	010	But when the perfect arrives, the imperfect passes away.
046	1CO	013	011	When I was a child, I spoke like a child, I understood like a child, I thought like a child. But when I became a man, I put aside the things of a child.
046	1CO	013	012	Now we see through a glass darkly. But then we shall see face to face. Now I know in part, but then I shall know, even as I am known.
046	1CO	013	013	But for now, these three continue: faith, hope, and charity. And the greatest of these is charity.
046	1CO	014	001	Pursue charity. Be zealous for spiritual things, but only so that you may prophesy.
046	1CO	014	002	For whoever speaks in tongues, speaks not to men, but to God. For no one understands. Yet by the Spirit, he speaks mysteries.
046	1CO	014	003	But whoever prophesies speaks to men for edification and exhortation and consolation.
046	1CO	014	004	Whoever speaks in tongues edifies himself. But whoever prophesies edifies the Church.
046	1CO	014	005	Now I want you all to speak in tongues, but more so to prophesy. For he who prophesies is greater than he who speaks in tongues, unless perhaps he interprets, so that the Church may receive edification.
046	1CO	014	006	But now, brothers, if I were to come to you speaking in tongues, how would it benefit you, unless instead I speak to you in revelation, or in knowledge, or in prophecy, or in doctrine?
046	1CO	014	007	Even those things that are without a soul can make sounds, whether it is a wind or a stringed instrument. But unless they present a distinction within the sounds, how will it be known which is from the pipe and which is from the string?
046	1CO	014	008	For example, if the trumpet made an uncertain sound, who would prepare himself for battle?
046	1CO	014	009	So it is with you also, for unless you utter with the tongue in plain speech, how will it be known what is said? For then you would be speaking into the air.
046	1CO	014	010	Consider that there are so many different kinds of languages in this world, and yet none is without a voice.
046	1CO	014	011	Therefore, if I do not understand the nature of the voice, then I shall be like a foreigner to the one with whom I am speaking; and he who is speaking will be like a foreigner to me.
046	1CO	014	012	So it is with you also. And since you are zealous for what is spiritual, seek the edification of the Church, so that you may abound.
046	1CO	014	013	For this reason, too, whoever speaks in tongues, let him pray for the interpretation.
046	1CO	014	014	So, if I pray in tongues, my spirit prays, but my mind is without fruit.
046	1CO	014	015	What is next? I should pray with the spirit, and also pray with the mind. I should sing psalms with the spirit, and also recite psalms with the mind.
046	1CO	014	016	Otherwise, if you have blessed only with the spirit, how can someone, in a state of ignorance, add an “Amen” to your blessing? For he does not know what you are saying.
046	1CO	014	017	In this case, certainly, you give thanks well, but the other person is not edified.
046	1CO	014	018	I thank my God that I speak in tongues for all of you.
046	1CO	014	019	But in the Church, I prefer to speak five words from my mind, so that I may instruct others also, rather than ten thousand words in tongues.
046	1CO	014	020	Brothers, do not choose to have the minds of children. Instead, be free of malice like infants, but be mature in your minds.
046	1CO	014	021	It is written in the law: “I will speak to this people with other tongues and other lips, and even so, they will not heed me, says the Lord.”
046	1CO	014	022	And so, tongues are a sign, not for believers, but for unbelievers; and prophecies are not for unbelievers, but for believers.
046	1CO	014	023	If then, the entire Church were to gather together as one, and if all were to speak in tongues, and then ignorant or unbelieving persons were to enter, would they not say that you were insane?
046	1CO	014	024	But if everyone prophesies, and one who is ignorant or unbelieving enters, he may be convinced by it all, because he understands it all.
046	1CO	014	025	The secrets of his heart are then made manifest. And so, falling to his face, he would adore God, proclaiming that God is truly among you.
046	1CO	014	026	What is next, brothers? When you gather together, each one of you may have a psalm, or a doctrine, or a revelation, or a language, or an interpretation, but let everything be done for edification.
046	1CO	014	027	If anyone is speaking in tongues, let there be only two, or at most three, and then in turn, and let someone interpret.
046	1CO	014	028	But if there is no one to interpret, he should remain silent in the church, then he may speak when he is alone with God.
046	1CO	014	029	And let the prophets speak, two or three, and let the others discern.
046	1CO	014	030	But then, if something is revealed to another who is sitting, let the first one become silent.
046	1CO	014	031	For you are all able to prophesy one at a time, so that all may learn and all may be encouraged.
046	1CO	014	032	For the spirits of the prophets are subject to the prophets.
046	1CO	014	033	And God is not of dissension, but of peace, just as I also teach in all the churches of the saints.
046	1CO	014	034	Women should be silent in the churches. For it is not permitted for them to speak; but instead, they should be subordinate, as the law also says.
046	1CO	014	035	And if they want to learn anything, let them ask their husbands at home. For it is disgraceful for a woman to speak in church.
046	1CO	014	036	So now, did the Word of God proceed from you? Or was it sent to you alone?
046	1CO	014	037	If anyone seems to be a prophet or a spiritual person, he should understand these things which I am writing to you, that these things are the commandments of the Lord.
046	1CO	014	038	If anyone does not recognize these things, he should not be recognized.
046	1CO	014	039	And so, brothers, be zealous to prophesy, and do not prohibit speaking in tongues.
046	1CO	014	040	But let everything be done respectfully and according to proper order.
046	1CO	015	001	And so I make known to you, brothers, the Gospel that I preached to you, which you also received, and on which you stand.
046	1CO	015	002	By the Gospel, too, you are being saved, if you hold to the understanding that I preached to you, lest you believe in vain.
046	1CO	015	003	For I handed on to you, first of all, what I also received: that Christ died for our sins, according to the Scriptures;
046	1CO	015	004	and that he was buried; and that he rose again on the third day, according to the Scriptures;
046	1CO	015	005	and that he was seen by Cephas, and after that by the eleven.
046	1CO	015	006	Next he was seen by more than five hundred brothers at one time, many of whom remain, even to the present time, although some have fallen asleep.
046	1CO	015	007	Next, he was seen by James, then by all the Apostles.
046	1CO	015	008	And last of all, he was seen also by me, as if I were someone born at the wrong time.
046	1CO	015	009	For I am the least of the Apostles. I am not worthy to be called an Apostle, because I persecuted the Church of God.
046	1CO	015	010	But, by the grace of God, I am what I am. And his grace in me has not been empty, since I have labored more abundantly than all of them. Yet it is not I, but the grace of God within me.
046	1CO	015	011	For whether it is I or they: so we preach, and so you have believed.
046	1CO	015	012	Now if Christ is preached, that he rose again from the dead, how is it that some among you say that there is no resurrection of the dead?
046	1CO	015	013	For if there is no resurrection of the dead, then Christ has not risen.
046	1CO	015	014	And if Christ has not risen, then our preaching is useless, and your faith is also useless.
046	1CO	015	015	Then, too, we would be found to be false witnesses of God, because we would have given testimony against God, saying that he had raised up Christ, when he had not raised him up, if, indeed, the dead do not rise again.
046	1CO	015	016	For if the dead do not rise again, then neither has Christ risen again.
046	1CO	015	017	But if Christ has not risen, then your faith is vain; for you would still be in your sins.
046	1CO	015	018	Then, too, those who have fallen asleep in Christ would have perished.
046	1CO	015	019	If we have hope in Christ for this life only, then we are more miserable than all men.
046	1CO	015	020	But now Christ has risen again from the dead, as the first-fruits of those who sleep.
046	1CO	015	021	For certainly, death came through a man. And so, the resurrection of the dead came through a man
046	1CO	015	022	And just as in Adam all die, so also in Christ all will be brought to life,
046	1CO	015	023	but each one in his proper order: Christ, as the first-fruits, and next, those who are of Christ, who have believed in his advent.
046	1CO	015	024	Afterwards is the end, when he will have handed over the kingdom to God the Father, when he will have emptied all principality, and authority, and power.
046	1CO	015	025	For it is necessary for him to reign, until he has set all his enemies under his feet.
046	1CO	015	026	Lastly, the enemy called death shall be destroyed. For he has subjected all things under his feet. And although he says,
046	1CO	015	027	“All things have been subjected to him,” without doubt he does not include the One who has subjected all things to him.
046	1CO	015	028	And when all things will have been subjected to him, then even the Son himself will be subjected to the One who subjected all things to him, so that God may be all in all.
046	1CO	015	029	Otherwise, what will those who are being baptized for the dead do, if the dead do not rise again at all? Why then are they being baptized for them?
046	1CO	015	030	Why also do we endure trials every hour?
046	1CO	015	031	Daily I die, by means of your boasting, brothers: you whom I have in Christ Jesus our Lord.
046	1CO	015	032	If, according to man, I fought with the beasts at Ephesus, how would that benefit me, if the dead do not rise again? “Let us eat and drink, for tomorrow we shall die.”
046	1CO	015	033	Do not be led astray. Evil communication corrupts good morals.
046	1CO	015	034	Be vigilant, you just ones, and do not be willing to sin. For certain persons have an ignorance of God. I say this to you with respect.
046	1CO	015	035	But someone may say, “How do the dead rise again?” or, “What type of body do they return with?”
046	1CO	015	036	How foolish! What you sow cannot be brought back to life, unless it first dies.
046	1CO	015	037	And what you sow is not the body that will be in the future, but a bare grain, such as of wheat, or of some other grain.
046	1CO	015	038	For God gives it a body according to his will, and according to each seed’s proper body.
046	1CO	015	039	Not all flesh is the same flesh. But one is indeed of men, another truly is of beasts, another is of birds, and another is of fish.
046	1CO	015	040	Also, there are heavenly bodies and earthly bodies. But while the one, certainly, has the glory of heaven, the other has the glory of earth.
046	1CO	015	041	One has the brightness of the sun, another the brightness of the moon, and another the brightness of the stars. For even star differs from star in brightness.
046	1CO	015	042	So it is also with the resurrection of the dead. What is sown in corruption shall rise to incorruption.
046	1CO	015	043	What is sown in dishonor shall rise to glory. What is sown in weakness shall rise to power.
046	1CO	015	044	What is sown with an animal body shall rise with a spiritual body. If there is an animal body, there is also a spiritual one.
046	1CO	015	045	Just as it was written that the first man, Adam, was made with a living soul, so shall the last Adam be made with a spirit brought back to life.
046	1CO	015	046	So what is, at first, not spiritual, but animal, next becomes spiritual.
046	1CO	015	047	The first man, being earthly, was of the earth; the second man, being heavenly, will be of heaven.
046	1CO	015	048	Such things as are like the earth are earthly; and such things as are like the heavens are heavenly.
046	1CO	015	049	And so, just as we have carried the image of what is earthly, let us also carry the image of what is heavenly.
046	1CO	015	050	Now I say this, brothers, because flesh and blood is not able to possess the kingdom of God; neither will what is corrupt possess what is incorrupt.
046	1CO	015	051	Behold, I tell you a mystery. Certainly, we shall all rise again, but we shall not all be transformed:
046	1CO	015	052	in a moment, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trumpet. For the trumpet will sound, and the dead will rise up, incorruptible. And we shall be transformed.
046	1CO	015	053	Thus, it is necessary for this corruptibility to be clothed with incorruptibility, and for this mortality to be clothed with immortality.
046	1CO	015	054	And when this mortality has been clothed with immortality, then the word that was written shall occur: “Death is swallowed up in victory.”
046	1CO	015	055	“O death, where is your victory? O death, where is your sting?”
046	1CO	015	056	Now the sting of death is sin, and the power of sin is the law.
046	1CO	015	057	But thanks be to God, who has given us victory through our Lord Jesus Christ.
046	1CO	015	058	And so, my beloved brothers, be steadfast and unmovable, abounding always in the work of the Lord, knowing that your labor is not useless in the Lord.
046	1CO	016	001	Now concerning the collections which are made for the saints: just as I have arranged for the churches of Galatia, so should it also be done with you.
046	1CO	016	002	On the first day of the week, the Sabbath, let each one of you take from himself, setting aside what will be well-pleasing to him, so that when I arrive, the collections will not have to be made then.
046	1CO	016	003	And when I am present, whomever you shall approve through letters, these I shall send to bear your gifts to Jerusalem.
046	1CO	016	004	And if it is fitting for me to go too, they shall go with me.
046	1CO	016	005	Now I will visit you after I have passed through Macedonia. For I will pass through Macedonia.
046	1CO	016	006	And perhaps I will stay with you, and even spend the winter, so that you may lead me on my way, whenever I depart.
046	1CO	016	007	For I am not willing to see you now only in passing, since I hope that I may remain with you for some length of time, if the Lord permits.
046	1CO	016	008	But I must remain at Ephesus, even until Pentecost.
046	1CO	016	009	For a door, great and unavoidable, has opened to me, as well as many adversaries.
046	1CO	016	010	Now if Timothy arrives, see to it that he may be among you without fear. For he is doing the work of the Lord, just as I also do.
046	1CO	016	011	Therefore, let no one despise him. Instead, lead him on his way in peace, so that he may come to me. For I am awaiting him with the brothers.
046	1CO	016	012	But concerning our brother, Apollo, I am letting you know that I pleaded with him greatly to go to you with the brothers, and clearly it was not his will to go at this time. But he will arrive when there is a space of time for him.
046	1CO	016	013	Be vigilant. Stand with faith. Act manfully and be strengthened.
046	1CO	016	014	Let all that is yours be immersed in charity.
046	1CO	016	015	And I beg you, brothers: You know the house of Stephanus, and of Fortunatus, and of Achaicus, that they are the first-fruits of Achaia, and that they have dedicated themselves to the ministry of the saints.
046	1CO	016	016	So you should be subject also to persons such as this, as well as to all who are cooperating and working with them.
046	1CO	016	017	Now I rejoice in the presence of Stephanus and Fortunatus and Achaicus, because what was lacking in you, they have supplied.
046	1CO	016	018	For they have refreshed my spirit and yours. Therefore, recognize persons such as this.
046	1CO	016	019	The churches of Asia greet you. Aquila and Priscilla greet you greatly in the Lord, with the church of their household, where I also am a guest.
046	1CO	016	020	All the brothers greet you. Greet one another with a holy kiss.
046	1CO	016	021	This is a greeting from my own hand, Paul.
046	1CO	016	022	If anyone does not love our Lord Jesus Christ, let him be anathema! Maran Atha.
046	1CO	016	023	May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all.
046	1CO	016	024	My charity is with all of you in Christ Jesus. Amen.
#
# BOOK	047	2CO	2 Corinthians	2 Corinthians
047	2CO	001	001	Paul, an Apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God, and Timothy, a brother, to the church of God which is at Corinth, with all the saints who are in all of Achaia:
047	2CO	001	002	Grace and peace to you from God our Father and from the Lord Jesus Christ.
047	2CO	001	003	Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of mercies and the God of all consolation.
047	2CO	001	004	He consoles us in all our tribulation, so that we too may be able to console those who are in any kind of distress, through the exhortation by which we also are being exhorted by God.
047	2CO	001	005	For just as the Passion of Christ abounds in us, so also, through Christ, does our consolation abound.
047	2CO	001	006	So, if we are in tribulation, it is for your exhortation and salvation, or if we are in consolation, it is for your consolation, or if we are exhorted, it is for your exhortation and salvation, which results in the patient endurance of the same passion which we also endure.
047	2CO	001	007	So may our hope for you be made firm, knowing that, just as you are participants in the suffering, so also shall you be participants in the consolation.
047	2CO	001	008	For we do not want you to be ignorant, brothers, about our tribulation, which happened to us in Asia. For we were weighed down beyond measure, beyond our strength, so that we became weary, even of life itself.
047	2CO	001	009	But we had within ourselves the response to death, so that we would not have faith in ourselves, but in God, who raises the dead.
047	2CO	001	010	He has rescued us, and he is rescuing us, from great peril. In him, we hope that he will continue to rescue us.
047	2CO	001	011	And you are assisting, with your prayers for us, so that from many persons, by that which is a gift in us, thanks may be given through many persons, because of us.
047	2CO	001	012	For our glory is this: the testimony of our conscience, which is found in simplicity of heart and in sincerity toward God. And it is not with worldly wisdom, but in the grace of God, that we have conversed with this world, and more abundantly toward you.
047	2CO	001	013	For we write nothing else to you other than what you have read and understood. And I hope that you will continue to understand, even unto the end.
047	2CO	001	014	And just as you have acknowledged us in our role, that we are your glory, so also you are ours, unto the day of our Lord Jesus Christ.
047	2CO	001	015	And with this confidence, I wanted to come to you sooner, so that you might have a second grace,
047	2CO	001	016	and through you to pass into Macedonia, and to return to you again from Macedonia, and so be led by you on my way to Judea.
047	2CO	001	017	Then, although I had intended this, did I act lightly? Or in the things that I consider, do I consider according to the flesh, so that there would be, with me, both Yes and No?
047	2CO	001	018	But God is faithful, so our word, which was set before you, was not, in him, both Yes and No.
047	2CO	001	019	For the Son of God, Jesus Christ, who was preached among you through us, through myself and Sylvanus and Timothy, was not Yes, and No; but was simply Yes in him.
047	2CO	001	020	For whatever promises are of God are, in him, Yes. For this reason, too, through him: Amen to God for our glory.
047	2CO	001	021	Now the One who confirms us with you in Christ, and who has anointed us, is God.
047	2CO	001	022	And he has sealed us, and he has placed the pledge of the Spirit in our hearts.
047	2CO	001	023	But I call God as a witness to my soul, that I was lenient with you, in that I did not return to Corinth:
047	2CO	001	024	not because we have dominion over your faith, but because we are assistants of your joy. For by faith you stand.
047	2CO	002	001	But I determined this within myself, not to return again to you in sorrow.
047	2CO	002	002	For if I make you sorrowful, then who is it that can make me glad, except the one who is made sorrowful by me?
047	2CO	002	003	And so, I wrote this same thing to you, so that I might not, when I arrive, add sorrow to sorrow for those with whom I ought to rejoice, having confidence in you in all things, so that my joy may be entirely yours.
047	2CO	002	004	For with much tribulation and anguish of heart, I wrote to you with many tears: not so that you would be sorrowful, but so that you might know the charity that I have more abundantly toward you.
047	2CO	002	005	But if anyone has brought sorrow, he has not sorrowed me. Yet, for my part, this is so that I might not burden all of you.
047	2CO	002	006	Let this rebuke be sufficient for someone like this, for it has been brought by many.
047	2CO	002	007	So then, to the contrary, you should be more forgiving and consoling, lest perhaps someone like this may be overwhelmed with excessive sorrow.
047	2CO	002	008	Because of this, I beg you to confirm your charity toward him.
047	2CO	002	009	It was for this reason, also, that I wrote, so that I might know, by testing you, whether you would be obedient in all things.
047	2CO	002	010	But anyone whom you have forgiven of anything, I also forgive. And then, too, anyone I have forgiven, if I have forgiven anything, it was done in the person of Christ for your sakes,
047	2CO	002	011	so that we would not be circumvented by Satan. For we are not ignorant of his intentions.
047	2CO	002	012	And when I had arrived at Troas, because of the Gospel of Christ, and a door had opened to me in the Lord,
047	2CO	002	013	I had no rest within my spirit, because I was not able to find Titus, my brother. So, saying goodbye to them, I set out for Macedonia.
047	2CO	002	014	But thanks be to God, who always brings triumph to us in Christ Jesus, and who manifests the fragrance of his knowledge through us in every place.
047	2CO	002	015	For we are the sweet fragrance of Christ for God, both with those who are being saved and with those who are perishing.
047	2CO	002	016	To the one, certainly, the fragrance is of death unto death. But to the other, the fragrance is of life unto life. And concerning these things, who is so suitable?
047	2CO	002	017	For we are not like many others, adulterating the Word of God. But instead, we speak with sincerity: from God, before God, and in Christ.
047	2CO	003	001	Must we begin again to commend ourselves? Or are we in need (as some are) of epistles of commendation for you, or from you?
047	2CO	003	002	You are our Epistle, written in our hearts, which is known and read by all men.
047	2CO	003	003	It has been made manifest that you are the Epistle of Christ, ministered by us, and written down, not with ink, but with the Spirit of the living God, and not on tablets of stone, but on the fleshly tablets of the heart.
047	2CO	003	004	And we have such faith, through Christ, toward God.
047	2CO	003	005	It is not that we are adequate to think anything of ourselves, as if anything was from us. But our adequacy is from God.
047	2CO	003	006	And he has made us suitable ministers of the New Testament, not in the letter, but in the Spirit. For the letter kills, but the Spirit gives life.
047	2CO	003	007	But if the ministration of death, engraved with letters upon stones, was in glory, (so much so that the sons of Israel were not able to gaze intently upon the face of Moses, because of the glory of his countenance) even though this ministration was ineffective,
047	2CO	003	008	how could the ministration of the Spirit not be in greater glory?
047	2CO	003	009	For if the ministration of condemnation is with glory, so much more is the ministration of justice abundant in glory.
047	2CO	003	010	And neither was it glorified by means of an excellent glory, though it was made illustrious in its own way.
047	2CO	003	011	For if even what was temporary has its glory, then what is lasting has an even greater glory.
047	2CO	003	012	Therefore, having such a hope, we act with much confidence,
047	2CO	003	013	and not as Moses did, in placing a veil over his face, so that the sons of Israel would not gaze intently at his face. This was ineffective,
047	2CO	003	014	for their minds were obtuse. And, even until this present day, the very same veil, in the readings from the Old Testament, remains not taken away (though, in Christ, it is taken away).
047	2CO	003	015	But even until today, when Moses is read, a veil is still set over their hearts.
047	2CO	003	016	But when they will have been converted to the Lord, then the veil shall be taken away.
047	2CO	003	017	Now the Spirit is Lord. And wherever the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty.
047	2CO	003	018	Yet truly, all of us, as we gaze upon the unveiled glory of the face of the Lord, are transfigured into the same image, from one glory to another. And this is done by the Spirit of the Lord.
047	2CO	004	001	Therefore, since we have this ministry, and in as much as we have obtained mercy for ourselves, we are not inadequate.
047	2CO	004	002	For we renounce dishonorable and hidden acts, not walking by craftiness, nor by adulterating the Word of God. Instead, by the manifestation of truth, we commend ourselves to the conscience of each man before God.
047	2CO	004	003	But if our Gospel is in some way hidden, it is hidden to those who are perishing.
047	2CO	004	004	As for them, the god of this age has blinded the minds of unbelievers, so that the light of the Gospel of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God, would not shine in them.
047	2CO	004	005	For we are not preaching about ourselves, but about Jesus Christ our Lord. We are merely your servants through Jesus.
047	2CO	004	006	For God, who told the light to shine out of darkness, has shined a light into our hearts, to illuminate the knowledge of the splendor of God, in the person of Christ Jesus.
047	2CO	004	007	But we hold this treasure in earthen vessels, so that what is sublime may be of the power of God, and not of us.
047	2CO	004	008	In all things, we endure tribulation, yet we are not in anguish. We are constrained, yet we are not destitute.
047	2CO	004	009	We suffer persecution, yet we have not been abandoned. We are thrown down, yet we do not perish.
047	2CO	004	010	We ever carry around the mortification of Jesus in our bodies, so that the life of Jesus may also be manifested in our bodies.
047	2CO	004	011	For we who live are ever handed over unto death for the sake of Jesus, so that the life of Jesus may also be manifested in our mortal flesh.
047	2CO	004	012	Therefore, death is at work in us, and life is at work in you.
