# BOOK	048	GAL	Galatians	Galatians
048	GAL	001	001	Paul, an Apostle, not from men and not through man, but through Jesus Christ, and God the Father, who raised him from the dead,
048	GAL	001	002	and all the brothers who are with me: to the churches of Galatia.
048	GAL	001	003	Grace and peace to you from God the Father, and from our Lord Jesus Christ,
048	GAL	001	004	who gave himself on behalf of our sins, so that he might deliver us from this present wicked age, according to the will of God our Father.
048	GAL	001	005	To him is glory forever and ever. Amen.
048	GAL	001	006	I wonder that you have been so quickly transferred, from him who called you into the grace of Christ, over to another gospel.
048	GAL	001	007	For there is no other, except that there are some persons who disturb you and who want to overturn the Gospel of Christ.
048	GAL	001	008	But if anyone, even we ourselves or an Angel from Heaven, were to preach to you a gospel other than the one that we have preached to you, let him be anathema.
048	GAL	001	009	Just as we have said before, so now I say again: If anyone has preached a gospel to you, other than that which you have received, let him be anathema.
048	GAL	001	010	For am I now persuading men, or God? Or, am I seeking to please men? If I still were pleasing men, then I would not be a servant of Christ.
048	GAL	001	011	For I would have you understand, brothers, that the Gospel which has been preached by me is not according to man.
048	GAL	001	012	And I did not receive it from man, nor did I learn it, except through the revelation of Jesus Christ.
048	GAL	001	013	For you have heard of my former behavior within Judaism: that, beyond measure, I persecuted the Church of God and fought against Her.
048	GAL	001	014	And I advanced in Judaism beyond many of my equals among my own kind, having proven to be more abundant in zeal toward the traditions of my fathers.
048	GAL	001	015	But, when it pleased him who, from my mother’s womb, had set me apart, and who has called me by his grace,
048	GAL	001	016	to reveal his Son within me, so that I might evangelize him among the Gentiles, I did not next seek the consent of flesh and blood.
048	GAL	001	017	Neither did I go to Jerusalem, to those who were Apostles before me. Instead, I went into Arabia, and next I returned to Damascus.
048	GAL	001	018	And then, after three years, I went to Jerusalem to see Peter; and I stayed with him for fifteen days.
048	GAL	001	019	But I saw none of the other Apostles, except James, the brother of the Lord.
048	GAL	001	020	Now what I am writing to you: behold, before God, I am not lying.
048	GAL	001	021	Next, I went into the regions of Syria and Cilicia.
048	GAL	001	022	But I was unknown by face to the churches of Judea, which were in Christ.
048	GAL	001	023	For they had only heard that: “He, who formerly persecuted us, now evangelizes the faith which he once fought.”
048	GAL	001	024	And they glorified God in me.
048	GAL	002	001	Next, after fourteen years, I went up again to Jerusalem, taking with me Barnabas and Titus.
048	GAL	002	002	And I went up according to revelation, and I debated with them about the Gospel that I am preaching among the Gentiles, but away from those who were pretending to be something, lest perhaps I might run, or have run, in vain.
048	GAL	002	003	But even Titus, who was with me, though he was a Gentile, was not compelled to be circumcised,
048	GAL	002	004	but only because of false brothers, who were brought in unknowingly. They entered secretly to spy on our liberty, which we have in Christ Jesus, so that they might reduce us to servitude.
048	GAL	002	005	We did not yield to them in subjection, even for an hour, in order that the truth of the Gospel would remain with you,
048	GAL	002	006	and away from those who were pretending to be something. (Whatever they might have been once, it means nothing to me. God does not accept the reputation of a man.) And those who were claiming to be something had nothing to offer me.
048	GAL	002	007	But it was to the contrary, since they had seen that the Gospel to the uncircumcised was entrusted to me, just as the Gospel to the circumcised was entrusted to Peter.
048	GAL	002	008	For he who was working the Apostleship to the circumcised in Peter, was also working in me among the Gentiles.
048	GAL	002	009	And so, when they had acknowledged the grace that was given to me, James and Cephas and John, who seemed like pillars, gave to me and to Barnabas the right hand of fellowship, so that we would go to the Gentiles, while they went to the circumcised,
048	GAL	002	010	asking only that we should be mindful of the poor, which was the very thing that I also was solicitous to do.
048	GAL	002	011	But when Cephas had arrived at Antioch, I stood against him to his face, because he was blameworthy.
048	GAL	002	012	For before certain ones arrived from James, he ate with the Gentiles. But when they had arrived, he drew apart and separated himself, fearing those who were of the circumcision.
048	GAL	002	013	And the other Jews consented to his pretense, so that even Barnabas was led by them into that falseness.
048	GAL	002	014	But when I had seen that they were not walking correctly, by the truth of the Gospel, I said to Cephas in front of everyone: “If you, while you are a Jew, are living like the Gentiles and not the Jews, how is it that you compel the Gentiles to keep the customs of the Jews?”
048	GAL	002	015	By nature, we are Jews, and not of the Gentiles, sinners.
048	GAL	002	016	And we know that man is not justified by the works of the law, but only by the faith of Jesus Christ. And so we believe in Christ Jesus, in order that we may be justified by the faith of Christ, and not by the works of the law. For no flesh will be justified by the works of the law.
048	GAL	002	017	But if, while seeking to be justified in Christ, we ourselves are also found to be sinners, would then Christ be the minister of sin? Let it not be so!
048	GAL	002	018	For if I rebuild the things that I have destroyed, I establish myself as a prevaricator.
048	GAL	002	019	For through the law, I have become dead to the law, so that I may live for God. I have been nailed to the cross with Christ.
048	GAL	002	020	I live; yet now, it is not I, but truly Christ, who lives in me. And though I live now in the flesh, I live in the faith of the Son of God, who loved me and who delivered himself for me.
048	GAL	002	021	I do not reject the grace of God. For if justice is through the law, then Christ died in vain.
048	GAL	003	001	O senseless Galatians, who has so fascinated you that you would not obey the truth, even though Jesus Christ has been presented before your eyes, crucified among you?
048	GAL	003	002	I wish to know only this from you: Did you receive the Spirit by the works of the law, or by the hearing of faith?
048	GAL	003	003	Are you so foolish that, though you began with the Spirit, you would now end with the flesh?
048	GAL	003	004	Have you been suffering so much without a reason? If so, then it is in vain.
048	GAL	003	005	Therefore, does he who distributes the Spirit to you, and who works miracles among you, act by the works of the law, or by the hearing of the faith?
048	GAL	003	006	It is just as it was written: “Abraham believed God, and it was reputed to him unto justice.”
048	GAL	003	007	Therefore, know that those who are of faith, these are the sons of Abraham.
048	GAL	003	008	Thus Scripture, foreseeing that God would justify the Gentiles by faith, foretold to Abraham: “All nations shall be blessed in you.”
048	GAL	003	009	And so, those who are of faith shall be blessed with faithful Abraham.
048	GAL	003	010	For as many as are of the works of the law are under a curse. For it has been written: “Cursed is everyone who does not continue in all the things that have been written in the book of the Law, so as to do them.”
048	GAL	003	011	And, since in the law no one is justified with God, this is manifest: “For the just man lives by faith.”
048	GAL	003	012	But the law is not of faith; instead, “he who does these things shall live by them.”
048	GAL	003	013	Christ has redeemed us from the curse of the law, since he became a curse for us. For it is written: “Cursed is anyone who hangs from a tree.”
048	GAL	003	014	This was so that the blessing of Abraham might reach the Gentiles through Christ Jesus, in order that we might receive the promise of the Spirit through faith.
048	GAL	003	015	Brothers (I speak according to man), if a man’s testament has been confirmed, no one would reject it or add to it.
048	GAL	003	016	The promises were made to Abraham and to his offspring. He did not say, “and to descendents,” as if to many, but instead, as if to one, he said, “and to your offspring,” who is Christ.
048	GAL	003	017	But I say this: the testament confirmed by God, which, after four hundred and thirty years became the Law, does not nullify, so as to make the promise empty.
048	GAL	003	018	For if the inheritance is of the law, then it is no longer of the promise. But God bestowed it to Abraham through the promise.
048	GAL	003	019	Why, then, was there a law? It was established because of transgressions, until the offspring would arrive, to whom he made the promise, ordained by Angels through the hand of a mediator.
048	GAL	003	020	Now a mediator is not of one, yet God is one.
048	GAL	003	021	So then, was the law contrary to the promises of God? Let it not be so! For if a law had been given, which was able to give life, truly justice would be of the law.
048	GAL	003	022	But Scripture has enclosed everything under sin, so that the promise, by the faith of Jesus Christ, might be given to those who believe.
048	GAL	003	023	But before the faith arrived, we were preserved by being enclosed under the law, unto that faith which was to be revealed.
048	GAL	003	024	And so the law was our guardian in Christ, in order that we might be justified by faith.
048	GAL	003	025	But now that faith has arrived, we are no longer under a guardian.
048	GAL	003	026	For you are all sons of God, through the faith which is in Christ Jesus.
048	GAL	003	027	For as many of you as have been baptized in Christ have become clothed with Christ.
048	GAL	003	028	There is neither Jew nor Greek; there is neither servant nor free; there is neither male nor female. For you are all one in Christ Jesus.
048	GAL	003	029	And if you are Christ’s, then are you the offspring of Abraham, heirs according to the promise.
048	GAL	004	001	But I say that, during the time an heir is a child, he is no different from a servant, even though he is the owner of everything.
048	GAL	004	002	For he is under tutors and caretakers, until the time which was predetermined by the father.
048	GAL	004	003	So also we, when we were children, were subservient to the influences of the world.
048	GAL	004	004	But when the fullness of time arrived, God sent his Son, formed from a woman, formed under the law,
048	GAL	004	005	so that he might redeem those who were under the law, in order that we might receive the adoption of sons.
048	GAL	004	006	Therefore, because you are sons, God has sent the Spirit of his Son into your hearts, crying out: “Abba, Father.”
048	GAL	004	007	And so now he is not a servant, but a son. But if he is a son, then he is also an heir, through God.
048	GAL	004	008	But then, certainly, while ignorant of God, you served those who, by nature, are not gods.
048	GAL	004	009	But now, since you have known God, or rather, since you have been known by God: how can you turn away again, to weak and destitute influences, which you desire to serve anew?
048	GAL	004	010	You serve the days, and months, and times, and years.
048	GAL	004	011	I am afraid for you, lest perhaps I may have labored in vain among you.
048	GAL	004	012	Brothers, I beg you. Be as I am. For I, too, am like you. You have not injured me at all.
048	GAL	004	013	But you know that, in the weakness of the flesh, I have preached the Gospel to you for a long time, and that your trials are in my flesh.
048	GAL	004	014	You did not despise or reject me. But instead, you accepted me like an Angel of God, even like Christ Jesus.
048	GAL	004	015	Therefore, where is your happiness? For I offer to you testimony that, if it could be done, you would have plucked out your own eyes and would have given them to me.
048	GAL	004	016	So then, have I become your enemy by telling you the truth?
048	GAL	004	017	They are not imitating you well. And they are willing to exclude you, so that you might imitate them.
048	GAL	004	018	But be imitators of what is good, always in a good way, and not only when I am present with you.
048	GAL	004	019	My little sons, I am giving birth to you again, until Christ is formed in you.
048	GAL	004	020	And I would willingly be present with you, even now. But I would alter my voice: for I am ashamed of you.
048	GAL	004	021	Tell me, you who desire to be under the law, have you not read the law?
048	GAL	004	022	For it is written that Abraham had two sons: one by a servant woman, and one by a free woman.
048	GAL	004	023	And he who was of the servant was born according to the flesh. But he who was of the free woman was born by the promise.
048	GAL	004	024	These things are said through an allegory. For these represent the two testaments. Certainly the one, on Mount Sinai, gives birth unto servitude, which is Hagar.
048	GAL	004	025	For Sinai is a mountain in Arabia, which is related to the Jerusalem of the present time, and it serves with her sons.
048	GAL	004	026	But that Jerusalem which is above is free; the same is our mother.
048	GAL	004	027	For it was written: “Rejoice, O barren one, though you do not conceive. Burst forth and cry out, though you do not give birth. For many are the children of the desolate, even more than of her who has a husband.”
048	GAL	004	028	Now we, brothers, like Isaac, are sons of the promise.
048	GAL	004	029	But just as then, he who was born according to the flesh persecuted him who was born according to the Spirit, so also it is now.
048	GAL	004	030	And what does Scripture say? “Cast out the woman servant and her son. For the son of a servant women shall not be an heir with the son of a free woman.”
048	GAL	004	031	And so, brothers, we are not the sons of the servant woman, but rather of the free woman. And this is the freedom with which Christ has set us free.
048	GAL	005	001	Stand firm, and do not be willing to be again held by the yoke of servitude.
048	GAL	005	002	Behold, I, Paul, say to you, that if you have been circumcised, Christ will be of no benefit to you.
048	GAL	005	003	For I again testify, about every man circumcising himself, that he is obligated to act according to the entire law.
048	GAL	005	004	You are being emptied of Christ, you who are being justified by the law. You have fallen from grace.
048	GAL	005	005	For in spirit, by faith, we await the hope of justice.
048	GAL	005	006	For in Christ Jesus, neither circumcision nor uncircumcision prevails over anything, but only faith which works through charity.
048	GAL	005	007	You have run well. So what has impeded you, that you would not obey the truth?
048	GAL	005	008	This kind of influence is not from him who is calling you.
048	GAL	005	009	A little leaven corrupts the whole mass.
048	GAL	005	010	I have confidence in you, in the Lord, that you will accept nothing of the kind. However, he who disturbs you shall bear the judgment, whomever he may be.
048	GAL	005	011	And as for me, brothers, if I still preach circumcision, why am I still suffering persecution? For then the scandal of the Cross would be made empty.
048	GAL	005	012	And I wish that those who disturb you would be torn away.
048	GAL	005	013	For you, brothers, have been called to liberty. Only you must not make liberty into an occasion for the flesh, but instead, serve one another through the charity of the Spirit.
048	GAL	005	014	For the entire law is fulfilled by one word: “You shall love your neighbor as yourself.”
048	GAL	005	015	But if you bite and devour one another, be careful that you are not consumed by one another!
048	GAL	005	016	So then, I say: Walk in the spirit, and you will not fulfill the desires of the flesh.
048	GAL	005	017	For the flesh desires against the spirit, and the spirit against the flesh. And since these are against one another, you may not do whatever you want.
048	GAL	005	018	But if you are led by the Spirit, you are not under the law.
048	GAL	005	019	Now the works of the flesh are manifest; they are: fornication, lust, homosexuality, self-indulgence,
048	GAL	005	020	the serving of idols, drug use, hostility, contentiousness, jealousy, wrath, quarrels, dissensions, divisions,
048	GAL	005	021	envy, murder, inebriation, carousing, and similar things. About these things, I continue to preach to you, as I have preached to you: that those who act in this way shall not obtain the kingdom of God.
048	GAL	005	022	But the fruit of the Spirit is charity, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, forbearance,
048	GAL	005	023	meekness, faith, modesty, abstinence, chastity. There is no law against such things.
048	GAL	005	024	For those who are Christ’s have crucified their flesh, along with its vices and desires.
048	GAL	005	025	If we live by the Spirit, we should also walk by the Spirit.
048	GAL	005	026	Let us not become desirous of empty glory, provoking one another, envying one another.
048	GAL	006	001	And, brothers, if a man has been overtaken by any offense, you who are spiritual should instruct someone like this with a spirit of leniency, considering that you yourselves might also be tempted.
048	GAL	006	002	Carry one another’s burdens, and so shall you fulfill the law of Christ.
048	GAL	006	003	For if anyone considers himself to be something, though he may be nothing, he deceives himself.
048	GAL	006	004	So let each one prove his own work. And in this way, he shall have glory in himself only, and not in another.
048	GAL	006	005	For each one shall carry his own burden.
048	GAL	006	006	And let him who is being taught the Word discuss it with him who is teaching it to him, in every good way.
048	GAL	006	007	Do not choose to wander astray. God is not to be ridiculed. For whatever a man will have sown, that also shall he reap.
048	GAL	006	008	For whoever sows in his flesh, from the flesh he shall also reap corruption. But whoever sows in the Spirit, from the Spirit he shall reap eternal life.
048	GAL	006	009	And so, let us not be deficient in doing good. For in due time, we shall reap without fail.
048	GAL	006	010	Therefore, while we have time, we should do good works toward everyone, and most of all toward those who are of the household of the faith.
048	GAL	006	011	Consider what kind of letters I have written to you with my own hand.
048	GAL	006	012	For as many of you as they desire to please in the flesh, they compel to be circumcised, but only so that they might not suffer the persecution of the cross of Christ.
048	GAL	006	013	And yet, neither do they themselves, who are circumcised, keep the law. Instead, they want you to be circumcised, so that they may glory in your flesh.
048	GAL	006	014	But far be it from me to glory, except in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, through whom the world is crucified to me, and I to the world.
048	GAL	006	015	For in Christ Jesus, neither circumcision nor uncircumcision prevails in any way, but instead there is a new creature.
048	GAL	006	016	And whoever follows this rule: may peace and mercy be upon them, and upon the Israel of God.
048	GAL	006	017	Concerning other matters, let no one trouble me. For I carry the stigmata of the Lord Jesus in my body.
048	GAL	006	018	May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit, brothers. Amen.
