# BOOK	049	EPH	Ephesians	Ephesians
049	EPH	001	001	Paul, an Apostle of Jesus Christ through the will of God, to all the saints who are at Ephesus and to the faithful in Christ Jesus.
049	EPH	001	002	Grace and peace to you from God the Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ.
049	EPH	001	003	Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us with every spiritual blessing in the heavens, in Christ,
049	EPH	001	004	just as he chose us in him before the foundation of the world, so that we would be holy and immaculate in his sight, in charity.
049	EPH	001	005	He has predestined us to adoption as sons, through Jesus Christ, in himself, according to the purpose of his will,
049	EPH	001	006	for the praise of the glory of his grace, with which he has gifted us in his beloved Son.
049	EPH	001	007	In him, we have redemption through his blood: the remission of sins in accord with the riches of his grace,
049	EPH	001	008	which is superabundant in us, with all wisdom and prudence.
049	EPH	001	009	So does he make known to us the mystery of his will, which he has set forth in Christ, in a manner well-pleasing to him,
049	EPH	001	010	in the dispensation of the fullness of time, so as to renew in Christ everything that exists through him in heaven and on earth.
049	EPH	001	011	In him, we too are called to our portion, having been predestined in accord with the plan of the One who accomplishes all things by the counsel of his will.
049	EPH	001	012	So may we be, to the praise of his glory, we who have hoped beforehand in Christ.
049	EPH	001	013	In him, you also, after you heard and believed the Word of truth, which is the Gospel of your salvation, were sealed with the Holy Spirit of the Promise.
049	EPH	001	014	He is the pledge of our inheritance, unto the acquisition of redemption, to the praise of his glory.
049	EPH	001	015	Because of this, and hearing of your faith that is in the Lord Jesus, and of your love toward all the saints,
049	EPH	001	016	I have not ceased giving thanks for you, calling you to mind in my prayers,
049	EPH	001	017	so that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give a spirit of wisdom and of revelation to you, in knowledge of him.
049	EPH	001	018	May the eyes of your heart be illuminated, so that you may know what is the hope of his calling, and the wealth of the glory of his inheritance with the saints,
049	EPH	001	019	and the preeminent magnitude of his virtue toward us, toward we who believe in accord with the work of his powerful virtue,
049	EPH	001	020	which he wrought in Christ, raising him from the dead and establishing him at his right hand in the heavens,
049	EPH	001	021	above every principality and power and virtue and dominion, and above every name that is given, not only in this age, but even in the future age.
049	EPH	001	022	And he has subjected all things under his feet, and he has made him the head over the entire Church,
049	EPH	001	023	which is his body and which is the fullness of him who accomplishes everything in everyone.
049	EPH	002	001	And you were once dead in your sins and offenses,
049	EPH	002	002	in which you walked in times past, according to the age of this world, according to the prince of the power of this sky, the spirit who now works in the sons of distrust.
049	EPH	002	003	And we too were all conversant in these things, in times past, by the desires of our flesh, acting according to the will of the flesh and according to our own thoughts. And so we were, by nature, sons of wrath, even like the others.
049	EPH	002	004	Yet still, God, who is rich in mercy, for the sake of his exceedingly great charity with which he loved us,
049	EPH	002	005	even when we were dead in our sins, has enlivened us together in Christ, by whose grace you have been saved.
049	EPH	002	006	And he has raised us up together, and he has caused us to sit down together in the heavens, in Christ Jesus,
049	EPH	002	007	so that he may display, in the ages soon to arrive, the abundant wealth of his grace, by his goodness toward us in Christ Jesus.
049	EPH	002	008	For by grace, you have been saved through faith. And this is not of yourselves, for it is a gift of God.
049	EPH	002	009	And this is not of works, so that no one may glory.
049	EPH	002	010	For we are his handiwork, created in Christ Jesus for the good works which God has prepared and in which we should walk.
049	EPH	002	011	Because of this, be mindful that, in times past, you were Gentiles in the flesh, and that you were called uncircumcised by those who are called circumcised in the flesh, something done by man,
049	EPH	002	012	and that you were, in that time, without Christ, being foreign to the way of life of Israel, being visitors to the testament, having no hope of the promise, and being without God in this world.
049	EPH	002	013	But now, in Christ Jesus, you, who were in times past far away, have been brought near by the blood of Christ.
049	EPH	002	014	For he is our peace. He made the two into one, by dissolving the intermediate wall of separation, of opposition, by his flesh,
049	EPH	002	015	emptying the law of commandments by decree, so that he might join these two, in himself, into one new man, making peace
049	EPH	002	016	and reconciling both to God, in one body, through the cross, destroying this opposition in himself.
049	EPH	002	017	And upon arriving, he evangelized peace to you who were far away, and peace to those who were near.
049	EPH	002	018	For by him, we both have access, in the one Spirit, to the Father.
049	EPH	002	019	Now, therefore, you are no longer visitors and new arrivals. Instead, you are citizens among the saints in the household of God,
049	EPH	002	020	having been built upon the foundation of the Apostles and of the Prophets, with Jesus Christ himself as the preeminent cornerstone.
049	EPH	002	021	In him, all that has been built is framed together, rising up into a holy temple in the Lord.
049	EPH	002	022	In him, you also have been built together into a habitation of God in the Spirit.
049	EPH	003	001	By reason of this grace, I, Paul, am a prisoner of Jesus Christ, for the sake of you Gentiles.
049	EPH	003	002	Now certainly, you have heard of the dispensation of the grace of God, which has been given to me among you:
049	EPH	003	003	that, by means of revelation, the mystery was made known to me, just as I have written above in a few words.
049	EPH	003	004	Yet, by reading this closely, you might be able to understand my prudence in the mystery of Christ.
049	EPH	003	005	In other generations, this was unknown to the sons of men, even as it has now been revealed to his holy Apostles and Prophets in the Spirit,
049	EPH	003	006	so that the Gentiles would be co-heirs, and of the same body, and partners together, by his promise in Christ Jesus, through the Gospel.
049	EPH	003	007	Of this Gospel, I have been made a minister, according to the gift of the grace of God, which has been given to me by means of the operation of his virtue.
049	EPH	003	008	Although I am the least of all the saints, I have been given this grace: to evangelize among the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ,
049	EPH	003	009	and to enlighten everyone concerning the dispensation of the mystery, hidden before the ages in God who created all things,
049	EPH	003	010	so that the manifold wisdom of God may become well-known to the principalities and powers in the heavens, through the Church,
049	EPH	003	011	according to that timeless purpose, which he has formed in Christ Jesus our Lord.
049	EPH	003	012	In him we trust, and so we approach with confidence, through his faith.
049	EPH	003	013	Because of this, I ask you not to be weakened by my tribulations on your behalf; for this is your glory.
049	EPH	003	014	By reason of this grace, I bend my knees to the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ,
049	EPH	003	015	from whom all paternity in heaven and on earth takes its name.
049	EPH	003	016	And I ask him to grant to you to be strengthened in virtue by his Spirit, in accord with the wealth of his glory, in the inner man,
049	EPH	003	017	so that Christ may live in your hearts through a faith rooted in, and founded on, charity.
049	EPH	003	018	So may you be able to embrace, with all the saints, what is the width and length and height and depth
049	EPH	003	019	of the charity of Christ, and even be able to know that which surpasses all knowledge, so that you may be filled with all the fullness of God.
049	EPH	003	020	Now to him who is able to do all things, more abundantly than we could ever ask or understand, by means of the virtue which is at work in us:
049	EPH	003	021	to him be glory, in the Church and in Christ Jesus, throughout every generation, forever and ever. Amen.
049	EPH	004	001	And so, as a prisoner in the Lord, I beg you to walk in a manner worthy of the vocation to which you have been called:
049	EPH	004	002	with all humility and meekness, with patience, supporting one another in charity.
049	EPH	004	003	Be anxious to preserve the unity of the Spirit within the bonds of peace.
049	EPH	004	004	One body and one Spirit: to this you have been called by the one hope of your calling:
049	EPH	004	005	one Lord, one faith, one baptism,
049	EPH	004	006	one God and Father of all, who is over all, and through all, and in us all.
049	EPH	004	007	Yet to each one of us there has been given grace according to the measure allotted by Christ.
049	EPH	004	008	Because of this, he says: “Ascending on high, he took captivity itself captive; he gave gifts to men.”
049	EPH	004	009	Now that he has ascended, what is left except for him also to descend, first to the lower parts of the earth?
049	EPH	004	010	He who descended is the same one who also ascended above all the heavens, so that he might fulfill everything.
049	EPH	004	011	And the same one granted that some would be Apostles, and some Prophets, yet truly others evangelists, and others pastors and teachers,
049	EPH	004	012	for the sake of the perfection of the saints, by the work of the ministry, in the edification of the body of Christ,
049	EPH	004	013	until we all meet in the unity of faith and in the knowledge of the Son of God, as a perfect man, in the measure of the age of the fullness of Christ.
049	EPH	004	014	So may we then no longer be little children, disturbed and carried about by every wind of doctrine, by the wickedness of men, and by the craftiness which deceives unto error.
049	EPH	004	015	Instead, acting according to truth in charity, we should increase in everything, in him who is the head, Christ himself.
049	EPH	004	016	For in him, the whole body is joined closely together, by every underlying joint, through the function allotted to each part, bringing improvement to the body, toward its edification in charity.
049	EPH	004	017	And so, I say this, and I testify in the Lord: that from now on you should walk, not as the Gentiles also walk, in the vanity of their mind,
049	EPH	004	018	having their intellect obscured, being alienated from the life of God, through the ignorance that is within them, because of the blindness of their hearts.
049	EPH	004	019	Such as these, despairing, have given themselves over to sexual immorality, carrying out every impurity with rapacity.
049	EPH	004	020	But this is not what you have learned in Christ.
049	EPH	004	021	For certainly, you have listened to him, and you have been instructed in him, according to the truth that is in Jesus:
049	EPH	004	022	to set aside your earlier behavior, the former man, who was corrupted, by means of desire, unto error,
049	EPH	004	023	and so be renewed in the spirit of your mind,
049	EPH	004	024	and so put on the new man, who, in accord with God, is created in justice and in the holiness of truth.
049	EPH	004	025	Because of this, setting aside lying, speak the truth, each one with his neighbor. For we are all part of one another.
049	EPH	004	026	“Be angry, but do not be willing to sin.” Do not let the sun set over your anger.
049	EPH	004	027	Provide no place for the devil.
049	EPH	004	028	Whoever was stealing, let him now not steal, but rather let him labor, working with his hands, doing what is good, so that he may have something to distribute to those who suffer need.
049	EPH	004	029	Let no evil words proceed from your mouth, but only what is good, toward the edification of faith, so as to bestow grace upon those who listen.
049	EPH	004	030	And do not be willing to grieve the Holy Spirit of God, in whom you have been sealed, unto the day of redemption.
049	EPH	004	031	Let all bitterness and anger and indignation and outcry and blasphemy be taken away from you, along with all malice.
049	EPH	004	032	And be kind and merciful to one another, forgiving one another, just as God has forgiven you in Christ.
049	EPH	005	001	Therefore, as most beloved sons, be imitators of God.
049	EPH	005	002	And walk in love, just as Christ also loved us and delivered himself for us, as an oblation and a sacrifice to God, with a fragrance of sweetness.
049	EPH	005	003	But let not any kind of fornication, or impurity, or rapacity so much as be named among you, just as is worthy of the saints,
049	EPH	005	004	nor any indecent, or foolish, or abusive talk, for this is without purpose; but instead, give thanks.
049	EPH	005	005	For know and understand this: no one who is a fornicator, or lustful, or rapacious (for these are a kind of service to idols) holds an inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and of God.
049	EPH	005	006	Let no one seduce you with empty words. For because of these things, the wrath of God was sent upon the sons of unbelief.
049	EPH	005	007	Therefore, do not choose to become participants with them.
049	EPH	005	008	For you were darkness, in times past, but now you are light, in the Lord. So then, walk as sons of the light.
049	EPH	005	009	For the fruit of the light is in all goodness and justice and truth,
049	EPH	005	010	affirming what is well-pleasing to God.
049	EPH	005	011	And so, have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but instead, refute them.
049	EPH	005	012	For the things that are done by them in secret are shameful, even to mention.
049	EPH	005	013	But all things that are disputed are made manifest by the light. For all that is made manifest is light.
049	EPH	005	014	Because of this, it is said: “You who are sleeping: awaken, and rise up from the dead, and so shall the Christ enlighten you.”
049	EPH	005	015	And so, brothers, see to it that you walk cautiously, not like the foolish,
049	EPH	005	016	but like the wise: atoning for this age, because this is an evil time.
049	EPH	005	017	For this reason, do not choose to be imprudent. Instead, understand what is the will of God.
049	EPH	005	018	And do not choose to be inebriated by wine, for this is self-indulgence. Instead, be filled with the Holy Spirit,
049	EPH	005	019	speaking among yourselves in psalms and hymns and spiritual canticles, singing and reciting psalms to the Lord in your hearts,
049	EPH	005	020	giving thanks always for everything, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to God the Father.
049	EPH	005	021	Be subject to one another in the fear of Christ.
049	EPH	005	022	Wives should be submissive to their husbands, as to the Lord.
049	EPH	005	023	For the husband is the head of the wife, just as Christ is the head of the Church. He is the Savior of his body.
049	EPH	005	024	Therefore, just as the Church is subject to Christ, so also should wives be subject to their husbands in all things.
049	EPH	005	025	Husbands, love your wives, just as Christ also loved the Church and handed himself over for her,
049	EPH	005	026	so that he might sanctify her, washing her clean by water and the Word of life,
049	EPH	005	027	so that he might offer her to himself as a glorious Church, not having any spot or wrinkle or any such thing, so that she would be holy and immaculate.
049	EPH	005	028	So, too, husbands should love their wives as their own bodies. He who loves his wife loves himself.
049	EPH	005	029	For no man has ever hated his own flesh, but instead he nourishes and cherishes it, as Christ also does to the Church.
049	EPH	005	030	For we are a part of his body, of his flesh and of his bones.
049	EPH	005	031	“For this reason, a man shall leave behind his father and mother, and he shall cling to his wife; and the two shall be as one flesh.”
049	EPH	005	032	This is a great Sacrament. And I am speaking in Christ and in the Church.
049	EPH	005	033	Yet truly, each and every one of you should love his wife as himself. And a wife should fear her husband.
049	EPH	006	001	Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this is just.
049	EPH	006	002	Honor your father and your mother. This is the first commandment with a promise:
049	EPH	006	003	so that it may be well with you, and so that you may have a long life upon the earth.
049	EPH	006	004	And you, fathers, do not provoke your children to anger, but educate them with the discipline and correction of the Lord.
049	EPH	006	005	Servants, be obedient to your lords according to the flesh, with fear and trembling, in the simplicity of your heart, as to Christ.
049	EPH	006	006	Do not serve only when seen, as if to please men, but act as servants of Christ, doing the will of God from the heart.
049	EPH	006	007	Serve with good will, as to the Lord, and not to men.
049	EPH	006	008	For you know that whatever good each one will do, the same will he receive from the Lord, whether he is servant or free.
049	EPH	006	009	And you, lords, act similarly toward them, setting aside threats, knowing that the Lord of both you and them is in heaven. For with him there is no favoritism toward anyone.
049	EPH	006	010	Concerning the rest, brothers, be strengthened in the Lord, by the power of his virtue.
049	EPH	006	011	Be clothed in the armor of God, so that you may be able to stand against the treachery of the devil.
049	EPH	006	012	For our struggle is not against flesh and blood, but against principalities and powers, against the directors of this world of darkness, against the spirits of wickedness in high places.
049	EPH	006	013	Because of this, take up the armor of God, so that you may be able to withstand the evil day and remain perfect in all things.
049	EPH	006	014	Therefore, stand firm, having been girded about your waist with truth, and having been clothed with the breastplate of justice,
049	EPH	006	015	and having feet which have been shod by the preparation of the Gospel of peace.
049	EPH	006	016	In all things, take up the shield of faith, with which you may be able to extinguish all the fiery darts of the most wicked one.
049	EPH	006	017	And take up the helmet of salvation and the sword of the Spirit (which is the Word of God).
049	EPH	006	018	Through every kind of prayer and supplication, pray at all times in spirit, and so be vigilant with every kind of earnest supplication, for all the saints,
049	EPH	006	019	and also for me, so that words may be given to me, as I open my mouth with faith to make known the mystery of the Gospel,
049	EPH	006	020	in such a manner that I may dare to speak exactly as I ought to speak. For I act as an ambassador in chains for the Gospel.
049	EPH	006	021	Now, so that you also may know the things that concern me and what I am doing, Tychicus, a most beloved brother and a faithful minister in the Lord, will make known everything to you.
049	EPH	006	022	I have sent him to you for this very reason, so that you may know the things that concern us, and so that he may console your hearts.
049	EPH	006	023	Peace to the brothers, and charity with faith, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
049	EPH	006	024	May grace be with all those who love our Lord Jesus Christ, unto incorruption. Amen.
