# BOOK	050	PHI	Philippians	Philippians
050	PHI	001	001	Paul and Timothy, servants of Jesus Christ, to all the saints in Christ Jesus who are at Philippi, with the bishops and deacons.
050	PHI	001	002	Grace and peace to you, from God our Father and from the Lord Jesus Christ.
050	PHI	001	003	I give thanks to my God, with every remembrance of you,
050	PHI	001	004	always, in all my prayers, making supplication for all of you with joy,
050	PHI	001	005	because of your communion in the Gospel of Christ, from the first day even until now.
050	PHI	001	006	I am confident of this very thing: that he who has begun this good work in you will perfect it, unto the day of Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	001	007	So then, it is right for me to feel this way about all of you, because I hold you in my heart, and because, in my chains and in the defense and confirmation of the Gospel, you all are partakers of my joy.
050	PHI	001	008	For God is my witness how, within the heart of Jesus Christ, I long for all of you.
050	PHI	001	009	And this I pray: that your charity may abound more and more, with knowledge and with all understanding,
050	PHI	001	010	so that you may be confirmed in what is better, in order that you may be sincere and without offense on the day of Christ:
050	PHI	001	011	filled with the fruit of justice, through Jesus Christ, in the glory and praise of God.
050	PHI	001	012	Now, brothers, I want you to know that the things concerning me happened for the advancement of the Gospel,
050	PHI	001	013	in such a way that my chains have become manifest in Christ in every place of judgment and in all other such places.
050	PHI	001	014	And many from among the brothers in the Lord, becoming confident through my chains, are now much bolder in speaking the Word of God without fear.
050	PHI	001	015	Certainly, some do so even because of envy and contention; and others, too, do so because of a good will to preach Christ.
050	PHI	001	016	Some act out of charity, knowing that I have been appointed for the defense of the Gospel.
050	PHI	001	017	But others, out of contention, announce Christ insincerely, claiming that their difficulties lift them up to my chains.
050	PHI	001	018	But what does it matter? As long as, by every means, whether under pretext or in truthfulness, Christ is announced. And about this, I rejoice, and moreover, I will continue to rejoice.
050	PHI	001	019	For I know that this will bring me to salvation, through your prayers and under the ministration of the Spirit of Jesus Christ,
050	PHI	001	020	by means of my own expectation and hope. For in nothing shall I be confounded. Instead, with all confidence, now just as always, Christ shall be magnified in my body, whether by life or by death.
050	PHI	001	021	For to me, to live is Christ, and to die is gain.
050	PHI	001	022	And while I live in the flesh, for me, there is the fruit of works. But I do not know which I would choose.
050	PHI	001	023	For I am constrained between the two: having a desire to be dissolved and to be with Christ, which is the far better thing,
050	PHI	001	024	but then to remain in the flesh is necessary for your sake.
050	PHI	001	025	And having this confidence, I know that I shall remain and that I shall continue to remain with all of you, for your advancement and for your joy in the faith,
050	PHI	001	026	so that your rejoicing may abound in Christ Jesus for me, through my return to you again.
050	PHI	001	027	Only let your behavior be worthy of the Gospel of Christ, so that, whether I return and see you, or whether, being absent, I hear about you, still you may stand firm with one spirit, with one mind, laboring together for the faith of the Gospel.
050	PHI	001	028	And in nothing be terrified by the adversaries. For what is to them an occasion of perdition, is to you an occasion of salvation, and this is from God.
050	PHI	001	029	For this has been given to you on behalf of Christ, not only so that you may believe in him, but even so that you may suffer with him,
050	PHI	001	030	engaging in the same struggle, of a kind which you also have seen in me, and which you now have heard from me.
050	PHI	002	001	Therefore, if there is any consolation in Christ, any solace of charity, any fellowship of the Spirit, any feelings of commiseration:
050	PHI	002	002	complete my joy by having the same understanding, holding to the same charity, being of one mind, with the same sentiment.
050	PHI	002	003	Let nothing be done by contention, nor in vain glory. Instead, in humility, let each of you esteem others to be better than himself.
050	PHI	002	004	Let each of you not consider anything to be your own, but rather to belong to others.
050	PHI	002	005	For this understanding in you was also in Christ Jesus:
050	PHI	002	006	who, though he was in the form of God, did not consider equality with God something to be seized.
050	PHI	002	007	Instead, he emptied himself, taking the form of a servant, being made in the likeness of men, and accepting the state of a man.
050	PHI	002	008	He humbled himself, becoming obedient even unto death, even the death of the Cross.
050	PHI	002	009	Because of this, God has also exalted him and has given him a name which is above every name,
050	PHI	002	010	so that, at the name of Jesus, every knee would bend, of those in heaven, of those on earth, and of those in hell,
050	PHI	002	011	and so that every tongue would confess that the Lord Jesus Christ is in the glory of God the Father.
050	PHI	002	012	And so, my most beloved, just as you have always obeyed, not only in my presence, but even more so now in my absence: work toward your salvation with fear and trembling.
050	PHI	002	013	For it is God who works in you, both so as to choose, and so as to act, in accord with his good will.
050	PHI	002	014	And do everything without murmuring or hesitation.
050	PHI	002	015	So may you be without blame, simple sons of God, without reproof, in the midst of a depraved and perverse nation, among whom you shine like lights in the world,
050	PHI	002	016	holding to the Word of Life, until my glory in the day of Christ. For I have not run in vain, nor have I labored in vain.
050	PHI	002	017	Moreover, if I am to be immolated because of the sacrifice and service of your faith, I rejoice and give thanks with all of you.
050	PHI	002	018	And over this same thing, you also should rejoice and give thanks, together with me.
050	PHI	002	019	Now I hope in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy to you soon, in order that I may be encouraged, when I know the things concerning you.
050	PHI	002	020	For I have no one else with such an agreeable mind, who, with sincere affection, is solicitous for you.
050	PHI	002	021	For they all seek the things that are of themselves, not the things that are of Jesus Christ.
050	PHI	002	022	So know this evidence of him: that like a son with a father, so has he served with me in the Gospel.
050	PHI	002	023	Therefore, I hope to send him to you immediately, as soon as I see what will happen concerning me.
050	PHI	002	024	But I trust in the Lord that I myself will also return to you soon.
050	PHI	002	025	Now I have considered it necessary to send to you Epaphroditus, my brother, and co-worker, and fellow soldier, and an attendant to my needs, but your Apostle.
050	PHI	002	026	For certainly, he has desired all of you, and he was saddened because you had heard that he was sick.
050	PHI	002	027	For he was sick, even unto death, but God took pity on him, and not only on him, but truly on myself also, so that I would not have sorrow upon sorrow.
050	PHI	002	028	Therefore, I sent him more readily, in order that, by seeing him again, you may rejoice, and I may be without sorrow.
050	PHI	002	029	And so, receive him with every joy in the Lord, and treat all those like him with honor.
050	PHI	002	030	For he was brought close even to death, for the sake of the work of Christ, handing over his own life, so that he might fulfill what was lacking from you concerning my service.
050	PHI	003	001	Concerning other things, my brothers, rejoice in the Lord. It is certainly not tiresome for me to write the same things to you, but for you, it is not necessary.
050	PHI	003	002	Beware of dogs; beware of those who work evil; beware of those who are divisive.
050	PHI	003	003	For we are the circumcised, we who serve God in the Spirit and who glory in Christ Jesus, having no confidence in the flesh.
050	PHI	003	004	Nevertheless, I might have confidence also in the flesh, for if anyone else seems to have confidence in the flesh, more so do I.
050	PHI	003	005	For I was circumcised on the eighth day, of the stock of Israel, from the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew among Hebrews. According to the law, I was a Pharisee;
050	PHI	003	006	according to zeal, I persecuted the Church of God; according to the justice that is in the law, I lived without blame.
050	PHI	003	007	But the things which had been to my gain, the same have I considered a loss, for the sake of Christ.
050	PHI	003	008	Yet truly, I consider everything to be a loss, because of the preeminent knowledge of Jesus Christ, my Lord, for whose sake I have suffered the loss of everything, considering it all to be like dung, so that I may gain Christ,
050	PHI	003	009	and so that you may be found in him, not having my justice, which is of the law, but that which is of the faith of Christ Jesus, the justice within faith, which is of God.
050	PHI	003	010	So shall I know him, and the power of his resurrection, and the fellowship of his Passion, having been fashioned according to his death,
050	PHI	003	011	if, by some means, I might attain to the resurrection which is from the dead.
050	PHI	003	012	It is not as though I have already received this, or were already perfect. But rather I pursue, so that by some means I might attain, that in which I have already been attained by Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	003	013	Brothers, I do not consider that I have already attained this. Instead, I do one thing: forgetting those things that are behind, and extending myself toward those things that are ahead,
050	PHI	003	014	I pursue the destination, the prize of the heavenly calling of God in Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	003	015	Therefore, as many of us as are being perfected, let us agree about this. And if in anything you disagree, God will reveal this to you also.
050	PHI	003	016	Yet truly, whatever point we reach, let us be of the same mind, and let us remain in the same rule.
050	PHI	003	017	Be imitators of me, brothers, and observe those who are walking similarly, just as you have seen by our example.
050	PHI	003	018	For many persons, about whom I have often told you (and now tell you, weeping,) are walking as enemies of the cross of Christ.
050	PHI	003	019	Their end is destruction; their god is their belly; and their glory is in their shame: for they are immersed in earthly things.
050	PHI	003	020	But our way of life is in heaven. And from heaven, too, we await the Savior, our Lord Jesus Christ,
050	PHI	003	021	who will transform the body of our lowliness, according to the form of the body of his glory, by means of that power by which he is even able to subject all things to himself.
050	PHI	004	001	And so, my most beloved and most desired brothers, my joy and my crown: stand firm in this way, in the Lord, most beloved.
050	PHI	004	002	I ask Euodia, and I beg Syntyche, to have the same understanding in the Lord.
050	PHI	004	003	And I also ask you, as my genuine companion, to assist those women who have labored with me in the Gospel, with Clement and the rest of my assistants, whose names are in the Book of Life.
050	PHI	004	004	Rejoice in the Lord always. Again, I say, rejoice.
050	PHI	004	005	Let your modesty be known to all men. The Lord is near.
050	PHI	004	006	Be anxious about nothing. But in all things, with prayer and supplication, with acts of thanksgiving, let your petitions be made known to God.
050	PHI	004	007	And so shall the peace of God, which exceeds all understanding, guard your hearts and minds in Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	004	008	Concerning the rest, brothers, whatever is true, whatever is chaste, whatever is just, whatever is holy, whatever is worthy to be loved, whatever is of good repute, if there is any virtue, if there is any praiseworthy discipline: meditate on these.
050	PHI	004	009	All the things that you have learned and accepted and heard and seen in me, do these. And so shall the God of peace be with you.
050	PHI	004	010	Now I rejoice in the Lord exceedingly, because finally, after some time, your feelings for me have flourished again, just as you formerly felt. For you had been preoccupied.
050	PHI	004	011	I am not saying this as if out of need. For I have learned that, in whatever state I am, it is sufficient.
050	PHI	004	012	I know how to be humbled, and I know how to abound. I am prepared for anything, anywhere: either to be full or to be hungry, either to have abundance or to endure scarcity.
050	PHI	004	013	Everything is possible in him who has strengthened me.
050	PHI	004	014	Yet truly, you have done well by sharing in my tribulation.
050	PHI	004	015	But you also know, O Philippians, that at the beginning of the Gospel, when I set out from Macedonia, not a single church shared with me in the plan of giving and receiving, except you alone.
050	PHI	004	016	For you even sent to Thessalonica, once, and then a second time, for what was useful to me.
050	PHI	004	017	It is not that I am seeking a gift. Instead, I seek the fruit that abounds to your benefit.
050	PHI	004	018	But I have everything in abundance. I have been filled up, having received from Epaphroditus the things that you sent; this is an odor of sweetness, an acceptable sacrifice, pleasing to God.
050	PHI	004	019	And may my God fulfill all your desires, according to his riches in glory in Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	004	020	And to God our Father be glory forever and ever. Amen.
050	PHI	004	021	Greet every saint in Christ Jesus.
050	PHI	004	022	The brothers who are with me greet you. All the saints greet you, but especially those who are of Caesar’s household.
050	PHI	004	023	May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.
