# BOOK	053	2TH	2 Thessalonians	2 Thessalonians
053	2TH	001	001	Paul and Sylvanus and Timothy, to the church of the Thessalonians, in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	001	002	Grace and peace to you, from God our Father and from the Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	001	003	We ought to give thanks always to God for you, brothers, in a fitting manner, because your faith is increasing greatly, and because the charity of each of you toward one another is abundant,
053	2TH	001	004	so much so that we ourselves even glory in you among the churches of God, because of your patience and faith in all of your persecutions and tribulations that you endure,
053	2TH	001	005	which are a sign of the just judgment of God, so that you may be held worthy of the kingdom of God, for which you also suffer.
053	2TH	001	006	For certainly, it is just for God to repay trouble to those who trouble you,
053	2TH	001	007	and to repay you, who are being troubled, with a repose with us, when the Lord Jesus is revealed from heaven with the Angels of his virtue,
053	2TH	001	008	granting vindication, by a flame of fire, against those who do not know God and who are not obedient to the Gospel of our Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	001	009	These shall be given the eternal punishment of destruction, apart from the face of the Lord and apart from the glory of his virtue,
053	2TH	001	010	when he arrives to be glorified in his saints, and to become a wonder in all those who have believed, in that day, because our testimony has been believed by you.
053	2TH	001	011	Because of this, too, we pray always for you, so that our God may make you worthy of his calling and may complete every act of his goodness, as well as his work of faith in virtue,
053	2TH	001	012	in order that the name of our Lord Jesus may be glorified in you, and you in him, in accord with the grace of our God and of the Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	002	001	But we ask you, brothers, concerning the advent of our Lord Jesus Christ and of our gathering to him,
053	2TH	002	002	that you not be readily disturbed or terrified in your minds, by any spirit, or word, or epistle, supposedly sent from us, claiming that the day of the Lord is close by.
053	2TH	002	003	Let no one deceive you in any way. For this cannot be, unless the apostasy will have arrived first, and the man of sin will have been revealed, the son of perdition,
053	2TH	002	004	who is an adversary to, and who is lifted up above, all that is called God or that is worshipped, so much so that he sits in the temple of God, presenting himself as if he were God.
053	2TH	002	005	Do you not recall that, when I was still with you, I told you these things?
053	2TH	002	006	And now you know what it is that holds him back, so that he may be revealed in his own time.
053	2TH	002	007	For the mystery of iniquity is already at work. And only one now holds back, and will continue to hold back, until he is taken from our midst.
053	2TH	002	008	And then that iniquitous one shall be revealed, the one whom the Lord Jesus shall bring to ruin with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy at the brightness of his return:
053	2TH	002	009	him whose advent is accompanied by the works of Satan, with every kind of power and signs and false miracles,
053	2TH	002	010	and with every seduction of iniquity, toward those who are perishing because they have not accepted the love of truth, so that they may be saved.
053	2TH	002	011	For this reason, God will send to them works of deception, so that they may believe in lies,
053	2TH	002	012	in order that all those who have not believed in the truth, but who have consented to iniquity, may be judged.
053	2TH	002	013	Yet we must always give thanks to God for you, brothers, beloved of God, because God has chosen you as first-fruits for salvation, by the sanctification of the Spirit and by faith in the truth.
053	2TH	002	014	He has also called you into truth through our Gospel, unto the acquisition of the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.
053	2TH	002	015	And so, brothers, stand firm, and hold to the traditions that you have learned, whether by word or by our epistle.
053	2TH	002	016	So may our Lord Jesus Christ himself, and God our Father, who has loved us and who has given us an everlasting consolation and good hope in grace,
053	2TH	002	017	exhort your hearts and confirm you in every good word and deed.
053	2TH	003	001	Concerning other things, brothers, pray for us, so that the Word of God may advance and be glorified, just as it is among you,
053	2TH	003	002	and so that we may be freed from pertinacious and evil men. For not everyone is faithful.
053	2TH	003	003	But God is faithful. He will strengthen you, and he will guard you from evil.
053	2TH	003	004	And we have confidence about you in the Lord, that you are doing, and will continue to do, just as we have instructed.
053	2TH	003	005	And may the Lord direct your hearts, in the charity of God and with the patience of Christ.
053	2TH	003	006	But we strongly caution you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, to draw yourselves away from every brother who is walking in disorder and not according to the tradition that they received from us.
053	2TH	003	007	For you yourselves know the manner in which you ought to imitate us. For we were not disorderly among you.
053	2TH	003	008	Nor did we eat bread from anyone for free, but rather, we worked night and day, in hardship and weariness, so as not to be burdensome to you.
053	2TH	003	009	It was not as if we had no authority, but this was so that we might present ourselves as an example to you, in order to imitate us.
053	2TH	003	010	Then, too, while we were with you, we insisted on this to you: that if anyone was not willing to work, neither should he eat.
053	2TH	003	011	For we have heard that there are some among you who act disruptively, not working at all, but eagerly meddling.
053	2TH	003	012	Now we charge those who act in this way, and we beg them in the Lord Jesus Christ, that they work in silence and eat their own bread.
053	2TH	003	013	And you, brothers, do not grow weak in doing good.
053	2TH	003	014	But if anyone does not obey our word by this epistle, take note of him and do not keep company with him, so that he may be ashamed.
053	2TH	003	015	But do not be willing to consider him as an enemy; instead, correct him as a brother.
053	2TH	003	016	Then may the Lord of peace himself give you an everlasting peace, in every place. May the Lord be with all of you.
053	2TH	003	017	The greeting of Paul with my own hand, which is the seal in every epistle. So do I write.
053	2TH	003	018	May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all. Amen.
#
# BOOK	054	1TI	1 Timothy	1 Timothy
054	1TI	001	001	Paul, an Apostle of Jesus Christ by the authority of God our Savior and Christ Jesus our hope,
054	1TI	001	002	to Timothy, beloved son in the faith. Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and from Christ Jesus our Lord.
054	1TI	001	003	Now I asked you to remain at Ephesus, while I went into Macedonia, so that you would speak strongly against certain ones who have been teaching a different way,
054	1TI	001	004	against those who have been paying attention to fables and endless genealogies. These things present questions as if they were greater than the edification that is of God, which is in faith.
054	1TI	001	005	Now the goal of instruction is charity from a pure heart, and a good conscience, and an unfeigned faith.
054	1TI	001	006	Certain persons, wandering away from these things, have been turned aside to empty babbling,
054	1TI	001	007	desiring to be teachers of the law, but understanding neither the things that they themselves are saying, nor what they are affirming about these things.
054	1TI	001	008	But we know that the law is good, if one makes use of it properly.
054	1TI	001	009	Knowing this, that the law was not set in place for the just, but for the unjust and the insubordinate, for the impious and sinners, for the wicked and the defiled, for those who commit patricide, matricide, or homicide,
054	1TI	001	010	for fornicators, for males who sleep with males, for kidnappers, for liars, for perjurers, and whatever else is contrary to sound doctrine,
054	1TI	001	011	which is in accord with the Gospel of the glory of the blessed God, the Gospel which has been entrusted to me.
054	1TI	001	012	I give thanks to him who has strengthened me, Christ Jesus our Lord, because he has considered me faithful, placing me in the ministry,
054	1TI	001	013	though previously I was a blasphemer, and a persecutor, and contemptuous. But then I obtained the mercy of God. For I had been acting ignorantly, in unbelief.
054	1TI	001	014	And so the grace of our Lord has abounded greatly, with the faith and love that is in Christ Jesus.
054	1TI	001	015	It is a faithful saying, and worthy of acceptance by everyone, that Christ Jesus came into this world to bring salvation to sinners, among whom I am first.
054	1TI	001	016	But it was for this reason that I obtained mercy, so that in me as first, Christ Jesus would display all patience, for the instruction of those who would believe in him unto eternal life.
054	1TI	001	017	So then, to the King of ages, to the immortal, invisible, solitary God, be honor and glory forever and ever. Amen.
054	1TI	001	018	This precept I commend to you, my son Timothy, in accord with the prophets who preceded you: that you serve among them like a soldier in a good war,
054	1TI	001	019	holding to faith and good conscience, against those who, by rejecting these things, have made a shipwreck of the faith.
054	1TI	001	020	Among these are Hymenaeus and Alexander, whom I have handed over to Satan, so that they may learn not to blaspheme.
054	1TI	002	001	And so I beg you, first of all, to make supplications, prayers, petitions, and thanksgivings for all men,
054	1TI	002	002	for kings, and for all who are in high places, so that we may lead a quiet and tranquil life in all piety and chastity.
054	1TI	002	003	For this is good and acceptable in the sight of God our Savior,
054	1TI	002	004	who wants all men to be saved and to arrive at an acknowledgment of the truth.
054	1TI	002	005	For there is one God, and one mediator of God and of men, the man Christ Jesus,
054	1TI	002	006	who gave himself as a redemption for all, as a testimony in its proper time.
054	1TI	002	007	Of this testimony, I have been appointed a preacher and an Apostle, (I speak the truth, I do not lie) as a teacher of the Gentiles, in faith and in truth.
054	1TI	002	008	Therefore, I want men to pray in every place, lifting up pure hands, without anger or dissension.
054	1TI	002	009	Similarly also, women should be dressed fittingly, adorning themselves with compunction and restraint, and not with plaited hair, nor gold, nor pearls, nor costly attire,
054	1TI	002	010	but in a manner proper for women who are professing piety by means of good works.
054	1TI	002	011	Let a woman learn in silence with all subjection.
054	1TI	002	012	For I do not permit a woman to teach, nor to be in authority over a man, but to be in silence.
054	1TI	002	013	For Adam was formed first, then Eve.
054	1TI	002	014	And Adam was not seduced, but the woman, having been seduced, was in transgression.
054	1TI	002	015	Yet she will be saved by bearing children, if she has continued in faith and love, and in sanctification accompanied by self-restraint.
054	1TI	003	001	It is a faithful saying: if a man desires the episcopate, he desires a good work.
054	1TI	003	002	Therefore, it is necessary for a bishop to be beyond reproach, the husband of one wife, sober, prudent, gracious, chaste, hospitable, a teacher,
054	1TI	003	003	not a drunkard, not combative but restrained, not quarrelsome, not covetous;
054	1TI	003	004	but a man who leads his own house well, having children who are subordinate with all chastity.
054	1TI	003	005	For if a man does not know how to lead his own house, how will he take care of the Church of God?
054	1TI	003	006	He must not be a new convert, lest, being elated by pride, he may fall under the sentence of the devil.
054	1TI	003	007	And it is necessary for him also to have good testimony from those who are outside, so that he may not fall into disrepute and the snare of the devil.
054	1TI	003	008	Similarly, deacons must be chaste, not double-tongued, not given to much wine, not pursuing tainted profit,
054	1TI	003	009	holding to the mystery of the faith with a pure conscience.
054	1TI	003	010	And these things should be proven first, and then they may minister, being without offense.
054	1TI	003	011	Similarly, the women must be chaste, not slanderers, sober, faithful in all things.
054	1TI	003	012	Deacons should be the husband of one wife, men who lead their own children and their own houses well.
054	1TI	003	013	For those who have ministered well will acquire for themselves a good position, and much confidence in the faith which is in Christ Jesus.
054	1TI	003	014	I am writing these things to you, with the hope that I will come to you soon.
054	1TI	003	015	But, if I am delayed, you should know the manner in which it is necessary to conduct yourself in the house of God, which is the Church of the living God, the pillar and the foundation of truth.
054	1TI	003	016	And it is clearly great, this mystery of piety, which was manifested in the flesh, which was justified in the Spirit, which has appeared to Angels, which has been preached to the Gentiles, which is believed in the world, which has been taken up in glory.
054	1TI	004	001	Now the Spirit has clearly said that, in the end times, some persons will depart from the faith, paying attention to spirits of error and the doctrines of devils,
054	1TI	004	002	speaking lies in hypocrisy, and having their consciences seared,
054	1TI	004	003	prohibiting marriage, abstaining from foods, which God has created to be accepted with thanksgiving by the faithful and by those who have understood the truth.
054	1TI	004	004	For every creature of God is good, and nothing is to be rejected which is received with thanksgiving;
054	1TI	004	005	for it has been sanctified by the Word of God and by prayer.
054	1TI	004	006	By proposing these things to the brothers, you will be a good minister of Christ Jesus, nourished by words of faith, and by the good doctrine that you have secured.
054	1TI	004	007	But avoid the silly fables of old women. And exercise yourself so as to advance in piety.
054	1TI	004	008	For the exercise of the body is somewhat useful. But piety is useful in all things, holding the promise of life, in the present and in the future.
054	1TI	004	009	This is a faithful saying and worthy of full acceptance.
054	1TI	004	010	For this reason we labor and are maligned: because we hope in the living God, who is the Savior of all men, most especially of the faithful.
054	1TI	004	011	Instruct and teach these things.
054	1TI	004	012	Let no one despise your youth, but be an example among the faithful in word, in behavior, in charity, in faith, in chastity.
054	1TI	004	013	Until I arrive, attend to reading, to exhortation, and to doctrine.
054	1TI	004	014	Do not be willing to neglect the grace that is within you, which was given to you through prophecy, with the imposition of the hands of the priesthood.
054	1TI	004	015	Meditate on these things, so that your progress may be manifest to all.
054	1TI	004	016	Pay attention to yourself and to doctrine. Pursue these things. For in doing so, you will save both yourself and those who listen to you.
054	1TI	005	001	You should not rebuke an old man, but rather plead with him, as if he were your father; with young men, like brothers;
054	1TI	005	002	with old women, like mothers; with young women, in all chastity, like sisters.
054	1TI	005	003	Honor those widows who are true widows.
054	1TI	005	004	But if any widow has children or grandchildren, let her first learn to manage her own household, and to fulfill, in turn, her own obligation to her parents; for this is acceptable before God.
054	1TI	005	005	But she who is truly a widow and is destitute, let her hope in God, and let her be urgent in supplications and prayers, night and day.
054	1TI	005	006	For she who is living in pleasures is dead, while living.
054	1TI	005	007	And give instruction in this, so that they may be beyond reproach.
054	1TI	005	008	But if anyone has no concern for his own, and especially for those of his own household, he has denied the faith, and he is worse than an unbeliever.
054	1TI	005	009	Let a widow be chosen who is no less than sixty years of age, who was the wife of one husband,
054	1TI	005	010	who has testimony of her good works: whether she has educated children, or has provided hospitality, or has washed the feet of the saints, or has ministered to those suffering tribulation, or has pursued any kind of good work.
054	1TI	005	011	But avoid the younger widows. For once they have flourished in Christ, they will want to marry,
054	1TI	005	012	resulting in damnation, because they have disregarded the primacy of faith.
054	1TI	005	013	And being at the same time also idle, they learn to go from house to house, being not only idle, but also talkative and curious, speaking of things which do not concern them.
054	1TI	005	014	Therefore, I want the younger women to marry, to procreate children, to be mothers of families, to provide no ready opportunity for the adversary to speak evil.
054	1TI	005	015	For certain ones have already been turned back to Satan.
054	1TI	005	016	If any among the faithful have widows, let him minister to them and not burden the Church, so that there may be enough for those who are true widows.
054	1TI	005	017	Let priests who lead well be held worthy of twice the honor, especially those who labor in the Word and in doctrine.
054	1TI	005	018	For Scripture says: “You shall not muzzle an ox as it is treading out the grain,” and, “The worker is worthy of his pay.”
054	1TI	005	019	Do not be willing to accept an accusation against a priest, except under two or three witnesses.
054	1TI	005	020	Reprove sinners in the sight of everyone, so that the others may have fear.
054	1TI	005	021	I testify before God and Christ Jesus and the elect Angels, that you should observe these things without prejudgment, doing nothing which shows favoritism to either side.
054	1TI	005	022	You should not be quick to impose hands on anyone, nor should you take part in the sins of outsiders. Keep yourself chaste.
054	1TI	005	023	Do not continue to drink only water, but make use of a little wine, for the sake of your stomach and your frequent infirmities.
054	1TI	005	024	The sins of some men have been made manifest, preceding them to judgment, but those of others are manifested later.
054	1TI	005	025	Similarly, too, good deeds have been made manifest, but even when they are not, they cannot remain hidden.
054	1TI	006	001	Whoever are servants under the yoke, let them consider their masters to be worthy of every honor, lest the name and doctrine of the Lord be blasphemed.
054	1TI	006	002	But those who have believing masters, let them not despise them because they are brothers, but rather serve them all the more because they are believing and beloved, participants of the same service. Teach and exhort these things.
054	1TI	006	003	If anyone teaches otherwise, and does not consent to the sound words of our Lord Jesus Christ, and to that doctrine which is in accord with piety,
054	1TI	006	004	then he is arrogant, knowing nothing, yet languishing amid the questions and quarrels of words. From these arise envy, contention, blasphemy, evil suspicions:
054	1TI	006	005	the conflicts of men who have been corrupted in mind and deprived of truth, who consider profit to be piety.
054	1TI	006	006	But piety with sufficiency is great gain.
054	1TI	006	007	For we brought nothing into this world, and there is no doubt that we can take nothing away.
054	1TI	006	008	But, having nourishment and some kind of covering, we should be content with these.
054	1TI	006	009	For those who want to become rich fall into temptation and into the snare of the devil and into many useless and harmful desires, which submerge men in destruction and in perdition.
054	1TI	006	010	For desire is the root of all evils. Some persons, hungering in this way, have strayed from the faith and have entangled themselves in many sorrows.
054	1TI	006	011	But you, O man of God, flee from these things, and truly pursue justice, piety, faith, charity, patience, meekness.
054	1TI	006	012	Fight the good fight of faith. Take hold of the eternal life to which you have been called, and make a good profession of faith in the sight of many witnesses.
054	1TI	006	013	I charge you, in the sight of God, who enlivens all things, and in the sight of Christ Jesus, who gave the testimony of a good profession under Pontius Pilate,
054	1TI	006	014	to observe the commandment, immaculately, irreproachably, unto the return of our Lord Jesus Christ.
054	1TI	006	015	For at the proper time, he shall reveal the blessed and only Power, the King of kings and the Lord of lords,
054	1TI	006	016	who alone holds immortality, and who inhabits the inaccessible light, whom no man has seen, nor even is able to see, to whom is honor and everlasting dominion. Amen.
054	1TI	006	017	Instruct the wealthy of this age not to have a superior attitude, nor to hope in the uncertainty of riches, but in the living God, who offers us everything in abundance to enjoy,
054	1TI	006	018	and to do good, to become rich in good works, to donate readily, to share,
054	1TI	006	019	to gather for themselves the treasure of a good foundation for the future, so that they may obtain true life.
054	1TI	006	020	O Timothy, guard what has been deposited with you, avoiding the voice of profane novelties and of opposing ideas, which are falsely called knowledge.
054	1TI	006	021	Certain persons, promising these things, have perished from the faith. May grace be with you. Amen.
