# BOOK	057	PHM	Philemon	Philemon
057	PHM	001	001	Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy, a brother, to Philemon, our beloved fellow laborer,
057	PHM	001	002	and to Apphia, most beloved sister, and to Archippus, our fellow soldier, and to the church which is in your house.
057	PHM	001	003	Grace and peace to you, from God our Father and from the Lord Jesus Christ.
057	PHM	001	004	I give thanks to my God, always keeping remembrance of you in my prayers,
057	PHM	001	005	(for I am hearing of your charity and faith, which you have in the Lord Jesus and with all the saints)
057	PHM	001	006	so that the participation of your faith may become evident by the recognition of every good work which is in you in Christ Jesus.
057	PHM	001	007	For I have found great joy and consolation in your charity, because the hearts of the saints have been refreshed by you, brother.
057	PHM	001	008	Because of this, I have enough confidence in Christ Jesus to command you concerning certain things,
057	PHM	001	009	but I beg you instead, for the sake of charity, since you are so much like Paul: an old man and now also a prisoner of Jesus Christ.
057	PHM	001	010	I beg you, on behalf of my son, whom I have begotten in my chains, Onesimus.
057	PHM	001	011	In times past, he was useless to you, but now he is useful both to me and to you.
057	PHM	001	012	So I have sent him back to you. And may you receive him like my own heart.
057	PHM	001	013	I myself wanted to retain him with me, so that he might minister to me, on your behalf, while I am in the chains of the Gospel.
057	PHM	001	014	But I was willing to do nothing without your counsel, so as not to make use of your good deed as if out of necessity, but only willingly.
057	PHM	001	015	So perhaps, then, he departed from you for a time, so that you might receive him again for eternity,
057	PHM	001	016	no longer as a servant, but, in place of a servant, a most beloved brother, especially to me: but how much more to you, both in the flesh and in the Lord!
057	PHM	001	017	Therefore, if you hold me to be a companion, receive him as you would me.
057	PHM	001	018	But if he has harmed you in any way, or if he is in your debt, charge it to me.
057	PHM	001	019	I, Paul, have written this with my own hand: I will repay. And I need not tell you, that you are also in debt yourself, to me.
057	PHM	001	020	So it is, brother. May I delight with you in the Lord! Refresh my heart in Christ.
057	PHM	001	021	I have written to you, trusting in your obedience, knowing, too, that you will do even more than what I say.
057	PHM	001	022	But also, at once, prepare a lodging for me. For I am hoping, through your prayers, to present myself to you.
057	PHM	001	023	Greet Epaphras, my fellow captive in Christ Jesus,
057	PHM	001	024	and Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my helpers.
057	PHM	001	025	May the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.
