# BOOK	058	HEB	Hebrews	Hebrews
058	HEB	001	001	In many places and in many ways, in past times, God spoke to the fathers through the Prophets;
058	HEB	001	002	lastly, in these days, he has spoken to us through the Son, whom he appointed as the heir of all things, and through whom he made the world.
058	HEB	001	003	And since the Son is the brightness of his glory, and the figure of his substance, and is carrying all things by the Word of his virtue, thereby accomplishing a purging of sins, he sits at the right hand of Majesty on high.
058	HEB	001	004	And having been made so much better than the Angels, he has inherited a name so much greater than theirs.
058	HEB	001	005	For to which of the Angels has he ever said: “You are my Son; today have I begotten you?” Or again: “I will be a Father to him, and he shall be a Son to me?”
058	HEB	001	006	And again, when he brings the only-begotten Son into the world, he says: “And let all the Angels of God adore him.”
058	HEB	001	007	And about the Angels, certainly, he says: “He makes his Angels spirits, and his ministers a flame of fire.”
058	HEB	001	008	But about the Son: “Your throne, O God, is forever and ever. The scepter of your kingdom is a scepter of equity.
058	HEB	001	009	You have loved justice, and you have hated iniquity. Because of this, God, your God, has anointed you with the oil of exultation, above your companions.”
058	HEB	001	010	And: “In the beginning, O Lord, you founded the earth. And the heavens are the work of your hands.
058	HEB	001	011	These shall pass away, but you will remain. And all will grow old like a garment.
058	HEB	001	012	And you will change them like a cloak, and they shall be changed. Yet you are ever the same, and your years will not diminish.”
058	HEB	001	013	But to which of the Angels has he ever said: “Sit at my right hand, until I make your enemies your footstool?”
058	HEB	001	014	Are they not all spirits of ministration, sent to minister for the sake of those who shall receive the inheritance of salvation?
058	HEB	002	001	For this reason, it is necessary for us to observe more thoroughly the things that we have heard, lest we let them slip away.
058	HEB	002	002	For if a word that was spoken through the Angels has been made firm, and every transgression and disobedience has received the recompense of a just retribution,
058	HEB	002	003	in what way might we escape, if we neglect such a great salvation? For though initially it had begun to be described by the Lord, it was confirmed among us by those who heard him,
058	HEB	002	004	with God testifying to it by signs and wonders, and by various miracles, and by the pouring out of the Holy Spirit, in accord with his own will.
058	HEB	002	005	For God did not subject the future world, about which we are speaking, to the Angels.
058	HEB	002	006	But someone, in a certain place, has testified, saying: “What is man, that you are mindful of him, or the Son of man, that you visit him?
058	HEB	002	007	You have reduced him to a little less than the Angels. You have crowned him with glory and honor, and you have set him over the works of your hands.
058	HEB	002	008	You have subjected all things under his feet.” For in as much as he has subjected all things to him, he has left nothing not subject to him. But in the present time, we do not yet perceive that all things have been made subject to him.
058	HEB	002	009	Yet we understand that Jesus, who was reduced to a little less than the Angels, was crowned with glory and honor because of his Passion and death, in order that, by the grace of God, he might taste death for all.
058	HEB	002	010	For it was fitting for him, because of whom and through whom all things exist, who had led many children into glory, to complete the authorship of their salvation through his Passion.
058	HEB	002	011	For he who sanctifies, and those who are sanctified, are all from One. For this reason, he is not ashamed to call them brothers, saying:
058	HEB	002	012	“I will announce your name to my brothers. In the midst of the Church, I will praise you.”
058	HEB	002	013	And again: “I will be faithful in him.” And again: “Behold, I and my children, whom God has given to me.”
058	HEB	002	014	Therefore, because children have a common flesh and blood, he himself also, in like manner, has shared in the same, so that through death, he might destroy him who held the dominion of death, that is, the devil,
058	HEB	002	015	and so that he might free those who, through the fear of death, had been condemned to servitude throughout their entire life.
058	HEB	002	016	For at no time did he take hold of the Angels, but instead he took hold of the offspring of Abraham.
058	HEB	002	017	Therefore, it is fitting for him to be made similar to his brothers in all things, so that he might become a merciful and faithful High Priest before God, in order that he might bring forgiveness to the offenses of the people.
058	HEB	002	018	For in as much as he himself has suffered and has been tempted, he also is able to assist those who are tempted.
058	HEB	003	001	Therefore, holy brothers, sharers in the heavenly calling, consider the Apostle and High Priest of our confession: Jesus.
058	HEB	003	002	He is faithful to the One who made him, just as Moses also was, with his entire house.
058	HEB	003	003	For this Jesus was considered worthy of greater glory than Moses, so much so that the house which he has built holds a greater honor than the former one.
058	HEB	003	004	For every house is built by someone, but God is the One who has created all things.
058	HEB	003	005	And certainly Moses was faithful, with his entire house, like any servant, as a testimony to those things that would soon be said.
058	HEB	003	006	Yet truly, Christ is like a Son in his own house. We are that house, if we firmly retain the faithfulness and the glory of hope, even unto the end.
058	HEB	003	007	Because of this, it is just as the Holy Spirit says: “If today you hear his voice,
058	HEB	003	008	harden not your hearts, as in the provocation, the very day of temptation, in the desert,
058	HEB	003	009	where your fathers tested me, even though they had seen and examined my works for forty years.
058	HEB	003	010	For this reason, I was enraged against this generation, and I said: They always wander astray in heart. For they have not known my ways.
058	HEB	003	011	So it is as I swore in my wrath: They shall not enter into my rest!”
058	HEB	003	012	Be cautious, brothers, lest perhaps there may be, in any of you, an evil heart of unbelief, turning aside from the living God.
058	HEB	003	013	Instead, exhort one another every day, while it is still called ‘today,’ so that none of you may become hardened through the falseness of sin.
058	HEB	003	014	For we have been made participants in Christ. This is only so, if we firmly retain the beginning of his substance, even unto the end.
058	HEB	003	015	For it has been said: “If today you hear his voice, harden not your hearts, in the same manner as in the former provocation.”
058	HEB	003	016	For some of those listening did provoke him. But not all of these had set forth from Egypt through Moses.
058	HEB	003	017	So against whom was he angry for forty years? Was it not those who had sinned, whose dead bodies lay prostrate in the desert?
058	HEB	003	018	But to whom did he swear that they would not enter into his rest, except to those who were incredulous?
058	HEB	003	019	And so, we perceive that they were not able to enter because of unbelief.
058	HEB	004	001	Therefore, we should be afraid, lest the promise of entering into his rest may be relinquished, and some of you may be judged to be lacking.
058	HEB	004	002	For this was announced to us in a similar manner as to them. But the mere hearing of the word did not benefit them, since it was not joined together with a faith in those things that they heard.
058	HEB	004	003	For we who have believed shall enter into rest, in the same manner as he said: “So it is as I have sworn in my wrath: They shall not enter into my rest!” And certainly, this is when the works from the foundation of the world have been finished.
058	HEB	004	004	For, in a certain place, he spoke about the seventh day in this manner: “And God rested on the seventh day from all his works.”
058	HEB	004	005	And in this place again: “They shall not enter into my rest!”
058	HEB	004	006	Therefore, this is because certain ones remain who are to enter into it, and those to whom it was announced first did not enter into it, because of unbelief.
058	HEB	004	007	Again, he defines a certain day, after so much time, saying in David, “Today,” just as it was stated above, “If today you hear his voice, harden not your hearts.”
058	HEB	004	008	For if Jesus had offered them rest, he would never have spoken, afterward, about another day.
058	HEB	004	009	And so, there remains a Sabbath of rest for the people of God.
058	HEB	004	010	For whoever has entered into his rest, the same has also rested from his works, just as God did from his.
058	HEB	004	011	Therefore, let us hasten to enter into that rest, so that no one may fall into the same example of unbelief.
058	HEB	004	012	For the Word of God is living and effective: more piercing than any two-edged sword, reaching to the division even between the soul and the spirit, even between the joints and the marrow, and so it discerns the thoughts and intentions of the heart.
058	HEB	004	013	And there is no created thing that is invisible to his sight. For all things are naked and open to the eyes of him, about whom we are speaking.
058	HEB	004	014	Therefore, since we have a great High Priest, who has pierced the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, we should hold to our confession.
058	HEB	004	015	For we do not have a high priest who is unable to have compassion on our infirmities, but rather one who was tempted in all things, just as we are, yet without sin.
058	HEB	004	016	Therefore, let us go forth with confidence toward the throne of grace, so that we may obtain mercy, and find grace, in a helpful time.
058	HEB	005	001	For every high priest, having been taken from among men, is appointed on behalf of men toward the things which pertain to God, so that he may offer gifts and sacrifices on behalf of sins;
058	HEB	005	002	he is able to commiserate with those who are ignorant and who wander astray, because he himself is also encompassed by infirmity.
058	HEB	005	003	And because of this, he also must make such offerings for sins even for himself, in the same manner as for the people.
058	HEB	005	004	Neither does anyone take up this honor himself, but rather he who is called by God, just as Aaron was.
058	HEB	005	005	Thus, even Christ did not glorify himself, so as to become High Priest, but instead, it was God who said to him: “You are my Son. Today I have begotten you.”
058	HEB	005	006	And similarly, he says in another place: “You are a priest forever, according to the order of Melchizedek.”
058	HEB	005	007	It is Christ who, in the days of his flesh, with a strong cry and tears, offered prayers and supplications to the One who was able to save him from death, and who was heard because of his reverence.
058	HEB	005	008	And although, certainly, he is the Son of God, he learned obedience by the things that he suffered.
058	HEB	005	009	And having reached his consummation, he was made, for all who are obedient to him, the cause of eternal salvation,
058	HEB	005	010	having been called by God to be the High Priest, according to the order of Melchizedek.
058	HEB	005	011	Our message about him is great, and difficult to explain when speaking, because you have been made feeble when listening.
058	HEB	005	012	For even though it is the time when you ought to be teachers, you are still lacking, so that you must be taught the things that are the basic elements of the Word of God, and so you have been made like those who are in need of milk, and not of solid food.
058	HEB	005	013	For anyone who is still feeding on milk is still unskillful in the Word of Justice; for he is like an infant.
058	HEB	005	014	But solid food is for those who are mature, for those who, by practice, have sharpened their mind, so as to discern good from evil.
058	HEB	006	001	Therefore, interrupting an explanation of the basics of Christ, let us consider what is more advanced, not presenting again the fundamentals of repentance from dead works, and of faith toward God,
058	HEB	006	002	of the doctrine of baptism, and also of the imposition of hands, and of the resurrection of the dead, and of eternal judgment.
058	HEB	006	003	And we shall do this, if indeed God permits it.
058	HEB	006	004	For it is impossible for those who were once illuminated, and have even tasted of the heavenly gift, and have become sharers in the Holy Spirit,
058	HEB	006	005	who, despite having tasted the good Word of God and the virtues of the future age,
058	HEB	006	006	have yet fallen away, to be renewed again to penance, since they are crucifying again in themselves the Son of God and are still maintaining pretenses.
058	HEB	006	007	For the earth accepts a blessing from God, by drinking in the rain that often falls upon it, and by producing plants that are useful to those by whom it is cultivated.
058	HEB	006	008	But whatever brings forth thorns and briers is rejected, and is closest to what is accursed; their consummation is in combustion.
058	HEB	006	009	But from you, most beloved, we are confident that there will be things better and closer to salvation; even though we speak in this way.
058	HEB	006	010	For God is not unjust, such that he would forget your work and the love that you have shown in his name. For you have ministered, and you continue to minister, to the saints.
058	HEB	006	011	Yet we desire that each one of you display the same solicitude toward the fulfillment of hope, even unto the end,
058	HEB	006	012	so that you may not be slow to act, but instead may be imitators of those who, through faith and patience, shall inherit the promises.
058	HEB	006	013	For God, in making promises to Abraham, swore by himself, (because he had no one greater by whom he might swear),
058	HEB	006	014	saying: “Blessing, I shall bless you, and multiplying, I shall multiply you.”
058	HEB	006	015	And in this way, by enduring patiently, he secured the promise.
058	HEB	006	016	For men swear by what is greater than themselves, and an oath as confirmation is the end of all their controversy.
058	HEB	006	017	In this matter, God, wanting to reveal more thoroughly the immutability of his counsel to the heirs of the promise, interposed an oath,
058	HEB	006	018	so that by two immutable things, in which it is impossible for God to lie, we may have the strongest solace: we who have fled together so as to hold fast to the hope set before us.
058	HEB	006	019	This we have as an anchor of the soul, safe and sound, which advances even to the interior of the veil,
058	HEB	006	020	to the place where the forerunner Jesus has entered on our behalf, so as to become the High Priest for eternity, according to the order of Melchizedek.
058	HEB	007	001	For this Melchizedek, king of Salem, priest of the Most High God, met Abraham, as he was returning from the slaughter of the kings, and blessed him.
058	HEB	007	002	And Abraham divided to him a tenth part of everything. And in translation his name is first, indeed, king of justice, and next also king of Salem, that is, king of peace.
058	HEB	007	003	Without father, without mother, without genealogy, having neither beginning of days, nor end of life, he is thereby likened to the Son of God, who remains a priest continuously.
058	HEB	007	004	Next, consider how great this man is, since the Patriarch Abraham even gave tithes to him from the principal things.
058	HEB	007	005	And indeed, those who are from the sons of Levi, having received the priesthood, hold a commandment to take tithes from the people in accord with the law, that is, from their brothers, even though they also went forth from the loins of Abraham.
058	HEB	007	006	But this man, whose lineage is not enumerated with them, received tithes from Abraham, and he blessed even the one who held the promises.
058	HEB	007	007	Yet this is without any contradiction, for what is less should be blessed by what is better.
058	HEB	007	008	And certainly, here, men who receive tithes still die; but there, he bears witness that he lives.
058	HEB	007	009	And so it may be said that even Levi, who received tithes, was himself a tithe through Abraham.
058	HEB	007	010	For he was still in the loins of his father, when Melchizedek met him.
058	HEB	007	011	Therefore, if consummation had occurred through the Levitical priesthood (for under it the people received the law), then what further need would there be for another Priest to rise up according to the order of Melchizedek, one who was not called according to the order of Aaron?
058	HEB	007	012	For since the priesthood has been transferred, it is necessary that the law also be transferred.
058	HEB	007	013	For he about whom these things have been spoken is from another tribe, in which no one attends before the altar.
058	HEB	007	014	For it is evident that our Lord arose out of Judah, a tribe about which Moses said nothing concerning priests.
058	HEB	007	015	And yet it is far more evident that, according to the likeness of Melchizedek, there rises up another priest,
058	HEB	007	016	who was made, not according to the law of a carnal commandment, but according to the virtue of an indissoluble life.
058	HEB	007	017	For he testifies: “You are a priest forever, according to the order of Melchizedek.”
058	HEB	007	018	Certainly, there is a setting aside of the former commandment, because of its weakness and lack of usefulness.
058	HEB	007	019	For the law led no one to perfection, yet truly it introduced a better hope, through which we draw near to God.
058	HEB	007	020	Moreover, it is not without an oath. For certainly, the others were made priests without an oath.
058	HEB	007	021	But this man was made a priest with an oath, by the One who said to him: “The Lord has sworn and he will not repent. You are a priest forever.”
058	HEB	007	022	By so much, Jesus has been made the sponsor of a better testament.
058	HEB	007	023	And certainly, so many of the others became priests because, due to death, they were prohibited from continuing.
058	HEB	007	024	But this man, because he continues forever, has an everlasting priesthood.
058	HEB	007	025	And for this reason, he is able, continuously, to save those who approach God through him, since he is ever alive to make intercession on our behalf.
058	HEB	007	026	For it was fitting that we should have such a High Priest: holy, innocent, undefiled, set apart from sinners, and exalted higher than the heavens.
058	HEB	007	027	And he has no need, daily, in the manner of other priests, to offer sacrifices, first for his own sins, and then for those of the people. For he has done this once, by offering himself.
058	HEB	007	028	For the law appoints men as priests, though they have infirmities. But, by the word of the oath that is after the law, the Son has been perfected for eternity.
058	HEB	008	001	Now the main point in the things that have been stated is this: that we have so great a High Priest, who is seated at the right hand of the throne of Majesty in the heavens,
058	HEB	008	002	who is the minister of holy things, and of the true tabernacle, which was established by the Lord, not by man.
058	HEB	008	003	For every high priest is appointed to offer gifts and sacrifices. Therefore, it is necessary for him also to have something to offer.
058	HEB	008	004	And so, if he were upon the earth, he would not be a priest, since there would be others to offer gifts according to the law,
058	HEB	008	005	gifts which serve as mere examples and shadows of the heavenly things. And so it was answered to Moses, when he was about to complete the tabernacle: “See to it,” he said, “that you make everything according to the example which was revealed to you on the mountain.”
058	HEB	008	006	But now he has been granted a better ministry, so much so that he is also the Mediator of a better testament, which has been confirmed by better promises.
058	HEB	008	007	For if the former one had been entirely without fault, then a place certainly would not have been sought for a subsequent one.
058	HEB	008	008	For, finding fault with them, he says: “Behold, the days shall arrive, says the Lord, when I will consummate a New Testament over the house of Israel and the house of Judah,
058	HEB	008	009	not according to the testament which I made with their fathers, on the day when I took them by the hand, so that I might lead them away from the land of Egypt. For they did not remain in my testament, and so I disregarded them, says the Lord.
058	HEB	008	010	For this is the testament which I will set before the house of Israel, after those days, says the Lord. I will instill my laws in their minds, and I will inscribe my laws on their hearts. And so, I will be their God, and they shall be my people.
058	HEB	008	011	And they will not teach, each one his neighbor, and each one his brother, saying: ‘Know the Lord.’ For all shall know me, from the least, even to the greatest of them.
058	HEB	008	012	For I will forgive their iniquities, and I will no longer remember their sins.”
058	HEB	008	013	Now in saying something new, he has made the former old. But that which decays and grows old is close to passing away.
058	HEB	009	001	Certainly, the former also had the justifications of worship and a holy place for that age.
058	HEB	009	002	For a tabernacle was made at first, in which were the lampstand, and the table, and the bread of the Presence, which is called Holy.
058	HEB	009	003	Then, beyond the second veil, was the tabernacle, which is called the Holy of Holies,
058	HEB	009	004	having a golden censer, and the ark of the testament, covered all around and on every part with gold, in which was a golden urn containing manna, and the rod of Aaron which had blossomed, and the tablets of the testament.
058	HEB	009	005	And over the ark were the Cherubim of glory, overshadowing the propitiatory. There is not enough time to speak about each of these things.
058	HEB	009	006	Yet truly, once such things were placed together, in the first part of the tabernacle, the priests were, indeed, continually entering, so as to carry out the duties of the sacrifices.
058	HEB	009	007	But into the second part, once a year, the high priest alone entered, not without blood, which he offered on behalf of the neglectful offenses of himself and of the people.
058	HEB	009	008	In this way, the Holy Spirit is signifying that the way to what is most holy was not yet made manifest, not while the first tabernacle was still standing.
058	HEB	009	009	And this is a parable for the present time. Accordingly, those gifts and sacrifices that are offered are not able, as concerns the conscience, to make perfect those things that serve only as food and drink,
058	HEB	009	010	as well as the various washings and justices of the flesh, which were imposed upon them until the time of correction.
058	HEB	009	011	But Christ, standing as the High Priest of future good things, through a greater and more perfect tabernacle, one not made by hand, that is, not of this creation,
058	HEB	009	012	entered once into the Holy of Holies, having obtained eternal redemption, neither by the blood of goats, nor of calves, but by his own blood.
058	HEB	009	013	For if the blood of goats and oxen, and the ashes of a calf, when these are sprinkled, sanctify those who have been defiled, in order to cleanse the flesh,
058	HEB	009	014	how much more will the blood of Christ, who through the Holy Spirit has offered himself, immaculate, to God, cleanse our conscience from dead works, in order to serve the living God?
058	HEB	009	015	And thus he is the Mediator of the new testament, so that, by his death, he intercedes for the redemption of those transgressions which were under the former testament, so that those who have been called may receive the promise of an eternal inheritance.
058	HEB	009	016	For where there is a testament, it is necessary for the death of the one who testifies to intervene.
058	HEB	009	017	For a testament is confirmed by death. Otherwise, it as yet has no force, as long as the one who testifies lives.
058	HEB	009	018	Therefore, indeed, the first was not dedicated without blood.
058	HEB	009	019	For when every commandment of the law had been read by Moses to the entire people, he took up the blood of calves and goats, with water and with scarlet wool and hyssop, and he sprinkled both the book itself and the entire people,
058	HEB	009	020	saying: “This is the blood of the testament which God has commanded for you.”
058	HEB	009	021	And even the tabernacle, and all the vessels for the ministry, he similarly sprinkled with blood.
058	HEB	009	022	And nearly everything, according to the law, is to be cleansed with blood. And without the shedding of blood, there is no remission.
058	HEB	009	023	Therefore, it is necessary for the examples of heavenly things to be cleansed, just as, indeed, these things were. Yet the heavenly things are themselves better sacrifices than these.
058	HEB	009	024	For Jesus did not enter by means of holy things made with hands, mere examples of the true things, but he entered into Heaven itself, so that he may appear now before the face of God for us.
058	HEB	009	025	And he did not enter so as to offer himself repeatedly, as the high priest enters into the Holy of Holies each year, with the blood of another.
058	HEB	009	026	Otherwise, he would need to have suffered repeatedly since the beginning of the world. But now, one time, at the consummation of the ages, he has appeared in order to destroy sin though his own sacrifice.
058	HEB	009	027	And in the same manner as it has been appointed for men to die one time, and after this, to be judged,
058	HEB	009	028	so also Christ was offered, one time, in order to empty the sins of so many. He shall appear a second time without sin, for those who await him, unto salvation.
058	HEB	010	001	For the law contains the shadow of future good things, not the very image of these things. So, by the very same sacrifices which they offer ceaselessly each year, they can never cause these to approach perfection.
058	HEB	010	002	Otherwise, they would have ceased to be offered, because the worshipers, once cleansed, would no longer be conscious of any sin.
058	HEB	010	003	Instead, in these things, a commemoration of sins is made every year.
058	HEB	010	004	For it is impossible for sins to be taken away by the blood of oxen and goats.
058	HEB	010	005	For this reason, as Christ enters into the world, he says: “Sacrifice and oblation, you did not want. But you have fashioned a body for me.
058	HEB	010	006	Holocausts for sin were not pleasing to you.
058	HEB	010	007	Then I said, ‘Behold, I draw near.’ At the head of the book, it has been written of me that I should do your will, O God.”
058	HEB	010	008	In the above, by saying, “Sacrifices, and oblations, and holocausts for sin, you did not want, nor are those things pleasing to you, which are offered according to the law;
058	HEB	010	009	then I said, ‘Behold, I have come to do your will, O God,’” he takes away the first, so that he may establish what follows.
058	HEB	010	010	For by this will, we have been sanctified, through the one time oblation of the body of Jesus Christ.
058	HEB	010	011	And certainly, every priest stands by, ministering daily, and frequently offering the same sacrifices, which are never able to take away sins.
058	HEB	010	012	But this man, offering one sacrifice for sins, sits at the right hand of God forever,
058	HEB	010	013	awaiting that time when his enemies will be made his footstool.
058	HEB	010	014	For, by one oblation, he has brought to fulfillment, for all time, those who are sanctified.
058	HEB	010	015	Now the Holy Spirit also testifies for us about this. For afterward, he said:
058	HEB	010	016	“And this is the testament which I will commit to them after those days, says the Lord. I will instill my laws in their hearts, and I will inscribe my laws on their minds.
058	HEB	010	017	And I will no longer remember their sins and iniquities.”
058	HEB	010	018	Now, when there is a remission of these things, there is no longer an oblation for sin.
058	HEB	010	019	And so, brothers, have faith in the entrance into the Holy of Holies by the blood of Christ,
058	HEB	010	020	and in the new and living Way, which he has initiated for us by the veil, that is, by his flesh,
058	HEB	010	021	and in the Great Priest over the house of God.
058	HEB	010	022	So, let us draw near with a true heart, in the fullness of faith, having hearts cleansed from an evil conscience, and bodies absolved with clean water.
058	HEB	010	023	Let us hold fast to the confession of our hope, without wavering, for he who has promised is faithful.
058	HEB	010	024	And let us be considerate of one another, so as to prompt ourselves to charity and to good works,
058	HEB	010	025	not deserting our assembly, as some are accustomed to do, but consoling one another, and even more so as you see that the day is approaching.
058	HEB	010	026	For if we sin willingly, after receiving knowledge of the truth, there is no sacrifice remaining for sins,
058	HEB	010	027	but instead, a certain terrible expectation of judgment, and the rage of a fire that shall consume its adversaries.
058	HEB	010	028	If someone dies for acting against the law of Moses, and is shown no compassion because of two or three witnesses,
058	HEB	010	029	how much more, do you think, someone would deserve worse punishments, if he has tread upon the Son of God, and has treated the blood of the testament, by which he was sanctified, as unclean, and has acted with disgrace toward the Spirit of grace?
058	HEB	010	030	For we know that he has said: “Vengeance is mine, and I will repay,” and again, “The Lord will judge his people.”
058	HEB	010	031	It is dreadful to fall into the hands of the living God.
058	HEB	010	032	But call to mind the former days, in which, after being enlightened, you endured a great struggle of afflictions.
058	HEB	010	033	And certainly, in one way, by insults and tribulations, you were made a spectacle, but in another way, you became the companions of those who were the object of such behavior.
058	HEB	010	034	For you even had compassion on those who were imprisoned, and you accepted with gladness being deprived of your goods, knowing that you have a better and more lasting substance.
058	HEB	010	035	And so, do not lose your confidence, which has a great reward.
058	HEB	010	036	For it is necessary for you to be patient, so that, by doing the will of God, you may receive the promise.
058	HEB	010	037	“For, in a little while, and somewhat longer, he who is to come will return, and he will not delay.
058	HEB	010	038	For my just man lives by faith. But if he were to draw himself back, he would not please my soul.”
058	HEB	010	039	So then, we are not sons who are drawn away to perdition, but we are sons of faith toward the securing of the soul.
058	HEB	011	001	Now, faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not apparent.
058	HEB	011	002	For this reason, the ancients were given testimony.
058	HEB	011	003	By faith, we understand the world to be fashioned by the Word of God, so that the visible might be made by the invisible.
058	HEB	011	004	By faith, Abel offered to God a much better sacrifice than that of Cain, through which he obtained testimony that he was just, in that God offered testimony to his gifts. And through that sacrifice, he still speaks to us, though he is dead.
058	HEB	011	005	By faith, Enoch was transferred, so that he would not see death, and he was not found because God had transferred him. For before he was transferred, he had testimony that he pleased God.
058	HEB	011	006	But without faith, it is impossible to please God. For whoever approaches God must believe that he exists, and that he rewards those who seek him.
058	HEB	011	007	By faith, Noah, having accepted an answer about those things which were not yet seen, being afraid, fashioned an ark for the salvation of his house. Through the ark, he condemned the world, and was established as the heir of the justice that occurs through faith.
058	HEB	011	008	By faith, the one called Abraham obeyed, going out to the place that he was to receive as an inheritance. And he went out, not knowing where he was going.
058	HEB	011	009	By faith, he stayed in the Land of the Promise as if in a foreign land, dwelling in cottages, with Isaac and Jacob, co-heirs of the same promise.
058	HEB	011	010	For he was awaiting a city having firm foundations, whose designer and builder is God.
058	HEB	011	011	By faith also, Sarah herself, being barren, received the ability to conceive offspring, even though she was past that age in life. For she believed him to be faithful, who had promised.
058	HEB	011	012	Because of this, there were also born, from one who himself was as if dead, a multitude like the stars of heaven, who are, like the sand of the seashore, innumerable.
058	HEB	011	013	All of these passed away, adhering to faith, not having received the promises, yet beholding them from afar and saluting them, and confessing themselves to be sojourners and guests upon the earth.
058	HEB	011	014	For those who speak in this way are themselves indicating that they seek a homeland.
058	HEB	011	015	And if, indeed, they had been mindful of the very place from which they departed, they certainly would have returned in time.
058	HEB	011	016	But now they hunger for a better place, that is, Heaven. For this reason, God is not ashamed to be called their God. For he has prepared a city for them.
058	HEB	011	017	By faith, Abraham, when he was tested, offered Isaac, so that he who had received the promises was offering up his only son.
058	HEB	011	018	To him, it was said, “Through Isaac, shall your offspring be summoned,”
058	HEB	011	019	indicating that God is even able to raise up from the dead. And thus, he also established him as a parable.
058	HEB	011	020	By faith, also, Isaac blessed Jacob and Esau, concerning future events.
058	HEB	011	021	By faith, Jacob, as he was dying, blessed each of the sons of Joseph; and he reverenced the summit of his rod.
058	HEB	011	022	By faith, Joseph, as he was dying, recalled the departure of the sons of Israel, and gave a commandment concerning his bones.
058	HEB	011	023	By faith, Moses, after being born, was hidden for three months by his parents, because they had seen that he was a graceful infant, and they did not fear the king’s edict.
058	HEB	011	024	By faith, Moses, after growing up, denied himself a place as the son of Pharaoh’s daughter,
058	HEB	011	025	choosing to be afflicted with the people of God, rather than to have the pleasantness of sin for a time,
058	HEB	011	026	valuing the reproach of Christ to be a greater wealth than the treasures of the Egyptians. For he looked forward to his reward.
058	HEB	011	027	By faith, he abandoned Egypt, not dreading the animosity of the king. For he pressed on, as if seeing him who is unseen.
058	HEB	011	028	By faith, he celebrated the Passover and the shedding of the blood, so that he who destroyed the firstborn might not touch them.
058	HEB	011	029	By faith, they crossed the Red Sea, as if on dry land, yet when the Egyptians attempted it, they were swallowed up.
058	HEB	011	030	By faith, the walls of Jericho collapsed, after being encircled for seven days.
058	HEB	011	031	By faith, Rahab, the harlot, did not perish with the unbelievers, after receiving the spies with peace.
058	HEB	011	032	And what should I say next? For time is not sufficient for me to give an account of Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah, David, Samuel, and the Prophets:
058	HEB	011	033	those who, by faith, conquered kingdoms, accomplished justice, obtained promises, closed the mouths of lions,
058	HEB	011	034	extinguished the violence of fire, escaped the edge of the sword, recovered from infirmities, showed strength in battle, turned back the armies of foreigners.
058	HEB	011	035	Women received their dead by means of resurrection. But others suffered severe punishment, not yet receiving redemption, so that they would find a better resurrection.
058	HEB	011	036	Truly, others were tested by mocking and lashes, and moreover by chains and imprisonment.
058	HEB	011	037	They were stoned; they were cut; they were tempted. With the slaughter of the sword, they were killed. They wandered about in sheepskin and in goatskin, in dire need, in anguish afflicted.
058	HEB	011	038	Of them, the world was not worthy, wandering in solitude on mountains, in the caves and caverns of the earth.
058	HEB	011	039	And all these, having been proven by the testimony of faith, did not receive the Promise.
058	HEB	011	040	God’s Providence holds something better for us, so that not without us would they be perfected.
058	HEB	012	001	Furthermore, since we also have so great a cloud of witnesses over us, let us set aside every burden and sin which may surround us, and advance, through patience, to the struggle offered to us.
058	HEB	012	002	Let us gaze upon Jesus, as the Author and the completion of our faith, who, having joy laid out before him, endured the cross, disregarding the shame, and who now sits at the right hand of the throne of God.
058	HEB	012	003	So then, meditate upon him who endured such adversity from sinners against himself, so that you may not become weary, failing in your souls.
058	HEB	012	004	For you have not yet resisted unto blood, while striving against sin.
058	HEB	012	005	And you have forgotten the consolation which speaks to you like sons, saying: “My son, do not be willing to neglect the discipline of the Lord. Neither should you become weary, while being rebuked by him.”
058	HEB	012	006	For whomever the Lord loves, he chastises. And every son whom he accepts, he scourges.
058	HEB	012	007	Persevere in discipline. God presents you to himself as sons. But what son is there, whom his father does not correct?
058	HEB	012	008	But if you are without that discipline in which all have become sharers, then you are of adultery, and you are not sons.
058	HEB	012	009	Then, too, we have certainly had the fathers of our flesh as instructors, and we reverenced them. Should we not obey the Father of spirits all the more, and so live?
058	HEB	012	010	And indeed, for a few days and according to their own wishes, they instructed us. But he does so to our benefit, so that we may receive his sanctification.
058	HEB	012	011	Now every discipline, in the present time, does not seem a gladness, of course, but a grief. But afterwards, it will repay a most peaceful fruit of justice to those who become trained in it.
058	HEB	012	012	Because of this, lift up your lazy hands and your lax knees,
058	HEB	012	013	and straighten the path of your feet, so that no one, being lame, may wander astray, but instead may be healed.
058	HEB	012	014	Pursue peace with everyone. Pursue sanctity, without which no one shall see God.
058	HEB	012	015	Be contemplative, lest anyone lack the grace of God, lest any root of bitterness spring up and impede you, and by it, many might be defiled,
058	HEB	012	016	lest any fornicator or worldly person be like Esau, who, for the sake of one meal, sold his birthright.
058	HEB	012	017	For you know that afterwards, when he desired to inherit the benediction, he was rejected. For he found no place for repentance, even though he had sought it with tears.
058	HEB	012	018	But you have not drawn near to a tangible mountain, or a burning fire, or a whirlwind, or a mist, or a storm,
058	HEB	012	019	or the sound of a trumpet, or a voice of words. Those who had experienced these things excused themselves, lest the Word be spoken to them.
058	HEB	012	020	For they could not bear what was said, and so, if even a beast would have touched the mountain, it would have been stoned.
058	HEB	012	021	And what was seen was so terrible that even Moses said: “I am terrified, and so, I tremble.”
058	HEB	012	022	But you have drawn near to mount Zion, and to the city of the living God, to the heavenly Jerusalem, and to the company of many thousands of Angels,
058	HEB	012	023	and to the Church of the first-born, those who have been inscribed in the heavens, and to God, the judge of all, and to the spirits of the just made perfect,
058	HEB	012	024	and to Jesus, the Mediator of the New Testament, and to a sprinkling of blood, which speaks better than the blood of Abel.
058	HEB	012	025	Be careful not to reject the One who is speaking. For if those who rejected him who was speaking upon the earth were not able to escape, so much more we who might turn away from the One who is speaking to us from heaven.
058	HEB	012	026	Then, his voice moved the earth. But now, he makes a promise, saying: “There is still one more time, and then I will move, not only the earth, but also heaven itself.”
058	HEB	012	027	And so, in saying, “There is still one more time,” he declares the transfer of the moveable things of creation, so that those things which are immoveable may remain.
058	HEB	012	028	Thus, in receiving an immoveable kingdom, we have grace. So, through grace, let us be of service, by pleasing God with fear and reverence.
058	HEB	012	029	For our God is a consuming fire.
058	HEB	013	001	May fraternal charity remain in you.
058	HEB	013	002	And do not be willing to forget hospitality. For by it, certain persons, without realizing it, have received Angels as guests.
058	HEB	013	003	Remember those who are prisoners, just as if you were imprisoned with them, and those who endure hardships, just as if you were in their place.
058	HEB	013	004	May marriage be honorable in every way, and may the marriage bed be immaculate. For God will judge fornicators and adulterers.
058	HEB	013	005	Let your behavior be without avarice; be content with what you are offered. For he himself has said, “I will not abandon you, and I will not neglect you.”
058	HEB	013	006	So then, we may confidently say, “The Lord is my helper. I will not fear what man can do to me.”
058	HEB	013	007	Remember your leaders, who have spoken the Word of God to you, whose faith you imitate, by observing the goal of their way of life:
058	HEB	013	008	Jesus Christ, yesterday and today; Jesus Christ forever.
058	HEB	013	009	Do not be led away by changing or strange doctrines. And it is best for the heart to be sustained by grace, not by foods. For the latter have not been as useful to those who walked by them.
058	HEB	013	010	We have an altar: those who serve in the tabernacle have no authority to eat from it.
058	HEB	013	011	For the bodies of those animals whose blood is carried into the Holy of holies by the high priest, on behalf of sin, are burned outside the camp.
058	HEB	013	012	Because of this, Jesus, too, in order to sanctify the people by his own blood, suffered outside the gate.
058	HEB	013	013	And so, let us go forth to him, outside the camp, bearing his reproach.
058	HEB	013	014	For in this place, we have no everlasting city; instead, we seek one in the future.
058	HEB	013	015	Therefore, through him, let us offer the sacrifice of continual praise to God, which is the fruit of lips confessing his name.
058	HEB	013	016	But do not be willing to forget good works and fellowship. For God is deserving of such sacrifices.
058	HEB	013	017	Obey your leaders and be subject to them. For they watch over you, as if to render an account of your souls. So then, may they do this with joy, and not with grief. Otherwise, it would not be as helpful to you.
058	HEB	013	018	Pray for us. For we trust that we have a good conscience, being willing to conduct ourselves well in all things.
058	HEB	013	019	And I beg you, all the more, to do this, so that I may be quickly returned to you.
058	HEB	013	020	Then may the God of peace, who led back from the dead that great Pastor of sheep, our Lord Jesus Christ, with the blood of the eternal testament,
058	HEB	013	021	equip you with all goodness, so that you may do his will. May he accomplish in you whatever is pleasing in his sight, through Jesus Christ, to whom is glory forever and ever. Amen.
058	HEB	013	022	And I beg you, brothers, that you may permit this word of consolation, especially since I have written to you with few words.
058	HEB	013	023	Know that our brother Timothy has been set free. If he arrives soon, then I will see you with him.
058	HEB	013	024	Greet all your leaders and all the saints. The brothers from Italy greet you.
058	HEB	013	025	Grace be with you all. Amen.
#
# BOOK	059	JAM	James	James
059	JAM	001	001	James, servant of God and of our Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes of the dispersion, greetings.
059	JAM	001	002	My brothers, when you have fallen into various trials, consider everything a joy,
059	JAM	001	003	knowing that the proving of your faith exercises patience,
059	JAM	001	004	and patience brings a work to perfection, so that you may be perfect and whole, deficient in nothing.
059	JAM	001	005	But if anyone among you is in need of wisdom, let him petition God, who gives abundantly to all without reproach, and it shall be given to him.
059	JAM	001	006	But he should ask with faith, doubting nothing. For he who doubts is like a wave on the ocean, which is moved about by the wind and carried away;
059	JAM	001	007	then a man should not consider that he would receive anything from the Lord.
059	JAM	001	008	For a man who is of two minds is inconstant in all his ways.
059	JAM	001	009	Now a humble brother should glory in his exaltation,
059	JAM	001	010	and a rich one, in his humiliation, for he will pass away like the flower of the grass.
059	JAM	001	011	For the sun has risen with a scorching heat, and has dried the grass, and its flower has fallen off, and the appearance of its beauty has perished. So also will the rich one wither away, according to his paths.
059	JAM	001	012	Blessed is the man who suffers temptation. For when he has been proven, he shall receive the crown of life which God has promised to those who love him.
059	JAM	001	013	No one should say, when he is tempted, that he was tempted by God. For God does not entice toward evils, and he himself tempts no one.
059	JAM	001	014	Yet truly, each one is tempted by his own desires, having been enticed and drawn away.
059	JAM	001	015	Thereafter, when desire has conceived, it gives birth to sin. Yet truly sin, when it has been consummated, produces death.
059	JAM	001	016	And so, do not choose to go astray, my most beloved brothers.
059	JAM	001	017	Every excellent gift and every perfect gift is from above, descending from the Father of lights, with whom there is no change, nor any shadow of alteration.
059	JAM	001	018	For by his own will he produced us through the Word of truth, so that we might be a kind of beginning among his creatures.
059	JAM	001	019	You know this, my most beloved brothers. So let every man be quick to listen, but slow to speak and slow to anger.
059	JAM	001	020	For the anger of man does not accomplish the justice of God.
059	JAM	001	021	Because of this, having cast away all uncleanness and an abundance of malice, receive with meekness the newly-grafted Word, which is able to save your souls.
059	JAM	001	022	So be doers of the Word, and not listeners only, deceiving yourselves.
059	JAM	001	023	For if anyone is a listener of the Word, but not also a doer, he is comparable to a man gazing into a mirror upon the face that he was born with;
059	JAM	001	024	and after considering himself, he went away and promptly forgot what he had seen.
059	JAM	001	025	But he who gazes upon the perfect law of liberty, and who remains in it, is not a forgetful hearer, but instead a doer of the work. He shall be blessed in what he does.
059	JAM	001	026	But if anyone considers himself to be religious, but he does not restrain his tongue, but instead seduces his own heart: such a one’s religion is vanity.
059	JAM	001	027	This is religion, clean and undefiled before God the Father: to visit orphans and widows in their tribulations, and to keep yourself immaculate, apart from this age.
059	JAM	002	001	My brothers, within the glorious faith of our Lord Jesus Christ, do not choose to show favoritism toward persons.
059	JAM	002	002	For if a man has entered your assembly having a gold ring and splendid apparel, and if a poor man has also entered, in dirty clothing,
059	JAM	002	003	and if you are then attentive to the one who is clothed in excellent apparel, so that you say to him, “You may sit in this good place,” but you say to the poor man, “You stand over there,” or, “Sit below my footstool,”
059	JAM	002	004	are you not judging within yourselves, and have you not become judges with unjust thoughts?
059	JAM	002	005	My most beloved brothers, listen. Has not God chosen the poor in this world to be rich in faith and heirs of the kingdom that God has promised to those who love him?
059	JAM	002	006	But you have dishonored the poor. Are not the rich the ones who oppress you through power? And are not they the ones who drag you to judgment?
059	JAM	002	007	Are not they the ones who blaspheme the good name which has been invoked over you?
059	JAM	002	008	So if you perfect the regal law, according to the Scriptures, “You shall love your neighbor as yourself,” then you do well.
059	JAM	002	009	But if you show favoritism to persons, then you commit a sin, having been convicted again by the law as transgressors.
059	JAM	002	010	Now whoever has observed the whole law, yet who offends in one matter, has become guilty of all.
059	JAM	002	011	For he who said, “You shall not commit adultery,” also said, “You shall not kill.” So if you do not commit adultery, but you kill, you have become a transgressor of the law.
059	JAM	002	012	So speak and act just as you are beginning to be judged, by the law of liberty.
059	JAM	002	013	For judgment is without mercy toward him who has not shown mercy. But mercy exalts itself above judgment.
059	JAM	002	014	My brothers, what benefit is there if someone claims to have faith, but he does not have works? How would faith be able to save him?
059	JAM	002	015	So if a brother or sister is naked and daily in need of food,
059	JAM	002	016	and if anyone of you were to say to them: “Go in peace, keep warm and nourished,” and yet not give them the things that are necessary for the body, of what benefit is this?
059	JAM	002	017	Thus even faith, if it does not have works, is dead, in and of itself.
059	JAM	002	018	Now someone may say: “You have faith, and I have works.” Show me your faith without works! But I will show you my faith by means of works.
059	JAM	002	019	You believe that there is one God. You do well. But the demons also believe, and they tremble greatly.
059	JAM	002	020	So then, are you willing to understand, O foolish man, that faith without works is dead?
059	JAM	002	021	Was not our father Abraham justified by means of works, by offering his son Isaac upon the altar?
059	JAM	002	022	Do you see that faith was cooperating with his works, and that by means of works faith was brought to fulfillment?
059	JAM	002	023	And so the Scripture was fulfilled which says: “Abraham believed God, and it was reputed to him unto justice.” And so he was called the friend of God.
059	JAM	002	024	Do you see that a man is justified by means of works, and not by faith alone?
059	JAM	002	025	Similarly also, Rahab, the harlot, was she not justified by works, by receiving the messengers and sending them out through another way?
059	JAM	002	026	For just as the body without the spirit is dead, so also faith without works is dead.
059	JAM	003	001	My brothers, not many of you should choose to become teachers, knowing that you shall receive a stricter judgment.
059	JAM	003	002	For we all offend in many ways. If anyone does not offend in word, he is a perfect man. And he is then able, as if with a bridle, to lead the whole body around.
059	JAM	003	003	For so we put bridles into the mouths of horses, in order to submit them to our will, and so we turn their whole body around.
059	JAM	003	004	Consider also the ships, which, though they are great and may be driven by strong winds, yet they are turned around with a small rudder, to be directed to wherever the strength of the pilot might will.
059	JAM	003	005	So also the tongue certainly is a small part, but it moves great things. Consider that a small fire can set ablaze a great forest.
059	JAM	003	006	And so the tongue is like a fire, comprising all iniquity. The tongue, stationed in the midst of our body, can defile the entire body and inflame the wheel of our nativity, setting a fire from Hell.
059	JAM	003	007	For the nature of all beasts and birds and serpents and others is ruled over, and has been ruled over, by human nature.
059	JAM	003	008	But no man is able to rule over the tongue, a restless evil, full of deadly poison.
059	JAM	003	009	By it we bless God the Father, and by it we speak evil of men, who have been made in the likeness of God.
059	JAM	003	010	From the same mouth proceeds blessing and cursing. My brothers, these things ought not to be so!
059	JAM	003	011	Does a fountain emit, out of the same opening, both sweet and bitter water?
059	JAM	003	012	My brothers, can the fig tree yield grapes? Or the vine, figs? Then neither is salt water able to produce fresh water.
059	JAM	003	013	Who is wise and well-taught among you? Let him show, by means of good conversation, his work in the meekness of wisdom.
059	JAM	003	014	But if you hold a bitter zeal, and if there is contention in your hearts, then do not boast and do not be liars against the truth.
059	JAM	003	015	For this is not wisdom, descending from above, but rather it is earthly, beastly, and diabolical.
059	JAM	003	016	For wherever envy and contention is, there too is inconstancy and every depraved work.
059	JAM	003	017	But within the wisdom that is from above, certainly, chastity is first, and next peacefulness, meekness, openness, consenting to what is good, a plenitude of mercy and good fruits, not judging, without falseness.
059	JAM	003	018	And so the fruit of justice is sown in peace by those who make peace.
059	JAM	004	001	Where do wars and contentions among you come from? Is it not from this: from your own desires, which battle within your members?
059	JAM	004	002	You desire, and you do not have. You envy and you kill, and you are unable to obtain. You argue and you fight, and you do not have, because you do not ask.
059	JAM	004	003	You ask and you do not receive, because you ask badly, so that you may use it toward your own desires.
059	JAM	004	004	You adulterers! Do you not know that the friendship of this world is hostile to God? Therefore, whoever has chosen to be a friend of this world has been made into an enemy of God.
059	JAM	004	005	Or do you think that Scripture says in vain: “The spirit which lives within you desires unto envy?”
059	JAM	004	006	But he gives a greater grace. Therefore he says: “God resists the arrogant, but he gives grace to the humble.”
059	JAM	004	007	Therefore, be subject to God. But resist the devil, and he will flee from you.
059	JAM	004	008	Draw near to God, and he will draw near to you. Cleanse your hands, you sinners! And purify your hearts, you duplicitous souls!
059	JAM	004	009	Be afflicted: mourn and weep. Let your laughter be turned into mourning, and your gladness into sorrow.
059	JAM	004	010	Be humbled in the sight of the Lord, and he will exalt you.
059	JAM	004	011	Brothers, do not choose to slander one another. Whoever slanders his brother, or whoever judges his brother, slanders the law and judges the law. But if you judge the law, you are not a doer of the law, but a judge.
059	JAM	004	012	There is one lawgiver and one judge. He is able to destroy, and he is able to set free.
059	JAM	004	013	But who are you to judge your neighbor? Consider this, you who say, “Today or tomorrow we will go into that city, and certainly we will spend a year there, and we will do business, and we will make our profit,”
059	JAM	004	014	consider that you do not know what will be tomorrow.
059	JAM	004	015	For what is your life? It is a mist that appears for a brief time, and afterwards will vanish away. So what you ought to say is: “If the Lord wills,” or, “If we live,” we will do this or that.
059	JAM	004	016	But now you exult in your arrogance. All such exultation is wicked.
059	JAM	004	017	Therefore, he who knows that he ought to do a good thing, and does not do it, for him it is a sin.
059	JAM	005	001	Act now, you who are wealthy! Weep and wail in your miseries, which will soon come upon you!
059	JAM	005	002	Your riches have been corrupted, and your garments have been eaten by moths.
059	JAM	005	003	Your gold and silver have rusted, and their rust will be a testimony against you, and it will eat away at your flesh like fire. You have stored up wrath for yourselves unto the last days.
059	JAM	005	004	Consider the pay of the workers who reaped your fields: it has been misappropriated by you; it cries out. And their cry has entered into the ears of the Lord of hosts.
059	JAM	005	005	You have feasted upon the earth, and you have nourished your hearts with luxuries, unto the day of slaughter.
059	JAM	005	006	You led away and killed the Just One, and he did not resist you.
059	JAM	005	007	Therefore, be patient, brothers, until the advent of the Lord. Consider that the farmer anticipates the precious fruit of the earth, waiting patiently, until he receives the early and the late rains.
059	JAM	005	008	Therefore, you too should be patient and should strengthen your hearts. For the advent of the Lord draws near.
059	JAM	005	009	Brothers, do not complain against one another, so that you may not be judged. Behold, the judge stands before the door.
059	JAM	005	010	My brothers, consider the Prophets, who spoke in the name of the Lord, as an example of departing from evil, of labor, and of patience.
059	JAM	005	011	Consider that we beatify those who have endured. You have heard of the patient suffering of Job. And you have seen the end of the Lord, that the Lord is merciful and compassionate.
059	JAM	005	012	But before all things, my brothers, do not choose to swear, neither by heaven, nor by the earth, nor in any other oath. But let your word ‘Yes’ be yes, and your word ‘No’ be no, so that you may not fall under judgment.
059	JAM	005	013	Is any of you sad? Let him pray. Is he even-tempered? Let him sing psalms.
059	JAM	005	014	Is anyone ill among you? Let him bring in the priests of the Church, and let them pray over him, anointing him with oil in the name of the Lord.
059	JAM	005	015	And a prayer of faith will save the infirm, and the Lord will alleviate him. And if he has sins, these will be forgiven him.
059	JAM	005	016	Therefore, confess your sins to one another, and pray for one another, so that you may be saved. For the unremitting prayer of a just person prevails over many things.
059	JAM	005	017	Elijah was a mortal man like us, and in prayer he prayed that it would not rain upon the earth. And it did not rain for three years and six months.
059	JAM	005	018	And he prayed again. And the heavens gave rain, and the earth brought forth her fruit.
059	JAM	005	019	My brothers, if anyone of you strays from the truth, and if someone converts him,
059	JAM	005	020	he ought to know that whoever causes a sinner to be converted from the error of his ways will save his soul from death and will cover a multitude of sins.
