# BOOK	061	2PE	2 Peter	2 Peter
061	2PE	001	001	Simon Peter, servant and Apostle of Jesus Christ, to those who have been allotted an equal faith with us in the justice of our God and in our Savior Jesus Christ.
061	2PE	001	002	Grace to you. And may peace be fulfilled according to the plan of God and of Christ Jesus our Lord,
061	2PE	001	003	in the same manner that all things which are for life and piety have been given to us by his Divine virtue, through the plan of him who has called us to our own glory and virtue.
061	2PE	001	004	Through Christ, he has given us the greatest and most precious promises, so that by these things you may become sharers in the Divine Nature, fleeing from the corruption of that desire which is in the world.
061	2PE	001	005	But as for you, taking up every concern, minister virtue in your faith; and in virtue, knowledge;
061	2PE	001	006	and in knowledge, moderation; and in moderation, patience; and in patience, piety;
061	2PE	001	007	and in piety, love of brotherhood; and in love of brotherhood, charity.
061	2PE	001	008	For if these things are with you, and if they abound, they will cause you to be neither empty, nor without fruit, within the plan of our Lord Jesus Christ.
061	2PE	001	009	For he who does not have these things at hand is blind and groping, being forgetful of his purification from his former offenses.
061	2PE	001	010	Because of this, brothers, be all the more diligent, so that by good works you may make certain your calling and election. For in doing these things, you do not sin at any time.
061	2PE	001	011	For in this way, you shall be provided abundantly with an entrance into the eternal kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ.
061	2PE	001	012	For this reason, I will always begin to admonish you about these things, even though, certainly, you know them and are confirmed in the present truth.
