061	2PE	001	015	Therefore, I will present a work for you to have, so that, frequently after my passing, you may call to mind these things.
061	2PE	001	016	For it was not by following fanciful doctrines that we made known to you the power and presence of our Lord Jesus Christ, but we were made eyewitnesses of his greatness.
061	2PE	001	017	For he received honor and glory from God the Father, whose voice descended to him from the magnificent glory: “This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased. Listen to him.”
061	2PE	001	018	We also heard this voice conveyed from heaven, when we were with him on the holy mountain.
061	2PE	001	019	And so, we have an even firmer prophetic word, to which you would do well to listen, as to a light shining within a dark place, until the day dawns, and the daystar rises, in your hearts.
061	2PE	001	020	Understand this first: that every prophecy of Scripture does not result from one’s own interpretation.
061	2PE	001	021	For prophecy was not conveyed by human will at any time. Instead, holy men were speaking about God while inspired by the Holy Spirit.
061	2PE	002	001	But there were also false prophets among the people, just as there will be among you lying teachers, who will introduce divisions of perdition, and they will deny him who bought them, the Lord, bringing upon themselves swift destruction.
061	2PE	002	002	And many persons will follow their indulgences; through such persons, the way of truth will be blasphemed.
061	2PE	002	003	And in avarice, they will negotiate about you with false words. Their judgment, in the near future, is not delayed, and their perdition does not sleep.
