# BOOK	062	1JO	1 John	1 John
062	1JO	001	001	He who was from the beginning, whom we have heard, whom we have seen with our eyes, upon whom we have gazed, and whom our hands have certainly touched: He is the Word of Life.
062	1JO	001	002	And that Life has been made manifest. And we have seen, and we testify, and we announce to you: the Eternal Life, who was with the Father, and who appeared to us.
062	1JO	001	003	He whom we have seen and heard, we announce to you, so that you, too, may have fellowship with us, and so that our fellowship may be with the Father and with his Son Jesus Christ.
062	1JO	001	004	And this we write to you, so that you may rejoice, and so that your joy may be full.
062	1JO	001	005	And this is the announcement which we have heard from him, and which we announce to you: that God is light, and in him there is no darkness.
062	1JO	001	006	If we claim that we have fellowship with him, and yet we walk in darkness, then we are lying and not telling the truth.
062	1JO	001	007	But if we walk in the light, just as he also is in the light, then we have fellowship with one another, and the blood of Jesus Christ, his Son, cleanses us from all sin.
062	1JO	001	008	If we claim that we have no sin, then we are deceiving ourselves and the truth is not in us.
062	1JO	001	009	If we confess our sins, then he is faithful and just, so as to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all iniquity.
062	1JO	001	010	If we claim that we have not sinned, then we make him a liar, and his Word is not in us.
062	1JO	002	001	My little sons, this I write to you, so that you may not sin. But if anyone has sinned, we have an Advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ, the Just One.
062	1JO	002	002	And he is the propitiation for our sins. And not only for our sins, but also for those of the whole world.
062	1JO	002	003	And we can be sure that we have known him by this: if we observe his commandments.
062	1JO	002	004	Whoever claims that he knows him, and yet does not keep his commandments, is a liar, and the truth is not in him.
062	1JO	002	005	But whoever keeps his word, truly in him the charity of God is perfected. And by this we know that we are in him.
062	1JO	002	006	Whoever declares himself to remain in him, ought to walk just as he himself walked.
062	1JO	002	007	Most beloved, I am not writing to you a new commandment, but the old commandment, which you had from the beginning. The old commandment is the Word, which you have heard.
062	1JO	002	008	Then too, I am writing to you a new commandment, which is the Truth in him and in you. For the darkness has passed away, and the true Light is now shining.
062	1JO	002	009	Whoever declares himself to be in the light, and yet hates his brother, is in the darkness even now.
062	1JO	002	010	Whoever loves his brother abides in the light, and there is no cause of offense in him.
062	1JO	002	011	But whoever hates his brother is in the darkness, and in darkness he walks, and he does not know where he is going. For the darkness has blinded his eyes.
062	1JO	002	012	I am writing to you, little sons, because your sins are forgiven for the sake of his name.
062	1JO	002	013	I am writing to you, fathers, because you have known him who is from the beginning. I am writing to you, adolescents, because you have overcome the evil one.
062	1JO	002	014	I am writing to you, little children, because you have known the Father. I am writing to you, young men, because you are strong, and the Word of God abides in you, and you have overcome the evil one.
062	1JO	002	015	Do not choose to love the world, nor the things that are in the world. If anyone loves the world, the charity of the Father is not in him.
062	1JO	002	016	For all that is in the world is the desire of the flesh, and the desire of the eyes, and the arrogance of a life which is not of the Father, but is of the world.
062	1JO	002	017	And the world is passing away, with its desire. But whoever does the will of God abides unto eternity.
062	1JO	002	018	Little sons, it is the last hour. And, as you have heard that the Antichrist is coming, so now many antichrists have arrived. By this, we know that it is the last hour.
062	1JO	002	019	They went out from among us, but they were not of us. For, if they had been of us, certainly they would have remained with us. But in this way, it is made manifest that none of them are of us.
062	1JO	002	020	Yet you have the anointing of the Holy One, and you know everything.
062	1JO	002	021	I have not written to you as to ones who are ignorant of the truth, but as to ones who know the truth. For no lie is of the truth.
062	1JO	002	022	Who is a liar, other than he who denies that Jesus is the Christ? This one is the Antichrist, who denies the Father and the Son.
062	1JO	002	023	No one who denies the Son also has the Father. Whoever confesses the Son, also has the Father.
062	1JO	002	024	As for you, let what you have heard from the beginning remain in you. If what you have heard from the beginning remains in you, then you, too, shall abide in the Son and in the Father.
062	1JO	002	025	And this is the Promise, which he himself has promised to us: Eternal Life.
062	1JO	002	026	I have written these things to you, because of those who would seduce you.
062	1JO	002	027	But as for you, let the Anointing that you have received from him abide in you. And so, you have no need of anyone to teach you. For his Anointing teaches you about everything, and it is the truth, and it is not a lie. And just as his Anointing has taught you, abide in him.
062	1JO	002	028	And now, little sons, abide in him, so that when he appears, we may have faith, and we may not be confounded by him at his advent.
062	1JO	002	029	If you know that he is just, then know, too, that all who do what is just are born of him.
062	1JO	003	001	See what kind of love the Father has given to us, that we would be called, and would become, the sons of God. Because of this, the world does not know us, for it did not know him.
062	1JO	003	002	Most beloved, we are now the sons of God. But what we shall be then has not yet appeared. We know that when he does appear, we shall be like him, for we shall see him as he is.
062	1JO	003	003	And everyone who holds this hope in him, keeps himself holy, just as he also is holy.
062	1JO	003	004	Everyone who commits a sin, also commits iniquity. For sin is iniquity.
062	1JO	003	005	And you know that he appeared in order that he might take away our sins. For in him there is no sin.
062	1JO	003	006	Everyone who abides in him does not sin. For whoever sins has not seen him, and has not known him.
062	1JO	003	007	Little sons, let no one deceive you. Whoever does justice is just, even as he also is just.
062	1JO	003	008	Whoever commits sin is of the devil. For the devil sins from the beginning. For this reason, the Son of God appeared, so that he might eradicate the works of the devil.
062	1JO	003	009	All those who have been born of God do not commit sin. For the offspring of God abides in them, and he is not able to sin, because he was born of God.
062	1JO	003	010	In this way, the sons of God are made manifest, and also the sons of the devil. Everyone who is not just, is not of God, as also anyone who does not love his brother.
062	1JO	003	011	For this is the announcement that you heard from the beginning: that you should love one another.
062	1JO	003	012	Do not be like Cain, who was of the evil one, and who killed his brother. And why did he kill him? Because his own works were wicked, but his brother’s works were just.
062	1JO	003	013	If the world hates you, brothers, do not be surprised.
062	1JO	003	014	We know that we have passed from death to life. For we love as brothers. Whoever does not love, abides in death.
062	1JO	003	015	Everyone who hates his brother is a murderer. And you know that no murderer has eternal life abiding within him.
062	1JO	003	016	We know the love of God in this way: because he laid down his life for us. And so, we must lay down our lives for our brothers.
062	1JO	003	017	Whoever possesses the goods of this world, and sees his brother to be in need, and yet closes his heart to him: in what way does the love of God abide in him?
062	1JO	003	018	My little sons, let us not love in words only, but in works and in truth.
062	1JO	003	019	In this way, we will know that we are of the truth, and we will commend our hearts in his sight.
062	1JO	003	020	For even if our heart reproaches us, God is greater than our heart, and he knows all things.
062	1JO	003	021	Most beloved, if our heart does not reproach us, we can have confidence toward God;
062	1JO	003	022	and whatever we shall request of him, we shall receive from him. For we keep his commandments, and we do the things that are pleasing in his sight.
062	1JO	003	023	And this is his commandment: that we should believe in the name of his Son, Jesus Christ, and love one another, just as he has commanded us.
062	1JO	003	024	And those who keep his commandments abide in him, and he in them. And we know that he abides in us by this: by the Spirit, whom he has given to us.
062	1JO	004	001	Most beloved, do not be willing to believe every spirit, but test the spirits to see if they are of God. For many false prophets have gone out into the world.
062	1JO	004	002	The Spirit of God may be known in this way. Every spirit who confesses that Jesus Christ has arrived in the flesh is of God;
062	1JO	004	003	and every spirit who contradicts Jesus is not of God. And this one is the Antichrist, the one that you have heard is coming, and even now he is in the world.
062	1JO	004	004	Little sons, you are of God, and so you have overcome him. For he who is in you is greater than he who is in the world.
062	1JO	004	005	They are of the world. Therefore, they speak about the world, and the world listens to them.
062	1JO	004	006	We are of God. Whoever knows God, listens to us. Whoever is not of God, does not listen to us. In this way, we know the Spirit of truth from the spirit of error.
062	1JO	004	007	Most beloved, let us love one another. For love is of God. And everyone who loves is born of God and knows God.
062	1JO	004	008	Whoever does not love, does not know God. For God is love.
062	1JO	004	009	The love of God was made apparent to us in this way: that God sent his only-begotten Son into the world, so that we might live through him.
062	1JO	004	010	In this is love: not as if we had loved God, but that he first loved us, and so he sent his Son as a propitiation for our sins.
062	1JO	004	011	Most beloved, if God has so loved us, we also ought to love one another.
062	1JO	004	012	No one has ever seen God. But if we love one another, God abides in us, and his love is perfected in us.
062	1JO	004	013	In this way, we know that we abide in him, and he in us: because he has given to us from his Spirit.
062	1JO	004	014	And we have seen, and we testify, that the Father has sent his Son to be the Savior of the world.
062	1JO	004	015	Whoever has confessed that Jesus is the Son of God, God abides in him, and he in God.
062	1JO	004	016	And we have known and believed the love that God has for us. God is love. And he who abides in love, abides in God, and God in him.
062	1JO	004	017	In this way, the love of God is perfected with us, so that we may have confidence on the day of judgment. For as he is, so also are we, in this world.
062	1JO	004	018	Fear is not in love. Instead, perfect love casts out fear, for fear pertains to punishment. And whoever fears is not perfected in love.
062	1JO	004	019	Therefore, let us love God, for God first loved us.
062	1JO	004	020	If anyone says that he loves God, but hates his brother, then he is a liar. For he who does not love his brother, whom he does see, in what way can he love God, whom he does not see?
062	1JO	004	021	And this is the commandment that we have from God, that he who loves God must also love his brother.
062	1JO	005	001	Everyone who believes that Jesus is the Christ, is born of God. And everyone who loves God, who provides that birth, also loves him who has been born of God.
062	1JO	005	002	In this way, we know that we love those born of God: when we love God and do his commandments.
062	1JO	005	003	For this is the love of God: that we keep his commandments. And his commandments are not heavy.
062	1JO	005	004	For all that is born of God overcomes the world. And this is the victory that overcomes the world: our faith.
062	1JO	005	005	Who is it that overcomes the world? Only he who believes that Jesus is the Son of God!
062	1JO	005	006	This is the One who came by water and blood: Jesus Christ. Not by water only, but by water and blood. And the Spirit is the One who testifies that the Christ is the Truth.
062	1JO	005	007	For there are Three who give testimony in heaven: the Father, the Word, and the Holy Spirit. And these Three are One.
062	1JO	005	008	And there are three who give testimony on earth: the Spirit, and the water, and the blood. And these three are one.
062	1JO	005	009	If we accept the testimony of men, then the testimony of God is greater. For this is the testimony of God, which is greater: that he has testified about his Son.
062	1JO	005	010	Whoever believes in the Son of God, holds the testimony of God within himself. Whoever does not believe in the Son, makes him a liar, because he does not believe in the testimony which God has testified about his Son.
062	1JO	005	011	And this is the testimony which God has given to us: Eternal Life. And this Life is in his Son.
062	1JO	005	012	Whoever has the Son, has Life. Whoever does not have the Son, does not have Life.
062	1JO	005	013	I am writing this to you, so that you may know that you have Eternal Life: you who believe in the name of the Son of God.
062	1JO	005	014	And this is the confidence which we have toward God: that no matter what we shall request, in accord with his will, he hears us.
062	1JO	005	015	And we know that he hears us, no matter what we request; so we know that we can obtain the things that we request of him.
062	1JO	005	016	Anyone who realizes that his brother has sinned, with a sin that is not unto death, let him pray, and life shall be given to him who has sinned not unto death. There is a sin which is unto death. I am not saying that anyone should ask on behalf of that sin.
062	1JO	005	017	All that is iniquity is sin. But there is a sin unto death.
062	1JO	005	018	We know that everyone who is born of God does not sin. Instead, rebirth in God preserves him, and the evil one cannot touch him.
062	1JO	005	019	We know that we are of God, and that the entire world is established in wickedness.
062	1JO	005	020	And we know that the Son of God has arrived, and that he has given us understanding, so that we may know the true God, and so that we may remain in his true Son. This is the true God, and this is Eternal Life.
062	1JO	005	021	Little sons, keep yourselves from false worship. Amen.
