# BOOK	064	3JO	3 John	3 John
064	3JO	001	001	The Elder, to Gaius, most beloved, whom I love in the truth.
064	3JO	001	002	Most beloved, concerning everything, I make it my prayer that you may benefit by advancing and succeeding in whatever may be to the benefit of your soul.
064	3JO	001	003	I was very glad when the brothers arrived, and when they offered testimony to the truth in you, that you are walking in the truth.
064	3JO	001	004	I have no greater grace than this, when I hear that my sons are walking in the truth.
064	3JO	001	005	Most beloved, you should act faithfully in whatever you do for the brothers, and those who are sojourners;
064	3JO	001	006	they have given testimony to your charity in the sight of the Church. You would do well to lead these ones worthily to God.
064	3JO	001	007	For they set out, on behalf of his name, accepting nothing from the unbelievers.
064	3JO	001	008	Therefore, we must accept such as these, in order that we may cooperate with the truth.
064	3JO	001	009	As it happens, I had written to the church. But Diotrephes, who loves to bear the highest rank among them, would not accept us.
064	3JO	001	010	Because of this, when I come, I will admonish his works which he does, babbling against us with malicious words. And as if this were not sufficient for him, he himself does not receive the brothers. And those who do receive them, he hinders, and he ejects them from the church.
064	3JO	001	011	Most beloved, do not be willing to imitate what is evil; instead imitate what is good. Whoever does good is of God. Whoever does evil has not seen God.
064	3JO	001	012	Testimony is being given for Demetrius by everyone, and by the truth itself. And we also offer testimony. And you know that our testimony is true.
064	3JO	001	013	I had many things to write to you, but I am not willing, through ink and pen, to write to you.
064	3JO	001	014	Yet I hope to see you soon, and then we will speak face to face. Peace to you. The friends greet you. Greet the friends by name.
