# BOOK	065	JUD	Jude	Jude
065	JUD	001	001	Jude, a servant of Jesus Christ, and brother of James, to those who are beloved in God the Father, and who are guarded and called in Jesus Christ:
065	JUD	001	002	May mercy, and peace, and love be fulfilled in you.
065	JUD	001	003	Most beloved, taking all care to write to you about your common salvation, I found it necessary to write to you in order to beg you to contend earnestly for the faith that was handed down once to the saints.
065	JUD	001	004	For certain men entered unnoticed, who were written of beforehand unto this judgment: impious persons who are transforming the grace of our God into self-indulgence, and who are denying both the sole Ruler and our Lord Jesus Christ.
065	JUD	001	005	So I want to caution you. Those who once knew everything that Jesus did, in saving the people from the land of Egypt, afterwards perished because they did not believe.
065	JUD	001	006	And truly, the Angels, who did not keep to their first place, but instead abandoned their own domiciles, he has reserved with perpetual chains under darkness, unto the great day of judgment.
065	JUD	001	007	And also Sodom and Gomorrah, and the adjoining cities, in similar ways, having given themselves over to fornication and to the pursuing of other flesh, were made an example, suffering the punishment of eternal fire.
065	JUD	001	008	Similarly also, these ones certainly defile the flesh, and they despise proper authority, and they blaspheme against majesty.
065	JUD	001	009	When Michael the Archangel, disputing with the devil, contended about the body of Moses, he did not dare to bring against him a judgment of blasphemy, so instead he said: “The Lord commands you.”
065	JUD	001	010	But these men certainly blaspheme against whatever they do not understand. And yet, whatever they, like mute animals, know from nature, in these things they are corrupted.
065	JUD	001	011	Woe to them! For they have gone after the way of Cain, and they have poured out the error of Balaam for profit, and they have perished in the sedition of Korah.
065	JUD	001	012	These ones are defiled within their banquets, enjoying themselves and feeding themselves without fear; waterless clouds, which are tossed about by winds; autumn trees, unfruitful, twice dead, uprooted;
065	JUD	001	013	raging waves of the sea, foaming from their own confusion; wandering stars, for whom the whirlwind of darkness has been reserved forever!
065	JUD	001	014	And about these, Enoch, the seventh from Adam, also prophesied, saying: “Behold, the Lord is arriving with thousands of his saints,
065	JUD	001	015	to execute judgment against everyone, and to reprove all the impious concerning all the works of their impiety, by which they have acted impiously, and concerning all the harsh things that impious sinners have spoken against God.”
065	JUD	001	016	These ones are complaining murmurers, walking according to their own desires. And their mouth is speaking arrogance, admiring persons for the sake of gain.
065	JUD	001	017	But as for you, most beloved, be mindful of the words which have been foretold by the Apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ,
065	JUD	001	018	who declared to you that, in the end time, there would arrive mockers, walking according to their own desires, in impieties.
065	JUD	001	019	These are the ones who segregate themselves; they are animals, not having the Spirit.
065	JUD	001	020	But you, most beloved, are building yourselves up by your most holy faith, praying in the Holy Spirit,
065	JUD	001	021	keeping yourselves in the love of God, and anticipating the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ unto eternal life.
065	JUD	001	022	So certainly, reprove them, after they have been judged.
065	JUD	001	023	Yet truly, save them, seizing them from the fire. And have mercy on others: in fear, hating even that which is of the flesh, the defiled garment.
065	JUD	001	024	Then, to him who has the power to keep you free from sin and to present you, immaculate, with exultation, before the presence of his glory at the advent of our Lord Jesus Christ,
065	JUD	001	025	to the only God, our Savior, through Jesus Christ our Lord: to him be glory and magnificence, dominion and power, before all ages, and now, and in every age, forever. Amen.
