# BOOK	066	REV	Revelation	Revelation
066	REV	001	001	The Revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave to him, in order to make known to his servants the things that must soon occur, and which he signified by sending his Angel to his servant John;
066	REV	001	002	he has offered testimony to the Word of God, and whatever he saw is the testimony of Jesus Christ.
066	REV	001	003	Blessed is he who reads or hears the words of this Prophecy, and who keeps the things that have been written in it. For the time is near.
066	REV	001	004	John, to the seven Churches, which are in Asia. Grace and peace to you, from him who is, and who was, and who is to come, and from the seven spirits who are in the sight of his throne,
066	REV	001	005	and from Jesus Christ, who is the faithful witness, the first-born of the dead, and the leader over the kings of the earth, who has loved us and has washed us from our sins with his blood,
066	REV	001	006	and who has made us into a kingdom and into priests for God and for his Father. To him be glory and dominion forever and ever. Amen.
066	REV	001	007	Behold, he arrives with the clouds, and every eye shall see him, even those who pierced him. And all the tribes of the earth shall lament for themselves over him. Even so. Amen.
066	REV	001	008	“I am the Alpha and the Omega, the Beginning and the End,” says the Lord God, who is, and who was, and who is to come, the Almighty.
066	REV	001	009	I, John, your brother, and a sharer in the tribulation and in the kingdom and in patient endurance for Christ Jesus, was on the island which is called Patmos, because of the Word of God and the testimony to Jesus.
066	REV	001	010	I was in the Spirit on the Lord’s day, and I heard behind me a great voice, like that of a trumpet,
066	REV	001	011	saying, “What you see, write in a book, and send it to the seven Churches, which are in Asia: to Ephesus, and to Smyrna, and to Pergamus, and to Thyatira, and to Sardis, and to Philadelphia, and to Laodicea.”
066	REV	001	012	And I turned around, so as to see the voice which was speaking with me. And having turned around, I saw seven golden lampstands.
066	REV	001	013	And in the midst of the seven golden lampstands was one resembling the Son of man, clothed to the feet with a vestment, and wrapped to the breast with a wide belt of gold.
066	REV	001	014	But his head and hair were bright, like white wool, or like snow; and his eyes were like a flame of fire;
066	REV	001	015	and his feet resembled shining brass, just as in a burning furnace; and his voice was like the voice of many waters.
066	REV	001	016	And in his right hand, he held the seven stars; and from his mouth went out a sharp two-edged sword; and his face was like the sun, shining with all its might.
066	REV	001	017	And when I had seen him, I fell at his feet, like one who is dead. And he laid his right hand upon me, saying: “Do not be afraid. I am the First and the Last.
066	REV	001	018	And I am alive, though I was dead. And, behold, I live forever and ever. And I hold the keys of death and of Hell.
066	REV	001	019	Therefore, write the things which you have seen, and which are, and which must occur afterward:
066	REV	001	020	the mystery of the seven stars, which you have seen in my right hand, and of the seven golden lampstands. The seven stars are the Angels of the seven Churches, and the seven lampstands are the seven Churches.”
066	REV	002	001	“And to the Angel of the Church of Ephesus write: Thus says the One who holds the seven stars in his right hand, who walks in the midst of the seven golden lampstands:
066	REV	002	002	I know your works, and your hardship and patient endurance, and that you cannot stand those who are evil. And so, you have tested those who declare themselves to be Apostles and are not, and you have found them to be liars.
066	REV	002	003	And you have patient endurance for the sake of my name, and you have not fallen away.
066	REV	002	004	But I have this against you: that you have relinquished your first charity.
066	REV	002	005	And so, call to mind the place from which you have fallen, and do penance, and do the first works. Otherwise, I will come to you and remove your lampstand from its place, unless you repent.
066	REV	002	006	But this you have, that you hate the deeds of the Nicolaitans, which I also hate.
066	REV	002	007	Whoever has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the Churches. To him who prevails, I will give to eat from the Tree of Life, which is in the Paradise of my God.
066	REV	002	008	And to the Angel of the Church of Smyrna write: Thus says the First and the Last, he who was dead and now lives:
066	REV	002	009	I know your tribulation and your poverty, but you are rich, and that you are blasphemed by those who declare themselves to be Jews and are not, but who are a synagogue of Satan.
066	REV	002	010	You should fear nothing amid those things which you will suffer. Behold, the devil will cast some of you into prison, so that you may be tested. And you will have tribulation for ten days. Be faithful even unto death, and I will give to you the crown of life.
066	REV	002	011	Whoever has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the Churches. Whoever will prevail, he shall not be harmed by the second death.
066	REV	002	012	And to the Angel of the Church of Pergamus write: Thus says he who holds the sharp two-edged spear:
066	REV	002	013	I know where you dwell, where the seat of Satan is, and that you hold to my name and have not denied my faith, even in those days when Antipas was my faithful witness, who was slain among you, where Satan dwells.
066	REV	002	014	But I have a few things against you. For you have, in that place, those who hold to the doctrine of Balaam, who instructed Balak to cast a stumbling block before the sons of Israel, to eat and to commit fornication.
066	REV	002	015	And you also have those who hold to the doctrine of the Nicolaitans.
066	REV	002	016	So do penance to the same extent. If you do less, I will come to you quickly and I will fight against these ones with the sword of my mouth.
066	REV	002	017	Whoever has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the Churches. To him who prevails, I will give the hidden manna. And I will give to him a white emblem, and on the emblem, a new name has been written, which no one knows, except the one who receives it.
066	REV	002	018	And to the Angel of the Church of Thyatira write: Thus says the Son of God, who has eyes like a flame of fire, and his feet are like shining brass.
066	REV	002	019	I know your works, and your faith and charity, and your ministry and patient endurance, and that your more recent works are greater than the earlier ones.
066	REV	002	020	But I have a few things against you. For you permit the woman Jezebel, who calls herself a prophetess, to teach and to seduce my servants, to commit fornication and to eat the food of idolatry.
066	REV	002	021	And I gave her a time, so that she might do penance, but she is not willing to repent from her fornication.
066	REV	002	022	Behold, I will cast her onto a bed, and those who commit adultery with her shall be in a very great tribulation, unless they repent from their works.
066	REV	002	023	And I will put her sons to death, and all the Churches shall know that I am the one who examines temperaments and hearts. And I will give to each one of you according to your works. But I say to you,
066	REV	002	024	and to the others who are at Thyatira: Whoever does not hold to this doctrine, and who has not ‘known the depths of Satan,’ as they say, I will not set any other weight upon you.
066	REV	002	025	Even so, that which you have, hold on to it until I return.
066	REV	002	026	And whoever will prevail and will observe my works even unto the end, I will give to him authority over the nations.
066	REV	002	027	And he shall rule them with an iron rod, and they shall be broken like the earthenware of a potter.
066	REV	002	028	The same I also have received from my Father. And I will give to him the morning star.
066	REV	002	029	Whoever has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the Churches.”
066	REV	003	001	“And to the Angel of the Church of Sardis write: Thus says he who has the seven spirits of God and the seven stars: I know your works, that you have a name which is alive, but you are dead.
066	REV	003	002	Be vigilant, and confirm the things that remain, lest they soon die out. For I do not find your works to be full in the sight of my God.
066	REV	003	003	Therefore, keep in mind the way that you have received and heard, and then observe it and repent. But if you will not be vigilant, I will come to you like a thief, and you will not know at what hour I will come to you.
066	REV	003	004	But you have a few names in Sardis who have not defiled their garments. And these shall walk with me in white, because they are worthy.
066	REV	003	005	Whoever prevails, so shall he be clothed in white vestments. And I will not delete his name from the Book of Life. And I will confess his name in the presence of my Father and in the presence of his Angels.
066	REV	003	006	Whoever has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the Churches.
066	REV	003	007	And to the Angel of the Church of Philadelphia write: Thus says the Holy One, the True One, he who holds the key of David. He opens and no one closes. He closes and no one opens.
066	REV	003	008	I know your works. Behold, I have set an open door before you, which no one is able to close. For you have little power, and you have observed my word, and you have not denied my name.
066	REV	003	009	Behold, I will take from the synagogue of Satan those who declare themselves to be Jews and are not, for they are lying. Behold, I will cause them to approach and to reverence before your feet. And they shall know that I have loved you.
066	REV	003	010	Since you have kept the word of my patient endurance, I also will keep you from the hour of temptation, which shall overcome the whole world in order to test those living upon the earth.
066	REV	003	011	Behold, I am approaching quickly. Hold on to what you have, so that no one may take your crown.
066	REV	003	012	Whoever prevails, I will set him as a column in the temple of my God, and he shall not depart from it anymore. And I will write upon him the name of my God, and the name of the city of my God, the new Jerusalem that descends out of heaven from my God, and my new name.
066	REV	003	013	Whoever has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the Churches.
066	REV	003	014	And to the Angel of the Church of Laodicea write: Thus says the Amen, the faithful and true Witness, who is the Beginning of the creation of God:
066	REV	003	015	I know your works: that you are neither cold, nor hot. I wish that you were either cold or hot.
066	REV	003	016	But because you are lukewarm and are neither cold nor hot, I will begin to vomit you out of my mouth.
066	REV	003	017	For you declare, ‘I am wealthy, and I have been enriched further, and I have need of nothing.’ And you do not know that you are wretched, and miserable, and poor, and blind, and naked.
066	REV	003	018	I urge you to buy from me gold, tested by fire, so that you may be enriched and may be clothed in white vestments, and so that the shame of your nakedness may disappear. And anoint your eyes with an eye salve, so that you may see.
066	REV	003	019	Those whom I love, I rebuke and chastise. Therefore, be zealous and do penance.
066	REV	003	020	Behold, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone will hear my voice and will open the door to me, I will enter to him, and I will dine with him, and he with me.
066	REV	003	021	Whoever prevails, I will grant to him to sit with me on my throne, just as I also have overcome and have sat down with my Father on his throne.
066	REV	003	022	Whoever has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the Churches.”
066	REV	004	001	After these things, I saw, and behold, a door was opened in heaven, and the voice that I heard speaking with me first was like a trumpet, saying: “Ascend to here, and I will reveal to you what must occur after these things.”
066	REV	004	002	And immediately I was in the Spirit. And behold, a throne had been placed in heaven, and there was One sitting upon the throne.
066	REV	004	003	And the One who was sitting there was similar in appearance to a stone of jasper and sardius. And there was an iridescence surrounding the throne, in aspect similar to an emerald.
066	REV	004	004	And surrounding the throne were twenty-four smaller thrones. And upon the thrones, twenty-four elders were sitting, clothed entirely in white vestments, and on their heads were gold crowns.
066	REV	004	005	And from the throne, lightnings and voices and thunders went forth. And there were seven burning lamps before the throne, which are the seven spirits of God.
066	REV	004	006	And in view of the throne, there was something that seemed like a sea of glass, similar to crystal. And in the middle of the throne, and all around the throne, there were four living creatures, full of eyes in front and in back.
066	REV	004	007	And the first living creature resembled a lion, and the second living creature resembled a calf, and the third living creature had a face like a man, and the fourth living creature resembled a flying eagle.
066	REV	004	008	And each of the four living creatures had upon them six wings, and all around and within they are full of eyes. And they took no rest, day or night, from saying: “Holy, Holy, Holy is the Lord God Almighty, who was, and who is, and who is to come.”
066	REV	004	009	And while those living creatures were giving glory and honor and blessings to the One sitting upon the throne, who lives forever and ever,
066	REV	004	010	the twenty-four elders fell prostrate before the One sitting upon the throne, and they adored him who lives forever and ever, and they cast their crowns before the throne, saying:
066	REV	004	011	“You are worthy, O Lord our God, to receive glory and honor and power. For you have created all things, and they became and were created because of your will.”
066	REV	005	001	And in the right hand of the One sitting upon the throne, I saw a book, written inside and out, sealed with seven seals.
066	REV	005	002	And I saw a strong Angel, proclaiming with a great voice, “Who is worthy to open the book and to break its seals?”
066	REV	005	003	And no one was able, neither in heaven, nor on earth, nor under the earth, to open the book, nor to gaze upon it.
066	REV	005	004	And I wept greatly because no one was found worthy to open the book, nor to see it.
066	REV	005	005	And one of the elders said to me: “Weep not. Behold, the lion from the tribe of Judah, the root of David, has prevailed to open the book and to break its seven seals.”
066	REV	005	006	And I saw, and behold, in the midst of the throne and the four living creatures, and in the midst of the elders, a Lamb was standing, as if it were slain, having seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven spirits of God, sent forth to all the earth.
066	REV	005	007	And he approached and received the book from the right hand of the One sitting upon the throne.
066	REV	005	008	And when he had opened the book, the four living creatures and the twenty-four elders fell down before the Lamb, each having stringed instruments, as well as golden bowls full of fragrances, which are the prayers of the saints.
066	REV	005	009	And they were singing a new canticle, saying: “O Lord, you are worthy to receive the book and to open its seals, because you were slain and have redeemed us for God, by your blood, from every tribe and language and people and nation.
066	REV	005	010	And you have made us into a kingdom and into priests for our God, and we shall reign over the earth.”
066	REV	005	011	And I saw, and I heard the voice of many Angels surrounding the throne and the living creatures and the elders, (and their number was thousands of thousands)
066	REV	005	012	saying with a great voice: “The Lamb who was slain is worthy to receive power, and divinity, and wisdom, and strength, and honor, and glory, and blessing.”
066	REV	005	013	And every creature that is in heaven, and on earth, and under the earth, and all that is within the sea: I heard them all saying: “To the One sitting upon the throne and to the Lamb be blessing, and honor, and glory, and authority, forever and ever.”
066	REV	005	014	And the four living creatures were saying, “Amen.” And the twenty-four elders fell down on their faces, and they adored the One who lives forever and ever.
066	REV	006	001	And I saw that the Lamb had opened one of the seven seals. And I heard one of the four living creatures saying, in a voice like thunder: “Draw near and see.”
066	REV	006	002	And I saw, and behold, a white horse. And he who was sitting upon it was holding a bow, and a crown was given to him, and he went forth conquering, so that he might prevail.
066	REV	006	003	And when he had opened the second seal, I heard the second living creature saying: “Draw near and see.”
066	REV	006	004	And another horse went forth, which was red. And it was granted to him who was sitting upon it that he would take peace from the earth, and that they would kill one another. And a great sword was given to him.
066	REV	006	005	And when he had opened the third seal, I heard the third living creature saying: “Draw near and see.” And behold, a black horse. And he who was sitting upon it was holding a balance in his hand.
066	REV	006	006	And I heard something like a voice in the midst of the four living creatures saying, “A double measure of wheat for a denarius, and three double measures of barley for a denarius, but do no harm to wine and oil.”
066	REV	006	007	And when he had opened the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth living creature saying: “Draw near and see.”
066	REV	006	008	And behold, a pale horse. And he who was sitting upon it, his name was Death, and Hell was following him. And authority was given to him over the four parts of the earth, to destroy by the sword, by famine, and by death, and by the creatures of the earth.
066	REV	006	009	And when he had opened the fifth seal, I saw, under the altar, the souls of those who had been slain because of the Word of God and because of the testimony that they held.
066	REV	006	010	And they were crying out with a loud voice, saying: “How long, O Holy and True Lord, will you not judge and not vindicate our blood against those who dwell upon the earth?”
066	REV	006	011	And white robes were given to each of them. And they were told that they should rest for a brief time, until their fellow servants and their brothers, who were to be slain even as they were slain, would be completed.
066	REV	006	012	And when he had opened the sixth seal, I saw, and behold, a great earthquake occurred. And the sun became black, like a haircloth sack, and the entire moon became like blood.
066	REV	006	013	And the stars from heaven fell upon the earth, just as when a fig tree, shaken by a great wind, drops its immature figs.
066	REV	006	014	And heaven receded, like a scroll being rolled up. And every mountain, and the islands, were moved from their places.
066	REV	006	015	And the kings of the earth, and the rulers, and the military leaders, and the wealthy, and the strong, and everyone, servant and free, hid themselves in caves and among the rocks of the mountains.
066	REV	006	016	And they said to the mountains and the rocks: “Fall over us and hide us from the face of the One sitting upon the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb.
066	REV	006	017	For the great day of their wrath has arrived. And who will be able to stand?”
